INSERT INTO main_app_journalentry VALUES(257,'2026-09-22','manual','ORB disabled — no gross edge (preregistered train/test, 37 variants)',replace('Opening Range Breakout is switched off in the stocks lane. It has no edge to fix.\n\nMEASUREMENT. The real engine was run over 5-minute bars for all nine watchlist\nnames, 2025-07-29 to 2026-09-22 (~286 sessions), split before any result was\nlooked at: TRAIN to 2026-04-30, TEST from 2026-05-01 held back for a single run.\nSeven mechanism-driven candidate families, 37 variants.\n\n  baseline TRAIN   1226 trades   -$1,321.50   -$6.96/day   CI [-10.84, -2.93]\n  baseline TEST     633 trades     -$507.95   -$5.35/day   CI [-12.39, +2.14]\n\nEvery variant lost on TRAIN. Stronger volume, narrower entry window, the whole\nstop x reward grid, long-only, short-only, releasing the one-trade-per-day token,\nand the crowded-bar filter: 37 of 37 negative.\n\nTHE DECISIVE TEST. With fees and slippage set to zero the strategy is\n-$0.09/trade on TRAIN (PF 0.977) and +$0.25/trade on TEST (PF 1.057) — both\nindistinguishable from zero. The signal carries no information. Everything it\nloses, it loses to cost, which is why every ''improvement'' above was really just\ntrading less and therefore paying less.\n\nTHE ONE THAT LOOKED REAL. A minimum stop width (cost-aware) improved net per\ntrade tenfold on TRAIN, -$1.08 -> -$0.13, monotonically from 0 to 60bps. Taken\nto TEST it was still negative (-$1.58/day), and the TRAIN argmax of 60bps came\nback WORSE than 40bps on TEST (-$2.27 vs -$1.58) — the overfit the protocol was\nwritten to catch. Nothing shipped.\n\nWHAT THIS IS NOT. It is not a verdict on opening-range breakout as a method.\nThe published work runs it across a broad universe of high-volatility movers;\nthis desk ran it on the nine largest names in the index, where an opening-range\nbreak is usually the index moving, not the stock. Re-running it on a volatile\nsmall/mid-cap universe is a new strategy needing its own forward evidence, and\nmust not be treated as a continuation of this one.\n\nALSO FIXED. trade_short sat in this row and was read by nothing — Strategy.__init__\ndrops any key with no matching Param. The config said ''no shorts'' while the\nstrategy shorted; AMZN was sold short on 2026-09-21 under that config. The knob\nis now a declared Param and is honoured.\n\nSTOCKS LANE AFTER THIS. ema_momentum (TEST +$2.79/day, CI [+1.04, +4.54], the\nonly stock strategy with a held-out lower bound above zero) and news_catalyst.\nvwap_reversion stays off: -$15.23/day TRAIN, -$13.90/day TEST.','\n',char(10)),'{"strategy": "orb", "decision": "disabled", "variants_tested": 37, "train": {"trades": 1226, "net": -1321.5, "per_day": -6.955, "ci": [-10.84, -2.93], "pf": 0.765}, "test": {"trades": 633, "net": -507.95, "per_day": -5.347, "ci": [-12.39, 2.14], "pf": 0.846}, "zero_cost_pf": {"train": 0.977, "test": 1.057}, "best_candidate": {"name": "min_stop_bps=40", "test_per_day": -1.582, "shipped": false}}','[]','2026-09-22 19:07:24.389255',1);
