INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(323,'alpaca:61835028','benzinga','2026-09-17 09:31:43','Hunter Biden’s LAPTOP Memecoin Crashes 99% Since Launch After Topping $50 Billion Market Cap — How It Compares With Official TRUMP Token in Debut Week','It&#39;s been a bloodbath for Hunter Biden&#39;s Laptop memecoin since its launch a week ago, far worse than that of President Donald Trump’s memecoin in its debut week.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61835028/hunter-biden-memecoin-laptop-comparison-donald-trump-launch-week','["BTC/USD", "TRUMP/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-17 10:16:36.652888','other','bearish',3,4,'days',1,'The significant drop in market cap indicates a severe lack of investor confidence.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 77563.640625, "TRUMP/USD": 1.937515}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.331}, "TRUMP/USD": {"60m": 0.257, "1d": 5.811}}','2026-09-18 10:20:23.831348','2026-09-17 10:16:28.647253','61835028',replace('It’s been a bloodbath for Hunter Biden’s Laptop (LAPTOP) memecoin since its launch a week ago, far worse than that of President Donald Trump’s memecoin in its debut week.\n\nThe Glitchy LAPTOP\n\nLAPTOP launched on Base, a Layer 2 blockchain developed by Coinbase Global Inc. (NASDAQ: COIN), at roughly $37, according to CoinMarketCap. Within minutes, it surged to a record high of $401.12, pushing its market cap to $50 billion.\n\nHowever, the frenzy was short-lived. \n\nAn hour later, LAPTOP crashed by 98%, with 80% of traders losing their money. On-chain data attributed the price collapse to insider distribution rather than ordinary selling.\n\nThe coin remains under heavy selling pressure and is down more than 99% in its first week.\n\nCryptocurrencyGains in First Week +/-Gains Since All-Time High +/-Price (Recorded at 3:00 a.m. EDT)Official Trump+2290%-97.4%$1.95Laptop               -99.56%-99.97%$0.1633\n\nWhat’s the TRUMP Story?\n\nThe Official Trump (CRYPTO: TRUMP) memecoin was launched in January 2025, days ahead of Trump’s swearing-in.\n\nThe coin started trading at $1.20, then surged to an all-time high of $75.35 within the next two days. Just like Hunter Biden’s LAPTOP memecoin, the pump quickly turned into a dump.\n\nTRUMP closed its first week at $28.89, netting a 2,290% return from the launch price. However, the decline from its peak has been severe, and the token has failed to reclaim lost ground.\n\nRead Also:\n\nDonald Trump Jr. Needed 2 Islands and Fireworks, Says Hunter Biden, as Lavish Bahamas Party Faces Scrutiny Over Putin-Linked Russian Oligarch\n\nBiden launched the memecoin, invoking the controversy surrounding his personal laptop recovered in 2020. He framed the memecoin as a symbol of resilience, redemption, and recovery.\n\nHe said that 20% of LAPTOP supply would be airdropped to wallets, including those that lost money on the TRUMP memecoin.\n\nRead Also:\n\nHunter Biden''s Memecoin Launch May Have ''Accidentally'' Helped Move the CLARITY Act Forward, Says Analyst: ''Now It Can''t Just Be About Trump''\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'aba56b043208aa11fe7b77eff9087e09a0de0fba','2026-09-17 09:31:43','2026-09-17 10:16:28.631357',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 09:31:43');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(324,'alpaca:61834976','benzinga','2026-09-17 09:28:30','Why Is Generac Stock Soaring On Thursday?','Generac issued Amazon warrants for up to 1.69 million shares at $200.9266 each, tied to a long-term data center generator supply agreement.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61834976/why-is-generac-stock-soaring-on-thursday','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-17 10:16:38.766716','partnership','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Generac''s stock is likely rising due to a significant supply agreement with Amazon.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 254.92}','{"AMZN": {"60m": -1.422}}','2026-09-18 10:20:23.831348','2026-09-17 10:16:28.649939','61834976',replace('Generac Holdings Inc. (NYSE:GNRC) shares are up about 33% during Thursday’s premarket session as investors react to a data-center supply agreement with Amazon.com, Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) disclosed on Wednesday.\n\nAmazon Data Center Generator Deal\n\nGenerac stated that it issued Amazon warrants to purchase up to 1.69 million Generac shares at around $200.93 per share.\n\nAs per the deal, Amazon’s wholly owned subsidiary, Amazon.com NV Investment Holdings LLC, received a warrant to purchase up to 1,693,745 shares of Generac common stock at $200.9266 per share.\n\nThis represents a potential investment of as much as $8 billion. Of the total warrant shares, 307,954 vested immediately, while the remaining shares will vest through multiple tranches based on aggregate gross payments, after certain offsets, made by Amazon and its affiliates to Generac and its global affiliates for backup power generators supplied to Amazon data centers.\n\nAt the time the warrant was issued, Generac and Amazon also entered into a long-term supply agreement, with initial generator deliveries expected to total $2.4 billion in 2027 and 2028.\n\nSubject to the applicable vesting requirements and other conditions under the Warrant and Transaction Agreement, Amazon may exercise the warrant, in whole or in part, through either a cash or cashless exercise on or before September 16, 2033.\n\nGNRC Earnings Preview And Analyst Price Targets\n\nLooking further out, the next major catalyst for the stock arrives with the October 28, 2026 (estimated) earnings report.\n\nEPS Estimate: $2.44 (Up from $1.83 YoY)\n\nRevenue Estimate: $1.33 Billion (Up from $1.11 Billion YoY)\n\nValuation: P/E of 40.3x (Indicates a premium valuation relative to peers)\n\nAnalyst Consensus & Recent Actions: The stock carries a Buy rating with an average price forecast of $289.71. Recent analyst moves include:\n\nUBS: Buy (Raises Target to $340.00) (August 4)\n\nStifel: Buy (Raises Target to $285.00) (July 30)\n\nCanaccord Genuity: Buy (Lowers Target to $275.00) (July 30)\n\nGNRC ETF Exposure And Passive Fund Flow Risk\n\nCorgi Battery Energy Storage Systems ETF (NASDAQ:WATS): 3.59% Weight\n\nMatrix Advisors Value ETF (NYSE:MAVF): 3.74% Weight\n\nSignificance: Because GNRC carries significant weight in these funds, any significant inflows or outflows for these ETFs will likely force automatic buying or selling of the stock.\n\nGNRC Stock Price Activity: Generac shares were up 33.06% at $233.01 during premarket trading on Thursday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBill Ackman Says Nike ‘Needs Help’ as Alexandre Arnault Joins Board: ‘Great Development’\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'0482c1df6ccd8bed6a9fd3b8b581749c4031e924','2026-09-17 09:28:30','2026-09-17 10:16:28.631357',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 09:28:31');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(325,'alpaca:61834920','benzinga','2026-09-17 09:19:39','Why Generac Shares Are Trading Higher By Around 35%; Here Are 20 Stocks Moving Premarket','Generac shares jumped 34.8% after an up-to-$8B Amazon data-center generator deal; other premarket movers included big gainers and losers.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61834920/why-generac-shares-are-trading-higher-by-around-35-here-are-20-stocks-moving-premarket','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-17 10:16:39.915788','mna','bullish',5,4,'hours',1,'A significant generator deal with Amazon likely boosts Generac''s revenue expectations.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 254.92}','{"AMZN": {"60m": -1.471}}','2026-09-18 09:20:06.917013','2026-09-17 10:16:28.652614','61834920',replace('Shares of Generac Holdings Inc (NYSE:GNRC) rose sharply in pre-market trading after the company announced a supply agreement with Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) for data center backup generators.\n\nGenerac and Amazon entered into a long-term supply agreement for up to $8 billion of backup power generators for Amazon data centers. Initial generator deliveries are expected to total $2.4 billion in 2027 and 2028.\n\nGenerac shares jumped 34.8% to $235.90 in pre-market trading.\n\nHere are some other stocks moving in pre-market trading.\n\nGainers\n\nCID HoldCo Inc (NASDAQ:DAIC) gained 116.6% to $4.35 in pre-market trading after the asset-tracking platform developer disclosed an acquisition of Envoy Technologies, Inc. and a debt restructuring.\n\nCheetah Net Supply Chain Service Inc (NASDAQ:CTNT) rose 117.5% to $0.091 in pre-market trading after dipping around 33% on Wednesday.\n\nKaixin Holdings (NASDAQ:KXIN) rose 92.1% to $2.17 in pre-market trading after the Chinese automotive retail platform and investment holding company reported a 602% increase in revenue for the first half of 2026.\n\nDigital Currency X Technology Inc (NASDAQ:DCX) gained 82.1% to $0.58 in pre-market trading after dipping 8% on Wednesday.\n\nReTo Eco-Solutions Inc (NASDAQ:RETO) rose 45.1% to $2.67 in pre-market trading after dipping 34% on Wednesday.\n\nLiberty Defense Holdings Ltd (NASDAQ:DETX) gained 27.5% to $2.84 in pre-market trading.\n\nVicor Corp (NASDAQ:VICR) rose 11.7% to $205.50 in pre-market trading after the company announced it granted a non-exclusive license to a new OEM licensee with the right to procure Vertical Power Delivery modules by its patents from unlicensed suppliers.\n\nGloo Holdings Inc (NASDAQ:GLOO) gained 13.4% to $4.61 in pre-market trading after jumping around 29% on Wednesday.\n\nHotel101 Global Holdings Corp (NASDAQ:HBNB) rose 9.4% to $5.62 in pre-market trading.\n\nLosers\n\nLongeveron Inc (NASDAQ:LGVN) tumbled 60% to $2.67 in pre-market trading after the company announced topline results from its Phase 2b ELPIS II clinical trial evaluating laromestrocel as a potential treatment for hypoplastic left heart syndrome.\n\nSynergy CHC Corp (NASDAQ:SNYR) fell 54% to $0.13 in pre-market trading after the company received Nasdaq delisting notice following Chapter 11 bankruptcy filing.\n\nDelixy Holdings Ltd (NASDAQ:DLXY) fell 31.1% to $1.58 in pre-market trading. Delixy Holdings shares skyrocketed 452% on Wednesday after the company disclosed a non-binding letter of intent for a potential transaction involving an oil and gas project in Kazakhstan.\n\nFluence Energy Inc (NASDAQ:FLNC) fell 19.5% to $7.28 in pre-market trading as the company cut its FY26 sales guidance below estimates. The company also named Bernerd Da Santos as chief operating officer.\n\nTreasure Global Inc (NASDAQ:TGL) fell 19.1% to $2.84 in pre-market trading. Treasure Global shares jumped 17% on Wednesday after the company announced its subsidiary Tadaa Technology secured a $52 million partnership to deploy EzyTrace for Malaysia’s Ministry of Agriculture and Food Security.\n\nQ/C Technologies Inc (NASDAQ:QCLS) declined 18.5% to $0.78 in pre-market trading after dipping 45% on Wednesday.\n\nGolden Sun Technology Group Ltd (NASDAQ:GSUN) fell 16% to $0.25 in pre-market trading after gaining 30% on Wednesday.\n\nUniverse Pharmaceuticals Inc (NASDAQ:UPC) fell 13.4% to $4.12 in pre-market trading after gaining around 7% on Wednesday.\n\nFreight Technologies Inc (NASDAQ:FRGT) fell 10.1% to $0.93 in pre-market trading after jumping 30% on Wednesday.\n\nRectitude Holdings Ltd (NASDAQ:RECT) fell 9.3% to $1.17 in pre-market trading.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'486a83d3cfb1484fa42f56bdd3c06b7fc1714c1e','2026-09-17 09:19:39','2026-09-17 10:16:28.631357',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 09:19:39');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(326,'alpaca:61837011','benzinga','2026-09-17 11:05:11','Nebius Reportedly Hikes GPU Prices Another 20%, Stock Jumps','Nebius stock rises over 9% on reports of a 20% GPU cloud price hike, highlighting tight AI computing capacity and booming demand.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61837011/nebius-reportedly-hikes-gpu-prices-another-20-stock-jumps','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 11:16:48.481550','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Stock rises on reports of increased GPU prices, indicating strong demand.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 217.54}','{"NVDA": {"60m": 0.863}}','2026-09-18 11:20:33.876043','2026-09-17 11:16:44.520652','61837011',replace('Nebius Group N.V. (NASDAQ:NBIS) stock rose over 9% in Thursday’s premarket trading following reports that the AI infrastructure company plans to raise prices across its GPU cloud services by about 20% as computing capacity remains tight.\n\nNasdaq futures are up 1.08%, while S&P; 500 futures have gained 0.84%.\n\nNebius Reportedly Raises GPU Cloud Prices 20%\n\nNebius is reportedly raising prices across its GPU cloud services, underscoring tight supplies of artificial intelligence computing capacity.\n\nThe new prices are set to take effect Oct. 1 and cover several NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) GPU models, including the H100, H200, B200 and B300, according to a WallstreetCN report carried by Futu.\n\nThe H100 hourly rate will reportedly rise 16.9% to $4.50 from $3.85. Meanwhile, the H200 rate will increase 20% to $5.40 from $4.50.\n\nNebius will also raise its B200 rate about 18.9% to $8.50 from $7.15. The B300 price will climb about 21% to $9.50 from $7.85.\n\nThis would mark Nebius’ second price increase in several months. In May, the company raised prices by an average of 29% for on-demand capacity and 51% for spot capacity.\n\nThe B300 rate has climbed about 56% from its pre-May level of roughly $6.10 per hour.\n\nHowever, Nebius had not publicly confirmed the latest price increase as of the report’s publication.\n\nAI Demand Stretches Into 2028\n\nThe report also cited an X user who said Nebius’ order visibility now extends beyond 24 months, up from about 18 months.\n\nSome customers have reportedly placed orders for the first and second quarters of 2028. Those contracts include deals covering tens of thousands of GPUs.\n\nThe reported price increases cover both older Hopper GPUs and newer Blackwell chips. That suggests strong demand extends across multiple generations of AI hardware.\n\nTight capacity could also give GPU infrastructure and data center providers greater pricing power as major cloud companies race to secure computing resources.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nTechnical Analysis\n\nNebius remains in a strong longer-term uptrend. At $228.50, the stock is 4.8% above its 20-day simple moving average of $217.52. It is also 7.7% above its 50-day SMA of $211.78 and 43% above its 200-day SMA of $159.47.\n\nThe moving averages remain in bullish alignment. The 20-day SMA is above the 50-day SMA, while the 50-day SMA remains well above the 200-day SMA.\n\nHowever, momentum is not overheated. The relative strength index stands at 46.92, signaling neutral momentum.\n\nTraders will be watching $230 as near-term resistance. Meanwhile, $195 remains an important support area if the stock reverses.\n\nAnalyst Outlook\n\nThe stock carries a Buy consensus rating and an average price forecast of $261.75.\n\nTruist Securities initiated coverage with a Buy rating and a $355 price forecast on Sept. 9. DA Davidson maintained a Neutral rating and raised its forecast to $250 on Aug. 18. Citigroup maintained a Buy rating and lifted its forecast to $324 on Aug. 14.\n\nBenzinga Edge Rankings\n\nThe Benzinga Edge scorecard highlights Nebius’ strong momentum but weak value profile.\n\nNebius has a Momentum score of 95.65, reflecting strong relative performance. However, its Value score is just 4.58, suggesting the stock screens as expensive on traditional valuation measures.\n\nThe setup remains heavily dependent on momentum and execution. That makes the $230 resistance level and $195 support area important markers for traders.\n\nTop ETF Exposure\n\nLeverage Shares 2X Long NBIS Daily ETF (NASDAQ:NBIG) has a 50.91% weighting in Nebius.\n\nGiven that concentration, flows into or out of the leveraged ETF can contribute to buying or selling pressure in Nebius shares.\n\nPrice Action\n\nNBIS Stock Price Activity: Nebius shares were up 9.14% at $228.51 in Thursday’s premarket session, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nCoreWeave or Nebius? Analyst Says the Risk-Reward Now Favors One AI Stock','\n',char(10)),'1974657fe0c402ef5f2171c3474214a2dfc29d28','2026-09-17 11:05:11','2026-09-17 11:16:44.516711',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 11:07:53');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(327,'alpaca:61836769','benzinga','2026-09-17 10:55:34','Trump’s Tariff Threat Over Fed Rate Decision ‘Makes No Economic Sense,’ Says Justin Wolfers: Kevin Warsh ''Called His Bluff’','Economist Justin Wolfers says Trump&#39;s tariff threats after a unanimous Fed rate hike &#39;makes no economic sense&#39; for domestic policy.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/economic-data/26/09/61836769/trumps-tariff-threat-over-fed-rate-decision-makes-no-economic-sense-says-justin-wolfers-kevin-warsh-called-his-bluff','["QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-17 11:16:50.077561','macro','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Economic commentary on Trump’s tariff threats and Fed decision.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 707.67, "SPY": 761.66}','{"QQQ": {"60m": 1.276}, "SPY": {"60m": 0.127}}','2026-09-18 11:20:33.876043','2026-09-17 11:16:44.523667','61836769',replace('Following the Federal Reserve’s decision to hike rates by 25 basis points, economist Justin Wolfers criticized President Donald Trump for threatening trade tariffs in response to central bank policy, stating the linkage “makes no economic sense.”\n\nPolicy Defiance\n\nWolfers highlighted the full consensus within the central bank as evidence that policy reflected economic data rather than political pressure.\n\n“Threatening tariffs on other countries because the Fed made a domestic rate decision makes no economic sense, and today’s vote made the point for me: 12 out of 12 FOMC members voted for this hike,” Wolfers stated.\n\nThreatening tariffs on other countries because the Fed made a domestic rate decision makes no economic sense, and today''s vote made the point for me: 12 out of 12 FOMC members voted for this hike. https://t.co/pFkzHcy1oX pic.twitter.com/JfXPs2dX29— Justin Wolfers (@JustinWolfers) September 17, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nElon Musk Once Said Psychedelics Could Help PTSD — Now FDA Holds Hearing as Optimi Health Advances MDMA Trial\n\nTariff Threat Reaction\n\nPrior to the meeting, President Trump posted demands for rates at 1% or less, threatening to stop trade with deficit nations if rates remained high. Wolfers dismissed the ultimatum, observing that trade deficits and domestic borrowing costs operate on unrelated economic principles.\n\nSource: Truth Social\n\n“The president was essentially threatening to do something really bizarre unless the Fed did what he wanted,” Wolfers noted, stating Chair Warsh “called his bluff.”\n\nWolfers concluded that “the only person who thinks rates should be lower is the White House, and I suspect that says more about politics than about the state of the economy.”\n\nHowever, after the Fed announced its decision, Trump told reporters that he asked Warsh to “vote with the board.”\n\n"Wait, did he really just say what I think he said?": @ErinBurnett’s stunned reaction after Trump claims he told Fed Chair Kevin Warsh to "go ahead and vote" to raise interest rates after months of pushing to lower rates. pic.twitter.com/Ll4Lp7CODn— Erin Burnett OutFront (@OutFrontCNN) September 17, 2026 \n\nUnanimous Rate Hike\n\nThe Federal Reserve raised the target federal funds rate by 0.25 percentage point to a range of 3.75% to 4.00%. All 12 voting members of the Federal Open Market Committee supported the increase.\n\nThe quarter-point increase represents the Federal Reserve’s first rate hike since 2023. Newly appointed Chair Kevin Warsh joined every voting member—including committee officials appointed by former Presidents Barack Obama, Joe Biden, and Donald Trump—in approving the policy move. The decision came despite explicit demands from the White House to slash interest rates to lower levels.\n\nThe CME Group’s FedWatch tool projections show markets pricing in a 54.2% likelihood of the Federal Reserve hiking interest rates after its October meeting. \n\nHow Have Stock Markets Performed in 2026?\n\nThe S&P; 500 index has advanced 10.32% year-to-date. Similarly, the Nasdaq Composite index is up 11.77%, and the Dow Jones gained 7.07% YTD.\n\nOn Wednesday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed mixed. SPY fell 0.44% to $754.05, while QQQ rose 0.026% to $704.72. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), also ended 1.15% lower at $515.22.\n\nIn premarket on Thursday, SPY was up 0.84%, QQQ gained 1.05% and DIA advanced 0.77%.\n\nRead Also:\n\n''Stickier Inflation'' Is Here, Market Strategist Warns After August CPI — ''One-Time Event'' Narrative Takes a Hit\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'89e2b4da4b58dd812cc1522a76795cae1b535f2c','2026-09-17 10:55:34','2026-09-17 11:16:44.516711',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 10:55:34');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(328,'alpaca:61836594','benzinga','2026-09-17 10:45:24','Why Is Snap Stock Trading Higher on Thursday?','Snap SPECS partnerships with Salesforce, AWS and Nvidia expand workplace AI use cases as SNAP shares rise in premarket trading.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61836594/why-is-snap-stock-trading-higher-on-thursday','["AMZN", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 11:16:51.366785','partnership','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Partnerships with major companies suggest growth potential for Snap.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 254.92, "NVDA": 217.54}','{"AMZN": {"60m": -1.518}, "NVDA": {"60m": 0.8}}','2026-09-18 11:20:33.876043','2026-09-17 11:16:44.526304','61836594',replace('Snap Inc. (NYSE:SNAP) shares rose about 3% in Thursday premarket trading after new enterprise partnerships expanded the use cases for its SPECS augmented reality glasses.\n\nThe stock also benefited from a risk-on backdrop, with S&P; 500 futures up about 0.9%.\n\nSNAP had gained more than 4% in after-hours trading on Wednesday.\n\nSalesforce, AWS And Nvidia Expand SPECS Push\n\nSnap announced partnerships with Salesforce Inc. (NYSE:CRM), Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) and Amazon.com Inc.’s (NASDAQ:AMZN) Amazon Web Services.\n\nThe partnerships bring AI and computing capabilities to SPECS for field service, remote support and retail applications.\n\nSalesforce’s Agentforce AI can help workers identify objects, create cases, retrieve information and update workflows. AWS is bringing workplace assistant Amazon Quick to SPECS, while Nvidia’s XR technology supports real-time guidance.\n\nSnap did not disclose financial terms.\n\nThe agreements expand the SPECS story beyond consumer AR by connecting the glasses to workplace applications. Advertising, however, remains Snap’s primary revenue source.\n\nThe partnerships also come around Snap’s SPECS hardware showcase in Los Angeles, where CEO Evan Spiegel is highlighting AI assistance, workplace tools, and shared experiences.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nEU Regulation Remains A Risk\n\nSnap’s advertising business could face additional pressure in Europe from a proposed "EU Kids Act."\n\nThe framework would reportedly restrict children under 15 from independently accessing social media and require age verification.\n\nUsers aged 13 and 14 could access platforms only through parent-created accounts with additional controls.\n\nStricter rules could affect engagement and advertising while Snap develops SPECS as an additional growth opportunity.\n\nSNAP Technicals Improve As Stock Approach $6\n\nShares were 6.8% above the 20-day simple moving average, 14.5% above the 50-day SMA, and 2.2% above the 200-day SMA.\n\nMACD is above its signal line with a positive histogram, indicating improving momentum.\n\nThe broader setup remains mixed, with the 50-day SMA still below the 200-day average. Key resistance is near $6.00.\n\nEarnings And Analyst Outlook\n\nSnap’s next estimated earnings report is scheduled for Nov. 4, 2026.\n\nAnalysts expect earnings of 4 cents per share, versus a loss of 6 cents a year earlier, on revenue of $1.73 billion, up from $1.51 billion.\n\nSNAP carries a Hold consensus rating with an average analyst price forecast of $7.32.\n\nSNAP Price Action: Snap shares were up 2.97% at $5.89 during premarket trading on Thursday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNetflix Content Chief Shrugs Off YouTube Threat: ‘Young People Only Watch Short Things’ Isn’t True\n\nPhoto Courtesy: BigTunaOnline via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'a0722968c198165b7a72eb498f566fb309e72173','2026-09-17 10:45:24','2026-09-17 11:16:44.516711',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 10:45:24');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(329,'alpaca:61836154','benzinga','2026-09-17 10:26:55','Elon Musk’s Tesla And SpaceX Sue Nanotech Firm TERA-Print Over ‘Terafab’ Name For Planned $16.8 Billion Texas AI Chip Factory','Tesla and SpaceX sued TERA-print over the Terafab name for their planned $16.8 billion Texas AI-chip complex, denying trademark confusion.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61836154/elon-musks-tesla-and-spacex-sue-nanotech-firm-tera-print-over-terafab-name-for-planned-16-8-billion-texas-ai-chip-factory','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 11:16:52.522170','legal','neutral',3,4,'days',1,'The lawsuit is a notable legal action involving Tesla and SpaceX.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 356.12}','{"TSLA": {"60m": 3.266}}','2026-09-18 11:20:33.876043','2026-09-17 11:16:44.529104','61836154',replace('Elon Musk’s Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) and Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) have sued Illinois nanotechnology company TERA-print LLC over the "Terafab" name planned for their $16.8 billion AI chip complex in Texas.\n\nMusk Companies Challenge TERA-Print Trademark Claim\n\nAccording to Reuters, Tesla and SpaceX filed the lawsuit on Tuesday in federal court in Austin, asking a judge to declare that their use of Terafab does not infringe TERA-print’s "Tera-Fab" trademark. The complaint says TERA-print sent a cease-and-desist letter after Tesla filed three Terafab trademark applications with the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office in May.\n\nTERA-print’s registered Tera-Fab mark covers a desktop photolithography system used in bioengineering and related applications. The company threatened litigation in June, arguing Musk’s companies could create consumer confusion. USPTO records show TERA-print owns a federal registration for TERA-FAB.\n\nTesla and SpaceX reject that argument. "No reasonable consumer is likely to believe" their chip plant is affiliated with TERA-print’s desktop lithography products, they said, arguing the companies serve different customers and technologies.\n\nRead Also:\n\nIntel Analyst Raises Price Target On Terafab, AI-Driven Turnaround\n\nTERA-Print Vows To Defend Its Rights\n\nTERA-print, meanwhile, said it discussed a settlement with Tesla as recently as Sept. 2. "Having been misled by Tesla’s professed interest in settling this matter, TERA-print will now vigorously defend its rights," the company said. \n\nTesla did not immediately respond to Benzinga’ request for comment.\n\nTerafab Project Scales Musk’s Chip Ambitions\n\nThe dispute lands as Musk pushes ahead with one of his largest manufacturing bets. Tesla and SpaceX confirmed Grimes County as Terafab’s home in August. Reuters reported at the time that the companies plan an initial $16.8 billion investment in the 100-million-square-foot complex, which will make, package and test advanced logic and memory chips under one roof.\n\nThe plant will supply chips for Tesla’s Optimus robots and Cybercabs and SpaceX’s proposed space-based data centers. Musk has previously estimated that about 75% of Terafab’s AI-compute output could go toward "AI spacecraft," compared with roughly 25% for Tesla’s Optimus robots, though he described the split as a "very approximate guess.\n\nSpaceX says Terafab will employ at least 3,000 people, while filings indicate future phases could push investment as high as $119 billion. Musk has called the facility essential for producing AI chips "at scale for use on Earth and in space."\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang Says Elon Musk’s Terafab May Look Audacious, But ‘If Anybody Could Do It, He Can’\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'a357eda996e64693fc3b3e398e1e597731670081','2026-09-17 10:26:55','2026-09-17 11:16:44.516711',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 10:26:55');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(330,'alpaca:61839005','benzinga','2026-09-17 12:07:25','Bitcoin, Ethereum ETFs Lose $1.11 Billion Over 2 Days: What''s Going On?','Bitcoin and Ethereum ETFs shed $1.11 billion after the Clarity Act failed and the Fed delivered its first rate hike since 2023.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61839005/bitcoin-ethereum-etfs-lose-1-11-billion-over-2-days-whats-going-on','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-17 12:16:59.900080','macro','bearish',4,5,'days',1,'Major market events like rate hikes and regulatory failures significantly impacted ETF values.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 77563.640625, "ETH/USD": 2414.179931640625, "SPY": 761.66}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.373}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 1.512}, "SPY": {"60m": 0.148}}','2026-09-18 12:20:44.771625','2026-09-17 12:16:56.475816','61839005',replace('U.S. spot Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) and Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) ETFs bled a combined $1.11 billion over two days after the CLARITY Act procedural vote failed and the Fed hiked rates for the first time in three years.\n\nWhat the ETF Data Shows\n\nBitcoin ETFs lost $295.98 million on Sept. 16, adding to the $450.33 million exit the day before for a two-day total of $746.31 million. The breakdown by fund:\n\nFundTickerOutflowBlackRock IBIT(NASDAQ:IBIT)$144.11 millionArk Invest ARKB(NYSE:ARKB)$84.40 millionFidelity FBTC(NASDAQ:FBTC)$52.72 millionSource: SoSoValue\n\nEthereum ETFs deteriorated further, with outflows jumping from $141.47 million on Sept. 15 to $224.11 million on Sept. 16, the largest single-day Ethereum ETF outflow since January 30, 2026. \n\nThe two-day total hit $365.58 million, with BlackRock’s ETHA (NASDAQ:ETHA) leading at $110.03 million and Fidelity’s FETH (NASDAQ:FETH) shedding $55.58 million.\n\nFed Delivers First Rate Hike Since 2023\n\nThe Block reported Wednesday that the FOMC voted 12-0 to raise the federal funds rate by 25 basis points to a 3.75% to 4% target range, the first hike since July 2023. \n\nChair Kevin Warsh was hawkish in his opening remarks, saying financial conditions are not restrictive. \n\n“I would be hard-pressed to describe broad financial conditions as restrictive,” Warsh said. “So we removed a dose of accommodation.” he added.\n\nSixteen of 18 policymakers project at least one additional quarter-point hike this year, with the Fed’s latest projections pointing to rates holding at 4.1% through end-2027.\n\nAnalysts Warn of Policy Overshoot Risk\n\nBitget analyst Lewis Huang told The Block that Bitcoin could absorb more of the immediate shock than equities, noting BTC moved roughly four times as much as the S&P; 500 (NYSE:SPY) on the prior two FOMC trading days. \n\nHe flagged a key risk: the Fed could still be tightening after the energy price impulse from the Iran conflict begins to fade, creating a policy overshoot scenario. \n\nGasoline prices rose nearly 4% in a month while diesel climbed 60% to an all-time high.\n\nWhere Bitcoin and Ethereum Stand Technically\n\nBTC holds at $76,647 Thursday, range-bound between $75,000 and $82,000 with a Supertrend sell signal capping upside at $78,582. \n\nETH holds at $2,444, testing the Supertrend flip level at $2,442 after a sharp rejection from $2,580.\n\nKey levels for BTC and ETH:\n\nBTC: $78,582 resistance, $75,000 range floor\n\nETH: $2,526 resistance, $2,360 range floor\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nEthereum Is ''the Big Daddy'' but Raoul Pal''s Biggest Bet Is Elsewhere','\n',char(10)),'b866c6fc488b9f74c708f13ecb24382de0542430','2026-09-17 12:07:25','2026-09-17 12:16:56.470573',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 12:07:25');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(331,'alpaca:61838516','benzinga','2026-09-17 11:58:36','What''s Going On With AMD Stock Thursday?','AMD rises 2.66% premarket. Bullish AI outlooks and strong technical momentum push shares toward key $530 resistance.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61838516/whats-going-on-with-amd-stock-thursday-10','["AMD"]','stocks','2026-09-17 12:17:01.404999','other','bullish',2,3,'minutes',1,'The stock rises in premarket due to positive sentiments and outlooks.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 459.75}','{"AMD": {"60m": 18.299}}','2026-09-18 12:20:44.771625','2026-09-17 12:16:56.479173','61838516',replace('Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) stock rose nearly 3% in Thursday premarket trading as risk appetite improved alongside U.S. stock futures.Nasdaq futures gained 1.05%, while S&P; 500 futures rose 0.80%.AMD’s early move appears tied to broader strength in growth and technology stocks. Traders are leaning into upside momentum ahead of the opening bell.However, AMD is already well above several long-term trend indicators. As a result, traders will watch whether buyers can push through nearby resistance or whether the rally loses steam.Piper Sandler: AI Market Is ‘Starving For Compute’Recent analyst optimism also supports sentiment. Piper Sandler initiated coverage of AMD with an Overweight rating and a $600 price forecast on Sept. 10. The firm cited accelerating AI compute demand and AMD’s growing position in server CPUs and GPUs.Piper Sandler said the AI market is “starving for more compute capacity,” with 2027 capacity already sold out and order books filling for 2028.The analysts estimate the global compute market could reach $2.2 trillion by 2030, driven largely by AI accelerators. They expect that expansion to support strong revenue and earnings growth across major semiconductor suppliers.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nTechnical AnalysisAMD remains in a strong long-term uptrend. The stock is about 49.7% above its 200-day simple moving average of $351.29.It is also 6.3% above its 50-day SMA of $495.03. That keeps the intermediate trend positive, although the stock could face pullback risk if momentum fades.The short-term picture is more mixed. The 20-day SMA remains below the 50-day SMA, signaling that the shorter-term trend has yet to fully strengthen.Still, AMD is trading 9.1% above its 20-day SMA of $482.30.Momentum is also improving. The MACD is above its signal line, while the histogram is positive. That suggests buyers are regaining momentum following the previous downswing.AMD is trading near the upper end of its 52-week range of $149.85 to $584.73. A move above $530 could put the 52-week high back in focus. Meanwhile, the $463 area represents an important support zone if shares retreat.Analyst OutlookAMD trades at a price-to-earnings ratio of about 130.7, reflecting a premium valuation. The stock carries a Buy consensus rating with an average price forecast of $604.Piper Sandler initiated coverage with an Overweight rating and a $600 price forecast on Sept. 10. Raymond James upgraded AMD to Strong Buy and raised its price forecast to $641 on Aug. 25. BMO Capital initiated coverage with an Outperform rating and a $550 price forecast on Aug. 21.Benzinga Edge RankingsThe Benzinga Edge scorecard shows AMD scoring strongly on momentum, quality and growth.AMD has a momentum score of 98.93, a quality score of 94.21 and a growth score of 95.58. However, its value score is just 3.85.The combination highlights AMD’s strong growth and momentum profile while also pointing to elevated valuation risk. That could leave the stock more sensitive to weaker growth expectations or guidance.Top ETF ExposureThe iShares Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SOXX) has an 8.22% weighting in AMD. The First Trust Nasdaq Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:FTXL) has a 6.55% weighting, while the Pacer Data and Digital Revolution ETF (NYSE:TRFK) has a 6.52% weighting.AMD’s sizable weight in these funds means ETF inflows and outflows can contribute to buying or selling pressure in the stock.Price ActionAMD Stock Price Activity: Advanced Micro Devices shares were up 2.66% at $526.12 during Thursday’s premarket session, according to Benzinga Pro data.Image via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nElon Musk Says SPCX''s Starship Could Deliver Up to 10 Million Tons to Orbit Every Year','\n',char(10)),'cb6f05659b37a080e2fa3a5a17059590cd15fb86','2026-09-17 11:58:36','2026-09-17 12:16:56.470573',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 11:58:36');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(332,'alpaca:61838347','benzinga','2026-09-17 11:53:53','Humanoid Robots Are Getting Smarter and Capable — But Researchers Mull If Their ‘ChatGPT Moment’ Is Here?','Citrini examines humanoid robotics progress in autonomy, hardware, real-world applications and the path toward commercialization.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61838347/humanoid-robots-are-getting-smarter-and-capable-but-researchers-mull-if-their-chatgpt-moment-is-here','["NVDA", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 12:17:02.656664','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The article discusses advancements in humanoid robotics but does not provide concrete impacts on prices.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 217.54, "TSLA": 356.12}','{"NVDA": {"60m": 0.837}, "TSLA": {"60m": 2.925}}','2026-09-18 12:20:44.771625','2026-09-17 12:16:56.482102','61838347',replace('Humanoid robots are showing meaningful progress beyond controlled demonstrations, with advances in autonomy, dexterity, and the ability to perform repetitive real-world tasks. But widespread commercial deployment still remains a work in progress.\n\nAfter spending a week meeting with leading robotics labs, engineers and investors across the San Francisco Bay Area, researchers found that most humanoid robots remain in development, training, and tele-operated demonstrations. Where real-world deployments exist, they are generally closer to pilots than clear return-on-investment opportunities, according to a report published Wednesday by Citrini Research.\n\nThe Robotics Test\n\nThe report examined whether robotics is approaching its own "ChatGPT moment," a point at which the technology becomes broadly recognized as useful and disruptive. It highlighted recent advances from GeneralistAI and Skild AI, along with Figure AI’s demonstration involving 250,000 packages, as examples of progress across learning, dexterous manipulation, locomotion and real-world automation.\n\nRather than one defining breakthrough, the report suggested robotics may advance through a "mosaic of signals," with improvements in hardware, training and autonomy gradually pushing the technology toward broader commercial use.\n\nThe report said basic humanoid locomotion is effectively a solved problem, while complex dexterity remains more difficult. Simple repetitive tasks are already trainable, creating opportunities for near-term automation as robotic models continue to improve.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMortgage Applications Hit ‘Lowest Since 1995,’ Says Reventure CEO; Nearly $2,800 Monthly Payments Weigh on Buyers\n\nBuilding The Ecosystem\n\nThe progress is also being matched by investment in the broader robotics infrastructure. Tesla Inc (NASDAQ:TSLA) has been preparing production lines for Optimus, while XPeng Inc (NYSE:XPEV) has launched an automated production line for its IRON humanoid robot.\n\nMeanwhile, NVIDIA Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) is supporting the computing side of physical AI. Figure AI is securing access to up to 100,000 Vera Rubin GPUs to train the models powering its humanoid robots.\n\nThe report concluded that robotic autonomy is developing along a curve rather than arriving through one decisive breakthrough, with “broad generalizability” remaining the longer-term goal.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nElon Musk’s Tesla And SpaceX Sue Nanotech Firm TERA-Print Over ‘Terafab’ Name For Planned $16.8 Billion Texas AI Chip Factory\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'d0c1f6bfbb931d46d1b33956efc374d5ecd09899','2026-09-17 11:53:53','2026-09-17 12:16:56.470573',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 11:53:53');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(333,'alpaca:61838083','benzinga','2026-09-17 11:41:51','Nokia Earns Jim Cramer''s Praise: ‘I Think It’s A Terrific Situation’','Cramer recommends Nokia and Seanergy Maritime, calls BWX too expensive, urges caution on Hub Group, and advises selling NextEra Energy.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/09/61838083/jim-cramer-recommends-buying-nokia-terrific-situation','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 12:17:04.252350','analyst','bullish',2,3,'days',1,'Analyst''s positive commentary could boost investor interest.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 217.54}','{"NVDA": {"60m": 0.86}}','2026-09-18 12:20:44.771625','2026-09-17 12:16:56.485240','61838083',replace('On CNBC’s “Mad Money Lightning Round,” Jim Cramer said he likes Nokia Oyj (NYSE:NOK) and recommended buying the same. “I’m glad you brought it to our attention. I think it’s a terrific situation,” he added.\n\nThe company will combine its Nokia Data Suite with Microsoft Fabric to help telecom providers access and integrate data faster for agentic AI applications. The system is designed to cut data-access times from weeks to minutes and enable AI to analyze data and perform some network operations, including improving coverage quality.\n\nNokia’s stock price jumped in pre-market trading on Thursday to about $10.61 per share at last check. That brings its 2026 gain to nearly 70%.\n\nWhen asked about BWX Technologies, Inc. (NYSE:BWXT), he said, “The price-to-earnings multiple at 30 times is too high. I think it’s a great company. I mean, really terrific, but it’s too expensive.”\n\nGuggenheim analyst Michael Ciarmoli initiated coverage on BWX Technologies on Tuesday with a Buy rating and a price target of $192.\n\nCramer said Seanergy Maritime Holdings Corp (NASDAQ:SHIP) is a buy. “Bulk transportation is on fire. I think it’s a terrific situation. It’s not an expensive stock, and I think the yield is safe,” he added.\n\nLending support to his choice, Seanergy Maritime reported better-than-expected second-quarter financial results on July 30.\n\n“That’s a tough one,” Cramer said when asked about Hub Group, Inc. (NASDAQ:HUBG). “It’s going to be rough for a little bit. Wait until oil calms down.”\n\nHub Group shares traded lower Wednesday afternoon after a short report published by J Capital Research. The report cited compounding operational and accounting risks at the logistics provider.\n\nNextEra Energy, Inc. (NYSE:NEE) is not a good stock to own, Cramer said. “Take the money and run.”\n\nNextEra Energy, on Monday, affirmed FY2026 adjusted earnings guidance of $3.92 to $4.02 per share.\n\nPrice Action\n\nNokia shares gained 3.1% to settle at $10.14 on Wednesday.\n\nSeanergy Maritime shares fell 1.2% to close at $18.28 during the session.\n\nHub Group declined 1% to settle at $33.12 on Wednesday.\n\nBWX Technologies shares fell 0.7% to close at $145.66.\n\nNextEra Energy shares declined 0.9% to settle at $80.37 on Wednesday.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'4c8d8d29783869373c6fd0dead3e3d8b5b4dd4ba','2026-09-17 11:41:51','2026-09-17 12:16:56.470573',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 11:41:51');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(334,'alpaca:61837528','benzinga','2026-09-17 11:21:49','Bernie Sanders Slams AI CEOs Over Political Spending: ''You Should Not be Spending Money Trying to Defeat'' AI Regulation','Bernie Sanders criticized AI CEOs for spending hundreds of millions through super PACs to oppose lawmakers seeking stronger AI regulation.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61837528/bernie-sanders-calls-out-ai-ceos-over-hundreds-of-millions-in-super-pac-spending','["AMD", "META", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 12:17:05.203496','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Political criticisms may influence public perception but do not directly affect asset prices.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 459.75, "META": 578.53, "NVDA": 217.54}','{"AMD": {"60m": 18.745}, "META": {"60m": 17.166}, "NVDA": {"60m": 0.965}}','2026-09-18 12:20:44.771625','2026-09-17 12:16:56.488173','61837528',replace('Sen. Bernie Sanders (I-Vt.) criticized AI industry leaders over their political spending, arguing that warnings about AI risks should be matched by support for lawmakers seeking stronger regulation.\n\nSanders Targets AI Super PAC Spending\n\nOn Wednesday, in a post on X, Sanders said, "If AI CEOs seriously believe that AI is a real danger, they should not be spending hundreds of millions of dollars through their super PACs to defeat candidates and members of Congress who want to regulate it."\n\nIn the CNN interview, Sanders said the AI industry was controlled by a few rich people, naming some including Larry Ellison, Jeff Bezos and Elon Musk. "We have an industry of extraordinary importance, the AI industry, which is controlled by a handful of the richest people in the world," Sanders added.\n\nSanders Calls For AI Regulation\n\nSanders argued that AI executives have only recently begun addressing the potential implications of the technology and criticized their political spending.\n\n"They are contributing hundreds of millions of dollars through their super PACs to prevent, I think, Congress from doing the right thing," Sanders said.\n\nSanders argued that AI executives should align their political actions with their warnings about the technology.\n\n"If they’re going to be honest about it and if they’re telling the American people that this is a real danger, then you should not be spending money trying to defeat candidates and members of Congress who want to do something about it," Sanders noted.\n\nIf AI CEOs seriously believe that AI is a real danger, they should not be spending hundreds of millions of dollars through their super PACs to defeat candidates and members of Congress who want to regulate it. pic.twitter.com/cLFe9VAP1P— Bernie Sanders (@BernieSanders) September 16, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nElizabeth Warren Wants Lawmakers to Decide Future of AI, Gets Told by Anthony Pompliano: Time to ''Press Pause'' on Politicians Interfering in the Free Market\n\nTrump Appointed Tech Executives to AI Council\n\nIn March, President Donald Trump appointed 13 technology executives to a presidential council advising the White House on AI policy, export controls and science strategy. \n\nThe council included executives from Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA), Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META), Oracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL), Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD), Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOGL) and Dell Technologies Inc. (NYSE:DELL), along with venture capitalist Marc Andreessen.\n\nSeveral members or their companies had also contributed to Trump-aligned political efforts. The council’s composition also drew attention for its focus on industry leaders rather than AI safety researchers, academics, or civil society representatives.\n\nAI Power and Political Influence\n\nLast month, Musk reportedly planned to spend $100 million to $120 million through America PAC to support Republican candidates in the 2026 midterm elections, after donating nearly $250 million to Donald Trump’s 2024 campaign.\n\nEarlier this year, Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei warned that AI power and wealth were becoming concentrated among a small group of companies, raising concerns about their growing economic and political influence.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSam Altman Says He Wants Money Out Of Politics, Pushes Back On OpenAI Lobbying Criticism: ''Love To See The Rules Across The Board Change''\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'4bf6c65b75670cd2eefa9999d0aede5ca70c7e5e','2026-09-17 11:21:49','2026-09-17 12:16:56.470573',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 11:21:49');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(335,'alpaca:61840880','benzinga','2026-09-17 12:59:33','XRP ETF Inflows Beat Bitcoin, Ethereum Again: What Is Going On?','XRP ETFs attract $3.5 million with zero outflows as Bitcoin and Ethereum funds lose $1.11 billion and XRP tests key support.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61840880/xrp-etf-inflows-beat-bitcoin-ethereum-again-what-is-going-on','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD", "XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-17 13:17:13.424366','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'XRP ETF inflows are notable but do not guarantee price movement.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 77563.640625, "ETH/USD": 2414.179931640625, "XRP/USD": 1.3027}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.326}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 1.358}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": -0.606, "1d": 1.417}}','2026-09-18 13:20:58.044767','2026-09-17 13:17:09.556457','61840880',replace('XRP (CRYPTO: XRP) spot ETFs pulled in $3.50 million over two days with zero outflows while Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) and Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) funds bled $1.11 billion combined.\n\nWhat the ETF Flows Show\n\nFranklin Templeton’s XRPZ (NYSE:XRPZ) drove the entire Sept. 16 inflow, adding 2.71 million XRP worth $3.50 million according to SoSoValue.\n\nCumulative XRP ETF inflows now stand at $1.72 billion with total net assets at $1.40 billion.\n\nThe divergence is hard to ignore: institutional money kept flowing into XRP even as the CLARITY Act failed to pass a procedural vote and the Fed’s first rate hike in three years triggered a broad retreat from crypto funds.\n\nWhat Polymarket Traders Are Pricing\n\nPolymarket odds for XRP price targets in September currently sit at:\n\nPrice TargetOddsRise to $1.4056%Fall to $1.2051%Rise to $1.6016%Fall to $1.0010%Source: Polymarket\n\nThat near-tie is not a coincidence. It mirrors exactly what the chart is showing: a market that broke out hard from $1.00 in late August, ran into resistance, and is now cooling with no clear directional conviction.\n\nWhy the Ripple-Stripe Integration Matters for XRP\n\nCoinDesk reported Thursday that Ripple updated its XRP Ledger AI Starter Kit to support the Machine Payments Protocol, a standard co-authored by Stripe and Tempo that lets AI agents pay for services automatically using XRP and RLUSD.\n\nThe update also adds the Open Wallet Standard, allowing software to manage wallets across multiple blockchains through one interface.\n\n“XRP and RLUSD are first-class options wherever developers are building,” RippleX head of product Jazzi Cooper posted on X. \n\nRipple now backs both MPP and x402, the web payments standard it added in June, giving developers on either standard a path to accept payments on the XRP Ledger.\n\nXRP Price Analysis: Key Levels to Watch\n\nXRP is trading flat Thursday, pulling back sharply after rejecting the $1.30 to $1.32 zone that held as support through most of September. \n\nPrice now tests the $1.26 to $1.28 support band that first launched the late August breakout from $1. \n\nRSI at 46.29 sits at its weakest reading since before the breakout, with the 20-day EMA at $1.3447 now acting as resistance overhead rather than support below.\n\nThe setup is straightforward: holding the support band keeps the recovery structure intact and gives $1.40 a realistic path. Losing it opens the door toward $1.20.\n\nKey levels for XRP:\n\n$1.40 — psychological resistance\n\n$1.34 — 20-day EMA, now resistance\n\n$1.25 to $1.28 — critical support band, must hold\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Made a Golden Cross—And Could Drop Below $75,000 Next, Analyst Says','\n',char(10)),'6bdc868e0ed9cd65c77097994b3f7b343232db7c','2026-09-17 12:59:33','2026-09-17 13:17:09.552337',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 12:59:33');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(336,'alpaca:61840411','benzinga','2026-09-17 12:40:43','Nokia Stock Jumps as Microsoft Deal Deepens Its AI Network Push','Nokia AI Momentum builds as Microsoft expansion, AI-RAN trials and 800G rollout support Thursday’s stock gain.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61840411/nokia-stock-jumps-as-microsoft-deal-deepens-its-ai-network-push','["MSFT", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 13:17:14.646396','partnership','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Nokia''s partnership with Microsoft is positively influencing its stock due to increased AI focus.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 501.15, "NVDA": 217.54}','{"MSFT": {"60m": -0.811}, "NVDA": {"60m": 0.878}}','2026-09-18 13:20:58.044767','2026-09-17 13:17:09.561407','61840411',replace('Nokia Corporation (NYSE:NOK) shares rose nearly 5% in Thursday premarket trading after the company expanded its Microsoft partnership around AI-driven network automation.\n\nThe move came against a risk-on backdrop, with S&P; 500 futures up 0.8%. Nokia shares have gained nearly 70% in 2026.\n\nMicrosoft Deal Extends Nokia’s AI Push\n\nNokia said it is extending its partnership with Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT) to create an "agentic, unified data foundation" combining Nokia Data Suite with Microsoft Fabric.\n\nThe platform aims to give telecom operators trusted network data "in minutes instead of weeks" and accelerate AI-driven automation.\n\nInitial use cases include autonomous VoNR assurance and "geo-experience," which combines subscriber, network and radio-frequency data.\n\nThe development builds on Nokia’s AI-RAN strategy. Eight operators are advancing trials, while the platform has demonstrated more than 20% spectral-efficiency gains. Further software improvements are planned for 2027 and 2028.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia’s AI Is Moving Into Cell Towers—and Nokia Is Already Testing It\n\nAI-RAN, Optical Networks Add Catalysts\n\nNokia is running AI-RAN trials across Europe, Asia-Pacific and the Middle East as Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) pushes AI deeper into radio networks.\n\nSeparately, Nokia will deploy ICE-X 800G ZR/ZR+ coherent pluggable optics with Telxius across networks in Europe, the U.S. and Latin America.\n\nThe 800G rollout includes automation for network provisioning, fault monitoring and performance management.\n\nNOK Technical Setup\n\nNokia’s 20-day SMA of $10.23 remains above its 50-day SMA of $10.21, while the 50-day average is above the 200-day SMA of $9.76.\n\nAt $10.61, shares were 3.8% above the 20-day SMA and about 4% above the 50-day average.\n\nThe stock remains 11.7% below its 100-day SMA of $12.02. RSI stands at 48.62, indicating neutral momentum.\n\nThe $10.50 area is being tested in premarket trading, while support sits near $9.50.\n\nEarnings, Analysts In Focus\n\nNokia is scheduled to report earnings Oct. 22. Analysts expect EPS of 8 cents, up from 7 cents a year earlier, on revenue of $5.81 billion versus $5.64 billion.\n\nThe stock carries a Buy consensus rating with an average price forecast of $17.\n\nRosenblatt recently initiated coverage with Buy and a $15 target. JPMorgan has an Overweight rating and $21 target, while Argus Research rates Nokia Buy with a $15 target.\n\nNOK Stock Price Activity: Nokia shares were up 5.62% to $10.71 in Thursday premarket trading, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNokia Earns Jim Cramer''s Praise: ‘I Think It’s A Terrific Situation’\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'dc1c9209a1a5348b642ebee03c0d8a72e014e131','2026-09-17 12:40:43','2026-09-17 13:17:09.552337',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 12:40:43');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(337,'alpaca:61840070','benzinga','2026-09-17 12:33:51','Wall Street’s Biggest Bull Cuts His S&P 500 Target: The Problem Isn’t Corporate Profits','Yardeni cut his S&amp;P 500 target without lowering earnings estimates. The Fed’s rate hike shows why strong growth can complicate stock valuations.','https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/analyst-color/26/09/61840070/sp500-yardeni-target-cut-fed-rate-hike-valuations','["SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-17 13:17:15.888857','analyst','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'A prominent analyst adjusting targets can influence investor sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"SPY": 761.66}','{"SPY": {"60m": 0.154}}','2026-09-18 13:20:58.044767','2026-09-17 13:17:09.564246','61840070',replace('In August, Ed Yardeni held the highest year-end target for the S&P; 500 on Wall Street at 8,400. \n\nThis week he cut it to 7,900.\n\nNothing broke in corporate earnings. What changed is the price of money.\n\nThe Fed Hiked, And The Bar For Another One Is Low\n\nThe Federal Open Market Committee raised the federal funds rate by 25 basis points on Wednesday to a target range of 3.75% to 4.00%. The vote was unanimous, 12-0. It was the first increase since July 2023.\n\nFed Chair Kevin Warsh was blunt at the press conference. \n\n“The plain fact is that inflation is too high and has been for too long,” he said.\n\nThe Summary of Economic Projections, the quarterly grid where each official pencils in where they think rates are headed, pointed to one more hike before year-end. \n\nFour participants penciled in a third. No cuts are projected for 2027, and inflation is not forecast to return fully to the 2% target until 2029.\n\nYardeni read the move as deliberately open-ended rather than a one-off adjustment.\n\nGrowth is strong, the labor market is at full employment, and Warsh himself declined to describe financial conditions as restrictive. \n\nWith that combination, the case for further hikes remains alive unless inflation clearly cools.\n\nThe Dow Jones Industrial Average – tracked by the SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF (NYSE:DIA) – fell 1.21% Wednesday, the S&P; 500 – tracked via the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) – slipped 0.45% and the Nasdaq Composite closed flat. \n\nHigher Yields Compress Stock Multiples\n\nThe mechanism behind Yardeni’s year-end target reduction for the S&P; 500 is a three-step chain.\n\nFirst, the 10-year Treasury yield closed Wednesday at roughly 5.01%, its highest level since 2007. \n\nSecond, a higher risk-free yield makes government bonds more competitive with stocks. \n\nThird, investors respond by paying less for each dollar of expected corporate profit.\n\nYardeni lowered his year-end forward price-to-earnings multiple for the index to 18.6 times from 19.8 times. Applied to unchanged earnings, that alone removes 500 points from the target.\n\nHe also raised the probability of his bearish scenario to 30% from 20%, trimming his “Roaring 2020s” base case to 70%. \n\n“The risks of a downturn have increased over the next three to six months,” he wrote. His old 8,400 target now sits in mid-2027.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEd Yardeni Rejects Bond Panic, Says Dalio and Dimon Are Too ''Pessimistic''\n\nThe Economy Is Not The Problem. Energy Is.\n\nThe data released alongside the decision made the case that demand is accelerating, not fading.\n\nAugust retail sales rose 1.2% month over month against expectations of 0.8%. The control group used to calculate gross domestic product jumped 1.4%, versus the expected 0.5%.\n\nThe Atlanta Fed’s GDPNow model lifted its third-quarter growth estimate to 5.1% from 4.4%.\n\nThe inflation side is where the pressure sits. Import prices rose 7.0% year over year in August, the fastest since 2022. \n\nExcluding petroleum, they still rose 5.5%. Imports from Hong Kong, Singapore, South Korea and Taiwan surged 12.6%, reflecting AI-related demand for chips, servers and memory running ahead of supply.\n\nBrent and West Texas Intermediate crude both trade above $100 a barrel, each up more than 20% over the past month as the conflict with Iran continues.\n\nFriday In Tokyo May Matter More Than Wednesday In Washington\n\nYardeni flagged Japan as an additional risk. The Bank of Japan is expected to raise its policy rate by 25 basis points to 1.25% on Friday. \n\nHigher Japanese rates and a firmer yen unwind the carry trade, in which investors borrowed cheaply in yen to buy higher-yielding bonds elsewhere. Unwinding it forces selling of those bonds, including Treasuries.\n\nYardeni’s revised target still implies roughly 4% upside from Tuesday’s close of 7,585.73. \n\nThe disagreement with his August self is about the multiple and the timing, not about the direction of corporate profits.\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'c0377f14bad79312c2e63481605e348b144f1717','2026-09-17 12:33:51','2026-09-17 13:17:09.552337',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 12:33:51');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(338,'alpaca:61839701','benzinga','2026-09-17 12:25:57','Intel Stock Could Nearly Double to $200 in 2 Years, Analyst Says — Potential Apple, Tesla, and AI Chip Deals Could Fuel the Rally','Intel stock could double to $200 within two years as potential Apple and Tesla foundry deals and AI demand drive earnings growth.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61839701/intel-stock-could-nearly-double-to-200-in-2-years-analyst-says-potential-apple-tesla-and-ai-chip-deals-could-fuel-the-rally','["AAPL", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 13:17:16.899519','analyst','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'Analyst commentary on potential future price increase without confirmation.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 325.14, "TSLA": 356.12}','{"AAPL": {"60m": 3.649}, "TSLA": {"60m": 3.003}}','2026-09-18 13:20:58.044767','2026-09-17 13:17:09.567798','61839701',replace('Shares of Intel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) could nearly double to $200, driven by foundry deals and stronger product earnings, according to an analyst at Melius Research.\n\nThe firm maintained a Buy rating on the chip manufacturer, with a price target of $165 per share. However, Melius analyst Ben Reitzes believes Intel’s shares could reach as high as $200 within the next two years, CNBC reported.\n\nReitzes suggested that this potential surge could be due to Intel’s prospective foundry agreements with Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) and other significant players. He highlighted Intel’s 14A, the company’s chip manufacturing process node used to build high-performance semiconductors, as a crucial factor.\n\nReitzes said, “If 14A takes on high-volume manufacturing in 2028 with Apple, Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) and one other hyperscaler committed… one could argue it can exit the year worthy of a 4x multiple … or about $100.”\n\nHe added that if server CPU pricing and agentic CPU attach remain strong through 2028, while the AI PC mix continues to lift client average selling prices, product earnings of more than $4 could naturally follow. “Add the two and the stock is $200 within two years, roughly a doubling from here,” Reitzes concluded.\n\nReitzes expects the stock’s rally to continue, citing structural tailwinds and strong leadership of CEO Lip-Bu Tan, which could drive further gains.\n\nIntel Gains From AI Chip Demand\n\nReitzes’ projection came on the heels of Intel reportedly being in talks with SK Hynix Inc. (NASDAQ:SKHY) to make memory chips at Intel’s planned Ohio facility. This move comes as part of the U.S. government’s push for companies to expand domestic production as AI demand surges.\n\nIntel declined to comment on media speculation about future business arrangements but noted that it was “committed to Ohio” and continues its investments to accelerate the site readiness. Reportedly, SK Hynix could lease part of Intel’s facility or form a joint venture with Intel and cloud firms. SK Hynix clarified that "nothing has been finalized regarding cooperation with any specific companies."\n\nIntel’s AI Turnaround Gains Momentum\n\nIntel’s partnership with Terafab, a $25 billion chip manufacturing project involving Tesla and Space Exploration Technologies Corp (NASDAQ:SPCX), makes Intel its primary foundry provider and strengthens its AI-focused turnaround, according to Tigress Financial Partners. Analyst Ivan Feinseth maintained a Buy rating and raised Intel’s price target to $145 from $118 citing catalysts across data-center computing, AI PCs, advanced semiconductor manufacturing, and foundry services.\n\nThe analyst said growing demand for AI inference, agentic computing, data orchestration, networking and enterprise workloads is increasing the role of CPUs alongside GPUs, benefiting Intel’s Xeon business. He said the Xeon 6 and 18A-based Xeon 6+ platforms position Intel to capitalize on this demand.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Rankings place Intel in the 99th percentile for momentum. Benzinga’s screener allows you to compare INTC’s performance with its peers.\n\nINTC Price Action: Year-to-date, Intel’s stock has surged about 173.85%, as per Benzinga Pro. On Wednesday, it closed 4.03% higher at $101.05. The stock rose about 3.19% to $104.27 premarket on Thursday.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSK Hynix, Intel May Make Memories in Ohio: These ETFs Are Along for the Ride\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'34832ed1a332ab6eae30e5a88d39874a61344f18','2026-09-17 12:25:57','2026-09-17 13:17:09.552337',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 12:25:57');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(339,'alpaca:61839636','benzinga','2026-09-17 12:22:03','Bitcoin Holds $76,000 After Fed Hike: Why Is BTC Strong While Equities Fall?','Bitcoin holds above $76,000 after the Fed hike, but persistent inflation, high yields and another potential hike threaten crypto liquidity and prices.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61839636/bitcoin-holds-76000-after-fed-hike-why-is-btc-strong-while-equities-fall','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-17 13:17:18.627300','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline describes market conditions without providing a definitive impact on Bitcoin''s price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 77563.640625, "ETH/USD": 2414.179931640625, "SOL/USD": 100.4325, "XRP/USD": 1.3027}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.358}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 1.514}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": 0.468, "1d": 5.115}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": -0.71, "1d": 1.417}}','2026-09-18 13:20:58.044767','2026-09-17 13:17:09.570886','61839636',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) trades above $76,000 on Thursday as crypto markets absorbed the Federal Reserve’s first interest-rate hike since 2023.\n\nThe muted move puts the focus on what comes next—whether Wednesday’s hike was a one-off adjustment or the start of a longer tightening cycle that could pressure liquidity across crypto markets.\n\nWhy BTC Isn’t Selling Off?\n\nSantiment Intelligence data noted on Thursday that Bitcoin’s ability to stay above $76,000 could reflect how heavily markets had positioned for tighter policy before the announcement.\n\nInstead of reacting to the 25-basis-point hike itself, traders are now assessing whether inflation forces the Fed into a more aggressive tightening cycle.\n\nThe Fed raised its 2026 PCE inflation forecast to 3.7% from 3.6%, with core inflation seen at 3.4%. Inflation is not expected to return to the Fed’s 2% target until 2029.\n\nFor crypto, inflation remains key:\n\nCooling inflation and stable Treasury yields could ease pressure on Bitcoin. \n\nBut persistent inflation, higher energy prices or rising yields could increase expectations for more Fed tightening.\n\nWhy Next Fed Hike Matters More For BTC\n\nSantiment cautioned that the bigger risk for crypto could be what happens after September.\n\nThe Fed’s latest projections show a median federal funds rate of 4.1% at the end of 2026, effectively pointing to another quarter-point increase from the current range.\n\n16 of 18 policymakers expect at least one more hike this year.\n\nThat leaves Bitcoin facing a liquidity test even as it absorbs Wednesday’s widely anticipated decision.\n\nHigher rates increase the appeal of cash and government bonds while raising financing costs and tightening financial conditions, potentially create a tougher backdrop for Bitcoin and higher-risk altcoins like Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH), Solana (CRYPTO: SOL) and XRP (CRYPTO: XRP)\n\nWhat’s Next For Crypto\n\nSantiment Intelligence sees the near-term crypto outlook as "uncomfortable."\n\nThe strong dollar, high Treasury yields and prospect of another Fed hike remain headwinds for crypto.\n\nBut September’s hike removed some uncertainty, shifting focus to upcoming inflation, energy and economic data for clues on whether further tightening is needed.\n\nCrypto-specific catalysts can also outweigh macro pressures.\n\nBitcoin’s next major move may depend on both Fed policy and U.S. crypto regulation. The CLARITY Act setback highlighted BTC’s strength in responding to regulatory developments.\n\n"The September hike is therefore neither automatically catastrophic nor secretly bullish," noted Santiment.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin, Ethereum, XRPHit by CLARITY Act ''Setback,'' Fed Hike: What''s Next?','\n',char(10)),'c14d62eac759d035f25174e565ab2212d8ff6896','2026-09-17 12:22:03','2026-09-17 13:17:09.552337',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 12:22:03');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(340,'alpaca:61844337','benzinga','2026-09-17 14:05:01','Amazon Stock Moves Higher: What''s Going On?','Amazon.com shares are rising Thursday after a multibillion-dollar Generac deal and as markets digest the Fed&#39;s first rate hike since 2023.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61844337/amazon-stock-moves-higher-whats-going-on','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-17 14:17:27.118152','other','bullish',2,3,'days',1,'Shares are rising due to recent events but the cause is not clearly defined.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 254.92}','{"AMZN": {"60m": -1.467}}','2026-09-18 14:21:10.965967','2026-09-17 14:17:23.532901','61844337',replace('Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) shares are rising Thursday. The company struck a multibillion-dollar generator supply deal with Generac, while broader markets digest the Federal Reserve’s first rate hike since 2023.\n\nAmazon.com stock is trading in a tight range. Where is AMZN stock headed?\n\nAmazon Secures Right to Buy Generac Stock in Data Center Power Deal\n\nGenerac Holdings Inc (NYSE:GNRC) stock spiked about 33% before Thursday’s opening bell once word got out about its new arrangement to supply Amazon’s data centers with backup power equipment. As part of the deal, Amazon’s investment vehicle, Amazon.com NV Investment Holdings LLC, picked up a warrant letting it buy close to 1.7 million Generac shares at just over $200 apiece, an arrangement that could ultimately be worth roughly $8 billion if fully exercised.\n\nA little more than 300,000 of those shares became available to Amazon right away, and the remainder will unlock gradually depending on how much money flows from Amazon and its various affiliates to Generac in exchange for the generators actually delivered to its facilities.\n\nBeyond the equity piece, the two companies also locked in a separate multiyear supply contract, projecting roughly $2.4 billion worth of generator shipments across 2027 and 2028 alone.\n\nFed Delivers Expected Hike, But Signals More Could Follow\n\nOn the macro side, the central bank moved its benchmark rate up by a quarter percentage point Wednesday, landing in a new 3.75% to 4% range, marking its first increase in roughly three years and matching what most on Wall Street had already priced in.\n\nWhat caught people off guard wasn’t the hike itself but the forward guidance behind it. Nearly all committee members, 16 out of 18, now anticipate at least one additional rate bump before the year wraps up, a dramatic jump from June, when only six officials expected that outcome. Policymakers’ median outlook now points toward a 4% to 4.25% range by December.\n\nAlongside that shift, the Fed nudged its inflation outlook higher to 3.7% and bumped its growth projection up to 2.3%, while trimming its jobless rate estimate down to 4.1%.\n\nHigher interest rates can affect Amazon given the scale of the company’s ongoing spending on data centers, warehouses and other infrastructure, since borrowing to fund that expansion becomes more expensive as rates climb. Rate increases can also weigh on how investors value growth-oriented stocks like Amazon more broadly, since future profits get discounted more heavily when rates are higher.\n\nAMZN Shares Are Rising\n\nAMZN Price Action: Amazon.com shares were up 1.62% at $249.95 at the time of publication on Thursday, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nHouse Passes Bipartisan Bill to Shield Americans From Higher Electricity Costs as AI Data Centers Drive Massive Power Demand\n\nImage: ACHPF/Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'ecff0035948389a42c4f06e68b53666583372b30','2026-09-17 14:05:01','2026-09-17 14:17:23.528420',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 14:05:01');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(341,'alpaca:61844153','benzinga','2026-09-17 14:01:40','AI Could Threaten Nuclear Command Systems, Warn US-China Experts— Urge Human Control and Emergency Hotline','US-China security experts urge AI safeguards for nuclear systems, cyberattacks and military escalation as AI risks grow.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61844153/ai-could-threaten-nuclear-command-systems-warn-us-china-experts-urge-human-control-and-emergency-hotline','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-17 14:17:28.501271','other','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'Concerns raised by experts about AI risks to nuclear systems and the need for safeguards.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 501.15}','{"MSFT": {"60m": -0.533}}','2026-09-18 14:21:10.965967','2026-09-17 14:17:23.536511','61844153',replace('Security specialists from the U.S. and China have called on their governments to brace for potential artificial intelligence (AI) threats that could compromise nuclear command networks or initiate military cyber operations.\n\nMelanie Sisson of the Brookings Institution and Tianjiao Jiang of Fudan University are part of a U.S.-China dialogue launched by Brookings and Tsinghua University’s Center for International Security and Strategy in 2019. Their proposals were released last week, ahead of government-level AI talks and a Sept. 24 meeting between President Donald Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping in Washington.\n\nThey suggested measures to prevent AI systems from triggering international incidents. These include defining boundaries around nuclear systems, ensuring human control over significant cyberattacks, and creating a hotline for incidents involving autonomous AI.\n\nBrookings’ Melanie Sisson argued that humans should retain sole authority to launch AI-enabled cyberattacks against nuclear command systems or strategically important infrastructure.\n\nNeither the U.S. nor China has officially endorsed the Brookings-Tsinghua proposals, Reuters reported. \n\nHowever, China has incorporated AI into its existing arms-control framework. In June, Chinese disarmament ambassador Shen Jian warned that military AI could affect strategic stability and increase the risk of miscalculation and escalation, while emphasizing that weapons should remain under human control. China has also argued that AI safety should not be used to justify technological restrictions, according to the publication. \n\nRead Also:\n\nChina, Russia Tell US to Halt Space Militarization After First Confirmation of Weapons in Orbit: ‘Stop Preparing for War’\n\nSanders Says AI Risk Tops Nuclear Threat\n\nSen. Bernie Sanders (I-VT), in an interview with CBS News, warned that the potential threat posed by AI to humanity is "probably greater" than that of nuclear weapons.\n\nSanders said he plans to introduce legislation next week that would permanently ban superintelligent AI systems more capable than humans and that could potentially escape human control, and pause the development of advanced AI. He also proposed severe penalties for violations, including up to 20 years in prison, arguing that laws protecting humanity from such technology should carry significant consequences.\n\nNadella, China Official Flag AI Risks\n\nMicrosoft Corp.’s (NASDAQ:MSFT) CEO Satya Nadella emphasized that AI safety should be a concern for China as well. Nadella suggested the possibility of “international norms” around AI, provided the risks are well understood.\n\nMeanwhile, China’s state security minister Chen Yixin identified six major AI risks. He warned that AI could enable more effective cyberattacks, large-scale data leaks, technological monopolies, social disruption and battlefield advantages through AI-powered targeting. He urged stronger AI guidelines and faster security controls to ensure its "healthy and orderly development" through "high-efficiency governance."\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nOpenAI, Anthropic Slowdown Call Won''t Derail AI Infrastructure Demand, Why One Fund Manager Sees No Spending Pause in Sight\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'864defd696949963feb82097e46018e8433100ce','2026-09-17 14:01:40','2026-09-17 14:17:23.528420',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 14:01:40');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(342,'alpaca:61844008','benzinga','2026-09-17 14:00:11','SpaceX Is Worth $2 Trillion. Why Does Its Stock Swing Like a Small-Cap?','SpaceX is worth about $2 trillion, but its shares swing roughly 4.5% a day as a small float and heavy retail trading drive volatility.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61844008/spacex-stock-volatility-small-cap-float','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-17 14:17:29.750175','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline provides analysis but no definitive news affecting stock price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 501.15}','{"MSFT": {"60m": -0.533}}','2026-09-18 14:21:10.965967','2026-09-17 14:17:23.539593','61844008',replace('Elon Musk‘s SpaceX (NASDAQ:SPCX) has a market cap of about $2 trillion, but its stock doesn’t trade like it.\n\nOver the past 22 trading sessions, the gap between SpaceX’s daily high and low averaged 4.53% of its closing price. \n\nThat compares with 4.52% for $38 billion Rocket Lab Corp. (NASDAQ:RKLB) and 1.89% for Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT), based on S&P; Global Market Intelligence daily price data.\n\nThree factors may help explain the gap: relatively little SpaceX stock is available to trade, investors are pricing several fast-changing businesses at once, and Musk has attracted an unusually committed retail shareholder base.\n\nA Mega-Cap With a Small Float\n\nSpaceX still has a relatively limited pool of stock available to trade. SpaceX has about 1.91 billion shares in its float, just 14% of its 13.57 billion shares outstanding, according to StockAnalysis.\n\nThose shares turn over quickly. About 77 million SpaceX shares have changed hands on an average day over the past 20 sessions, equal to roughly 4% of its float. For Microsoft, the comparable figure is 0.27%.\n\nThat supply is expanding as post-IPO lockups expire. Up to 328.4 million additional SpaceX shares become eligible for sale Sept. 24, two days after the current target for Starship Flight 14.\n\nS3 Partners estimated short interest, or bets against the stock, peaked at about 34% of SpaceX’s tradable float in early August. It fell to roughly 11% within a week as shares rebounded and an Aug. 6 lockup expiration made about 912 million more shares eligible for sale.\n\nS&P; Global separately called SpaceX a “focal point for disagreement” and said it was July’s largest single-stock securities-lending revenue generator, with nearly $29 billion worth of shares out on loan on average.\n\nSpaceX Has More Than One Story\n\nInvestors are simultaneously valuing SpaceX as a reusable-rocket company, global broadband network, potential mobile carrier, frontier-AI lab, AI infrastructure provider and, further out, an orbital data-center operator.\n\nStarship Flight 14 shows how those narratives can converge. SpaceX is targeting Sept. 22, pending regulatory approval, for Starship’s first orbital flight and the deployment of 26 Starlink V3 satellites.\n\nTraders on Polymarket give Flight 14 a 91% chance of launching by Sept. 30. Roughly $676,000 has traded across the broader Flight 14 market.\n\nThe ‘Cult Stock’ Factor\n\nSteve Eisman called SpaceX a potential “retail cult stock” before its IPO and later said Musk has “believers, not investors.”\n\nRetail behavior has given that argument some backing. Vanda Research data cited by Reuters showed SpaceX recorded no day of net retail selling from its June 12 IPO through Aug. 5, including when shares fell as much as 12.9% after earnings.\n\nSpaceX may already be worth $2 trillion, but investors are still deciding what kind of company they own. That leaves plenty of room for each new launch, AI announcement or Musk comment to move the stock like a much smaller company.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nCathie Wood Says SpaceX Didn''t Need an IPO—Until Data Centers in Space Came Along','\n',char(10)),'cb8d4acd6f6184a604cc8286797ecc8e3a835943','2026-09-17 14:00:11','2026-09-17 14:17:23.528420',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 14:00:11');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(343,'alpaca:61843268','benzinga','2026-09-17 13:47:23','Crypto Bull Market Doesn''t Depend on CLARITY Act, Bitwise Exec Says','Bitwise CIO Matt Hougan says the Clarity Act’s failure is only a speed bump as SEC and CFTC crypto rules move forward.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61843268/crypto-bull-market-doesnt-depend-on-clarity-act-bitwise-exec-says','["BTC/USD", "SOL/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-17 14:17:30.921853','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Analyst comments on market conditions are usually neutral.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 77563.640625, "SOL/USD": 101.35}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.411}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": -0.316, "1d": 7.498}}','2026-09-18 14:21:10.965967','2026-09-17 14:17:23.542504','61843268',replace('Bitwise Chief Investment Officer Matt Hougan on Wednesday walked back his bearish CLARITY Act call, telling clients the bill’s failure may matter far less than the headlines suggest.\n\nBitcoin’s Rally Weakens the Bearish CLARITY Act Case\n\nHougan wrote in a note to clients that he previously predicted six more weeks of difficult markets if the bill failed. \n\nOne data point changed his view: Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) climbed from roughly $57,950 on July 1 to above $80,000 by Sept. 4, while Polymarket odds of the CLARITY Act passing fell from 39% to 18% over the exact same stretch. \n\n“If the bull market depended on CLARITY’s passage, you would have expected falling odds to mean falling prices,” Hougan wrote. “We got the opposite.”\n\nWhy Wall Street Never Waited \n\nHougan pointed out that major institutions kept building through the entire legislative uncertainty. Robinhood (NASDAQ:HOOD) launched its own blockchain, Morgan Stanley (NYSE:MS) launched a Solana (CRYPTO: SOL) ETF, and the DTCC settled its first batch of tokenized stock trades, all without a single vote from Congress. \n\nHis explanation: firms already had confidence in a pro-crypto SEC and CFTC locked in until 2029.\n\nSEC Chair Paul Atkins told CNBC in July the agency is “ready, willing, and able to come out with rules that address the same issues as Clarity,” and followed through with the proposed Regulation Crypto Assets in August. \n\nMeanwhile, CFTC Chair Mike Selig doubled down Wednesday morning, saying the agency is “locked in and ready to ship its rules for the new frontier of finance.”\n\nReversible Agency Rules Remain the Main Regulatory Risk\n\nHougan was not dismissing the failure entirely. Agency rules can be reversed by a future administration, and only Congress can give the CFTC direct authority over crypto spot markets. \n\nLegislative clarity would have been more durable. Bitcoin fell roughly 4% following Tuesday’s vote, with Hougan citing interest rates and oil prices as contributing factors alongside the news.\n\nWhat This Means Going Forward\n\nHougan’s overall framing is that crypto sits in a “heads we win big, tails we still win” regulatory setup. \n\nThe current market weakness likely persists until Atkins and Selig announce their next rulemaking proposals, at which point attention shifts back to institutional adoption. \n\n“The bull market ahead of us has a few more speed bumps,” Hougan wrote, while arguing the destination has not changed.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nHow To Earn $500 A Month From Worthington Enterprises Stock Ahead Of Q1 Earnings','\n',char(10)),'b0df77988f35cffbd5a4985170bb3d427efdf872','2026-09-17 13:47:23','2026-09-17 14:17:23.528420',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 13:47:23');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(344,'alpaca:61843217','benzinga','2026-09-17 13:46:49','Bond King Jeffrey Gundlach Wants Out of the AI ''Epicenter'': Inside His Zero-Exposure Portfolio','Bond King Jeffrey Gundlach warns of an AI stock fallout. See why he is dumping Big Tech for equal-weight ETFs, gold, and EM debt.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61843217/bond-king-jeffrey-gundlach-wants-out-of-the-ai-epicenter-inside-his-zero-exposure-portfolio','["META", "MSFT", "NVDA", "QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-17 14:17:32.282719','analyst','bearish',3,3,'weeks',1,'Jeffrey Gundlach''s warning may influence market sentiment towards AI stocks.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 578.53, "MSFT": 501.15, "NVDA": 217.54, "QQQ": 707.67, "SPY": 761.66}','{"META": {"60m": 18.006}, "MSFT": {"60m": -0.533}, "NVDA": {"60m": 0.841}, "QQQ": {"60m": 1.303}, "SPY": {"60m": 0.127}}','2026-09-18 14:21:10.965967','2026-09-17 14:17:23.545613','61843217',replace('The DoubleLine Capital founder and CEO Jeffrey Gundlach, also known as the Bond King, said he wants to be “out of the epicenter” of the AI race, citing widening credit spreads and extreme valuations.\n\nEscalating AI Credit Cracks\n\nSpeaking on The Julia La Roche Show, Gundlach cited the S&P; 500 Shiller CAPE ratio exceeding 42 as a historical indicator of negative real returns over the coming decade.\n\nWhile broad junk bonds remain resilient, debt linked to AI borrowing and corporate issuers like Oracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL) have experienced visible spread widening as the bond market rejects aggressive pricing.\n\n"You’re going to have fallout and losers in the AI, you know, race for the holy grail," Gundlach said. "I think we’re close enough to there that I want to be out of the epicenter."\n\nThe AI space is currently dominated by companies like Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA), Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOG) (NASDAQ:GOOGL), Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META), and Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT), among others.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump’s Tariff Threat Over Fed Rate Decision ‘Makes No Economic Sense,’ Says Justin Wolfers: Kevin Warsh ''Called His Bluff’\n\nStrategic Zero-AI Portfolio Allocation\n\n“What I am recommending now is 30% in one thing equal weighted index. It is the Fortune 500 index,” said Gundlach, adding that “so you don’t have 40% of your portfolio in AI, you have almost nothing.” The Fortune 500 is tracked by ETFs like the DoubleLine Fortune 500 Equal Weight ETF (NYSE:DFVE).\n\nHis remaining portfolio allocates 30% to fixed income, split evenly between low-risk core bonds and local-currency emerging market debt, which is tracked by ETFs like VanEck JP Morgan EM Local Currency Bond ETF (NYSE:EMLC).\n\nReal assets account for 20%, split between physical gold, often tracked by ETFs like SPDR Gold Trust (NYSE:GLD) and the DoubleLine Commodity Strategy ETF (NYSE:DCMT). The remaining 20% serves as “dry powder,” split between the DoubleLine Commercial Real Estate ETF (NYSE:DCRE) and the DoubleLine Flexible Income I (NASDAQ:DFLEX).\n\nPrivate Credit and Rating Arbitrage Warnings\n\nGundlach also warned of systemic vulnerabilities in private credit, citing rating agency arbitrage that echoes structural flaws seen during the 2008 financial crisis with underwriters like Wells Fargo.\n\nHow Have Stocks and Bonds Performed in 2026?\n\nAt the last check, the 30-year Treasury bond yielded 5.32%, the 10-year Treasury bond was at 4.97%, and the two-year bond was at 4.71%.\n\nThe S&P; 500 index has advanced 10.11% year-to-date. Similarly, the Nasdaq Composite index was up 11.80%, and the Dow Jones gained 6.36% YTD.\n\nOn Wednesday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed mixed. SPY fell 0.44% to $754.05, while QQQ rose 0.026% to $704.72. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), also ended 1.15% lower at $515.22.\n\nOn Thursday, SPY is up about 0.92%, QQQ gained 1.32%, and DIA advanced 0.44%.\n\nRead Also:\n\nS&P; 500 Could Deliver Another 6% by Year-End as JPMorgan Calls Bears an ‘Extinct Species’ — Polymarket Bettors Price 35% Odds\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'c7d71691431f461d3bf889d7b120844bbda6fd3c','2026-09-17 13:46:49','2026-09-17 14:17:23.528420',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 13:46:49');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(345,'alpaca:61846924','benzinga','2026-09-17 15:02:58','NVIDIA Boss Slams AI Doom Mongers, Stock Bounces','NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang rejects calls for new AI regulations at a Salesforce event, declaring safety an engineering challenge as Nvidia stock rebounds 3%.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61846924/nvidia-boss-slams-ai-doom-mongers-stock-bounces','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 15:17:40.543044','other','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Positive remarks from the CEO promote investor confidence.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 217.54}','{"NVDA": {"60m": 0.841}}','2026-09-18 15:21:30.157679','2026-09-17 15:17:36.970888','61846924',replace('NVIDIA Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) stock traded up almost 3% on Thursday as risk-on appetite lifted mega-cap tech alongside a broader market rebound. The Nasdaq is up 1.57%, while the S&P; 500 is up 1.01%.\n\nCEO Jensen Huang is pushing back against calls to slow artificial intelligence development while the company navigates a widening global debate over AI safety, regulation and data-center expansion.\n\nHuang Rejects New AI Regulations\n\nSpeaking at a Salesforce Inc. (NYSE:CRM) event, Huang argued that companies can develop AI quickly while maintaining safety standards.\n\n"We don’t need new laws — we don’t need new regulations," Huang said. He called the choice between safety and speed a "false choice," adding, "You can definitely have both at the same time," Bloomberg reported on Wednesday.\n\nHuang said companies should delay products when safety concerns arise but described safety primarily as an engineering responsibility.\n\n"Safety is paramount," he said. "In a lot of ways, it’s job one. However, safety is an engineering problem."\n\nHis comments followed Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei’s call to slow frontier-model development, which intensified concerns that tighter safeguards could reduce AI infrastructure spending. NVIDIA shares fell 3.4% Monday amid those concerns.\n\nHuang Joins Broader AI Policy Debate\n\nEarlier this week, Huang took a live call from President Donald Trump during the All-In Summit. Both pushed back against slowing AI and data-center development, Bloomberg reported on Tuesday.\n\nHuang is also scheduled to attend an AI forum convened by King Charles III in Scotland alongside executives from OpenAI, Google DeepMind and Anthropic. The event will focus on AI safety and international cooperation, Bloomberg reported on Thursday.\n\nSeparately, Huang is expected to attend Trump’s state dinner with Chinese leader Xi Jinping next week, Bloomberg reported on Wednesday.\n\nChina And Data Centers Remain In Focus\n\nTrump previously eased restrictions on some NVIDIA chip exports to China, although only older-generation processors can currently enter the market.\n\nNVIDIA remains a major supplier of AI accelerators powering the ongoing data-center buildout, placing the company at the center of debates over both AI expansion and its associated risks.\n\nTop ETF Exposure\n\nGoldman Sachs ActiveBeta US Large Cap Equity ETF (NYSE:GSLC): 9.83% Weight\n\nSapient Quality Select ETF (NASDAQ:SQS): 9.87% Weight\n\nPacer Data and Digital Revolution ETF (NYSE:TRFK): 9.92% Weight\n\nSignificance: Because NVDA carries such a heavy weight in these funds, any significant inflows or outflows for these ETFs will likely force automatic buying or selling of the stock.\n\nPrice Action\n\nNVDA Stock Price Activity: NVIDIA shares are trading higher by 2.54% at $219.33 at the time of publication on Thursday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nImage via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nNVIDIA CEO Says AI Spending Flywheel Is ‘Really, Really Flying’','\n',char(10)),'d41efdc273c0715db1554ba8de9fa0ba323db1e5','2026-09-17 15:02:58','2026-09-17 15:17:36.966246',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 15:02:58');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(346,'alpaca:61846721','benzinga','2026-09-17 14:57:59','Steve Eisman Calls AI ''Terminator'' Fears ''Garbage'': If You''re Scared, ''Postpone Your IPO''','Steve Eisman challenged AI labs to postpone IPOs if they believe runaway AI risks justify slowing development.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61846721/steve-eisman-ai-fears-anthropic-ipo-nvidia','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 15:17:42.516188','analyst','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Analyst commentary on AI risks and IPOs.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 217.54}','{"NVDA": {"60m": 0.841}}','2026-09-18 15:21:30.157679','2026-09-17 15:17:36.977945','61846721',replace('‘Big Short’ investor Steve Eisman called fears of runaway artificial intelligence “garbage” Thursday and challenged AI companies that warn the technology is moving too fast to back it up by postponing their IPOs and capital raises.\n\n“I think this whole Terminator thing is garbage. Just garbage,” Eisman told CNBC. “Put your money where your mouth is. Postpone your IPO,” he later added. \n\nEisman, who said he has stopped adding to his AI positions and trimmed some exposure, warned that weakness at the leading AI labs could ripple through Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) and the broader AI trade. Nvidia is considering investing as much as $10 billion as an anchor investor in Anthropic’s planned IPO.\n\nThe comments come days after Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei called for slowing frontier AI development.\n\nEisman Says AI Labs Lack a Moat\n\nEisman offered a different explanation for the urgency around AI safety.\n\n“Token maxing is over, the open-weight models are taking big market share,” he said.\n\nToken maxing refers to maximizing use of tokens, the units of text AI models bill by, often with little regard for cost. Cheaper open-weight models, which developers can download and run themselves, give cost-conscious customers an alternative.\n\n“They realize that there are no moats around their business whatsoever,” Eisman said.\n\nHe went further, arguing the companies are “trying to manufacture a crisis” that could lead to regulation they could use to “create the moats” and “create the duopoly that they want.”\n\nEisman later acknowledged that he does not know the companies’ motives.\n\nIn July, Eisman said he would be “petrified” running OpenAI or Anthropic as cheaper Chinese models threatened to pressure pricing.\n\nAnthropic Eyes $2 Trillion IPO\n\nAnthropic is preparing what could become the largest IPO ever, potentially raising as much as $100 billion at a valuation around $2 trillion. That would roughly double the $965 billion valuation it received in a May funding round, Reuters reported.\n\n“Is anybody talking about postponing IPOs or postponing raising capital?” Eisman said. “I haven’t heard anything.”\n\nPolymarket gives Anthropic an 87% chance of listing by Dec. 31, with about $3.2 million traded on the timing market.\n\nA separate market puts roughly a 73% chance on Anthropic closing its first trading day with a market cap of at least $2 trillion. The most likely range is $2 trillion to $2.25 trillion, at 27%, followed by $2.25 trillion to $2.5 trillion at 25%.\n\nWhy Nvidia Investors Should Care\n\nEisman said Nvidia, hyperscalers and the broader AI infrastructure buildout depend on OpenAI and Anthropic remaining healthy businesses. He called OpenAI “the weaker company” of the two.\n\nOpenAI CEO Sam Altman said last week the company will not go public in 2026, citing the safety work ahead. Eisman tied the delay to that weakness. “I think that’s one reason why they postponed their IPO,” he said.\n\n“If something were to happen to one of those two companies, then the chain would really fall apart,” Eisman said.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nCathie Wood Says SpaceX Didn''t Need an IPO—Until Data Centers in Space Came Along','\n',char(10)),'b28e98ae392f1140bf5219ea8c7f146bfc6cfd7c','2026-09-17 14:57:59','2026-09-17 15:17:36.966246',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 14:57:59');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(347,'alpaca:61846547','benzinga','2026-09-17 14:51:25','EXCLUSIVE: Google Is Racing to Secure Nuclear Power for AI—The Fuel Problem Comes Next','Google is locking up nuclear power for AI, but a uranium expert warns Big Tech may need to invest more in the fuel supply chain.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/commodities/26/09/61846547/google-ai-nuclear-fuel','["AMZN", "META", "MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-17 15:17:43.810327','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses strategic moves but lacks confirmation of immediate impact.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 254.92, "META": 578.53, "MSFT": 501.15}','{"AMZN": {"60m": -1.467}, "META": {"60m": 18.006}, "MSFT": {"60m": -0.533}}','2026-09-18 15:21:30.157679','2026-09-17 15:17:36.981125','61846547',replace('Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOGL) (NASDAQ:GOOG) Google is securing nuclear electricity for decades as it races to expand AI infrastructure, but locking up reactor output is only one piece of the equation. \n\nThe bigger question may be what fuels those reactors: Christo Liebenberg, co-founder and president of LIS Technologies, told Benzinga in an exclusive email interview. Liebenberg noted that Big Tech is signing power deals faster than it is committing money to the nuclear fuel supply chain.\n\nGoogle Locks Up Nuclear Power\n\nGoogle announced Sept. 9 that it will invest €13 billion ($15.1 billion) in Finland over 2027 and 2028 to expand digital infrastructure, including data-center capacity. As part of the investment, Google signed a 22-year agreement covering up to 50% of the capacity of Finland’s Loviisa nuclear plant, supporting its life extension through 2050.\n\nThe deal illustrates the increasingly direct connection between AI infrastructure and nuclear power. Google is not simply building more data centers and hoping the grid can keep up; it is helping secure long-duration nuclear generation to support that expansion.\n\nRead Also:\n\nGoogle-Parent Alphabet Just Helped Turn This German Nuclear Fusion Startup Into a $2.4 Billion Company\n\nThe move also fits a broader hyperscaler trend. Alphabet, Amazon.com Inc (NASDAQ:AMZN), Meta Platforms Inc (NASDAQ:META) and Microsoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT) have all pursued nuclear power agreements or partnerships as AI pushes their electricity requirements higher. \n\nA Carnegie analysis estimates those commitments could represent roughly 6.9 gigawatts of nuclear capacity by the early 2030s, although some projects depend on reactors that have yet to be commercialized.\n\nThe Fuel Gap\n\nThat’s where Liebenberg’s exclusive Benzinga interview introduces a different part of the nuclear story.\n\n"What we see are a lot of hyperscalers investing into PPA’s (power purchase agreements) with reactor companies, but very little FPA’s (fuel purchase agreements) into the nuclear fuel supply chain," Liebenberg said.\n\nHis point is not that Big Tech has no role in nuclear fuel. Rather, the financial commitment to securing electricity is becoming much more visible than commitments to the infrastructure required to produce the fuel behind that electricity.\n\nThat distinction matters because nuclear power requires a chain extending from uranium mining through conversion, enrichment and fuel fabrication. Liebenberg argues that the U.S. has underbuilt several of those stages after years of relying on foreign supply.\n\nThe issue is particularly relevant for advanced reactors, which may require specialized fuels such as HALEU. The U.S. government is already spending billions to rebuild domestic enrichment capacity, while companies including Centrus are developing additional production.\n\nFor investors, that could broaden the nuclear opportunity beyond reactor operators to uranium and fuel-cycle names such as Cameco Corp (NYSE:CCJ), Centrus Energy Corp. (NYSE:LEU) and Uranium Energy Corp. (AMEX:UEC), as demand for nuclear power increasingly puts pressure on fuel supply.\n\nAI Needs More Than Power\n\nLiebenberg says Big Tech and the U.S. government will need to help fund that broader infrastructure if the nuclear buildout is going to match rising electricity demand.\n\nThat creates an unusual second-order AI trade. The first wave of hyperscaler nuclear spending is helping secure power for data centers. The next question is whether some of that capital eventually moves upstream into uranium, enrichment and fuel manufacturing.\n\nFor investors, that could make the nuclear opportunity considerably broader than the reactor companies and uranium miners getting the most attention today. Google’s Loviisa deal secures the electricity; the emerging challenge is ensuring there is enough fuel infrastructure behind it to keep that electricity flowing.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia''s AI Boom Hits Its Next Challenge: Power\n\nPhoto Courtesy: ZikG on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'e2a913530d98f6acb9c71eb5c7c626bfb351639c','2026-09-17 14:51:25','2026-09-17 15:17:36.966246',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 14:51:25');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(348,'alpaca:61846415','benzinga','2026-09-17 14:47:42','Peter Schiff: Bitcoin Failed ''Digital Gold'' Test, Higher Yields Could Hurt BTC','Peter Schiff warns persistent inflation could push Treasury yields above 6%, pressuring stocks and Bitcoin while strengthening gold’s appeal.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61846415/peter-schiff-bitcoin-failed-digital-gold-test-higher-yields-could-hurt-btc','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-17 15:17:45.360132','other','bearish',2,3,'days',1,'Schiff''s comments suggest negative sentiment around Bitcoin due to macroeconomic factors.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 77563.640625}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.468}}','2026-09-18 15:21:30.157679','2026-09-17 15:17:36.984056','61846415',replace('Longtime Bitcoin critic Peter Schiff sees persistently high inflation driving Treasury yields substantially higher, which could create pressure on stocks and cryptocurrencies while strengthening the case for gold.\n\nGold Vs. Bitcoin Debate Heats Up\n\nSchiff argued in an interview with Bitcoin Magazine on Sept. 16. that higher inflation ultimately strengthens gold’s investment case, even if expectations for Fed tightening create short-term volatility.\n\nGold has rebounded 2.4% following the Fed decision as traders reassess the outlook for inflation, interest rates and the dollar.  \n\nBitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC), Schiff contended, has failed to behave like "digital gold" and should increasingly be measured against gold rather than simply against the U.S. dollar.\n\nHe maintained his long-held view that the cryptocurrency lacks the underlying value that gives gold its monetary properties.\n\nWhy Higher Yields Could Hit BTC\n\nSchiff warned that persistently higher Treasury yields could pressure Bitcoin by making lower-risk assets more attractive and tightening financial conditions.\n\nWith the 10-year Treasury yield hovering around 5%, Schiff said yields could eventually climb above 6% if inflation remains elevated.\n\nA rate-driven stock market sell-off would be "very bearish" for Bitcoin and the broader crypto market and higher borrowing costs and tighter liquidity could further weigh on speculative assets.\n\nWhile Bitcoin has absorbed the Fed’s latest hike relatively well, Schiff cautioned that BTC may not digest further rate increases as well.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Holds $76,000 After Fed Hike: Why Is BTC Strong While Equities Fall?','\n',char(10)),'67223be0a5b7c8e0e28aa3d5e1cb24b0e5d848b9','2026-09-17 14:47:42','2026-09-17 15:17:36.966246',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 14:47:42');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(349,'alpaca:61845505','benzinga','2026-09-17 14:25:58','Huawei Takes Aim at Nvidia, AMD with Over 10 new AI Chipsets — But Can the Chinese Tech Giant Close the Gap?','Huawei unveils over 10 new AI chips, challenging Nvidia, AMD and Intel in the global AI infrastructure market.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61845505/huawei-takes-aim-at-nvidia-amd-with-over-10-new-ai-chipsets-but-can-the-chinese-tech-giant-close-the-gap','["AMD", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 15:17:49.082781','product','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Huawei launches new AI chips to compete with existing market players.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 459.75, "NVDA": 217.54}','{"AMD": {"60m": 18.495}, "NVDA": {"60m": 0.841}}','2026-09-18 15:21:30.157679','2026-09-17 15:17:36.987193','61845505',replace('Chinese tech giant Huawei unveiled over 10 new chipsets for AI computing infrastructure on Thursday in a bid to challenge Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA), Advanced Micro Devices (NASDAQ:AMD) and Intel Corp.‘s (NASDAQ:INTC) dominance in the market.\n\nThe new chipsets include next-generation AI accelerators, CPUs, and high-speed connectivity chips. Huawei’s rotating chairman, David Wang, stated that the company’s primary objective is to assist industries in establishing crucial AI infrastructure, providing an alternative for China and the world, Nikkei Asia reported. \n\nThe next-generation Ascend 960 DT AI accelerator is on track to launch officially in the first quarter of 2027, with development progressing ahead of schedule and performance expected to be twice that of its predecessor. The Ascend 960PR is slated for release in the third quarter of 2027.\n\nDuring his keynote at the annual Huawei Connect event in Shanghai, Wang highlighted the Ascend chip’s importance to the broader system and confirmed that Huawei plans to maintain a one-generation-per-year pace for Ascend product development.\n\nEric Xu, another rotating chairman at Huawei, stated that domestic demand significantly exceeds supply, causing the company to currently limit its aggressive expansion into international markets. However, Huawei is testing and providing limited supply to several countries with strong demand, Xu said.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAs Xi Jinping and Trump Meeting Looms, China''s Top Newspaper Accuses US of ''Naked Double Standards'' on AI Distillation\n\nNvidia Faces Pressure in China AI Chip Market\n\nThis move by Huawei comes as the competitive landscape in the AI chip industry heats up. Chinese AI chipmaker Enflame Technology, backed by Tencent Holdings Ltd. (OTC:TCEHY), saw a soaring debut in Shanghai, raising about $912 million in its initial public offering. Enflame is considered one of China’s "four little dragons" of AI chipmaking.\n\nMeanwhile, Nvidia has continued supplying China with limited batches of its H200 AI chips, with shipments approved for select customers in mainland China. ByteDance and Tencent Holdings have each received roughly 10,000 H200 processors over the past few weeks, while other Chinese technology companies could soon receive approval for shipments of a similar size\n\nVeteran technology analyst Dan Ives said Nvidia remains significantly ahead of Huawei in China, claiming even a lower-tier Nvidia chip is roughly year and a half to two years ahead of Huawei’s technology. He said semiconductor industry discussions suggest major Chinese tech companies would still choose Nvidia processors if given the option. Ives argued that this technological lead will be difficult for competitors to close as AI demand expands from large-language-model training into areas such as physical AI and autonomous systems.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nChina’s Nasdaq-Focused ETF Frenzy Sends Premiums to 24% as Investors Rush for US Stocks\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'66754ba2ce6d8c87f159f1c6edae27afb462ae2b','2026-09-17 14:25:58','2026-09-17 15:17:36.966246',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 14:25:58');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(350,'alpaca:61849239','benzinga','2026-09-17 16:02:07','QUICK SPARK: Generac Soars Nearly 20% on $8 Billion Amazon Data Center Deal','Generac opened 27.8% higher on a long-term generator supply agreement with Amazon, then eased to 19%. Initial deliveries total $2.4 billion.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61849239/generac-gnrc-stock-amazon-deal','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-17 16:17:57.806634','partnership','bullish',4,4,'days',1,'A significant long-term supply agreement with a major customer.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 254.92}','{"AMZN": {"60m": -1.467}}','2026-09-18 16:21:45.011219','2026-09-17 16:17:53.084071','61849239',replace('Generac Holdings Inc. (NYSE:GNRC) jumped 19.1% to $208.48 by late Thursday morning, pulling back modestly from an opening spike of 27.8% that had the stock poised for its best session ever.\n\nThe catalyst for the move is a long-term supply agreement to provide industrial backup generators for Amazon.com Inc.’s (NASDAQ:AMZN) global data center infrastructure. Initial deliveries total $2.4 billion across 2027 and 2028, with purchases potentially reaching $8 billion over the life of the deal.\n\nThe agreement reprices Generac from a hurricane-season consumer name into AI infrastructure. \n\nBackup power has become a binding constraint on data center buildouts, and Amazon just locked up years of capacity with one supplier.\n\nThe stock entered Thursday already up 41% over 30 days.\n\nQUICK CONTEXT: Generac Lands Amazon Data-Center Power Deal\n\nGenerac disclosed on Sept. 16 that it entered a long-term supply arrangement tied to Amazon data centers, marking a major expansion of its role in backup power for large computing facilities.\n\nUnder the filing, Generac issued Amazon.com NV Investment Holdings, an Amazon subsidiary, a warrant to buy up to 1.69 million Generac shares at $200.9266 each. About 307,954 shares vested immediately, while the rest vest as Amazon-related payments for data-center backup generators rise, up to $8 billion.\n\nThe first deliveries under the arrangement are expected to total $2.4 billion in 2027 and 2028. Generac said the warrant can be exercised through Sept. 16, 2033, and is subject to standard adjustment provisions.\n\nGenerac is a Wisconsin-based energy technology company founded in 1959. Its products include power generation equipment, energy storage systems, energy management devices and other power products for residential, commercial, data center, telecom, rental and industrial markets.\n\nThe deal matters because Generac has traditionally been associated with home and business backup generators, but data centers are becoming a larger power-reliability market as cloud and AI workloads increase the need for resilient electricity infrastructure.\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'a9be4267023f9ccc30fcd753f0874d3a9c211b03','2026-09-17 16:02:07','2026-09-17 16:17:53.078408',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 16:02:07');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(351,'alpaca:61848891','benzinga','2026-09-17 15:54:05','SpaceX Stock for Free? Board Member is Giving Away Shares to Early Backers','One of the biggest backers of SpaceX stock is giving away shares to early investors. Here&#39;s why.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61848891/spacex-stock-for-free-board-member-is-giving-away-shares-to-early-backers','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 16:17:59.020053','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses a giveaway of shares without detailing its potential market impact.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 356.12}','{"TSLA": {"60m": 2.786}}','2026-09-18 16:21:45.011219','2026-09-17 16:17:53.087428','61848891',replace('Early SpaceX (NASDAQ:SPCX) investor Antonio Gracias is turning his private equity company’s stake into profits for backers of the company through a donation of shares, a move that comes as the stock is soaring higher.\n\nSpaceX Investor Gives Away Shares\n\nThe SpaceX IPO helped make CEO Elon Musk the world’s first trillionaire. While he’s not worth a trillion dollars, Valor Equity Partners CEO and founder Antonio Gracias also has gained significant net worth in 2026 thanks to the public offering.\n\nGracias is worth an estimated $20.5 billion according to Bloomberg, ranking 127th on the Bloomberg Billionaires Index. The investor has added $5.82 billion in wealth in 2026.\n\nA Form4 filing from Gracias and Valor shows that the investor gave away around 8.5% of the company’s SpaceX holdings (42,790,223) shares. After the giveaway, Valor still owns 460,624,307 SpaceX shares, representing around 3.4% of the space company, as reported by Bloomberg.\n\nThe $8.5 billion in shares donated to early investors could be done for tax advantages and is meant to reward the investors in Valor Equity Partners who were early backers in the space company. The move allows investors in Valor Equity to take profits from the space company, while the private equity firm retains the majority of its SpaceX holdings.\n\nGracias currently serves on the Board of Directors of SpaceX and remains one of the largest shareholders with his large ownership stake in Valor Equity Partners.\n\nThe investor mentioned returning capital via distributions back in June prior to the IPO, according to Bloomberg.\n\nWhile Gracias is allowing some of the Valor investors the chance to take profits from the SpaceX IPO, he previously said he planned on holding the stock for the long term.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSpaceX Stock Faces a Risk That Keeps Coming Back in Waves\n\nBeliever in Elon Musk\n\nGracias was previously introduced to Musk via David Sacks. Valor began investing in SpaceX in 2008 and, by 2021, had invested around $400 million in the company.\n\nAlong with being one of the biggest backers of SpaceX, Gracias and Valor are also invested in Tesla Inc (NASDAQ:TSLA). Gracias was previously a member of the Tesla Board of Directors from 2007 to 2021, before stepping down.\n\nGracias and Valor also invested in Musk’s The Boring Company earlier this year.\n\nSpaceX Stock Price Action\n\nSpaceX stock is up 2.2% to $154.20 versus a 52-week trading range of $104.83 to $225.64. SpaceX stock hit its highest level since July 9 with Thursday’s stock gains.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSpaceX-Tesla Merger: Ron Baron Told Elon Musk ''Whatever You Decide… Is What I''m Going to Support''\n\nPhoto Courtesy: JOCA_PH on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'1ec5e2dd96b3f7dbfe8671ece0ff0960087a11e4','2026-09-17 15:54:05','2026-09-17 16:17:53.078408',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 15:54:05');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(352,'alpaca:61848172','benzinga','2026-09-17 15:38:04','Micron Jumps 5% as Intel CEO Says Memory Prices Have Surged Over 500%','Micron shares jumped as Intel CEO Lip-Bu Tan warned memory prices have surged five to seven times amid tight AI-driven supply.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61848172/micron-stock-memory-prices-intel-ai-shortage','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 16:18:00.256681','other','bullish',3,3,'hours',1,'Intel CEO''s remarks on memory prices boost sentiment for Micron''s shares.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 217.54}','{"NVDA": {"60m": 0.841}}','2026-09-18 16:21:45.011219','2026-09-17 16:17:53.091183','61848172',replace('Micron Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MU) jumped more than 5% Thursday as memory stocks rallied, two days after Intel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) CEO Lip-Bu Tan warned that the memory shortage could worsen next year.\n\nBarron’s reported that Tan’s comments helped drive the move. SK hynix Inc. (NASDAQ:SKHY) also gained about 5%, while the Nasdaq rose more than 1% as the broader market rallied following Wednesday’s Federal Reserve decision.\n\nMicron reports fiscal fourth-quarter results Sept. 30, when investors will get the next read on whether the memory shortage is still pushing prices and margins higher.\n\nPrediction traders remain bullish on the AI spending cycle supporting memory demand. Polymarket gives Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) about a 71% chance of ending 2026 as the world’s largest company, with more than $7 million traded.\n\nThat matters for Micron because Nvidia’s AI accelerators require large amounts of high-bandwidth memory, one of the tightest parts of the memory market. Micron CEO Sanjay Mehrotra said in June that supply should improve only gradually in 2028.\n\nTan Says Memory Pressure Could Worsen in 2027\n\nTan made the comments Tuesday at the AI Infrastructure Summit in Santa Clara.\n\nMemory chip prices have climbed between five and seven times as limited supply struggles to keep pace with AI demand, Tan said. He added that the bottleneck could worsen next year.\n\nThe warning echoes concerns across the memory industry. SK hynix CEO Kwak Noh-jung told Reuters in July that 2027 would be the worst year in the industry’s history for supply.\n\nTrendForce estimates server DRAM contract prices rose 64% in the second half of 2025 and could climb another 270% during 2026. Compounded, that would put prices at roughly six times their mid-2025 level by the end of 2026.\n\nWhy 2027 Matters for Micron\n\nMicron is already turning tight supply into sharply higher profits. Fiscal third-quarter revenue reached $41.46 billion, up from $9.30 billion a year earlier, while non-GAAP gross margin hit 84.9%. The company guided to roughly $50 billion in fourth-quarter revenue and an 86% gross margin.\n\nMicron said in June that 14 of its first 16 strategic customer agreements carried about $100 billion in minimum contracted revenue. The agreements use price bands designed to give Micron and customers more visibility through the memory cycle.\n\nHigh prices can eventually curb demand and encourage additional capacity. TrendForce nevertheless expects memory pricing to remain elevated in 2027 even as new supply comes online.\n\nYorkville America CEO Steve Neamtz told Benzinga this week that new factories capable of materially easing the memory shortage may not reach full production until 2028 or 2029. That timeline would leave Micron benefiting from tight supply well beyond 2027 if demand holds up.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nSpaceX Is Worth $2 Trillion. Why Does Its Stock Swing Like a Small-Cap?','\n',char(10)),'8a37fcccc18b85610ef26c0c0559e123b6f86860','2026-09-17 15:38:04','2026-09-17 16:17:53.078408',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 15:38:04');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(353,'alpaca:61848046','benzinga','2026-09-17 15:35:30','Meta''s Custom AI Chips Could Save It $8.5 Billion, Analyst Says','BofA reiterates Buy on Meta Platforms (NASDAQ: META) with an $810 price forecast, citing custom AI chip cost savings and the Meta One subscription launch.','https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/price-target/26/09/61848046/metas-custom-ai-chips-could-save-it-8-5-billion-analyst-says','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-17 16:18:01.866521','analyst','bullish',3,3,'weeks',1,'Analyst upgrade based on potential cost savings.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 578.53}','{"META": {"60m": 18.006}}','2026-09-18 16:21:45.011219','2026-09-17 16:17:53.094337','61848046',replace('Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) kept its Buy rating at BofA Securities in a research note on Wednesday, with the firm maintaining an $810 price forecast against a closing price of $673.31 that day, implying 20.3% upside.\n\nThe analysts said Meta’s artificial intelligence plans are advancing on two fronts at once: the chips that run its AI systems and the products that charge users for them. BofA identified five potential catalysts for the stock earlier this year and said three have now been announced.\n\nCustom Chips Could Cut Infrastructure Costs\n\nCiting a Bloomberg report, BofA said Meta plans to deploy third-generation MTIA 450 chips, known as Arke, in the first half of 2027, followed by the higher-performance MTIA 500, or Astrid, from late 2027. The chips are developed with Broadcom Inc. (NASDAQ:AVGO) and built for AI inference — the stage where a trained model answers user requests. Meta expects to deploy more than one gigawatt of custom-chip capacity over 12 months, which BofA estimates costs upward of $8 billion.\n\nThe Math Behind The Savings Estimate\n\nBofA modeled Meta deploying 5-6 gigawatts of owned capacity in 2027 at a cost of $200 billion, with chips making up 60% of that. At a 40% saving versus third-party chips, the firm calculated roughly $8.5 billion in savings. The analysts called custom silicon “strategically important” to Meta’s AI roadmap, pointing to Alphabet Inc.‘s (NASDAQ:GOOGL) (NASDAQ:GOOG) results with its own processors. Bloomberg also reported Meta canceled a combined training-and-inference chip after concluding the design could cost about 30% more.\n\nMeta One Subscription Adds A Revenue Line\n\nMeta launched Meta One globally with more than 50 features, bundling higher AI usage limits, customization and creator tools. Consumer plans range from $2.99 per month for individual apps to $19.99 for a premium bundle; creator and business tiers range from $14.99 to $499. Meta said existing subscription offerings have drawn 15 million subscribers and trials.\n\nWhat Each Percentage Point Is Worth\n\nBofA called that figure a constructive early demand signal and used Snapchat Plus penetration of about 5.5% of daily users as a benchmark. Assuming global average revenue per user of roughly $10 a month, each 1% conversion — about 36 million users — could add approximately $4.3 billion in annual revenue, or 1.2% above consensus 2028 estimates.\n\nRemaining Catalysts\n\nTwo catalysts remain: the Connect conference and the Watermelon model launch. BofA does not expect significant AI news at Connect but said a frontier-level Watermelon language model could support expectations for advertising system improvements and API licensing fees. \n\nThe $810 price forecast is based on 24 times 2027 estimated GAAP earnings per share. Listed risks include advertising revenue’s sensitivity to the economy, AI spending pressure on margins, reduced cost flexibility from a larger fixed-asset base and competition for users and ad budgets.\n\nMETA Stock Price Activity: Meta Platforms shares are trading higher by 0.31% at $675.37 at the time of publication on Thursday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'12a0307895542dd6103a1923a2311553577c3fc8','2026-09-17 15:35:30','2026-09-17 16:17:53.078408',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 15:35:30');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(354,'alpaca:61847834','benzinga','2026-09-17 15:28:47','Nvidia Is an ‘Awesome Company,’ but Its Stock Is Priced as ‘Greatest Company Ever,’ Damodaran Says','Aswath Damodaran says Nvidia is an “awesome company” but warns its valuation assumes extraordinary AI growth.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61847834/nvidia-stock-valuation-aswath-damodaran-ai-growth','["AAPL", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 16:18:03.029539','analyst','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst comments suggest overvaluation concerns for Nvidia''s stock.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 325.14, "NVDA": 217.54}','{"AAPL": {"60m": 3.675}, "NVDA": {"60m": 0.841}}','2026-09-18 16:21:45.011219','2026-09-17 16:17:53.097666','61847834',replace('Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) is worth over $5 trillion after another year of explosive growth, but NYU Stern finance professor Aswath Damodaran says the stock still asks investors to assume an extraordinary payoff from the artificial intelligence boom.\n\n“Nvidia is an awesome company, but it’s being priced as the greatest company ever,” Damodaran said on the BiggerPockets Money podcast Tuesday.\n\nDamodaran bought Nvidia in 2018 at a split-adjusted $1.80 a share and later sold down the position in stages, with Benzinga reporting in January that he had fully exited. Nvidia now trades at more than 100 times his original cost basis.\n\nThe AI Revenue Bar Gets Higher\n\nIn January, while discussing investment in large language models, Damodaran said AI would eventually need roughly $2 trillion to $4 trillion in revenue to justify the capital pouring into the sector.\n\nHis new estimate is much larger, though it covers the broader AI infrastructure buildout.\n\nDamodaran puts current AI product and service revenue at roughly $250 billion a year. Against more than $2 trillion already invested in AI infrastructure, he estimates those revenues may eventually need to reach $8 trillion to $10 trillion annually to justify the buildout, roughly 32 to 40 times today’s level.\n\nDamodaran argues AI only gets close to that scale if it moves beyond helping workers and starts replacing them. If AI remains primarily a productivity tool, he estimates the potential market at closer to $2 trillion.\n\nCompanies worldwide pay roughly $26 trillion a year in wages and other employee compensation, according to Damodaran. Replacing part of that labor could open a much larger market for AI agents, but it also creates a problem: displaced workers lose the income they use to buy goods and services.\n\n“What are all these companies that have replaced their employees with agents? Who are they going to sell this stuff to?” Damodaran said.\n\nTraders See Nvidia Staying on Top\n\n“Nvidia’s already made its money,” Damodaran said. He called the chipmaker a beneficiary of the spending boom and compared the cycle to musical chairs: “Nvidia doesn’t want the music to stop.”\n\nThe current numbers show why investors remain willing to pay up. Nvidia’s latest quarterly results showed revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, while Data Center revenue jumped 117% to $89 billion.\n\nNear-term prediction markets aren’t pricing a major reversal.\n\nPolymarket gives Nvidia a 71% chance of finishing 2026 as the world’s largest company, versus 20% for Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL), with more than $7.3 million traded.\n\nNvidia’s roughly $5.17 trillion market value leads Apple’s $4.85 trillion by about $320 billion, so a relative move of around 6% would flip the ranking.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nSteve Eisman Calls AI ''Terminator'' Fears ''Garbage'': If You''re Scared, ''Postpone Your IPO''','\n',char(10)),'9c09353e0b58fbe85ad0650d0076689896f7040e','2026-09-17 15:28:47','2026-09-17 16:17:53.078408',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 15:28:47');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(355,'alpaca:61851209','benzinga','2026-09-17 17:03:55','XRP Up 3% as Ripple Adds XRP Payments to Stripe, Tempo’s AI Standard','XRP gains as Ripple adds XRPL support for Stripe-Tempo’s AI payment protocol, enabling agent payments in XRP, RLUSD and tokens. Traders watch $1.30','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61851209/xrp-up-3-as-ripple-adds-xrp-payments-to-stripe-tempos-ai-standard','["XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-17 17:18:12.253269','partnership','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Ripple''s integration with Stripe-Tempo enhances XRP''s utility.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"XRP/USD": 1.30371}','{"XRP/USD": {"60m": -0.625}}','2026-09-18 17:21:59.924014','2026-09-17 17:18:07.607027','61851209',replace('XRP (CRYPTO: XRP) gained Thursday as Ripple expanded the XRP Ledger into AI-driven payments, adding XRP support to the Machine Payments Protocol co-authored by Stripe and Tempo.\n\nWhy XRP, RLUSD Could Be Top Developer Choices\n\nRipple released version 1.1 of its XRP Ledger AI Starter Kit, adding support for the Machine Payments Protocol (MPP) and the Open Wallet Standard.\n\nMPP is an open standard developed by Stripe and Tempo that allows AI agents to pay for online services without traditional accounts or checkout flows.\n\nThe integration makes XRPL a settlement option within MPP, allowing AI agents to make single payments using XRP, issued assets such as Ripple USD (CRYPTO: RLUSD) and Multi-Purpose Tokens.\n\nXRP also supports MPP session payments through XRPL Payment Channels.\n\nStablecoin-based session payments are not yet available and depend on a proposed XRPL upgrade.\n\n"Agentic payments will be multi-platform and multi-rail," RippleX Head of Product Jazzi Cooper said, adding that Ripple’s goal is to make XRP and RLUSD "first-class options wherever developers are building."\n\nWill XRP Hold $1.30?\n\nXRP traded around $1.30 on Thursday after suffering a sell-off earlier this week.\n\nTrader Cryptollica highlighted an extreme momentum reading, saying XRP’s two-week relative strength index has fallen to its lowest level in the 13-year chart history.\n\nIt is below the readings recorded during the 2018 bear market, the 2020 COVID crash and the 2022 downturn.\n\nDespite the deeply oversold reading, the trader noted that XRP remains above its long-term rising structure.\n\nCryptollica argued that the combination of washed-out momentum and intact long-term support could become significant if the structure continues to hold.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nXRP Could Crater If the CLARITY Act Vote Fails—Here''s Why','\n',char(10)),'dce81d45aa790bfd0669e3d18c3589c64a178492','2026-09-17 17:03:55','2026-09-17 17:18:07.601029',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 17:03:55');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(356,'alpaca:61851205','benzinga','2026-09-17 17:03:50','Lucid Stock Gains on Bolt Deal To Deploy Autonomous Vehicles','Lucid shares rise about 10% after partnering with Bolt to develop and deploy SAE Level 4 autonomous mobility services across Europe.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61851205/lucid-stock-gains-on-bolt-deal-to-deploy-autonomous-vehicles','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 17:18:13.463294','partnership','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'The partnership with Bolt suggests growth potential for Lucid''s autonomous vehicle services.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 217.54}','{"NVDA": {"60m": 0.841}}','2026-09-18 17:21:59.924014','2026-09-17 17:18:07.611836','61851205',replace('Lucid Group, Inc. (NASDAQ:LCID) shares are trading higher by about 10% on Thursday. \n\nThe company disclosed a strategic partnership with European shared mobility platform Bolt to develop and deploy SAE Level 4 autonomous mobility services across Europe.\n\nLucid And Bolt Partner On Autonomous Vehicle Fleet In Europe\n\nUsing vehicles based on Lucid’s upcoming Midsize platform, Bolt plans to deploy at least 25,000 fully autonomous vehicles across multiple European cities and countries, supporting its goal of 100,000 autonomous vehicles on its platform by 2035.\n\n The vehicles are expected to use NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) Hyperion, a production-ready autonomous vehicle architecture combining high-performance computing and a standardized sensor suite.\n\nRead Also:\n\nLucid Stock in Focus Friday Following Major NHTSA Recall Announcement\n\nLucid Technologies will lead the partnership for Lucid, bringing together its AI, ADAS, autonomy and digital capabilities. \n\nBolt Autonomous Driving Solutions will oversee vehicle requirements, software, safety, rider experience, fleet infrastructure, operating systems and city partnerships, with plans to own and operate the fleet. \n\nThe companies will also work with technology partners, regulators and policymakers to support the safe and scalable rollout of autonomous mobility services across Europe.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nLCID Technical Outlook: Trend Still Bearish, Momentum Improving\n\nEven after Thursday’s pop, LCID is still in a longer-term downtrend: it’s trading 5.8% below the $4.70 20-day SMA, 24.7% below the $5.87 50-day SMA, and 45.6% below the $8.13 200-day SMA. The bearish structure is reinforced by the 20-day SMA sitting below the 50-day SMA, and the 50-day SMA sitting below the 200-day SMA.\n\nMomentum is the more interesting part of the setup right now: MACD is above its signal line and the histogram is positive, which points to improving upside pressure versus the prior downswing. In plain English, when MACD is above its signal line, it suggests sellers are losing control even if price hasn’t reclaimed key longer-term averages yet.\n\nKey Resistance: $4.70 — a direct test of the 20-day SMA area that the stock is still trading below\n\nKey Support: $4.45 — the current price zone, which often acts as a near-term "line in the sand" after a sharp intraday move\n\nLCID Earnings Preview And Analyst Price Targets\n\nLooking further out, the next major catalyst for the stock arrives with the November 4, 2026 (estimated) earnings report.\n\nEPS Estimate: $-2.38 (Up from $-2.65 YoY)\n\nRevenue Estimate: $430.64 million (Up from $336.58 million YoY)\n\nAnalyst Consensus & Recent Actions: The stock carries a Hold rating with an average price forecast of $10.20. Recent analyst moves include:\n\nCitigroup: Buy (Lowers Target to $11.00) (Aug. 19)\n\nRBC Capital: Sector Perform (Lowers Target to $7.00) (July 13)\n\nCitigroup: Buy (Lowers Target to $14.00) (May 15)\n\nLCID Price Action: Lucid Group shares were up 8.04% at $4.36 at the time of publication on Thursday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'ae44b0c6d0c988d514313db8a8b4d30e35de35c8','2026-09-17 17:03:50','2026-09-17 17:18:07.601029',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 17:03:51');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(357,'alpaca:61850950','benzinga','2026-09-17 16:55:27','Why Is BitMine Stock Surging on Thursday?','BitMine Immersion Technologies stock rebounded Thursday following gains in Ethereum and a detailed treasury update from Eightco Holdings.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61850950/why-is-bitmine-stock-surging-on-thursday-2','["ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-17 17:18:14.766551','other','bullish',2,3,'days',1,'Stock price increase attributed to broader market trends and company updates.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"ETH/USD": 2414.179931640625}','{"ETH/USD": {"60m": 1.307}}','2026-09-18 17:21:59.924014','2026-09-17 17:18:07.615500','61850950',replace('BitMine Immersion Technologies Inc. (NYSE:BMNR) stock is trading higher on Thursday following a gain in Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH), which rose 1.49% to $2,450.60 over the last 24 hours. The movement follows Wednesday’s decline in BMNR stock amid broader sector pressure tied to the U.S. Senate’s vote against advancing the Clarity Act.\n\nEightco Discloses Holdings\n\nEightco Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:ORBS) backed by BitMine Immersion provided an update on its total holdings on Thursday, Eightco reported total assets of approximately $380 million. Eightco reported holding a $90 million indirect investment in OpenAI, an $18 million investment in Beast Industries, a $1 million stake in Mythical Games, 301,971,219 Worldcoin tokens valued at 37 cents each, 16,278 Ethereum and approximately $120 million in cash and stablecoins. Eightco also repurchased over 26 million shares of common stock this quarter.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: Google Is Racing to Secure Nuclear Power for AI—The Fuel Problem Comes Next\n\nTechnical Analysis\n\nFrom a trend perspective, BMNR is still in "rebuild mode" after a steep 12-month slide of 58.66%, but the intermediate trend has improved as price holds above the 50-day, 100-day, and 200-day moving averages. The stock is trading 17.7% above its 50-day SMA ($20.05) and 6.8% above its 200-day SMA ($22.10), which typically keeps dip-buyers engaged.\n\nNear-term, the stock is bumping into overhead friction: it’s trading 2.6% below the 20-day SMA ($24.24), a common spot where rallies can pause while the market decides whether momentum can re-accelerate. The 20-day SMA is also above the 50-day SMA (bullish), but the longer-term "death cross" from January (50-day below the 200-day) is still a reminder that the bigger-picture trend only recently stabilized.\n\nRSI is the cleaner momentum read right now, sitting at 53.55, which points to neutral momentum rather than an overbought or oversold extreme.\n\nKey Resistance: $27 — a nearby round-number zone that can act as an overhead supply area if the rebound extends\n\nKey Support: $23 — a close-by floor near the current price where buyers may defend the recent range\n\nTop ETF Exposure\n\nBitMine has significant exposure across several crypto-focused ETFs, including the Corgi Crypto Infrastructure ETF (NASDAQ:BLCK) at a 5.87% weight, the Bitwise Crypto Industry Innovators ETF (NYSE:BITQ) at 7.00%, and the Global X Blockchain ETF (NASDAQ:BKCH) at 9.97%. Given BMNR’s sizable allocations in these funds, substantial ETF inflows or outflows could create additional buying or selling pressure on the stock as fund managers adjust their holdings.\n\nBMNR Stock Price Activity: BitMine Immersion shares are trading higher by 5.72% at $23.52 at the time of publication on Thursday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMark Kelly Calls for Reversal of Trump’s Healthcare Cuts: ''Making Sure Every American Can Afford Quality Care''\n\nPhoto: PJ McDonnell / Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'cc6fd33a9c9fd401331ba2a0a24784d79ffe36f2','2026-09-17 16:55:27','2026-09-17 17:18:07.601029',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 16:55:27');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(358,'alpaca:61850736','benzinga','2026-09-17 16:45:41','What''s Going On With Apple Stock Today?','Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL) shares are trading higher Thursday, extending a push toward the stock&#39;s 52-week high as fresh data shows Apple gaining smartphone market share.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61850736/whats-going-on-with-apple-stock-today-5','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-17 17:18:15.618347','other','bullish',2,2,'hours',1,'Headline questions the stock''s movement without confirming specific events.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 325.14}','{"AAPL": {"60m": 3.675}}','2026-09-18 17:21:59.924014','2026-09-17 17:18:07.620013','61850736',replace('Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL) shares are trading higher Thursday, extending a push toward the stock’s 52-week high as fresh data shows Apple gaining smartphone market share.\n\nApple stock is trading near recent highs. What should traders watch with AAPL?\n\nApple Gains Ground as Rivals Raise Prices\n\nCounterpoint Research data shows Apple’s phone shipments climbing 13% from a year earlier, pushing its share of the global smartphone market to an all-time high of 21% for the quarter.\n\nAnalysts at the firm credited that surge largely to strong consumer appetite for the iPhone 17 lineup. Notably, Apple stood alone among the major phone makers in holding the line on pricing, even as rising memory chip costs pushed competitors to raise theirs.\n\nBofA also said in a note on Thursday that phone carrier promotions are acting as a tailwind for iPhone upgrades, which should help offset higher prices on new iPhones. The analyst firm expects the Duo release and Siri AI to help drive increased interest in upgrading, leading to a strong upgrade cycle.\n\nApple’s Chart Shows a Clean Uptrend Nearing Resistance\n\nFrom a technical perspective, every major trend indicator lines up in Apple’s favor right now, with the 20-day average recently crossing above the 50-day, and the 50-day comfortably above the 200-day. Apple stock is currently trading above all key moving averages with shares roughly 4% higher than the 20-day benchmark near $321 and about 17% above the 200-day mark closer to $286, a lineup that gives a remarkably clear read on where momentum currently points.\n\nMomentum-wise, MACD is above its signal line, which points to improving upside pressure versus the prior downswing. When MACD is above the signal line it suggests buyers are gaining control and pullbacks are getting absorbed faster.\n\nKey resistance for Apple sits at the 52-week high of $344.57. A break above that level could lead to price discovery at higher share prices, whereas a failure at the highs could turn into a short-term "double-top" style stall.\n\nAAPL Price Action: Apple shares were up 0.98% at $335.69 at the time of publication on Thursday. The stock is approaching its 52-week high of $344.56, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nElon Musk’s X And SpaceXAI Dropped Apple From Their Antitrust Fight Without Explaining Why — Now a Federal Judge Wants to See the Deal\n\nImage: sdx15/Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'fd0ef175d555eb713ea9d6d39b97ae2a9bd6057e','2026-09-17 16:45:41','2026-09-17 17:18:07.601029',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 16:45:41');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(359,'alpaca:61850690','benzinga','2026-09-17 16:44:47','SpaceX Adds $100B in One Day—That’s More Than Two Rocket Labs','SpaceX gains $100 billion to reach a $2 trillion market cap on Starship launch hopes, dwarfing Rocket Lab amid volatility and lockup risks.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61850690/spacex-adds-100b-in-one-day-thats-more-than-two-rocket-labs','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-17 17:18:17.485860','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Significant market cap increase reported, but driven by speculation and hopes.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 254.92}','{"AMZN": {"60m": -1.467}}','2026-09-18 17:21:59.924014','2026-09-17 17:18:07.623798','61850690',replace('SpaceX (NASDAQ:SPCX) gained about $100 billion in market value Wednesday. Two and a half times the market cap of Rocket Lab Corp. (NASDAQ:RKLB), which gained in a single session.\n\nThe rocket and satellite company closed at $150.88 per share, up 5.15% from Tuesday’s $143.49 finish, lifting its market capitalization to roughly $2 trillion.\n\nRocket Lab, the closest thing the sector has to a pure-play public rival, carries a market cap of about $38.1 billion. One day of SpaceX tape swallowed more than two of them. \n\nSPCX stock is moving. See the real-time price action here. \n\nWhat Moved the Stock\n\nTwo catalysts sit behind the bid. SpaceX is targeting Sept. 22 for Starship Flight 14, the vehicle’s first fully orbital attempt and the first mission meant to deploy third-generation Starlink satellites at a cadence Falcon 9 cannot match. \n\nRead Also:\n\n''This Selloff Makes Zero Sense'': An Analysis from WallStreetBets\n\nSuccess would validate the economics underpinning a $2 trillion valuation, while failure would do the opposite. \n\nPassive demand is the second leg. Elon Musk‘s SpaceX entered the Nasdaq-100 on July 7, less than a month after its debut, one of the fastest inclusions ever under Nasdaq’s revised fast-entry rules, and J.P. Morgan estimated the addition could pull in $4.3 billion of passive flows. Index weight updates keep forcing benchmarked funds to buy.\n\nVolatility Is the Baseline Here\n\nNothing about a $100 billion day is unusual for SpaceX. Shares priced at $135, jumped 19% on their June 12 debut to a market value near $2.1 trillion, and vaulted past Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) within days as newly listed options fueled a trading frenzy. \n\nThen came the giveback, when more than $1 trillion in market value was shed through early August. The 52-week range runs from $104.83 to $225.64, per Benzinga Pro market data. \n\nSupply remains the overhang traders watch. Lockup restrictions lifting through Dec. 8 will raise the tradable float to 40% of the company, with the remaining 60%, including Musk’s stake, locked until mid-2027. \n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nSPCX Price Action\n\nSPCX Stock Price Activity: SpaceX stock was up 1.98% at $153.87 at the time of publication Thursday, according to market data from Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nThese 10 Stocks Are Squeeze Candidates Waiting to Happen\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'f4039643ae57fd2c7d8f34d171693a899b88e15b','2026-09-17 16:44:47','2026-09-17 17:18:07.601029',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 16:44:47');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(360,'alpaca:61850431','benzinga','2026-09-17 16:35:41','Amazon Is Coming After Walmart’s Biggest Delivery Advantage','Amazon eyes a 10x same-day delivery boost via Project Mercury to counter Walmart. BofA sets a $320 target with a Buy rating.','https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/reiteration/26/09/61850431/amazon-is-coming-after-walmarts-biggest-delivery-advantage','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-17 17:18:18.495082','product','bullish',3,3,'weeks',1,'Amazon''s initiative could improve its competitive position in delivery services.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 254.92}','{"AMZN": {"60m": -1.467}}','2026-09-18 17:21:59.924014','2026-09-17 17:18:07.626879','61850431',replace('Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) could dramatically expand its same-day delivery network as it takes aim at a key advantage held by Walmart Inc. (NASDAQ:WMT), according to Bank of America analyst Justin Post.\n\nPost reiterated a Buy rating on the stock with a $320 price forecast. He said the company’s proposed Project Mercury could expand its same-day delivery footprint more than tenfold.\n\nAmazon Targets 1,000-Plus Same-Day Facilities\n\nCiting a Business Insider report, Post said Amazon is considering expanding its Sub Same-Day fulfillment network to more than 1,000 facilities by 2031 from 85 today.\n\nThe facilities stock about 90,000 of Amazon’s fastest-selling products. That includes household essentials, Fresh items and medicines.\n\nAmazon estimates a three-year investment of $6.8 billion could generate $7.1 billion in economic value over 10 years. The project could become cash-flow positive by 2030.\n\nTaking On Walmart’s Delivery Advantage\n\nBank of America said the expansion could help Amazon challenge Walmart’s proximity advantage.\n\nWalmart uses about 5,000 stores to support rapid fulfillment. Its network puts fast delivery within 10 miles of 90% of the U.S. population.\n\nProject Mercury could put the company’s same-day capacity within 10 miles of 80% of U.S. Prime members by 2031.\n\nPost said the direct financial returns from Mercury appear modest. However, he views the project as strategically important. The $6.8 billion investment would represent less than 5% of Bank of America’s estimated annual Amazon retail capital spending.\n\nThe analyst also expects the company’s denser fulfillment network and continued automation to support retail margin improvement for several years. He added that progress across AWS, chips and Bedrock leaves Amazon positioned to benefit from AI in both cloud computing and retail.\n\nAMZN Stock Price Activity: Amazon.com shares were up 2.30% at $251.61 at the time of publication on Thursday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: Google Is Racing to Secure Nuclear Power for AI—The Fuel Problem Comes Next','\n',char(10)),'65cb7c8d3e554b301efd4c76ed6f82119a0da42e','2026-09-17 16:35:41','2026-09-17 17:18:07.601029',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 16:35:41');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(361,'alpaca:61849887','benzinga','2026-09-17 16:19:05','Snap Just Turned Its $2,195 Glasses Into an Nvidia AI Story','Snap&#39;s $2,195 SPECS glasses are bringing Nvidia&#39;s AI stack into the workplace, opening a new frontier for AI agents and edge computing.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/09/61849887/snap-nvidia-ai-glasses','["AMZN", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 17:18:19.500482','product','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Integration of Nvidia AI into Snap''s new product could enhance demand and interest.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 254.92, "NVDA": 217.54}','{"AMZN": {"60m": -1.467}, "NVDA": {"60m": 0.841}}','2026-09-18 16:21:45.011219','2026-09-17 17:18:07.630143','61849887',replace('Snap Inc. (NYSE:SNAP) $2,195 SPECS glasses are being pitched as a new computer, not another pair of smart glasses. \n\nThat distinction matters for Nvidia Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA): Snap is putting Nvidia’s AI stack inside a wearable designed to understand the physical world, potentially creating a new edge-AI workload as companies move AI agents from screens into factories, stores and field operations.\n\nNvidia Meets Physical AI\n\nSnap announced partnerships with Nvidia, Salesforce, Inc. (NYSE:CRM) and Amazon.com, Inc‘s (NASDAQ:AMZN) Amazon Web Services on Wednesday to bring SPECS into enterprise environments. Nvidia will bring agents built on its XR AI stack to the glasses, allowing them to interpret a worker’s surroundings and provide real-time guidance.\n\nThat is where the Nvidia connection becomes more interesting than a simple technology partnership.\n\nNvidia’s XR AI framework is designed to combine live camera and microphone inputs with AI models, enterprise tools and agent orchestration across cloud, data-center, workstation and edge environments. \n\nIn other words, it is built for AI that can perceive what is happening around a user and respond to it. SPECS gives that architecture a physical interface.\n\nRead Also:\n\nApple''s AI Pin Vs China''s AI Pendants: The Wearable Arms Race Begins\n\nFrom Chatbots to AI Agents\n\nSnap’s enterprise examples show where the opportunity could develop. Salesforce’s Agentforce can help workers identify objects, retrieve information and update workflows through the glasses, while AWS is connecting its AI assistant to tasks such as checking inventory. Trifork and Hololight are developing applications for remote technical support and spatial workstations.\n\nFor Nvidia, the significance is not necessarily how many SPECS Snap sells. It is whether AR glasses become another endpoint where AI agents need continuous visual understanding and inference.\n\nNvidia has already been pushing that broader thesis. Its XR AI platform is designed for agents that can process video, audio and spatial context, reason about the next action and interact with enterprise software.\n\nSPECS could therefore become an early test of that vision outside the traditional data center.\n\nThe Bigger AI Bet\n\nSnap has priced SPECS at $2,195, with shipping expected later this fall in the U.S., U.K. and France. The company is also introducing SPECS Intelligence, an anticipatory AI service designed to understand users’ goals, routines and priorities across iPhone, Mac and the glasses.\n\nThat gives Snap a much bigger ambition than selling hardware. CEO Evan Spiegel has described SPECS as a computer that puts computing into the world rather than asking people to look down at a screen.\n\nFor Nvidia investors, the key question is whether that vision catches on across enterprise environments. If it does, glasses could represent another class of AI endpoint — and another reason the AI infrastructure story may eventually extend well beyond data centers.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia''s AI Boom Hits Its Next Challenge: Power\n\nShutterstock AI Generator','\n',char(10)),'c5eca6f2f03b7cd945462973be0a9d9af41b9d58','2026-09-17 16:19:05','2026-09-17 17:18:07.601029',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 16:19:05');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(362,'alpaca:61853199','benzinga','2026-09-17 18:11:42','Why Is IonQ Stock Surging Thursday?','IonQ (NYSE: IONQ) surged 9% following award-winning quantum research with NVIDIA and Synopsys. Read the full analysis.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61853199/why-is-ionq-stock-surging-thursday','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 18:18:28.438980','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'IonQ experienced a notable stock increase due to recognition of its research efforts.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 217.54}','{"NVDA": {"60m": 0.841}}','2026-09-18 18:22:14.902217','2026-09-17 18:18:24.103916','61853199',replace('IonQ Inc. (NYSE:IONQ) stock rose more than 9% Thursday after the quantum computing company detailed two research breakthroughs. A broader rally in technology stocks also supported the move.The Nasdaq gained 1.68%, while the S&P; 500 rose 1.13%.IonQ Teams With NVIDIA, SynopsysIonQ said its research presented at IEEE Quantum Week 2026 in Toronto showed potential gains in industrial simulation and quantum optimization.The company published joint research with Synopsys Inc. (NASDAQ:SNPS). The study showed that adding a quantum algorithm to Synopsys’ Ansys LS-DYNA software cut industrial simulation processing times by up to 14.6%.The approach could help reduce computing bottlenecks in complex simulations, including crash tests and jet engine modeling.In separate research announced Wednesday, IonQ worked with Oak Ridge National Laboratory, NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) and the University of Tennessee, Knoxville.The researchers used generative AI to create quantum optimization circuits directly. The method removes a time-consuming parameter-tuning process.Tests using NVIDIA H200 GPUs and the CUDA-Q platform kept circuit-generation time near 28 seconds as problems became larger. The previous method increased from 34 seconds to more than 11 minutes.Both studies won Best Paper Awards at IEEE Quantum Week 2026.Technical AnalysisIonQ is trading about 3% above its 20-day SMA of $39.43 and 50-day SMA of $39.37. However, it remains 14% below its 100-day SMA of $47.22 and 7.5% below its 200-day SMA of $43.89.The RSI stands at 52.21, indicating neutral momentum.The 20-day SMA remains above the 50-day SMA. However, the 50-day SMA is still below the 200-day SMA following an August death cross.Resistance sits near $44.50, close to the 200-day moving-average area. Support is near $37.Analyst OutlookIonQ carries a Buy consensus rating and an average price forecast of $67.75 across 15 analysts.Mizuho maintained an Outperform rating on Sept. 9 and lowered its price forecast to $52. Rosenblatt maintained Buy with a $100 forecast, while Needham maintained Buy with a $65 forecast.Benzinga Edge RankingsIonQ has a Momentum score of 8.09 on the Benzinga Edge scorecard. The weak score suggests Thursday’s rally has yet to reverse the stock’s softer longer-term momentum profile.IonQ shares remain down 37.92% over the past 12 months.ETF ExposureIonQ has a 15.79% weighting in the Corgi Quantum Computing 2x Daily ETF (NASDAQ:XQTM) and a 5.55% weighting in the WisdomTree Quantum Computing Fund ETF (NASDAQ:WQTM). The State Street SPDR FactSet Innovative Technology ETF (NYSE:XITK) has a 1.70% weighting in IonQ.Price ActionIONQ Stock Price Activity: IonQ shares were up 9.47% at $40.33 at the time of publication Thursday, according to Benzinga Pro data.Image via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBond King Jeffrey Gundlach Wants Out of the AI ''Epicenter'': Inside His Zero-Exposure Portfolio','\n',char(10)),'4d6f5d6831b79cc4e613c91565a3fbaa7a46967e','2026-09-17 18:11:42','2026-09-17 18:18:24.099730',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 18:11:42');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(363,'alpaca:61852525','benzinga','2026-09-17 17:50:56','Bitcoin''s Fair Value Is Around $105,000, Rise Is ''Programmed,'' Mark Yusko Says','Mark Yusko says Bitcoin’s halving-driven scarcity and rising adoption create a built-in price escalator, with BTC undervalued near $75,000 and Oct. 5 pivotal.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61852525/bitcoins-fair-value-is-around-105000-rise-is-programmed-mark-yusko-says','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-17 18:18:30.258800','analyst','bullish',3,3,'weeks',1,'Analyst provides a price target indicating potential for upside.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 77563.640625}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.369}}','2026-09-18 18:22:14.902217','2026-09-17 18:18:24.107163','61852525',replace('Morgan Creek Capital founder and CEO Mark Yusko on Wednesday said Bitcoin‘s (CRYPTO: BTC) long-term appreciation is effectively built into the network as adoption expands and new supply keeps falling.\n\nYusko argues that BTC remains undervalued despite its evolution from a speculative trade toward a global store of value.\n\nWhy Yusko Sees BTC Having a “Built-In Escalator“\n\nSpeaking in a Bitcoin Magazine interview, Yusko made the case Bitcoin’s four-year cycle is rooted in its programmed supply schedule rather than speculation alone.\n\n"If that happened and nothing changed, half the miners would go out of business," Yusko said. "So what happens is naturally the price has a built-in escalator."\n\nHe pointed to a network-value model from Timothy Peterson, which currently estimates Bitcoin’s fair value at roughly $105,000.\n\n"It’s about $105,000, but it’s $75,000. Great. So it’s on sale," Yusko said.\n\nHe described Bitcoin’s market cycle as moving through several phases.\n\nLong-term investors accumulate below perceived fair value,\n\nTraders arrive as momentum builds,\n\nMiners hedge once prices exceed production costs\n\nAnd leveraged speculation eventually pushes prices above fundamentals. \n\nThat final stage, Yusko argued, creates the conditions for sharp corrections.\n\nYusko Sees Bitcoin Adoption Growing\n\nYusko sees Bitcoin as a store of value and “better form of money” because its scarcity, portability and divisibility offer advantages over gold.\n\nHe argues its long-term appreciation partly reflects currency debasement and says its low historical correlation with stocks and bonds can make it a portfolio diversifier.\n\nYusko believes the next stage of adoption as moving from the "fringe" through early adopters and now toward the early majority. They are the investors treating Bitcoin as a long-term wealth-preservation asset alongside gold.\n\nWhile institutional derivatives could increasingly influence prices, Yusko says Bitcoin ultimately does not depend on legislation such as the Clarity Act because it can be owned and transferred without permission.\n\nYusko highlighted Oct. 5 as a date to watch, noting it marks 364 days since the previous cycle peak.\n\nHe said the previous three Bitcoin cycles reached a similar transition point precisely 364 days after their respective peaks.\n\n"By Oct.5, it’s likely that we head back toward the accumulation phase of the cycle," Yusko said.\n\nHe also said higher interest rates could curb excessive leverage and make Bitcoin’s boom-and-bust cycles less extreme.\n\nYusko expects percentage gains to shrink as Bitcoin’s market cap grows. However, expanding network adoption will continue driving long-term value appreciation.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nPeter Schiff: Bitcoin Failed ''Digital Gold'' Test, Higher Yields Could Hurt BTC','\n',char(10)),'2677cd9e037dd9d81eaa8a0f6eef737511ae424d','2026-09-17 17:50:56','2026-09-17 18:18:24.099730',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 17:50:56');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(364,'alpaca:61852446','benzinga','2026-09-17 17:48:04','Goldman Slashes Tesla Q3 Delivery Forecast to 435,000: What Do Prediction Markets Say?','Goldman sees Tesla Q3 deliveries at 435,000, well below Kalshi traders near 480,000.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61852446/tesla-q3-deliveries-goldman-kalshi-480000','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 18:18:32.161845','analyst','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'Goldman''s downward revision of delivery forecasts typically impacts investor sentiment negatively.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 356.12}','{"TSLA": {"60m": 2.786}}','2026-09-18 18:22:14.902217','2026-09-17 18:18:24.110104','61852446',replace('Goldman Sachs has cut its third-quarter delivery forecast for Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) to 435,000 vehicles, while prediction traders are centered around 480,000.\n\nGoldman analyst Mark Delaney lowered his estimate from 490,000 while maintaining a Neutral rating and $360 price target. His forecast also sits below the 456,000 Visible Alpha consensus.\n\nYes shares on Kalshi for Tesla topping 480,000 deliveries traded at 57 cents Thursday. That puts the market’s midpoint at least 45,000 vehicles above Goldman’s call.\n\nKalshi Traders Were Far Closer in Q2\n\nGoldman and Kalshi split the same way before Tesla’s previous quarter report.\n\nDelaney raised Goldman’s Q2 estimate to 420,000 on June 16. By June 26, Tesla’s company-compiled analyst consensus stood at 406,024.\n\nHours before Tesla reported on July 2, Benzinga reported Kalshi gave Tesla a 66% chance of topping 475,000 and a 56% chance of topping 480,000.\n\nTesla ultimately delivered 480,126 vehicles, almost exactly where Kalshi’s odds were centered, more than 60,000 above Goldman’s June estimate and roughly 74,000 above the broader consensus.\n\nGoldman Sees More Pressure This Time\n\nGoldman’s new forecast follows weaker-than-expected sales across the U.S., China and Europe.\n\nTesla sold an estimated 40,816 vehicles in the U.S. in August, down 26% from 55,500 a year earlier. The year-ago figure was inflated as buyers rushed to claim as buyers rushed to claim the $7,500 federal EV tax credit before it expired Sept. 30.\n\nChina retail sales fell 12.4% year over year to 50,047 vehicles in August.\n\nQ2’s 480,126 deliveries also benefited from an inventory drawdown. Tesla delivered about 28,000 more vehicles than it produced, meaning matching that result may require higher production or another drawdown.\n\nGoldman sees one offset. Export markets supplied by Tesla’s Shanghai factory are growing, which could partly cushion weakness in the U.S., China and Europe.\n\nThat leaves a clear divide: Goldman’s 435,000 forecast implies a meaningful drop from Q2, while Kalshi traders are centered around 480,000, roughly in line with last quarter.\n\nTesla has not announced its Q3 delivery date. Its second-quarter tally arrived two days after the quarter ended.\n\nKalshi and Benzinga have an existing data collaboration agreement.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia Is an ‘Awesome Company,’ but Its Stock Is Priced as ‘Greatest Company Ever,’ Damodaran Says','\n',char(10)),'62486dd46aaf028e0852df082b1dcb889add1e3a','2026-09-17 17:48:04','2026-09-17 18:18:24.099730',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 17:48:04');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(365,'alpaca:61852348','benzinga','2026-09-17 17:44:06','Apple’s iPhone Upgrade Cycle Looks Strong As Carrier Incentives Hit $1,200','BofA reiterates Buy on Apple (AAPL) with a $370 price forecast, citing strong carrier trade-in promos and edge AI upgrade potential.','https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/analyst-color/26/09/61852348/apples-iphone-upgrade-cycle-looks-strong-as-carrier-incentives-hit-1200','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-17 18:18:33.301308','analyst','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst upgrade based on observed incentives and potential upgrade cycle.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 325.14}','{"AAPL": {"60m": 3.675}}','2026-09-18 18:22:14.902217','2026-09-17 18:18:24.113570','61852348',replace('Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) could see a strong iPhone upgrade cycle as richer U.S. carrier promotions help consumers absorb higher device prices, according to Bank of America analyst Wamsi Mohan.Mohan reiterated a Buy rating on Apple with a $370 price forecast. The analyst cited capital returns, Apple’s potential to emerge as a winner in edge AI and opportunities in new products and markets.Apple iPhone Carrier Incentives Hit $1,200Bank of America said U.S. wireless carriers have increased incentives for Apple’s latest iPhones.Maximum trade-in credits for the iPhone 18 Pro Max have climbed to $1,200. That compares with $1,100 for the iPhone 17 Pro Max and $1,000 for the iPhone 16 Pro Max. Mohan said the richer promotions largely offset Apple’s higher pricing this year.The analyst expects a strong iPhone cycle, supported by higher average selling prices and adoption of the iPhone Duo. Apple’s Siri AI features could also increase consumer interest in upgrading.Bank of America noted that current promotions target customers with relatively recent iPhones. Verizon Communications Inc. and AT&T; Inc. generally require an iPhone 14 or newer to qualify for the maximum $1,200 credit. T-Mobile U.S. Inc. generally requires an iPhone 15 Pro or newer.AI, Services Support Bull CaseMohan’s broader bullish thesis rests on a multiyear iPhone upgrade cycle driven partly by the hardware needed for generative AI features. He also expects faster Services growth, margin benefits from Apple’s internally developed silicon and continued capital returns.Bank of America’s $370 price forecast is based on 37 times its calendar 2027 earnings estimate of $9.98 per share. The firm believes a premium valuation is warranted by opportunities in agentic AI, a multiyear upgrade cycle, Apple’s cash position and potential expansion into new markets.Risks include a weaker iPhone cycle, slower Services growth, execution challenges around agentic Siri, tariffs and longer smartphone replacement cycles.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nApple Stock Nears 52-Week HighApple stock rose nearly 1% Thursday as a broad market rally lifted mega-cap technology stocks. The Nasdaq gained 1.66%, while the S&P; 500 rose 1.06%.Apple remains in a strong longer-term uptrend. The stock is trading above its 20-day, 50-day, 100-day and 200-day simple moving averages.Shares are about 4.4% above the 20-day SMA of $321.32. They are also 17.3% above the 200-day SMA of $286.07. Apple has gained 40.38% over the past 12 months.Momentum also remains positive. The MACD is above its signal line, while the histogram is positive. That suggests buyers have maintained control of the recent trend.In addition, the 20-day SMA remains above the 50-day SMA. The 50-day average is also above the 200-day average.Resistance sits near $344.50, close to Apple’s 52-week high of $344.57. Support is around $300.50.ETF ExposureApple is a major holding in several ETFs. The iShares S&P; 100 ETF (NYSE:OEF) has a 9.69% weighting, while the Motley Fool 100 Index ETF (BATS:TMFC) has a 9.74% weighting. The VistaShares Target 15 Berkshire Select Income ETF (NYSE:OMAH) has a 9.97% weighting.As a result, large inflows or outflows from these funds can translate into additional buying or selling of Apple shares.AAPL Price Action: Apple shares were up 1.00% at $335.72 at the time of publication on Thursday. The stock is approaching its 52-week high of $344.56, according to Benzinga Pro data.Photo via Shutterstock \n\nRead Also:\n\nIntel Stock Could Nearly Double to $200 in 2 Years, Analyst Says — Potential Apple, Tesla, and AI Chip Deals Could Fuel the Rally','\n',char(10)),'1319658c15bb18e6d8f17a032c1b142e2719e517','2026-09-17 17:44:06','2026-09-17 18:18:24.099730',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 17:44:06');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(366,'alpaca:61852092','benzinga','2026-09-17 17:35:24','10 Consumer Discretionary Stocks With Whale Alerts In Today’s Session',replace('This whale alert can help traders discover the next big trading opportunities.\nWhales are entities with large sums of money and we track their transactions here at Benzinga on our options activity scanner.\nTraders will','\n',char(10)),'https://www.benzinga.com/markets/options/26/09/61852092/10-consumer-discretionary-stocks-whale-alerts-today-s-session','["AMZN", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 18:18:34.333337','other','neutral',2,2,'minutes',1,'The headline discusses tracking large transactions without indicating actual price movement.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 254.92, "TSLA": 356.12}','{"AMZN": {"60m": -1.467}, "TSLA": {"60m": 2.786}}','2026-09-18 18:22:14.902217','2026-09-17 18:18:24.116807','61852092',replace('This whale alert can help traders discover the next big trading opportunities.\nWhales are entities with large sums of money and we track their transactions here at Benzinga on our options activity scanner.\nTraders will search for circumstances when the market estimation of an option diverges heavily from its normal worth. High amounts of trading activity could push option prices to exaggerated or underestimated levels. \nBelow are some instances of options activity happening in the Consumer Discretionary sector: \n\nSymbol\nPUT/CALL\nTrade Type\nSentiment\nExp. Date\nStrike Price\nTotal Trade Price\nOpen Interest\nVolume\n\nTSLA\nCALL\nSWEEP\nBULLISH\n09/18/26\n$370.00\n$93.9K\n21.8K\n150.0K\n\nLVS\nCALL\nTRADE\nBEARISH\n03/19/27\n$40.00\n$125.0K\n121\n527\n\nAMZN\nPUT\nTRADE\nBEARISH\n10/16/26\n$270.00\n$102.2K\n3.5K\n512\n\nCROX\nPUT\nSWEEP\nBEARISH\n10/16/26\n$125.00\n$37.2K\n10\n471\n\nBABA\nPUT\nSWEEP\nBEARISH\n02/19/27\n$105.00\n$91.8K\n699\n222\n\nDKNG\nPUT\nSWEEP\nBULLISH\n06/17/27\n$22.50\n$27.3K\n495\n139\n\nDKS\nCALL\nSWEEP\nBEARISH\n11/20/26\n$135.00\n$29.6K\n462\n126\n\nJD\nPUT\nSWEEP\nBULLISH\n12/18/26\n$28.00\n$26.4K\n3.8K\n120\n\nDECK\nPUT\nTRADE\nBEARISH\n06/17/27\n$75.00\n$84.2K\n77\n98\n\nORLY\nPUT\nTRADE\nBEARISH\n09/17/27\n$90.00\n$53.7K\n1\n85\n\nExplanation\nThese bullet-by-bullet explanations have been constructed using the accompanying table. \n• For TSLA (NASDAQ:TSLA), we notice a call option sweep that happens to be bullish, expiring in 1 day(s) on September 18, 2026. This event was a transfer of 313 contract(s) at a $370.00 strike. This particular call needed to be split into 30 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $93.9K, with a price of $300.0 per contract. There were 21868 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 150077 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• Regarding LVS (NYSE:LVS), we observe a call option trade with bearish sentiment. It expires in 183 day(s) on March 19, 2027. Parties traded 250 contract(s) at a $40.00 strike. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $125.0K, with a price of $500.0 per contract. There were 121 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 527 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• Regarding AMZN (NASDAQ:AMZN), we observe a put option trade with bearish sentiment. It expires in 29 day(s) on October 16, 2026. Parties traded 50 contract(s) at a $270.00 strike. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $102.2K, with a price of $2044.0 per contract. There were 3599 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 512 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• For CROX (NASDAQ:CROX), we notice a put option sweep that happens to be bearish, expiring in 29 day(s) on October 16, 2026. This event was a transfer of 60 contract(s) at a $125.00 strike. This particular put needed to be split into 9 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $37.2K, with a price of $620.0 per contract. There were 10 open contracts a