(s) were bought and sold. \n• For DECK (NYSE:DECK), we notice a put option trade that happens to be bearish, expiring in 273 day(s) on June 17, 2027. This event was a transfer of 98 contract(s) at a $75.00 strike. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $84.2K, with a price of $860.0 per contract. There were 77 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 98 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• For ORLY (NASDAQ:ORLY), we notice a put option trade that happens to be bearish, expiring in 365 day(s) on September 17, 2027. This event was a transfer of 48 contract(s) at a $90.00 strike. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $53.7K, with a price of $1120.0 per contract. There were 1 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 85 contract(s) were bought and sold. \nOptions Alert Terminology\n - Call Contracts: The right to buy shares as indicated in the contract.\n - Put Contracts: The right to sell shares as indicated in the contract.\n - Expiration Date: When the contract expires. One must act on the contract by this date if one wants to use it.\n - Premium/Option Price: The price of the contract. \nFor more information, read more about unusual options activity. \nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'c7a9e2fb5d4f4611f88047ba91e5388c3cad7628','2026-09-17 17:35:24','2026-09-17 18:18:24.099730',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 17:35:24');
