 This particular put needed to be split into 6 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $91.9K, with a price of $918.0 per contract. There were 6621 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 715 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• For RGTI (NASDAQ:RGTI), we notice a put option sweep that happens to be bearish, expiring in 29 day(s) on October 16, 2026. This event was a transfer of 390 contract(s) at a $15.00 strike. This particular put needed to be split into 14 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $30.0K, with a price of $76.0 per contract. There were 13498 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 669 contract(s) were bought and sold. \nOptions Alert Terminology\n - Call Contracts: The right to buy shares as indicated in the contract.\n - Put Contracts: The right to sell shares as indicated in the contract.\n - Expiration Date: When the contract expires. One must act on the contract by this date if one wants to use it.\n - Premium/Option Price: The price of the contract. \nFor more information, read more about unusual options activity. \nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'b0c2d30ef8f763f750fded5b08710edfbd263c80','2026-09-17 17:35:23','2026-09-17 18:18:24.099730',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 17:35:23');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(368,'alpaca:61851724','benzinga','2026-09-17 17:18:45','Triple Witching, Falling Oil, and Fed Hopium Drive Up Stocks, But Downside Risks Remain',replace('\n\n\n\nTriple Witching\n\n\n\nPlease click here for an enlarged chart of SPDR S&amp;P 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) which represents the benchmark stock market index S&amp;P 500 (SPX).\n\n\n\nNote the following:\n\n\n\n\nThe chart shows','\n',char(10)),'https://www.benzinga.com/Opinion/26/09/61851724/triple-witching-falling-oil-and-fed-hopium-drive-up-stocks-but-downside-risks-remain','["AAPL", "AMZN", "BTC/USD", "META", "MSFT", "NVDA", "QQQ", "SPY", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-17 18:18:37.997995','macro','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'Market commentary on stock movements due to various factors without specific asset news.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 325.14, "AMZN": 254.92, "BTC/USD": 77563.640625, "META": 578.53, "MSFT": 501.15, "NVDA": 217.54}','{"AAPL": {"60m": 3.675}, "AMZN": {"60m": -1.467}, "BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.642}, "META": {"60m": 18.006}, "MSFT": {"60m": -0.533}, "NVDA": {"60m": 0.841}}','2026-09-18 17:21:59.924014','2026-09-17 18:18:24.123414','61851724',replace('Triple Witching\n\nPlease click here for an enlarged chart of SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) which represents the benchmark stock market index S&P; 500 (SPX).\n\nNote the following:\n\nThe chart shows that yesterday the stock market fell below the low band of zone 2 (support) before recovering to close at the low band of zone 2.\n\nThe chart shows that this morning the stock market is jumping and has already reached the upper band of zone 2.  The jump this morning is coming for three reasons:\n\nTriple witching is tomorrow.  In triple witching, stock index futures, options on indexes, and options on stocks expire on the same day.  Triple witching appears to be to the upside.\n\nPresident Trump said he has directly spoken to Iranians.  President Trump’s comment is bringing oil lower.  President Trump is expected to meet Gulf leaders in New York on Tuesday.\n\nPreviously, momo gurus were urging their followers to buy stocks because they claimed to know that Fed Chair Warsh would go for a dovish rate hike.  As usual, momo gurus were wrong.  The rate hike was not dovish.  Yesterday, the stock market reacted negatively.  Momo gurus are on the job with a new narrative to run up the stock market.  The new narrative is that they know for sure that there will not be many rate hikes in the future.\n\nBuying is especially strong in AI stocks.  Of note is new data from CoreWeave Inc (NASDAQ:CRWV) and Nebius Group NV (NASDAQ:NBIS) that compute prices are going higher.  In our analysis, higher prices may support current valuations.\n\nInitial jobless claims came at 196K vs. 209K consensus.  This shows the jobs picture remains well behaved.\n\nHousing\n\nHousing is becoming weaker as interest rates rise.  Here is the latest data:\n\nHousing starts came at 1.275M vs. 1.325M consensus.\n\nBuilding permits came at 1.394M vs. 1.410M consensus.\n\nU.K.\n\nIn spite of the Fed and European Central Bank (ECB) raising rates, the Bank of England (BOE) decided to leave its key interest rate unchanged.  However, BOE is signaling that it is open to future rate hikes.\n\nInflation in the U.K. in August was at 3.1% year-over-year vs. BOE target of 2%.\n\nEurozone\n\nInflation in the eurozone came as expected.  Here is the data:\n\nCPI came at 0.4% month-over-month vs. 0.4% consensus.\n\nCore CPI came at 0.2% month-over-month vs. 0.2% consensus.\n\nMagnificent Seven Money Flows\n\nMost portfolios are now heavily concentrated in the Mag 7 stocks.  For this reason, it is important to pay attention to early money flows in the Mag 7 stocks on a daily basis. \n\nIn the early trade, money flows are positive in Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL), Amazon.com, Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN), Alphabet Inc Class C ((NASDAQ: GOOG), Meta Platforms Inc (NASDAQ:META), Microsoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT), NVIDIA Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA), and Tesla Inc (NASDAQ:TSLA).\n\nIn the early trade, money flows are positive in S&P; 500 ETF (SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust Series 1 (NASDAQ:QQQ).\n\nMomo Crowd And Smart Money In Stocks\n\nInvestors can gain an edge by knowing money flows in SPY and QQQ.  Investors can get a bigger edge by knowing when smart money is buying stocks, gold, and oil.  The most popular ETF for gold is SPDR Gold Trust (GLD).  The most popular ETF for silver is iShares Silver Trust (SLV).  The most popular ETF for oil is United States Oil ETF (USO).\n\nBitcoin\n\nBitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) is range bound.\n\nWhat To Do Now\n\nConsider continuing to hold good, very long term, existing positions and add tactical positions based on signals.\n\nThe Arora Report is known for its accurate calls. The Arora Report correctly called the big artificial intelligence rally before anyone else, the new bull market of 2023, the bear market of 2022, new stock market highs right after the virus low in 2020, the virus drop in 2020, the DJIA rally to 30,000 when it was trading at 16,000, the start of a mega bull market in 2009, and the financial crash of 2008. Please click here to sign up for a free forever Generate Wealth Newsletter.\n\nBenzinga Disclaimer: This article is from an unpaid external contributor. It does not represent Benzinga’s reporting and has not been edited for content or accuracy.','\n',char(10)),'2663845c9b5686f39e28bc691c36392763fa6396','2026-09-17 17:18:45','2026-09-17 18:18:24.099730',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 17:22:45');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(369,'alpaca:61851798','benzinga','2026-09-17 17:22:35','Nasdaq 100 Rallies as Oil Slides, Yields Retreat: Stock Market Today','Wall Street snapped a two-day losing streak Thursday as oil retreated from its geopolitical spike and the 10-year Treasury yield slipped back below 5%. Chipmakers led the rebound, with Intel, AMD and Micron all posting outsized gains, while gold climbed 2.5% to $4,369 an ounce. The bounce came one day after the Federal Reserve delivered its first interest rate hike since 2023 and signaled at least one more this year.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61851798/nasdaq-100-rallies-as-oil-slides-yields-retreat-stock-market-today','["AMD", "QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-17 18:18:36.586272','macro','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'The overall market rallied due to a rebound in sentiment from falling oil prices and Treasury yields.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 459.75, "QQQ": 707.67, "SPY": 761.66}','{"AMD": {"60m": 18.495}, "QQQ": {"60m": 1.303}, "SPY": {"60m": 0.127}}','2026-09-18 18:22:14.902217','2026-09-17 18:18:24.126553','61851798',replace('U.S. stocks rebounded sharply Thursday, erasing two sessions of losses as crude oil retreated from its geopolitical spike and Treasury yields eased back below 5%, one day after the Federal Reserve delivered its first interest rate hike since 2023.\n\nThe S&P; 500 rose 1.1% to 7,635.21, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average lagged with a 0.7% advance, up 365 points to 51,827.04. \n\nThe Nasdaq 100 outperformed, jumping 1.8% to 29,450.56.\n\nWest Texas Intermediate fell 1.6% to $100.81 a barrel\n\nBrent dropped 2.5% to $103.23, a one-week low\n\nFed Chair Kevin Warsh and a unanimous FOMC lifted the fed funds target range by 25 basis points to 3.75%-4% on Wednesday and projected at least one further increase this year, citing inflation that remains too high at 3.4% and a labor market at effectively full employment.\n\nTreasury Yields Retreat, Volatility Cools \n\nThe 10-year Treasury yield fell to 4.95%, down 8 basis points and back under the 5.04% level hit earlier this week, which had marked a 19-year high. \n\nThe policy-sensitive 2-year yield slipped 6 basis points to 4.69%, while the 30-year eased 7 basis points to 5.30%.\n\nThe CBOE Volatility Index slid 11.4% to 15.69, unwinding the fear premium built up around the Fed decision and the Middle East supply scare.\n\nGold was the standout in commodities, jumping 2.5% to $4,368.71 an ounce as real yields retreated, with silver surging 4.1% to $65.86. \n\nOn the macro front, initial jobless claims fell 10,000 to 196,000, well below the 206,500 consensus and close to July’s 60-year low, while the Philadelphia Fed manufacturing index slowed to 37.8 from 47.4 but comfortably beat the 32.1 estimate. \n\nRead Also:\n\nFed Rate Hikes Are Supposed to Hurt Bonds: This One Is Doing the Opposite\n\nThursday’s Performance In Major US Indices\n\nIndexLast% ChangeMTDYTDS&P; 5007,635.21+1.1%-0.7%+11.5%Dow Jones51,827.04+0.7%-2.6%+7.8%Nasdaq 10029,450.56+1.8%0.0%+16.6%Russell 20002,891.07+1.1%-2.2%+16.5%Updated by 12:15 PM ET\n\nAccording to the Benzinga Pro platform:\n\nThe Vanguard S&P; 500 ETF (NYSE:VOO) gained 1.1%.\n\nThe SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA) rose 0.7%.\n\nThe Invesco QQQ Trust (NASDAQ:QQQ) climbed 1.7%.\n\nThe iShares Russell 2000 ETF (NYSE:IWM) advanced 1.0%.\n\nChip Rebound Powers Tech\n\nThe Technology Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLK) was the clear leader, rising 2.2% as semiconductor names extended a rebound from Monday’s AI-safety-driven selloff. \n\nThe Consumer Discretionary Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLY) followed with a 1.4% gain.\n\nAt the other end, the Communication Services Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLC) fell 0.4% and the Consumer Staples Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLP) slipped 0.1%. \n\nThe Energy Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLE) was flat despite the crude selloff, while the Materials Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLB) and Utilities Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLU) added 0.9% and 0.8%, respectively.\n\nAt the industry level, the Invesco Solar ETF (NYSE:TAN) led with a 4.1% jump and the Invesco WilderHill Clean Energy ETF (NYSE:PBW) rose 3.8%, both riding the same power-generation theme that dominated the tape. \n\nThe VanEck Gold Miners ETF (NYSE:GDX) climbed 3.6% alongside bullion, the SPDR S&P; Metals & Mining ETF (NYSE:XME) added 3.1% and the VanEck Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SMH) gained 2.6%. \n\nThe laggard was the SPDR S&P; Oil & Gas Exploration & Production ETF (NYSE:XOP), which ended the morning essentially flat.\n\nThe chip complex did the heavy lifting. Intel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) surged 9.7% on more than 77 million shares, nearly twice its normal pace, while Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) rose 6.9%, Micron Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MU) added 5.4% and Oracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL) climbed 5.6%. \n\nSuper Micro Computer Inc. (NASDAQ:SMCI) jumped 8.8% and Hewlett Packard Enterprise Co. (NYSE:HPE) rose 8.0%.\n\nDefense Names are the Session’s Dead Weight\n\nRTX Corp. (NYSE:RTX) fell 2.3%, Lockheed Martin Corp. (NYSE:LMT) dropped 1.9%, General Dynamics Corp. (NYSE:GD) slid 1.7% and The Boeing Company (NYSE:BA) lost 1.5%, a clean unwind of the Middle East risk premium.\n\nOn the earnings front, Lennar Corp. (NYSE:LEN) was the only major name to report after Wednesday’s close, missing on both lines with adjusted EPS of $1.23 versus $1.29 consensus and revenue of $8.05 billion against $8.37 billion expected. \n\nThe homebuilder cut its full-year delivery guidance to 80,000-81,000 units from 82,000-83,000 and saw home-sales gross margin compress to 15.8% from 17.5%. \n\nShares fell roughly 1.5%, with the iShares U.S. Home Construction ETF (BATS:ITB) still managing a 0.9% gain.\n\nThe Day’s Big Winners\n\nGenerac Holdings Inc. (NYSE:GNRC), up 20.1%, after disclosing Wednesday evening that it issued Amazon warrants for up to 1.69 million shares at $200.93 – roughly $340 million – tied to a backup-generator supply agreement for AWS data centers, with initial deliveries of about $2.4 billion across 2027 and 2028 and full warrant vesting at $8 billion of aggregate payments.\n\nVicor Corp. (NASDAQ:VICR) rallied 14.3% after announcing Wednesday it licensed its Vertical Power Delivery patent portfolio to an unnamed leading AI OEM on a non-exclusive basis, layering a royalty stream on top of product sales. The news follows a raised fiscal 2026 revenue outlook of more than $600 million and a 145% jump in backlog.\n\nTempus AI Inc. (NASDAQ:TEM) gained 13.7% following a Morgan Stanley note that quantified the company’s reimbursement tailwind, with management pointing to roughly $80 million to $100 million of incremental revenue next year from xT pricing and $250 million to $300 million annually from xF approval and pricing.\n\nNuclear-adjacent power names Oklo Inc. (NYSE:OKLO) and X-Energy Inc. (NASDAQ:XE) rose 12.3% and 11.5%, respectively, with no company-specific news in the tape. Both appear to be trading in sympathy with the broader data-center power complex after the House passed the Ratepayer Protection Act 417-3 on Wednesday, shifting generation and transmission costs onto large data centers. X-Energy’s most recent release, a Sept. 15 UK partnership with Centrica, was met with a nearly 4% decline that day.\n\nOther notable gainers included IonQ Inc. (NYSE:IONQ), up 9.9%, SiTime Corp. (NASDAQ:SITM), up 8.7%, and Moderna Inc. (NASDAQ:MRNA), up 8.1%, as the iShares Biotechnology ETF (NASDAQ:IBB) added 2.2%.\n\nOn the Downside\n\nAutoNation Inc. (NYSE:AN) dropped 3.9% after CFO Thomas Szlosek flagged third-quarter headwinds at the same Morgan Stanley conference, citing softer service growth, model-year changeover pressure, affordability and lower EV penetration following the expiration of federal incentives.\n\nFurther up the auto value chain, General Motors Co. (NYSE:GM) shrugged off the same read-across, rising 3.6%.\n\nReddit Inc. (NYSE:RDDT) slid 3.9%, extending losses after a Sept. 15 Wells Fargo note lowered confidence that the company can renegotiate its AI content-licensing agreement with Google on favorable terms. \n\nThird-party data cited in recent sell-side work showed Google search traffic to Reddit down roughly 10% year-over-year so far in September, after a 7% decline in August.\n\nKarman Holdings Inc. (NYSE:KRMN) rounded out the losers, down 3.8% consistent with the broader unwind in aerospace and defense as the Middle East risk premium deflated.\n\nElsewhere, T-Mobile US Inc. (NASDAQ:TMUS) fell 3.1% to lead S&P; 100 decliners, weighing on the communications sector alongside Salesforce and Verizon.\n\nThursday’s Russell 1000 Top Gainers\n\nName% changeGenerac Holdings Inc.+20.12%Vicor Corporation+14.27%Tempus AI, Inc.+13.73%Oklo Inc.+12.33%X-Energy, Inc.+11.52%\n\nThursday’s Russell 1000 Top Losers\n\nName% changeMasTec, Inc. . (NYSE:MTZ)-4.58%ATI Inc.  (NYSE:ATI)-4.42%AutoNation, Inc.-3.90%Reddit, Inc.-3.86%Karman Holdings Inc.-3.83%\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'906dd8230eccc126ca6cf60d6de94c11cea6275b','2026-09-17 17:22:35','2026-09-17 18:18:24.099730',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 17:22:35');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(370,'alpaca:61856481','benzinga','2026-09-17 20:15:24','Bitcoin Holds $76,000 as Ethereum, XRP, Dogecoin Spike 2%','Bitcoin stays above $76,000 after Fed hike as institutional demand weakens. Traders see this could be the shortest bear market as BTC defies the 4-year cycle.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61856481/bitcoin-holds-76000-as-ethereum-xrp-dogecoin-spike-2','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "ETH/USD", "SHIB/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-17 20:18:50.936898','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Headline discusses market behavior but lacks major news.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 77563.640625, "DOGE/USD": 0.08181925, "ETH/USD": 2414.179931640625, "SHIB/USD": 5.14e-06, "SOL/USD": 101.121, "XRP/USD": 1.297265}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.334}, "DOGE/USD": {"60m": -0.19}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 1.301}, "SHIB/USD": {"60m": 1.362}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": 0.167}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 0.225}}','2026-09-18 20:22:46.378901','2026-09-17 20:18:47.072396','61856481',replace('Bitcoin traded sideways on Thursday as crypto markets digest the Federal Reserve’s 25 basis points rate hike.CryptocurrencyTickerPriceBitcoin(CRYPTO: BTC)$76,574Ethereum(CRYPTO: ETH)$2,450Solana(CRYPTO: SOL)$101.41XRP(CRYPTO: XRP)$1.30Dogecoin(CRYPTO: DOGE)$0.0817Shiba Inu(CRYPTO: SHIB)$0.055182Notable Statistics:\nCoinglass data shows 150,510 traders were liquidated in the past 24 hours for $1.83 billion.       \n\nSoSoValue data shows net inflows of $517.2 million from spot Bitcoin ETFs on Wednesday. Spot Ethereum ETFs saw net inflows of $189.2 million.\n\nIn the past 24 hours, top gainers include XRP, Hyperliquid and Pepe.\nNotable Developments:\nPeter Schiff: Bitcoin Failed ‘Digital Gold’ Test, Higher Yields Could Hurt BTC\n\nXRP Up 3% as Ripple Adds XRP Payments to Stripe, Tempo’s AI Standard\n\nCrypto Bull Market Doesn’t Depend on CLARITY Act, Bitwise Exec Says\n\nBitcoin Holds $76,000 After Fed Hike: Why Is BTC Strong While Equities Fall?\n\nBitcoin, Ethereum ETFs Lose $1.11 Billion Over 2 Days: What’s Going On?\n\nBitcoin’s Fair Value Is Around $105,000, Rise Is ‘Programmed,’ Mark Yusko Says\n\nPURR Jumps 8% as SEC Approves ‘Innovation Exemption’ for Tokenized Stock Trading\nTrader Notes:Trader KillaXBT predicts Bitcoin is unlikely to hit $100,000 in 2026, with re-accumulation and range-bound trading the more probable path. He expects $100,000 to break next year.Trader Jelle noted Bitcoin appears to be breaking the traditional four-year cycle, with a shorter and shallower bear market unless BTC makes a new low around October.He added, “this will have been the shortest bear market by far, while also being much shallower than usual.” What that means for the next bull run remains unclear.Crypto investor Rekt Capital sees Bitcoin’s bear market running out of time, based on the historical roughly 365-day duration. Image: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nPeter Schiff: Bitcoin Failed ''Digital Gold'' Test, Higher Yields Could Hurt BTC','\n',char(10)),'323fc612d1ad232f5cd5ed4ebecafcb1e326e76f','2026-09-17 20:15:24','2026-09-17 20:18:47.067024',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 20:15:24');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(371,'alpaca:61855556','benzinga','2026-09-17 19:54:55','JPMorgan Says Bitcoin Could Beat Gold as Analyst Predicts It''ll ''Triple'' Gold','JPMorgan says Bitcoin could outperform gold if ETF hedging eases, while Eric Balchunas sees Bitcoin ETFs tripling gold in assets.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61855556/jpmorgan-says-bitcoin-could-beat-gold','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-17 20:18:52.136627','analyst','bullish',3,2,'weeks',1,'Analyst predicts potential performance improvement for Bitcoin compared to gold.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 77563.640625}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.334}}','2026-09-18 20:22:46.378901','2026-09-17 20:18:47.077040','61855556',replace('JPMorgan Chase & Co (NYSE:JPM) said Thursday that Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) could outperform gold if ETF hedging eases, as Bloomberg’s Eric Balchunas predicted Bitcoin ETFs will eventually triple gold in assets.\n\nWhat JPMorgan’s Report Says\n\nIn a note cited by The Block, JPMorgan analysts led by Nikolaos Panigirtzoglou pointed out that gold ETFs have fully recovered all their 2026 outflows while Bitcoin ETFs have recovered only about half. \n\nThe debasement trade that drove inflows into both assets after the July Fed meeting has weakened over the past week as inflation-adjusted bond yields rose and the CLARITY Act failed in the Senate.\n\nMoreover, short interest in BlackRock’s (NYSE:BLK) iShares Bitcoin Trust (NASDAQ:IBIT) sits near its highest level this year, while short interest in the SPDR Gold Shares ETF (NYSE:GLD) sits below its historical average.\n\nThe put-to-call ratio is also higher for IBIT than GLD, pointing to elevated hedging demand around Bitcoin relative to gold.\n\n“This contrast suggests that Bitcoin still faces an overall more skeptical positioning backdrop than gold,” the analysts wrote, adding that if hedging demand falls, it could give Bitcoin more support than gold from current levels.\n\nWhy Balchunas Sees Bitcoin Tripling Gold\n\nBloomberg senior ETF analyst Eric Balchunas said in a video posted on X that Bitcoin ETFs will ultimately triple gold ETFs in total assets, driven by generational wealth transfer and growing institutional comfort as Bitcoin’s volatility falls. \n\n“As the younger investors get more money and grow up with Bitcoin as their store of value, I do believe that Bitcoin ETFs will triple gold in assets,” Balchunas said.\n\nHe noted that big institutional money still prefers gold today because of Bitcoin’s higher volatility and its historical tendency to move like the Nasdaq 100. \n\nBut as volatility and correlation to equities both decline, he sees an inflection point coming where large institutions treat Bitcoin as a reliable store of value and safe haven. \n\n“Bitcoin is like gold as a teenager,” Balchunas said. “Gold is 5,000 years old. Bitcoin is 17 years old.”\n\nWhy the Gap Between Bitcoin and Gold Matters Now\n\nJPMorgan’s data shows Bitcoin ETF demand has pulled back more than gold over the past week, leaving more room for a recovery if sentiment improves. \n\nFutures positioning in both assets remains elevated, suggesting institutional investors have not walked away from either trade.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin''s Fair Value Is Around $105,000, Rise Is ''Programmed,'' Mark Yusko Says','\n',char(10)),'457539b1e03d4ed5a4e1bad75ab3806992176b4b','2026-09-17 19:54:55','2026-09-17 20:18:47.067024',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 19:54:55');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(372,'alpaca:61855216','benzinga','2026-09-17 19:41:42','Fed Rate Hike in October or December? Benzinga Viewers Say This is More Likely','The Federal Reserve indicated another rate hike could happen before the end of the year. Here&#39;s what Benzinga viewers predict.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/economic-data/26/09/61855216/fed-rate-outlook-next-hike-october-or-december','["SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-17 20:18:53.459208','macro','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The headline presents speculation about interest rates without confirming specific actions.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"SPY": 761.66}','{}','2026-09-18 20:22:46.378901','2026-09-17 20:18:47.081206','61855216',replace('The Federal Reserve raised interest rates by 25 basis points Wednesday, marking the first rate hike since 2023. While that move was widely expected in recent weeks, attention now turns to whether there will be another increase before the end of the year. Here’s what Benzinga readers think and how that compares with prediction markets.\n\nAnother Rate Hike?\n\nWednesday’s Federal Reserve decision, which was unanimous, also came with the dot plot, which implies another rate hike is likely before the end of the year.\n\nWith the Fed set to meet in October and December, investors and economists now try to pinpoint when exactly a policy tightening could happen, if at all.\n\n"The dot plot signals another hike, what do you think?" Benzinga asked viewers of "PreMarket Playbook" Thursday morning.\n\nThe results are:\n\nHike in December: 43%\n\nNo More Hikes: 25%\n\nHike in October: 22%\n\nHike in Both: 10%\n\nBenzinga viewers point to a rate increase in December being most likely of the four options, and twice as likely as one in October. A quarter of the 210 respondents said no more hikes is most likely, while 10% see rate rises coming in both October and December.\n\nPrediction market Kalshi shows the odds of a rate hike in October at 48%, while there is 53% odds of the rate being maintained in the next FOMC meeting. The Benzinga viewer odds imply a 32% chance of a rate hike in October based on the results for Hike in October and Hike in Both.\n\nAnother prediction market on Kalshi asks how many rate hikes will there be in 2026. The odds are 57% for exactly 2 and 23% for exactly 3. Benzinga viewers imply a 65% chance of exactly two hikes and 10% for exactly 3.\n\nThe odds for exactly 1 rate hike, which would mean no more, are 19% on Kalshi, which is slightly lower than the 25% odds from Benzinga viewers.\n\nTime will tell whether Benzinga viewers or prediction markets were more accurate with their guesses and odds.\n\n"PreMarket Playbook" airs Monday through Friday on Benzinga’s YouTube channel and is hosted by Ryan Faloona.\n\nRead Also:\n\nFed Rate Hikes Are Supposed to Hurt Bonds: This One Is Doing the Opposite\n\nThe Market Reacts\n\nThe SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY), which tracks the S&P; 500, closed at $754.05 on Wednesday. This was less than 1% lower than Tuesday’s closing price of $757.39.\n\nIn a prior Benzinga viewer poll, 33% of viewers predicted the SPY would trade lower on the day of the Federal Reserve’s September rate decision, while 49% predicted the ETF would be higher on the day. The remaining 18% predicted no change.\n\nWhile the S&P; 500 was down slightly on Wednesday, the markets are rallying higher on Thursday as the rate hike news is digested.\n\nThe SPY trades at $762.66 at the time of writing, up 1.1% on the day and trading ahead of Tuesday’s closing price.\n\nKalshi and Benzinga have an existing data collaboration agreement.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla''s Hottest Growth Story? Readers Say It Walks, Not Drives\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'b5da745d7b87c6a25a57f847e900b7f1aa69731f','2026-09-17 19:41:42','2026-09-17 20:18:47.067024',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 19:41:42');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(373,'alpaca:61854623','benzinga','2026-09-17 19:18:35','Trump''s Inflation Approval Slumps to 19%: What Do Prediction Markets Say About the Midterms?','Trump’s inflation approval fell to 19% as prediction markets moved toward Democrats ahead of the midterms.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61854623/trump-inflation-approval-midterms-democrats-polymarket','["QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-17 20:18:54.442051','macro','bearish',3,3,'weeks',1,'Lower approval ratings may suggest economic concerns impacting market sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 707.67, "SPY": 761.66}','{}','2026-09-18 19:22:29.104036','2026-09-17 20:18:47.085152','61854623',replace('President Donald Trump‘s approval on inflation has fallen to 19%, a new low in the latest Marquette Law School poll. \n\nCNN chief data analyst Harry Enten called the resulting minus-61 net rating the worst presidential inflation reading on record.\n\n“This is literally the worst net approval rating on inflation for any president,” Enten said Thursday.\n\n“Even Republicans have turned against the President of the United States on inflation,” he added, pointing to net ratings of minus 95 among Democrats, minus 74 among independents and minus 4 among Republicans.\n\nMidterm Markets Shift Toward Democrats\n\nPolymarket traders put a Democratic sweep of the House and Senate at about 60%, up from 51% on Sept. 1. More than $12 million has traded on its congressional balance-of-power market.\n\nThe sweep contract is effectively becoming a Senate bet in disguise. Traders put Democratic Senate control at 60%, while the scenario in which Democrats win the Senate but Republicans retain the House sits below 1%.\n\nDemocrats lead Republicans 54% to 41% among likely voters in the latest Marquette poll, widening from a 51% to 45% lead in July.\n\nPolymarket Traders Price Another Fed Hike\n\nThe Marquette results landed the same day the Federal Reserve raised rates 25 basis points to 3.75%-4%, its first hike since 2023. Sixteen of 18 policymakers expect at least one more increase this year.\n\nPolymarket traders put the chance of at least one more hike this year at 81%.\n\nThe S&P; 500 fell 0.44% Wednesday after the Fed raised rates, but was up about 1.1% in Thursday trading as Treasury yields and oil prices eased. SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY), which tracks the index, followed it higher.\n\nThe tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite finished nearly flat Wednesday before rising about 1.6% Thursday, lifting Invesco QQQ Trust (NASDAQ:QQQ), which tracks the Nasdaq-100.\n\nTariffs Add to Price Pressure\n\nA Cato Institute/Morning Consult survey published Thursday found 75% of registered voters say tariffs will matter to their midterm vote, while 74% say Trump’s tariffs have increased prices. Even 66% of Republicans said tariffs raised prices.\n\nAmong voters who say tariffs will influence their midterm vote, 55% plan to back the Democratic congressional candidate, compared with 36% who plan to vote Republican.\n\nThe shift from 2024 is stark. An October 2024 ABC News/Ipsos poll found registered voters trusted Trump over Kamala Harris on inflation by seven points. Marquette now gives Democrats an 11-point advantage over Republicans on handling inflation and the cost of living.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia Is an ‘Awesome Company,’ but Its Stock Is Priced as ‘Greatest Company Ever,’ Damodaran Says','\n',char(10)),'9c640870290efeb536305feebeacb9381105d6ec','2026-09-17 19:18:35','2026-09-17 20:18:47.067024',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 19:18:35');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(374,'alpaca:61857634','benzinga','2026-09-17 21:00:20','Grayscale: Bitcoin Put in the Bottom at $58,000, ''Green Light'' From Here','Grayscale says Bitcoin’s $58,000 June low marked the cycle bottom and gives clients a green light to allocate while highlighting Zcash.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61857634/grayscale-bitcoin-put-in-the-bottom-at-58000-green-light-from-here','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-17 21:19:01.878241','other','bullish',2,2,'days',1,'Grayscale''s assertion indicates potential positive sentiment towards Bitcoin but lacks concrete confirmation.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 77563.640625}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": -1.334}}','2026-09-18 21:22:54.007465','2026-09-17 21:18:58.597667','61857634',replace('Grayscale Head of Research Zach Pandl told clients Thursday that Bitcoin’s (CRYPTO: BTC) $58,000 June low was the cycle bottom and the firm is now giving a green light to allocate.\n\nWhat Pandl Said About the Bottom\n\nPandl told The Block at Avalanche Summit in New York that Grayscale called the bottom at $58,000 at the end of June and he is sticking with that view. \n\nBitcoin trades above $76,000 Thursday, up 1% over 24 hours, but still roughly 39% below its record high of around $126,000.\n\nGrayscale uses a three-part framework before advising clients to allocate, covering the long-term structural trend, the stage of the market cycle, and the macroeconomic backdrop.\n\nPandl said all three conditions are now clear. “In my view, you can check all of those boxes today,” he said. “So we are certainly giving the green light to our clients.”\n\nThe call echoes Coinbase (NASDAQ:COIN) CEO Brian Armstrong, who said on September 10 that Bitcoin has bottomed for the current cycle and expects a two-year upward trend heading into the next halving.\n\nWhy Pandl Is Also Watching Zcash\n\nPandl also told The Block that Grayscale has offered a Zcash (CRYPTO: ZEC) investment product for roughly nine years, and his thesis rests on a gap that Bitcoin leaves open: privacy. \n\n“Bitcoin needs a privacy layer, digital currencies need a privacy layer, Bitcoin is missing that,” Pandl said.\n\nHis view is that Zcash occupies an underexplored design space rather than competing with Bitcoin directly. \n\nDifferent blockchains make different trade-offs, and Zcash prioritizes privacy at the expense of some of the transparency Bitcoin offers. \n\nWith AI growing more powerful and personal data more exposed, Pandl argued that Zcash gives investors a direct way to express a view on financial and personal privacy as a theme.\n\nWhy the Timing Matters\n\nPandl’s green light comes in the immediate aftermath of two market hits in one week: the Clarity Act’s Senate defeat and the Fed’s first rate hike in three years. \n\nDespite both, he is not pulling back his bottom call or his allocation recommendation. \n\nThat conviction, coming from one of the largest institutional crypto asset managers, puts a floor under the narrative at a moment when sentiment across the broader market is fragile.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin, Ethereum ETFs Lose $1.11 Billion Over 2 Days: What''s Going On?','\n',char(10)),'332a8a2419dd12e9f6f80aa3690d606d2e70ba91','2026-09-17 21:00:20','2026-09-17 21:18:58.559559',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 21:00:21');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(375,'alpaca:61857522','benzinga','2026-09-17 20:51:04','Ten-Year Treasury Yield Hits 5%: Why QQQ Could Face More Pressure Than Value ETFs','Ten-year Treasury yields near 5% could pressure growth-heavy QQQ, putting value ETFs in focus as rate risks rise.','https://www.benzinga.com/etfs/sector-etfs/26/09/61857522/treasury-yield-5-percent-qqq-versus-value-etfs','["AAPL", "MSFT", "NVDA", "QQQ"]','stocks','2026-09-17 21:19:03.163388','macro','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'Rising treasury yields are generally seen as a negative for growth stocks.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 325.14, "MSFT": 501.15, "NVDA": 217.54, "QQQ": 707.67}','{}','2026-09-18 21:22:54.007465','2026-09-17 21:18:58.601622','61857522',replace('The 10-year Treasury yield is back near 5%, putting pressure on the valuation premium carried by growth-heavy ETFs such as the Invesco QQQ Trust (NASDAQ:QQQ).\n\nThe benchmark yield briefly crossed 5% this week before retreating to around 4.95%-4.99%. The level matters because history shows equity returns have weakened when the 10-year Treasury carries a 5-handle.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nAccording to a Substack article by Bespoke Investment Group, highlighted by GuruFocus, on trading days since 1962 when the 10-year Treasury yield carried a 5-handle, the S&P; 500 averaged a 0.4% gain over the following three months, with positive returns 56% of the time. Six-month and one-year gains averaged 1.3% and 4.1%, respectively, versus long-term averages of 2.2%, 4.4% and 9.1%.\n\nThat does not mean stocks must fall. But it raises the question of whether growth-heavy ETFs face greater valuation pressure than value-focused funds if yields remain elevated.\n\nQQQ’s rate sensitivity comes into focus\n\nQQQ tracks the Nasdaq-100 and has substantial exposure to mega-cap technology and AI-related companies. Nvidia Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) accounted for 8.34% of the ETF, Apple, Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL) 7.90%, Microsoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT) 6% and Micron Technology, Inc (NASDAQ:MU) 4.69%.\n\nHigher Treasury yields can weigh on such stocks by increasing the discount rate applied to future earnings and making relatively low-risk bonds more competitive with equities.\n\nThe valuation gap between stocks and Treasuries is already worth watching. Market data from ChartVault showed the S&P; 500’s earnings yield at 3.88% against a 5.01% 10-year Treasury yield as of Sept. 1.\n\nVTV offers a different exposure\n\nThe Vanguard Value ETF (NYSE:VTV) tracks large-cap value stocks rather than the Nasdaq-100’s growth-heavy universe. It held 308 stocks as of July 31, with a P/E ratio of almost 21x.\n\nRecent performance also shows the two ETFs can behave differently. Over the three months through Sept. 16, QQQ fell about 2.5%, while VTV gained 1.5%.\n\nThe key variable now is whether the 10-year yield merely tests 5% or stays there. A sustained higher-rate regime could make valuation discipline increasingly important for growth-heavy ETFs, while the relative performance of value will still depend on earnings, economic growth and sector composition.\n\nA 5% Treasury yield is not a sell signal for QQQ. It is, however, a higher hurdle for richly valued growth exposure.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMortgage Rates Near 7% Are Testing This 10%-Yield ETF. Is REM’s Income Worth the Rate Risk?\n\nPhoto: Drozd Irina via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'2294766b157d3fc6eb044eb80b252779cd83404a','2026-09-17 20:51:04','2026-09-17 21:18:58.559559',1,NULL,'2026-09-17 20:51:04');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(376,'alpaca:61859812','benzinga','2026-09-18 03:57:05','Scott Bessent Says Financing Iran With Crypto ''Not Beyond'' Treasury''s Reach, Sanctions Bitcoin Exchange Tied to Iranian Financier Babak Zanjani','Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said new sanctions on a Bitcoin exchange tied to Babak Zanjani send a clear message on Iran financing.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/politics/26/09/61859812/scott-bessent-iran-crypto-financing-treasury-sanctions-babak-zanjani-exchange','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 04:19:28.138205','regulatory','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'New sanctions could limit Bitcoin''s appeal due to regulatory pressures.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 1.925}}','2026-09-19 04:23:13.616854','2026-09-18 04:19:23.984579','61859812',replace('Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said Thursday that new sanctions targeting a Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) exchange linked to Iranian financier Babak Zanjani showed that crypto-based efforts to finance the Iranian regime won’t escape Treasury’s reach.\n\nTreasury Targets Zanjani’s Digital Asset Network\n\n“Today’s designations of Iranian digital asset infrastructure make perfectly clear that efforts to finance the Iranian regime using cryptocurrencies are not beyond OFAC’s reach,” Bessent said in a post on X. \n\nHe added that the department will sanction those who support the regime. \n\nToday’s designations of Iranian digital asset infrastructure make perfectly clear that efforts to finance the Iranian regime using cryptocurrencies are not beyond OFAC’s reach. If you support the Iranian regime, the Department of the Treasury will sanction you. https://t.co/lM73Do5HZ8— Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent (@SecScottBessent) September 17, 2026 \n\nThe OFAC sanctioned BitBank, a digital asset exchange controlled by Zanjani, along with its developer, Pishtaz Simorgh Electronic Trade Company. \n\nThree of Zanjani’s associates, Hossein Ali Zaker Hossein, Mohammad ​Mahdi Zaker Hossein​, and Seyed Adel ⁠Heidari, were also sanctioned.\n\nThe designation is part of “Operation Economic Outcast,” Treasury’s campaign launched in August to isolate Iran economically and disrupt its global financial, commercial, and logistical networks.\n\nRead Also:\n\nElizabeth Warren Calls Kevin Warsh a ''Sock Puppet'' After Trump Claims He Told Him How to Vote for a Rate Hike: Peter Schiff Asks If It''s ''Another Lie''\n\nBitBank Moved Money to the IRGC\n\nTreasury said Zanjani used BitBank between June and July to transfer hundreds of millions of dollars in Bitcoin to the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps.\n\nA previously sanctioned entity, Hormuz Safe Marine Services Authority, has used BitBank since June to funnel payments to the Iranian regime. \n\nTreasury’s Broader Push Against Iranian Crypto\n\nIn July, the Treasury sanctioned a separate Zanjani-linked network, targeting nine firms and four individuals, including two UK-registered exchanges Zedcex and Zedxion accused of processing more than $94 million tied to the IRGC.\n\nZanjani was sentenced to death in 2016 for embezzlement, though his sentence was commuted in 2024, and he resurfaced the following year as a backer of Iranian government economic projects.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Said Kennedy Center Could Be ''Ripped Down,'' Now Judge Orders 30-Day Notice Before Any Demolition\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nImage via Shutterstock/ Maxim Elramsisy','\n',char(10)),'bc964a5d447202bd69fc4fd7c985e2a379583503','2026-09-18 03:57:05','2026-09-18 04:19:23.979960',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 03:57:05');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(377,'alpaca:61860116','benzinga','2026-09-18 05:42:41','Stock Market: Will S&P 500 Open Up or Down Today?','Will S&amp;P 500 open higher? Polymarket odds hit 65% as Wall Street digests Fed independence debates, crypto sanctions, and cooling oil prices.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61860116/stock-market-will-sp-500-open-up-or-down-today-40','["BTC/USD", "QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-18 06:19:38.334575','other','neutral',1,1,'minutes',1,'The headline speculates on market movement without definitive information.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.447}}','2026-09-19 06:23:19.182204','2026-09-18 06:19:34.362311','61860116',replace('U.S. stock futures are posting slight gains early Friday as investors digest targeted geopolitical sanctions, debates over Federal Reserve independence, and the Bank of Japan’s 31-year high rate-hike decision. \n\nThe Polymarket (CRYPTO: POL) crowd is leaning bullish for the Sept. 18 trading session. The “S&P; 500 (SPX) Up or Down on September 18?” contract currently reflects a 65% chance of a higher open.\n\nWhy That Number Matters\n\nTraders are navigating a complex macro environment featuring crypto-targeted sanctions and central bank drama:\n\nSlightly Positive Index Futures: Equity futures point to a muted but green open for major benchmarks. Dow Jones futures rose 0.11%, and S&P; 500 futures advanced 0.11%. Nasdaq 100 futures ticked up 0.09%, while Russell 2000 futures dipped a marginal 0.01%.\n\nFed Independence & Yields: Following the Fed’s unanimous 25-basis-point rate hike, controversy erupted after President Donald Trump claimed he instructed Fed Chair Kevin Warsh to vote with the board. Senator Elizabeth Warren (D-Mass.) called Warsh a “sock puppet,” while investor Peter Schiff questioned the narrative’s validity. Economist Mohamed El-Erian defended the Fed’s credibility, noting the unanimous 12-0 vote and stabilizing bond markets. The 10-year Treasury yield cooled to 4.93% after briefly topping 5% earlier in the week. \n\nGeopolitics, Crypto Sanctions & Energy: Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent escalated “Operation Economic Outcast” by sanctioning BitBank, a Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) exchange linked to Iranian financier Babak Zanjani, for moving hundreds of millions to the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps. Meanwhile, energy prices retreated from recent highs; Brent crude fell 1.27% to $103.49 a barrel, and WTI crude dropped 0.96% to $100.93. \n\nEarnings & Eco Data: Friday’s earnings slate is relatively light, featuring reports from NioCorp Developments Ltd. (NASDAQ:NB), Trio-Tech International (NYSE:TRT), and Celularity Inc. (NASDAQ:CELU). Economically, August’s industrial production data will be released at 9:15 a.m. ET.\n\nThe Bull Case and Market Outlook\n\nJeffrey Roach, Chief Economist for LPL Financial, notes that despite the Fed’s hawkish pivot, the underlying U.S. economy keeps powering forward. Fed officials recently revised growth projections higher for 2026 and 2027, anticipating 2.4% expansion and sustained low unemployment.\n\nInternationally, easing U.S.-China trade tensions are providing a constructive backdrop. Washington and Beijing are reportedly weighing reciprocal tariff cuts on $30 billion of trade ahead of the upcoming leaders’ summit.\n\nRoach argues that steady policy accommodation from China and a potential stimulus package could spark a meaningful move in global risk appetite, helping offset the tension of a hawkish Fed and the Bank of Japan’s 25-basis-point rate hike.\n\nHow the Previous Bet Played Out\n\nThe Sept. 17 Polymarket contract resolved “Up,” recording $50,476 in total trading volume. \n\nOn Thursday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed higher. SPY rose 1.13% to $762.60, while QQQ rose 1.73% to $716.92. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), also ended 0.61% higher at $518.35.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Said Kennedy Center Could Be ''Ripped Down,'' Now Judge Orders 30-Day Notice Before Any Demolition\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'f4ca1db5bf3f5911af9f64ecb52a9de15a238d3a','2026-09-18 05:42:41','2026-09-18 06:19:34.355115',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 05:42:41');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(378,'alpaca:61860581','benzinga','2026-09-18 06:45:50','Nasdaq Jumps Over 400 Points as Crude Oil Falls: Investor Sentiment Improves, Greed Index Remains in ‘Fear’ Zone','Markets rallied as yields and oil fell; tech led gains, but CNN’s Fear &amp; Greed Index improved to 29, remaining in the Fear zone.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/market-summary/26/09/61860581/nasdaq-jumps-over-400-points-as-crude-oil-falls-investor-sentiment-improves-greed-index-remains-in-fear-zone','["AMD"]','stocks','2026-09-18 07:19:45.844104','macro','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Overall market rally may positively impact tech stocks including AMD.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78}','{}','2026-09-19 07:23:27.998090','2026-09-18 07:19:42.016476','61860581',replace('The CNN Money Fear and Greed index showed some improvement in the overall market sentiment, while the index remained in the “Fear” zone on Thursday.\n\nU.S. stocks settled higher on Thursday, with the Nasdaq Composite gaining more than 400 points during the session following a decline in Treasury yields and crude oil prices.\n\nThe Federal Reserve, on Wednesday, raised the federal funds target range by 25 basis points to 3.75%-4.00% on Wednesday, marking its first rate increase since 2023.\n\nOn the economic data front, initial jobless claims fell 10,000 to 196,000, well below the 206,500 consensus and close to July’s 60-year low, while the Philadelphia Fed manufacturing index slowed to 37.8 from 47.4 but comfortably beat the 32.1 estimate.\n\nThe Technology Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLK) was the clear leader, as semiconductor names extended a rebound from Monday’s AI-safety-driven selloff.\n\nIntel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) surged around 8%, while Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) jumped more than 6% on Thursday.\n\nMost sectors on the S&P; 500 closed on a positive note, with information technology, consumer discretionary and utilities stocks recording the biggest gains on Thursday. However, financial and consumer staples stocks bucked the overall market trend, closing the session lower.\n\nThe Dow Jones closed higher by around 316 points to 51,778.04 on Thursday. The S&P; 500 jumped 1.14% to 7,637.76, while the Nasdaq Composite surged 1.69% at 26,418.30 during Wednesday’s session.\n\nWhat is CNN Business Fear & Greed Index?\n\nAt a current reading of 29, the index remained in the “Fear” zone on Thursday, versus a prior reading of 27.\n\nThe Fear & Greed Index is a measure of the current market sentiment. It is based on the premise that higher fear exerts pressure on stock prices, while higher greed has the opposite effect. The index is calculated based on seven equal-weighted indicators. The index ranges from 0 to 100, where 0 represents maximum fear and 100 signals maximum greediness.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'3e95384af52f5c51ff2843a7f35f0ca876bd11f1','2026-09-18 06:45:50','2026-09-18 07:19:42.000441',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 06:45:50');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(379,'alpaca:61861407','benzinga','2026-09-18 08:14:46','Ric Edelman Predicts $500,000 Bitcoin by 2030, Says BTC Could Follow Amazon’s 1999 Trajectory: ‘Everybody Owns It’','Ric Edelman explains why Bitcoin is the Amazon of 1999, how it lowers portfolio risk, and why soon &#39;everybody&#39; will own the digital asset.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61861407/ric-edelman-predicts-500000-bitcoin-by-2030-says-btc-could-follow-amazons-1999-trajectory-everybody-owns-it','["AMZN", "BTC/USD"]','stocks','2026-09-18 08:19:54.669173','analyst','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'The prediction is speculative and not a confirmed event.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.447}}','2026-09-19 08:23:31.012025','2026-09-18 08:19:50.682042','61861407',replace('Financial advisor Ric Edelman states that the debate over investing in Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) mirrors the 1999 skepticism surrounding Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN), predicting the digital asset will become a widely held portfolio asset.\n\nThe Amazon Trajectory\n\nSpeaking on BMTV, the Edelman Financial Engines founder noted that the financial industry’s dialogue around Bitcoin is a temporary phase. “Back in 1999, people were arguing over whether to invest in Amazon,” Edelman stated.\n\n“Nobody has that argument. Everybody owns it, and Bitcoin will have the same trajectory in the future”.\n\nWhile he faced industry pushback in 2013 and 2014, Edelman notes that traditional finance professionals now acknowledge cryptocurrency as a permanent asset class.\n\nJUST IN: Legendary American financial advisor Ric Edelman compares buying Bitcoin today to buying Amazon in 1999:"Back in 1999 people were arguing over whether to invest in Amazon. Nobody has that argument. Everybody owns it, and Bitcoin will have the same trajectory in the… pic.twitter.com/cw7YvbYvwT— Bitcoin Magazine (@BitcoinMagazine) September 17, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nJPMorgan Says Bitcoin Could Beat Gold as Analyst Predicts It''ll ''Triple'' Gold\n\nLowering Portfolio Risk\n\nEdelman argues Bitcoin fundamentally improves standard portfolio management. For decades, the traditional 60/40 split of stocks and bonds served as the foundation of wealth management, but elevated macroeconomic risks have forced advisors to adapt.\n\nEdelman notes wealth managers now target a 2% Bitcoin allocation to improve risk-adjusted returns. Because the asset moves independently of traditional markets—or “zigs when the others zag”—it provides crucial rebalancing opportunities.\n\nThe addition of Bitcoin “actually lowers the risk,” Edelman explained, pointing to 16 years of historical performance data and established metrics like the Sharpe ratio.\n\nTokenization and the $500,000 Target\n\nLooking ahead, Edelman projects Bitcoin will reach $500,000 by 2030. He bases this calculation on a simple global adoption metric rather than technical market analysis. Edelman says a 1% allocation of global assets to Bitcoin would imply a price of roughly $500,000 per coin.\n\nHe characterized this projection as conservative, suggesting the price could climb higher and hit the target before the end of the decade. Additionally, Edelman predicts Wall Street will rapidly tokenize real-world assets, calling real estate tokenization the upcoming “holy grail” of the industry.\n\nHow Has BTC Performed?\n\nAt the last check, BTC was 1.40% higher at $77,442.97 per coin in the last 24 hours. It was down by 38.5% from its Oct. 6, 2025, all-time high of $126,080 per coin.\n\nWhile the cryptocurrency was 20.5% higher over the last month, it was 34.1% lower over the year.\n\nRead Also:\n\nPeter Schiff: Bitcoin Failed ''Digital Gold'' Test, Higher Yields Could Hurt BTC\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'b02a77c820916769afee59124f90f638c12b6024','2026-09-18 08:14:46','2026-09-18 08:19:50.676379',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 08:14:46');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(380,'alpaca:61862065','benzinga','2026-09-18 09:14:22','Stock Market Today: S&P 500, Dow Futures Pare Gains, Nasdaq 100 Up as Trump Weighs ''Big Decision'' on Iran Military Strikes— OKLO, MCD, BB, NUE in Focus (UPDATED)','U.S. stock futures advanced on Friday, as the Dow Jones, S&amp;P 500 and Nasdaq 100 indices rose, following Thursday&#39;s higher close.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61862065/stock-market-today-sp-500-nasdaq-100-futures-rise-as-trump-weighs-big-decision-on-iran-military-strikes-oklo-mcd-bb-nue-in-focus','["BTC/USD", "QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-18 13:20:57.862104','macro','neutral',2,3,'hours',1,'Stock market movements are impacted by macroeconomic events and geopolitical news.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 6.107}}','2026-09-19 09:23:41.422619','2026-09-18 09:19:59.796208','61862065',replace('Editor’s Note: The ETFs tracking benchmark indices, the lede, and the headline were updated in the story.\n\nU.S. stock futures turned mixed on Friday, as the Dow Jones, S&P; 500 indices fell, and the Nasdaq 100 index rose, following Thursday’s higher close.\n\nCrude oil slipped while gas prices continued to climb as President Donald Trump weighs a “big decision” on potential military strikes against Iran ahead of upcoming talks with Gulf leaders regarding a postwar endgame. \n\nThe escalating Middle East tension comes alongside reports of a tanker detained by Iranian forces and warnings from former counterterrorism chief Joe Kent that “there is no military solution.”\n\nMeanwhile, the 10-year Treasury bond yielded 4.94%, and the 2-year Treasury bond yielded 4.69% at the last check. The CME Group’s FedWatch tool projections show markets pricing in a 53.1% likelihood of the Federal Reserve hiking interest rates after its October meeting.\n\nIndexPerformance (+/-)Dow Jones-0.31%S&P; 500-0.09%Nasdaq 1000.09%Russell 2000-0.39%\n\nThe SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 index and Nasdaq 100 index, respectively, were mixed in premarket trading on Friday. The SPY was down 0.059% at $760.26, while the QQQ advanced 0.15% to $717.99.\n\nRead Also:\n\nStock Market: Will S&P; 500 Open Up or Down Today?\n\nStocks In Focus\n\nNucor\n\nNucor Corp. (NYSE:NUE) dropped 3.07% in premarket on Friday despite raising its third-quarter earnings guidance to $5.55 to $5.65 per diluted share, up from $2.63 per share in the year-ago quarter,\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that NUE maintains a strong price trend in the long, short, and medium terms, with a moderate growth score.\n\nBlackBerry\n\nBlackBerry Ltd. (NYSE:BB) was 1.76% higher following a partnership announcement between Sift, a data infrastructure platform for mission-critical hardware, and QNX, BlackBerry’s embedded software division.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that BB maintains a weak price trend in the short and medium terms but a strong trend in the long term, with a poor value score.\n\n5E Advanced Materials\n\n5E Advanced Materials Inc. (NASDAQ:FEAM) dropped 4.37% as it posted a loss of 14 cents per share for the fourth quarter, compared to market estimates of a loss of 32 cents per share.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that FEAM maintains a strong price trend in the medium and short terms, but a strong trend in the long term.\n\nMcDonald’s\n\nMcDonald’s Corp. (NYSE:MCD) was 0.41% higher as it raised its quarterly dividend from $1.86 to $1.93 per share.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that MCD maintains a weak price trend in the long, medium and short terms with a poor value score.\n\nOklo\n\nOklo Inc. (NYSE:OKLO) was 1.34% higher in premarket on Friday following House approval of a plan requiring large data centers to absorb more of their own grid infrastructure costs. The legislation boosted investor interest in dedicated energy providers; however, no nuclear firm secured new contracts as a result of the vote.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that OKLO maintains a weak price trend in the long, medium, and short terms.\n\nRead Also:\n\nRic Edelman Predicts $500,000 Bitcoin by 2030, Says BTC Could Follow Amazon’s 1999 Trajectory: ‘Everybody Owns It’\n\nCues From Last Session\n\nInformation technology, consumer discretionary, and utilities stocks recorded the biggest gains on Thursday, while financial and consumer staples bucked the market trend to close lower.\n\nIndexPerformance (+/-)ValueDow Jones0.61%51,778.04S&P; 5001.14%7,637.76Nasdaq Composite1.69%26,418.30Russell 20000.55%2,874.63\n\nInsights From Analysts\n\nInvestment strategy analyst at Wells Fargo, Tony Miano projects that heavy public and private debt issuance will drive U.S. bond yields higher and weigh on fixed-income returns, though he remains optimistic about long-term economic growth.\n\nMiano notes that corporate borrowing to fund artificial intelligence infrastructure will ultimately boost overall productivity. He emphasizes that “investing in technology makes workers and machines more productive and, over time, promotes stronger economic growth.”\n\nWhile acknowledging that “the U.S. Treasury’s current pace of borrowing is unsustainable,” Miano reassures investors that default is neither “imminent or inevitable” because corporate earnings remain resilient.\n\nRather than signaling market panic, rising yields reflect that “investors want to be paid more as more debt issuers—public and private—come to the marketplace.”\n\nBecause “this surge of borrowing seems unlikely to end soon, which should pressure yields higher,” Miano foresees ongoing yield pressure. To navigate this environment, he expects better stability in short-term fixed income, recommending that investors allocate new cash there while holding existing long-term bonds to maturity.\n\nUpcoming Economic Data\n\nHere’s what investors will be keeping an eye on Friday:\n\nIndustrial production data for August will be released by 9:15 a.m. ET.\n\nCommodities, Crypto, And Global Equity Markets\n\nCrude Oil WTI futures were trading lower in the early New York session by 1.69% to hover around $100.19 per barrel.\n\nGold Spot US Dollar rose 1.11% to hover around $4,389.84 per ounce. The U.S. Dollar Index spot was 0.06% higher at the 100.3100 level.\n\nMeanwhile, Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) was trading 2.00% higher at $77,939.67 per coin over the last 24 hours.\n\nAsian markets were higher on Friday, except for Australia’s ASX 200 index. Japan’s Nikkei 225, India’s Nifty 50, South Korea’s Kospi, China’s CSI 300, and Hong Kong’s Hang Seng indices rose. European markets were lower in early trading.\n\nRead Also:\n\nS&P; 500 Could Deliver Another 6% by Year-End as JPMorgan Calls Bears an ‘Extinct Species’ — Polymarket Bettors Price 35% Odds\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'ba911df8e03d6e6d952c27a36be52a8fe673b61a','2026-09-18 09:14:22','2026-09-18 09:19:59.786839',2,NULL,'2026-09-18 12:40:46');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(381,'alpaca:61861775','benzinga','2026-09-18 08:53:25','Anthropic Says Claude Now Leads 26% of Its AI R&D, Up From Just 1% in March','Anthropic said Claude led 26% of its AI research in August, highlighting AI’s growing role in developing the next generation of AI.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61861775/anthropic-says-claude-now-leads-26-of-its-ai-rd-up-from-just-1-in-march','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 09:20:05.542239','other','neutral',3,4,'days',1,'Anthropic''s internal shift in AI research focus is a notable update but does not directly impact NVDA''s market position.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 09:23:41.422619','2026-09-18 09:19:59.806867','61861775',replace('On Thursday, Anthropic said Claude is taking on an increasingly central role in the development of the company’s next-generation AI models, with the chatbot now leading more than one-quarter of its measured research and development work.\n\nClaude’s Role In AI Research Surges\n\nIn a blog post, the AI startup said that Claude was responsible for leading 26% of its AI research and development work in August, up sharply from just 1% in March.\n\nThis is based on a measurement framework developed by independent nonprofit Epoch AI.\n\nAnthropic stressed that Claude was not working fully autonomously in any of the areas covered by the measurement. Instead, the figure reflects situations where AI played the leading role while working alongside human researchers.\n\nMore than 90% of Anthropic’s AI R&D; work in August was performed at the "AI collaborates" level or higher, according to the company’s measurement.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAnthropic Nears OpenAI Territory With Reported $800 Billion Valuation Chatter As Explosive Claude Growth And IPO Hopes Ignite Silicon Valley\n\n30,000 AI Agents Work Inside Anthropic\n\nAnthropic said approximately 30,000 AI agents were conducting research and engineering work at any one time on its most-used internal platform in August.\n\nThe company stated it screens every action the agents take before execution. Of more than a billion decisions made during the month, roughly one in 47,000 was blocked.\n\nAnthropic Details AI Safety Spending\n\nClaude parent also disclosed that about 6% of the computing power it used for AI research during a sample week in July went toward safety research. For research conducted by AI itself, the share was approximately 12%.\n\nAnthropic said those figures were conservative because computing used for work that advanced both AI capabilities and safety was classified as capability-related.\n\nAmodei Urges AI Development Slowdown\n\nLast week, Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei called on AI companies to slow the pace of development in an essay published amid growing warnings from researchers about potentially catastrophic risks.\n\nThis came after Anthropic researcher Jacob Coxon resigned, citing concerns over the company’s approach.\n\nAnthropic, OpenAI Seek Massive Funding\n\nEarlier this week, it was reported that Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) is considering investing as much as $10 billion in Anthropic’s potential IPO, as the Claude developer seeks to raise up to $100 billion at a valuation of roughly $2 trillion.\n\nAnthropic rival OpenAI is reportedly holding preliminary talks with major investors about a new funding round that could value the ChatGPT maker at around $1.2 trillion.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAnthropic Is Racing Toward An IPO. Its Co-Founder Wants A Way To Slow AI Down, Says The Industry ''Doesn''t Have A Brake Pedal''\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'ee0825513d768a639987067ca764c4eef6cb7520','2026-09-18 08:53:25','2026-09-18 09:19:59.786839',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 08:53:25');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(382,'alpaca:61861660','benzinga','2026-09-18 08:41:51','Senator Elissa Slotkin Sounds Alarm Over Possible Trump-BYD Meeting: ‘Watch What the President Does, Not What He Says’','Sen. Slotkin warned Thursday that BYD&#39;s CEO joining Xi&#39;s delegation could signal a deal letting Chinese automakers into the U.S','https://www.benzinga.com/news/politics/26/09/61861660/elissa-slotkin-warns-a-trump-byd-meeting-could-cost-michigans-auto-industry-its-jobs','["NVDA", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 09:20:06.728056','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Commentary on potential political implications for automakers.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37, "TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-19 09:23:41.422619','2026-09-18 09:19:59.821758','61861660',replace('Sen. Elissa Slotkin (D-Mich.) warned Thursday that if BYD Co. Ltd.‘s (OTC:BYDDF) (OTC:BYDDY) CEO Wang Chuanfu joins Chinese President Xi Jinping‘s business delegation to the White House next week, it could signal that discussions are underway over whether to allow Chinese automakers greater access to the U.S. market, a move she said would be “a terrible outcome” for Michigan’s auto industry.\n\n‘Watch What the President Does, Not What He Says’\n\n“As always, watch what the President does, not what he says,” Slotkin said in a post on social media platform X.\n\nShe warned that Chinese automakers, “propped up by the Chinese government,” would “undercut our manufacturers and suppliers, wreak havoc on our industry, and take our jobs” if allowed into the country, threatening the 1.2 million Michigan jobs tied to the auto industry.\n\nAs always, watch what the President does, not what he says. If the President of BYD comes with the Chinese President to the White House next week, we can only assume there are deals afoot to allow Chinese cars to be imported, or Chinese companies are being invited to set up shop…— Sen. Elissa Slotkin (@SenatorSlotkin) September 17, 2026 \n\nTrump told Fox News’s Laura Ingraham last week that he would be open to Chinese automakers building cars in the U.S. with American workers, while opposing Chinese-built vehicles being shipped into the U.S. from Mexico.\n\nRead Also:\n\nRic Edelman Predicts $500,000 Bitcoin by 2030, Says BTC Could Follow Amazon’s 1999 Trajectory: ‘Everybody Owns It’\n\nBYD Is Reportedly Under Consideration for Xi’s Delegation\n\nChinese officials are considering BYD founder for Xi’s business delegation ahead of the leaders’ Sept. 24 summit in Washington, Bloomberg reported, citing people familiar with the matter, though the list isn’t final. \n\nThe Pentagon added BYD to its expanded “1260H list” in June, identifying companies it believes have ties to China’s military or defense-industrial sector. \n\nBYD has separately denied Pentagon allegations linking it to China’s military.\n\nA 100% Tariff Wall on Chinese EVs\n\nThe U.S. has slapped a steep 100% tariff on Chinese electric vehicles, effectively shutting Chinese automakers out of the American market entirely.\n\nXi’s business delegation would mark his largest since 2015, when he brought Chinese tech and banking executives to the U.S.\n\nTrump has previously brought large U.S. business delegations to China, including Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang and Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) CEO Elon Musk, with 18 executives joining his May visit.\n\nTrump and Xi are scheduled to meet in Washington on Sept. 24\n\nRead Also:\n\nRobert F. Kennedy Tells Anti-Vaccine Group They Have a ''Strong and Steadfast Friend'' in the White House: Trump Continues to ''Demand Answers''\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'3766a99f79926fd7f4c9319e4edd2bcd9b6d67e3','2026-09-18 08:41:51','2026-09-18 09:19:59.786839',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 08:41:51');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(383,'alpaca:61862668','benzinga','2026-09-18 09:59:47','Charlie Bilello Warns of $100 Billion Iran War Fuel Shock as $4.43 Gas Prices Show the ‘Inflation Problem’ Isn’t Over','Charlie Bilello explains how record $4.43 gas prices act as a $100 billion tax on consumers, proving the inflation problem is far from over.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/commodities/26/09/61862668/charlie-bilello-warns-of-100-billion-iran-war-fuel-shock-as-4-43-gas-prices-show-the-inflation-problem-isnt-over','["QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-18 10:20:16.571013','macro','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'Rising gas prices indicate ongoing inflation concerns that may impact consumer spending and overall market confidence.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-19 10:23:45.858906','2026-09-18 10:20:12.495255','61862668',replace('U.S. gas prices hit a record $4.43 per gallon for September, driven by the ongoing war in Iran. Market strategist Charlie Bilello warns that this energy surge adds a $100 billion burden on consumers, signaling that the broader inflation problem is far from over.\n\nWar Drives Energy Prices Higher\n\nCrude oil has crossed $100 a barrel following the prolonged war in Iran over the Strait of Hormuz. At the last check, Brent Crude futures were down 2.10% to $102.63, and WTI Crude futures were down 1.67% to $100.21 per barrel.\n\nThe disruption has pushed U.S. gasoline prices up 45% to $4.35 a gallon on Thursday, while diesel has surged 67% to a record high above $6 a gallon.\n\nJet fuel and agricultural commodities like wheat, corn, and fertilizer have also spiked. Bilello emphasizes that elevated energy and transportation costs will “take time to feed” into broader consumer prices.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBond King Jeffrey Gundlach Wants Out of the AI ''Epicenter'': Inside His Zero-Exposure Portfolio\n\nA $100 Billion Burden on Consumers\n\nThe surge in fuel costs represents an added burden on American households exceeding $100 billion. This burden far outpaces the projected $69 billion Americans will spend this year on nursery, elementary, and secondary education combined.\n\nBilello points out that consumer prices have risen at a 4% annualized rate since January 2020, roughly twice the Federal Reserve’s 2% inflation target, even as the Cleveland Fed projects September CPI inflation could reach 3.49% to 4%.\n\nRecent data show the pressure on purchasing power: real average hourly earnings fell 0.1% in August and were down 0.3% from a year earlier, according to the Bureau of Labor Statistics.\n\nThe Fed’s Tightening Dilemma\n\nRising energy prices have forced the Fed to adjust policy. Under Chairman Kevin Warsh, the Fed unanimously raised the federal funds rate by 25 basis points to a range of 3.75% to 4.00%. Warsh noted that “the plain fact is that inflation is too high and has been for too long.”\n\nWith the 2-year Treasury yield trading near 4.69%, Bilello notes the market signals the Fed remains behind the curve. He argued that persistently elevated energy prices could keep upward pressure on inflation and interest rates unless oil prices fall sharply.\n\nHow Have Stocks and Bonds Performed in 2026?\n\nAt the last check, the 30-year Treasury bond yielded 5.28%, the 10-year Treasury bond was at 4.94%, and the two-year bond was at 4.69%.\n\nThe primary ETF specifically tracking the long end of the U.S. Treasury yield curve—including the 30-year benchmark bond—is the iShares 20+ Year Treasury Bond ETF (NASDAQ:TLT), which closed 1.11% higher at $81.78 on Thursday. It was down 6.92% year-to-date, up 0.53% over the last month and 9.25% over the last year.\n\nThe S&P; 500 index has advanced 11.36% year-to-date. Similarly, the Nasdaq Composite index was up 13.70%, and the Dow Jones gained 7.02% YTD.\n\nOn Thursday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed higher. SPY rose 1.13% to $762.60, while QQQ rose 1.73% to $716.92. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), also ended 0.61% higher at $518.35.\n\nIn premarket on Friday, SPY was up 0.30%, QQQ gained 0.53%, and DIA advanced 0.17%.\n\nRead Also:\n\nRic Edelman Predicts $500,000 Bitcoin by 2030, Says BTC Could Follow Amazon’s 1999 Trajectory: ‘Everybody Owns It’\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'87bc4390d89df3836cb6353ad924d1386ac617f3','2026-09-18 09:59:47','2026-09-18 10:20:12.477317',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 09:59:47');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(384,'alpaca:61862613','benzinga','2026-09-18 09:58:34','Insights Into Amazon.com''s Performance Versus Peers In Broadline Retail Sector','In the ever-evolving and intensely competitive business landscape, conducting a thorough company analysis is of utmost importance for investors and industry followers. In this article, we will carry out an in-depth','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61862613/insights-amazon-com-s-performance-versus-peers-broadline-retail-sector','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-18 10:20:18.136144','other','neutral',1,2,'days',1,'The article provides insights but does not indicate a clear impact on Amazon''s price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18}','{}','2026-09-19 10:23:45.858906','2026-09-18 10:20:12.498481','61862613',replace('In the ever-evolving and intensely competitive business landscape, conducting a thorough company analysis is of utmost importance for investors and industry followers. In this article, we will carry out an in-depth industry comparison, assessing Amazon.com (NASDAQ:AMZN) alongside its primary competitors in the Broadline Retail industry. By meticulously examining key financial metrics, market positioning, and growth prospects, we aim to offer valuable insights to investors and shed light on company''s performance within the industry.\nAmazon.com Background\nAmazon is the leading online retailer and marketplace for third party sellers. Retail related revenue represents approximately 74% of total, followed by Amazon Web Services (17%), and advertising services (9%). International segments constitute 22% of Amazon''s total revenue, led by Germany, the United Kingdom, and Japan.\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nAmazon.com Inc\n20.21\n4.91\n3.52\n12.61%\n$102.16\n$104.83\n19.62%\n\nMercadoLibre Inc\n49.65\n11.81\n2.63\n6.17%\n$0.96\n$4.16\n49.76%\n\neBay Inc\n23.72\n10.77\n4.32\n12.12%\n$0.83\n$2.3\n14.8%\n\nDillard''s Inc\n14.53\n4.67\n1.50\n4.71%\n$0.17\n$0.62\n-0.36%\n\nGlobal E Online Ltd\n43.61\n7.13\n6.19\n5.26%\n$0.05\n$0.13\n39.15%\n\nMacy''s Inc\n7.93\n1.15\n0.26\n3.46%\n$0.46\n$2.21\n1.2%\n\nOllie''s Bargain Outlet Holdings Inc\n17.04\n2.39\n1.67\n4.51%\n$0.13\n$0.32\n9.09%\n\nKohl''s Corp\n7.17\n0.45\n0.13\n3.69%\n$0.43\n$1.62\n-0.87%\n\nSavers Value Village Inc\n61.73\n3.19\n0.86\n4.95%\n$0.07\n$0.25\n7.43%\n\nHour Loop Inc\n43.50\n6.89\n0.40\n12.6%\n$0.0\n$0.02\n25.24%\n\nAverage\n29.88\n5.38\n2.0\n6.39%\n$0.34\n$1.29\n16.16%\n\nBy thoroughly analyzing Amazon.com, we can discern the following trends: \n\nA Price to Earnings ratio of 20.21 significantly below the industry average by 0.68x suggests undervaluation. This can make the stock appealing for those seeking growth.\n\nWith a Price to Book ratio of 4.91, significantly falling below the industry average by 0.91x, it suggests undervaluation and the possibility of untapped growth prospects.\n\nThe Price to Sales ratio of 3.52, which is 1.76x the industry average, suggests the stock could potentially be overvalued in relation to its sales performance compared to its peers.\n\nWith a Return on Equity (ROE) of 12.61% that is 6.22% above the industry average, it appears that the company exhibits efficient use of equity to generate profits.\n\nWith higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $102.16 Billion, which is 300.47x above the industry average, the company demonstrates stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nThe gross profit of $104.83 Billion is 81.26x above that of its industry, highlighting stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nThe company''s revenue growth of 19.62% exceeds the industry average of 16.16%, indicating strong sales performance and market outperformance.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio is a measure that indicates the level of debt a company has taken on relative to the value of its assets net of liabilities.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nIn light of the Debt-to-Equity ratio, a comparison between Amazon.com and its top 4 peers reveals the following information:\n\nWhen comparing the debt-to-equity ratio, Amazon.com is in a stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers.\n\nThe company has a lower level of debt relative to its equity, indicating a more favorable balance between the two with a lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.4.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor Amazon.com, the PE and PB ratios suggest that the stock is undervalued compared to its peers in the Broadline Retail industry. However, the high PS ratio indicates that the stock may be overvalued based on revenue. In terms of ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and revenue growth, Amazon.com outperforms its industry peers, showcasing strong financial health and growth potential.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'b552b13cad9772d124eaa195e9b5394c53e7504d','2026-09-18 09:58:34','2026-09-18 10:20:12.477317',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 09:58:34');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(385,'alpaca:61862612','benzinga','2026-09-18 09:58:30','Industry Comparison: Evaluating Microsoft Against Competitors In Software Industry','In the ever-evolving and intensely competitive business landscape, conducting a thorough company analysis is of utmost importance for investors and industry followers. In this article, we will carry out an in-depth','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61862612/industry-comparison-evaluating-microsoft-against-competitors-software-industry','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-18 10:20:19.670874','other','neutral',1,1,'weeks',1,'The headline discusses an industry comparison without specific impacts on price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 498.48}','{}','2026-09-19 10:23:45.858906','2026-09-18 10:20:12.500641','61862612',replace('In the ever-evolving and intensely competitive business landscape, conducting a thorough company analysis is of utmost importance for investors and industry followers. In this article, we will carry out an in-depth industry comparison, assessing Microsoft (NASDAQ:MSFT) alongside its primary competitors in the Software industry. By meticulously examining key financial metrics, market positioning, and growth prospects, we aim to offer valuable insights to investors and shed light on company''s performance within the industry.\nMicrosoft Background\nMicrosoft develops and licenses consumer and enterprise software. It is known for its Windows operating systems and Office productivity suite. The company is organized into three equally sized broad segments: productivity and business processes (legacy Microsoft Office, cloud-based Office 365, Exchange, SharePoint, Skype, LinkedIn, Dynamics), intelligence cloud (infrastructure- and platform-as-a-service offerings Azure, Windows Server OS, SQL Server), and more personal computing (Windows Client, Xbox, Bing search, display advertising, and Surface laptops, tablets, and desktops).\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nMicrosoft Corp\n27.73\n8.35\n11.18\n8.35%\n$55.91\n$60.48\n17.75%\n\nOracle Corp\n23.60\n7.37\n6.16\n9.42%\n$10.39\n$11.61\n29.61%\n\nPalo Alto Networks Inc\n937.65\n11.16\n24.96\n-1.02%\n$0.07\n$2.3\n34.46%\n\nCrowdStrike Holdings Inc\n6552\n49.31\n46.58\n0.11%\n$0.11\n$1.1\n25.83%\n\nServiceNow Inc\n86.54\n11.44\n9.79\n2.46%\n$0.91\n$2.82\n24.01%\n\nFortinet Inc\n60.98\n81.64\n17.15\n47.73%\n$0.76\n$1.64\n25.64%\n\nGen Digital Inc\n17.67\n6.81\n3.65\n8.16%\n$0.57\n$1.03\n6.28%\n\nCheck Point Software Technologies Ltd\n13.97\n5.08\n5.27\n6.98%\n$0.2\n$0.57\n1.26%\n\nUiPath Inc\n20.54\n3.68\n4.29\n1.87%\n$0.04\n$0.33\n13.42%\n\nQualys Inc\n30.94\n10.97\n9.08\n9.26%\n$0.06\n$0.15\n11.04%\n\nCommVault Systems Inc\n95.38\n118.47\n5.36\n71.0%\n$0.04\n$0.26\n11.4%\n\nDolby Laboratories Inc\n24.46\n2.08\n4.08\n1.1%\n$0.06\n$0.26\n-3.34%\n\nBlackBerry Ltd\n79.40\n6.20\n8.15\n1.14%\n$0.02\n$0.12\n25.64%\n\nTenable Holdings Inc\n601\n20.02\n4.07\n1.7%\n$0.02\n$0.21\n8.58%\n\nMonday.Com Ltd\n38.28\n6.18\n3.30\n0.5%\n$0.02\n$0.32\n21.94%\n\nTeradata Corp\n6.16\n4.59\n1.67\n8.0%\n$0.08\n$0.24\n0.49%\n\nAverage\n572.57\n23.0\n10.24\n11.23%\n$0.89\n$1.53\n15.75%\n\nBy conducting an in-depth analysis of Microsoft, we can identify the following trends: \n\nThe Price to Earnings ratio of 27.73 is 0.05x lower than the industry average, indicating potential undervaluation for the stock.\n\nConsidering a Price to Book ratio of 8.35, which is well below the industry average by 0.36x, the stock may be undervalued based on its book value compared to its peers.\n\nThe Price to Sales ratio of 11.18, which is 1.09x the industry average, suggests the stock could potentially be overvalued in relation to its sales performance compared to its peers.\n\nWith a Return on Equity (ROE) of 8.35% that is 2.88% below the industry average, it appears that the company exhibits potential inefficiency in utilizing equity to generate profits.\n\nThe company has higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $55.91 Billion, which is 62.82x above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nThe company has higher gross profit of $60.48 Billion, which indicates 39.53x above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nThe company is experiencing remarkable revenue growth, with a rate of 17.75%, outperforming the industry average of 15.75%.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio provides insights into the proportion of debt a company has in relation to its equity and asset value.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nWhen comparing Microsoft with its top 4 peers based on the Debt-to-Equity ratio, the following insights can be observed:\n\nMicrosoft is in a relatively stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers, as evidenced by its lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.13.\n\nThis implies that the company relies less on debt financing and has a more favorable balance between debt and equity.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor Microsoft in the Software industry, the PE and PB ratios suggest the stock is undervalued compared to peers, indicating potential for growth. However, the high PS ratio implies the stock may be overvalued based on revenue. In terms of ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and revenue growth, Microsoft shows strong performance and growth potential, outperforming industry peers.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'bee0c3b02e653cc43f6884c503d647a8e806ecfc','2026-09-18 09:58:30','2026-09-18 10:20:12.477317',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 09:58:30');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(386,'alpaca:61862611','benzinga','2026-09-18 09:58:27','Performance Comparison: Apple And Competitors In Technology Hardware, Storage &amp; Peripherals Industry','In today&#39;s rapidly changing and highly competitive business world, it is imperative for investors and industry observers to carefully assess companies before making investment choices. In this article, we will','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61862611/performance-comparison-apple-and-competitors-technology-hardware-storage-amp-peripherals-industry','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-18 10:20:21.026217','other','neutral',1,2,'days',1,'The headline is a performance comparison without a specific impact on the stock price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}','2026-09-19 10:23:45.858906','2026-09-18 10:20:12.502764','61862611',replace('In today''s rapidly changing and highly competitive business world, it is imperative for investors and industry observers to carefully assess companies before making investment choices. In this article, we will undertake a comprehensive industry comparison, evaluating Apple (NASDAQ:AAPL) vis-à-vis its key competitors in the Technology Hardware, Storage & Peripherals industry. Through a detailed analysis of important financial indicators, market standing, and growth potential, our goal is to provide valuable insights and highlight company''s performance in the industry.\nApple Background\nApple is among the largest companies in the world, with a broad portfolio of hardware and software products targeted at consumers and businesses. Apple''s iPhone accounts for the majority of the firm''s sales, and Apple''s other products, such as the Mac, iPad, and Watch, are designed around the iPhone as the focal point of an expansive software ecosystem. Apple has progressively worked to add new applications, such as streaming video, subscription bundles, and augmented reality. The firm designs its own software and semiconductors and works with subcontractors such as Foxconn and TSMC to build its products and chips. Slightly less than half of Apple''s sales come directly through its flagship stores, with the majority coming indirectly through partnerships and distribution.\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nApple Inc\n38.65\n45.74\n10.67\n27.84%\n$39.02\n$54.77\n16.36%\n\nSanDisk Corp\n21.89\n15.02\n12.36\n46.78%\n$7.89\n$7.58\n371.59%\n\nSeagate Technology Holdings PLC\n57.78\n84.28\n15.08\n79.34%\n$1.64\n$1.9\n48.49%\n\nWestern Digital Corp\n15.75\n17.24\n12.57\n34.3%\n$3.36\n$2.03\n43.84%\n\nHewlett Packard Enterprise Co\n31.46\n3.06\n2.06\n5.83%\n$2.33\n$4.9\n33.68%\n\nNetApp Inc\n27.81\n25.87\n5.34\n26.35%\n$0.55\n$1.42\n29.89%\n\nEverpure Inc\n142.45\n22.49\n8.46\n4.97%\n$0.11\n$0.81\n37.73%\n\nSuper Micro Computer Inc\n12.38\n2.59\n0.72\n12.83%\n$1.57\n$1.94\n93.16%\n\nLogitech International SA\n18.81\n6.24\n3.07\n10.33%\n$0.28\n$0.61\n6.93%\n\nDiebold Nixdorf Inc\n21.02\n2.22\n0.59\n1.56%\n$0.09\n$0.24\n1.7%\n\nCorsair Gaming Inc\n43.58\n2.20\n1\n1.04%\n$0.02\n$0.1\n-1.8%\n\nImmersion Corp\n22.12\n0.84\n0.14\n1.93%\n$0.01\n$0.06\n0.81%\n\nAverage\n37.73\n16.55\n5.58\n20.48%\n$1.62\n$1.96\n60.55%\n\nThrough an analysis of Apple, we can infer the following trends: \n\nNotably, the current Price to Earnings ratio for this stock, 38.65, is 1.02x above the industry norm, reflecting a higher valuation relative to the industry.\n\nWith a Price to Book ratio of 45.74, which is 2.76x the industry average, Apple might be considered overvalued in terms of its book value, as it is trading at a higher multiple compared to its industry peers.\n\nThe stock''s relatively high Price to Sales ratio of 10.67, surpassing the industry average by 1.91x, may indicate an aspect of overvaluation in terms of sales performance.\n\nThe Return on Equity (ROE) of 27.84% is 7.36% above the industry average, highlighting efficient use of equity to generate profits.\n\nThe company has higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $39.02 Billion, which is 24.09x above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nThe company has higher gross profit of $54.77 Billion, which indicates 27.94x above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nThe company''s revenue growth of 16.36% is significantly below the industry average of 60.55%. This suggests a potential struggle in generating increased sales volume.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio is a measure that indicates the level of debt a company has taken on relative to the value of its assets net of liabilities.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nIn terms of the Debt-to-Equity ratio, Apple can be assessed by comparing it to its top 4 peers, resulting in the following observations:\n\nCompared to its top 4 peers, Apple has a stronger financial position indicated by its lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.78.\n\nThis suggests that the company relies less on debt financing and has a more favorable balance between debt and equity, which can be seen as a positive attribute by investors.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor Apple, the PE, PB, and PS ratios are all high compared to its peers in the Technology Hardware, Storage & Peripherals industry, indicating potentially overvalued stock. On the other hand, Apple''s high ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and low revenue growth suggest strong operational efficiency and profitability relative to industry competitors.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'67ef5f5c0df6bb5e19d258cbfe9a0a08a41270d9','2026-09-18 09:58:27','2026-09-18 10:20:12.477317',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 09:58:27');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(387,'alpaca:61862610','benzinga','2026-09-18 09:58:22','Exploring The Competitive Space: NVIDIA Versus Industry Peers In Semiconductors &amp; Semiconductor Equipment','Amidst the fast-paced and highly competitive business environment of today, conducting comprehensive company analysis is essential for investors and industry enthusiasts. In this article, we will delve into an extensive','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61862610/exploring-competitive-space-nvidia-versus-industry-peers-semiconductors-amp-semiconductor-equipment','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 10:20:21.883189','other','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'The headline suggests an analysis article but does not provide actionable news.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 10:23:45.858906','2026-09-18 10:20:12.504883','61862610',replace('Amidst the fast-paced and highly competitive business environment of today, conducting comprehensive company analysis is essential for investors and industry enthusiasts. In this article, we will delve into an extensive industry comparison, evaluating NVIDIA (NASDAQ:NVDA) in comparison to its major competitors within the Semiconductors & Semiconductor Equipment industry. By analyzing critical financial metrics, market position, and growth potential, our objective is to provide valuable insights for investors and offer a deeper understanding of company''s performance in the industry.\nNVIDIA Background\nNvidia is a leading developer of graphics processing units. Traditionally, GPUs were used to enhance the experience on computing platforms, most notably in gaming applications on PCs. GPU use cases have since emerged as important semiconductors used in artificial intelligence to run large language models. Nvidia not only offers AI GPUs, but also a software platform, Cuda, used for AI model development and training. Nvidia is also expanding its data center networking solutions, helping to tie GPUs together to handle complex workloads.\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nNVIDIA Corp\n27.73\n23.13\n17.66\n28.12%\n$72.86\n$72.14\n105.85%\n\nBroadcom Inc\n44.30\n16.63\n19.04\n13.97%\n$18.27\n$20.46\n85.5%\n\nMicron Technology Inc\n22.10\n10.96\n12.34\n32.62%\n$35.58\n$35.06\n345.72%\n\nAdvanced Micro Devices Inc\n139.05\n13.24\n21.77\n3.49%\n$3.35\n$6.2\n50.11%\n\nTexas Instruments Inc\n39.23\n13.09\n12.14\n11.32%\n$2.95\n$3.35\n22.82%\n\nMarvell Technology Inc\n79.72\n11.68\n22.59\n1.68%\n$0.77\n$1.46\n36.55%\n\nQualcomm Inc\n21.57\n7.29\n4.61\n7.29%\n$3.04\n$5.28\n-4.03%\n\nAnalog Devices Inc\n43.07\n5.24\n12.83\n3.98%\n$2.13\n$2.71\n39.63%\n\nNXP Semiconductors NV\n19.45\n5.04\n4.39\n6.87%\n$1.27\n$2.0\n19.48%\n\nMonolithic Power Systems Inc\n71.36\n14.75\n17.48\n6.8%\n$0.32\n$0.54\n47.56%\n\nMicrochip Technology Inc\n104.15\n5.96\n7.58\n3.14%\n$0.49\n$0.94\n38.05%\n\nCredo Technology Group Holding Ltd\n59.24\n11.59\n20.16\n5.4%\n$0.14\n$0.31\n114.73%\n\nON Semiconductor Corp\n44.64\n3.68\n4.45\n3.12%\n$0.43\n$0.62\n9.18%\n\nGLOBALFOUNDRIES Inc\n35.81\n2.16\n3.69\n1.41%\n$0.48\n$0.51\n5.81%\n\nTower Semiconductor Ltd\n86.66\n8.03\n14.64\n2.99%\n$0.17\n$0.14\n23.66%\n\nFirst Solar Inc\n12.40\n2.09\n4.03\n4.18%\n$0.61\n$0.61\n-3.73%\n\nMACOM Technology Solutions Holdings Inc\n83.80\n13.04\n17.36\n6.81%\n$0.14\n$0.2\n35.77%\n\nAverage\n56.66\n9.03\n12.44\n7.19%\n$4.38\n$5.02\n54.18%\n\nWhen closely examining NVIDIA, the following trends emerge: \n\nA Price to Earnings ratio of 27.73 significantly below the industry average by 0.49x suggests undervaluation. This can make the stock appealing for those seeking growth.\n\nIt could be trading at a premium in relation to its book value, as indicated by its Price to Book ratio of 23.13 which exceeds the industry average by 2.56x.\n\nThe stock''s relatively high Price to Sales ratio of 17.66, surpassing the industry average by 1.42x, may indicate an aspect of overvaluation in terms of sales performance.\n\nThe Return on Equity (ROE) of 28.12% is 20.93% above the industry average, highlighting efficient use of equity to generate profits.\n\nThe Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $72.86 Billion is 16.63x above the industry average, highlighting stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nCompared to its industry, the company has higher gross profit of $72.14 Billion, which indicates 14.37x above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nThe company''s revenue growth of 105.85% exceeds the industry average of 54.18%, indicating strong sales performance and market outperformance.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio helps evaluate the capital structure and financial leverage of a company.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nWhen examining NVIDIA in comparison to its top 4 peers with respect to the Debt-to-Equity ratio, the following information becomes apparent:\n\nNVIDIA demonstrates a stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers in the sector.\n\nWith a lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.17, the company relies less on debt financing and maintains a healthier balance between debt and equity, which can be viewed positively by investors.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor NVIDIA in the Semiconductors & Semiconductor Equipment industry, the PE, PB, and PS ratios indicate that the stock is relatively undervalued compared to its peers. However, the high ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and revenue growth suggest that NVIDIA is performing exceptionally well in terms of profitability and operational efficiency within the industry sector.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'a3eca45885a61654b8720913ec7a882323667872','2026-09-18 09:58:22','2026-09-18 10:20:12.477317',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 09:58:22');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(388,'alpaca:61862598','benzinga','2026-09-18 09:56:36','$105 Oil Is Quietly Engineering Its Own Demise','Oil tops $105 as the Iran conflict tightens markets. JPMorgan abandons base-case models, signaling accelerated EV adoption ahead.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/commodities/26/09/61862598/105-oil-is-quietly-engineering-its-own-demise','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 10:20:22.947680','macro','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'Increased oil prices may lead to faster adoption of electric vehicles, negatively impacting oil demand.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-19 10:23:45.858906','2026-09-18 10:20:12.509846','61862598',replace('Seven months into the Iran war, crude has once again touched above $105 a barrel, just weeks after trading as low as $68. Refined-product markets have tightened systemically, forcing commodity desks to abandon the models they relied on when hostilities began.The strain is now as physical as it is financial. Saudi Arabia shut its 7 million barrel-a-day East-West pipeline after a drone strike from Iraq, removing the largest overland bypass to the Strait of Hormuz, where daily transits remain in the low teens, against more than 120 before the conflict.Diesel is the acute pressure point. Wholesale prices have averaged $161 a barrel over the past six months, 59% above pre-war expectations, according to the Center for Research on Energy and Clean Air.The turmoil has spread to the bond market, with 10-year Treasury trading above 5% this week, and inflation fears contributing to the unanimous interest rate hike.In short, the market has exhausted the predictable bounds of conflict containment. With JPMorgan declaring the endgame impossible to model, the prolonged shock risks something more durable than a spike — structural demand destruction through faster EV adoption.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Growth Stocks\n\nJPMorgan Abandons Its Base CaseJPMorgan entered the war expecting a clear playbook – once oil topped $100, gasoline neared $5 a gallon, and 10-year yields crossed 5%, Washington would be compelled to negotiate a lasting Hormuz pact.Two of three lines have now been crossed, yet the off-ramps have vanished since June’s brief truce collapsed within weeks.“For the first time since the start of the Iran conflict, we don’t have a baseline view,” Natasha Kaneva, the bank’s head of global commodities strategy, wrote in a note to clients. “We simply don’t know how to model the endgame.”Fundamentals and risk premiums have dislocated. According to Bloomberg, the bank puts Brent’s September fair value near $90 a barrel, yet even the latest pullback, the spot still trades around $100.Buffers that cushioned the shock are thinning. Demand running more than 4 million barrels a day below year-earlier levels and record U.S. output held inventory draws to about 555 million barrels, a third of JPMorgan’s initial projection. But Chinese refiners are reaccelerating runs to capture wide diesel margins.The bank flagged the Sept. 24 Trump–Xi meeting in Washington as the last near-term inflection point before disruptions are priced as structural.High Prices as an EV CatalystConventional wisdom held that EV sales were insulated from fuel prices. Persistent fuel inflation, paired with affordable mass-market EVs from Chinese manufacturers, Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA), Volkswagen AG (OTC:VWAGY) and Hyundai Motor Co. (OTC:HYMTF), is upending that thesis.Momentum is fractured. French BEV sales rose 69% through July, Germany’s 51%, and BEVs are expected to reach about 40% of Chinese sales this year. Tariff-shielded U.S. automakers lag at roughly 6%.Wood Mackenzie’s latest report maps a scenario where the 2040 global EV fleet is about 50% larger than its base case. The consultancy also notes that commodity material constraints like copper, lithium, and grid capacity represent manageable friction rather than a hard barrier.Still, achieving that accelerated trajectory requires overcoming three hurdles: supply chains diversified away from China, continued fast-charging breakthroughs, and consumer conviction that volatile fuel costs are permanent.“The electrification of road transport was already under way,” wrote Ed Crooks, Wood Mackenzie’s vice chair for the Americas. “The conflict in the Middle East could supercharge it.”Image via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Weighs ''Big Decision'' Amid Iran War as Ex-Counterterrorism Chief Warns ''There Is No Military Solution''','\n',char(10)),'a543ce1213f3a523ec9d8989a14808c8ae0e7e69','2026-09-18 09:56:36','2026-09-18 10:20:12.477317',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 09:56:36');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(389,'alpaca:61862259','benzinga','2026-09-18 09:36:41','Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Expects Chip Sales To Double Next Year as He Downplays AI Slowdown Calls: ''When a Product is Not Safe...''','Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang expects chip sales to double next year as AI demand surges, while discussing AI safety at a U.K. summit.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61862259/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-expects-chip-sales-to-double-next-year-as-he-downplays-ai-slowdown-calls-when-a-product-is-not-safe','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 10:20:23.765383','guidance','bullish',3,3,'weeks',1,'CEO''s optimistic sales outlook suggests strong future demand for products.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 10:23:45.858906','2026-09-18 10:20:12.521096','61862259',replace('Nvidia Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang expects the company to double its chip sales in the coming year.\n\n“I expect Nvidia to sell twice as many chips as this next year as we do this year,” Huang said at a summit with King Charles III in Scotland on Thursday, CNBC reported. He attributed this expected growth to rising demand for AI across sectors and economies. “You can see that in almost every single country that we’re in, people want to invest in AI,” he said.\n\nNvidia does not disclose its total chip sales volume. In the GTC October 2025 Keynote, Huang reported that Nvidia had shipped 6 million Blackwell GPUs in the four quarters.\n\nThe Nvidia CEO, alongside representatives from Alphabet Inc.‘s Google (NASDAQ:GOOG) (NASDAQ:GOOG), DeepMind, OpenAI and Anthropic, attended the U.K. summit to discuss AI safety, an issue that has drawn growing attention amid concerns over humanity’s ability to control increasingly advanced AI.\n\nHuang, who has acknowledged AI safety issues but pushed back on a broader slowdown call, said, "When a product is not safe, we should hold it back and keep engineering it." \n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia Is Fighting the AI Slowdown Narrative—With Power as Its Next Problem\n\nHuang Sees AI Spending Surge Ahead\n\nEarlier this month, Huang described Nvidia as the ‘World’s First and Only Growth Value Stock’, positioning its expanding AI platform, broad customer base, and infrastructure partnerships to capture the next phase of global AI spending. He anticipates AI infrastructure spending to reach $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\n\nHuang’s comments follow Nvidia CFO Colette Kress’s projection of approximately 70% revenue growth for the fiscal year ending January 2028, as discussed during the company’s Q2 earnings call. \n\nEarlier this month, Huang emphasized the value of AI computing hardware as a financeable asset. He noted that the rental prices for Nvidia’s older H100 GPUs continue to climb, reinforcing his view that ‘NVIDIA compute is fungible, durable and highly rentable’.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nHuawei Takes Aim at Nvidia, AMD with Over 10 new AI Chipsets — But Can the Chinese Tech Giant Close the Gap?\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'ffe1d834f903c5b58a15d97d3b19a316e81f64e5','2026-09-18 09:36:41','2026-09-18 10:20:12.477317',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 09:36:41');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(390,'alpaca:61863926','benzinga','2026-09-18 11:00:47','What''s Going On With Micron Technology Stock Friday?','Micron (MU) up 478% over 12 months. Get key technical levels, US fab expansion updates, and analyst price targets ahead of earnings.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61863926/whats-going-on-with-micron-technology-stock-friday-6','["AMD", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 11:20:32.094791','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline indicates current interest without confirming new information.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 11:23:49.407016','2026-09-18 11:20:28.062599','61863926',replace('Micron Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MU) stock rose more than 1% in Friday premarket trading as semiconductor stocks benefited from a firmer technology backdrop.Nasdaq futures gained 0.54%, while S&P; 500 futures edged 0.03% higher.Micron shares have surged 478.78% over the past 12 months. Investors are now looking ahead to the memory chipmaker’s earnings report on Sept. 30.Micron Expands U.S. Memory ProductionMeanwhile, Micron is expanding U.S. production as memory manufacturers race to add capacity amid a global supply shortage.The company is building the first advanced memory fabrication plant in the U.S. in Boise, Idaho. The company also has another facility under construction in Clay, New York.The expansion comes as tight memory supplies push major chip companies to secure additional capacity. NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) and Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) are among the companies seeking more supply, CNBC reported Thursday.However, a shortage of skilled workers could complicate the industry’s expansion. The U.S. could face a shortage of as many as 157,000 semiconductor workers by 2030. Meanwhile, 73% of chip employers report significant difficulty filling engineering positions.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nTechnical AnalysisMicron recently traded at $989.34. That puts the stock 3.5% above its 20-day simple moving average of $957.53 and 6.9% above its 50-day average of $926.77.It also trades 55.8% above its 200-day average of $636.27. The 20-day average remains above the 50-day, while the 50-day remains above the 200-day. That structure points to a continuing long-term uptrend.Meanwhile, Micron’s relative strength index stands at 53.95. The neutral reading suggests momentum is neither overbought nor oversold.Traders may watch $1,012 as a potential resistance area. On the downside, $887.50 represents a key support level.Analyst OutlookMicron carries a Buy consensus rating with an average price forecast of $1,521.74.Mizuho maintained an Outperform rating in August but lowered its price forecast to $1,300. New Street Research upgraded Micron to Buy with a $1,250 forecast, while Citigroup maintained Buy and lowered its forecast to $1,150.Benzinga Edge RankingsMicron scores strongly on momentum, quality and growth in the Benzinga Edge scorecard.Its Momentum score stands at 99.41, while Quality is 96.56 and Growth is 93.82. However, its Value score is lower at 25.39.MU Stock Price ActionMicron shares rose 1.23% to $989.50 in Friday premarket trading, according to Benzinga Pro data.Image via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nStock Market Today: S&P; 500, Nasdaq 100 Futures Rise as Trump Weighs ''Big Decision'' on Iran Military Strikes— OKLO, MCD, BB, NUE in Focus','\n',char(10)),'ac0797ed29a92ba348d6748bd62e84eae3417d50','2026-09-18 11:00:47','2026-09-18 11:20:28.048864',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 11:02:12');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(391,'alpaca:61863429','benzinga','2026-09-18 10:33:59','AMD Says AI Adoption Is Still Early, Sees No Slowdown in Demand','AMD stock rises as CTO Mark Papermaster signals surging AI demand, shift to inference, and new system-level integration.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61863429/amd-says-ai-adoption-is-still-early-sees-no-slowdown-in-demand','["AMD"]','stocks','2026-09-18 11:20:33.813309','other','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'AMD signals strong demand for AI despite early adoption phase.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78}','{}','2026-09-19 11:23:49.407016','2026-09-18 11:20:28.067429','61863429',replace('Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) stock is trading higher by almost 1% in Friday premarket trading. The move follows bullish comments from AMD Chief Technology Officer Mark Papermaster on artificial intelligence demand.Nasdaq futures rose 0.44%, while S&P; 500 futures slipped 0.05%.AMD CTO Says AI Demand Isn’t SlowingAMD sees no slowdown in AI demand as businesses seek bigger productivity gains from the technology, CNBC-TV18 reported Thursday, citing Papermaster.Papermaster said businesses remain in the early stages of AI adoption. Companies may become more selective about workloads to control costs. However, AMD does not expect that shift to slow overall demand.“AI is speeding up everything in the industry,” Papermaster said. He added that AMD is also using AI to accelerate its own product development.Agentic AI could provide another growth opportunity. Unlike applications focused on individual tasks, agentic systems can connect multiple tasks and reason across broader workflows. Papermaster said that could deliver significant productivity gains.AI Workloads Shift Toward InferenceMeanwhile, AMD expects the computing mix to change as AI moves from training toward inference and real-world applications.Papermaster said businesses will need a combination of CPUs, GPUs and networking. For some AI workloads, the CPU-to-GPU ratio could move closer to one-to-one. Earlier systems typically used one CPU for every eight GPUs.AMD also expects more established AI workloads to move toward on-premise data centers and AI-enabled PCs as companies seek to lower costs.AMD Expands Beyond ChipsAMD is also expanding from individual processors into complete computing systems.The company plans to introduce AI rack-level integration later this year. Its broader offering will combine computing hardware with software and networking capabilities.“We have transformed from being a computer chip provider to a solution provider,” Papermaster said.The strategy could give AMD greater exposure to AI infrastructure spending as customers increasingly seek integrated computing platforms rather than individual chips.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nTechnical AnalysisAMD remains well above its major moving averages. At $550.25, the stock is 13.4% above its 20-day simple moving average of $486.23. It is also 11.3% above its 50-day SMA of $495.58 and 56.3% above its 200-day SMA of $352.92.However, the short-term setup remains mixed. The 20-day SMA is below the 50-day SMA. Meanwhile, the 50-day SMA remains above the 200-day SMA, supporting the longer-term uptrend.Momentum has improved. The MACD is above its signal line, while the histogram is positive. That points to strengthening buying pressure.Resistance sits near $561.50. A break above that level could bring AMD’s 52-week high of $584.73 back into focus. Support sits near $463.Analyst OutlookThe stock carries a Buy consensus rating and an average price forecast of $604.Piper Sandler initiated coverage with an Overweight rating and a $600 price forecast on Sept. 10. Raymond James upgraded AMD to Strong Buy and raised its forecast to $641 on Aug. 25. BMO Capital initiated coverage with an Outperform rating and a $550 forecast on Aug. 21.Benzinga Edge RankingsAMD scores strongly on momentum, quality and growth in the Benzinga Edge scorecard.Its momentum score stands at 99 out of 100, while quality is 94.64 and growth is 95.6. However, its value score is just 3.72, reflecting the stock’s premium valuation.ETF ExposureAMD has an 8.22% weighting in the iShares Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SOXX). It also accounts for 6.55% of the First Trust Nasdaq Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:FTXL) and 6.52% of the Pacer Data and Digital Revolution ETF (NYSE:TRFK).These weightings give AMD meaningful exposure to broader semiconductor and technology ETF flows.Price ActionAMD Stock Price Activity: Advanced Micro Devices shares rose 0.95% to $550.25 in Friday premarket trading, according to Benzinga Pro data.Photo via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nNVIDIA Boss Slams AI Doom Mongers, Stock Bounces','\n',char(10)),'40a6cc20cd3e535a5c63e11d7c8392cf523e25ea','2026-09-18 10:33:59','2026-09-18 11:20:28.048864',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 10:49:59');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(392,'alpaca:61865346','benzinga','2026-09-18 12:10:33','Forget the AI Bubble: VanEck’s Nick Frasse Explains How MU, SK Hynix, ASML, and TSMC Control the Pace of ''Token Factories''','VanEck’s Nick Frasse breaks down AI bottlenecks, &#39;token factories&#39;, and why MU, SK Hynix, ASML, and TSMC control the data center buildout.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61865346/forget-the-ai-bubble-vanecks-nick-frasse-explains-how-mu-sk-hynix-asml-and-tsmc-control-the-pace-of-token-factories','["AAPL", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 12:20:41.960683','other','neutral',1,2,'days',1,'Analysis piece discussing industry dynamics without new developments.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 12:23:56.540931','2026-09-18 12:20:37.913056','61865346',replace('VanEck product manager Nick Frasse stated that physical construction delays for chip suppliers like ASML Holding NV (NASDAQ:ASML) and Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Co. Ltd. (NYSE:TSM) control the expansion pace of data centers, while investor focus shifts toward memory producers Micron Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MU) and SK Hynix Inc. (NASDAQ:SKHY).\n\nData Centers Function as Token Factories\n\nFrasse, who is part of the management team of VanEck’s $67.79 billion VanEck Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SMH), stated in a conversation with Phil Rosen that artificial intelligence (AI) deployment remains in its early infancy, remarking, “we’re probably still in the batting cages for it.”\n\nHe explained that data centers operate essentially as “token factories” that burn tokens at accelerating rates as agentic AI executes broader prompts. Frasse noted overall semiconductor demand has exceedingly outpaced supply across all technology sectors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBeyond Nvidia: Why Software Stocks Just Crushed Semiconductors in a Historic 25-Year Shift\n\nIntegrated Semiconductor Supply Stack\n\nFrasse outlined how semiconductor companies operate through collaborative supply chain layers rather than direct head-to-head competition.\n\nFabless design firms outsource chip manufacturing to foundries like TSMC, which produces hardware for Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA), Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL), and Broadcom Inc. (NASDAQ:AVGO).\n\nTSMC relies on ASML, with Frasse emphasizing “there’s only one ASML in the entire world” manufacturing EUV lithography machinery. Consequently, demand increases at foundries automatically drive revenue for equipment suppliers.\n\nRotation Into Memory Bottlenecks\n\nFollowing early packaging constraints on GPUs, Frasse identified memory as a current major bottleneck in the AI buildout.\n\nProducing high-bandwidth memory requires building new fabrication plants, extending supply timelines. Frasse noted multi-year commitments from corporate balance sheets reduce historical industry cyclicality.\n\nFrasse said that there are cycles even in bull markets and thinks there could be reversions to the mean. He added that there are investors who “don’t want to pay up for Nvidia right now” but may put capital into memory suppliers like Micron and SK Hynix.\n\nPhysical Constraints Act as AI Governor\n\nAddressing investor concerns regarding massive capital expenditure and potential market bubbles, Frasse argued that physical infrastructure timelines naturally govern industry expansion.\n\nConstructing a semiconductor fabrication plant or standing up a data center requires two to three years. Frasse explained that these physical time limitations create an “inherent governor” that will “help a giant bubble from being created,” as compute constraints prevent overbuilding.\n\nHow Have These Stocks Performed?\n\nStocks1-Month6-MonthsYTD1-Year5-YearsASML-13.46%17.31%52.00%86.83%89.53%TSM-0.16%24.36%43.62%63.73%265.40%MU-3.39%111.72%242.49%510.98%1215.61%SKHY6.77%7.64% (Since Listing)–––\n\nRead Also:\n\nIs The Rise Of AI Fatigue Beginning To Drive S&P; 500 Lower?\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'8b3f22598882e31c2cef4301d7e268fc7c3583eb','2026-09-18 12:10:33','2026-09-18 12:20:37.907652',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 12:10:33');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(393,'alpaca:61865253','benzinga','2026-09-18 12:06:39','Bitcoin''s Much Less Volatile Than It Used to Be. BlackRock Says It Played a Part in That.','BlackRock’s Jay Jacobs says Bitcoin volatility has fallen to 35–40, paving the way for wider institutional adoption through IBIT.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61865253/bitcoins-much-less-volatile-than-it-used-to-be-blackrock-says-it-played-a-part-in-that','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 12:20:43.265303','macro','bullish',3,3,'weeks',1,'Lower volatility could encourage more institutional investment in Bitcoin.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 6.107}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 7.798}}','2026-09-19 12:23:56.540931','2026-09-18 12:20:37.919842','61865253',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) has been trading in a tight range for over a month since its push above $80,000 in August.\n\nBlackRock’s (NYSE:BLK) Head of U.S. Equity ETFs Jay Jacobs says that is a feature, not a bug.\n\nWhat Jacobs Said About Bitcoin’s Volatility\n\nJacobs joined Anthony Pompliano’s podcast Thursday to point out that volatility for Bitcoin has compressed from around 80 to the 35 to 40 range. \n\nOne of the drivers of this development: the buildout of BlackRock’s IBIT (NASDAQ:IBIT) and the options market around it/\n\nMore participants means more long-term buyers acting as a counterbalance to short-term traders, making Bitcoin accessible to institutions that previously could not justify the risk.\n\n“When we end up in an environment where people are more concerned about geopolitics or fiat currency debasement, Bitcoin should benefit,” he said, adding that the fundamental diversifying nature of Bitcoin still holds even as the investor base has shifted.\n\nWhy IBIT Changed the Conversation\n\nBefore IBIT, financial advisers and institutions could avoid the Bitcoin question entirely because they had no easy way to access it. \n\nOnce it became as simple as clicking a button on a brokerage account, it forced a decision: does Bitcoin belong in a portfolio? \n\nIn-kind transactions are now available at a $1.5 million minimum, down sharply from earlier thresholds, opening the door to participants who want to financialize their Bitcoin by borrowing against it or layering options strategies on top.\n\nHow BlackRock Thinks About Its Crypto Lineup\n\nBlackRock’s strategy is deliberate concentration rather than breadth. \n\nBitcoin and Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) together make up two-thirds to three-quarters of the total digital asset market cap, and the firm wants to be the best at those two before going wider. \n\nThe current lineup covers IBIT for Bitcoin, ETHA (NASDAQ:ETHA) for unstaked Ethereum, ETHB (NASDAQ:ETHB) for staked Ethereum with an added yield stream, and BIDI, a Bitcoin covered call ETF for investors who want Bitcoin exposure alongside a cash flow component.\n\nWhat Jacobs Said About AI\n\nBlackRock now treats AI as a macro factor on par with GDP growth and interest rates, Jacobs argued. \n\nThe firm built an AI value chain framework spanning power companies, data centers, chip manufacturers, and application developers. \n\nBAI is its actively managed AI ETF run by fundamental stock picker Tony Kim, with targeted products like PWR for power infrastructure and IDGT for digital real estate available for investors who want more granular exposure.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nWhat''s Going On With Strategy Stock Friday?','\n',char(10)),'44bfca29a1e125d2c82ad37f8dbf161ae90c44fb','2026-09-18 12:06:39','2026-09-18 12:20:37.907652',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 12:06:39');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(394,'alpaca:61864454','benzinga','2026-09-18 11:30:05','Josh Shapiro Slams Trump''s Decision to Sell ''Most Advanced'' Chips to China Amid AI Race, Giving Them an Edge: ''That Was a Mistake''','Pennsylvania Governor Josh Shapiro has criticized President Donald Trump&#39;s administration for allegedly assisting China in the AI race.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61864454/josh-shapiro-slams-trumps-decision-to-sell-most-advanced-chips-to-china-amid-ai-race-giving-them-an-edge-that-was-a-mistake','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 12:20:44.708418','other','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'Political criticism regarding AI chip sales may influence public perception but not immediate asset value.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 12:23:56.540931','2026-09-18 12:20:37.973092','61864454',replace('Pennsylvania Governor Josh Shapiro has criticized President Donald Trump‘s administration for allegedly assisting China in the artificial intelligence (AI) race.\n\nShapiro, speaking at the AI Horizons 2026 Summit in Pittsburgh on Thursday, claimed that the Trump administration’s actions contradicted its own calls for the U.S. to outpace China in AI development.\n\nHe accused the Trump administration of selling some of America’s “most advanced chips” to Chinese companies, thereby giving them an advantage over American entrepreneurs. He said, “that was a mistake” and called for effective leadership.\n\n“Real leadership means keeping America ahead of China in AI innovation,” he said, adding that Washington should stop alienating the allies and lead international efforts to bring countries together around a framework for responsible AI regulation and safety.\n\nThe Democrat also used his speech to emphasize that AI should be a top agenda item when Trump meets with Chinese President Xi Jinping next week. He urged the U.S. to pursue international standards for advanced AI systems while maintaining a technological edge over Beijing.\n\nThe governor also called for tighter oversight of frontier AI models, greater transparency requirements and independent evaluations of advanced systems before their widespread deployment. \n\nRead Also:\n\nChina’s Spy Chief Warns AI Could Threaten ‘Regime Security’ — Deepfakes, Cyberattacks and AI Warfare Among 6 Major Risks\n\nNvidia at the Center of US-China AI War\n\nThe governor’s comments came as an August report suggested that limited batches of Nvidia Corp.‘s (NASDAQ:NVDA) H200 AI chips were shipped to China, despite restrictions. Chinese tech giants like ByteDance and Tencent Holdings Ltd. (OTC:TCEHY) received around 10,000 H200 processors each.\n\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang is expected to attend a White House dinner during Xi’s visit to Washington on Sept. 24. The White House said Trump invited prominent U.S. business leaders and wants to prioritize deals that benefit the U.S. Huang has maintained close ties with Trump, joining the president on his May trip to China and attending a dinner hosted by the Chinese President for Trump.\n\nTrump, China Clash Over AI Regulation\n\nTrump dismissed AI-safety concerns as a "hoax," arguing that existing government powers are sufficient and that tighter regulations could weaken the U.S. against China. \n\nLast week, China’s People’s Daily accused the U.S. of applying "double standards" to AI model distillation and urged the U.S. and China to cooperate on AI risks. It called for an open, inclusive AI development environment and warned against turning the technology into a tool of great-power competition.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAI Could Threaten Nuclear Command Systems, Warn US-China Experts— Urge Human Control and Emergency Hotline\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'164ce121e8bf29bead16dc6972a64c746edd18b3','2026-09-18 11:30:05','2026-09-18 12:20:37.907652',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 11:30:05');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(395,'alpaca:61866059','benzinga','2026-09-18 12:37:53','Apple Raises the Premium Bet: iPhone 18 Pro Hits Stores, First Foldable Arrives Next','iPhone 18 Pro &amp; Pro Max land with powerful Siri AI, advanced camera upgrades, and $1,199 starting price. See specs &amp; release news.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61866059/apple-raises-the-premium-bet-iphone-18-pro-hits-stores-first-foldable-arrives-next','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-18 13:20:53.470933','product','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'New product release could drive sales and interest in the stock.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}','2026-09-19 13:24:04.863024','2026-09-18 13:20:49.382794','61866059',replace('Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) is rolling out its latest iPhone lineup under new CEO John Ternus, with higher-priced premium models launching first and the company’s inaugural foldable device set to follow.\n\niPhone 18 Pro Models Hit Stores\n\nCNBC reported on Friday that Apple’s iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max models are hitting stores with higher price points than previous new-device models.\n\nThe launch marks Apple’s first major product release under Ternus, who previously served as the company’s senior vice president of hardware engineering before succeeding Tim Cook as CEO.\n\nFoldable Duo Takes Center Stage\n\nMuch of the attention around Apple’s new smartphone lineup is focused on the Duo, the company’s first foldable iPhone.\n\nApple plans to debut the Duo in about a month, giving the company another premium hardware format alongside its traditional iPhones.\n\nCNBC highlighted the foldable model’s larger-screen appeal.\n\niPhone 18 Pro Adds AI And Camera Upgrades\n\nApple is positioning the iPhone 18 Pro lineup around faster AI performance, improved cameras and longer battery life as it targets another major upgrade cycle.\n\nThe iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max use Apple’s new 2-nanometer A20 Pro chip, which the company says delivers faster AI performance.\n\nApple’s upgraded Siri AI can take actions across more than 300,000 apps. The Pro models also add a variable-aperture main camera and offer up to 36 hours of video playback on the Pro and 45 hours on the Pro Max.\n\nThe iPhone 18 Pro starts at $1,199, while the Pro Max starts at $1,299.\n\nBank of America Sees Strong Upgrade Cycle\n\nBank of America Securities analyst Wamsi Mohan reiterated a Buy rating and $370 price forecast, citing a potential multiyear upgrade cycle, edge AI opportunities and faster Services growth.\n\nMohan said U.S. carrier trade-in incentives of up to $1,200 largely offset higher iPhone pricing. He expects higher average selling prices, Siri AI and adoption of the upcoming iPhone Duo to support demand.\n\nAAPL Price Action: Apple shares were down 0.03% at $336.90 during premarket trading on Friday. The stock is approaching its 52-week high of $344.56, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nImage via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nApple, Nvidia Eye Major Entry into AI Servers: Report','\n',char(10)),'6db11205ce6d3c6ed39d97dfc27868927427151f','2026-09-18 12:37:53','2026-09-18 13:20:49.331041',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 12:37:53');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(396,'alpaca:61866043','benzinga','2026-09-18 12:36:40','Bitcoin Cracks $78,000 and Ethereum, XRP, Dogecoin May Be ''About To Explode''','Bitcoin reclaims $78,000 as analysts see long-term upside; ETH targets $2,570-$3,000, XRP could reach $2, and DOGE signals a potential major rebound.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61866043/bitcoin-cracks-78000-and-ethereum-xrp-dogecoin-may-be-about-to-explode','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "ETH/USD", "XRP/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 13:20:55.159829','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline presents analyst opinions and potential future movements without confirmed events.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 6.107}, "DOGE/USD": {"60m": 7.703, "1d": 8.94}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 7.798}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 8.243, "1d": 11.037}}','2026-09-19 13:24:04.863024','2026-09-18 13:20:49.387011','61866043',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) on Friday picked up momentum to reclaim $78,000 for the first time in three days, while Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) followed higher to touch $2,500.\n\nXRP (CRYPTO: XRP) climbed above $1.30, while Dogecoin (CRYPTO: DOGE) jumped roughly 6%.\n\nRipple Chief Legal Officer Stuart Alderoty said politics took precedence over crypto policy this week, but argued that the roughly 67 million Americans who own or use crypto "are not going anywhere."\n\nWhy the Long-Term Outlook Remains Strong\n\nIndustry expert Scott Melker predicted about a month ago that "crypto is about to explode." \n\nSpeaking to the "When Shift Happens" podcast in August, Melker had reiterated his conviction even as near-term sentiment was subdued before Bitcoin’s surge above $75,000.\n\nUnlike 2021–2022, when the industry faced aggressive U.S. enforcement and existential concerns, Bitcoin now has spot ETFs, governments discussing strategic reserves, Bitcoin mining, and growing adoption of blockchain infrastructure.\n\nMelker’s thesis is to focus on Bitcoin’s long-term adoption rather than trying to predict the exact catalyst for the next rally.\n\nETH, XRP, DOGE Predicted To Move Higher\n\nCrypto chart analyst Ali Martinez on Friday said Ethereum remains inside its four-hour channel despite recent volatility. With ETH testing the lower boundary, he sees potential for a rebound toward $2,570.\n\nA strong four-hour close above $2,570 with volume could confirm a breakout, putting $2,700 and potentially $3,000 in focus.\n\nMartinez sees XRP forming the right shoulder of an inverse head-and-shoulders pattern, with $1.55 as the key neckline.\n\nA confirmed breakout above could complete the bullish pattern and trigger a 35% rally toward $2, with potential for further upside.\n\nTrader Tardigrade highlighted Dogecoin has touched its long-term weekly support trendline for the third time, which he views as confirmation of a potential bottom.\n\nHe said the setup mirrors previous DOGE cycles, when tests of the same trendline preceded rallies to new peaks, suggesting another major rebound could follow.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin''s Fair Value Is Around $105,000, Rise Is ''Programmed,'' Mark Yusko Says','\n',char(10)),'9c398645b0a22cc3abc7ca7b2308de64192439a6','2026-09-18 12:36:40','2026-09-18 13:20:49.331041',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 12:36:40');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(397,'alpaca:61865873','benzinga','2026-09-18 12:31:04','Apple To Rally Around 13%? Here Are 10 Top Analyst Forecasts For Friday','Analysts downgraded XENE, NFLX and MGA, while raising price targets for OCS, INSW, ABEO and STNG.','https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/price-target/26/09/61865873/apple-to-rally-around-13-here-are-10-top-analyst-forecasts-for-friday','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-18 13:20:56.590673','analyst','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'Analyst forecasts are speculative and not confirmed.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}','2026-09-19 13:24:04.863024','2026-09-18 13:20:49.391297','61865873',replace('Top Wall Street analysts changed their outlook on these top names. For a complete view of all analyst rating changes, including upgrades and downgrades, please see our analyst ratings page.\n\nDeutsche Bank cut the price target for Xenon Pharmaceuticals Inc (NASDAQ:XENE) from $90 to $46. Deutsche Bank analyst David Hoang downgraded the stock from Buy to Hold. Xenon Pharmaceuticals shares closed at $57.35 on Thursday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nWells Fargo slashed Netflix Inc (NASDAQ:NFLX) price target from $80 to $57. Wells Fargo analyst Steven Cahall downgraded the stock from Equal-Weight to Underweight. Netflix shares closed at $75.31 on Thursday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nHC Wainwright & Co. raised price target for Oculis Holding AG (NASDAQ:OCS) from $26 to $39. HC Wainwright & Co. analyst Yi Chen maintained a Buy rating. Oculis Holding shares closed at $9.98 on Thursday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nBTIG raised the price target for International Seaways Inc (NYSE:INSW) from $100 to $130. BTIG analyst Gregory Lewis maintained a Buy rating. International Seaways shares closed at $110.53 on Thursday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nCantor Fitzgerald raised Abeona Therapeutics Inc (NASDAQ:ABEO) price target from $28 to $30. Cantor Fitzgerald analyst Kristen Kluska maintained an Overweight rating. Abeona Therapeutics shares closed at $5.59 on Thursday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nBMO Capital slashed Magna International Inc (NYSE:MGA) price target from $76 to $70. BMO Capital analyst Tamy Chen downgraded the stock from Outperform to Market Perform. Magna International shares closed at $64.82 on Thursday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nBTIG increased Scorpio Tankers Inc (NYSE:STNG) price target from $100 to $110. BTIG analyst Gregory Lewis maintained a Buy rating. Scorpio Tankers shares closed at $87.85 on Thursday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nFreedom Capital Markets cut the price target for Minerals Technologies Inc (NYSE:MTX) from $92 to $90. Freedom Capital Markets analyst David Silver maintained a Buy rating. Minerals Technologies shares closed at $68.62 on Thursday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nEvercore ISI Group raised Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL) price target from $365 to $380. Evercore ISI Group analyst Amit Daryanani maintained an Outperform rating. Apple shares closed at $337.00 on Thursday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nTigress Financial raised Alphabet Inc (NASDAQ:GOOGL) price target from $415 to $485. Tigress Financial analyst Ivan Feinseth maintained a Strong Buy rating. Alphabet shares closed at $347.33 on Thursday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nConsidering buying AAPL stock? Here’s what analysts think:\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'c0e2a36d3b27ec539a4e115da8edbd3cd8f8f866','2026-09-18 12:31:04','2026-09-18 13:20:49.331041',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 12:31:04');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(398,'alpaca:61868964','benzinga','2026-09-18 13:52:34','AI Capex Boom Risks ''Massive Capital Destruction'' in the US, Warns Veteran Market Strategist: ''You Could Get Some News Item That Suddenly…''','Jefferies’ Chris Wood warns trillion-dollar AI spending could trigger massive capital destruction as hyperscalers turn to debt.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61868964/ai-capex-boom-risks-massive-capital-destruction-in-the-us-warns-veteran-market-strategist-you-could-get-some-news-item-that-suddenly','["AMZN", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-18 14:21:07.173259','macro','bearish',3,3,'weeks',1,'Concerns about AI spending impacting overall market stability.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-19 14:24:12.265707','2026-09-18 14:21:02.872820','61868964',replace('Chris Wood, Global Head of Equity Strategy at Jefferies, raised concerns over the sustainability of the current trend in AI investments, warning of a potential implosion due to a shift towards debt financing and the risk of a funding break.\n\nWood, in an interview with CNBC-TV18 on Thursday, expressed apprehension about the “enormous” amounts being invested in AI by American hyperscalers, with an estimated trillion dollars expected next year. \n\nAccording to him, these investments may not yield returns that justify the capital deployed. “My base case there’ll be massive loss of capital destruction in the U.S.,” he said. \n\nHowever, as long as the market doesn’t question the capex “aggressively,” semiconductor stocks will continue to profit, he said. \n\nThe Equity Head also pointed out a shift in the funding model. Initially, these investments were primarily cash-funded. Now, three and a half years into the trend, debt is increasingly financing these investments.\n\nWood cautioned that a market decision to withdraw credit could trigger a swift end to this trend. While there is no clear timeline for this scenario, he emphasized the importance of monitoring the situation closely.\n\n“You could get some news item that suddenly makes people question this whole cycle,” he cautioned. \n\nThe Jeffries Equity Head stated that the key macroeconomic issue for stock markets right now is the outlook for AI capital expenditure.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEd Yardeni Slashes Year-End S&P; 500 Target Amid Downturn Risks: ''Proceed With Caution''\n\nHyperscaler AI Spending Nears $1.2 Trillion\n\nLast month, Economist Torsten Slok said U.S. hyperscaler AI capital spending could reach 3.1% of GDP in 2027. That means today’s AI capex race could become almost three times larger relative to the economy. Hyperscalers are expected to spend about $916 billion over the next 12 months, rising to nearly $1.2 trillion the following year.\n\nCurrent consensus estimates indicate that six U.S. hyperscalers — Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN), Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOGL), Microsoft Corp., Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META), Oracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL), and Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) could collectively spend roughly $916 billion over the next 12 months, with spending projected to rise to approximately $1.17 trillion over the following year.\n\nDespite calls for an AI slowdown, sustained infrastructure spending by big tech could lead to its continued growth, according to Hendi Susanto, a portfolio manager at Gabelli Funds. Even if leading AI labs such as Anthropic and OpenAI decelerate their progress, "second- and third-tier players" will seize the chance to level up, maintaining high demand for AI infrastructure, according to the tech fund manager.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nIntel Stock Could Nearly Double to $200 in 2 Years, Analyst Says — Potential Apple, Tesla, and AI Chip Deals Could Fuel the Rally\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'18b7763d088975a6c4d3763a73fee7737f307dfa','2026-09-18 13:52:34','2026-09-18 14:21:02.848441',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 13:52:34');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(399,'alpaca:61868516','benzinga','2026-09-18 13:43:26','Oracle, CoreWeave Dump on AI''s $3.6 Trillion Financing Bill','Oracle and CoreWeave stand out for leverage in a $3.6 trillion AI financing web as investors weigh debt, leases and circular funding risks.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61868516/oracle-coreweave-ai-financing-3-6-trillion','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 14:21:09.492186','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses financing risks without a specific impact on asset prices.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 14:24:12.265707','2026-09-18 14:21:02.882101','61868516',replace('CoreWeave (NASDAQ:CRWV) shares fell over 4% Thursday after the AI infrastructure company announced plans to raise $3 billion through convertible debt, with an option for another $500 million.\n\nThe fresh financing comes as new research mapping $3.6 trillion across the AI industry highlights CoreWeave and Oracle (NYSE:ORCL) as two of the most leveraged companies in the supply chain. \n\nCoreWeave opened the door to selling as many as 35 million shares, as Benzinga reported Thursday.\n\nAI Financing Comes Full Circle\n\nLondon credit hedge fund Sona Asset Management mapped $3.6 trillion of AI-related financing across 176 deals involving 202 entities. Sona flagged about 120 of those deals as highly circular, meaning the same companies often show up as investors, customers and suppliers.\n\nOne example is Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA). The chipmaker has conditionally committed up to about $100 billion to OpenAI. OpenAI, meanwhile, has committed hundreds of billions of dollars to cloud providers including Oracle, which are themselves major buyers of Nvidia chips.\n\nA separate Sona chart looked at leverage across the AI supply chain. Oracle and CoreWeave stood out as two of the most heavily indebted companies relative to their earnings.\n\nOracle’s Commitments Stretch Years Ahead\n\nOracle had $125.3 billion of borrowings as of Aug. 31. It has also disclosed another $288 billion of mostly data-center leases that have not yet started.\n\nThose leases typically run for 15 to 19 years, meaning Oracle is locking in costs far into the future.\n\nThe company also has $664 billion of contracted future business. Oracle expects only about 13% of that to turn into revenue over the next 12 months.\n\nA large share of Oracle’s backlog reportedly comes from OpenAI. The Financial Times noted that OpenAI does not have positive unadjusted earnings.\n\nCoreWeave Needs Markets to Stay Open\n\nCoreWeave had $35.6 billion of debt as of June 30. S&P; Global Ratings gives the company a B+ rating with a positive outlook.\n\nThe company expects to spend between $35 billion and $39 billion on capital expenditures this year, after raising its guidance in August as demand for AI capacity increased.\n\nThat makes continued access to capital markets central to CoreWeave’s growth. The company needs to finance enormous amounts of new infrastructure before much of the revenue from that capacity arrives.\n\nIf financing becomes more expensive or AI demand slows, that model could come under pressure.\n\nTraders See Little Chance of a Full Bust\n\nPolymarket traders currently put an AI-industry downturn by Dec. 31 at 12%, with about $2.38 million traded on the contract.\n\nThe contract sets a high bar: at least three of six stress events must occur within 90 days, including Nvidia falling 50%, an OpenAI or Anthropic bankruptcy, or a 50% drop in any of five big AI-hardware suppliers such as Taiwan Semiconductor or Broadcom.\n\nSona’s broader point is that much of the AI buildout rests on the same source of demand. With OpenAI at the center of many of those commitments, any slowdown in its spending or funding could quickly ripple through Oracle, CoreWeave and their suppliers.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nSpaceX Is Worth $2 Trillion. Why Does Its Stock Swing Like a Small-Cap?','\n',char(10)),'3b4090160efdf6b826199c5575ed7cf5cc0ed6a1','2026-09-18 13:43:26','2026-09-18 14:21:02.848441',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 13:43:26');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(400,'alpaca:61867797','benzinga','2026-09-18 13:33:46','XRP ETFs Post $5M Outflow as Reserves Hit a 7-Year Low: Bullish or Bearish?','XRP ETFs post a $5.15 million outflow as exchange reserves hit a seven-year low and a historic RSI signal tests long-term support.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61867797/xrp-etfs-post-5m-outflow-as-reserves-hit-a-7-year-low-bullish-or-bearish','["XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-18 14:21:10.940080','other','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'The outflow from XRP ETFs and low reserves suggest negative sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"XRP/USD": {"60m": 8.125, "1d": 10.856}}','2026-09-19 14:24:12.265707','2026-09-18 14:21:02.911555','61867797',replace('XRP (CRYPTO: XRP) spot ETFs posted a $5.15 million outflow Thursday, their biggest since Sept. 2, even as exchange reserves fell to a 7-year low.\n\nWhat the ETF Flow Data Shows\n\nCanary Capital’s XRPC (NASDAQ:XRPC) lost $1.37 million while 21Shares’ TOXR (BATS:TOXR) accounted for the remaining $3.78 million according to SoSoValue. \n\nDespite Thursday’s outflow, XRP ETFs remain up $9.60 million for the week, keeping the fund on course for a 10th consecutive week of net inflows. \n\nFriday’s session is the only hurdle left: a weekly outflow exceeding $9.60 million would break the streak, while anything below that keeps the run alive. \n\nWhat the On-Chain Data Shows\n\nAnalyst Dark Defender posted on X that XRP sits 25% below its August high, but the fundamentals underneath tell a stronger story. \n\nExchange reserves have dropped to a seven-year low near 1.7 billion XRP, leaving far less supply available for sale on the open market. \n\nThat tightening supply comes as RLUSD (CRYPTO: RLUSD), Ripple’s dollar-pegged stablecoin, grows to 88% of all stablecoin liquidity on the XRP Ledger, and as the network moves ahead with a roadmap targeting quantum-safe cryptography by 2028. “Wave 3 does not ask for permission,” Dark Defender wrote.\n\nWhat the RSI Data Says\n\nWidely-followed crypto analyst Cryptollica posted on X that XRP recently hit its lowest two-week RSI reading in 13 years, a deeper momentum washout than three prior cycle lows:\n\n2018 bear market\n\n2020 COVID crash\n\n2022 cycle bottom\n\nThe catch: XRP’s long-term ascending support line connecting major lows across those same cycles is still holding.\n\nCryptollica’s case is conditional rather than a confirmed breakout. Hold that support and the historic RSI low marks a sentiment floor. Break it and the thesis falls apart. \n\n“Almost nobody wants it when RSI is printing a 13-year low and the chart looks broken,” Cryptollica wrote. \n\n“By the time the crowd feels safe again, you may already be looking at XRP from behind,” the analyst added.\n\nFor context, the current two-week RSI sits at 43.78 against a historical low of 33.52, both above the standard oversold threshold of 30. Cryptollica is calling it a low relative to XRP’s own history, not the textbook definition.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nCFTC Expands Regulatory Relief for Crypto Developers','\n',char(10)),'d903bba114af57de09fb4109da4350c0bd720b60','2026-09-18 13:33:46','2026-09-18 14:21:02.848441',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 13:33:46');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(401,'alpaca:61872017','benzinga','2026-09-18 15:09:14','Tesla’s Optimus Has a New Problem: Figure’s Humanoid Is Getting Better at the Unknown','Figure AI’s Helix 2.5 raises the bar for Tesla Optimus with zero-shot humanoid tasks across 30 unfamiliar homes.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/09/61872017/tesla-optimus-figure-ai','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 15:21:20.592553','product','bearish',3,3,'weeks',1,'Competitor advancements may challenge Tesla''s market position.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-19 15:24:19.683247','2026-09-18 15:21:15.321758','61872017',replace('The next battleground in humanoid robotics may not be how well a robot performs a chore, but how much it already knows before entering the room. Figure AI says its latest model completed household tasks across 30 unfamiliar homes, suggesting broad human-behavior data could become as important to robots as hardware itself.\n\nFigure Raises The Bar\n\nFigure’s Helix 2.5 was tested in 30 Bay Area homes the robots had never seen, with no data collected in those homes and no environment-specific fine-tuning. The humanoids were asked to tidy living rooms, fold towels and make beds — tasks requiring navigation, perception, manipulation and whole-body coordination.\n\nThe striking result came from Figure’s Index pretraining. According to the company, an otherwise identical model trained from scratch succeeded on just 9% of blind zero-shot trials, while the Index-pretrained version reached 56%. Figure says the only experimental difference was Index pretraining, with architecture, optimization, downstream data and evaluation held constant.\n\n"Zero-shot" does not mean the robot learned these tasks without training. Rather, the homes and objects used for testing were new to the model. The result suggests a robot can carry knowledge from human experience into environments it has never encountered.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: The Biggest Robotics Problem Isn''t AI. It''s ROI\n\nTesla Has A Different Data Moat\n\nThat puts an interesting spotlight on Tesla, Inc‘s (NASDAQ:TSLA) Optimus strategy.\n\nTesla has said it is using its strengths in real-world AI data to advance Optimus, its general-purpose autonomous humanoid robot. Its broader AI strategy is built around training neural networks on billions of examples of real-world data.\n\nTesla therefore has a potentially significant data advantage from its vehicle fleet and AI infrastructure. But Figure is attacking the same generalization problem from a different direction: collecting human behavior specifically to teach robots how people navigate and manipulate the physical world.\n\nFigure says its Index dataset is now generating roughly 35 minutes of new human experience every second. It has also committed $3.5 billion of compute to training Helix through a partnership with Nscale.\n\nThat makes the competitive question less about which humanoid looks most capable in a controlled demonstration and more about which company can build the better physical-intelligence training loop.\n\nThe Next Test Is Scale\n\nFigure’s 56% result is notable, but it does not mean humanoid robotics is solved. More than four in 10 trials still failed, and the evaluation covered three household behaviors.\n\nFor Tesla investors, the more important question is whether the company can turn its real-world AI data advantage into the kind of generalization Figure is now demonstrating.\n\nThat is the metric worth watching as both companies scale: not just whether Optimus or Figure can complete a task, but whether each new piece of training data makes the robot capable of handling environments it has never seen before. The company that solves that problem at scale could move humanoid robotics closer to mass deployment.\n\nRead Also:\n\nHumanoid Robots Could Match Humans in Five Years\n\nImage via IM Imagery/Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'31f9d961079fce7572b04a2d55377c38f756cb13','2026-09-18 15:09:14','2026-09-18 15:21:15.310292',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 15:09:14');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(402,'alpaca:61871752','benzinga','2026-09-18 15:01:57','Bitcoin Cracks $80,000, Ethereum, XRP Surge 4% on $170M Short Liquidations','Bitcoin reclaims $80,000 as Fed liquidity lifts Ethereum and XRP, triggering $170 million in crypto short liquidations.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61871752/bitcoin-cracks-80000-ethereum-xrp-surge-4-on-170m-short-liquidations','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD", "XRP/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 15:21:23.854877','macro','bullish',4,4,'hours',1,'Bitcoin''s significant price movement and liquidation events indicate strong market activity.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.676}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 6.821}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 7.708}}','2026-09-19 15:24:19.683247','2026-09-18 15:21:15.325122','61871752',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) has reclaimed $80,000 as Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) and XRP (CRYPTO: XRP) shot up 4%\n\nMarket commentator Bull Theory posted on X that over $170 million in shorts were liquidated in just 60 minutes and $130 billion added to the total crypto market cap in 24 hours.\n\nThe Wolf of All Streets podcast host Scott Melker said Bitcoin holding at $78,000 through a rate hike and the CLARITY Act’s defeat was itself the signal to watch.\n\n“Bitcoin’s up 32% this quarter and nobody’s even paying attention,” Melker wrote, pointing to exchange collapses and heavy selling that failed to move price lower. \n\n“I told you in my opinion that we had likely bottomed because bad news stopped mattering,” he added.\n\nMeanwhile, popular market commentator Ash Crypto pointed out that the Fed will inject $16.5 billion into the economy starting Friday, with liquidity hitting markets over three consecutive weeks.\n\nUnder the New York Fed’s schedule, the central bank plans roughly $15.6 billion in Treasury bill purchases between Sept. 15 and Oct. 14, split across five operations. \n\nThe first settled Sept. 18, with the rest continuing through mid-October.\n\nIt is worth noting these are reinvestment purchases, not new quantitative easing. The buys replace principal payments from maturing agency debt and mortgage-backed securities rather than expanding the Fed’s balance sheet outright. \n\nBTC, ETH, XRP Price Analysis: Key Levels to Watch\n\nAssetPrice MoveKey SignalResistanceSupportBTC+6% RSI 62.56, breaks descending triangle$82,000 (Sept high)$77,185 (20-day EMA)XRP+7%Bounces off $1.26–$1.29 demand zone$1.47 (SAR flip level)$1.35 (20-day EMA)ETH+5%RSI 60.97, strongest since January$2,672 (0.618 Fib)$2,447 (0.5 Fib)\n\nBitcoin broke decisively above its descending triangle resistance Friday, with the 20-day EMA reclaimed as support and the path now open toward a retest of the $82,000 September high.\n\nXRP bounces sharply off the support zone that has held since the late-August breakout from $1. The SAR sitting above price means the trend needs a clean break above $1.47 to confirm a full flip back to bullish.\n\nMeanwhile, Ethereum pushes into the 0.5 to 0.618 Fibonacci retracement zone from its October 2025 to January 2026 decline. A weekly close above $2,672 opens the path toward $2,950 to $3,000.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nXRP ETFs Post $5M Outflow as Reserves Hit a 7-Year Low: Bullish or Bearish?','\n',char(10)),'075aa3e1bb04d236a01f457737f8266ce1df7f38','2026-09-18 15:01:57','2026-09-18 15:21:15.310292',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 15:01:57');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(403,'alpaca:61871667','benzinga','2026-09-18 15:00:45','Ohio Rep. David Taylor Bought Up to $30K Worth of Installed Building Prods Stock','A September filing shows that Representative David Taylor reported a purchase in Installed Building Prods (NYSE:IBP), valued between $2,002 and $30,000. The transaction date is listed as September 8, 2026, with the','https://www.benzinga.com/government/26/09/61871667/ohio-rep-david-taylor-bought-30k-worth-installed-building-prods-stock','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-18 15:21:26.263209','other','neutral',2,3,'weeks',1,'This is a disclosure of stock purchase by a governmental representative.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 498.48}','{}','2026-09-19 15:24:19.683247','2026-09-18 15:21:15.329261','61871667',replace('A September filing shows that Representative David Taylor reported a purchase in Installed Building Prods (NYSE:IBP), valued between $2,002 and $30,000. The transaction date is listed as September 8, 2026, with the report published on September 17, 2026.\nAt present, Installed Building Prods shares are trading down 1.82% at $199.05.\nRepresentative''s Recent Trading Activity\nOver the past three years, David Taylor executed 226 trades totaling over $352 thousand. The largest of these trades were in UnitedHealth Group and Eli Lilly stock. Some of the key transactions the Rep. has executed recently include: \n\nMicrosoft (NASDAQ:MSFT): $15,001 - $50,000 Sale\nInstalled Building Prods (NYSE:IBP): $1,001 - $15,000 Purchase\nProcter & Gamble (NYSE:PG): $1,001 - $15,000 Purchase\n\nHere is a list of David Taylor''s most recent trades:\n\nCompany\nTicker\nStock Type\nAmount\nTransaction Type\nTransaction Date\n\nInstalled Building Prods\nIBP\nSTOCK\n$1,001 - $15,000\nP\n2026-09-08\n\nProcter & Gamble\nPG\nSTOCK\n$1,001 - $15,000\nP\n2026-09-08\n\nAmerican Electric Power\nAEP\nSTOCK\n$1,001 - $15,000\nP\n2026-08-26\n\nAmerican Electric Power\nAEP\nSTOCK\n$1,001 - $15,000\nP\n2026-08-26\n\nAmgen\nAMGN\nSTOCK\n$1,001 - $15,000\nS\n2026-08-26\n\nWant to keep up with David Taylor and other congressional members’ stock activities? Check out our government trades tool for real-time updates!\nThe Importance of Congressional Transactions\nA congressional transaction is when any representative or senator either buys or sells an individual stock.\nAnyone working in Congress must file a Periodic Transaction Report to inform the public of their recent transaction within 30 days of being notified of the transaction and within 45 days of the transaction date.\nIn April 2012, Former President Barack Obama signed the STOCK Act into law. The act prohibits members of Congress from using private information given to them by their position for personal gain such as buying or selling a stock. The act also expanded disclosure requirements for members of Congress by requiring them to file a monthly disclosure.\nWhy Congressional Transactions Matter\nCongressional transactions shouldn''t be the primary reason for an investing decision, but they can be an important factor for an investor to consider.\nWhen a senator or representative makes a new purchase, it could be an indication they expect the stock to rise.\nA sale, on the other hand, can be made for a variety of reasons, and may not necessarily mean the seller thinks the stock will go down.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'56ee5571d47a07b83e25e810efd5b9e6200cf665','2026-09-18 15:00:45','2026-09-18 15:21:15.310292',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 15:00:45');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(404,'alpaca:61871184','benzinga','2026-09-18 14:45:55','Micron, SanDisk Face New China Rival: Trouble for MU and SNDK Ahead?','CXMT is preparing a NAND push after taking 9.5% of DRAM revenue, raising a new long-term threat for Micron and SanDisk.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61871184/cxmt-nand-micron-sandisk','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 15:21:27.577630','other','neutral',2,3,'weeks',1,'CXMT''s entry into NAND market poses a potential threat, reported by credible source.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 15:24:19.683247','2026-09-18 15:21:15.339366','61871184',replace('China’s CXMT Corp. is reportedly preparing to enter NAND flash memory after capturing nearly 10% of global DRAM revenue, a move that could eventually pressure Micron Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MU) and SanDisk Corp. (NASDAQ:SNDK) in a fast-growing part of the AI memory boom.\n\nMicron’s NAND revenue jumped 99.2% from the prior quarter to $11.85 billion in the second quarter, while SanDisk’s climbed 50.7% to nearly $8.97 billion, according to TrendForce.\n\nCXMT now reportedly wants in.\n\nThe Chinese chipmaker plans to establish a NAND research and development line at a new Beijing plant and has discussed the project with potential customers, including an AI startup, Reuters reported Friday.\n\nIt remains unclear when the line would start operating or whether CXMT plans to move beyond R&D; and trial production into large-scale commercial manufacturing.\n\nCXMT Has Already Shaken Up DRAM\n\nCXMT’s global DRAM revenue share reached 9.5% in the second quarter, up from 7.6% three months earlier, according to TrendForce.\n\nIts shares surged 466% in their July Shanghai debut, vaulting CXMT to the top of China’s stock market by valuation on its first day after an $8.6 billion IPO. CXMT closed at 55.54 yuan Friday in Shanghai, about 13% above its first-day close and more than six times its IPO price.\n\nThe NAND push would take CXMT into another memory market benefiting from the AI boom. Data centers require growing amounts of solid-state storage, while manufacturers have prioritized investment in DRAM and high-bandwidth memory, limiting additions to NAND capacity.\n\nTrendForce expects tight NAND supply to ease only in the second half of 2027.\n\nChina’s NAND Push Won’t Fix Today’s Shortage\n\nChina already has one major NAND producer in YMTC, the country’s leading flash-memory manufacturer. Counterpoint Research says YMTC shipped about 14% of global NAND bits in the second quarter, making it the world’s third-largest supplier by volume.\n\nCXMT’s move into NAND could eventually give China a second major domestic supplier and add more competition for Micron and SanDisk. But that threat is longer term.\n\nPrediction market traders remain bullish on the wider AI spending cycle driving memory demand. Polymarket traders give Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) a 74% chance of ending 2026 as the world’s largest company, with about $7.4 million wagered.\n\nFor Micron and SanDisk, CXMT looks more like a future competitive threat than an answer to tight supply today. Benzinga reported earlier this week that new factories capable of materially easing the broader memory shortage may not reach full production until 2028 or 2029.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nOracle, CoreWeave Dump on AI''s $3.6 Trillion Financing Bill','\n',char(10)),'8a851f450062232d41096a5ba85e8aceea83a415','2026-09-18 14:45:55','2026-09-18 15:21:15.310292',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 14:45:55');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(405,'alpaca:61870963','benzinga','2026-09-18 14:39:47','Jim Cramer Flags ''Boatload'' of Bullish Option Buying in Micron, Sandisk, Intel','Jim Cramer flagged over $90M in short-dated chip calls, suggesting Leopold Aschenbrenner’s fund may be behind the trades, though unconfirmed.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61870963/jim-cramer-flags-boatload-of-bullish-option-buying-in-micron-sandisk-intel','["AMD"]','stocks','2026-09-18 15:21:30.093990','analyst','neutral',2,2,'hours',1,'The mention of bullish option buying indicates interest, but lacks confirmation.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78}','{}','2026-09-19 15:24:19.683247','2026-09-18 15:21:15.342602','61870963',replace('CNBC host Jim Cramer spotted a wave of short-dated call buying across memory and chip names Friday morning — more than $90 million in premium — and pointed at a familiar suspect.\n\n“‘Someone’ just bought a boatload of short data (October2) calls Intel 115 $3.8 m; Marvell 250sm $3.8 million; Sandisk 1600s $41 million, Micron $1000s $44 million,” Cramer wrote in a post on X. “If i didn’t know any better I would say Leopold is back!!!”\n\n"Someone" just bought a boatload of short data (October2) calls Intel 115 $3.8 m; Marvell 250sm $3.8 million; Sandisk 1600s $41 million, Micron $1000s $44 million. If i didn''t know any better I would say Leopold is back!!!— Jim Cramer (@jimcramer) September 18, 2026 \n\nMRVL stock is moving. See the real-time price action here. \n\nThe Leopold in question is Leopold Aschenbrenner, whose AI-focused hedge fund, Situational Awareness, ran from roughly $225 million at inception to about $45 billion before leveraged AI bets unwound in days, with the portfolio sinking 67% in July and much of it sold to Citadel. \n\nThe fund still finished that stretch up 80% for the year, and the Securities and Exchange Commission has since sought information from banks that financed the trades.\n\nWhy the Nod Lands\n\nCramer’s shorthand carries weight because the fund has form in exactly these tickers. Situational Awareness held roughly $5.7 billion in Sandisk and $5.6 billion in Micron at the end of June, before the blowup. \n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Admin Launches $215M Quantum Competition: IonQ, D-Wave, Rigetti Take Notice\n\nAnd the fund has already resurfaced in the derivatives market: CNBC reported last week that the firm has been buying options tied to Advanced Micro Devices (NASDAQ:AMD), Bloom Energy (NYSE:BE) and CoreWeave (NASDAQ:CRWV).  \n\nWhether Friday’s flow belongs to the fund is unconfirmed.\n\nWhere the Strikes Sit\n\nMicron Technology, Inc. (NASDAQ:MU) traded near $990.48, up 1.33%, putting the $1,000 strike at the money against a 52-week high of $1,255. \n\nSandisk Corp. (NASDAQ:SNDK) changed hands around $1,669.28, up 3.40% and already above the $1,600 line, well off a peak of $2,354.39. \n\nIntel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) sat at $109.42, up 0.57%, leaving $115 only a modest hop away. \n\nMarvell Technology, Inc. (NASDAQ:MRVL) was roughly flat at $240.86.\n\nIt is worth noting that the October expiration falls after Micron’s fiscal fourth-quarter report, a print that tends to move the whole memory complex.\n\nCramer has stayed constructive on the group, arguing in August that AI data-center demand and supply discipline have reset a boom-and-bust industry. Short-dated calls in the size flagged by Cramer Friday morning leave no room for patience.\n\nRead Also:\n\nThese 10 Stocks Are Squeeze Candidates Waiting to Happen\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'3ac8b2630707d30b9d236ddd2625ec811dd4a194','2026-09-18 14:39:47','2026-09-18 15:21:15.310292',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 14:39:47');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(406,'alpaca:61874434','benzinga','2026-09-18 16:15:16','Strategy CEO Says ''We''re Never Going To Stop'' Buying Bitcoin as MSTR Surges 11%','MSTR stock jumps 11% as Strategy CEO Phong Le vows to keep buying Bitcoin while allowing small strategic sales.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61874434/strategy-ceo-says-were-never-going-to-stop-buying-bitcoin-as-mstr-surges-11','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 16:21:38.447620','other','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'CEO''s commitment to buying Bitcoin is likely to boost investor confidence.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.676}}','2026-09-19 16:24:30.546355','2026-09-18 16:21:34.089124','61874434',replace('Strategy (NASDAQ:MSTR) is up 11% Friday after CEO Phong Le said the company will remain a permanent Bitcoin accumulator, even as it stays open to selling small amounts when it makes sense.\n\nLe said in an interview with Bitcoin magazine on X that Strategy holds 840,050 Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC), making it the largest Bitcoin holder in the world, and that position is not changing. \n\n“This is not a sell Bitcoin forever strategy. This is a buy Bitcoin forever strategy,” Le said.\n\nHe also opened the door to occasional selling as part of a broader push to integrate Bitcoin and DeFi markets into traditional finance. \n\nWith $55 billion worth of Bitcoin on the balance sheet, Le argued the company needs flexibility beyond a pure buy-and-hold approach, particularly as traditional finance moves deeper into Bitcoin custody. \n\n“Sometimes sales in the short term can actually be accretive in real Bitcoin terms,” he said.\n\nWhy MSTR Trading Volume Stands Out\n\nBitcoin News flagged on X that Strategy’s stock now regularly trades more shares than Berkshire Hathaway (NYSE:BRK), a crossover that first happened in late December 2025 and has held through 2026. \n\nSome August sessions saw 46 million to 49 million shares change hands, with turnover reaching $4.4 billion, putting MSTR among the 10 most actively traded U.S. stocks.\n\nMSTR Price Analysis: Key Levels to Watch\n\nMSTR breaks decisively above its descending trendline from the May $199 high Friday, climbing to $147.37 in a clean breakout off the ascending triangle base built since the July $84 low. \n\nRSI Divergence Indicator at 63.56 marks its strongest reading since the September highs, confirming genuine momentum without stretching into extreme territory. \n\nThe 20-day EMA at $128.49 has been decisively cleared, with both the 50-day and 100-day EMAs now flipping to support well below current price.\n\nKey levels for MSTR:\n\n$152 — 200-day EMA, the next real test above\n\n$128 — 20-day EMA, must hold to keep the move intact\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'f3c1cf3add4f3e6e67cb278b234efb1e5106f269','2026-09-18 16:15:16','2026-09-18 16:21:34.082868',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 16:15:16');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(407,'alpaca:61873238','benzinga','2026-09-18 15:36:30','Why Is BitMine Stock Surging on Friday?','BitMine stock is climbing Friday as a sharp rebound in Ethereum lifts crypto-related shares. Eightco’s disclosed holdings, BMNR’s bullish technical setup and significant ETF exposure add further context to the stock’s latest move.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61873238/why-is-bitmine-stock-surging-on-friday','["ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 16:21:40.051460','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'The stock''s rise is linked to broader market trends and specific technical factors.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"ETH/USD": {"60m": 6.821}}','2026-09-19 16:24:30.546355','2026-09-18 16:21:34.140710','61873238',replace('BitMine Immersion Technologies Inc. (NYSE:BMNR) shares are surging Friday, driven by a strong rebound in Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH). Ethereum was trading at $2,558.39, up 4.62% over the past 24 hours, providing a boost to BitMine. The Nasdaq is down 0.04% while the S&P; 500 has shed 0.44% and Technology (XLK) is lower by 0.19%.\n\nEightco Discloses Holdings\n\nEightco Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:ORBS) backed by BitMine Immersion provided an update on its total holdings on Thursday, Eightco reported total assets of approximately $380 million. Eightco reported holding a $90 million indirect investment in OpenAI, an $18 million investment in Beast Industries, a $1 million stake in Mythical Games, 301,971,219 Worldcoin tokens valued at 37 cents each, 16,278 Ethereum and approximately $120 million in cash and stablecoins. Eightco also repurchased over 26 million shares of common stock this quarter.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEvery AI Agent Needs a Gatekeeper: 3 Cybersecurity Stocks to Watch\n\nTechnical Analysis\n\nThe stock is trading above its major moving averages, including the 20-day SMA ($24.46) and the 200-day SMA ($22.08), which keeps the intermediate trend pointed up. It’s also well above the 50-day SMA ($20.28) and 100-day SMA ($19.13), suggesting the recent rebound has real distance behind it.\n\nThe longer-term picture is mixed because the 20-day SMA is above the 50-day SMA (bullish), but the 50-day SMA remains below the 200-day SMA after the death cross in January. Traders will often treat that combination as "short-term improving, long-term still repairing," especially after the swing low in June and the swing high in September.\n\nKey Resistance: $27 — a nearby round-number area where rebounds can stall if momentum stays choppy\n\nKey Support: $23 — a nearby pivot zone that sits close to the 20-day EMA ($23.64), making it a practical first line of defense\n\nTop ETF Exposure\n\nBitMine has significant exposure across several crypto-focused ETFs, including the Corgi Crypto Infrastructure ETF (NASDAQ:BLCK) at a 5.87% weight, the Bitwise Crypto Industry Innovators ETF (NYSE:BITQ) at 7.00%, and the Global X Blockchain ETF (NASDAQ:BKCH) at 9.97%. Given BMNR’s sizable allocations in these funds, substantial ETF inflows or outflows could create additional buying or selling pressure on the stock as fund managers adjust their holdings.\n\nBMNR Stock Price Activity: BitMine Immersion shares are trading higher by 7.85% at $25.77 at the time of publication on Friday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nRead Also:\n\nJim Cramer Flags ''Boatload'' of Bullish Option Buying in Micron, Sandisk, Intel\n\nPhoto: PJ McDonnell / Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'a0d998d8fb5d8bf594465836ef0e5c003eb91b94','2026-09-18 15:36:30','2026-09-18 16:21:34.082868',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 15:36:30');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(408,'alpaca:61873173','benzinga','2026-09-18 15:34:31','What''s Going On With Sandisk Stock Friday?','Sandisk stock surges over 6% as tight supply and booming AI memory demand drive price increases across the sector.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61873173/whats-going-on-with-sandisk-stock-friday-5','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 16:21:42.120197','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Increased demand for AI memory drives stock price higher.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 16:24:30.546355','2026-09-18 16:21:34.143412','61873173',replace('Sandisk Corp. (NASDAQ:SNDK) stock rose more than 6% Friday, sharply outperforming the broader technology sector as AI-driven memory demand, higher industry prices and tight supply supported memory stocks.\n\nThe Nasdaq gained 0.06%, while the S&P; 500 fell 0.34%.\n\nAI infrastructure continues to consume more memory, tightening industry supply. NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) CFO Colette Kress recently cited "extreme pricing conditions in memory," saying increases have exceeded expectations and could rise further next year.\n\nMeanwhile, TechInsights expects memory-market tightness to intensify through at least the end of 2027. The firm expects DRAM prices to rise more than 200% year over year, with meaningful new supply potentially not arriving until late 2027 or early 2028.\n\nThe backdrop is supporting memory names despite weak market breadth. Only two of the 11 S&P; 500 sectors were higher Friday.\n\nTechnical Analysis\n\nSandisk remains in a strong long-term uptrend. The stock is 60.6% above its 200-day simple moving average of $1,067.86 and 14.1% above its 50-day SMA of $1,502.68.\n\nIts 20-day SMA of $1,587.61 also remains above the 50-day average. Meanwhile, the MACD is above its signal line, and the histogram remains positive. Both signals point to bullish momentum.\n\nResistance sits near $1,807.50. Support is near $1,416.50.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nAnalyst Outlook\n\nThe stock carries a Buy consensus rating with an average price forecast of $2,282.69.\n\nMizuho recently maintained an Outperform rating while lowering its price forecast to $1,875. RBC Capital raised its forecast to $1,600 with a Sector Perform rating. Wells Fargo raised its forecast to $1,550 while maintaining an Equal-Weight rating.\n\nBenzinga Edge Rankings\n\nThe Benzinga Edge scorecard gives Sandisk a Momentum score of 99.88. Its Value score stands at 11.22.\n\nThe scores point to strong relative price momentum but limited support from valuation.\n\nETF Exposure\n\nSandisk has notable exposure through the First Trust US Equity Opportunities ETF (NYSE:FPX), Invesco S&P; 500 Pure Growth ETF (NYSE:RPG) and Invesco Dorsey Wright Technology Momentum ETF (NASDAQ:PTF).\n\nPrice Action\n\nSandisk shares were up 6.30% at $1,716.09 at the time of publication Friday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nImage via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nSandisk Surges as Analysts Hail Supply Crunch and Unstoppable Memory Outlook','\n',char(10)),'e83c78b5fb144bbcf912404d0b335c57539c2f96','2026-09-18 15:34:31','2026-09-18 16:21:34.082868',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 15:34:31');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(409,'alpaca:61873031','benzinga','2026-09-18 15:30:38','$100 Invested In Meta Platforms 10 Years Ago Would Be Worth This Much Today','Meta Platforms (NASDAQ:META) has outperformed the market over the past 10 years by 4.58% on an annualized basis producing an average annual return of 17.92%. Currently, Meta Platforms has a market capitalization of','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61873031/100-invested-meta-platforms-10-years-ago-would-be-worth-much-today','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-18 16:21:43.395621','other','neutral',1,1,'days',1,'The headline presents historical performance information without making a prediction.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-19 16:24:30.546355','2026-09-18 16:21:34.145918','61873031',replace('Meta Platforms (NASDAQ:META) has outperformed the market over the past 10 years by 4.58% on an annualized basis producing an average annual return of 17.92%. Currently, Meta Platforms has a market capitalization of $1.72 trillion. \nBuying $100 In META: If an investor had bought $100 of META stock 10 years ago, it would be worth $520.31 today based on a price of $676.09 for META at the time of writing.\nMeta Platforms’s Performance Over Last 10 Years\n\nFinally -- what’s the point of all this? The key insight to take from this article is to note how much of a difference compounded returns can make in your cash growth over a period of time.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'2f256c80d7c8d25e383d17debff12cdcb7fc88e3','2026-09-18 15:30:38','2026-09-18 16:21:34.082868',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 15:30:38');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(410,'alpaca:61872584','benzinga','2026-09-18 15:20:23','This Crude Refiner Has Beaten Every Magnificent Seven Stock in the Last 2 Years','Valero Energy has risen more than 200% in two years, outpacing every Magnificent Seven stock, including Nvidia. Almost the entire move came in 2026, driven by a collapse in global refining capacity rather than by the oil price. The average analyst price target now sits 31% below the stock.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61872584/this-crude-refiner-has-beaten-every-magnificent-seven-stock-in-the-last-2-years','["AAPL", "AMZN", "META", "MSFT", "NVDA", "SPY", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 16:21:44.635351','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The article discusses recent stock performance without new information impacting the stock directly.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48, "NVDA": 219.37, "SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-19 15:24:19.683247','2026-09-18 16:21:34.159351','61872584',replace('Investors who spent the past two years chasing the AI trade through Magnificent Seven stocks would have made far more money buying a company that turns crude oil into fuel.\n\nValero Energy Corp. (NYSE:VLO) traded at $415 on Friday morning after setting a fresh record intraday high of $416.66. \n\nThe stock has now rallied over 200% in the last two years.\n\nOver the same period, the strongest Magnificent Seven stock was Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOGL), up 119%. Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA), the company at the center of the artificial intelligence trade, gained 93.5%.\n\nStockSept. 18, 2024Sept. 18, 20262-Year ChangeValero Energy Corp. (VLO)$136.66$415.45+203.8%Alphabet Inc. $159.81$351.09+119.9%Nvidia Corp.$113.37$219.37+93.5%Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA)$227.20$366.99+61.5%Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL)$220.69$333.30+51.0%Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN)$186.43$252.58+35.5%Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META)$537.95$674.80+25.4%Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT)$430.81$759.17 +14.06%SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY)$561.40$759.17+35.2%\n\nValero Stock Became A Scarcity Trade\n\nValero is not an oil producer. It buys crude and earns money from the difference between input costs and refined-product prices.\n\nThat difference is known as a crack spread. \n\nWhen gasoline or diesel becomes scarcer than crude, the spread widens and refinery profits can rise rapidly.\n\nThat mechanism has become especially powerful in 2026.\n\n The closure of the Strait of Hormuz and disruptions to global fuel flows have tightened both crude and refined-product markets.\n\nOn Friday morning, ultra-low-sulfur diesel futures traded at $4.9192 a gallon. A barrel holds 42 gallons, so a barrel of diesel was worth about $206.61. \n\nWest Texas Intermediate crude, the U.S. benchmark, traded at $102.\n\nThe difference is roughly $104 a barrel of gross margin on diesel alone, a new record. \n\nThe historical norm for the blended 3-2-1 refining margin, which mixes two barrels of gasoline with one of diesel, is around $19 a barrel. That blended measure sits near $61 today.\n\nValero owns 14 refineries across the U.S., Canada and the U.K., with roughly 3 million barrels per day of throughput capacity.\n\nThe Earnings Are Showing Up\n\nValero reported second-quarter revenue of $44.48 billion, up 48.8% year-over-year, and adjusted earnings of $12.54 per share against $2.28 a year earlier.\n\nRefining margin per barrel of throughput reached $23.62, compared with $12.35 in the same quarter of 2025. Throughput averaged 2.95 million barrels a day across 15 refineries.\n\nThe company generated $6.97 billion in operating cash flow in the first half of 2026. It returned $2.84 billion through buybacks and $714 million in dividends over the same period.\n\nTrailing twelve-month earnings per share reached $23.93 through the second quarter, against full-year 2025 net income of $2.34 billion. The stock trades at 17.2 times trailing earnings with a 1.16% dividend yield and a market value of $119.7 billion.\n\nThe Average Wall Street Analyst Is Still Behind The Move\n\nValero carries a consensus Overweight rating from 15 analysts tracked by Benzinga Analyst Ratings, with an average price target of $283. \n\nThat is 31.4% below where the stock trades.\n\nYet, the average masks a recent shift. Every target set in the past three weeks sits far above it.\n\nDateFirmAnalystActionRatingPrice TargetSep 14, 2026Raymond JamesJustin JenkinsPT RaiseStrong Buy$350 → $450Sep 14, 2026Morgan StanleyJoe LaetschPT RaiseEqual-Weight$255 → $411Sep 8, 2026UBSManav GuptaPT RaiseBuy$355 → $450Sep 3, 2026Piper SandlerJohn RoyallPT RaiseOverweight$329 → $435Sep 1, 2026Wells FargoSam MargolinPT RaiseOverweight$356 → $389Aug 4, 2026MizuhoNitin KumarPT RaiseNeutral$289 → $300\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'e1a4e3f6219930f1087b8a5592652d3e3a7d3097','2026-09-18 15:20:23','2026-09-18 16:21:34.082868',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 15:20:23');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(411,'alpaca:61875859','benzinga','2026-09-18 17:05:36','Grayscale Says Rate Hike Is ''Unlikely to Drive Major Shifts'' In Bitcoin','Grayscale says the Fed’s 25-basis-point hike will have little impact on Bitcoin or the broader crypto market.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61875859/grayscale-says-rate-hike-is-unlikely-to-drive-major-shifts-in-bitcoin','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 17:21:54.395458','macro','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Grayscale''s analysis suggests limited impact on Bitcoin prices.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.982}}','2026-09-19 17:24:38.414087','2026-09-18 17:21:49.477833','61875859',replace('Grayscale Head of Research Zach Pandl told clients Thursday that the Fed’s 25-basis-point hike is unlikely to move crypto markets much, calling it a mid-cycle adjustment rather than a shift in policy direction.\n\nWhy Pandl Isn’t Worried About the Hike\n\nPandl wrote in a note published Thursday that Wednesday’s move to a 3.75% to 4% target range differs fundamentally from the Fed’s 2022 tightening cycle. Two cycles, two very different outcomes for crypto:\n\nCycleMagnitudeImpact on BitcoinMarch 2022–July 2023+550 basis pointsWeighed heavily on Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC), raised opportunity cost of holding non-yielding assetsSeptember 2026+25 basis pointsOne-off adjustment, minimal expected impactSource: Grayscale Research Note\n\nPandl drew a direct historical parallel to March 1997, when the Greenspan Fed delivered a similar mid-cycle hike and the Nasdaq bull market kept running afterward. \n\nHe expects the one or two additional hikes still possible in 2026 to have a similarly limited effect on capital allocation into digital assets.\n\nWhere Higher Rates Could Actually Matter\n\nNot all of crypto is equally exposed to rate policy, Pandl noted. Two areas stand out:\n\nStablecoin issuers — Circle (NYSE:CRCL) and Tether (CRYPTO: USDT) earn higher revenue as cash rates rise, since reserves sit in short-term Treasuries and money market instruments\n\nTokenized bonds and money market funds — higher yields on these products could pull more capital on-chain as they become more attractive relative to holding cash off-chain\n\nHis broader point: crypto is not one monolithic asset class, and rate policy hits different corners of it differently, much like it does across traditional finance.\n\nHow This Builds on Grayscale’s Bottom Call\n\nAs Benzinga reported Thursday, Pandl told The Block at Avalanche Summit in New York that Bitcoin’s roughly $58,000 low from late June marked the bottom of the current cycle, giving Grayscale clients a green light to allocate. \n\nHe also flagged Zcash (CRYPTO: ZEC) as a separate thesis built around the privacy layer Bitcoin lacks, arguing growing AI capability and data exposure make that theme increasingly relevant.\n\nThursday’s note extends that same conviction through the Fed decision. Pandl is treating the rate hike as background noise rather than a reason to revise the bottom call, keeping Grayscale’s institutional stance intact even as the Clarity Act’s failure and the rate hike hit crypto sentiment in the same week.\n\nRead Also:\n\nXRP Up 3% as Ripple Adds XRP Payments to Stripe, Tempo’s AI Standard\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'223d8ab30959d2ed523a2b2745fc64c99facf9a7','2026-09-18 17:05:36','2026-09-18 17:21:49.436820',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 17:05:36');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(412,'alpaca:61875729','benzinga','2026-09-18 17:00:41','Bakkt Stock Climbs Friday: What''s Going On?','Shares of Bakkt Holdings Inc. (NYSE: BKKT) are trading higher Friday afternoon, lifted by a broader rally across crypto-linked equities.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61875729/bakkt-stock-climbs-friday-whats-going-on','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 17:21:55.878459','other','neutral',2,3,'hours',1,'Stock price increase attributed to general market conditions rather than company-specific news.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.982}}','2026-09-19 17:24:38.414087','2026-09-18 17:21:49.480837','61875729',replace('Shares of Bakkt Holdings Inc. (NYSE:BKKT) are trading higher Friday afternoon, lifted by a broader rally across crypto-linked equities. The upward momentum is closely tied to a surge in Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) prices, driven by renewed optimism surrounding domestic digital asset regulation following the recent failure of the Clarity Act in the U.S. Senate.\n\nHere’s what investors need to know.\n\nBakkt stock is charging ahead with explosive momentum. Why is BKKT stock surging?\n\nCFTC and SEC Step In Following Clarity Act Stagnation\n\nThe primary catalyst for Friday’s sector-wide strength stems from an agency-level push to establish a definitive framework for digital assets. On Thursday, the Commodity Futures Trading Commission (CFTC) submitted a formal proposal to regulate crypto asset transactions and markets. \n\nThis move, combined with coordinated announcements from both the CFTC and the Securities and Exchange Commission on Thursday signals to investors that regulatory agencies are proactively stepping in to fill the legislative void left by the stalled Clarity Act.\n\nFor institutional-focused digital asset platforms like Bakkt, the prospect of clear regulatory guidelines serves as a significant operational tailwind. As federal agencies move to establish definitive rules for crypto market transactions and custody, compliance-first companies are structurally positioned to benefit from increased institutional adoption.\n\nBKKT Shares Climb Friday Afternoon\n\nBKKT Price Action: Bakkt shares were up 8.45% at $8.09 at the time of publication on Friday. The stock is near its 52-week low of $6.71, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nRead Also:\n\nRobinhood Stock Rises with Bitcoin Amid CFTC''s New Crypto Proposal\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'4764734cbf756f7054f19e39ad1b09f488fe41a8','2026-09-18 17:00:41','2026-09-18 17:21:49.436820',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 17:00:41');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(413,'alpaca:61875543','benzinga','2026-09-18 16:55:21','Bitcoin Tops $80,000, S&P 500 Slips as Yields Reclaim 5%: Stock Market Today','Crypto-linked equities ripped higher as Bitcoin cleared $80,000, but the S&amp;P 500 slipped with the 10-year Treasury yield back above 5%.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61875543/bitcoin-tops-80000-crypto-stocks-soar-yields-reclaim-5-percent-markets-friday','["AMZN", "BTC/USD", "META", "MSFT", "NVDA", "QQQ", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 17:21:57.261175','macro','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Bitcoin reaching $80,000 may lead to increased investor interest and buying in crypto-linked equities.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "BTC/USD": 76528.6, "META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48, "NVDA": 219.37, "QQQ": 716.89}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.676}}','2026-09-19 17:24:38.414087','2026-09-18 17:21:49.486203','61875543',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) punched through $80,000 on Friday, driving a rally in crypto equities even as broader markets stalled under rising bond yields. \n\nKansas City Fed President Jeffrey Schmid delivered a hawkish signal, defending rate hikes against sticky, broad-based inflation above 3%. \n\nBond yields spiked in response:\n\nThe 10-year Treasury note surging 7 basis points back to 5%.\n\nThe 2-year yield rose 7 basis points to 4.75%\n\nThe 30-year climbed 4 basis points to 5.34%.\n\nEnergy Prices Offer Rare Bit of Relief\n\nWest Texas Intermediate crude eased 0.4% to $101.50 a barrel and Brent slipped 0.5% to $104.26, extending a mid-week retreat even as supply concerns tied to Saudi Arabia and the broader Middle East stayed live.\n\nNatural gas moved the other way, adding 0.8% to $2.92 per MMBtu, keeping the energy inflation story on the table.\n\nThe S&P; 500 slipped 0.2% to 7,621.16, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average gave back 222 points, or 0.4%, to 51,555.73. \n\nInternational Business Machines Corp. (NYSE:IBM) was the heaviest weight on the blue-chip index, falling 3%. \n\nThe Nasdaq 100 was the most resilient of the majors, hovering just below the flatline at 29,425.62. \n\nThe Russell 2000 was the clear laggard again, down 0.9% to 2,848.24 and now off 3.7% for September.\n\nGold firmed as the pullback in crude eased near-term inflation anxiety, with spot bullion up 0.4% to $4,358 an ounce and the SPDR Gold Shares (NYSE:GLD) gaining 0.4%. Silver outpaced it, rising 1.6% to $66.24.\n\nFriday’s Performance In Major US Indices\n\nIndexLast% ChangeMTDYTDS&P; 5007,621.16-0.2%-0.9%+11.3%Dow Jones51,555.73-0.4%-3.1%+7.3%Nasdaq 10029,425.62-0.1%-0.1%+16.5%Russell 20002,848.24-0.9%-3.7%+14.8%Updated by 12:15 p.m. ET\n\nAccording to the Benzinga Pro platform:\n\nThe Vanguard S&P; 500 ETF (NYSE:VOO) fell 0.2%.\n\nThe SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA) slid 0.7%.\n\nThe Invesco QQQ Trust (NASDAQ:QQQ) edged down 0.1%.\n\nThe iShares Russell 2000 ETF (NYSE:IWM) dropped 0.9%.\n\nMaterials, Solar Lead Sector Drag As Chips Buck Trend\n\nThe Energy Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLE) rose 0.2%, with the Technology Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLK) essentially flat behind it.\n\nThe Materials Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLB) was the worst performer, down 1.5%, followed by the Communication Services Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLC) and the Utilities Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLU), both off 1.1%. The Financial Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLF) shed 0.2% as banks and asset managers traded in the red on the back-up in yields.\n\nAt the industry level, the SPDR S&P; Metals & Mining ETF (NYSE:XME) was the day’s biggest casualty, down 2.3%, with the Invesco Solar ETF (NYSE:TAN) off 2.2% and the VanEck Agribusiness ETF (NYSE:MOO) down 1.7%. \n\nSemiconductors bucked the tape, with the VanEck Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SMH) up 0.6% and the U.S. Global Jets ETF (NYSE:JETS) adding 0.2%.\n\nThe chip rebound was led by equipment names, with Lam Research Corp. (NASDAQ:LRCX) up 5.1%, Applied Materials Inc. (NASDAQ:AMAT) up 4.1% and Micron Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MU) adding 1.4%, recovering some ground lost when AI security concerns prompted investors to reconsider the pace of datacenter spending. Sandisk Corp. (NASDAQ:SNDK) rose 7.3% on the memory bid.\n\nAI hyperscalers went the other way on their debt issuance spree, with Oracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL) down 3.3%.\n\nThe Session’s Dominant Story Sits Outside Sector Map\n\nBitcoin extended a roughly 5% weekly advance, after the Securities and Exchange Commission granted an innovation exemption enabling trading in tokenized stocks. \n\nStrategy Inc. (NASDAQ:MSTR) surged 12.9% to $149.25 as the most levered listed proxy on the token, and Bitmine Immersion Technologies Inc. (AMEX:BMNR) climbed 7.4% on the same digital-asset treasury trade.\n\nThe exchanges and brokers rode the same wave. Coinbase Global Inc. (NASDAQ:COIN) jumped 10.6% to $192.32 on volumes and the SEC tokenization exemption, while Bullish (NYSE:BLSH) added 7.4%, extending Thursday’s gains on the same ruling. \n\nRobinhood Markets Inc. (NASDAQ:HOOD) rose 7.7% to $118.22, with analysts this week raising targets on accelerating Robinhood Chain fee growth and expanding prediction-market volumes. Galaxy Digital Inc. (NASDAQ:GLXY) gained 7.6%. \n\nThe pain was concentrated in steel and speculative growth. \n\nNucor Corp. (NYSE:NUE) sank 6% after guiding third-quarter earnings to $5.55-$5.65 per diluted share late Thursday, well short of the roughly $6.20 analysts were modeling, with weaker raw materials pricing and shipments offsetting higher steel mill realizations. Steel Dynamics Inc. (NASDAQ:STLD) slid alongside it on its own soft guide.\n\nSpace Gives Back Recent Gains\n\nAST SpaceMobile Inc. (NASDAQ:ASTS) fell 7.1% to $58.26 and Rocket Lab Corp. (NASDAQ:RKLB) dropped 5.4% to $64.17, with Planet Labs PBC (NYSE:PL) down 4% alongside them.\n\nIonQ Inc. (NYSE:IONQ) fell 5.6% to $38.07, another high-beta casualty of the rotation out of long-duration speculative growth as real yields pushed higher.\n\nQUALCOMM Inc. (NASDAQ:QCOM) was the odd name out in a rising semiconductor tape, sliding 5.8% to $177.70. The move follows a roughly 18% one-month run built on the company’s multi-generational AI datacenter collaboration with Amazon announced Sept. 8, and looks like profit-taking against the Apple modem revenue cliff still ahead. \n\nGeneral Motors Co. (NYSE:GM) also fell 5.1% as record-high diesel prices pressure demand for full-size pickups and SUVs that generate the bulk of GM’s margin. \n\nFriday’s Russell 1000 Top Gainers\n\nName% changeStrategy Inc.+12.85%Coinbase Global, Inc.+10.55%Robinhood Markets, Inc.+7.66%Bullish+7.38%Bitmine Immersion Technologies, Inc.+7.35%\n\nFriday’s Russell 1000 Top Losers\n\nName% changeAST SpaceMobile, Inc.-7.10%Nucor Corporation-5.95%QUALCOMM Incorporated-5.83%IonQ, Inc.-5.62%Rocket Lab Corporation-5.39%\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'b21ca0878dddad3ff173134a2f3b3f9533f85f9a','2026-09-18 16:55:21','2026-09-18 17:21:49.436820',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 16:55:21');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(414,'alpaca:61875310','benzinga','2026-09-18 16:44:49','Robinhood Stock Rises with Bitcoin Amid CFTC''s New Crypto Proposal','Robinhood Markets shares are popping Friday as crypto-linked stocks rally on fresh regulatory moves from the CFTC and SEC this week.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61875310/robinhood-stock-rises-with-bitcoin-amid-cftcs-new-crypto-proposal','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 17:21:58.538481','macro','bullish',2,3,'days',1,'Robinhood''s stock rise is connected to overall crypto market enthusiasm due to regulatory news.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.676}}','2026-09-19 17:24:38.414087','2026-09-18 17:21:49.489048','61875310',replace('Robinhood Markets Inc. (NASDAQ:HOOD) shares are popping Friday as crypto-linked stocks rally following new regulatory moves from the CFTC and SEC this week, coming just after the Senate failed to advance the CLARITY Act.\n\nRobinhood Markets shares are powering higher. What’s driving HOOD stock higher?\n\nCFTC Eases Rules for Prediction Market Software Providers\n\nRegulators at the CFTC cleared the way this week for developers building what the agency calls “passive software” to plug users into regulated derivatives products, prediction markets included, without registering as brokers themselves, provided they avoid touching customer money or steering how trades get executed.\n\nThe move builds on groundwork already laid with crypto wallet Phantom, whose more than 20 million users have had access to similar prediction market functionality, and the exemption stays in place only until the CFTC finalizes formal rules.\n\nSEC Opens a Path for Tokenized U.S. Stocks\n\nSeparately, the SEC rolled out a temporary five-year window letting approved venues bring blockchain-based versions of U.S. stocks to market, provided those digital shares preserve normal shareholder rights like dividends and voting power, and pause trading whenever the underlying stock’s exchange halts.\n\nRobinhood has effectively been rehearsing for this moment already. CEO Vlad Tenev has pointed to 200 tokenized U.S. stocks currently trading through the company’s international arm across more than 120 countries, though U.S. customers remain locked out of that offering for now.\n\nThis new pathway could help Robinhood eventually connect that overseas experiment to the much larger domestic market, even though the exemption comes with real limits and isn’t permanent.\n\nRegulators Step in After CLARITY Act Fails in the Senate\n\nBoth moves arrive after a setback in Congress, where the CLARITY Act fell 11 votes short of the 60 needed to advance this week. Sen. Cynthia Lummis, the bill’s leading advocate, effectively declared the push finished. With lawmakers unable to deliver a broader framework, the CFTC and SEC appear willing to act on their own rather than wait on Congress.\n\nHOOD Shares Are Jumping\n\nHOOD Price Action: Robinhood shares were up 8.58% at $119.23 at the time of publication on Friday, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSEC Gives Tokenized Stocks a Five-Year Onchain Runway, Robinhood CEO Vlad Tenev Says ‘It’s a Good Day for US Innovation’\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'047f308cf0ababbcc094b72a5ce75a91e06a5730','2026-09-18 16:44:49','2026-09-18 17:21:49.436820',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 16:47:08');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(415,'alpaca:61875249','benzinga','2026-09-18 16:42:56','Why Is MARA Stock Surging on Friday?','MARA Holdings stock is climbing Friday as Bitcoin rebounds sharply, while a higher Morgan Stanley price forecast adds to the momentum. Here’s a look at MARA’s technical setup, analyst outlook and exposure across crypto-focused ETFs.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61875249/why-is-mara-stock-surging-on-friday','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 17:21:59.865943','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'MARA stock is rising due to a rebound in Bitcoin and a higher price forecast from Morgan Stanley.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.676}}','2026-09-19 17:24:38.414087','2026-09-18 17:21:49.495669','61875249',replace('MARA Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:MARA) stock is surging Friday, supported by a sharp rebound in Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) prices and a higher analyst price forecast. The Nasdaq is up 0.05% while the S&P; 500 has shed 0.34%.\n\nBitcoin was trading at $80,997.20, up 6.09% over the past 24 hours. Meanwhile, Morgan Stanley maintained its Underweight rating on MARA but raised its price forecast to $11 on Friday.\n\nMoreover, shares of crypto-linked companies are trading higher after the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission submitted a proposal Thursday to establish a regulatory framework for crypto asset transactions and markets. The move, along with announcements from the CFTC and U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission on Wednesday, signals continued regulatory action after the CLARITY Act failed to advance in the Senate, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEvery AI Agent Needs a Gatekeeper: 3 Cybersecurity Stocks to Watch\n\nTechnical Analysis\n\nFrom a trend perspective, MARA is back in a constructive posture: it’s trading 11.7% above its 20-day SMA ($11.39) and 13.8% above its 50-day SMA ($11.18), which typically signals buyers are defending pullbacks. It’s also 16.2% above the 200-day SMA ($10.95), keeping the longer-term bias pointed upward even after a rough 12-month stretch (down 31.22%).\n\nThe moving-average structure supports that view, with the 20-day SMA above the 50-day SMA and a golden cross (50-day above 200-day) that occurred in June. That said, the stock is still working through overhead supply from earlier in the year, with a recent swing high logged in July and a swing low in August that traders will use as the near-term "range map."\n\nKey Resistance: $13 — a nearby round-number area where rebounds can stall\n\nKey Support: $11.50 — a nearby floor that sits close to the stock’s short-term moving-average zone\n\nAnalysts Take A Mixed View On MARA\n\nMARA Holdings carries a Buy consensus, with an average analyst price forecast of $17. Recent analyst actions have been mixed, with JPMorgan downgrading the stock to Underweight and lowering its price target to $11 on Monday, while HC Wainwright & Co. maintained a Buy rating with a $20 forecast on Sept. 11.\n\nMARA Has Significant Crypto ETF Exposure\n\nMARA is also a notable holding across several crypto-focused ETFs, including the Bitwise Crypto Industry Innovators ETF (NYSE:BITQ) at a 3.87% weight, the Global X Blockchain ETF (NASDAQ:BKCH) at 3.98%, and the Fidelity Crypto Industry and Digital Payments ETF (NASDAQ:FDIG) at 2.83%. Significant inflows or outflows from these funds could lead to corresponding buying or selling of MARA shares as the ETFs rebalance their portfolios.\n\nMARA Stock Price Activity: MARA Holdings shares were up 8.93% at $12.68 at the time of publication on Friday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nRead Also:\n\nJim Cramer Flags ''Boatload'' of Bullish Option Buying in Micron, Sandisk, Intel\n\nPhoto: Minh8686 / Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'955096eafec1afa4812b4e3ea865de7814ed6207','2026-09-18 16:42:56','2026-09-18 17:21:49.436820',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 16:42:56');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(416,'alpaca:61877591','benzinga','2026-09-18 18:03:28','Japan Outpaces S&P 500 By 81%—Yen Drops After BOJ Hike, Raising Spillover Risks For The US',replace('\n\n\n\nReaction To Japan Rate Hike\n\n\n\nPlease click here for an enlarged chart comparing SPDR S&amp;P 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) which represents the benchmark stock market index S&amp;P 500 (SPX) and iShares MSCI Japan ETF','\n',char(10)),'https://www.benzinga.com/Opinion/26/09/61877591/japan-outpaces-sp500-by-81-percent-yen-drops-after-boj-hike-raising-spillover-risks-for-us','["AAPL", "AMZN", "BTC/USD", "META", "MSFT", "NVDA", "QQQ", "SPY", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 18:22:09.751867','macro','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses broader market performance and its implications without detailing specific impacts on individual assets.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "AMZN": 251.18, "BTC/USD": 76528.6, "META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48, "NVDA": 219.37}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.982}}','2026-09-19 18:24:50.228210','2026-09-18 18:22:04.605072','61877591',replace('Reaction To Japan Rate Hike\n\nPlease click here for an enlarged chart comparing SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) which represents the benchmark stock market index S&P; 500 (SPX) and iShares MSCI Japan ETF (NYSE:EWJ).\n\nNote the following:\n\nThe chart shows Japan ETF EWJ has outperformed S&P; 500 by 81%.  Excluding the impact of the currencies, Nikkei 225 has outperformed the S&P; by about 152% year-to-date.\n\nOvernight, Bank of Japan (BOJ) increased its key interest rate to 1.25%.  This is the highest rate in three decades.\n\nExpectations were that if BOJ were to raise its key rate, the yen would strengthen.  However, the yen has fallen on the news.  In our analysis, the reason for the perverse reaction is that the vote in favor of a rate hike was 7 to 2.   This indicates division at BOJ.  Such division may make further rate hikes difficult.  In our analysis, the risk in Japan is inflation going above 2%.  In such an environment, further rate hikes will be needed.  \n\nThe move in the yen is creating a policy headache for the U.S.\n\nJapan is a large holder of U.S. Treasuries.  To protect the yen, Japan may need to sell U.S. Treasuries so that it has dollars to intervene in the forex market.  Such a selling will increase yields in the U.S.  Yields are already rising in the U.S. creating headaches and leading the Fed to raise interest rates for the first time since July 2023.\n\nThere is risk to the U.S. stock market from the carry trade, in addition to the risk from rising yields emanating from Japan.  In the carry trade, funds have borrowed hundreds of billions of dollars in Japan to invest in the U.S., primarily in the AI trade.\n\nAs a full disclosure Japan ETF EWJ is in our portfolio.  \n\nToday is triple witching.  In triple witching, stock index futures, options on indexes, and options on stocks expire on the same day.  Yesterday, the stock market, especially semiconductor stocks, staged a major rally driven by triple witching.  In the early trade today, there is upward pressure from triple witching.\n\nIn important news, hackers used Anthropic’s Claude to break into OpenAI systems.  Although the stock market has dismissed AI safety issues, AI safety issues continue to be a risk.\n\nMagnificent Seven Money Flows\n\nMost portfolios are now heavily concentrated in the Mag 7 stocks.  For this reason, it is important to pay attention to early money flows in the Mag 7 stocks on a daily basis. \n\nIn the early trade, money flows are positive in Amazon.com, Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN), Alphabet Inc Class C (NASDAQ:GOOG), Meta Platforms Inc (NASDAQ:META), and Tesla Inc (NASDAQ:TSLA).\n\nIn the early trade, money flows are neutral in Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL), Microsoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT), and NVIDIA Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA).\n\nIn the early trade, money flows are neutral in S&P; 500 ETF (SPY) and positive in Invesco QQQ Trust Series 1 (NASDAQ:QQQ).\n\nMomo Crowd And Smart Money In Stocks\n\nInvestors can gain an edge by knowing money flows in SPY and QQQ.  Investors can get a bigger edge by knowing when smart money is buying stocks, gold, and oil.  The most popular ETF for gold is SPDR Gold Trust (GLD).  The most popular ETF for silver is iShares Silver Trust (SLV).  The most popular ETF for oil is United States Oil ETF (USO).\n\nBitcoin\n\nBitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) is seeing buying.\n\nWhat To Do Now\n\nConsider continuing to hold good, very long term, existing positions and add tactical positions based on signals.\n\nThe Arora Report is known for its accurate calls. The Arora Report correctly called the big artificial intelligence rally before anyone else, the new bull market of 2023, the bear market of 2022, new stock market highs right after the virus low in 2020, the virus drop in 2020, the DJIA rally to 30,000 when it was trading at 16,000, the start of a mega bull market in 2009, and the financial crash of 2008. Please click here to sign up for a free forever Generate Wealth Newsletter.\n\nBenzinga Disclaimer: This article is from an unpaid external contributor. It does not represent Benzinga’s reporting and has not been edited for content or accuracy.','\n',char(10)),'d0ac5be5639301a358f29ae2a59e9dbed83f860c','2026-09-18 18:03:28','2026-09-18 18:22:04.600859',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 18:09:10');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(417,'alpaca:61877257','benzinga','2026-09-18 17:51:41','Coinbase Stock Rises as CFTC Proposes Crypto Regulations','Coinbase Global shares are surging Friday, along with other crypto-linked stocks, as Bitcoin rises on a CFTC regulatory proposal.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61877257/coinbase-stock-rises-as-cftc-proposes-crypto-regulations','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 18:22:12.036394','regulatory','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'The proposal by CFTC is likely to create a more favorable regulatory environment for cryptocurrencies.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.982}}','2026-09-19 18:24:50.228210','2026-09-18 18:22:04.612919','61877257',replace('Coinbase Global Inc. (NASDAQ:COIN) shares are surging Friday along with other crypto-linked stocks as Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) rises following a CFTC proposal this week to regulate crypto asset transactions and markets.\n\nCoinbase Global stock is among today’s top performers. Why are COIN shares rallying?\n\nSEC Creates a Framework for Tokenized Stock Trading\n\nThe SEC introduced a five-year pilot program allowing qualified trading platforms to offer blockchain versions of U.S.-listed equities, with a catch: those tokenized shares have to carry the same dividend payments and voting rights as ordinary shares, and trading has to freeze whenever the actual stock’s exchange pauses activity.\n\nRobinhood has positioned itself well ahead of this shift, having already run a similar model overseas. CEO Vlad Tenev has noted the company offers around 200 tokenized versions of U.S. stocks to customers in more than 120 countries internationally, though that access still isn’t extended to American users.\n\nThe SEC’s new pilot program could eventually give Robinhood room to bring that international offering stateside, though the rules governing it remain both temporary and narrowly defined for now.\n\nCFTC Loosens Requirements for Prediction Market Platforms\n\nAt the same time, the CFTC gave the green light this week to a category of technology providers it labels “passive software,” letting them connect users to CFTC-regulated products, including prediction markets, without having to register as brokers themselves, so long as they stay out of handling customer funds and don’t influence how trades get carried out.\n\nThe framework mirrors an approach already in use at crypto wallet Phantom, where more than 20 million users can already access similar prediction market features, and it remains valid only until the agency puts permanent rules in place.\n\nRegulators Move Forward After Congress Stalls On CLARITY Act\n\nBoth regulatory actions land just after Congress hit a wall on crypto legislation, with the CLARITY Act coming up 11 votes shy of the 60 required to move forward this week. Wyoming Sen. Cynthia Lummis, who had pushed hardest for the bill’s passage, signaled that effort was essentially dead.\n\nWith Capitol Hill unable to pass comprehensive crypto rules, the CFTC and SEC appear to be filling that vacuum on their own, moving forward with regulatory action independent of congressional gridlock.\n\nCOIN Shares Are Flying\n\nCOIN Price Action: Coinbase shares were up 12.16% at $195.12 at the time of publication on Friday, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Tops $80,000, S&P; 500 Slips as Yields Reclaim 5%: Stock Market Today\n\nImage: miss.cabul/Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'2c7727f6dd709d3f9f3bdfa902a80463b821a4c5','2026-09-18 17:51:41','2026-09-18 18:22:04.600859',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 17:51:41');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(418,'alpaca:61877048','benzinga','2026-09-18 17:45:06','XRP Skyrockets 6% as Whale Binance Inflows Hit 6-Month High','XRP rebounds to $1.40 as Binance whale inflows hit a six-month high; Evernorth raises $30M to buy XRP ahead of its Nasdaq debut.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61877048/xrp-skyrockets-6-as-whale-binance-inflows-hit-6-month-high','["XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-18 18:22:13.607442','other','bullish',3,3,'hours',1,'Significant inflows to Binance indicate strong market interest in XRP.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"XRP/USD": {"60m": 8.37, "1d": 9.639}}','2026-09-19 18:24:50.228210','2026-09-18 18:22:04.618700','61877048',replace('XRP (CRYPTO: XRP) jumped 6 over the past 24 hours ,briefly touching $1.40 as whale inflows to Binance surged to a six-month high.\n\nThe sharp price rebound comes after XRP suffered a steep selloff earlier this week following the failed Senate vote to advance the Clarity Act.\n\nHow XRP Whale Inflows Help?\n\nCryptoQuant data on Friday shows cumulative XRP whale inflows to Binance over the past 30 days reaching almost 1.6 billion XRP, the highest level since March.\n\nThe metric declined steadily through May, June and July before recovering in August and accelerating in recent weeks.\n\nHigher exchange inflows put more XRP within easy reach of the market, potentially increasing short-term selling pressure.\n\nHowever, transfers to Binance do not necessarily mean whales intend to sell, as they may also reflect trading, liquidity management or portfolio repositioning.\n\nThe signal could turn more bearish if elevated whale inflows coincide with rising net exchange deposits, trading volumes and reserves. Without corresponding selling pressure, the flows may instead reflect increased trading activity.\n\nWill Spot XRP ETF Bounce?\n\nXRP-focused treasury management company Evernorth reportedly raised $30 million through convertible notes issued to South Korean institutional investor NH Investment & Securities.\n\nThe financing is contingent on the successful completion of Evernorth’s planned SPAC merger.\n\nEvernorth plans to deploy the proceeds into spot XRP ahead of its public-market debut.\n\nFollowing the SPAC transaction, the company intends to list on Nasdaq under the ticker XRPN.\n\nRead Also:\n\nXRP Up 3% as Ripple Adds XRP Payments to Stripe, Tempo’s AI Standard\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'2bece0c19cabf974a0a8f7ffc0102c210fcb50c5','2026-09-18 17:45:06','2026-09-18 18:22:04.600859',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 17:45:06');
