It expires in 91 day(s) on December 18, 2026. Parties traded 2300 contract(s) at a $30.00 strike. This particular call needed to be split into 3 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $207.0K, with a price of $90.0 per contract. There were 9428 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 3062 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• Regarding ORCL (NYSE:ORCL), we observe a call option sweep with bullish sentiment. It expires in 7 day(s) on September 25, 2026. Parties traded 438 contract(s) at a $157.50 strike. This particular call needed to be split into 7 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $25.8K, with a price of $59.0 per contract. There were 2170 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 1381 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• For RIOT (NASDAQ:RIOT), we notice a call option sweep that happens to be bearish, expiring in 14 day(s) on October 2, 2026. This event was a transfer of 853 contract(s) at a $26.00 strike. This particular call needed to be split into 22 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $39.5K, with a price of $47.0 per contract. There were 3632 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 1381 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• For AAPL (NASDAQ:AAPL), we notice a put option sweep that happens to be bearish, expiring in 91 day(s) on December 18, 2026. This event was a transfer of 26 contract(s) at a $350.00 strike. This particular put needed to be split into 6 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $61.3K, with a price of $2360.0 per contract. There were 839 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 854 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• For NBIS (NASDAQ:NBIS), we notice a call option trade that happens to be bearish, expiring in 7 day(s) on September 25, 2026. This event was a transfer of 77 contract(s) at a $210.00 strike. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $112.8K, with a price of $1465.0 per contract. There were 476 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 700 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• For SWKS (NASDAQ:SWKS), we notice a put option sweep that happens to be bearish, expiring in 28 day(s) on October 16, 2026. This event was a transfer of 131 contract(s) at a $85.00 strike. This particular put needed to be split into 19 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $47.1K, with a price of $359.0 per contract. There were 925 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 672 contract(s) were bought and sold. \nOptions Alert Terminology\n - Call Contracts: The right to buy shares as indicated in the contract.\n - Put Contracts: The right to sell shares as indicated in the contract.\n - Expiration Date: When the contract expires. One must act on the contract by this date if one wants to use it.\n - Premium/Option Price: The price of the contract. \nFor more information, read more news on unusual options activity. \nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'fb58b696c1e5bdf5cbf1c305085143bdbc48ba29','2026-09-18 17:35:13','2026-09-18 18:22:04.600859',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 17:35:13');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(420,'alpaca:61879307','benzinga','2026-09-18 19:15:33','$3.2T Chip Boom: Which Semiconductor ETFs Get The Biggest Slice?','Bank of America sees the semiconductor market reaching $3.2T by 2030. Here’s how AI, memory and chip-equipment ETFs could benefit.','https://www.benzinga.com/etfs/sector-etfs/26/09/61879307/3-2t-chip-boom-which-semiconductor-etfs-get-the-biggest-slice','["AMD", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 19:22:24.148484','macro','bullish',3,3,'weeks',1,'A significant market expansion forecast could positively impact semiconductor ETFs.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 19:24:59.841319','2026-09-18 19:22:19.332639','61879307',replace('Bank of America expects the global semiconductor market to reach $3.2 trillion by 2030, up from $1.7 trillion in 2026 — about 88% growth. The bank also raised its U.S. semiconductor CAGR forecast through 2030 to 18%, up from 14%, per an Investors Hub article, with memory and data-center products driving much of the gain.\n\nThat raises a more specific ETF question: which parts of the semiconductor supply chain are best positioned to capture it?\n\nMemory Could Be The Biggest Growth Engine\n\nBank of America expects memory sales to increase from $937 billion in 2026 to $1.8 trillion by 2030, a roughly 92% increase. Server-related sales are projected to climb from $359 billion to $848 billion over the same period, implying growth of about 136%.\n\nThat makes memory and data-center exposure particularly relevant to the semiconductor ETF trade.\n\nBroad funds already provide significant exposure to memory. VanEck Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SMH), for example, holds Micron Technology Inc (NASDAQ:MU) at 5.54%. SMH’s largest holding was Nvidia Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) at 22.09%, followed by Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing (NYSE:TSM) at 9.75%. The fund held 26 securities. \n\niShares Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SOXX) also has Micron among its largest holdings at 9.17%, alongside Nvidia at 9.18%, Advanced Micro Devices Inc (NASDAQ:AMD) at 8.75% and Broadcom, Inc (NASDAQ:AVGO) at 7.07%. \n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nBank of America’s Forecast Extends Beyond Chips\n\nWafer-fabrication equipment spending is expected to more than double from $155.9 billion in 2026 to $359.8 billion by 2030.\n\nThat could put semiconductor equipment companies such as Applied Materials Inc (NASDAQ:AMAT), Lam Research Corp (NASDAQ:LRCX) and KLA Corp (NASDAQ:KLAC) in focus. All three are among SOXX’s top 10 holdings.\n\nSMH also holds Applied Materials at 4.19%, Lam Research at 4.23% and KLA at 3.86%. \n\nThis gives broad semiconductor ETFs exposure not only to AI accelerators but also to the companies supplying the equipment required to manufacture increasingly sophisticated chips.\n\nBroad Chip ETFs Offer Different Exposure\n\nThe distinction becomes clearer when comparing broad funds.\n\nSMH has a concentrated portfolio, with Nvidia accounting for more than one-fifth of assets. SOXX spreads exposure across 30 holdings and, as of Sept. 9, had 79.55% of its portfolio in semiconductors and 20.38% in semiconductor equipment. \n\nState Street SPDR S&P; Semiconductor ETF (NYSE:XSD), meanwhile, takes a more diversified approach. Its largest holding, Impinj Inc (NASDAQ:PI), represents just 4.04%, while Nvidia accounted for 2.98% and Micron 2.89%.\n\nThat difference matters if BofA’s forecast ultimately broadens from a handful of AI leaders to the wider semiconductor ecosystem.\n\nThe $3.2 trillion semiconductor forecast points to three main AI-driven growth areas: AI computing, memory and chipmaking equipment. For ETF investors, that means looking beyond broad semiconductor funds to more targeted exposure. The trade-off is that elevated valuations and AI-spending expectations make concentration, fees, and volatility important considerations.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSandisk Options Surge As SNXX Ranks Among Most Active ETFs. What Investors Are Betting On\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'58fad557a63b58127f4a0c47c230bcc9578d7cd3','2026-09-18 19:15:33','2026-09-18 19:22:19.327030',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 19:15:33');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(421,'alpaca:61878667','benzinga','2026-09-18 18:48:21','Bitcoin Breaks Above $80,000 as CoinShares Warns Of a ''Difficult Setup'' Into Year-End','Bitcoin price tops $80,000 despite CoinShares warning that a hawkish Fed and Clarity Act failure could weigh on crypto into year-end.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61878667/bitcoin-breaks-above-80000-as-coinshares-warns-of-a-difficult-setup-into-year-end','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 19:22:25.968735','other','neutral',3,4,'days',1,'Bitcoin''s price movement occurs amid external warnings about the future.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.982}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 7.139}}','2026-09-19 19:24:59.841319','2026-09-18 19:22:19.339637','61878667',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) broke above $80,000 Friday, surging 6%, even as CoinShares warned of a difficult setup heading into year-end.\n\nWhy CoinShares Sees Two Headwinds Stacking Up\n\nCoinShares Head of Research James Butterfill wrote in a Friday note that two developments now weigh on Bitcoin into year-end.\n\nHawkish Fed\n\nRemoving expected easing through 2027 from the dot plot matters more than the hike itself\n\nSupports the dollar and delays the liquidity conditions Bitcoin typically feeds on\n\nIran’s ongoing conflict keeps energy prices elevated, raising odds of another hike this year\n\nClarity Act failure\n\nNot a multi-year delay, in Butterfill’s view\n\nStablecoin issuers now buy meaningful US government debt at elevated yields, keeping the bill bipartisan-relevant\n\nA revised version could return as early as next year\n\nThe impact also lands unevenly. Bitcoin stays relatively insulated given its clearer regulatory footing, while Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) and other altcoins carry more exposure since much of the stablecoin payment infrastructure runs on those networks.\n\nWhy Rate Policy Alone May Not Matter This Much\n\nAs Benzinga reported Thursday, Grayscale’s Head of Research Zach Pandl offered a more measured read on the same rate hike, calling it a mid-cycle adjustment rather than a policy shift. \n\nHe compared it to the Greenspan Fed’s 1997 mid-cycle hike, after which the Nasdaq bull market kept running, and expects one or two more hikes in 2026 to have limited effect on capital allocation into digital assets. \n\nPandl also flagged that stablecoin issuers like Circle (NYSE:CRCL) and Tether (CRYPTO: USDT) actually benefit from higher rates through their Treasury and money market reserves, showing rate policy hits different corners of crypto differently rather than uniformly.\n\nBTC Price Prediction: Key Levels to Watch\n\nBTC breaks sharply out of its descending triangle Friday, climbing to $80,804 in a move that clears both the falling trendline and the EMA cluster in one candle. \n\nThe MACD just turned bullish, crossing back above its signal line after weeks of fading momentum. The 20-day EMA at $77,217 has been reclaimed as support.\n\nKey levels for BTC:\n\n$82,000 — September high and triangle origin, next major test\n\n$77,217 — 20-day EMA, must hold to keep momentum intact\n\nRead Also:\n\nStrategy CEO Says ''We''re Never Going To Stop'' Buying Bitcoin as MSTR Surges 11%\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'4d66ebb48aa25ff92629f6c4d7120d98147e6923','2026-09-18 18:48:21','2026-09-18 19:22:19.327030',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 18:48:21');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(422,'alpaca:61878548','benzinga','2026-09-18 18:42:49','Brad Gerstner Says AI Labs Need $180B Revenue Run Rate to Keep Nvidia Trade Alive','Brad Gerstner says AI labs need a $180B revenue run rate by year-end to sustain the AI trade and justify hyperscaler spending.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61878548/ai-labs-180-billion-revenue-gerstner','["AMZN", "MSFT", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 19:22:27.511111','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The statement discusses expectations without confirming any specific event.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "MSFT": 498.48, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 19:24:59.841319','2026-09-18 19:22:19.342409','61878548',replace('Brad Gerstner says leading AI labs need to lift their combined annualized revenue from roughly $100 billion to at least $180 billion by year-end to keep the AI trade intact.\n\nThe Altimeter Capital founder, whose firm held nearly $1.9 billion of Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) shares at the end of June, called AI lab revenue "the single most important data point in the market today" at the All-In Summit.\n\nAI Revenue Has to Keep Exploding\n\nGerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and SpaceX (NASDAQ:SPCX), which owns xAI, had a combined run rate of roughly $100 billion based on figures circulating in July.\n\nGerstner said the companies need to reach at least $180 billion by year-end, up about 80% from his July estimate, "just to keep the AI trade intact."\n\n"These revenues have never happened before in the history of capitalism," Gerstner said.\n\nHe argued investors are already trading on those figures. Anthropic’s revenue run rate reportedly reached $65 billion in July, up from $47 billion in May.\n\n"We ripped off the bottom because the fuse was lit by Anthropic’s monthly revenue," Gerstner said of the spring rally. He said stocks later consolidated after the $65 billion figure fell short of the roughly $75 billion investors had expected.\n\n‘Somebody Has to Pay for It’\n\nGerstner said the revenue growth is needed to support the huge sums Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT) and Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOGL) are spending on AI infrastructure.\n\n"If you’re going to build a trillion and a half dollars a year in capex, somebody has to pay for it," he said.\n\nThe two companies are building computing capacity that AI labs such as OpenAI and Anthropic pay to use.\n\n"Microsoft’s not paying for it. They’re building it to rent it. Google’s not paying for it. They’re building it to rent it," Gerstner said.\n\nThe labs, he argued, need enough revenue from consumers and businesses to keep paying for that capacity. "Otherwise, we can’t build this much capex," he said.\n\nGerstner Has Skin in the Trade\n\nAltimeter held 9.41 million Nvidia shares worth $1.88 billion at June 30, about 19% of its reported U.S. equity portfolio. Its filing also listed $303.5 million of SpaceX shares, while Altimeter holds stakes in Anthropic and OpenAI.\n\nGerstner called the boom "the largest capex buildout, the largest super cycle in the history of technology," and said semiconductors have generated 70% of the Nasdaq’s return this year.\n\nThat revenue test matters for Nvidia because its chips sit at the center of the infrastructure buildout Gerstner is describing. On Polymarket, traders give Nvidia a 74% chance of finishing 2026 as the world’s largest company. The market has attracted roughly $7.4 million in volume.\n\nNvidia shares are trading around $220 Friday morning after gaining 2.5% Thursday.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nOracle, CoreWeave Dump on AI''s $3.6 Trillion Financing Bill','\n',char(10)),'b649c71e87b4573418fcfb76539022248815889e','2026-09-18 18:42:49','2026-09-18 19:22:19.327030',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 18:42:49');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(423,'alpaca:61878323','benzinga','2026-09-18 18:35:45','S&P Growth Is a Feature, Not a Bug, Goldman Says','It may feel like 2000, but Goldman Sachs argues that it&#39;s just a temporary peak driven by three specific, identifiable factors.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61878323/goldman-sachs-profits-bubble-cyclical-peak','["AMZN", "META", "MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-18 19:22:28.814392','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline reflects an analyst''s interpretation of market conditions without a definitive impact on asset prices.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48}','{}','2026-09-19 19:24:59.841319','2026-09-18 19:22:19.345114','61878323',replace('Goldman Sachs strategist Ben Snider is pushing back on the idea that today’s sky-high corporate profits are a “bubble” about to pop.\n\nYes, earnings are growing much faster than normal — up 51% year over year in Q2 and 26% over the past year — and valuations (CAPE ratio) are near dot-com-era highs. That combination sounds alarming, like 2000 all over again.\n\nYet, the bank sees the surge as an orderly cyclical peak rather than an impending crash.\n\n“Our base case is for S&P; 500 earnings growth to decelerate, not collapse, in coming years,” strategist Ben Snider wrote in a client note.\n\nValuations Tell a Split Story\n\nThe cyclically adjusted price-to-earnings ratio sits near record highs, a level topped in recent decades only at the dot-com peak. Yet the forward 12-month multiple has slid to 19x from 23x a year ago, matching its 10-year average.\n\n“Market pricing embeds an outlook for continued earnings growth but healthy skepticism regarding the sustainability of current profitability,” Snider said.\n\nGoldman set a 12-month S&P; 500 target of 8,700, implying a 14% return, and expects EPS to climb 11% in both 2027 and 2028, to $415 and $460, respectively. That is more cautious than consensus, which Bloomberg Intelligence data show calling for 19% and 17% growth.\n\nSolid GDP expansion and a 1-2 percentage-point productivity boost from AI adoption support the outlook.\n\n“Our 12-month S&P; 500 return forecast of +14% (to 8,700) reflects the view that earnings growth, rather than expanding valuations, will remain the primary driver of the bull market,” Snider concluded.\n\n3 Temporary Dynamics\n\nFirst, consider the hyperscaler capex wave. Amazon (NASDAQ:AMZN), Meta (NASDAQ:META), Alphabet (NASDAQ:GOOGL) and Microsoft (NASDAQ:MSFT) are on track to spend $800 billion in 2026, up 94% from 2025. The AI investment boom accounts for nearly half of this year’s index EPS growth. Goldman expects that tailwind to shrink from an 11 percentage-point boost today to a marginal drag by 2028 as spending growth slows and depreciation mounts.\n\nSecond, memory makers are posting gross margins near 80%. That’s more than double their historical average, with margin expansion driving about a quarter of chip-sector earnings growth in 2026. Should industry gross margins fall from 70% to their 15-year average of 55%, Goldman estimates S&P; 500 earnings would take a roughly 10% hit.\n\nThird, there is non-operating income. Mega-cap tech booked more than $150 billion in “other income” from private investment gains in the second quarter alone, equal to 12% of index EPS. Goldman expects that contribution to fade, creating an 8 percentage-point drag on 2027 growth comparisons.\n\nThe Risk: AI’s Circular Financing\n\nHyperscalers, chipmakers and model developers are increasingly one another’s customers, suppliers and investors, so a single disappointment could ripple across the group. \n\nAmazon’s $53.4 billion in other income last quarter came largely from Anthropic-related gains, and Nvidia has disclosed over $108 billion in maximum guarantee exposure to ecosystem partners. \n\nBank of America strategists Jared Woodard and Michael Hartnett warned positioning is too bullish given slowing profit growth, even as equity funds pulled in nearly $64 billion last week, the strongest inflow in three months.\n\nGoldman Expects Gradual Cooling, Not a Crash\n\nThe firm expects the over-earning phase to subside, as baseline demand replaces initial buildout tailwinds.\n\nWhether newly built AI capacity earns above its cost of capital remains to be seen.\n\nImage created using artificial intelligence via Gemini.','\n',char(10)),'64eee8458d177277172fc3acf7f7b876d88ff828','2026-09-18 18:35:45','2026-09-18 19:22:19.327030',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 18:35:45');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(424,'alpaca:61881383','benzinga','2026-09-18 20:12:53','Congressman Ditches Magnificent Seven Stocks for Consumer Staples: Here''s What He Bought','A US congressman sold some Magnificent Seven stocks and replaced them with a couple consumer staples. Here&#39;s the trades.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/politics/26/09/61881383/congressman-ditches-magnificent-seven-stocks-for-consumer-staples-heres-what-he-bought','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-18 20:22:36.778267','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'A politician''s trading activity is noteworthy but not likely to move the stock market significantly.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}','2026-09-19 20:25:04.162099','2026-09-18 20:22:32.365014','61881383',replace('A member of Congress recently disclosed numerous stock trades, with some new names bought and some of the Magnificent Seven stocks sold. Here’s a look at the trades and the Congress member’s trading history.\n\nCongressman Buys Consumer Names\n\nRep. Scott Franklin (R-Fla.) recently made his first stock trades since February, moves that can be viewed on the Benzinga Government Trades page.\n\nAmong the transactions disclosed were:\n\nAug. 20: Sold $1,000 to $15,000 in Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL) stock\n\nAug. 20: Sold $1,000 to $15,000 in Alphabet (NASDAQ:GOOG) stock\n\nAug. 20: Sold $1,000 to $15,000 in Alphabet stock\n\nAug. 26: Bought $1,000 to $15,000 in McDonald’s Corp (NYSE:MCD) stock\n\nAug. 26: Bought $1,000 to $15,000 in PepsiCo (NASDAQ:PEP) stock\n\nAug. 26: Bought $1,000 to $15,000 in PepsiCo stock\n\nA look at the trades above show a switch from Magnificent Seven and big technology names to consumer goods like PepsiCo and McDonald’s, a top restaurant.\n\nThe moves may be risky given the rising inflation and higher consumer costs on goods at McDonald’s and from PepsiCo. Franklin’s timing may indicate he thinks the worst of inflation is behind consumers and that the companies could be winners moving forward.\n\nFranklin also sold JPMorgan (NYSE:JPM) stock and bought shares of Accenture (NYSE:ACN) and Novo Nordisk (NYSE:NVO).\n\nRead Also:\n\nNancy Pelosi, Donald Trump Bet On The Same 10 Stocks – Some Might Surprise You\n\nFranklin’s Trading History\n\nAs mentioned above, these were the first disclosed transactions by the congressman since February, but are certainly not among his first overall.\n\nFranklin has made 290 stock trades totaling $80.9 million since 2021, according to data from Quiver Quantitative.\n\nThe majority of that trading occurred in 2021, totaling $62.1 million.\n\nLast year, Franklin bought and sold $4.8 million in shares. This year, the total is around $187,000.\n\nIn recent years, Franklin has been selling more than buying, which could indicate profit-taking, bearishness, or tax-related activity.\n\nRead Also:\n\nFlorida Governor Candidate Sells 2 Stocks, Buys This Tech Underperformer\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'e846a9c40567c61b53b154013286e6da7f3b522c','2026-09-18 20:12:53','2026-09-18 20:22:32.359667',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 20:12:53');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(425,'alpaca:61881343','benzinga','2026-09-18 20:11:49','Fed Raises Rates, Yields Hit 2007 Highs as Fuel Costs Set Records: This Week On Wall Street','The Fed hiked for the first time since 2023; the 10-year yield touched 5.04%, and record diesel prices hit truckers and automakers.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/commodities/26/09/61881343/fed-raises-rates-yields-2007-highs-fuel-costs-records-this-week-wall-street','["AMZN", "BTC/USD", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 20:22:39.036591','macro','bearish',3,4,'days',1,'The rate hike may negatively impact market sentiment and borrowing costs.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "BTC/USD": 76528.6, "NVDA": 219.37}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.982}}','2026-09-19 20:25:04.162099','2026-09-18 20:22:32.368097','61881343',replace('The Federal Reserve raised interest rates Wednesday for the first time since 2023, lifting its benchmark a quarter point to 3.75%-4%.\n\nThe vote was unanimous, 12-0, and 16 of the 18 policymakers who submitted forecasts penciled in at least one more increase this year.\n\nInflation is running at 3.4%, unchanged from July but well above the Fed’s 2% target. The U.S. Central Bank now sees a return to the objective no earlier than 2029.\n\nOfficials revised their forecasts for inflation and growth higher, and unemployment lower.\n\nFed Chair Kevin Warsh said the central bank had removed “a dose of accommodation.”\n\nAsked what message he had for President Donald Trump, who has spent months demanding cuts, Warsh said he had “nothing for you.”\n\nThe Fed’s next meeting is in late October, days before the midterm elections.\n\nThe Bond Market Had Already Moved\n\nThe 10-year Treasury yield touched 5.04% ahead of the decision, its highest level since 2007, as investors weighed whether the Fed could contain price pressures with oil above $100 a barrel.\n\nThe iShares 7-10 Year Treasury Bond ETF (NASDAQ:IEF) closed the third straight week of losses, reaching November 2023 lows. \n\nThe move was not confined to the 10-year maturity. \n\nThe 2-year yield climbed to 4.75% and the 30-year to 5.34%, leaving the curve repriced for a central bank that has stopped easing and started tightening.\n\nChart: 10-Year Treasury Close The Week At 5% Yield, Highest Since 2007\n\nFuel Was The Week’s Real Disruption\n\nDiesel set fresh records, with the average topping $6.30 a gallon, after a drone strike damaged pumping stations on Saudi Arabia’s East-West pipeline, the line carrying crude to the Red Sea.\n\nThose costs are already reaching earnings.\n\nJ.B. Hunt Transport Services Inc. (NASDAQ:JBHT), one of the largest U.S. trucking and intermodal carriers, warned Wednesday that third-quarter profit would fall 5% to 10%, citing $25 million in added driver expenses and more than $10 million from fuel.\n\nChief Financial Officer Brad Delco described “some of the most radical and abnormal swings” in fuel prices the company has experienced.\n\nThe stock dropped sharply on the warning and finished the week down 13.2%, the worst performer in the S&P; 500. Schneider National Inc. (NYSE:SNDR), Old Dominion Freight Line Inc. (NASDAQ:ODFL), Knight-Swift Transportation Holdings Inc. (NYSE:KNX), XPO Inc. (NYSE:XPO) and Landstar System Inc. (NASDAQ:LSTR) fell with it.\n\nDetroit’s automakers logged a second straight losing week. \n\nGeneral Motors Co. (NYSE:GM) fell about 4%, Ford Motor Co. (NYSE:F) roughly 5%. \n\nCybersecurity Led The Winners\n\nThe week’s best S&P; 500 performer came from an unrelated argument about artificial intelligence.\n\nCrowdStrike Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:CRWD) rose 16.1%, the top gainer in the index, after Anthropic Chief Executive Dario Amodei used a weekend post to call on the AI industry to slow the pace of development. \n\nInvestors read the debate as a durable bid for security spending rather than a threat to it, and the stock touched a record $247.20 on Friday. \n\nStephens lifted its price target to $280 and Bank of America to $260.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEvery AI Agent Needs a Gatekeeper: 3 Cybersecurity Stocks to Watch\n\nMajor Players Followed\n\nPalo Alto Networks Inc. (NASDAQ:PANW) gained 9.7% and Fortinet Inc. (NASDAQ:FTNT) 8.5%.\n\nRevvity Inc. (NYSE:RVTY) climbed 14.9%, the second-best in the index, on analyst upgrades and deal flow.\n\nKeyBanc raised its target to $165 with an Overweight rating after stronger second-quarter demand trends, and a bolt-on acquisition of France-based Human Cell Design pushes the life sciences company deeper into diabetes, obesity and GLP-1 metabolic research. \n\nThe shares hit January 2023 highs. \n\nCoinbase Global Inc. (NASDAQ:COIN) advanced 10.9% as Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) cleared $80,000, capping the token’s strongest week in years, after the Securities and Exchange Commission granted an innovation exemption enabling trading in tokenized stocks. \n\nStrategy Inc. (NASDAQ:MSTR), Robinhood Markets Inc. (NASDAQ:HOOD) and Bullish (NYSE:BLSH) all rallied alongside it.\n\nGenerac Holdings Inc. (NYSE:GNRC) rose 9.8% on the week’s biggest corporate headline of the week.\n\nThe generator maker signed a long-term agreement to supply backup power for Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) data centers, an arrangement Generac valued at up to $8 billion over its life, with $2.4 billion of deliveries expected across 2027 and 2028. \n\nAmazon’s investment arm received a warrant for up to 1.7 million Generac shares, nearly 3% of the company, at $201 each. Cantor Fitzgerald reiterated Overweight with a $333 target.\n\nFactSet Research Systems Inc. (NYSE:FDS) rounded out the leaders, up 9.4%.\n\nAnd The Losers Beyond Trucking\n\nCharter Communications Inc. (NASDAQ:CHTR) fell 11.4% after Wolfe Research cut the stock to Underperform from Peer Perform with a $118 price target, arguing broadband industry dynamics “look worse.” \n\nThe shares are down roughly 49% over the past year.\n\nCorning Inc. (NYSE:GLW) dropped 10.1% after launching an at-the-market equity offering of up to $2 billion through Goldman Sachs Group Inc. (NYSE:GS), raising concerns about dilution.\n\nThe specialty glass and optical fiber maker had entered the week up roughly 91% for the year on AI infrastructure demand, hyperscaler agreements and Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA)-backed capacity expansion. \n\nRead Also:\n\nFreight Stocks Plummet as Record-High Diesel Squeezes Profit Margins: 7 Names To Watch\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'1fc7946703c37823e1b68101b9aefdbf442b9a08','2026-09-18 20:11:49','2026-09-18 20:22:32.359667',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 20:11:49');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(426,'alpaca:61880990','benzinga','2026-09-18 20:07:11','EXCLUSIVE: Nvidia''s AI Token Trade Has a Catch: ''Attention Correlates. Returns Don''t''','Nvidia earnings can trigger AI-token rallies, but CoinMarketCap data shows attention and returns don&#39;t necessarily move together.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61880990/nvidia-ai-token-trade','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 20:22:40.780579','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses market behavior related to Nvidia''s earnings and AI tokens without any specific event.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 20:25:04.162099','2026-09-18 20:22:32.371532','61880990',replace('Nvidia Corp’s (NASDAQ:NVDA) influence on AI tokens is becoming harder to ignore, but CoinMarketCap data suggests investors should not confuse attention with performance. \n\nAI tokens can rally sharply around Nvidia events, yet their longer-term returns often look nothing like the chipmaker’s, making the connection more event-driven than fundamental.\n\nNvidia Earnings Move Tokens\n\nThe relationship is clearest around major Nvidia catalysts. Alice Liu, Head of Research at CoinMarketCap, told Benzinga that page views, trending rankings and social-keyword activity for AI tokens tend to spike around Nvidia earnings, product launches and AI model releases.\n\n"Attention correlates. Returns don’t," Liu said in an exclusive email interview with Benzinga.\n\nThe August earnings cycle offered a fresh example, she noted. AI tokens rallied as much as 60% in the week before Nvidia’s Aug. 27 results. Nvidia then reported about $96 billion in revenue versus $92 billion expected, but several AI tokens sold off on the print.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Quality Stocks\n\n"Crypto leads on risk appetite because it trades first and trades always," Liu said. "It does not lead on AI fundamentals, and August proved it."\n\nThat distinction matters for investors treating crypto moves as a signal for AI stocks. Tokens can front-run an Nvidia event without accurately predicting the stock’s reaction.\n\nReturns Tell Another Story\n\nOver the longer term, the performance gap is striking. Nvidia was up 33% over the year covered by CoinMarketCap’s data as of Sept. 10, while Bittensor fell 26%, Render dropped 63% and FET declined 74%.\n\nShorter-term performance tells a different story. Over 30 days, AI tokens gained between 13% and 100%, while Nvidia rose about 3%.\n\nLiu said that divergence reflects different underlying drivers. AI tokens respond to crypto liquidity, Ethereum’s direction and protocol-specific catalysts, while Nvidia is driven primarily by data-center capital spending.\n\n"Nvidia’s earnings move AI tokens for about a week; the other 51 weeks they trade like altcoins," Liu said.\n\nAI Is Not One Trade\n\nThe distinction could become increasingly important as investors look beyond traditional technology stocks for AI exposure. Nvidia’s valuation is tied to demand for GPUs and AI infrastructure, while tokens such as Bittensor, Render, FET and Venice depend on their own networks, liquidity and adoption.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTokenized Nvidia and Tesla Are Becoming Trending Crypto Trades, CoinMarketCap Says\n\nIn other words, an AI token rally can signal rising speculative appetite around the theme without necessarily offering a read-through to Nvidia’s fundamentals.\n\nCoinMarketCap data, as cited by Liu, suggests investors should view the relationship as a sentiment bridge– not a fundamental correlation. Nvidia can pull attention toward AI tokens, while crypto can reveal shifts in risk appetite before traditional markets open, but the two trades can quickly move in opposite directions.\n\nFor Nvidia investors, the next AI-token surge may be worth watching — just not necessarily as a forecast for where NVDA goes next.\n\nNote: All performance data cited above with CoinMarketCap reference to is as of Sept. 10, 2026\n\nRead Also:\n\nAI Crosses Critical Threshold, Tokens Now Profitable\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'c3b10a08d993317b37010767de08b10e97bbfa8d','2026-09-18 20:07:11','2026-09-18 20:22:32.359667',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 20:07:11');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(427,'alpaca:61880616','benzinga','2026-09-18 20:00:26','Is Bitcoin Quantum-Proof? Yes and No, VanEck''s Matthew Sigel Says','VanEck&#39;s Matthew Sigel says quantum computing threatens Bitcoin, but developers have upgrade paths. He adds that visible leverage isn&#39;t a systemic risk.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61880616/is-bitcoin-quantum-proof-yes-and-no-vanecks-matthew-sigel-says','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 20:22:42.265112','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The headline discusses a potential issue without confirmed outcomes.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.982}}','2026-09-19 20:25:04.162099','2026-09-18 20:22:32.374421','61880616',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) faces a potential long-term threat from quantum computing, but the developer community already recognizes the risk and has potential solutions, according to VanEck digital assets research head Matthew Sigel.\n\nCan Bitcoin Beat Quantum Risk?\n\nSigel told CNBC in an interview on Thursday that concerns about increasingly powerful computing systems breaking existing cryptography represent a legitimate risk for Bitcoin.\n\n"Yes, it’s a risk," Sigel said, adding that the Bitcoin community has already "recognized the scope of the issue."\n\nDevelopers and researchers are working toward a framework for upgrading the network, but the challenge is that Bitcoin’s decentralized governance can make major upgrades slower than changes at a conventional technology company.\n\nSigel said Bitcoin upgrades move slowly because its decentralized governance lacks a CEO directing developers.\n\nStill, he noted that technological paths do exist to make Bitcoin quantum resistant.\n\nWhy BTC Leverage Looks Different\n\nSigel also pushed back against concerns that the crypto market currently faces the same hidden leverage risks that contributed to the failures of FTX, Genesis, BlockFi and Celsius during the previous cycle.\n\nHe said much of today’s leverage is more visible, including futures exposure through the CME and debt issued by public companies through regulated U.S. capital markets.\n\nCurrent leverage doesn’t present a systemic risk, Sigel said.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nCFTC Expands Regulatory Relief for Crypto Developers','\n',char(10)),'6d62571cab5951d2e8d069ce0e7624c9a3b55946','2026-09-18 20:00:26','2026-09-18 20:22:32.359667',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 20:00:26');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(428,'alpaca:61880462','benzinga','2026-09-18 19:56:53','Ethereum Reclaims $2,600 After a Week — Is a Bigger Rally Ahead?','Ethereum reclaims $2,600 as fees plunge. Analysts see $2,700-$3,000 upside above $2,570, though demand remains uncertain.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61880462/ethereum-reclaims-2600-after-a-week-is-a-bigger-rally-ahead','["ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-18 20:22:43.275154','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The price recovery is notable but demand remains uncertain.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"ETH/USD": {"60m": 7.139}}','2026-09-19 20:25:04.162099','2026-09-18 20:22:32.377994','61880462',replace('Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) gained to reclaim $2,600 on Friday as network transaction costs fall sharply from their 2026 peak. Trader eyes the next potential breakout.\n\nWhy Did ETH Price Jump?\n\nChart analyst Ali Martinez said on Sep.17 that Ethereum remains inside its four-hour price channel despite heightened volatility in recent sessions.\n\nETH recently tested the channel’s lower boundary, setting up a potential rebound toward the midpoint and eventually the upper boundary around $2,570.\n\nMartinez identified $2,570 as the key breakout level which the altcoin broke on Friday.\n\nA strong four-hour close above that level, supported by volume, could open the door to $2,700 and potentially $3,000.\n\nThe bullish technical setup places focus on whether buyers can extend the recovery into the $2,570 resistance zone.\n\nWhat Favors ETH?\n\nSantiment Intelligence data on Friday shows Ethereum’s average transaction fee has dropped to just $0.095 per transfer, compared with a 2026 peak of $0.72 on April 21.\n\nThe on-chain platform attributed the decline partly to softer mainnet demand during the bearish summer but also pointed to ETH’s expanding network capacity.\n\nSantiment highlighted Fusaka, higher blob throughput, a 60 million gas limit and Layer-2 networks absorbing execution that previously competed for Ethereum mainnet block space.\n\nLower fees make swaps, token transfers, DeFi transactions and stablecoin activity cheaper for users, potentially reducing one of Ethereum’s longstanding barriers to broader network usage.\n\nSantiment cautioned that cheaper transactions alone do not signal stronger demand.\n\nHowever, ETH prices recovering while execution costs remain low could provide a more favorable environment if network participation picks up.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nEthereum at $2,400: Is a Deeper Correction Coming?','\n',char(10)),'4fa30b653ec6fb8ca42c9b740cb02ef2ea37970b','2026-09-18 19:56:53','2026-09-18 20:22:32.359667',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 19:56:53');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(429,'alpaca:61879630','benzinga','2026-09-18 19:28:15','Ripple-Backed Treasury Lines Up $30M: Can XRP Reach $3 in 2026?','Ripple-backed Evernorth lines up $30M tied to its Nasdaq merger as traders price a 6% chance XRP reaches $3 this year.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61879630/xrp-treasury-30-million-xrp-3','["XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-18 20:22:45.342867','other','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'Article speculates on XRP''s future price without confirmed outcomes.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"XRP/USD": {"60m": 8.981, "1d": 10.112}}','2026-09-19 20:25:04.162099','2026-09-18 20:22:32.388057','61879630',replace('Ripple-backed XRP treasury company Evernorth Holdings has lined up $30 million in new financing as it prepares to go public through a merger with Armada Acquisition Corp. II (NASDAQ:XRPN).\n\nThe deal would bring Evernorth onto Nasdaq under the XRPN ticker, giving public-market investors exposure to a company built around accumulating XRP (CRYPTO: XRP) and deploying it across the XRP ecosystem.\n\nEvernorth said the new financing may be used to buy more XRP and fund other ecosystem investments. The $30 million arrives when the merger closes, which the company expects in the fourth quarter.\n\nEvernorth and an affiliate held 473.1 million XRP at the end of 2025. At around $1.38 per token, $30 million would buy roughly another 21.7 million XRP, or less than 5% of that existing position.\n\nNotes Convert at $10.20 After One Year\n\nEvernorth disclosed Thursday that the financing consists of $30 million of 4% convertible notes due in 2031, purchased by NH Investment & Securities as trustee for a South Korean investment fund.\n\nAfter one year, the notes become convertible at an initial price of about $10.20 per share.\n\nArmada shareholders are scheduled to vote on the merger Sept. 30.\n\nXRP Slump Already Changed the Deal\n\nEvernorth amended the merger terms in August after XRP fell from the $2.36 price used when the deal was signed. The revised structure adjusts the share count at closing based on XRP’s value, which Evernorth said should give each share a larger interest in the treasury if the token remains below that original price.\n\nThe company also bought 84.4 million XRP in November 2025 at an average price of about $2.54 per token.\n\nTraders See $1 as More Likely Than $3\n\nPolymarket traders give XRP a 31% chance of falling to $1 again this year, against 6% for a touch of $3.\n\nFrom around $1.38, a move to $1 would represent a decline of roughly 28%, while reaching $3 would require a gain of about 117%.\n\nThe market also puts the chance of XRP reaching $2.60 at 11%, roughly the level needed to exceed the $2.54 average Evernorth paid for its 84.4 million-token cash purchase.\n\nThe next major catalyst comes Sept. 30, when Armada shareholders vote on the Evernorth merger. Approval would clear a key hurdle toward the XRPN listing and release the new financing.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nOracle, CoreWeave Dump on AI''s $3.6 Trillion Financing Bill','\n',char(10)),'2a3c63cfc2b50fed43fc282596115893c030ebee','2026-09-18 19:28:15','2026-09-18 20:22:32.359667',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 19:28:15');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(430,'alpaca:61879416','benzinga','2026-09-18 19:18:59','QUICK SPARK: Want Nvidia on Crypto Rails? ‘Tokenized Stock Is the Honest Way’','Tokenized Nvidia offers 24/7 crypto-based access to NVDA, while AI tokens represent a separate bet, CoinMarketCap’s Alicia Liu says.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61879416/tokenized-nvidia-crypto','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-18 20:22:46.316949','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The article discusses options for accessing Nvidia shares through tokenization, which is a concept rather than an event.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-19 19:24:59.841319','2026-09-18 20:22:32.391840','61879416',replace('Nvidia Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) exposure is no longer limited to Wall Street’s opening bell. For investors who want the chipmaker’s stock on crypto rails, CoinMarketCap’s Alice Liu says there is an important distinction between owning a tokenized Nvidia product and buying an AI token.\n\nNvidia, But 24/7\n\n"For a global retail investor who wants Nvidia at midnight with fractional size and leverage, it already is," Liu, Head of Research at CoinMarketCap, told Benzinga in an exclusive email interview. "The tokenized stock is the honest way to do it; the AI token is a different bet wearing the same jersey."\n\nThe difference matters. A tokenized Nvidia product is designed to track Nvidia itself. CoinMarketCap’s NVDAX was roughly flat over the month covered by the interview, broadly matching the underlying stock.\n\nAn AI Token is a Separate Crypto Asset\n\nWhile Nvidia-related events can drive attention toward AI tokens, their returns can diverge sharply from NVDA. TAO gained 24% over 30 days, while Render fell 63% over the year, as of Sept. 10.\n\nTokenized equities are also gaining traction. CoinMarketCap tracked 1,851 instruments with about $2.3 billion in market capitalization and roughly $2 billion in daily volume.\n\nFor investors, the message is straightforward: tokenized Nvidia is an access layer for NVDA; an AI token is a different investment.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nShutterstock','\n',char(10)),'c44a1ea951b9b8b0b93bef420afc2f3051a9b3bf','2026-09-18 19:18:59','2026-09-18 20:22:32.359667',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 19:18:59');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(431,'alpaca:61881760','benzinga','2026-09-18 20:29:48','Bitcoin Reclaims $80,000 as Ethereum, XRP, Dogecoin Jump Over 6% in Risk-On Rally','Bitcoin tops $80,000 as spot ETFs sees $159.5 million inflows, fueling a risk-on rally despite. Traders watch $82,000 breakout.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61881760/bitcoin-reclaims-80000-as-ethereum-xrp-dogecoin-jump-over-6-in-risk-on-rally','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "ETH/USD", "SHIB/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-18 21:22:53.786608','other','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Bitcoin''s price increase is driven by significant inflows into spot ETFs.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "SHIB/USD": 5.21e-06, "SOL/USD": 101.29, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.982}, "DOGE/USD": {"60m": 7.519, "1d": 7.631}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 7.139}, "SHIB/USD": {"60m": 4.798, "1d": 5.566}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": 11.827, "1d": 9.191}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 8.478, "1d": 9.076}}','2026-09-19 21:25:08.102623','2026-09-18 21:22:50.269347','61881760',replace('Bitcoin reclaimed $80,000 for the first time since early September as spot BTC ETF flows turned positive, adding momentum to a broader risk-on rally.CryptocurrencyTickerPriceBitcoin(CRYPTO: BTC)$80,943.63Ethereum(CRYPTO: ETH)$2,617.20Solana(CRYPTO: SOL)$112.48XRP(CRYPTO: XRP)$1.39Dogecoin(CRYPTO: DOGE)$0.08751Shiba Inu(CRYPTO: SHIB)$0.055469Notable Statistics:\nCoinglass data shows 111,660 traders were liquidated in the past 24 hours for $547.80 million.       \n\nSoSoValue data shows net inflows of $159.5 million from spot Bitcoin ETFs on Thursday. Spot Ethereum ETFs saw net outflows of $39.2 million.\n\nIn the past 24 hours, top gainers include Akedo, NEAR Protocol and Arbitrum.\nNotable Developments:\nXRP Skyrockets 6% as Whale Binance Inflows Hit 6-Month High\n\nStrategy CEO Says ‘We’re Never Going To Stop’ Buying Bitcoin as MSTR Surges 11%\n\nGrayscale Says Rate Hike Is ‘Unlikely to Drive Major Shifts’ In Bitcoin\n\nBitcoin Breaks Above $80,000 as CoinShares Warns Of a ‘Difficult Setup’ Into Year-End\n\nCLARITY Act Failure ‘Begins and Ends With Trump,’ Industry Leader Fumes\n\nBitcoin’s Much Less Volatile Than It Used to Be. BlackRock Says It Played a Part in That.\n\nBitcoin Cracks $78,000 and Ethereum, XRP, Dogecoin May Be ‘About To Explode’\nTrader Notes:Altcoin Sherpa predicts Bitcoin needs a strong break above $82,000 to open the door toward the $100,000 region.Minor pullbacks could occur, but a breakout from its nearly month-long range is key.KillaXBT plans to hedge 50% of his Bitcoin long exposure around $82,000-$84,000, with invalidation at $86,700. He remains heavily long but sees continued range-bound trading as the most likely near-term scenario.Wick sees Bitcoin is attempting a Phase 2 continuation breakout but needs to reclaim stronger market structure to confirm further upside.He emphasized managing risk amid heightened crypto volatility while turning daily setups into longer-term positions.Image: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nCLARITY Act Failure ''Begins and Ends With Trump,'' Industry Leader Fumes','\n',char(10)),'beef9485555e3fe9da750c823f403e8a2cb6c6e4','2026-09-18 20:29:48','2026-09-18 21:22:50.226796',1,NULL,'2026-09-18 20:29:48');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(432,'alpaca:61884010','benzinga','2026-09-19 07:21:05','Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang Rejects Calls to Slow Down AI Development: ‘We Are Going to Go as Fast We Can, But…''','Huang backed rapid AI development, saying the industry should move “as fast as we can” while ensuring products are safe before release.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61884010/nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-rejects-calls-to-slow-down-ai-development-we-are-going-to-go-as-fast-we-can-but','["META", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-19 07:23:27.865469','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Huang''s remarks reflect ongoing industry discussions about AI development.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-20 07:25:39.280729','2026-09-19 07:23:22.213778','61884010',replace('On Friday, Nvidia Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang pushed back against growing calls to slow artificial intelligence development, arguing that companies should move quickly while ensuring their products are safe before release.\n\nJensen Huang Defends Rapid AI Development\n\nIn a teaser video shared by CBS News, Huang told correspondent Jo Ling Kent that the AI industry should continue advancing at full speed. "We should go as fast as we can, irrespective of anybody else."\n\nHuang noted that “we are going to go as fast we can, but” that does not mean releasing unsafe technology. He said companies should avoid shipping products before they are ready or "unsafe."\n\nThe Nvidia CEO also framed rapid AI progress as important to U.S. economic growth, saying companies are expected to help make the country "as prosperous as possible."\n\nThe full interview will be released on Sunday.\n\nEXCLUSIVE: Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang tells CBS News'' @jolingkent that he does not believe the U.S. should slow down in the AI race against China, but added, "we would never, ever and never should ship products before they''re ready." Watch the interview this weekend on @CBSSunday. pic.twitter.com/t5pJnvygIq— CBS News (@CBSNews) September 18, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang Expects Chip Sales To Double Next Year as He Downplays AI Slowdown Calls: ''When a Product is Not Safe…''\n\nAnthropic CEO Calls for AI Slowdown\n\nHuang’s comments come as concerns over AI’s rapid development intensify.\n\nAnthropic CEO Dario Amodei has argued that the technology is advancing at an "exponential" rate and warned that safety measures need to keep pace. He said the industry should slow down rather than stop developing AI altogether.\n\nAmodei has also called for independent third-party evaluators to assess AI companies’ safety practices and urged companies to work together on common safety standards.\n\nEarlier, former Anthropic researcher Jacob Coxon raised concerns that AI companies are prioritizing rapid innovation over adequate security measures, saying stronger safeguards are needed as the technology becomes more capable.\n\nEarlier this week, Meta Platforms, Inc. (NASDAQ:META) CEO Mark Zuckerberg said the company delayed its Muse AI agent for several months to address safety and security concerns. "Every lab has the responsibility and incentive to move at the pace required to train its models safely, and the ability to take its own actions to ensure that happens," Zuckerberg wrote on X.\n\nPrice Action: Nvidia shares closed at $222.27 on Friday, up 1.34%. It edged 0.12% higher to $222.53 in after-hours trading, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nAccording to Benzinga Edge Rankings, Nvidia ranks in the 98th percentile for Growth and shows positive short-, medium- and long-term price trends.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia Is Fighting the AI Slowdown Narrative—With Power as Its Next Problem\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'23e1fd51ff1d13d29749a0a67d03a7c37dcc30a5','2026-09-19 07:21:05','2026-09-19 07:23:22.209479',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 07:21:05');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(433,'alpaca:61884130','benzinga','2026-09-19 09:12:26','Nvidia-backed Nscale Wants to Ride the AI Infrastructure Boom to Wall Street: Files for NYSE IPO','London cloud company Nscale, backed by Microsoft and Nvidia, has filed to sell shares publicly on the New York Stock Exchange.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61884130/nscale-ipo-nyse-nscl-nvidia-microsoft','["AMZN", "MSFT", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-19 09:23:39.955515','listing','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'The filing for an IPO indicates strong growth potential in the AI infrastructure sector.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "MSFT": 498.48, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-20 09:25:51.288750','2026-09-19 09:23:35.073871','61884130',replace('Nvidia (NASDAQ:NVDA)-backed British AI infrastructure provider Nscale filed for an initial public offering (IPO) on the New York Stock Exchange this week, seeking to list under the ticker “NSCL” as it rides explosive demand for computing power.\n\nRevenue Surges, but Losses Mount\n\nLondon-based Nscale reported $140.6 million in revenue for the six months ended Jun. 30, according to its IPO prospectus. That was a 1,252% increase from the $10.4 million it reported during the same period a year earlier.\n\nHowever, the neocloud provider’s net losses also increased, reaching $1.02 billion compared with $368.9 million a year earlier. Nscale also reported $56.4 billion in remaining performance obligations. More than half of its revenue during the first half of the year came from one unnamed customer.\n\nBig-Name Backers and AI Deals\n\nNscale rents Nvidia GPUs to AI companies such as OpenAI and Anthropic, both of which are preparing for their own potential public offerings. It also has a partnership with Microsoft (NASDAQ:MSFT).\n\nThe company competes with Amazon (NASDAQ:AMZN) as well as other neocloud providers CoreWeave (NASDAQ:CRWV) and Nebius (NASDAQ:NBIS).\n\nRecently, Humanoid robotics startup Figure AI has also committed $3.5 billion of compute to Nscale, underscoring demand beyond traditional AI labs.\n\nAs of Aug. 31, Nscale had 25,000 active GPUs, with another 461,000 either active or under contract. These GPUs were spread across five active data centers and 12 contracted facilities.\n\n The company’s investors include Blue Owl, Dell (NYSE:DELL), Nvidia and Fidelity. In March, Nscale raised $2 billion, valuing it at $14.6 billion. The company has more than $8 billion in debt, CNBC reported.\n\nFounder and CEO Josh Payne, in a letter to prospective investors included with the filing, wrote: “From inception, we built Nscale with an infrastructure-first thesis, building against contracted customer demand, underwriting projects to attractive long-term returns, maintaining prudent leverage and seeking to match the duration of our capital commitments with the strong revenues supporting them.”\n\nRead Also:\n\nSam Altman Heads to UN Security Council, Prepares to Brief World Powers on AI Safety Amid Global Regulation Push: Report\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'5d57859708e0bbaec2f1fefec81fe90921a29696','2026-09-19 09:12:26','2026-09-19 09:23:35.068535',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 09:12:26');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(434,'alpaca:61884068','benzinga','2026-09-19 08:31:34','Gavin Newsom Orders California to Advance Creation of AI ‘Kill Switch’ — Says Trump and Congress Are ‘Failing to Lead’ on AI Oversight','Newsom ordered tighter AI oversight and a review of “kill switches” for advanced models, criticizing Washington’s lack of federal safeguards.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/politics/26/09/61884068/gavin-newsom-orders-california-to-advance-creation-of-ai-kill-switch-says-trump-and-congress-are-failing-to-lead-on-ai-oversight','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-19 09:23:41.303651','regulatory','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'State-level regulatory action on AI with implications for tech companies like NVIDIA.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-20 09:25:51.288750','2026-09-19 09:23:35.076713','61884068',replace('California Gov. Gavin Newsom (D) has ordered the state to accelerate independent oversight of AI companies and explore an emergency "kill switch" for advanced AI models.\n\nNewsom Orders AI Oversight, Explore ‘Kill Switch’\n\nOn Friday, Newsom signed the executive order directing California officials to speed up implementation of two AI laws enacted last week that establish independent verification organizations and a registry for AI auditors.\n\nThe order also calls for a group of experts to develop recommendations within two months.\n\nThe recommendations will examine whether frontier AI companies should have independent evaluators working onsite and whether their most advanced models should have an emergency shutdown mechanism.\n\nNewsom said the state needs to act because Washington has not established what he considers sufficient federal AI oversight.\n\n"The federal government’s abject failure to create any form of meaningful AI oversight or accountability should alarm every American," Newsom said.\n\nHe called California’s framework a potential national baseline and urged President Donald Trump and Congress to adopt it.\n\nOn X, he said, "With Donald Trump and Congress failing to lead, California is stepping up to keep all Americans safe."\n\nBREAKING: I just signed an EXECUTIVE ORDER to dramatically accelerate independent oversight of AI companies and advance the creation of an "AI kill switch."With Donald Trump and Congress failing to lead, California is stepping up to keep all Americans safe. pic.twitter.com/7ydkG0fdQM— Gavin Newsom (@GavinNewsom) September 18, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Escalates Economic Pressure on Russia With New Sanctions Law That Could Hit Moscow’s Biggest Trading Partners With Tariffs\n\nAI Regulation Debate Intensifies\n\nThe move comes as lawmakers and AI executives debate whether development of advanced models should slow down to allow safety measures to catch up.\n\nSen. Elizabeth Warren (D-Mass.) called this week for a pause in advanced AI development, arguing that decisions about the technology should be made by elected representatives rather than companies.\n\nSens. Bernie Sanders (I-Vt.) and Rep. Greg Casar (D-Texas) have also proposed legislation that would permanently ban the development and deployment of artificial superintelligence and temporarily pause advanced AI development until federal safety rules are established.\n\nAnthropic CEO Dario Amodei has also urged the industry to "pace the frontier," while proposing greater third-party oversight of AI systems. OpenAI CEO Sam Altman and Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) have backed calls for a slower development pace.\n\nTrump, meanwhile, has rejected calls to slow AI development, saying the U.S. needs to maintain its lead over China.\n\n"I’m telling you it’s all a hoax. The data centers are great. They make people wealthy. They make states wealthy. AI is bigger than the internet. These people are playing right into the hands of China. We’re not going to let that happen," he told Nvidia Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang during a call.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Escalates Fight With Media, Bans CNN, MS NOW and Politico From White House, Warns More Could Face Same Fate\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'bf24a1b13ae06436d9b4b7d96b06157b7e93f1bd','2026-09-19 08:31:34','2026-09-19 09:23:35.068535',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 08:31:34');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(435,'alpaca:61884239','benzinga','2026-09-19 12:00:44','Benzinga Bulls and Bears: Generac, Salesforce, Netflix','Benzinga examined the prospects for many investors’ favorite stocks over the last week — here’s a look at some of our top stories.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/market-summary/26/09/61884239/benzinga-bulls-and-bears-generac-salesforce-netflix','["AMZN", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-19 12:23:56.406599','other','neutral',1,3,'days',1,'Summary of stock outlooks for various companies without specific actionable content.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-20 12:26:08.187173','2026-09-19 12:23:52.313611','61884239',replace('Benzinga examined the prospects for many investors’ favorite stocks over the last week — here’s a look at some of our top stories.\n\nU.S. stocks finished a volatile week with mixed results as investors adjusted to the Federal Reserve’s first interest-rate hike since 2023 and rising energy costs. The S&P; 500 slipped for a second straight week, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average recorded its sharpest weekly decline since March. The Nasdaq Composite managed a weekly gain, helped by a late-week technology rally, but markets remained under pressure as the 10-year Treasury yield approached 5% and oil prices remained elevated amid tensions in the Middle East.\n\nThe Fed raised its benchmark rate by 25 basis points on Wednesday to a range of 3.75%-4%, with the decision passing unanimously. The move followed a week of rising Treasury yields and crude prices, which had already pressured stocks and increased concerns about inflation. Brent crude climbed above $100 a barrel and briefly approached $110, while higher fuel costs pushed gasoline and diesel prices to records.\n\nAttention now turns to how far the Fed may raise rates as inflation remains elevated. Sixteen of the 18 Fed policymakers who submitted forecasts projected at least one additional rate increase this year. With the 10-year Treasury yield near 5% and oil prices still above $100, investors are weighing the impact of tighter monetary policy and higher energy costs on economic growth, corporate earnings and technology valuations.\n\nBenzinga provides daily reports on the stocks most popular with investors. Here are a few of this past week’s most bullish and bearish posts that are worth another look.\n\nThe Bulls\n\nGenerac Stock Soars on $8 Billion Amazon Data Center Deal, by Adam Eckert, reports that Generac Holdings Inc. (NYSE:GNRC) shares surged after the company announced a long-term supply agreement with Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) to provide backup generators for Amazon’s data centers. The agreement covers up to $8 billion in generator purchases, with initial deliveries expected to total $2.4 billion in 2027 and 2028, giving Generac visibility into demand tied to Amazon’s expanding data-center infrastructure. As part of the transaction, Generac issued an Amazon subsidiary a warrant to purchase up to approximately 1.69 million Generac shares at $200.93 per share.\n\nSalesforce’s Anthropic Bet Likely Worth ‘Tens of Billions’ — And Benioff Plans to Cash In, by Erica Kollmann, reports that Salesforce Inc. (NYSE:CRM) CEO Marc Benioff said the company could eventually sell its stake in Anthropic, potentially turning an investment worth hundreds of millions of dollars into proceeds worth "tens of billions." Salesforce Ventures first invested in the AI company in 2023, and Anthropic’s valuation has since climbed sharply, reaching $965 billion after a $65 billion Series H financing in May. The investment generated a $2.6 billion gain for Salesforce in its latest quarter and contributed significantly to its reported profit. Benioff said Salesforce would likely use proceeds from a future sale to repay debt taken on to fund its $25 billion accelerated share repurchase, which retired about 103 million shares.\n\nSpaceX Adds $100B in One Day — That’s More Than Two Rocket Labs, by Erica Kollmann, reports that SpaceX (NASDAQ:SPCX) gained about $100 billion in market value Wednesday, lifting its market capitalization to roughly $2 trillion after shares closed at $150.88, up 5.15%. The move was driven in part by expectations surrounding Starship Flight 14, targeted for Sept. 22 and expected to be the vehicle’s first fully orbital attempt and its first mission designed to deploy third-generation Starlink satellites. A successful launch would provide a test of the economics behind SpaceX’s valuation, while the company is also benefiting from continued index-related buying after joining the Nasdaq-100 in July; J.P. Morgan estimated the inclusion could generate about $4.3 billion in passive fund flows.\n\nFor additional bullish calls of the past week, check out the following:\n\nModerna Stock More Than Doubled in a Month. Now Comes the Hard Part.\n\nRobinhood’s 24/7 Stock Dream Just Got A Boost From The SEC\n\nTesla Gets Love From Ron Baron for Not Hitting Ducks: ‘Time to Buy The Stock is Now’\n\nThe Bears\n\nNetflix Viewer Trends ‘Look Worrying’: Wells Fargo Slashes Target on Stock, by Erica Kollmann, reports that Netflix Inc. (NASDAQ:NFLX) shares fell after Wells Fargo downgraded the streaming company to Underweight from Equal Weight and cut its price target to $57 from $80, citing weakening viewer engagement and concerns about Netflix’s content slate. Analyst Steven Cahall said engagement trends were "worrying," arguing that Netflix needs more breakout original hits as it expands into gaming, live sports, reality programming, documentaries and video podcasts. Netflix reported that viewing hours rose just 2% in the first half of 2026, while the company plans to increase content spending by 10% for the full year. Cahall expects viewership for Netflix’s top 100 originals to decline 21% year over year in the second half, with potential churn pressure building into 2027.\n\nSysco Stock Slides on $1 Billion Offering, by Adam Eckert, reports that Sysco Corp. (NYSE:SYY) shares fell after the foodservice distributor announced a $1 billion common stock offering to help finance its pending acquisition of Jetro Restaurant Depot. Sysco plans to sell 12.35 million shares at $81 each and has granted underwriters a 30-day option to purchase up to another $150 million of stock. The offering price represented a discount to Sysco’s $83.54 closing price on Sept. 14 and will increase the company’s outstanding share count. Sysco agreed in March to acquire Jetro Restaurant Depot in a transaction valued at about $29.1 billion, with Jetro shareholders receiving $21.6 billion in cash and 91.5 million Sysco shares.\n\nRed Cat, Ondas Miss the Cut in Pentagon’s Latest Drone Dominance Round, by Erica Kollmann, reports that Red Cat Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:RCAT) and Ondas Inc. (NASDAQ:ONDS) were left out of the top five in their respective mission areas in the Pentagon’s latest Gauntlet II drone competition. Ten finalists were selected after August testing at Fort Carson, Colorado, with five each in Deep Strike and Close Quarters Battle. Perennial Autonomy led Deep Strike with 80.1 points, while Neros topped Close Quarters Battle with 88.1 points; all 10 finalists are privately held. Both companies remain eligible for future Gauntlet competitions. The results also drew attention to Unusual Machines Inc. (AMEX:UMAC), which supplies drone components, while larger defense companies including Kratos Defense & Security Solutions Inc. (NASDAQ:KTOS) and AeroVironment Inc. (NASDAQ:AVAV) remain exposed to the broader expansion in military drone spending.\n\nFor more bearish takes, be sure to see these posts:\n\nBig Bank Stocks Tumble After Moynihan’s Grim Outlook\n\nLennar Posts Q3 Double Miss, Shares Slip\n\nSalesforce’s AI Business Is Booming, Why Isn’t CRM Stock?\n\nKeep up with all the latest breaking news and trading ideas by following Benzinga on X.\n\nImage created using artificial intelligence via Midjourney.','\n',char(10)),'d82614e19e0210def04b8b6434ef610075cd3c35','2026-09-19 12:00:44','2026-09-19 12:23:52.310004',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 12:00:44');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(436,'alpaca:61884324','benzinga','2026-09-19 13:00:39','This Week in TSLA: Elon Musk Touts Roadster Debut, Fuels SpaceX Merger  Talks and More','From the Terafab lawsuit, to a lower Q3 delivery forecast by a major investment bank, here are some of Tesla&#39;s top stories for the week.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61884324/this-week-in-tsla-elon-musk-touts-roadster-debut-fuels-spacex-merger-talks-and-more','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-19 13:24:02.858728','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline summarizes various news about Tesla without indicating a clear positive or negative impact.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-20 13:26:11.301228','2026-09-19 13:24:00.086910','61884324',replace('From legal battles over trademark infringement and a potential merger between Tesla and SpaceX, as we wrap up another eventful week, let’s take a look at some of the key stories about Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) and CEO Elon Musk that made the headlines.\n\nTesla Roadster Reveal in October\n\nMusk has promised that the upcoming unveiling of the Tesla Roadster high-performance vehicle next month on October 1 will far exceed expectations. The CEO guaranteed excitement at the event. So much so that he has said people may think the reveal is AI-generated. Read the full article here.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla’s Cybercab ‘Held Me Hostage for an Hour,’ Rider Says — This Cybercab Limitation Just Turned a Short Austin Trip Into 70-Minute Detour\n\nTesla and SpaceX’s Legal Battle Over ‘Terafab’\n\nTesla and SpaceX, both led by Musk, have sued Illinois nanotechnology company TERA-print LLC over the “Terafab” name planned for their $16.8 billion AI chip complex in Texas. The lawsuit was filed in response to a cease-and-desist letter from TERA-print. Read the full article here.\n\nGoldman Cuts Tesla’s Q3 Delivery Forecast\n\nGoldman Sachs Group Inc. (NYSE:GS) has revised its Q3 delivery forecast for Tesla, bringing it down to 435,000 vehicles from the previous estimate of 490,000. Despite this, prediction traders are still optimistic, with estimates centered around 480,000. Read the full article here.\n\nPotential SpaceX-Tesla Merger\n\nMusk also fueled talks of a potential merger between Tesla and Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) during an appearance on the All In Podcast. Musk was asked why Tesla and SpaceX were still separate companies, to which he hinted that there may be a merger on the way. Read the full article here.\n\nTesla’s Cybercab Certification Questions\n\nThe U.S. National Highway Traffic Safety Administration has ordered Tesla to answer 21 detailed questions about its Cybercab robotaxi’s compliance with federal safety standards under oath. The responses are due by September 30. Read the full article here.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSpaceX-Tesla Merger: Ron Baron Told Elon Musk ''Whatever You Decide… Is What I''m Going to Support''\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by a Benzinga editor.\n\nCheck out more of Benzinga’s Future Of Mobility coverage by following this link.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'67fa46d8393b802622715b585ab61e557de9b324','2026-09-19 13:00:39','2026-09-19 13:24:00.079078',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 13:00:39');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(437,'alpaca:61884295','benzinga','2026-09-19 12:30:24','Intel, Apple, Nvidia and More: 5 Stocks Investors Couldn''t Stop Buzzing About This Week','Retail investors talked up 5 stocks during the week (Sept. 14 to Sept.18) on X and Reddit&#39;s r/WallStreetBets: INTC, AAPL, NVDA, NBIS, ORCL','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61884295/intel-apple-nvidia-and-more-5-stocks-investors-couldnt-stop-buzzing-about-this-week','["AAPL", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-19 13:24:04.728468','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Retail investor interest does not directly impact stock prices.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-20 13:26:11.301228','2026-09-19 13:24:00.089256','61884295',replace('Retail investors talked up five hot stocks during the week (Sept. 14 to Sept.18) on X and Reddit’s r/WallStreetBets, driven by retail hype, earnings, AI infrastructure momentum, and corporate news flow.\n\nIntel Corp. (NYSE:INTC), Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL), Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA), Nebius Group NV (NASDAQ:NBIS), and Oracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL), spanning the semiconductor, consumer electronics, AI hardware, cloud infrastructure, and enterprise software sectors, reflected strong retail interest.\n\nIntel\n\nIntel shares fell roughly on Monday this week amid a broader semiconductor selloff triggered by AI industry leaders calling for slower frontier-model development over safety concerns and efficiency gains from models like DeepSeek that could reduce hardware demand. The stock rebounded mid-week after Altera, in which Intel holds a 49% stake, confidentially filed for a U.S. IPO. Additionally, Reuters reported on Sept. 16 that SK Hynix Inc. (NASDAQ:SKHY) was in exploratory talks to potentially manufacture memory chips at Intel’s facilities.\n\nMany retail investors were bullish on INTC, expecting a steady upside.\n\nSource: Reddit\n\nThe stock has traded in a 52-week range of $28.73 to $142.35, trading around $107 to $112 per share, as of the publication of this article. It advanced by 336.95% over the last year and 146.94% over the last six months. The stock was up 194.85% year-to-date.\n\nAccording to Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings, INTC was maintaining a strong price trend over the short, medium and long terms.\n\nApple\n\nApple’s major stories this week centered on the ongoing rollout and reception of products unveiled under new CEO John Ternus on Sept. 9: the iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max, along with iPhone Duo, new Apple Watch models, and AirPods 5, with pre-orders underway and availability beginning Sept. 18. On Sept. 14, iOS 27 and the Siri AI beta with enhanced conversational capabilities powered in part by partnerships with Google and OpenAI became available. Analysts tracked mixed-to-improving early demand signals for the Pro models—including shorter ship times and strong carrier trade-in promotions up to $1,200. \n\nFollowing its new launches, some retail traders were highly bullish on the AAPL stock.\n\nSource: Reddit\n\nThe stock had a 52-week range of $240.21 to $344.57, trading around $336 to $338 per share, as of the publication of this article. It advanced by 41.01% over the year and rose 32.56% in the last six months. The stock was up 23.96% YTD.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings showed that AAPL had a strong price trend in the short, long, and medium terms, with a moderate growth score.\n\nNvidia\n\nNVIDIA shares fell on Monday this week amid a broader semiconductor selloff triggered by AI leaders, including Anthropic’s Dario Amodei calling for a slowdown in frontier model development over safety risks, alongside reports that NVIDIA and others were limiting use of certain third-party models due to data-privacy concerns. The company also expanded its CUDA-Q quantum platform that day and faced speculation of a potential up-to-$10 billion anchor investment in Anthropic’s IPO. Later in the week, CEO Jensen Huang appeared at Salesforce’s Dreamforce, NVIDIA joined an AI energy-management alliance with Google and Emerald AI, and preliminary MLPerf results highlighted strong performance for its next-gen Vera Rubin platform. \n\nRetail investors were anxious about NVDA’s moment on Reddit.\n\nSource: Reddit\n\nThe stock had a 52-week range of $164.27 to $236.54, trading around $218 to $220 per share, as of the publication of this article. It rose by 28.80% over the year and 20.56% in the last six months. The stock was down 15.61% YTD.\n\nNVDA maintains a strong price trend over the long, medium, and short terms, with a good quality score, as per Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings. \n\nOracle\n\nOracle co-founder Larry Ellison canceled a planned 10b5-1 sale of up to 50 million shares of roughly $7.5 billion that had been disclosed shortly before, with no shares sold and no new sale plans announced. The company also disclosed higher restructuring costs, an extra ~$700 million, pushing the fiscal 2026 total near $2.8 billion, and initiated a fresh round of layoffs as part of ongoing cost-cutting while investing heavily in AI infrastructure. \n\nSome ORCL investors were hoping for continued stock momentum.\n\nSource: Reddit\n\nThe stock had a 52-week range of $114.50 to $329.50, trading around $149 to $151 per share, as of the publication of this article. It dropped by 50.04% over the year, fell 2.65% over the last six months, and is lower by 22.74% YTD.\n\nAccording to Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings, ORCL was maintaining a strong price trend over the short term and a strong trend in the long and medium terms, with a good growth score. \n\nNebius Group\n\nNBIS announced it would raise on-demand AI compute prices effective Oct. 1, increasing rates for Nvidia GPUs by roughly 17–21% along with AMD EPYC CPU rates by about 25% and memory pricing by 41%, citing persistently strong demand. Market strategists like Shay Boloor identified $150 per share as a target entry level for NBIS, about 31.19% lower than the current level, citing its conversion of power capacity into cloud revenue. "If it goes below 150 that is my pounding the table level," Boloor stated. He expects the stock to trade at a commodity multiple until achieving EBIT profitability or operating profit by early 2028.\n\nRetail investors were highly bullish on NBIS stock.\n\nSource: Reddit\n\nThe stock has traded in the 52-week range of $73.52 to $299.86, trading around $216 to $218 per share, as of the publication of this article. It rose by 131.71% over the year, rose 87.39% over the last six months, and is up 160.43% YTD.\n\nAccording to Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings, NBIS was maintaining a strong price trend over the long, short, and medium terms, with a poor value score. \n\nRetail focus comprised AI infrastructure momentum, earnings, and corporate news-driven narratives, with broader market action during the week.\n\nRead Also:\n\nGameStop, Oracle, Apple and More: Five Stocks Investors Couldn''t Stop Buzzing About This Week\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'dcc6f81f0fa84add557c3b4ac2d668dad47d42e6','2026-09-19 12:30:24','2026-09-19 13:24:00.079078',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 12:30:24');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(438,'alpaca:61884376','benzinga','2026-09-19 13:31:30','Bitcoin, Zcash, Hyperliquid in Focus as Industry Expert Sees Crypto Nearing a ''Major Turning Point''','Crypto may be nearing a cyclical bottom as volumes slump; analysts favor Bitcoin, Ethereum and Dogecoin, while privacy coin Zcash gains attention.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61884376/bitcoin-zcash-hyperliquid-in-focus-as-industry-expert-sees-crypto-nearing-a-major-turning-point','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-19 14:24:12.126221','analyst','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'Analysts suggest a cyclical bottom without concrete evidence.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 6.155}, "DOGE/USD": {"60m": 9.169, "1d": 4.146}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 7.64}}','2026-09-20 14:26:18.925913','2026-09-19 14:24:08.907922','61884376',replace('Zcash (CRYPTO: ZEC) gained 22% over the last week after Grayscale offered a Zcash investment product for roughly nine years, citing privacy as a key part of its investment thesis. The asset manager also gave the green light to add Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) to investor portfolios\n\nGlassnode data reinforced that thesis, showing how privacy coins such as Zcash have emerged as one of crypto’s standout trades.\n\nHyperliquid (NASDAQ:PURR) added 11% in weekly gains as SEC approved the Innovation Exemption, a temporary order allowing tokenized stock trading on-chain for the first time.\n\nThe order requires trading on public, permissionless blockchains using auditable smart contracts, closely aligning with HYPE’s on-chain DEX model.\n\nCrypto analyst Kevin Capital said investors seeking "life-changing gains" should include Bitcoin as their largest crypto position pushing the crypto king around 4% higher over the week.\n\nEchoing a similar sentiment, hedge fund manager Richard Galvin sees Bitcoin and the broader cryptocurrency market may be approaching a major cyclical turning point.\n\nHe argued that depressed trading activity, tokenization and artificial intelligence could combine to drive the next expansion.\n\nWhy Crypto Is Nearing A Bottom\n\nSpeaking with Real Vision CEO Raoul Pal on Sep.17, Galvin noted crypto appears to be "at or pretty close" to a cyclical bottom in trading volumes, even if prices face another leg lower before a sustained recovery.\n\nGalvin sees decentralized trading volume as a key cycle gauge. After surging to $500 billion in January 2025, volumes have fallen to around $130 billion-$140 billion, resembling previous crypto bottoms.\n\nWhile another decline remains possible in October, November or even January, he said trying to perfectly time the bottom risks missing the larger move.\n\nHis view aligns with recent institutional calls around Bitcoin.\n\nGalvin Vouches For Zcash, HYPE\n\nGalvin also highlighted Zcash, arguing that financial privacy remains one of crypto’s most durable use cases.\n\nHis firm initially backed privacy assets including Monero years ago, based on the thesis that a growing BTC economy would eventually require a privacy-focused counterpart.\n\nHe believes Zcash is increasingly filling that role.\n\nGalvin added that decentralized exchanges, lending protocols and perpetual futures platforms have already survived several brutal crypto cycles, demonstrating that blockchain infrastructure can operate cheaply and at scale.\n\nNow, TradFi is beginning to move assets onto those rails.\n\n“Basically, every exchange in the world either has a plan or is already moving or migrating some of its business on chain,” Galvin highlighted.\n\nThat thesis supports Hyperliquid and its role in the broader crypto market.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Cracks $78,000 and Ethereum, XRP, Dogecoin May Be ''About To Explode''','\n',char(10)),'c849007a715c558c939b8510ad262055939827c0','2026-09-19 13:31:30','2026-09-19 14:24:08.904422',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 13:31:30');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(439,'alpaca:61884472','benzinga','2026-09-19 15:00:17','Bill Ackman Said ‘Hell Is Coming’ in 2020 — How a $27 Million Hedge Turned Into $2.6 Billion as He Bought the Crash','Bill Ackman turned a $27M COVID-era credit hedge into $2.6B, then bought discounted stocks during the 2020 market crash.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61884472/bill-ackman-said-hell-is-coming-in-2020-how-a-27-million-hedge-turned-into-2-6-billion-as-he-bought-the-crash','["QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-19 15:24:19.548702','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses past investment strategies without indicating immediate future effects.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-20 15:26:22.492844','2026-09-19 15:24:15.650540','61884472',replace('Pershing Square CEO Bill Ackman warned that "hell is coming" in March 2020 before executing a $27 million credit hedge that generated $2.6 billion in proceeds, which he subsequently redeployed into equities during the COVID-19 market crash.\n\nThe Misunderstood Warning\n\nDuring a 28-minute CNBC segment in 2020, Ackman recounted a private conversation he held with Hilton Hotels Corp. (NYSE:HLT) leadership. Ackman advised the company to draw down credit lines, deposit cash, and defer capital expenditures because a global economic shutdown was imminent. “Hell is coming,” Ackman stated. \n\nThe "hell is coming" portion of the interview drew significant attention as U.S. stocks were plunging.\n\nThe broader market was down 6% when Ackman began his interview and dropped to 10% by the time he finished. Despite the public reaction, Ackman maintained his appearance was intended to signal market opportunity.\n\nHe stated in the CAZ Investments podcast with Tony Robbins, on Sept. 8, 2026, that he went on television to announce Pershing Square was actively “buying stocks.” He advised the U.S. president to mandate a 30-day national “spring break” to let the virus pass, arguing that such a policy would stabilize the country and present an unprecedented buying window.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBill Ackman Says Nike''s New Board Pick Alexandre Arnault Is a ''Great Development'' for the Struggling Sportswear Retailer\n\nExecuting the $2.6 Billion Hedge\n\nAckman said in the podcast that he began tracking the health and economic risks of COVID-19 in January 2020. Concluding by February that the global economy would need to close, he built a large defensive position in the credit default swap (CDS) market.\n\nWhen global markets plunged just two weeks later, this $27 million investment turned into $2.6 billion.\n\nA Contrarian Shopping Spree\n\nRather than holding the cash, Ackman redirected the $2.6 billion windfall into the equity market in March 2020. Pershing Square purchased shares across its existing portfolio, securing positions in Hilton at $55 a share and home improvement retailer Lowe’s Companies Inc. (NYSE:LOW) at $70 a share, said Ackman.\n\nAckman credited Pershing Square’s permanent-capital structure with giving him flexibility to invest during the market turmoil.\n\nBecause he did not face short-term redemption pressures from investors, he could ignore the immediate volatility and purchase durable businesses at steep discounts while the rest of the market panicked.\n\nHow Have Markets Performed Since the COVID-19 Crash?\n\nThe COVID-19 crash began on Feb. 20, 2020, when the S&P; 500 index closed at 3,373.23, now 126.42% higher at 7,637.76 points. Similarly, the Nasdaq 100 has risen from 9,627.83 to 29,446.98, a 205.85% change, and the Dow Jones Index gained 77.20% from 29,219.98 to 51,778.04 points.\n\nIn 2026, the S&P; 500 index has advanced 11.36% year-to-date. Similarly, the Nasdaq Composite index was up 13.70%, and the Dow Jones gained 7.02% YTD.\n\nOn Thursday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed higher. SPY rose 1.13% to $762.60, while QQQ rose 1.73% to $716.92. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), also ended 0.61% higher at $518.35.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTop 4 Stocks to Buy Now Regardless of Fed Rate Hikes, According to InfraCap Investment Chief Jay Hatfield\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Things on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'02bf5513b51c6043843a7dc4174ea90ea6cc54f1','2026-09-19 15:00:17','2026-09-19 15:24:15.643559',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 15:00:17');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(440,'alpaca:61884589','benzinga','2026-09-19 16:15:06','Altcoin Season Index Nears 50 as Crypto Fear and Greed Index Jumps','Here&#39;s why the Altcoin Season Index has jumped and is nearing 50 amid the ongoing Crypto Fear and Greed Index rally.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/26/09/61884589/altcoin-season-index-nears-50-as-crypto-fear-and-greed-index-jumps','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD", "SOL/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-19 16:24:28.294576','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The index movements could influence sentiment but don''t guarantee price changes.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "SOL/USD": 101.29}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 6.155}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 7.64}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": 9.488}}','2026-09-20 16:26:25.347535','2026-09-19 16:24:24.391331','61884589',replace('The Altcoin Season Index continued rising, reaching its highest level in months, as many tokens hit their multi-month highs and as the Crypto Fear and Greed Index moved to the greed zone of 78. \n\nAltcoin Season Index is Surging \n\nThe index, which looks at the performance of the top 100 coins relative to Bitcoin in the last 90 days, has continued rising. It jumped to 48 today, much higher than where it was a few weeks ago.\n\nAltcoin Season Index | Source: CoinMarketCap\n\nThis rally coincided with the ongoing rally of most altcoins. NEAR Protocol (CRYPTO: NEAR) token has jumped by 50% in the last seven days. Tezos (CRYPTO: XTZ) jumped by 48%, while Arbitrum (CRYPTO: ARB), Uniswap (CRYPTO: UNI), Ethena (CRYPTO: ENA), and Zcash (CRYPTO: ZEC) have soared by over 40% in this period. \n\nOn the other hand, Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) has remained within a narrow range in the past few weeks. While it jumped to $81,503 today, it remains slightly below this month’s high of $82,135. \n\nMost altcoins, including large names like Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) and Solana (CRYPTO: SOL) have jumped by double digits from their lowest levels this year.\n\nThe ongoing rebound has coincided with the rising Fear and Greed Index, which has remained in the greed zone in the past few weeks. It rose to 74 on Saturday and is nearing the extreme greed area. In most cases, crypto prices do well when there is a sense of greed in the market.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Escalates Economic Pressure on Russia With New Sanctions Law That Could Hit Moscow’s Biggest Trading Partners With Tariffs\n\nCrypto Fear and Greed Index | Source: CMC\n\nBitcoin Rebound Has Boosted Altcoins\n\nOne reason for the rally is that investors are buying the dip as most of them plunged by double digits from their highest levels this year. The dip-buying is also happening after Bitcoin rebounded following the surge in US debt, which crossed the $40 trillion mark in July. \n\nBitcoin is often seen as a safe-haven asset because of its strong tokenomics, which includes a supply cap of 21 million coins. In most cases, altcoins tend to do well when Bitcoin is rising and vice versa.\n\nAt the same time, there are signs that demand for altcoins is rising in the United States. SoSoValue data shows that spot Solana ETFs have had over $28 million in inflows this year. Similarly, spot Ethereum ETFs have added $187 million, while XRP has added $41 million. ETF inflows are signs that investors expect them to keep rising.\n\nRead Also:\n\nDiesel Squeeze Nobody Hedged: 4 Refiners Just Logged Their 6th Straight Week of Gains\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'acf8e1829cdef835b1d78ab1d46f44c8f710c33a','2026-09-19 16:15:06','2026-09-19 16:24:24.387667',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 16:15:06');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(441,'alpaca:61884531','benzinga','2026-09-19 15:30:25','United Airlines CEO Scott Kirby Has a Simple PowerPoint Rule — And This Strict Limit Shows How Seriously He Takes It','United CEO Scott Kirby limits meetings to four hours daily, bans slide-reading and favors prepared decks and concise discussion.','https://www.benzinga.com/personal-finance/entrepreneurship/26/09/61884531/united-airlines-ceo-scott-kirby-has-a-simple-powerpoint-rule-and-this-strict-limit-shows-how-seriously-he-takes-it','["AMZN", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-19 16:24:30.416700','other','neutral',1,3,'days',1,'This describes the CEO''s management style without direct market impact.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-20 16:26:25.347535','2026-09-19 16:24:24.393896','61884531',replace('United Airlines Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:UAL) CEO Scott Kirby caps meetings at four hours a day and has a blunt rule for PowerPoint, which is: send the deck beforehand, then come ready to talk.\n\nKirby Wants Conversation, Not Slide Reading\n\n"My meetings are also quick, and my meetings are almost all conversational," Kirby told Semafor during an interview last week. "I want to talk—really, don’t go through decks. If you want to send a deck, send it to me in advance, and then we’re just going to talk about it. But you’re not going to read slides to me."\n\nKirby says the point is not to pack more tasks into the day. "The further you go in your career—certainly by the time you’re the CEO—your job is not to work hard; it’s to think hard," he said. He spends about three hours a day reading and says CEOs should focus "over the horizon" rather than yesterday’s metrics.\n\nThat approach comes as United expands aggressively. United had installed Starlink on 450 mainline and United Express aircraft by the end of the second quarter and expects nearly 1,000 aircraft to have the service by year-end, with the entire fleet targeted for Starlink by the end of 2027. United’s Starlink rollout has become a major part of its customer strategy.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang Expects Chip Sales To Double Next Year as He Downplays AI Slowdown Calls: ''When a Product is Not Safe…''\n\nBezos And Huang Rewrite Meeting Norms\n\nKirby is hardly alone in rejecting conventional executive routines. Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) founder Jeff Bezos eliminated PowerPoint presentations at Amazon in 2004. The company instead uses narrative memos of up to six pages, which participants read silently before discussion. Amazon CEO Andy Jassy later said in a shareholder letter that the format makes presenters work harder but helps audiences understand substantive issues and ask better questions.\n\nNvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang takes an even less conventional approach. Huang, who has about 60 direct reports, told Stripe that he does not hold one-on-one meetings because he wants information to flow broadly. "Almost everything that I say, I say to everybody all at the same time," he said.\n\nAirline CEOs Push For Shorter Meetings\n\nOther airline leaders share Kirby’s impatience with long meetings. Delta Air Lines Inc. (NYSE:DAL) CEO Ed Bastian told Great Place to Work that his ideal meeting lasts about 10 minutes.\n\nBenzinga Edge Rankings show UAL stock provides a Value score in the 85th percentile and a Growth score in the 93rd percentile.\n\nRead Also:\n\nWarren Buffett, Donald Trump Bet on Same 17 Stocks — Some Might Surprise You\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'f2c565e8dc3bf6a288b8de6bcd57029387d8294e','2026-09-19 15:30:25','2026-09-19 16:24:24.387667',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 15:30:25');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(442,'alpaca:61884616','benzinga','2026-09-19 16:45:09','Solana Price Forms Bullish Flag as ETF and Staking Inflows Jump','Solana has formed a bullish flag pattern, pointing to more gains, as the SOL ETF and staking inflows jump.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/26/09/61884616/solana-price-forms-bullish-flag-as-etf-and-staking-inflows-jump','["SOL/USD"]','degen','2026-09-19 17:24:38.379437','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The headline discusses a price pattern and inflows without confirmed results.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"SOL/USD": 101.29}','{"SOL/USD": {"60m": 9.548, "1d": 8.351}}','2026-09-20 17:26:32.600664','2026-09-19 17:24:34.221824','61884616',replace('Solana (CRYPTO: SOL) broke out above a key resistance level as the broader crypto rally continued and inflows into its ETFs and staking kept climbing. SOL jumped to $111.78, its highest level since January and 85% above its year-to-date low.\n\nSolana ETF and Staking Inflows are Rising\n\nSOL token continued rising this week, helped by its improving fundamentals and rising demand. The developers activated a major upgrade that dropped its slot time from 300 milliseconds to 250, a 17% boost. A slot refers to the short window given to one validator to build and publish a block. By shrinking the time, it helped the network become much faster.\n\nThe upgrade comes as Solana continues to test the Alpenglow upgrade, which will cut the finality time from about 12.8 seconds to 100 milliseconds. It will also replace Tower BFT with Votor and Rotor. Voter swaps on-chain voting for off-chain signature certificates, while Rotor replaces the older Turbine system to slash transaction finality time.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBill Ackman Said ‘Hell Is Coming’ in 2020 — How a $27 Million Hedge Turned Into $2.6 Billion as He Bought the Crash\n\nSolana’s fundamentals are also improving. Its decentralized exchanges handled more than $47 billion in trading volume so far this month, down from $62 billion in August, yet still the most of any blockchain. Solana’s stablecoin supply has also climbed above $15 billion.\n\nThese numbers partly explain why investors are piling into SOL tokens. SoSoValue data shows that spot Solana ETFs have had over $28 million in inflows this month. It is the third consecutive month of inflows, with their total assets under management being $1.62 billion. The biggest of these funds are by companies like Fidelity, Bitwise, Grayscale, and Morgan Stanley. \n\nInvestors are also piling into Solana’s staking pools. Over 439 million SOL tokens worth $49 billion have been staked. This gives it a staking ratio of nearly 70%, with the staking rate being 6.36%. Rising staking market cap is a sign that investors expect the price to continue rising.\n\nSolana Price Prediction: Technical Analysis\n\nSOL price chart | Source: TradingView\n\nThe daily chart shows that the SOL token has rebounded and is now hovering at the highest level since January. It has formed a golden cross pattern as the 50-day moving average crossed the 200-day one. \n\nThe token has also moved above the key resistance level of $110, the upper side of the bullish flag pattern. This pattern is made up of a vertical line and a descending channel. \n\nTherefore, the token may continue rising, with the next important target to watch being at $150. A drop below the support level of $96 will invalidate the bullish outlook.\n\nRead Also:\n\nCrude Oil Price Rises on Hyperliquid as Houthi Hits Riyadh Airport\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'fdce1d744fe963e401e9c3114fb73ba26fc6f920','2026-09-19 16:45:09','2026-09-19 17:24:34.217963',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 16:45:09');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(443,'alpaca:61884662','benzinga','2026-09-19 18:16:10','Hyperliquid, Uniswap Tokens Surge as SEC Amends Tokenized Stock Trading Rules','Top DeFi protocols like Hyperliquid (HYPE) and Uniswap (UNI) are soaring today after the SEC amended tokenized stock trading rules','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/26/09/61884662/hyperliquid-uniswap-tokens-surge-as-sec-amends-tokenized-stock-trading-rules','["HYPE/USD"]','degen','2026-09-19 18:24:48.936787','regulatory','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'SEC rule changes positively impact tokenized stock trading.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"HYPE/USD": 86.3115}','{"HYPE/USD": {"60m": 6.279}}','2026-09-20 18:26:40.704286','2026-09-19 18:24:43.702032','61884662',replace('Top decentralized finance (DeFi) tokens like Hyperliquid (CRYPTO: HYPE) and Uniswap (CRYPTO: UNI) have jumped in the past few weeks as demand from investors has continued to rise. \n\nHYPE token has jumped by 78% in the last 30 days and is hovering near its all-time high, with its market capitalization rising to over $23 billion. UNI has soared by 142% in this period and is now trading at its highest level since November last year.\n\nOther popular DeFi tokens like Raydium, Lighter, PancakeSwap, and Aerodrome Finance have continued to rise this month. \n\nSEC Amends Tokenized Stock Trading Rules\n\nHYPE and UNI tokens jumped after the SEC issued an order granting temporary, conditional exemptive relief to tokenized securities venues (TSV) to trade tokenized National Market System (NMS) stock using automated market makers and liquidity pools. \n\nThe agency noted that the innovation exemption marked an important milestone to open the capital markets for tokenized securities. This is important because Uniswap and Hyperliquid have become big players in the Real World Asset (RWA) tokenization industry. Top companies like Coinbase (NASDAQ:COIN) and Robinhood Markets (NASDAQ:HOOD) are also top beneficiaries of this change. \n\nRead Also:\n\nSolana Price Forms Bullish Flag as ETF and Staking Inflows Jump\n\nTokenized stocks have become highly popular among traders, especially during the recent crypto winter when Bitcoin and most altcoins were in a strong sell-off. However, they have come under criticism from some of the top players in the US. For example, AMC Entertainment’s (NYSE:AMC) CEO, Adam Aron, has criticized tokenized stocks for not being real assets. \n\nRobinhood apparently is behind an effort related to "tokenized real-world assets including Stock Tokens" for AMC Entertainment (and supposedly 190+ other companies). They are not registered under U.S. securities laws !!!!!!I find this practice to be contemptible, outrageous,…— Adam Aron (@CEOAdam) September 3, 2026 \n\nThe announcement came at a time when their volume and futures open interest have continued rising. HYPE’s surge also came at a time when Hyperliquid is considering entering the US, a move that Donald Trump and the CFTC support. Hyperliquid’s perpetual trading volume jumped to over $240 billion in the last 30 days. \n\nHYPE Price Rally is Accelerating\n\nHyperliquid token chart | Source: TradingView\n\nThe daily chart shows that the HYPE token has been in a strong surge, moving from a low of $20.3 in January to $93 today. It recently crossed the important resistance level of $76, its highest level on June 16. It has also retested that level, confirming a break-and-retest pattern. \n\nHYPE has jumped above the key resistance level of $89.38, its previous all-time high. Also, it remains above all moving averages, while the Average Directional Index (ADX) is at 41. Therefore, the token will likely continue rising as bulls target the key resistance at $100.\n\nUniswap Price Prediction\n\nUNI price chart | Source: TradingView\n\nThe daily chart also shows that the UNI token bottomed at $2.31 in June to a high of $9.5 this week. It recently crossed the important resistance level of $7.47, its highest level on September 6. \n\nThe token has jumped above the 50-day and 200-day moving averages, while the Relative Strength Index (RSI) has soared to 77.7. The most likely scenario is that it retreats and retests the support of $7.47 and then resumes the uptrend.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAltcoin Season Index Nears 50 as Crypto Fear and Greed Index Jumps\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'611daf25defe1d3bfa9a960aec108bb196b2ff23','2026-09-19 18:16:10','2026-09-19 18:24:43.696442',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 18:16:10');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(444,'alpaca:61884640','benzinga','2026-09-19 17:31:09','Bitcoin Bull Says Cancer Took Both Parents By 18, Thought He’d Die Young Too—Until He ''Uncovered a Hack'' to Living Well','Willy Woo, a well-known Bitcoin advocate and cryptocurrency analyst, recounted how nonstop world travel after a tough chapter altered his view of life.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61884640/bitcoin-advocate-cancer-parents-died-young-living-well-hack','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-19 18:24:50.164147','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses a personal story and perspective without financial implications.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.142}}','2026-09-20 18:26:40.704286','2026-09-19 18:24:43.710168','61884640',replace('Willy Woo, a well-known Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) advocate and cryptocurrency analyst, recounted how nonstop world travel after a tough chapter altered his view of life.\n\nThe ‘Hack’ After Dread\n\nIn an X post from Sept. 12, Woo said that after losing both parents to cancer by the age of 18, a deep sense of negativity took hold, and he started believing he too would die young.\n\nFor the next 10 years, he lived with this dread until he finally uncovered a “hack.”\n\n“At 28, I quit my corporate engineering job and traveled the world. A new place every 2-3 days,” Woo stated. “I lived a lifetime in that 6-month trip.”\n\nI lost both my parents to cancer by 18. Thought I would die young too.Then uncovered a hack…At 28 I quit my corporate engineering job and traveled the world. A new place every 2-3 days. I lived a lifetime in that 6 month trip. Upon return a colleague said "hey, I thought… https://t.co/4RMMsZiqot— Willy Woo (@willywoo) September 12, 2026 \n\nWoo Started Chasing ‘Newness’\n\nThose six months felt like two years to Woo, yet only two months to his colleagues—a phenomenon he described as "12x time compression."\n\nThe Bitcoin maximalist said the world trip gave him a new sense of purpose.\n\n“I went on to quit my job, started businesses and lived nomadically, optimising my life, not for happiness or money, but for newness,” Woo added.\n\nWoo quoted a neurosurgeon’s explanation of routine-induced time compression, who then asked X users to share their personal hacks on breaking daily patterns.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAmerica''s Richest Donors Are Tilting Republican — 16 of the Top 20 Billionaires Back GOP as Crypto, AI and Deregulation Shape Donations: Report\n\nWoo is a leading cryptocurrency analyst known for his expertise in on-chain metrics, market commentary, Bitcoin network insights and price predictions.\n\nWoo launched Crest, which functions as a search, data, risk-mitigation and product firm.\n\nHe publishes his findings on his website, Woobull, and in a paid weekly subscription newsletter, Bitcoin Vector Lite.\n\nRead Also:\n\nStrategic Bitcoin Reserve Bill Heads to House Committee: What You Need to Know\n\nPhoto Courtesy: fizkes on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'d3c97f79d02425602ba3f6b4f183a02ed21c8541','2026-09-19 17:31:09','2026-09-19 18:24:43.696442',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 17:31:09');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(445,'alpaca:61884720','benzinga','2026-09-19 19:16:03','OpenAI Cash Burn to Hit $280 Billion by 2030 as Anthropic Profit Surges','OpenAI predicts that its cash burn will jump to $280 billion by 2030, while Anthropic continues its profitability run ahead of IPO.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61884720/openai-cash-burn-to-hit-280-billion-by-2030-as-anthropic-profit-surges','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-19 19:24:58.442691','other','neutral',2,3,'weeks',1,'OpenAI''s prediction is not a confirmed event and does not directly impact NVDA.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-20 19:26:47.778236','2026-09-19 19:24:55.027032','61884720',replace('OpenAI, the company behind ChatGPT, expects to burn through $280 billion in cash between 2026 and 2030, mostly on computing power and infrastructure. It projects revenue will climb from $36 billion this year to $350 billion by 2030.\n\nAccording to The Financial Times, the company continues to make substantial losses, as it focuses on boosting its capacity, improving its models, and gaining market share. The company predicts that its cash burn will be about $278 billion between 2026 and 2030. Most of its expenditures will be on computing power.\n\nOpenAI also predicts that its annual revenue will total $840 billion between this year and 2030. It made these revelations to investors as it seeks to raise more capital at a $1.2 trillion valuation. Its last capital raising, which included a $30 billion investment from Nvidia (NASDAQ:NVDA), valued it at over $850 billion.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSolana Price Forms Bullish Flag as ETF and Staking Inflows Jump\n\nOpenAI is Facing Major Risks\n\nOpenAI is confronting numerous challenges, with Anthropic being the biggest one. Anthropic has become one of the fastest-growing companies in the artificial intelligence industry. \n\nAccording to The Financial Times, the company made an adjusted operating profit in the second quarter as its revenue jumped 14-fold from a year earlier. Its annualized revenue jumped to $65 billion at the end of July, a figure that analysts expect will hit $120 billion at the end of the year. This growth may help to justify its $2 trillion valuation when it launches its initial public offering (IPO) later this year. \n\nIn addition to Anthropic, the company is facing substantial competition from open-weight models, especially from China. These models by companies like Moonshot Alibaba (NYSE:BABA), and DeepSeek have proven to be highly capable and cheaper for consumers.\n\nOpenAI’s most advanced model, GPT-6 Astra, completes a task at about $3.26, while Kimi K3 Max costs just $2. Google’s Gemini and Meta Platforms’ Muse are also highly affordable. As a result, there is a likelihood that the price war will affect its profitability and growth.\n\nMost importantly, OpenAI, like other AI models, is confronting the AI safety issues that have come up recently. Just this week, it was revealed that hackers used Anthropic’s Claude to break into OpenAI. \n\nOpenAI’s models hacked Hugging Face a few months ago, while Google’s AI models hacked three companies. These events, coupled with the rising threat of human extinction, may lead to more regulations in the future. \n\nRead Also:\n\nAltcoin Season Index Nears 50 as Crypto Fear and Greed Index Jumps\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'bf2b3ea332cc83759b0c79ae491f53df1d0eb622','2026-09-19 19:16:03','2026-09-19 19:24:55.023216',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 19:16:03');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(446,'alpaca:61884699','benzinga','2026-09-19 18:45:32','XRP Price Prediction as Multiple Catalysts Point to Further Gains','This XRP price prediction explores what to expect as several catalysts, including ETF inflows and RLUSD stablecoin growth continues.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/26/09/61884699/xrp-price-prediction-as-multiple-catalysts-point-to-further-gains','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD", "XRP/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-19 19:24:59.711358','other','neutral',2,1,'weeks',1,'The headline discusses potential future gains without confirming any actual events.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 5.142}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 5.795}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 7.639, "1d": 8.02}}','2026-09-20 19:26:47.778236','2026-09-19 19:24:55.029541','61884699',replace('Ripple (CRYPTO: XRP) rose for a second straight day, reaching its highest level since Tuesday and climbing 15% from this week’s low. The rebound could continue after the token formed a bullish flag pattern and as inflows into its exchange-traded funds (ETFs) kept rising.\n\nXRP Price Rebounding Amid the Crypto Market Rally\n\nXRP token continued rising on Saturday as the crypto market rally intensified. Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) price crossed the important resistance level of $81,000, while Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) jumped above $2,600. The market capitalization of all cryptocurrencies jumped to $2.8 trillion, while the Altcoin Season Index has continued to soar. \n\nXRP’s fundamentals are also improving. For example, spot XRP ETFs continued to add assets this week, a sign that American retail and institutional investors expect it to keep rising. The funds have added $41 million in inflows this month, continuing a winning streak that started in April this year. \n\nRead Also:\n\nCrude Oil Price Rises on Hyperliquid as Houthi Hits Riyadh Airport\n\nRipple USD (CRYPTO: RLUSD) has continued to add assets this month. The stablecoin now has $2.37 billion in assets, with $1.03 billion being on the XRP Ledger and the rest being on Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH). This performance is a sign that XRPL’s utility is growing.\n\nRipple Labs believes that RLUSD will continue growing, driven by key areas like corporate treasury, payroll, and cross-border payments. A surge in usage will lead to more fees, which will translate into more XRP burns. \n\nXRP price has also jumped because of the rising volume and open interest. Its 24-hour volume rose by 2.7% to $4.07 billion, with its futures open interest rising to over $2.7 billion. \n\nRipple Price Technical Analysis Points to More Gains\n\nXRP price chart | Source: TradingView\n\nTechnicals, especially on the daily chart, suggest that the XRP price has more gains to go. It formed a morning star candle on September 16. This pattern is made up of a small body and small upper and lower shadows, and is one of the most bullish reversal signs in technical analysis.\n\nThe token is in the process of forming a bullish flag pattern. This pattern happens after a strong rally followed by a descending channel. It is now trading along the upper side of the descending channel. \n\nXRP is about to form a golden cross pattern as the spread between the 50-day and 200-day Exponential Moving Averages (EMA) narrows. Therefore, this pattern points to a strong bullish breakout, potentially to last month’s high of $1.70. A move above that level will point to more gains to $2.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBill Ackman Said ‘Hell Is Coming’ in 2020 — How a $27 Million Hedge Turned Into $2.6 Billion as He Bought the Crash\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'7659dee0f561f4e4164cece7aef31c5bec66573c','2026-09-19 18:45:32','2026-09-19 19:24:55.023216',1,NULL,'2026-09-19 18:45:32');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(447,'alpaca:61885005','benzinga','2026-09-20 06:02:29','Trump Says Son Donald Trump Jr. ‘Paid’ Russian Boxing Chief Umar Kremlev Over Bahamas Wedding Gift','Trump confirms son Don Jr. repaid Russian boxing chief Umar Kremlev for lavish Bahamas wedding gifts amid ethics scrutiny.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/politics/26/09/61885005/trump-don-jr-repays-umar-kremlev-bahamas-wedding-gifts','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-20 06:25:36.648125','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Involves personal financial matters and ethics scrutiny without direct impact on the asset.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}','2026-09-21 06:27:50.015212','2026-09-20 06:25:32.245274','61885005',replace('President Donald Trump said Friday that his eldest son, Donald Trump Jr., has repaid Umar Kremlev, president of the International Boxing Association, for financing lavish gifts tied to his wedding celebration in the Bahamas earlier this year.\n\nOval Office Remarks Address Ethics Concerns\n\nSpeaking to reporters at the White House, the president called the arrangement “totally allowed” and said such gestures are common at weddings. “That’s very common; I’ve heard of many people giving wedding parties,” Trump said. “I hear he’s paid him back,” he added, describing Kremlev as “a friend” of his son’s.\n\nKremlev, a Russian businessman with reported ties to the Kremlin, reportedly financed a private island rental and fireworks display worth hundreds of thousands of dollars, according to a ProPublica report. The Russian businessman’s Kremlin connections have drawn scrutiny over potential foreign influence near the presidential family.\n\nCouple Disputes Wedding Ceremony Link\n\nEarlier this week, Trump Jr. and his wife, Bettina Trump, addressed the gifts on social media, saying the island gathering was not their wedding ceremony but rather “an already planned weekend” with friends. They described their relationship with Kremlev as a friendship and said he hosted two nights of celebrations afterward as a wedding gift, denying any political motive behind the gesture.\n\nPresident Trump did not attend the event.\n\nWedding Has Drawn Scrutiny Before\n\nThis is not the first time the wedding has faced ethics scrutiny. In May, Sen. Adam Schiff (D-Calif.) linked Trump’s initial absence from the ceremony to a separate $620 million conditional Pentagon loan for Vulcan Elements, a company that makes high-performance rare earth permanent magnets. \n\nTrump Jr.’s investment firm, 1789 Capital, had an undisclosed stake in the company. Schiff described the loan as a taxpayer-funded "wedding present."\n\nA Pattern of Scrutinized Gifts\n\nGift-giving has repeatedly drawn scrutiny during Trump’s second term. \n\nIn May 2025, Qatar’s royal family gifted the president a $400 million Boeing Co. (NYSE:BA) 747-8 jet, which economist Peter Schiff and former Treasury Secretary Larry Summers called “banana-republic-level corruption.” \n\nIn August 2025, Apple‘s (NASDAQ:AAPL) then CEO Tim Cook presented Trump with a 24-karat gold-based plaque, days before Apple secured a tariff exemption on imported chips. \n\nFinancial disclosures show Trump gave a total of $155,000 in holiday cash gifts to four close aides, including $45,000 to Natalie Harp, who also traveled with Trump on a secret flight out of Turkey after a sudden change of planes.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSanders, Pelosi, Newsom Slam Trump''s White House Press Ban: ‘We Will Not Accept Authoritarianism’\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'77338acb292f15c428dc5291d7eddc65eb50605a','2026-09-20 06:02:29','2026-09-20 06:25:32.241620',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 06:02:29');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(448,'alpaca:61885100','benzinga','2026-09-20 08:36:34','Box CEO Says Companies Will Have to ‘Build Something That Agents Want’ as AI Agents Become New Consumers','Levie says AI agents could reshape consumer tech by completing tasks for users and becoming new gatekeepers for companies.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61885100/box-ceo-says-companies-will-have-to-build-something-that-agents-want-as-ai-agents-become-new-consumers','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-20 09:25:51.169853','other','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'CEO comments on AI trends could influence strategic decisions but are speculative.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-21 09:28:16.920754','2026-09-20 09:25:46.143319','61885100',replace('Box Inc. (NYSE:BOX) CEO Aaron Levie argued that AI agents could fundamentally reshape consumer technology by forcing companies to design products that agents can navigate and operate on users’ behalf.\n\nAI Agents Could Become New Digital Gatekeepers\n\nOn Saturday, in a post on X, Box CEO said the rise of personal agents would create a new model in which people delegate tasks to AI systems that can complete them from start to finish.\n\n"Personal agents are the ultimate manifestation of ‘build something that agents want,’" Levie wrote.\n\nHe pointed to products such as Muse, saying users increasingly want to "hand off a task to the agent and ensure that it is fully completed end to end."\n\nFor that to happen, agents need to interact directly with the tools and services required to complete tasks. \n\nLevie said they should be able to "use your MCP or CLI, easily navigate your site, be able to transact, and more."\n\nAI Agents Could Become New Digital Gatekeepers\n\nLevie argued that companies may soon have to compete for the attention of AI agents rather than directly for consumers.\n\n"The new attention you need to compete for is not from the user itself but instead for the agent," he said.\n\nHe highlighted tools that allow agents to order food, conduct e-commerce transactions, book flights and interact with data as examples of services that could benefit from the shift.\n\nLevie said this transformation could represent "the biggest opportunity and shakeup in consumer tech since the App Store itself."\n\nPersonal agents are the ultimate manifestation of "build something that agents want".The form factor of a product like Muse is you want to be able to hand off a task to the agent and ensure that it is fully completed end to end. To do this, the agent must be able to… https://t.co/33UJK9moAI— Aaron Levie (@levie) September 19, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nEvery AI Agent Needs a Gatekeeper: 3 Cybersecurity Stocks to Watch\n\nAI Agents Raise Safety and Control Concerns\n\nLast week, Anthropic said Claude performed 26% of its measured AI R&D; work in August, up from 1% in March, while about 30,000 AI agents handled research and engineering tasks. \n\nMore than 90% of the measured AI R&D; work reached the “AI collaborates” level or higher. Anthropic also reported that about 6% of its AI R&D; compute was devoted to safety research in a July snapshot.\n\nMeta Platforms, Inc. (NASDAQ:META) CEO Mark Zuckerberg said the company delayed its Muse AI agent for months to address safety and security concerns. \n\nHe supported independent evaluators and said companies that failed to prioritize AI alignment could face liability if systems caused harm.\n\nMicrosoft CEO Satya Nadella said AI development needed human control, rigorous testing and stronger safeguards. \n\nHe warned that persistent AI agents could create new insider risks, including manipulating business records, and called for third-party evaluations and greater transparency.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nDaniel Newman Praises Zuckerberg For ''Doing The Right Thing'' With Muse AI Safety Despite Investor Pressure: ''Didn’t Feel The Need to Bring Bernie Sanders Into'' This\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'bee3cc031de1cd01df1d07c0900f06d6821b1fa8','2026-09-20 08:36:34','2026-09-20 09:25:46.135826',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 08:36:34');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(449,'alpaca:61885260','benzinga','2026-09-20 11:00:21','iPhone 18 Pro Hits Stores, Samsung Retakes Smartphone Throne and More: This Week in Appleverse','Apple&#39;s week included the iPhone 18 Pro launch, AI server talks with Nvidia, and Musk dropping his antitrust lawsuit claim.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61885260/apple-aapl-weekly-recap-iphone-18-pro-nvidia-ai-server-musk-lawsuit','["AAPL", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-20 11:26:01.351328','product','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'The iPhone 18 Pro launch is notable but expected news.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-21 11:28:47.343240','2026-09-20 11:25:57.671256','61885260',replace('It’s been a busy week for Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) with new iPhone launches, analyst predictions, and major AI server developments. Here’s a round-up of the top stories from the past week.\n\nApple Raises The Premium Bet With iPhone 18 Pro Launch\n\nApple has unveiled its latest iPhone lineup, with the premium models hitting stores first. The company’s first foldable device is set to follow.\n\nAccording to a report by CNBC, the iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max models are launching with higher price points than previous new-device models. This marks the first major product release under new CEO John Ternus.\n\n“This is a big bet on the premium segment, and it’s a bet that’s going to pay off,” said Ternus.\n\nRead the full article here.\n\nApple’s iPhone Upgrade Cycle Looks Strong As Carrier Incentives Hit $1200\n\nApple could witness a robust iPhone upgrade cycle, thanks to richer U.S. carrier promotions that help consumers absorb higher device prices. This was suggested by Bank of America (NYSE:BAC) analyst Wamsi Mohan.\n\nMohan reiterated a Buy rating on Apple with a $370 price forecast. The analyst cited capital returns, Apple’s potential to emerge as a winner in edge AI and opportunities in new products and markets.\n\nRead the full article here.\n\nApple, Nvidia Eye Major Entry Into AI Servers: Report\n\nApple is reportedly working on an AI server that could use two or four planned M8 Ultra chips, as per a report by The Information. The company is considering Nvidia Corp‘s (NASDAQ:NVDA) NVLink Fusion technology to connect the processors.\n\nThis partnership could potentially integrate Apple’s custom chips with NVIDIA’s broader data-center systems. The project would extend Apple’s chip strategy beyond consumer devices.\n\nRead the full article here.\n\nSamsung Retakes Smartphone Throne\n\nDespite a 7% global smartphone market decline in the second quarter of 2026, Samsung Electronics Co. Ltd. (OTC:SSNLF) reclaimed the top position with a 23% share of global smartphone shipments. Its shipments increased 9% year over year.\n\nAnalysts attributed this to favorable pricing and competitive dynamics. Counterpoint Research reported that developed markets proved more resilient due to their greater exposure to premium devices.\n\nRead the full article here.\n\nElon Musk Makes Nice With Apple, Dismisses Antitrust Lawsuit\n\nElon Musk‘s xAI and X Corp have dropped Apple from their antitrust lawsuit but are maintaining the pressure on OpenAI. The lawsuit, which accused Apple of monopolistic practices, was initially filed in August 2025.\n\nxAI withdrew its claims against Apple in the lawsuit, which U.S. District Judge Mark Pittman approved. While xAI dropped its claims against Apple, it continues to pursue its case against OpenAI.\n\nRead the full article here.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto: Skorzewiak / Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'9d8ea06e24461639616ba7bb333c755e29fb7382','2026-09-20 11:00:21','2026-09-20 11:25:57.667593',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 11:00:22');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(450,'alpaca:61885317','benzinga','2026-09-20 12:00:08','Brace For Fuel Hike, Tesla Faces NHTSA Scrutiny and More: This Week in Mobility','Airlines, Tesla, Waymo and China’s automakers dominated business headlines this week amid rising fuel costs and more.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61885317/brace-for-fuel-hike-tesla-faces-nhtsa-scrutiny-and-more-this-week-in-mobility','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-20 12:26:08.093835','regulatory','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'Tesla is under scrutiny by the NHTSA which could affect investor sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-21 12:28:59.599060','2026-09-20 12:26:04.203346','61885317',replace('This week has been a rollercoaster ride for the business world. From airlines grappling with fuel price hikes due to the ongoing Iran war to Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) facing regulatory scrutiny and revised delivery forecasts, there’s a lot to unpack.\n\nLet’s dive into the top stories of the week.\n\nUnited, American Airlines Signal Capacity Cuts Over Elevated Fuel Costs\n\nThe war in Iran is causing turbulence in the aviation sector, with fuel costs soaring. United Airlines Holdings Inc. and American Airlines Group Inc. have hinted at potential capacity cuts. United CFO Michael Leskinen, speaking at Morgan Stanley’s Laguna Conference, stated that the airline is prepared to adapt to the changing global landscape.\n\nRead the full article here.\n\nNHTSA Orders Tesla to Answer Cybercab Certification Questions\n\nThe U.S. National Highway Traffic Safety Administration has ordered Tesla Inc. to respond to 21 detailed questions regarding the self-certification of its Cybercab robotaxi. The responses, due by Sept. 30, must be made under oath by a Tesla officer.\n\nRead the full article here.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTSLA Critic Gordon Johnson Rips Cybercab Launch After Elon Musk''s ‘Storm of Cybercabs’ Promise: ‘The Robotaxi Story Was Never About Robotaxis''\n\nGoldman Cuts Tesla Q3 Delivery Forecast to 435,000\n\nGoldman Sachs has revised its third-quarter delivery forecast for Tesla Inc. to 435,000 vehicles, a significant drop from the previous estimate of 490,000. This new forecast is also below the 456,000 Visible Alpha consensus.\n\nRead the full article here.\n\nWaymo Expands Robotaxi Battle to Las Vegas\n\nAlphabet Inc.-backed Robotaxi service Waymo is expanding its autonomous vehicles in Las Vegas and planning a 2027 rollout in Tokyo. The majority of the fleet in Las Vegas will comprise the Geely Automobile Holdings Ltd.-backed Zeekr’s co-developed “Ojai” Robotaxis.\n\nRead the full article here.\n\nTrump’s China Car U-Turn?\n\nPresident Donald Trump has hinted at a possible change in stance towards Chinese automakers entering the U.S. market. In an interview with Fox News, Trump dismissed rumors of a framework allowing Chinese automakers to enter the U.S., but suggested he might be okay with them building vehicles in the country.\n\nRead the full article here.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Weighs ''Big Decision'' Amid Iran War as Ex-Counterterrorism Chief Warns ''There Is No Military Solution''\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'1ece4b0099252981b20c040afd7143bc55531b1b','2026-09-20 12:00:08','2026-09-20 12:26:04.199681',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 12:00:08');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(451,'alpaca:61885437','benzinga','2026-09-20 13:30:21','EXCLUSIVE: Tesla Vehicles Maintain Nearly 19% Junk Title Rate Across Age Groups, VIN Analysis Shows','EpicVIN data shows Tesla has the highest EV junk-title rate at 18.5%, versus 1%-9.5% for leading legacy automaker EVs.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61885437/exclusive-tesla-vehicles-maintain-nearly-19-junk-title-rate-across-age-groups-vin-analysis-shows','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-20 14:26:18.851545','other','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'High junk title rate may negatively impact consumer perception of Tesla vehicles.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-21 14:29:37.158486','2026-09-20 14:26:14.349252','61885437',replace('Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) has consistently led the U.S. EV sales charts with the Model Y, which first hit the roads in 2020 and has since emerged as one of the Elon Musk-led automaker’s best-selling vehicles.\n\nHowever, an analysis by EpicVIN, a vehicle history provider, compiled a dataset of 296 million vehicles based on sales listings and auction records from providers like Copart and IAAI, and points to the high rates of junk titles for Tesla vehicles.\n\nA salvage or junk title is a state title brand generally associated with vehicles that have been declared a total loss. Depending on state rules and the extent of damage, some salvage vehicles can be repaired and returned to the road. With that said, let’s take a closer look.\n\nTesla Salvage Rates Far Exceed Other EVs in EpicVIN Dataset\n\nOf the 296 million vehicles, the data analyzed 70 models that were purely electric, meaning that it had no Plug-In Hybrids (PHEVs), Hybrid Vehicles, or Extended Range Electric Vehicles (EREVs), EpicVIN said.\n\nThe dataset comprised 2,807,799 EVs, of which Tesla vehicles made up 751,766. The dataset also did not include models that had fewer than 1,000 vehicles and omitted models with the same name for both internal combustion engines (ICE) and electrified vehicles.\n\nRead Also:\n\nJim Farley Reaffirms 2027 Launch for Ford’s $28K Cybertruck Rival, the Fathom EV — the Price Gap Could Buy You a Tesla Model Y\n\nThe Tesla line-up, including the Model Y, Model S, Model X, Model 3 and the Cybertruck, comprised 138,839 salvage titles out of 751,766 vehicles, representing an 18.5% salvage rate.\n\nThe model-wise breakdown for Tesla vehicles that held junk titles included 64,749 units of 341,078 Tesla Model 3 vehicles, comprising 19%, while 42,900 of 225,106 of Tesla Model Y vehicles held junk titles, comprising 19.1% of vehicles.\n\nFor the Tesla Model S vehicles, 21,539 units held junk titles, according to the data, from a total of 114,449 units, making up 18.8% of the model. 9,035 units out of 64,759 Model X vehicles held junk titles, making up 14.0%. The Tesla Cybertruck, which is the newest and most expensive member of the Tesla line-up, was the lowest, with 616 units holding junk titles out of 6,374 vehicles, making up nearly 10%.\n\nIt’s worth noting that because Tesla exclusively builds battery-electric vehicles (BEVs) and maintains higher cumulative EV sales volumes than traditional automakers, Tesla models may make up over a quarter of all fully electric vehicles in the dataset.\n\nImportantly, the figures do not represent the salvage rate of Tesla vehicles on U.S. roads. EpicVIN’s data comes from auction and sales-listing records, including Copart and IAAI, rather than state title registries, meaning the percentages reflect vehicles appearing in those records.\n\nHow Legacy Automakers Compare\n\nFor reference, the 10 largest non-Tesla EV volume models from Legacy automakers show salvage rates ranging from 1.0% to 9.5% across model lines, each exceeding 60,000 units in the dataset, EpicVIN said.\n\nThe data consisted of the Nissan Motor Co. Ltd.‘s (OTC:NSANY) Leaf, where 9.5% or 17,443 of 183,095 units held junk titles. The data also showed that from 138,593 of the General Motors Co. (NYSE:GM) Chevrolet Bolt EV vehicles, 7,920 had salvage or junk titles, which equaled 5.7%. 737 units, or 1.1% of 68,163 Cadillac Lyriq vehicles, had salvage titles, whereas 761 units out of 76,861 Chevrolet Equinox EV vehicles were up for the scrapyard, equivalent to 1% of the total.\n\nFor South Korean automakers, out of 67,273 Kia EV6 vehicles, 2,434 have salvage or junk titles, making up 3.6% of the total. On the other hand, out of 159,202 Hyundai Ioniq 5 vehicles, 3,843 were deemed a total loss, equaling 2.4%. 81,657 Honda Motor Company, Ltd. (NYSE:HMC) Prologue vehicles were also analyzed in the data, out of which 1.4% or 1,111 had salvage or junk titles.\n\nThe Volkswagen ID.4, with 3,272 salvage titles from a total of 101,308 units, made up 3.2%. Of the 73,084 total BMW i4 vehicles in the dataset, 1,997 held salvage or junk titles, which equals 2.7%. EpicVIN also analyzed 195,448 units of the Ford Motor Co. (NYSE:F) Mustang Mach-E vehicle, out of which 2.6% or 5,150 units had salvage titles.\n\nThe Volume & Age Divergence\n\nBecause salvage rates typically scale with age, the dataset factors in vehicle maturity. Tesla’s high sales volume over a longer timeline gives its vehicles an average age of 5.4 years in this dataset, compared to 3.0 years for the 65 non-Tesla models, EpicVIN data showed.\n\nWhen comparing vehicles of similar age, non-Tesla EV salvage rates increase as cars mature, whereas Tesla’s salvage rates remain static near 18% across all age groups, the data showed. FOr \n\nTesla models, like the Model Y and the Cybertruck, when compared with data from non-Tesla models aged under 5 years, also showcase nearly 19% junk title data. 18.8% or 43,516 vehicles of 231,480 Cybertrucks and Model Ys held junk titles. \n\nWhile 2.3% or 36,829 of 1,625,624 from non-Tesla makers comprising over 50 models held junk titles, the data said. When comparing models older than five years and up to eight years, Tesla vehicles remain above 18%.  \n\n18.2% or 73,784 of 405,837 Tesla Model 3 and Model X vehicles held salvage titles. On the other hand, 5.8% or 10,095 of 174,542 vehicles aged five to eight years from non-Tesla makers held junk titles.\n\nThe story remains similar when accounting for vehicles aged eight to 11 Years, with 18.8% or 21,539 of 114,449 Model S vehicles being total losses, compared with 9.5% or 23,711 of 249,631 vehicles from traditional automakers.\n\nEven after grouping vehicles by average age, the EpicVIN dataset shows Tesla’s salvage-title rate remaining around 18%-19%, while the comparable non-Tesla groups show lower rates.\n\nRead Also:\n\nRoss Gerber Says He Found ‘Secret’ Lot With Hundreds of Waymo Robotaxis: ‘Something Crazy Is About to Happen’\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by a Benzinga editor.\n\nCheck out more of Benzinga’s Future Of Mobility coverage by following this link.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'3645043b0afaeee7188332e385d6a9e6d1b64cab','2026-09-20 13:30:21','2026-09-20 14:26:14.345605',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 13:30:21');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(452,'alpaca:61885631','benzinga','2026-09-20 16:45:18','Bitcoin Price Stabilizes Above $80,000 as ETF Inflows Jump, Bullish Patterns Form','Bitcoin price has stabilized above the crucial support level of $80,000 as several bullish patterns suggest that a rebound is possible','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/26/09/61885631/bitcoin-price-stabilizes-above-80k-as-etf-inflows-jump-bullish-patterns-form','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-20 17:26:32.536152','other','bullish',2,3,'days',1,'Bullish patterns suggest potential upward movement in Bitcoin price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 6.058}}','2026-09-21 17:30:22.919850','2026-09-20 17:26:28.810838','61885631',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) has held above the key support level of $80,000 as investors follow new developments in crypto ETFs and the recent setback for the CLARITY Act. BTC was trading at $80,582, roughly $1,400 below its weekend high of $82,000.\n\nBitcoin ETF Inflows are Rising\n\nAmerican investors are continuing to buy Bitcoin this month, a sign that they expect it to continue rising. Data shows that these ETFs had over $433 million in inflows on Friday, higher than Thursday’s $133 million.\n\nSpot Bitcoin ETFs have attracted more than $313 million in net inflows so far this month, following $3.52 billion last month. Cumulative net inflows now total $55.1 billion, while total net assets stand at $102.5 billion. BlackRock’s IBIT leads with $63 billion in assets, followed by Fidelity’s FBTC at $14.3 billion.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBroadcom Stock Remains in Bear Territory as Analysts Signal a Floor\n\nBitcoin ETF inflows happened in a difficult week in which the Federal Reserve hiked interest rates by 0.25% to between 3.75% and 4%. It also happened after the US Senate failed to pass the CLARITY Act. Odds that the bill will become law have slumped on Polymarket. \n\nMost notably, investors are buying Bitcoin assets as the US-Iran crisis escalates, leading to higher diesel prices in the US. The average price has jumped to a record high of $6.50, and there are chances that it will hit $7 in the coming days. Gasoline prices have jumped to $4.47. \n\nBitcoin’s rise has coincided with the ongoing rally of the Crypto Fear and Greed Index, which has remained in the greed zone. It jumped to the greed area of 71, a sign that sentiment is rising. \n\nBitcoin Price Prediction: Technical Analysis\n\nBTC price chart | Source: TradingView\n\nTechnicals suggest that Bitcoin is about to break out. It has formed a pattern that resembles a cup-and-handle pattern, which is a common continuation sign in technical analysis. It is now in the handle section of this pattern.\n\nThe coin has also formed a bullish flag pattern, which is made up of a vertical line and a descending channel. It has already moved above the upper side of this channel.\n\nBitcoin sits above the 100-day Exponential Moving Average. These patterns suggest that the coin will stage a strong comeback, potentially to the psychological level of $85,000. This view will be confirmed if it moves above the key resistance at $82,135, its highest point in May. \n\nRead Also:\n\nOpenAI Cash Burn to Hit $280 Billion by 2030 as Anthropic Profit Surges\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'bc8eb90f6c32667756818a8f057019f73b933d96','2026-09-20 16:45:18','2026-09-20 17:26:28.807293',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 16:45:18');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(453,'alpaca:61885704','benzinga','2026-09-20 17:45:09','Micron Stock Eyes a Big Move as Closely Watched Q4 Earnings Report Nears','Micron stock may be on the cusp of a strong bullish breakout as the company prepares to publish its fourth quarter earnings report.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61885704/micron-stock-eyes-a-big-move-as-closely-watched-q4-earnings-report-nears','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-20 18:26:39.541180','earnings','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The headline discusses a potential move ahead of earnings, indicating uncertainty.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-21 18:30:33.670447','2026-09-20 18:26:35.653967','61885704',replace('Micron Technology (NASDAQ:MU) stock has traded sideways since July, in line with other leading memory chipmakers. Shares currently trade at $1,015, up 212% year to date. This consolidation could end soon, as the company is set to report its financial results later this month.\n\nMicron Technology Earnings to Publish Strong Earnings\n\nMU stock has held steady in the past few months in line with other memory companies like SK Hynix, Samsung Electronics, SanDisk (NASDAQ:SNDK), and Western Digital (NASDAQ:WDC).\n\nThe company is expected to publish strong financial results next week since it has become a top beneficiary of the AI boom. Recent results by its biggest clients like Nvidia (NASDAQ:NVDA), AMD, Microsoft, and Amazon, have all published strong numbers and hinted of more spending. \n\nThe average estimate among Wall Street analysts is that Micron’s fourth-quarter revenue will come in at $50.9 billion, up by 350% from a year earlier. If this is correct, it will bring its full-year figure to $129 billion, up by 247% YoY. Historically, Micron has a strong record of beating estimates, meaning that its real numbers will be much better.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBroadcom Stock Remains in Bear Territory as Analysts Signal a Floor\n\nAnalysts expect Micron’s revenue to jump to $245 billion in the next financial year. Earnings per share are forecast to reach $73, followed by $156.50 the year after. The stock could extend its gains if earnings and guidance come in well above expectations.\n\nThese numbers come at a time when the company is still a bargain. The company has a forward price-to-earnings ratio of 13.8, much lower than the technology sector median of 22.80. The multiple is also much lower than the five-year average of 74. \n\nThe challenge, however, there is a fear that the AI sector will start slowing down as safety concerns remain. Some of the top executives in the industry, including those from Anthropic and OpenAI have called for a slowdown. \n\nMicron Stock Has Formed an Ascending Triangle Pattern\n\nMU stock chart | Source: TradingView\n\nTechnicals suggest that MU stock may be on the cusp of a strong bullish breakout. It has formed an ascending triangle pattern, which is made up of an ascending trendline and a horizontal resistance. This pattern often results into a strong bullish breakout. \n\nMicron remains above the 50-day Exponential Moving Average (EMA) and the Supertrend indicator. These technicals suggest that the stock may have a strong bullish breakout in the near term, possibly after earnings. \n\nIf this happens, the next level to watch will be at $1,255, its highest point in June. This view aligns with what analysts expect, with the consensus among analysts being $1,295. Top analysts from companies like RBC, TD Cowen, and New Street Research expect it to continue rising. \n\nRead Also:\n\nOpenAI Cash Burn to Hit $280 Billion by 2030 as Anthropic Profit Surges\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'09099880d99b81de2d77fb6b6e54b4740db0f4e2','2026-09-20 17:45:09','2026-09-20 18:26:35.650258',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 17:45:09');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(454,'alpaca:61885678','benzinga','2026-09-20 17:31:05','VOO & Chill: Why Vanguard’s S&P 500 ETF is Beating SPY and IVV','VOO ETF has continued to have substantial inflows this year and is continuing to beat popular funds like SPY and IVV','https://www.benzinga.com/etfs/sector-etfs/26/09/61885678/voo-chill-why-vanguards-sp-500-etf-is-beating-spy-and-ivv','["SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-20 18:26:40.639238','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The statement reflects ongoing performance trends without indicating a definitive price movement.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-21 18:30:33.670447','2026-09-20 18:26:35.656484','61885678',replace('The Vanguard S&P; 500 ETF (NYSE:VOO) has drawn heavy investor interest this year, helped by the growing “VOO and Chill” trend, where investors buy the fund and hold it for the long term. The approach leans on the fund’s strong track record and its low fees. \n\nVOO ETF Inflows are Surging\n\nETF Db data shows that the fund has had over $139.4 billion in inflows this year, much higher than the $137 billion it added last year. This growth has brought its assets under management (AUM) to over $1.07 trillion. On average, the fund is having over $15 billion in inflows per month.\n\nVOO ETF inflows | Source: ETF Db\n\nIn contrast, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF (NYSE:SPY), which was the biggest ETF in the world for years, has had over $3.6 billion in outflows this year, with its AUM sitting at $800 billion. The iShares Core S&P; 500 ETF (NYSE:IVV) has lost over $13.6 billion in assets this year.\n\nOne potential reason for the ongoing "VOO & Chill" phenomenon is the expense ratio. VOO charges 0.03%, meaning that a $100,000 investment will cost just $30 a year. SPY, on the other hand, charges 0.09%, meaning that a similar investment costs $90 a year. \n\nRead Also:\n\nCrude Oil Price Rises on Hyperliquid as Houthi Hits Riyadh Airport\n\nThe smaller State Street SPDR Portfolio S&P; 500 (NYSE:SPYM), which charges 0.02% a year, has had over $58 billion in inflows this year and now holds over $169.6 billion in AUM. \n\nAnother key reason why VOO is beating SPY is how it is structured. SPY is structured as a unit investment trust, meaning that it cannot reinvest dividends between payouts and lend securities. It also has less flexibility than VOO, and in most cases, long-term holders don’t have a reason to accept the drag.\n\nVOO ETF Has Some Bullish Catalysts\n\nWhile VOO and other S&P; 500 ETFs have stalled recently, technicals and fundamentals points to a strong rebound in the coming days or weeks. The most notable fundamentals are the strong earnings growth.\n\nS&P; 500 companies, fueled by energy and technology, had earnings growth of over 50% in the second quarter, much higher than expected. This growth was also driven by the tariff refunds. \n\nFactSet (NYSE:FDS) data shows that analysts expect third-quarter earnings growth to be 28%. Since the real figure is usually higher, there is a possibility that the growth will be over 40%. \n\nFurther, the index is fairly cheap, with the forward price-to-earnings ratio being 19.1, down from the five-year average of 19.8. \n\nTechnicals also points to a rebound since it is in the process of forming a bullish flag pattern on the daily chart. This pattern forms after a big jump, which is then followed by a descending channel. It normally leads to a continuation. \n\nRead Also:\n\nSolana Price Forms Bullish Flag as ETF and Staking Inflows Jump\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'dc43dd3069b9a70d4d1ea55152cb3794c9af6a85','2026-09-20 17:31:05','2026-09-20 18:26:35.650258',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 17:31:05');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(455,'alpaca:61885749','benzinga','2026-09-20 18:45:33','Ethereum Treasury Stocks SharpLink and BitMine Eye Further Upside as ETH Targets $3,000 Rebound','Top Ethereum Treasury companies, SharpLink and BitMine are eying a strong rally as ETH price targets the key resistance at $3,000.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61885749/ethereum-treasury-stocks-sharplink-and-bitmine-eye-further-upside-as-eth-targets-3k-rebound','["ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-20 19:26:47.713441','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The headline discusses potential future price movements without confirmation of actual events.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"ETH/USD": {"60m": 8.965}}','2026-09-21 19:30:46.500426','2026-09-20 19:26:43.899532','61885749',replace('Top Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) treasury companies have staged a comeback this month, and the rally could extend in the coming weeks or months.\n\nBitMine Immersion (NASDAQ:BMNR) jumped to $26 on Friday, up 104% from its lowest level this year and near its highest level since January. SharpLink (NASDAQ:SBET) rose to $9.35, a gain of 109% from its low for the year.\n\nThe two companies are the biggest Ethereum holders in the world. Tom Lee’s BitMine has accumulated 5,956,378 coins worth $15.46 billion. It has less than 44,000 coins to buy to hit its 5% target. SharpLink, on the other hand, has 868,699 coins currently worth over $2.25 billion. \n\nThese stocks could keep rising as Ethereum’s technicals and fundamentals improve. On the fundamental side, U.S. investors have continued to accumulate ETH this month, with net inflows of $187 million on track for a third straight month of gains. Staking demand is also growing, with the share of ETH staked climbing to 35.50%. Whale buyers have also continued their accumulation this month.\n\nRead Also:\n\nXRP Price Prediction as Multiple Catalysts Point to Further Gains\n\nEthereum’s usage is also rising. For example, the total value locked (TVL) in its decentralized finance (DeFi) ecosystem has jumped to over $52 billion, while the stablecoin market cap hit $146 billion. Most notably, the amount of assets in its real-world asset (RWA) ecosystem has jumped to over $13.4 billion. \n\nEthereum Price Technicals Point to More Gains Ahead\n\nETH price chart | Source: TradingView\n\nThe daily chart shows that ETH price has some of the most bullish technicals today. It has flipped the important resistance at $2,461 into a support level. \n\nThe coin has continued forming a bullish flag pattern, which is made up of a vertical line and a horizontal channel. This pattern normally leads to more gains over time. \n\nAt the same time, it has formed a golden cross pattern, which happens when the 50-day and 200-day moving averages cross each other. It remains above the Supertrend indicator. \n\nTherefore, there is a likelihood that the coin will have a strong bullish breakout, potentially to the psychological level of $3,000. Such a move will drive the value of BitMine and SharpLink’s Ethereum holdings to $17.8 billion and $2.6 billion, respectively.\n\nIt also means that their staking revenue will continue rising. Assuming that Ethereum averages $3,000, it means that BitMine will make over $480 million in annual revenue. SharpLink would make over $70 million.\n\nRead Also:\n\nOpenAI Cash Burn to Hit $280 Billion by 2030 as Anthropic Profit Surges\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'fa189120b7da6bedcdedfadbfc86ae8706a6450e','2026-09-20 18:45:33','2026-09-20 19:26:43.895875',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 18:45:33');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(456,'alpaca:61885837','benzinga','2026-09-20 19:47:45','Bessent Meets Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng Ahead of High-Stakes Trump-Xi Summit','Bessent and China’s He Lifeng met in New York ahead of the Trump-Xi summit, focusing on AI, tariffs, rare earths and trade tensions.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/politics/26/09/61885837/bessent-meets-chinese-vice-premier-he-lifeng-ahead-of-high-stakes-trump-xi-summit','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-20 20:26:55.580927','partnership','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'meeting could lead to discussions on trade but no immediate impact on NVDA',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-21 20:30:55.341958','2026-09-20 20:26:51.419626','61885837',replace('Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent on Sunday met with Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng in New York City before the anticipated summit between President Donald Trump and President Xi Jinping.\n\nThe discussions are set to address key economic issues, including artificial intelligence, tariffs, and rare earths.\n\nBessent Anticipates ‘Focused, Fulsome’ Talks\n\nBessent shared on X that these talks are crucial for setting the stage for the upcoming summit in Washington, D.C., on September 24. He emphasized the importance of these discussions in advancing U.S. economic interests and delivering results for the American people.\n\nIn New York City, Vice Premier He Lifeng and I are continuing our discussions on the U.S.-China economic and trade relationship ahead of @POTUS’ historic summit with President Xi in Washington. These talks help lay the groundwork for President Trump to advance America’s economic… pic.twitter.com/phmF11Aoxi— Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent (@SecScottBessent) September 20, 2026 \n\nBefore the meeting at JPMorgan Chase & Co. (NYSE:JPM), Bessent expressed his anticipation for "focused, fulsome and constructive talks" that would pave the way for the summit, according to a CNBC report. The meeting precedes Xi’s significant visit to Washington, marking his first during Trump’s second term.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: Tesla Vehicles Maintain Nearly 19% Junk Title Rate Across Age Groups, VIN Analysis Shows\n\nThe meeting also occurs amid ongoing debates in Washington over AI safety and national security, with the Trump administration advocating for voluntary safeguards. The report stated that notable figures like JPMorgan CEO Jamie Dimon and Citigroup Inc. (NYSE:C) chief Jane Fraser are expected at a state dinner during Xi’s visit.\n\nPrecursor to Trump-Xi Summit\n\nThe meeting between Bessent and He Lifeng is a precursor to the high-stakes summit between Trump and Xi, which comes amid heightened tensions over technology and trade. Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang is reportedly expected to attend a state dinner with Trump and Xi, highlighting the significance of tech discussions during the summit.\n\nAdditionally, China’s top newspaper has accused the U.S. of “naked double standards” in AI, emphasizing the importance of AI as a new domain for human development. This underscores the critical nature of AI discussions between the two nations.\n\nFurthermore, President Trump has announced plans to appoint a new AI adviser and establish an “AI force,” indicating the administration’s focus on AI as a strategic priority.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin, Zcash, Hyperliquid in Focus as Industry Expert Sees Crypto Nearing a ''Major Turning Point''\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'69cc416cc07eebe87f41528dad1a85e7a0e8fd8d','2026-09-20 19:47:45','2026-09-20 20:26:51.413571',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 19:47:45');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(457,'alpaca:61885803','benzinga','2026-09-20 19:45:08','Top Four Catalysts for the S&P 500 and Dow Jones This Week','Here are the top four catalysts for the S&amp;P 500 and Dow Jones indices this week, including the upcoming XI-Trump meeting.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61885803/top-4-catalysts-for-the-sp-500-and-dow-jones-this-week','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-20 20:26:56.759904','other','neutral',1,2,'weeks',1,'The headline discusses potential market catalysts without confirming any specific impact or event.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-21 20:30:55.341958','2026-09-20 20:26:51.426233','61885803',replace('The S&P; 500 and Dow Jones have traded sideways for the past few weeks, hovering just below their record highs. Both indexes have shown only muted reactions to recent catalysts, including corporate earnings and last week’s Federal Reserve rate decision. This article covers the key stock market news to watch this week.\n\nUS Stocks to React to Trump-Xi Meeting\n\nPresident Donald Trump will host Xi Jinping, his Chinese counterpart, this week. The two sides will discuss some important issues, including artificial intelligence (AI), trade, and the ongoing wars between the US and Iran and between Ukraine and Russia. \n\nThis is an important meeting that may have some major implications on the stock market. For example, Xi Jinping may make some announcements on the 200-jet Boeing (NYSE:BA) order that was discussed during Trump’s visit to Beijing. A breakthrough on the ongoing US-Iran war may also boost the stock market. \n\nThe two sides may also discuss the AI industry as safety issues remain. Also, the discussion may include the ability for Nvidia (NASDAQ:NVDA) to ship more chips to China.\n\nKey Corporate Earnings This Week\n\nThe S&P; 500 and Dow Jones will react mildly to some important earnings that will come out this week. Costco Wholesale (NASDAQ:COST), the giant American retail group, will be the main company to watch when it releases its results on Thursday. These numbers will provide more information on the health of US consumers. \n\nThe other top companies that will release their numbers this week are Darden Restaurant, TD Synnex, AutoZone, Cintas, Paychex, and General Mills. While all these companies are big ones, their impact on the stock market in general will be limited.\n\nInstead, investors are waiting for the next earnings season to start. A FactSet (NYSE:FDS) report estimates that third-quarter earnings growth will be nearly 30%.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAltcoin Season Index Nears 50 as Crypto Fear and Greed Index Jumps\n\nBond Market Jitters and US Macro Data\n\nThe Dow Jones and S&P; 500 indices reacted mildly to last week’s Federal Reserve decision, in which officials decided to hike interest rates for the first time this year. Officials also hinted that they will hike again this year to combat the rising inflation. \n\nThe stock market will react to any new developments in the bond market. Bond yields have been in a strong upward trend this month, with the ten-year hovering above 5%. A continued surge in bond yields will negatively impact the stock market. \n\nIn line with this, there will be some notable macro numbers from the US, including the flash manufacturing and services PMI and durable goods data. \n\nUS-Iran, Saudi Arabia-Houthi, Russia-Ukraine Wars\n\nGeopolitics will have an impact on the US stock market. There are signs of escalation across different theatres. Ukraine bombarded Russia with the biggest drone strikes, while Houthis attacked Riyadh Airport. Iran continued to attack ships attempting to cross the Strait of Hormuz. President Trump also ended his trip to Camp David early. \n\nAn escalation will likely lead to higher crude oil prices, which will lead to higher inflation. A higher inflation environment, on the other hand, will have an impact on the Federal Reserve interest rates.\n\nRead Also:\n\nOpenAI Cash Burn to Hit $280 Billion by 2030 as Anthropic Profit Surges\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'3b6fe1b7d92aaa4e619ef0f9de55111e64dc8402','2026-09-20 19:45:08','2026-09-20 20:26:51.413571',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 19:45:08');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(458,'alpaca:61885915','benzinga','2026-09-20 20:45:54','Nvidia Stock Keeps Failing to Retest Its Record High as Headwinds Rise','Nvidia stock has slumped and is struggling to retest its all-time high as it faces some major technical and fundamental headwinds.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61885915/nvidia-stock-keeps-failing-to-retest-its-record-high-as-headwinds-rise','["AMZN", "MSFT", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-20 21:27:03.062861','other','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'The stock is currently struggling and facing significant challenges.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "MSFT": 498.48, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-21 21:31:03.991393','2026-09-20 21:26:59.789978','61885915',replace('Nvidia (NASDAQ:NVDA) has spent the past few months trying to retest its all-time high, but every attempt has failed as the company contends with significant headwinds. The technical picture also suggests that a successful retest will take time.\n\nNvidia is Contending With Some Major Headwinds\n\nJensen Huang’s Nvidia is contending with some major headwinds. One of them is that there is a growing call for the AI development to slow down, a move that would affect its business. Huang, together with President Donald Trump, has insisted that the AI industry needs to continue growing to give the US a lead against China. \n\nConcerns about the data center industry are also leading to project delays or cancellations. A good example of this is Project Jupiter, which is being built by Oracle (NASDAQ:ORCL) in a 14,000-acre piece of land in New Mexico. The project is facing delays amid environmental concerns.\n\nThe company is also contending with the rising competition in the GPU industry. OpenAI has developed its Jalapeno chip in a collaboration with Broadcom (NASDAQ:AVGO). In a statement, Sam Altman has said that the chip is beating those made by Nvidia in some metrics.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Price Stabilizes Above $80,000 as ETF Inflows Jump, Bullish Patterns Form\n\nOther top Nvidia clients like Microsoft (NASDAQ:MSFT), Meta Platforms (NASDAQ:MSFT), and Amazon (NASDAQ:AMZN) are also building their own chips. This is notable since these big-tech companies account for about 50% of its revenue. \n\nSmaller companies like SambaNova, Euclyd, and Etched have also received millions of dollars in investments to challenge Nvidia. Samsung Electronics invested in Euclyd, a Dutch company, last week.\n\nNvidia stock is also struggling as some of the companies it has invested in retreat. This includes neocloud companies like CoreWeave, Nebius, and IREN, which have all slipped into a bear market. \n\nOn the positive side, Nvidia’s growth continues despite these challenges. Its latest results showed that second-quarter revenue more than doubled, and management expects revenue to grow by more than 77% in the next financial year.\n\nThe company may also benefit from the upcoming Trump-Xi meeting in Washington. A deal for the company to sell its most advanced chips to China would lead to faster revenue growth. \n\nNvidia is also trading at bargain prices. It trades at a forward price-to-earnings ratio of 23, lower than the five-year average of 58.\n\nNvidia Stock Has Formed a Break-and-Retest Pattern\n\nNVDA stock chart | Source: TradingView\n\nThe daily chart shows that NVDA stock has formed a risky pattern that may lead to more downside in the near term. It formed a rising wedge pattern, which is made up of two ascending and converging trendlines. This pattern normally leads to a strong bearish breakout.\n\nNotably, the stock has retested the lower side of this pattern, confirming a break-and-retest pattern. A retest usually confirms a bearish breakout. The Relative Strength Index (RSI) has also formed a bearish divergence pattern. \n\nTherefore, there is a risk that the stock will resume the downward trend, potentially to this month’s low of $209. \n\nRead Also:\n\nCrude Oil Price Rises on Hyperliquid as Houthi Hits Riyadh Airport\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'8f8c3176681acf8c3d13735a1118116aad40bd00','2026-09-20 20:45:54','2026-09-20 21:26:59.784010',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 20:45:54');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(459,'alpaca:61885903','benzinga','2026-09-20 20:41:10','Shorts Prevail as Oklo and NuScale Stocks Dive as SMR Risks Rise','Oklo and NuScale stocks have plunged this year, with short sellers making billions of dollars as risks in the SMR industry rise.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61885903/shorts-prevail-as-oklo-and-nuscale-stocks-dive-as-smr-risks-rise','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-20 21:27:04.469563','other','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'The decline in stocks indicates increasing risk perception in the SMR industry.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-21 21:31:03.991393','2026-09-20 21:26:59.792998','61885903',replace('Top small modular reactor (SMR) stocks have fallen sharply this year, handing short sellers substantial gains. Oklo (NYSE:OKLO) has dropped 49% year-to-date and now trades 80% below its record high. NuScale Power Corporation (NYSE:SMR) has fared similarly, losing 43% this year and sitting 86% below its peak.\n\nOklo and NuScale Have Slumped as SMR Risks Remain\n\nThe ongoing retreat has benefited short sellers. Oklo has a short interest of 17%, while NuScale has 16%, a sign that many investors expect them to keep falling in the coming months. In a recent report, the FT estimated that these short sellers had made over $2 billion this year, while their market capitalizations have fallen by over $30 billion. \n\nThere are several reasons why these stocks have slumped this year. The most notable is the fact that Oklo, which is backed by Sam Altman, and NuScale are not yet making money. Instead, they are doing their R&D; and hoping that their technology will become widespread, especially as the AI boom continues. \n\nRead Also:\n\nMicron Stock Eyes a Big Move as Closely Watched Q4 Earnings Report Nears\n\nThe fact that they are pre-revenue has pushed them to dilute their investors substantially. In August, the company filed to raise $750 million through share sales. Its outstanding shares have jumped to 410 million from just 23 million in 2021. \n\nOklo has done the same, with management filing to raise $1 billion in a share sale. Its outstanding shares have soared to 185 million from 122 million in 2024. This dilution will likely continue as the companies are too far away from profitability. For one, the companies are experience a shortage of high-assay low-enriched uranium, which is expected to come online in the second half of 2028.\n\nWyckoff Theory Explains Why Oklo and NuScale are Slumping\n\nOklo vs NuScale stocks chart | Source: TradingView\n\nTraditional theories like Wyckoff also explain why the stocks are in a freefall. This theory, which has been around for over 100 years. \n\nThe theory identifies the four stages that assets go through: accumulation, markup, distribution, and markdown. These stocks remained in the accumulation stage in 2024 and then surged in 2025. This rally happened after several deals, including a large one between Oklo and Meta Platforms (NASDAQ:META). \n\nThe two stocks have now moved to the markdown phase, which is characterized by panic selling. \n\nStill, shorting these companies carries risk, as they are prime candidates for short squeezes. A short squeeze occurs when a heavily shorted stock rallies sharply, forcing short sellers to buy back shares to limit their losses, which in turn pushes the price even higher.\n\nRead Also:\n\nVOO & Chill: Why Vanguard’s S&P; 500 ETF is Beating SPY and IVV\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'1c1ea207e3bc3362f9248fc4479cb95be9487440','2026-09-20 20:41:10','2026-09-20 21:26:59.784010',1,NULL,'2026-09-20 20:41:10');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(460,'alpaca:61886452','benzinga','2026-09-21 02:02:54','Bitcoin Touches $82,000, Ethereum, XRP, Dogecoin Also Gain Amid Tokenization Push by SEC: Analyst Confirms ''Breakout'' in This Major Coin','Leading cryptocurrencies rallied on Sunday, September 20, as risk appetite surged following the SEC’s push to introduce tokenized-stock products in the U.S.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61886452/bitcoin-ethereum-xrp-dogecoin-crypto-sec-tokenization','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "ETH/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-21 02:27:22.908232','macro','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst comments on market movement related to SEC initiatives.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "SOL/USD": 101.29, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 10.91}, "DOGE/USD": {"60m": 12.385, "1d": 22.122}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 11.406}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": 13.672, "1d": 16.128}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 13.3, "1d": 16.781}}','2026-09-22 02:31:25.072939','2026-09-21 02:27:18.975986','61886452',replace('Leading cryptocurrencies rallied on Sunday as risk appetite surged amid the Securities and Exchange Commission’s push to introduce tokenized-stock products.Cryptocurrency24-Hour Gains +/-Price (Recorded at 9:23 p.m. EDT)Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC)+0.93%$81,912.30Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH)               +2.68%$2,693.75XRP (CRYPTO: XRP)                         +2.03%$1.42Solana (CRYPTO: SOL)                         +2.18%$112.77Dogecoin (CRYPTO: DOGE)             +2.15%$0.08899Crypto Market RalliesBitcoin spiked late evening, briefly surpassing $82,000 before pulling back. Similarly, Ethereum surged past $2,700, supported by a 41% jump in 24-hour volume.Sentiment has improved after the SEC introduced a regulatory pathway allowing certain tokenized U.S. stocks to trade on blockchains.Nearly $400 million in cryptocurrency positions were liquidated over the past 24 hours, with shorts taking the heaviest losses, according to Coinglass data.Bitcoin’s open interest rose 0.90% over the last 24 hours and nearly 10% over the week. On Binance, both retail and whale derivatives traders stayed neutral on the apex cryptocurrency.“Greed” sentiment returned to the market, according to the Crypto Fear & Greed Index.Top Gainers (24 Hours) Cryptocurrency (Market Cap>$100 M)Gains +/-Price (Recorded at 9:23 p.m. EDT)Backack (BP)      +39.06%    $0.8662STONK (STONK)                   +28.83%    $0.3622Bitway (BTW)              +24.63%    $0.7419The global cryptocurrency market capitalization stood at $2.81 trillion, up 1.12% over the last 24 hours.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Price Stabilizes Above $80,000 as ETF Inflows Jump, Bullish Patterns Form\n\nStock Futures SpikeStock futures lifted overnight on Sunday. The Dow Jones Industrial Average Futures rose 115 points, or 0.22%, as of 8:44 p.m. EDT. S&P; 500 futures were up 0.34%, while Nasdaq 100 Futures added 0.53%.Middle East tensions escalated as Yemen-based Houthis targeted a key Saudi Arabian airport and a fuel depot belonging to Saudi Aramco.Meanwhile, the State Department warned Americans to reconsider travel to and through the Middle East and “exercise increased caution.”Bitcoin Headed Higher?Killa, a widely followed cryptocurrency analyst and trader, said they’re targeting Bitcoin at $89,070 and advised against shorting near $81,000“I’m not interested in shorting the same $81,000 highs again & again. Compression within an uptrend will always lead to expansion eventually,” the analyst added. “Even if we range here for longer, I’d rather wait for higher prices.”\nI’ll be looking to $BTC at 89,070.I’m not interested in shorting the same 81K highs again & again. Compression within an uptrend will always lead to expansion eventually. It''s simply a matter of when, and I’m not willing to take that risk. Even if we range here for longer,… pic.twitter.com/zxOYiaeZcI— Killa (@KillaXBT) September 20, 2026 \nAli Martinez, another well-known chartist and on-chain researcher, noted Ethereum’s breakout above $2,560 with a clean retest as support.“With the breakout holding, I’m watching $2,760 as the next major target,” the analyst added.\nETHEREUM BREAKOUT CONFIRMED$ETH broke above $2,560, successfully retested it as support, and is now pushing higher.With the breakout holding, I’m watching $2,760 as the next major target. https://t.co/JfsSCIMGZk pic.twitter.com/j1pP0i6H8b— Ali Charts (@alicharts) September 20, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nAltcoin Index Soars, SEC''s Crypto Rules, Bitcoin''s Milestone, Binance''s Zero Tolerance and More: This Week in Crypto\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Marc Bruxelle on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'107b8ec9ccdad53769ac898355c8e2994ebef961','2026-09-21 02:02:54','2026-09-21 02:27:18.971999',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 02:02:54');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(461,'alpaca:61886575','benzinga','2026-09-21 03:24:58','Elizabeth Warren Says ''We Will Win in November'' — Here''s What Crypto Prediction Market Says About Democrats'' Midterm Chances','Sen. Elizabeth Warren expressed optimism on Sunday, September 20, that Democrats would win the midterms in November despite the growing influence of &#34;dark money.&#34;','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61886575/elizabeth-warren-democrats-midterm-chances-crypto-prediction-market','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 04:27:32.427245','other','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'The statement reflects a political opinion rather than direct market impact.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 10.91}}','2026-09-22 03:31:34.325181','2026-09-21 04:27:28.526451','61886575',replace('Sen. Elizabeth Warren (D-Mass.) expressed optimism on Sunday that Democrats would win the November midterms despite the growing influence of “dark money.”Anonymous Money Entering Elections?Warren said in an X post that dark money groups have spent “record sums” in this year’s elections.Roughly $1 billion in anonymous funds has shaped 2026 races, according to a New York Times analysis of ad data, filings and tax records. The report found that secret funding has influenced or is expected to influence “every major primary and battleground race.”\nDark money groups are pouring record sums into our elections.But the 2026 primaries have shown that when people organize and show up, billionaires don’t get to decide who wins. Grassroots power still matters. And we will in November.— Elizabeth Warren (@ewarren) September 20, 2026 \n‘We Will Win in November’Warren said that “grassroots” progressive candidates have succeeded despite the powerful influence of wealthy donors.Notably, Abdul El-Sayed won Michigan’s Senate primary by narrowly defeating Rep. Haley Stevens (D-MI) by less than one percentage point. El-Sayed’s “grassroots” campaign reportedly drove record turnout in the Democratic primary, while other reports suggested he overcame more than $60 million in opposition spending and assembled a 12,000-strong volunteer network.“Grassroots power still matters. And we will in November,” Warren said.The senior Democrat had earlier targeted groups tied to AI, cryptocurrency and the American Israel Public Affairs Committee for spending millions to influence the selection of congressional representatives.\n\nRead Also:\n\nElizabeth Warren Demands Congress Stop ''Drawn-Out Discussions'' on AI and Pass ''Meaningful Regulations'' to Protect People\n\nWhat Do Crypto Punters Think?Meanwhile, Polygon (CRYPTO: POL)-based Polymarket currently prices in a 61% chance that the Dems take control of both the House and Senate, up from 49% a month ago.Source: PolymarketDemocrats were the frontrunners to take control of the House, with 91% odds. The Senate race was closer, with the blue party holding a 61% chance of reclaiming control.The Republicans currently controls both the House and the Senate. The midterm elections are scheduled for Nov. 3.\n\nRead Also:\n\nElizabeth Warren Calls Kevin Warsh a ''Sock Puppet'' After Trump Claims He Told Him How to Vote for a Rate Hike: Peter Schiff Asks If It''s ''Another Lie''\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Bryan J. Scrafford on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'7ce864ca53984abf04e51f32cbc50de40ab4ef1c','2026-09-21 03:24:58','2026-09-21 04:27:28.518922',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 03:24:58');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(462,'alpaca:61886672','benzinga','2026-09-21 04:27:39','Bitcoin, Dogecoin Rose, but This Obscure AI Token Delivered 255% Weekly Gain Last Week','Momentum shifted back into the cryptocurrency market last week, with lesser-known tokens delivering powerful returns.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61886672/bitcoin-dogecoin-obscure-ai-token-255-percent-weekly-gain','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "ETH/USD", "XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-21 05:27:39.369891','other','neutral',1,3,'days',1,'The headline reports on market performance without making predictions.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 10.91}, "DOGE/USD": {"60m": 14.366}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 11.406}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 14.761}}','2026-09-22 04:31:42.553850','2026-09-21 05:27:35.458710','61886672',replace('Momentum shifted back into the cryptocurrency market last week, with lesser-known tokens delivering powerful returns.\n\nAkedo Makes Heads Turn\n\nAkedo (AKE), a BNB Chain (CRYPTO: BNB) token, topped the charts after surging more than 250%. The coin surged to an all-time high of $0.1467 on Sunday but has since pulled back sharply. \n\nAKE is the utility token of Akedo, a multi-agent AI framework designed to turn text prompts into playable video games. The token powers game creation, staking, governance and provides liquidity for new projects.\n\nNotably, 2.11 billion AKE tokens, or 2.11% of the 100 billion total supply, are scheduled to be unlocked on Monday, according to DropsTab, potentially adding inflationary pressure.\n\nCryptocurrency7-Day Gains +/-Price (Recorded at 9:30 p.m. EDT)Akedo+255.40%$0.05281NEAR Protocol               +81.80%$1,731.49Arbitrum                        +59.90%$0.219\n\nNEAR (CRYPTO: NEAR), the token powering the AI-native blockchain, NEAR Protocol, surged more than 80% to secure the second spot. Arbitrum (CRYPTO: ARB), the native token of Ethereum’s (CRYPTO: ETH) Layer 2, rallied nearly 60%.\n\nPrivacy-based token Zcash (CRYPTO: ZEC) also extended its bull run, gaining 41% over the week.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Price Stabilizes Above $80,000 as ETF Inflows Jump, Bullish Patterns Form\n\nHits and Misses\n\nMarket heavyweights, including Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) and Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH), rose 5.5% and 6.8%, respectively, last week. Meme giant Dogecoin (CRYPTO: DOGE) rallied 6%.\n\nIt was a bittersweet week for cryptocurrencies. While the much-anticipated CLARITY Act failed to clear a key Senate vote, SEC efforts to create a regulatory pathway for trading tokenized U.S. stocks cheered the market.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAltcoin Index Soars, SEC''s Crypto Rules, Bitcoin''s Milestone, Binance''s Zero Tolerance and More: This Week in Crypto\n\nPhoto: Sebastian Duda on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'28600567a9d52d11d7cea04aacf16b46e143d40c','2026-09-21 04:27:39','2026-09-21 05:27:35.453801',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 04:27:39');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(463,'alpaca:61886941','benzinga','2026-09-21 05:58:17','Stock Market: Will S&P 500 Open Up or Down Today?','Will S&amp;P 500 open higher? Polymarket odds reach 81% as Wall Street digests cooling oil prices, Trump&#39;s Iran warnings, and retail earnings.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61886941/stock-market-will-sp-500-open-up-or-down-today-41','["QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-21 06:27:47.063983','other','neutral',1,2,'hours',1,'The headline poses a speculative question about market movements.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-22 06:32:00.429116','2026-09-21 06:27:42.403198','61886941',replace('U.S. stock futures are trending higher early Monday as investors digest a stark warning from President Donald Trump to Iran alongside cooling crude oil prices, while looking ahead to a week of key consumer retail earnings.\n\nThe Polymarket (CRYPTO: POL) crowd is heavily bullish for the Sept. 21 trading session. The “S&P; 500 (SPX) Up or Down on September 21?” contract currently reflects an 81% chance of a higher open. \n\nWhy That Number Matters\n\nTraders are navigating a mix of geopolitical escalations, AI sector debates, and a busy week of economic insights:\n\nPositive Index Futures: Equity futures point to a green open across major benchmarks. Dow Jones futures rose 0.35%. S&P; 500 futures advanced 0.41%. Nasdaq 100 futures gained 0.56%, and Russell 2000 futures ticked up 0.34%.\n\nGeopolitics & Energy: President Trump warned Iran of severe economic consequences or the destruction of its leadership if Tehran refuses to reach a deal. Iran’s military responded by threatening sustained retaliation against U.S. bases. The confrontation widened over the weekend with Houthi missile and drone strikes on sensitive targets in Riyadh. Despite this, oil prices retreated; Brent crude dropped to $102.05 a barrel, down 1.75%, and WTI crude fell to $94.33 by 1.82%.\n\nAI Developments: Over the weekend, President Trump polled the public on renaming artificial intelligence, suggesting terms like “Superior Intelligence,” and proposed a new “AI Force” and an “AI Czar” to monitor the industry. This comes as the U.S. and China prepare for bilateral discussions covering AI safety, with China recently accusing the U.S. of applying “naked double standards” on AI model distillation.\n\nThe Bull Case and Market Outlook\n\nDespite the recent wave of central bank rate hikes, the global stock bull market remains remarkably resilient, according to Ed Yardeni. “Central banks in the US, Europe, and Japan all raised their policy rates over the last two weeks,” yet “neither development has broken the global stock bull market, as earnings forecasts keep getting marked up,” he said.\n\nHow the Previous Bet Played Out\n\nThe Sept. 18 Polymarket contract resolved “Up,” recording $94,541 in total trading volume.\n\nOn Friday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed higher. SPY rose 0.13% to $761.69, while QQQ rose 0.63% to $721.45. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), ended 0.25% lower at $515.88.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBessent Proposes US-China AI Alert System Ahead of Trump-Xi Summit: ‘We Want a Shared Vision’\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'ee60d47a018e56c069a152b1210ae83ee9dd071b','2026-09-21 05:58:17','2026-09-21 06:27:42.395238',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 05:58:17');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(464,'alpaca:61886896','benzinga','2026-09-21 05:52:19','Michael Saylor Says, ''A Little More Orange'': Will Strategy Report BTC Purchases After Hitting Pause for 3 Weeks?','Strategy Inc. Chair Michael Saylor indicated on Sunday, September 20, that the firm could announce Bitcoin purchases, following the cryptocurrency’s upward momentum last week.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61886896/michael-saylor-strategy-bitcoin-purchases-three-week-pause','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 06:27:48.890606','rumour','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'Speculation on potential BTC purchases based on Saylor''s comments.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 12.289}}','2026-09-22 06:32:00.429116','2026-09-21 06:27:42.406204','61886896',replace('Strategy Inc. (NASDAQ:MSTR) Chair Michael Saylor indicated on Sunday that the firm could announce fresh Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) purchases, following the cryptocurrency’s upward momentum last week.\n\nSaylor Getting Orange-Pilled?\n\nSaylor posted Strategy’s Bitcoin accumulation chart on X, where orange circles mark each purchase.\n\n“A good time to add more dots," Saylor wrote. These weekend posts usually came before the purchase disclosures on the following Monday.\n\nHowever, that hasn’t been the case lately. From late June through early August, Strategy halted new Bitcoin purchases and sold 6,916 BTC to bolster its cash reserves.\n\nA little more orange. pic.twitter.com/Z3n9jDAEpn— Michael Saylor (@saylor) September 20, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nElizabeth Warren Says ''We Will Win in November'' — Here''s What Crypto Prediction Market Says About Democrats'' Midterm Chances\n\nWill the Lull End?\n\nThe company ended the two-month buying drought on Aug. 31, acquiring 4,603 BTC for $370 million at an average price of $80,382 per coin. However, no further acquisitions have been reported since.\n\nAs of this writing, Strategy holds 845,050 BTC, worth nearly $69 billion. The company has nearly $9 billion in unrealized losses on its Bitcoin holdings. The firm reported unrealized gains exceeding $5 billion on its BTC stash.\n\nBitcoin rose over 5% last week as the SEC’s push to build a regulatory framework for cryptocurrency, including tokenized U.S. stocks, outweighed the CLARITY Act’s failure.\n\nPrice Action: At the time of writing, BTC was exchanging hands at $81,275.32, up 1.13% in the last 24 hours, according to data from Benzinga Pro.\n\nStrategy shares closed 16.39% higher at $153.92 during Friday’s regular trading session. According to Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings, the stock shows a stronger price trend in the short- and medium-term but lags over the long term.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nPhoto: Hi my name is Jacco on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'5b44c65c562cbdf019e35a50e0c4b3dfbbade293','2026-09-21 05:52:19','2026-09-21 06:27:42.395238',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 05:52:19');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(465,'alpaca:61886877','benzinga','2026-09-21 05:46:46','Tesla Reopens Roadster Reservations Ahead of Oct. 1 Reveal: Here’s What You Need to Know','Tesla reopens Roadster reservations ahead of its Oct. 1 launch, requiring $5,000 upfront plus $45,000 by wire.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61886877/tesla-reopens-roadster-reservations-ahead-of-oct-1-reveal-heres-what-you-need-to-know','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 06:27:49.950599','product','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Reopening reservations indicates strong demand and upcoming product launch.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-22 06:32:00.429116','2026-09-21 06:27:42.408916','61886877',replace('Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) has reopened reservations for its long-delayed next-generation Roadster, asking prospective buyers for a $50,000 payment ahead of the electric sports car’s as the Elon Musk-led automaker gears up for an October 1st debut.\n\n$5,000 Initial Payment\n\nOn Saturday, the automaker’s official website showed a reserve now tab on the Roadster page. Tesla says that the vehicle would require an initial $5,000 credit card payment, which would be fully refundable, following which interested buyers would be required to pay an additional $45,000 via wire transfer within 10 days of the initial $5,000 payment.\n\nRead Also:\n\nThis Week in TSLA: Elon Musk Touts Roadster Debut, Fuels SpaceX Merger Talks and More\n\n“Reservations are not final until the wire transfer payment is received,” Tesla said. In the Roadster terms and conditions, Tesla also says that it can only provide an estimated purchase price of the Roadster. “We are still working on what options, features and hardware the vehicle will have and so cannot confirm the exact price just yet,” Tesla said.\n\nThe automaker also said that upon reservation, buyers would be invited by Tesla to configure their vehicles as the production of the vehicle nears. Tesla said buyers will receive an “order agreement” from the company. “You will be issuedan updated Order Agreement whenever you or we make changes to your configuration,” Tesla said.\n\nAs far as refunds or cancellations are concerned, Tesla says that reservations can be cancelled by the buyer or Tesla as long as there is no “Motor Vehicle Purchase Agreement” between the two parties. Tesla said that it will issue a full refund in the event of a cancellation.\n\nExcitement is Guaranteed, Says Elon Musk\n\nLast week, Musk, during an appearance on the All-In Podcast, said that the Roadster’s debut would need to have an audience present to verify that the demo is not AI-generated. “Success is not guaranteed, but excitement is,” Musk said during his appearance.\n\nThe Roadster has been an elusive vehicle in the automotive industry, with tech leaders like OpenAI’s Sam Altman, as well as influencers like Marques Brownlee, aka MKBHD, having made reservations for the vehicle at some point.\n\nAccording to Benzinga Edge Rankings, Tesla scores moderately on the Growth and Quality metrics, but offers poor Value and Momentum. TSLA also fails to provide a favorable price trend in the Medium and Long term.\n\nPrice Action: TSLA shares grew 0.69% to $366.79 during overnight trading.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: Tesla Vehicles Maintain Nearly 19% Junk Title Rate Across Age Groups, VIN Analysis Shows\n\nCheck out more of Benzinga’s Future Of Mobility coverage by following this link.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'55e724537c7379aa5b9931f6fb2dbe2e8276ca64','2026-09-21 05:46:46','2026-09-21 06:27:42.395238',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 05:46:46');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(466,'alpaca:61887328','benzinga','2026-09-21 06:54:37','Jensen Huang Isn''t ''Afraid'' of Paying $8 Billion in California''s Billionaire Tax: Nvidia CEO Says This Is What Scares Him Instead',replace('Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang says he would view paying billions of dollars in additional taxes as a privilege as California considers a one-time levy on the state’s wealthiest residents.\n\n\n\nHuang Says $8','\n',char(10)),'https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61887328/jensen-huang-nvidia-8-billion-california-billionaire-tax-what-scares-him','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 07:27:57.391932','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'CEO''s comments reflect a personal opinion on taxation.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-22 07:32:04.410994','2026-09-21 07:27:53.223002','61887328',replace('Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang says he would view paying billions of dollars in additional taxes as a privilege as California considers a one-time levy on the state’s wealthiest residents.\n\nHuang Says $8 Billion Tax Bill Would Be A Privilege\n\nIn an interview with CBS News correspondent Jo Ling Kent, Huang said he would not object to paying billions more in taxes if California voters approve the proposed billionaires’ tax this fall.\n\nThe measure would impose a one-time 5% tax on Californians with a net worth of at least $1 billion.\n\nHuang, whose fortune is estimated at $184 billion, said paying as much as $8 billion over five years would not bother him.\n\n"The fact that I can afford to pay $8 billion in taxes over five years is a privilege," Huang said. "I feel it’s a privilege. It’s a responsibility. And nothing would give me more joy than to be able to pay even more taxes."\n\nHuang also offered a humorous take on his enormous fortune.\n\n"I’m not afraid of paying taxes — I’m just afraid of being poor," he said.\n\nJensen Huang could pay ~$8B in taxes over next 5 years and says "I’m not afraid of paying taxes. I’m just afraid of being poor."That mindset also shows up in how $NVDA pays people where he says "I try to pay people as much as possible." pic.twitter.com/Cn2DhPHBjn— Shay Boloor (@StockSavvyShay) September 20, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang Rejects Calls to Slow Down AI Development: ‘We Are Going to Go as Fast We Can, But…''\n\nNvidia CEO Calls Himself ‘the Ultimate American Dream’\n\nHuang described himself as "the ultimate American dream," crediting the U.S. with providing the educational and professional opportunities that helped him become an entrepreneur.\n\nThe Nvidia CEO also recalled his early career, saying he worked as a dishwasher at Denny’s before eventually co-founding the chipmaker.\n\n"I was just really, really focused on doing dishes like no dishwasher ever did dishes," Huang said, describing how far his career has taken him from those early days.\n\nHuang’s Journey From Nvidia Co-Founder to AI Chip Leader\n\nHuang co-founded Nvidia in 1993 and has served as its CEO and president ever since. He owns roughly 4% of the company, which went public in 1999.\n\nBorn in Taiwan, Huang moved to Thailand as a child before his family sent him and his brother to the U.S. amid civil unrest.\n\nUnder Huang’s leadership, Nvidia’s GPUs evolved from powering video games to driving the AI boom, pushing the company’s market value past $5 trillion in 2025.\n\nPrice Action: Nvidia shares ended 1.34% higher at $222.27 on Friday, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nAccording to Benzinga Edge Rankings, Nvidia ranks in the 98th percentile for Growth, with positive short-, medium- and long-term price trends.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nJensen Huang Says AI Is a ''Five-Layer Cake.'' Nvidia Is Just One Slice\n\nPhoto: jamesonwu1972 from Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'abfd4f70eb530b75a1e060c44ebfd32c47f81ec6','2026-09-21 06:54:37','2026-09-21 07:27:53.208984',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 06:54:37');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(467,'alpaca:61887725','benzinga','2026-09-21 07:32:59','Will Howie Buffett Keep Berkshire Ahead of the S&P 500? What Retail Investors Need to Know','Warren Buffett is out. As Howie Buffett takes over Berkshire Hathaway, can BRK.B still beat the S&amp;P 500? What retail investors need to know.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/market-summary/26/09/61887725/will-howie-buffett-keep-berkshire-ahead-of-the-sp-500-what-retail-investors-need-to-know','["SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-21 08:28:04.891784','other','neutral',1,2,'weeks',1,'The headline speculates on future performance rather than reporting an event.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-22 08:32:14.341204','2026-09-21 08:28:01.026780','61887725',replace('Warren Buffett has stepped down as chairman of Berkshire Hathaway Inc. (NYSE:BRK) (NYSE:BRK), handing the position to his son, Howie Buffett. As the $1.091 trillion conglomerate completes its leadership transition, retail investors are weighing whether the company can keep beating the S&P; 500.\n\nBRK.B Versus S&P; 500\n\nBerkshire Class B shares have generated an 84.19% return over the past five years, outperforming the S&P; 500 tracker, State Street SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) 72.56% gain. However, short-term performance has lagged, with the stock up 1.42% year-to-date compared to SPY’s 11.70% rise.\n\nStock/ETF1-Month6-MonthsYTD1-Year5-YearsBRK-B1.35%5.22%1.42%3.93%84.19%S&P; 500 Index-0.54%15.48%11.76%15.36%72.58%\n\nRead Also:\n\nWarren Buffett Steps Down as Berkshire''s Chair — Son Howard Takes to Succeed: ''Father Time Always Wins''\n\n‘Uncharted Territory’\n\nHoward Buffett, also known as Howie, 71, assumes the role after serving on the board for 33 years. Finance Professor David Kass observed on social media that the transition ushers in a new era and puts the conglomerate in “uncharted territory.”\n\nBuffett, 96, will remain on the board as chairman emeritus. In his shareholder letter, the billionaire investor accepted the limits of aging, writing, “Father Time always wins.”\n\nHe also clarified the corporate structure: “Greg runs the company; Howard will guard its culture and values – both worth more than anything on our balance sheet.” Buffett further described his son as “a policy the shareholders own and hope never to claim against.”\n\nHowie Buffett’s appointment as chairman ushers in a new era at Berkshire Hathaway, and puts the conglomerate in uncharted territory https://t.co/71LIf9obvJ via @WSJ— David Kass (@DrDavidKass) September 20, 2026 \n\nBerkshire Reshapes Portfolio Under Abel\n\nGreg Abel, who took over as CEO at the end of 2025, is actively reshaping the portfolio. Berkshire’s latest 13F filing revealed a 58% reduction in its Capital One Financial Corp. (NYSE:COF) stake.\n\nConversely, the company expanded its holdings in Alphabet Inc. Class C (NASDAQ:GOOG) by 658%, making the tech giant a top-three investment. Berkshire also initiated a small new position in D.R. Horton Inc. (NYSE:DHI) while fully exiting Constellation Brands Inc. (NYSE:STZ).\n\nInstitutional Moves and Index Fund Strategy\n\nAs Berkshire enters its next chapter, institutional holders are adjusting. The Gates Foundation Trust recently cut its Berkshire position by 14%, shifting $800 million into Home Depot Inc. (NYSE:HD) and FedEx Freight Holding Company Inc. (NYSE:FDXF).\n\nFor retail investors, Warren Buffett’s long-standing advice remains relevant. Buffett has repeatedly recommended low-cost S&P; 500 index funds for investors who don’t want to select individual stocks, such as the Vanguard S&P; 500 ETF (NYSE:VOO), over active stock picking.\n\nInvestors must now decide if Berkshire’s cultural safeguards and new capital strategies will continue to outpace the broader market.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMarjorie Taylor Greene Slams Trump Plan to Turn Arch Into ''Top Grade'' Military Complex: ''Power Hungry Ego Obsessed'' President Will ''Soon Lose Power''\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: paparazzza / Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'5a57b5e49a325a65e88725b6fc6522c7b9f7b5c0','2026-09-21 07:32:59','2026-09-21 08:28:01.008109',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 07:32:59');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(468,'alpaca:61887673','benzinga','2026-09-21 07:28:43','Jason Calacanis Calls Bitcoin a ''Dead Cat'' Which Continues to Bounce—Cathie Wood Argues BTC Has ''Many Lives Ahead''''','Ark Invest CEO Cathie Wood on Saturday, September 19, rebutted the argument that Bitcoin is an outdated and &#34;boring&#34; store of value.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61887673/jason-calacanis-bitcoin-dead-cat-cathie-wood-many-lives-ahead','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 08:28:06.071807','analyst','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'Comments have differing opinions on Bitcoin''s value.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 12.289}}','2026-09-22 07:32:04.410994','2026-09-21 08:28:01.033015','61887673',replace('Ark Invest CEO Cathie Wood on Saturday rebutted the argument that Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) is an outdated and “boring” store of value.\n\n‘No Longer Capturing the Public’s Attention’\n\nIn an X post, Venture capitalist Jason Calacanis argued that 17 years after its creation, Bitcoin lacks strong utility in transactions or smart contracts and is “no longer capturing the public’s imagination.”\n\n“It’s a boring store of value, trusted as that—which is its biggest value,” he added.\n\nCalacanis posted Bitcoin’s 1-year price chart, showing a 30% decline with a recent rebound, and said, “The dead cat continues to bounce.”\n\nBitcoin is not a dead cat, @Jason ! It has many lives ahead. Check out our latest Bitcoin Brainstorm with @bitcoinpark_ focused on the convergence between AI and Bitcoin. https://t.co/4i2ZFyUjAx— Cathie Wood (@CathieDWood) September 19, 2026 \n\nWood’s Defense\n\nWood, a long-time Bitcoin advocate, was far from convinced. \n\n“Bitcoin is not a dead cat, Jason! It has many lives ahead,” the veteran investor stated.\n\nWood also pointed to the latest episode of the Ark Invest-hosted “Bitcoin Brainstorm” podcast, where she discussed the convergence of AI and Bitcoin and noted that advanced AI models can be a double-edged sword for the cryptocurrency.\n\nWood has previously framed Bitcoin as a "wealth insurance policy" that AI-driven growth investments cannot offer.\n\nNotably, Ark Invest cashed out $40 million worth of ARK 21Shares Bitcoin ETF (BATS: ARKB) shares shortly before the CLARITY Act’s legislative defeat last week.\n\nFocused on the convergence between #AI and #Bitcoin, this episode of Bitcoin Brainstorm is one of our best yet with @bitcoinpark_ and @rodroudi. https://t.co/EwHwnQ7NEP— Cathie Wood (@CathieDWood) September 19, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nEthereum Treasury Stocks SharpLink and BitMine Eye Further Upside as ETH Targets $3,000 Rebound\n\nSaylor, Armstrong Also Push Back\n\nWood wasn’t the only one opposing Calacanis’ arguments. Strategy Inc. (NASDAQ:MSTR) founder Michael Saylor emphasized Bitcoin’s evolution since 2011 into an asset with a market capitalization of more than $1.6 trillion.\n\n“Preserving wealth across generations is a bigger ambition than entertaining a dinner party,” Saylor added.\n\nJason, you’ve watched Bitcoin grow since 2011. It’s now a $1.6 trillion success and the world’s most valuable digital asset. Digital Capital is the killer app. Preserving wealth across generations is a bigger ambition than entertaining a dinner party. The orange tie stays.— Michael Saylor (@saylor) September 18, 2026 \n\nCoinbase Global Inc. (NASDAQ:CEO) CEO Brian Armstrong deemed Bitcoin as “Digital Gold,” which is here to stay.\n\nIt''s digital gold – here to stay, and as important as ever.— Brian Armstrong (@brian_armstrong) September 19, 2026 \n\nPrice Action: At the time of writing, BTC was exchanging hands at $81,562, up 1.40% in the last 24 hours, according to data from Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin, Zcash, Hyperliquid in Focus as Industry Expert Sees Crypto Nearing a ''Major Turning Point''\n\nPhoto: Hi my name is Jacco on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'3223213e06b61cd79715cf50efe7a29255f02a56','2026-09-21 07:28:43','2026-09-21 08:28:01.008109',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 07:28:43');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(469,'alpaca:61888716','benzinga','2026-09-21 09:22:39','Paramount Reportedly Nears California AG Deal to Clear WBD Merger Hurdle, Weighs $1.5 Billion Investment — PSKY, WBD Surge Over 7% (UPDATED)','Paramount Skydance considers a $1.5 billion California investment as states seek stronger job and editorial protections for its WBD deal.','https://www.benzinga.com/m-a/26/09/61888716/paramount-nears-california-ag-deal-to-clear-wbd-merger-hurdle-weighs-1-5-billion-investment-as-ny-connecticut-seek-more-concessions','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-21 11:28:47.279742','mna','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'The reported deal is expected to help clear merger hurdles.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18}','{}','2026-09-22 09:32:24.517360','2026-09-21 09:28:10.974132','61888716',replace('Editor’s Note: This story has been updated to reflect the movement in shares of Paramount Skydance and Warner Bros. Discovery.\n\nParamount Skydance Corp. (NASDAQ:PSKY) is reportedly in advanced settlement talks with California’s attorney general Rob Bonta, who is leading a coalition of states challenging its roughly $110 billion acquisition of Warner Bros. Discovery (NASDAQ:WBD), with potential concessions including a $1.5 billion investment in California film and television production.\n\nShares of Paramount Skydance and Warner Bros. Discovery surged 7.30%, each during Monday’s pre-market trading session.\n\nThe negotiations include Paramount’s commitment to remain in the state and retain its studio lots, after the company had previously considered relocating amid opposition to the deal, according to a report by The Wall Street Journal.\n\nAdditional potential penalties were discussed if Paramount fails to meet its earlier commitment to produce 30 movies annually post-merger. These penalties could include selling its stake in Miramax, the division known for classic films such as “No Country for Old Men” and “Pulp Fiction”.\n\nOther measures being considered include selling some cable channels and establishing an editorial board to safeguard CNN’s independence. Paramount had been considering such a board even before the lawsuit, but no final agreement has been reached, and the terms remain uncertain.\n\nHowever, some states are seeking additional concessions, with New York AG Letitia James pushing for specific job guarantees for Warner Bros. employees and Connecticut AG William Tong seeking stronger safeguards for CNN and CBS News’ editorial independence, CNN reported on Sunday.\n\nParamount did not immediately respond to Benzinga’s request for comments. \n\nRead Also:\n\nDisney Escalates Fight With Trump Administration, Asks Judge to Block FCC’s Unusual Early Review of 8 ABC Licenses\n\nUS Antitrust Fight Delays Paramount Deal\n\nIn July, Paramount delayed its planned purchase of Warner Bros. to as late as June 2027, due to a multistate antitrust fight. The company called the revised schedule a "significant win," saying it provides a direct path to trial while challenging the states’ market definitions as disconnected from current market realities.\n\nA coalition of Democratic-led states led by Bonta and the Writers Guild of America sued to block the Paramount-Warner merger, citing antitrust concerns and potential job losses for Hollywood writers.\n\nIn August, a federal judge scheduled the antitrust trial over Paramount’s proposed acquisition of Warner Bros. Discovery for March 2, 2027, delaying the merger by at least seven months. The delay is expected to cost Paramount more than $1 billion in ticking fees by the time the March trial begins.\n\nDespite the U.S. hurdles, Paramount secured European Union antitrust approval for its acquisition after agreeing to end its film distribution joint venture with Universal Pictures.\n\nEllison Confident in WBD Deal\n\nLast month, Paramount Skydance Corp’s CEO David Ellison expressed high confidence in the deal with WBD, downplaying the antitrust lawsuits as not being about competition but about trust. In an Op-ed published by The New York Times, Ellison said, "I believe this fight is not really about market share…The issue is whether I can be trusted as a steward of Warner’s CNN."\n\nDuring the company’s second-quarter earnings call, the CEO stated that the merger would strengthen the company’s streaming and content business, making it better positioned to compete with larger rivals like Netflix Inc. (NASDAQ:NFLX) and Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN).\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNetflix Viewer Trends ''Look Worrying'': Wells Fargo Slashes Target on Stock\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'74d33503d7bbc78d8e1bae3fb07f0af54b281c14','2026-09-21 09:22:39','2026-09-21 09:28:10.968215',2,NULL,'2026-09-21 11:02:37');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(470,'alpaca:61888303','benzinga','2026-09-21 08:38:19','Austin to San Antonio in Under 30 Minutes? Elon Musk Says Boring Company Is Working on 200+ MPH Tunnel to Beat Traffic','Elon Musk says The Boring Company plans a 200+ mph Austin–San Antonio tunnel, which could significantly reduce travel time.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/private-markets/26/09/61888303/austin-to-san-antonio-in-under-30-minutes-elon-musk-says-boring-company-is-working-on-200-mph-tunnel-to-beat-traffic','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 09:28:16.817640','product','bullish',3,3,'weeks',1,'Potentially innovative transportation project could boost investor interest in Tesla.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-22 09:32:24.517360','2026-09-21 09:28:10.992020','61888303',replace('Elon Musk says The Boring Company is working on a high-speed tunnel between Austin and San Antonio that could cut travel times to less than 30 minutes.\n\nSpeeds Above 200 MPH\n\nIn a post on X, Musk shared an old video by user Aze Alter that showcased what the future could look like. Musk then responded to his own post, touting a new hyperloop. “Boring Company is working on a simple, precursor Hyperloop tunnel between Austin and San Antonio (>200 mph),” Musk said.\n\nHe added that because of “traffic congestion,” the journey between the two cities could take up to two and a half hours. He added that the Boring Company could “reduce that to a consistent <30 mins.”\n\nBoring Company is working on a simple, precursor Hyperloop tunnel between Austin and San Antonio (>200 mph). Due to traffic congestion, that journey can currently take up to 2.5 hours. @BoringCompany can reduce that to a consistent <30 mins.— Elon Musk (@elonmusk) September 20, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nBernie Sanders Slams Trump as Gas Hits $4.44, Diesel Hits Record $6.40: ‘Families Can’t Afford’ High Energy Costs\n\nBoring Company’s Latest Funding Round\n\nEarlier this month, the tunneling company, in its latest funding round, raised $3 billion, led mainly by UAE-based entities, bringing the company’s total valuation to $23 billion. Notably, Boring Co. said that the UAE partnership may also involve over 93 miles of underground infrastructure down the road, building on its previously announced Dubai Loop project.\n\nElsewhere, Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) is gearing up for the debut of the Roadster high-performance vehicle on October 1st, which, Musk has said, would have “guaranteed” excitement. Tesla also began taking reservations for the Roadster again, ahead of the launch, charging prospective buyers $50,000 to make their reservation.\n\nA Tesla SpaceX Merger?\n\nLast week, the billionaire also fueled speculation of a possible merger between Tesla and commercial spaceflight company Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) during an appearance on the All In Podcast, citing deep collaboration between Tesla and SpaceX.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: Tesla Vehicles Maintain Nearly 19% Junk Title Rate Across Age Groups, VIN Analysis Shows\n\nCheck out more of Benzinga’s Future Of Mobility coverage by following this link.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'26e5ada632e76b1f445d203211a13a3a7a233904','2026-09-21 08:38:19','2026-09-21 09:28:10.968215',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 08:38:19');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(471,'alpaca:61889508','benzinga','2026-09-21 10:17:14','AI Investment Boom Is ''Massive'' — Top Economist Says US Spending Is Moving Away From Homes and Toward Data Centers','Fed economist Adam Shapiro flags a pivotal U.S. investment shift as computer spending overtakes residential investment amid AI expansion.','https://www.benzinga.com/real-estate/26/09/61889508/ai-investment-boom-is-massive-top-economist-says-us-spending-is-moving-away-from-homes-and-toward-data-centers','["AMZN", "META", "MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-21 10:28:24.126656','macro','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst comments on a significant investment trend affecting multiple sectors.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48}','{}','2026-09-22 10:32:44.934710','2026-09-21 10:28:20.477697','61889508',replace('Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco Vice President Adam Shapiro has highlighted a shift in U.S. investment, saying spending is moving away from residential investment and toward computers as the AI investment boom accelerates.\n\nIn a Friday LinkedIn post, Shapiro wrote, "We’re seeing a pivotal shift in the US economy: investment is shifting away from residential investment and towards computers." He pointed out that inflation-adjusted spending on information-processing equipment, which includes data centers and computer hardware, now exceeds residential investment.\n\nInvestment Shifts\n\nData from the Bureau of Economic Analysis released in August shows real private residential fixed investment at $748 billion in the second quarter, while information-processing equipment reached $752 billion. Shapiro said the AI investment boom is "massive."\n\nShapiro also noted that residential investment is more sensitive to borrowing costs, while AI investment has been less sensitive to interest rates.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAustin to San Antonio in Under 30 Minutes? Elon Musk Says Boring Company Is Working on 200+ MPH Tunnel to Beat Traffic\n\nAI Capex Accelerates\n\nThe AI investment cycle is also expanding rapidly. Data-center capex is projected to rise from 1.4% of GDP in 2025 to 3.1% in 2027, an increase of roughly 0.85 percentage points a year.\n\n"The AI cycle is building at close to twice the pace of the housing boom at its fastest," Torsten Slok, Partner and Chief Economist at Apollo Global Management, said.\n\nHyperscaler capital expenditures are expected to reach about $916 billion over the next 12 months and nearly $1.2 trillion the following year.\n\nSpending And Risk\n\nS&P; Global estimated capital expenditures from Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOG) (NASDAQ:GOOGL), Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN), Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT), Meta Platforms, Inc. (NASDAQ:META), Oracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL) and Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) will exceed $1.3 trillion in 2027, S&P; Global Ratings reported that all six hyperscalers are expected to generate negative free operating cash flow in 2026 and 2027, with recovery not projected until 2029.\n\nThe firm is also monitoring AI investment monetization, demand durability and overcapacity risk, while its models generally assume a 2028 inflection point, with revenue accelerating and capital expenditure growth moderating.\n\nRead Also:\n\nPete Buttigieg Slams ‘Corruption’ in US Politics: ‘Corporate Money Is Flooding the Election’ and Big Pharma Will ‘Get Their Way’\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'111cc50bb013a02319068316b326e2bfa7b3187e','2026-09-21 10:17:14','2026-09-21 10:28:20.474179',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 10:17:14');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(472,'alpaca:61889443','benzinga','2026-09-21 10:11:52','Elon Musk Agrees Viral Robot Moves Were ‘Essentially Remote Controlled’ — Tesla AI Chief Warns Robot Safety is a Bigger Challenge Than AI Safety','Tesla AI chief says viral Optimus combat moves were remote-controlled, warning physical-robot safety is far harder than large-model safety.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61889443/elon-musk-agrees-viral-robot-moves-were-essentially-remote-controlled-tesla-ai-chief-warns-robot-safety-is-a-bigger-challenge-than-ai-safety','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 10:28:26.230397','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The statement provides insight into robot safety issues without a direct impact on Tesla''s market performance.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-22 10:32:44.934710','2026-09-21 10:28:20.480285','61889443',replace('Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) AI chief Ashok Elluswamy warned that keeping physical robots safe poses a far harder challenge than today’s large-model safeguards after clarifying that the eye-catching combat moves in a viral humanoid-robot video were not autonomous.\n\nElluswamy Warns Physical AI Raises Stakes\n\n"For those who don’t know, these robot moves are essentially remote controlled," Elluswamy wrote on X. "The robot rather blindly performs those while maintaining balance and such. AI safety for physical robots makes the current crop of AI safety for large models look like child’s play. Extremely important to get it right."\n\n💯— Elon Musk (@elonmusk) September 20, 2026 \n\nElon Musk responded to Elluswamy’s post with a "100" emoji, signaling agreement.\n\nTeleoperation Still Falls Short Of Autonomy\n\nThe distinction matters because teleoperation can produce impressive motion without the robot deciding what to do on its own. Tesla on its website describes Optimus’ end goal as a "general purpose, bi-pedal, autonomous humanoid robot" whose software must handle balance, navigation, perception and interaction with the physical world.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla Reopens Roadster Reservations Ahead of Oct. 1 Reveal: Here’s What You Need to Know\n\nMusk made a similar distinction during Tesla’s second-quarter earnings call. He said many impressive humanoid demonstrations online are "pre-programmed or remote controlled" and that no humanoid robot can yet perform generalized tasks on command without programming. The company’s Q2 discussion also highlighted the challenge of turning Optimus into a genuinely general-purpose machine.\n\nIn a special report last month, Reuters documented the same gap across the broader humanoid industry. Chinese robots have demonstrated kung-fu-style moves and other athletic routines, but many still struggle with dexterity, adaptability and reliable autonomous factory work.\n\nThat gap raises the stakes around "embodied AI," where software decisions translate into physical movement. The International Federation of Robotics said about 7,000 humanoids were sold globally for industrial and professional-service uses in 2025, with most still used for research and AI-data collection rather than productive commercial work, Reuters reported.\n\nTesla Pushes Optimus Toward Commercial Scale\n\nTesla is nevertheless scaling its bet. Elluswamy took responsibility for Optimus after program chief Milan Kovac left in June 2025. Tesla later installed its first-generation Optimus production line in Fremont. Elluswamy said Optimus has "big shoes to fill", while Musk cautioned that initial production will be "extremely slow".\n\nPrice Action: TSLA shares grew 1.63% to $370.20 during pre-market trading on Monday.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: Tesla Vehicles Maintain Nearly 19% Junk Title Rate Across Age Groups, VIN Analysis Shows\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'8ac7a293fca9525b560b85f7f2ef179ca8698509','2026-09-21 10:11:52','2026-09-21 10:28:20.474179',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 10:11:52');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(473,'alpaca:61888941','benzinga','2026-09-21 09:55:43','This Analyst Loves Apple’s Duo, but Says the Stock Is ‘Relatively Rich’','Apple iPhone 18 Pro demand holds steady amid higher supply, while anticipation builds for &#39;revolutionary&#39; Duo foldable device.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61888941/this-analyst-loves-apples-duo-but-says-the-stock-is-relatively-rich','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-21 10:28:37.175883','analyst','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Analyst commentary on Apple stock valuation.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}','2026-09-22 10:32:44.934710','2026-09-21 10:28:20.482587','61888941',replace('Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) is seeing steady early demand for its latest iPhones, while Wall Street is increasingly focused on the company’s upcoming Duo foldable device.Morgan Stanley analyst Erik Woodring said early demand for the iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max “seems fine,” even as Apple enters the cycle with more supply than a year ago.Speaking to CNBC on Friday, Woodring said delivery lead times for the Pro models were roughly two to four weeks, depending on the region. That is broadly unchanged from last year.Better Supply Supports Lead TimesWoodring cautioned against placing too much weight on lead times because they reflect both supply and demand.Apple’s Pro and Pro Max production is up about 18% year over year for the second half of the calendar year, he said. Therefore, flat lead times alongside higher supply could point to healthy demand.China is the exception, with shorter lead times compared with last year.Woodring believes some Chinese consumers may be waiting for Apple’s Duo foldable before choosing between the new premium models.He said China has historically been the strongest market for foldable smartphones. Apple is expected to make the Duo available in mid-October.Woodring said investors should watch whether iPhone lead times rise or begin to fall about two weeks after availability, when they typically peak.Cramer Calls Duo ‘Revolutionary’CNBC’s Jim Cramer also turned his attention to Apple’s upcoming Duo, calling the foldable device “revolutionary” while describing the iPhone 18 as a more incremental upgrade.Cramer praised the foldable device’s display and crease-free design after testing it ahead of launch. He said the Duo could become particularly useful for travel, entertainment and multitasking.Cramer also highlighted the iPhone 18’s battery life and camera improvements after visiting an Apple Store in New York.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nApple Valuation Remains A Key RiskDespite optimism around the Duo, Woodring said Apple’s valuation leaves less room for disappointment.Woodring said he remains highly optimistic about the Duo and expects Apple could sell nearly every foldable it produces over the next 12 months. However, he noted that Apple shares have already rallied sharply ahead of the iPhone launch and now trade at a ‘relatively rich valuation’. The stock is valued at about 33 times its fiscal 2027 earnings estimate and 30 times fiscal 2028 earnings, compared with a historical peak multiple of roughly 34 to 35 times.Woodring said Apple is trading at a “relatively rich” valuation of about 33 times his fiscal 2027 earnings estimate, close to its historical peak multiple of roughly 34 to 35 times.Woodring said further stock gains may require analysts to raise earnings estimates.He also pointed to Apple’s Services business as an important factor. Services growth is expected to fall below 10% in the September quarter for the first time in several years.Woodring expects growth to accelerate again. However, he said a deeper slowdown in Services could weigh on the valuation investors are willing to assign Apple.Stock Performance And Technical AnalysisApple stock edged lower in Monday’s premarket session, even as Nasdaq futures rose 0.98% and S&P; 500 futures gained 0.63%.The stock remains near recent highs but could stay range-bound until it clears resistance near $344.50.Apple remains in a strong uptrend, trading 3.9% above its 20-day SMA, 4.7% above its 50-day SMA and 17.1% above its 200-day SMA. The bullish moving-average alignment supports the broader trend.Momentum also remains positive, with the MACD above its signal line and a positive histogram.Key support sits near $300.50. A pullback that holds above shorter-term moving averages would suggest consolidation rather than a broader reversal.Apple Analyst OutlookApple trades at a price-to-earnings ratio of about 38.5, reflecting a premium valuation. The stock carries a consensus Buy rating with an average price forecast of $335.57.Evercore ISI recently maintained an Outperform rating and raised its price forecast to $380. Bank of America maintained a Buy rating with a $370 price forecast, while TD Cowen maintained a Buy rating with a $400 forecast.Top ETF ExposureApple has significant weightings in several exchange-traded funds.The stock accounts for about 9.68% of the Direxion Daily Technology Bull 3X ETF (NYSE:TECL), 9.74% of the Motley Fool 100 Index ETF (BATS:TMFC) and 9.97% of the VistaShares Target 15 Berkshire Select Income ETF (NYSE:OMAH).Large ETF inflows or outflows can therefore create additional buying or selling pressure in Apple shares.Apple Price ActionAAPL Stock Price Activity: Apple shares were trading lower by 0.31% at $335.09 during premarket trading on Monday, according to Benzinga Pro data.Photo courtesy of Apple\n\nRead Also:\n\nApple Raises the Premium Bet: iPhone 18 Pro Hits Stores, First Foldable Arrives Next','\n',char(10)),'dd6f8b57d6dd649c73b2691e479c69b87ca36bd8','2026-09-21 09:55:43','2026-09-21 10:28:20.474179',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 10:10:55');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(474,'alpaca:61889124','benzinga','2026-09-21 10:02:50','Stock Market Today: S&P 500, Nasdaq 100, Dow Jones Futures Gain as Trump Issues Fresh Warning to Iran — MRVL, AAPL, ACN in Focus (UPDATED)','U.S. stock futures advanced on Monday, as the Dow Jones, S&amp;P 500 and Nasdaq 100 indices rose, following Friday&#39;s mixed close.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61889124/stock-market-today-sp-500-nasdaq-100-futures-gain-as-trump-issues-fresh-warning-to-iran-mrvl-aapl-acn-in-focus','["AAPL", "BTC/USD", "META", "MSFT", "QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-21 13:29:20.560261','macro','bullish',2,3,'hours',1,'U.S. stock futures rose indicating potential short-term market gains.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "BTC/USD": 76528.6, "META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48, "QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 13.014}}','2026-09-22 10:32:44.934710','2026-09-21 10:28:20.491936','61889124',replace('Editor’s Note: The ETFs tracking benchmark indices and the headline were updated in the story.\n\nU.S. stock futures advanced on Monday, as the Dow Jones, S&P; 500 and Nasdaq 100 indices rose, following Friday’s mixed close.\n\nGeopolitical tensions spiked over the weekend after President Donald Trump issued fresh warnings to Iran while Tehran threatened sustained retaliation against U.S. bases. Energy markets remain on high alert as persistent shipping restrictions in the Strait of Hormuz coincide with new Houthi drone and missile strikes on sensitive targets in Saudi Arabia. \n\nWith the Federal Reserve’s rate hike in the rearview, investors are turning their focus to earnings from major consumer-facing companies this week, like Costco Wholesale Corp. (NASDAQ:COST), General Mills Inc. (NYSE:GIS), and Darden Restaurants Inc. (NYSE:DRI) for insight into household spending strength. Markets will also be closely monitoring a circuit of speeches from five central bank officials for monetary policy clues, as well as Meta Platforms Inc.‘s (NASDAQ:META) developer conference for updates on its AI strategy. \n\nMeanwhile, the 10-year Treasury bond yielded 4.96%, and the 2-year Treasury bond yielded 4.72%, at the last check. The CME Group’s FedWatch tool projections show markets pricing in a 53.1% likelihood of the Federal Reserve hiking interest rates after its October meeting.\n\nIndexPerformance (+/-)Dow Jones0.84%S&P; 5000.69%Nasdaq 1001.11%Russell 20000.72%\n\nThe SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 index and Nasdaq 100 index, respectively, rose in premarket on Monday. The SPY was up 0.68% at $766.86, while the QQQ advanced 1.04% to $728.92.\n\nRead Also:\n\nStock Market: Will S&P; 500 Open Up or Down Today?\n\nStocks In Focus\n\nAccenture\n\nAccenture Plc (NYSE:ACN) rose 5.47% in premarket on Monday after it announced a partnership to establish a team of embedded evaluators at Anthropic.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that ACN maintains a strong price trend in the short and medium terms but a weak trend in the long term, with a moderate quality score.\n\nLobo Technologies\n\nLobo Technologies Ltd. (NASDAQ:LOBO) jumped 26.98% in Monday premarket after reporting a strong year-over-year increase in its financial results during the first half of the current fiscal.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that LOBO maintains a weak price trend in the short, medium, and long terms.\n\nApple\n\nApple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) was 0.19% lower in premarket after it undertook another round of layoffs, according to a Bloomberg report. Jobs were slashed in its Fitness+ audio-content team. \n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that AAPL maintains a strong price trend in the long, medium and short terms, with a moderate growth score.\n\nRocket Lab\n\nRocket Lab Corp. (NASDAQ:RKLB) was 1.51% higher as it launched its 96th electron mission for Synspective, delivering the 12th StriX SAR satellite into a 572 km orbit. This marks its 17th launch in 2026.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that RKLB maintains a weak price trend in the long, medium and short terms.\n\nMarvell Technology\n\nMarvell Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MRVL) rose 2.56% in premarket trading following momentum from last week, when the stock jumped nearly 5% after securing an expanded silicon-germanium chip capacity deal with GlobalFoundries for its AI data center connectivity products and launching a new Azure-integrated cloud payment security service alongside Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT) and Utimaco.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that MRVL maintains a strong price trend in the long, medium, and short terms.\n\nRead Also:\n\nWill Howie Buffett Keep Berkshire Ahead of the S&P; 500? What Retail Investors Need to Know\n\nCues From Last Session\n\nInformation technology and industrials stocks bucked the overall market trend to close higher on Friday, while utilities, materials, and real estate led most S&P; 500 sectors into negative territory.\n\nIndexPerformance (+/-)ValueDow Jones-0.18%51,682.64S&P; 5000.17%7,650.50Nasdaq Composite0.39%26,522.54Russell 2000-0.50%2,860.40\n\nInsights From Analysts\n\nMohamed El-Erian views the U.S. stock market and economy as entering a delicate phase shaped by lingering interest rate risks and shifting monetary policy.\n\nFollowing the Federal Reserve’s first rate hike since 2023, El-Erian notes that Chair Kevin Warsh temporarily anchored policy expectations, which helped catalyze a “broad relief rally in equities.”\n\nHowever, he cautions that this market optimism remains “temporary and reversible” as energy market shocks and rising bond yields reassert pressure on global markets.\n\nLooking ahead, El-Erian expects the real economy’s resilience to be tested. While households and corporations previously insulated themselves by locking in low borrowing costs, he highlights that “the transmission of interest rate risk to credit and earnings” is now a primary theme to watch.\n\nFurthermore, with sovereign debt managers continuing to “auction unprecedented volumes of paper to fund persistent fiscal deficits,” the market’s capacity to absorb supply without spiking term premia will be crucial.\n\nUltimately, El-Erian anticipates that incoming economic data on consumer sentiment and labor markets will determine whether underlying economic strength can withstand these mounting financial headwinds.\n\nUpcoming Economic Data\n\nHere’s what investors will be keeping an eye on this week.\n\nNo data is scheduled to be released on Monday.\n\nOn Tuesday, Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond President Thomas Barkin will speak to the CFA Society Baltimore at 1:00 p.m. ET.\n\nOn Wednesday, September’s flash U.S. manufacturing PMI and flash U.S. services PMI data will be released by 9:45 a.m. ET.\n\nOn Thursday, weekly initial jobless claims for the week ending Sept. 19 and an Economic Club of Washington, DC event featuring Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond President Thomas Barkin will both take place at 8:30 a.m. ET.\n\nAugust’s new home sales data will be out by 10:00 a.m., and September’s Kansas City Fed manufacturing survey data will be released by 11:00 a.m. ET.\n\nOn Friday, August’s durable goods orders data will be released by 8:30 a.m., and September’s final University of Michigan consumer sentiment survey data will be out by 10:00 a.m. ET.\n\nCommodities, Crypto, And Global Equity Markets\n\nCrude Oil WTI futures were trading lower in the early New York session by 2.16% to hover around $94.00 per barrel.\n\nGold Spot US Dollar fell 0.50% to hover around $4,356.34 per ounce. The U.S. Dollar Index spot was 0.05% higher at the 100.2690 level.\n\nMeanwhile, Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) was trading 3.00% higher at $83,666.08 per coin over the last 24 hours.\n\nAsian markets were higher on Monday, as Australia’s ASX 200, Japan’s Nikkei 225, India’s Nifty 50, South Korea’s Kospi, China’s CSI 300, and Hong Kong’s Hang Seng indices rose. European markets were also higher in early trading.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'c371dd74f965341f3484161a0d66b42e92f73602','2026-09-21 10:02:50','2026-09-21 10:28:20.474179',2,NULL,'2026-09-21 12:29:40');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(475,'alpaca:61888979','benzinga','2026-09-21 09:58:35','Investigating Amazon.com''s Standing In Broadline Retail Industry Compared To Competitors','In today&#39;s rapidly evolving and fiercely competitive business landscape, it is crucial for investors and industry analysts to conduct comprehensive company evaluations. In this article, we will undertake an in-depth','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61888979/investigating-amazon-com-s-standing-broadline-retail-industry-compared-competitors','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-21 10:28:32.665417','other','neutral',1,2,'days',1,'The headline discusses an investigation without any concrete outcome.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18}','{}','2026-09-22 10:32:44.934710','2026-09-21 10:28:20.498059','61888979',replace('In today''s rapidly evolving and fiercely competitive business landscape, it is crucial for investors and industry analysts to conduct comprehensive company evaluations. In this article, we will undertake an in-depth industry comparison, assessing Amazon.com (NASDAQ:AMZN) alongside its primary competitors in the Broadline Retail industry. By meticulously examining crucial financial indicators, market positioning, and growth potential, we aim to provide valuable insights to investors and shed light on company''s performance within the industry.\nAmazon.com Background\nAmazon is the leading online retailer and marketplace for third party sellers. Retail related revenue represents approximately 74% of total, followed by Amazon Web Services (17%), and advertising services (9%). International segments constitute 22% of Amazon''s total revenue, led by Germany, the United Kingdom, and Japan.\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nAmazon.com Inc\n20.41\n4.96\n3.56\n12.61%\n$102.16\n$104.83\n19.62%\n\nMercadoLibre Inc\n48.62\n11.57\n2.58\n6.17%\n$0.96\n$4.16\n49.76%\n\neBay Inc\n23.50\n10.67\n4.28\n12.12%\n$0.83\n$2.3\n14.8%\n\nDillard''s Inc\n14.58\n4.69\n1.51\n4.71%\n$0.17\n$0.62\n-0.36%\n\nGlobal E Online Ltd\n43.25\n7.07\n6.14\n5.26%\n$0.05\n$0.13\n39.15%\n\nMacy''s Inc\n8.04\n1.16\n0.26\n3.46%\n$0.46\n$2.21\n1.2%\n\nOllie''s Bargain Outlet Holdings Inc\n16.96\n2.38\n1.66\n4.51%\n$0.13\n$0.32\n9.09%\n\nKohl''s Corp\n7.10\n0.45\n0.12\n3.69%\n$0.43\n$1.62\n-0.87%\n\nSavers Value Village Inc\n60.27\n3.12\n0.84\n4.95%\n$0.07\n$0.25\n7.43%\n\nHour Loop Inc\n44.25\n7.01\n0.41\n12.6%\n$0.0\n$0.02\n25.24%\n\nAverage\n29.62\n5.35\n1.98\n6.39%\n$0.34\n$1.29\n16.16%\n\nAfter thoroughly examining Amazon.com, the following trends can be inferred: \n\nWith a Price to Earnings ratio of 20.41, which is 0.69x less than the industry average, the stock shows potential for growth at a reasonable price, making it an interesting consideration for market participants.\n\nThe current Price to Book ratio of 4.96, which is 0.93x the industry average, is substantially lower than the industry average, indicating potential undervaluation.\n\nThe stock''s relatively high Price to Sales ratio of 3.56, surpassing the industry average by 1.8x, may indicate an aspect of overvaluation in terms of sales performance.\n\nWith a Return on Equity (ROE) of 12.61% that is 6.22% above the industry average, it appears that the company exhibits efficient use of equity to generate profits.\n\nCompared to its industry, the company has higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $102.16 Billion, which is 300.47x above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nThe company has higher gross profit of $104.83 Billion, which indicates 81.26x above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nThe company''s revenue growth of 19.62% exceeds the industry average of 16.16%, indicating strong sales performance and market outperformance.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio assesses the extent to which a company relies on borrowed funds compared to its equity.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nWhen examining Amazon.com in comparison to its top 4 peers with respect to the Debt-to-Equity ratio, the following information becomes apparent:\n\nIn terms of the debt-to-equity ratio, Amazon.com has a lower level of debt compared to its top 4 peers, indicating a stronger financial position.\n\nThis implies that the company relies less on debt financing and has a more favorable balance between debt and equity with a lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.4.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor Amazon.com in the Broadline Retail industry, the PE and PB ratios suggest the stock is undervalued compared to peers. However, the high PS ratio indicates the stock may be overvalued based on revenue. In terms of profitability, Amazon.com shows strong performance with high ROE, EBITDA, and gross profit margins. Additionally, the company''s high revenue growth rate further highlights its competitive position within the industry.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'bbb1f20a44eb130b36e454b672ae0a8fc24f6f05','2026-09-21 09:58:35','2026-09-21 10:28:20.474179',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 09:58:35');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(476,'alpaca:61888978','benzinga','2026-09-21 09:58:30','Inquiry Into Microsoft''s Competitor Dynamics In Software Industry','Amidst the fast-paced and highly competitive business environment of today, conducting comprehensive company analysis is essential for investors and industry enthusiasts. In this article, we will delve into an extensive','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61888978/inquiry-microsoft-s-competitor-dynamics-software-industry','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-21 10:28:33.515426','other','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'The inquiry suggests ongoing analysis but lacks specific actionable information.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 498.48}','{}','2026-09-22 10:32:44.934710','2026-09-21 10:28:20.500326','61888978',replace('Amidst the fast-paced and highly competitive business environment of today, conducting comprehensive company analysis is essential for investors and industry enthusiasts. In this article, we will delve into an extensive industry comparison, evaluating Microsoft (NASDAQ:MSFT) in comparison to its major competitors within the Software industry. By analyzing critical financial metrics, market position, and growth potential, our objective is to provide valuable insights for investors and offer a deeper understanding of company''s performance in the industry.\nMicrosoft Background\nMicrosoft develops and licenses consumer and enterprise software. It is known for its Windows operating systems and Office productivity suite. The company is organized into three equally sized broad segments: productivity and business processes (legacy Microsoft Office, cloud-based Office 365, Exchange, SharePoint, Skype, LinkedIn, Dynamics), intelligence cloud (infrastructure- and platform-as-a-service offerings Azure, Windows Server OS, SQL Server), and more personal computing (Windows Client, Xbox, Bing search, display advertising, and Surface laptops, tablets, and desktops).\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nMicrosoft Corp\n27.51\n8.29\n11.09\n8.35%\n$55.91\n$60.48\n17.75%\n\nOracle Corp\n23.14\n7.22\n6.04\n9.42%\n$10.39\n$11.61\n29.61%\n\nPalo Alto Networks Inc\n908.95\n10.82\n24.20\n-1.02%\n$0.07\n$2.3\n34.46%\n\nCrowdStrike Holdings Inc\n6337.33\n47.70\n45.05\n0.11%\n$0.11\n$1.1\n25.83%\n\nServiceNow Inc\n84.67\n11.19\n9.58\n2.46%\n$0.91\n$2.82\n24.01%\n\nFortinet Inc\n60.01\n80.34\n16.87\n47.73%\n$0.76\n$1.64\n25.64%\n\nGen Digital Inc\n16.96\n6.54\n3.51\n8.16%\n$0.57\n$1.03\n6.28%\n\nCheck Point Software Technologies Ltd\n13.61\n4.95\n5.13\n6.98%\n$0.2\n$0.57\n1.26%\n\nUiPath Inc\n19.99\n3.58\n4.17\n1.87%\n$0.04\n$0.33\n13.42%\n\nQualys Inc\n30.35\n10.76\n8.90\n9.26%\n$0.06\n$0.15\n11.04%\n\nCommVault Systems Inc\n92.68\n115.12\n5.21\n71.0%\n$0.04\n$0.26\n11.4%\n\nDolby Laboratories Inc\n24.53\n2.09\n4.10\n1.1%\n$0.06\n$0.26\n-3.34%\n\nBlackBerry Ltd\n79.90\n6.24\n8.20\n1.14%\n$0.02\n$0.12\n25.64%\n\nTenable Holdings Inc\n590.17\n19.66\n3.99\n1.7%\n$0.02\n$0.21\n8.58%\n\nMonday.Com Ltd\n36.07\n5.82\n3.11\n0.5%\n$0.02\n$0.32\n21.94%\n\nTeradata Corp\n6.08\n4.53\n1.65\n8.0%\n$0.08\n$0.24\n0.49%\n\nAverage\n554.96\n22.44\n9.98\n11.23%\n$0.89\n$1.53\n15.75%\n\nThrough a detailed examination of Microsoft, we can deduce the following trends: \n\nThe Price to Earnings ratio of 27.51 is 0.05x lower than the industry average, indicating potential undervaluation for the stock.\n\nConsidering a Price to Book ratio of 8.29, which is well below the industry average by 0.37x, the stock may be undervalued based on its book value compared to its peers.\n\nThe Price to Sales ratio of 11.09, which is 1.11x the industry average, suggests the stock could potentially be overvalued in relation to its sales performance compared to its peers.\n\nWith a Return on Equity (ROE) of 8.35% that is 2.88% below the industry average, it appears that the company exhibits potential inefficiency in utilizing equity to generate profits.\n\nCompared to its industry, the company has higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $55.91 Billion, which is 62.82x above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nWith higher gross profit of $60.48 Billion, which indicates 39.53x above the industry average, the company demonstrates stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nWith a revenue growth of 17.75%, which surpasses the industry average of 15.75%, the company is demonstrating robust sales expansion and gaining market share.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio assesses the extent to which a company relies on borrowed funds compared to its equity.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nWhen comparing Microsoft with its top 4 peers based on the Debt-to-Equity ratio, the following insights can be observed:\n\nMicrosoft is in a relatively stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers, as evidenced by its lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.13.\n\nThis implies that the company relies less on debt financing and has a more favorable balance between debt and equity.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor Microsoft in the Software industry, the PE and PB ratios suggest the stock is undervalued compared to peers, indicating potential for growth. However, the high PS ratio implies the stock may be overvalued based on revenue. In terms of ROE, Microsoft''s performance is lower than industry peers, while its high EBITDA and gross profit indicate strong operational efficiency. The high revenue growth rate suggests Microsoft is expanding rapidly compared to competitors in the sector.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'3e86833c47eec802cf133129e192bb94e7661fc3','2026-09-21 09:58:30','2026-09-21 10:28:20.