INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(477,'alpaca:61888977','benzinga','2026-09-21 09:58:27','Understanding Apple''s Position In Technology Hardware, Storage &amp; Peripherals Industry Compared To Competitors','In today&#39;s rapidly changing and fiercely competitive business landscape, it is essential for investors and industry enthusiasts to thoroughly analyze companies. In this article, we will conduct a comprehensive','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61888977/understanding-apple-s-position-technology-hardware-storage-amp-peripherals-industry-compared-competi','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-21 10:28:34.715167','other','neutral',1,1,'weeks',1,'The headline is an opinion piece regarding Apple''s industry position.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}','2026-09-22 10:32:44.934710','2026-09-21 10:28:20.502642','61888977',replace('In today''s rapidly changing and fiercely competitive business landscape, it is essential for investors and industry enthusiasts to thoroughly analyze companies. In this article, we will conduct a comprehensive industry comparison, evaluating Apple (NASDAQ:AAPL) against its key competitors in the Technology Hardware, Storage & Peripherals industry. By examining key financial metrics, market position, and growth prospects, we aim to provide valuable insights for investors and shed light on company''s performance within the industry.\nApple Background\nApple is among the largest companies in the world, with a broad portfolio of hardware and software products targeted at consumers and businesses. Apple''s iPhone accounts for the majority of the firm''s sales, and Apple''s other products, such as the Mac, iPad, and Watch, are designed around the iPhone as the focal point of an expansive software ecosystem. Apple has progressively worked to add new applications, such as streaming video, subscription bundles, and augmented reality. The firm designs its own software and semiconductors and works with subcontractors such as Foxconn and TSMC to build its products and chips. Slightly less than half of Apple''s sales come directly through its flagship stores, with the majority coming indirectly through partnerships and distribution.\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nApple Inc\n38.55\n45.62\n10.64\n27.84%\n$39.02\n$54.77\n16.36%\n\nSanDisk Corp\n24.29\n16.67\n13.72\n46.78%\n$7.89\n$7.58\n371.59%\n\nSeagate Technology Holdings PLC\n61.78\n90.12\n16.13\n79.34%\n$1.64\n$1.9\n48.49%\n\nWestern Digital Corp\n16.40\n17.95\n13.08\n34.3%\n$3.36\n$2.03\n43.84%\n\nHewlett Packard Enterprise Co\n31.32\n3.04\n2.05\n5.83%\n$2.33\n$4.9\n33.68%\n\nNetApp Inc\n27.94\n25.99\n5.36\n26.35%\n$0.55\n$1.42\n29.89%\n\nEverpure Inc\n142.66\n22.52\n8.47\n4.97%\n$0.11\n$0.81\n37.73%\n\nSuper Micro Computer Inc\n11.99\n2.50\n0.70\n12.83%\n$1.57\n$1.94\n93.16%\n\nLogitech International SA\n18.55\n6.16\n3.03\n10.33%\n$0.28\n$0.61\n6.93%\n\nDiebold Nixdorf Inc\n20.93\n2.21\n0.59\n1.56%\n$0.09\n$0.24\n1.7%\n\nCorsair Gaming Inc\n43.16\n2.18\n0.99\n1.04%\n$0.02\n$0.1\n-1.8%\n\nImmersion Corp\n21.21\n0.80\n0.14\n1.93%\n$0.01\n$0.06\n0.81%\n\nAverage\n38.2\n17.29\n5.84\n20.48%\n$1.62\n$1.96\n60.55%\n\nThrough a detailed examination of Apple, we can deduce the following trends: \n\nNotably, the current Price to Earnings ratio for this stock, 38.55, is 1.01x above the industry norm, reflecting a higher valuation relative to the industry.\n\nWith a Price to Book ratio of 45.62, which is 2.64x the industry average, Apple might be considered overvalued in terms of its book value, as it is trading at a higher multiple compared to its industry peers.\n\nWith a relatively high Price to Sales ratio of 10.64, which is 1.82x the industry average, the stock might be considered overvalued based on sales performance.\n\nWith a Return on Equity (ROE) of 27.84% that is 7.36% above the industry average, it appears that the company exhibits efficient use of equity to generate profits.\n\nThe company exhibits higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $39.02 Billion, which is 24.09x above the industry average, implying stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nThe gross profit of $54.77 Billion is 27.94x above that of its industry, highlighting stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nThe company''s revenue growth of 16.36% is significantly below the industry average of 60.55%. This suggests a potential struggle in generating increased sales volume.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio indicates the proportion of debt and equity used by a company to finance its assets and operations.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nIn light of the Debt-to-Equity ratio, a comparison between Apple and its top 4 peers reveals the following information:\n\nWhen considering the debt-to-equity ratio, Apple exhibits a stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers.\n\nThis indicates that the company has a favorable balance between debt and equity, with a lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.78, which can be perceived as a positive aspect by investors.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor Apple, the PE, PB, and PS ratios are all high compared to its peers in the Technology Hardware, Storage & Peripherals industry, indicating potentially overvalued stock. On the other hand, Apple''s high ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and low revenue growth suggest strong operational efficiency and profitability relative to its industry counterparts.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'3ec4eeec71a393ab953daeaaf891f9cad8cc3108','2026-09-21 09:58:27','2026-09-21 10:28:20.474179',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 09:58:27');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(478,'alpaca:61888976','benzinga','2026-09-21 09:58:21','Assessing NVIDIA''s Performance Against Competitors In Semiconductors &amp; Semiconductor Equipment Industry','In today&#39;s fast-paced and competitive business landscape, it is essential for investors and industry enthusiasts to thoroughly analyze companies before making investment decisions. In this article, we will conduct a','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61888976/assessing-nvidia-s-performance-against-competitors-semiconductors-amp-semiconductor-equipment-indust','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 10:28:36.027182','other','neutral',1,2,'days',1,'The headline discusses performance analysis without providing actionable news.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-22 10:32:44.934710','2026-09-21 10:28:20.505372','61888976',replace('In today''s fast-paced and competitive business landscape, it is essential for investors and industry enthusiasts to thoroughly analyze companies before making investment decisions. In this article, we will conduct a comprehensive industry comparison, evaluating NVIDIA (NASDAQ:NVDA) against its key competitors in the Semiconductors & Semiconductor Equipment industry. By examining key financial metrics, market position, and growth prospects, we aim to provide valuable insights for investors and shed light on company''s performance within the industry.\nNVIDIA Background\nNvidia is a leading developer of graphics processing units. Traditionally, GPUs were used to enhance the experience on computing platforms, most notably in gaming applications on PCs. GPU use cases have since emerged as important semiconductors used in artificial intelligence to run large language models. Nvidia not only offers AI GPUs, but also a software platform, Cuda, used for AI model development and training. Nvidia is also expanding its data center networking solutions, helping to tie GPUs together to handle complex workloads.\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nNVIDIA Corp\n28.10\n23.44\n17.90\n28.12%\n$72.86\n$72.14\n105.85%\n\nBroadcom Inc\n45.61\n17.12\n19.61\n13.97%\n$18.27\n$20.46\n85.5%\n\nMicron Technology Inc\n22.96\n11.39\n12.82\n32.62%\n$35.58\n$35.06\n345.72%\n\nAdvanced Micro Devices Inc\n142.81\n13.59\n22.36\n3.49%\n$3.35\n$6.2\n50.11%\n\nTexas Instruments Inc\n40.52\n13.52\n12.53\n11.32%\n$2.95\n$3.35\n22.82%\n\nMarvell Technology Inc\n80.88\n11.85\n22.92\n1.68%\n$0.77\n$1.46\n36.55%\n\nQualcomm Inc\n20.31\n6.86\n4.34\n7.29%\n$3.04\n$5.28\n-4.03%\n\nAnalog Devices Inc\n44.62\n5.43\n13.29\n3.98%\n$2.13\n$2.71\n39.63%\n\nMonolithic Power Systems Inc\n74.30\n15.36\n18.20\n6.8%\n$0.32\n$0.54\n47.56%\n\nNXP Semiconductors NV\n19.45\n5.04\n4.39\n6.87%\n$1.27\n$2.0\n19.48%\n\nMicrochip Technology Inc\n107.75\n6.17\n7.84\n3.14%\n$0.49\n$0.94\n38.05%\n\nCredo Technology Group Holding Ltd\n61.93\n12.12\n21.08\n5.4%\n$0.14\n$0.31\n114.73%\n\nON Semiconductor Corp\n45.74\n3.77\n4.56\n3.12%\n$0.43\n$0.62\n9.18%\n\nGLOBALFOUNDRIES Inc\n37.36\n2.26\n3.85\n1.41%\n$0.48\n$0.51\n5.81%\n\nTower Semiconductor Ltd\n88.39\n8.19\n14.93\n2.99%\n$0.17\n$0.14\n23.66%\n\nMACOM Technology Solutions Holdings Inc\n87.85\n13.67\n18.20\n6.81%\n$0.14\n$0.2\n35.77%\n\nFirst Solar Inc\n12.08\n2.04\n3.92\n4.18%\n$0.61\n$0.61\n-3.73%\n\nAverage\n58.29\n9.27\n12.8\n7.19%\n$4.38\n$5.02\n54.18%\n\nUpon a comprehensive analysis of NVIDIA, the following trends can be discerned: \n\nA Price to Earnings ratio of 28.1 significantly below the industry average by 0.48x suggests undervaluation. This can make the stock appealing for those seeking growth.\n\nThe elevated Price to Book ratio of 23.44 relative to the industry average by 2.53x suggests company might be overvalued based on its book value.\n\nThe Price to Sales ratio of 17.9, which is 1.4x the industry average, suggests the stock could potentially be overvalued in relation to its sales performance compared to its peers.\n\nThe Return on Equity (ROE) of 28.12% is 20.93% above the industry average, highlighting efficient use of equity to generate profits.\n\nThe company exhibits higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $72.86 Billion, which is 16.63x above the industry average, implying stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nThe gross profit of $72.14 Billion is 14.37x above that of its industry, highlighting stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nThe company''s revenue growth of 105.85% exceeds the industry average of 54.18%, indicating strong sales performance and market outperformance.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio indicates the proportion of debt and equity used by a company to finance its assets and operations.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nBy considering the Debt-to-Equity ratio, NVIDIA can be compared to its top 4 peers, leading to the following observations:\n\nIn terms of the debt-to-equity ratio, NVIDIA has a lower level of debt compared to its top 4 peers, indicating a stronger financial position.\n\nThis implies that the company relies less on debt financing and has a more favorable balance between debt and equity with a lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.17.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor NVIDIA in the Semiconductors & Semiconductor Equipment industry, the PE ratio is low compared to peers, indicating potential undervaluation. The PB and PS ratios are high, suggesting overvaluation relative to industry standards. In terms of ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and revenue growth, NVIDIA demonstrates strong performance compared to its competitors, reflecting favorable financial health and growth prospects.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'0f058bd1179004d402bfe6057144c871fd182626','2026-09-21 09:58:21','2026-09-21 10:28:20.474179',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 09:58:21');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(479,'alpaca:61890631','benzinga','2026-09-21 11:11:03','Kevin O''Leary Is Certain Ethereum Won''t Be the ''Standard'' Across Industry Sectors — The ''Shark'' Says These Coins Could Gain Interest','Influential investor and media personality Kevin O’Leary expressed doubts on Sunday, September 20, about Ethereum&#39;s dominance in the cryptocurrency space, hinting at potential investments in chains like Solana and Avalanche.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61890631/kevin-oleary-is-certain-ethereum-wont-be-the-standard-across-different-industry-sectors-the-shark-instead-thinks-solana-and-avalanche-could-draw-interest','["AVAX/USD", "BTC/USD", "ETH/USD", "SOL/USD"]','degen','2026-09-21 11:28:44.722459','analyst','bearish',2,3,'days',1,'O''Leary''s doubts about Ethereum''s potential dominance may negatively influence investor sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AVAX/USD": 7.631703886, "BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "SOL/USD": 101.29}','{"AVAX/USD": {"60m": 43.912, "1d": 42.958}, "BTC/USD": {"60m": 13.014}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 12.919}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": 15.984, "1d": 15.347}}','2026-09-22 11:32:56.078381','2026-09-21 11:28:40.301393','61890631',replace('Influential investor and media personality Kevin O’Leary expressed doubts on Sunday about Ethereum’s (CRYPTO: ETH) dominance in the cryptocurrency space, hinting at potential investments in chains like Solana (CRYPTO: SOL) and Avalanche (CRYPTO: AVAX).\n\nO’Leary Questions Ethereum’s Dominance\n\nO’Leary, also known as “Mr. Wonderful,” said with “certainty” that Ethereum may not become the standard across the different sectors of the stock market, citing its speed as a concern.\n\nIn his view, Solana (CRYPTO: SOL) and Avalanche (CRYPTO: AVAX) were instead emerging as networks of potential interest to the industry.\n\n“They’re looking for much faster transactional speeds with variance of volumes,” O’Leary stated. \n\nAs of this writing, Solana is processing over 1,262 transactions per second, compared with Ethereum’s 22.44 transactions per second, according to data from Chainspect. However, Avalanche was slower, facilitating only 10.40 transactions per second.\n\nI have to put some bets down on chains that are gonna get adopted. I now know with certainty that ETH will not be the, in my view, the standard across all 11 sectors, primarily because a lot of people think it''s too slow. They’re looking for much faster transactional speeds with… pic.twitter.com/okRAs6TdEW— Kevin O''Leary aka Mr. Wonderful (@kevinolearytv) September 20, 2026 \n\nWhat to Have in a Portfolio?\n\nO’Leary further stressed Avalanche’s “multi-chain” feature, called subnets, which have their own customized rules and independent validator sets while plugging into the broader Avalanche ecosystem.\n\nThe “Shark” said that “a lot of interesting things” are going on and added that investors might be forced to actively rebalance positions as new facts emerge.\n\nRead Also:\n\nElizabeth Warren Says ''We Will Win in November'' — Here''s What Crypto Prediction Market Says About Democrats'' Midterm Chances\n\nO’Leary Rethinks ETH’s Role\n\nO’Leary’s remarks signaled a departure from his long-held belief that owning Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) and Ethereum alone is sufficient to capture 97.5% of the cryptocurrency market’s volatility and yield.\n\nHe has been a known investor in cryptocurrency infrastructure companies, including Circle Internet Group Inc. (NYSE:CRCL), Coinbase Global Inc. (NASDAQ:COIN), and Robinhood Markets Inc. (NASDAQ:HOOD).\n\nEarlier in June, O’Leary said that the "next big thing" in cryptocurrency would be determined by its adoption across different sectors of the S&P; 500.\n\nPrice Action: At the time of writing, ETH was exchanging hands at $2,698.08, up 4.90% in the last 24 hours, according to data from Benzinga Pro. \n\nAVAX traded up 15.60% at $11.16, while SOL jumped 7.1% to $116.05.\n\nRead Also:\n\nJason Calacanis Calls Bitcoin a ''Dead Cat'' Which Continues to Bounce—Cathie Wood Argues BTC Has ''Many Lives Ahead''''\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'4b09b5507ee4403716c595061373c6b2db40b6db','2026-09-21 11:11:03','2026-09-21 11:28:40.289297',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 11:11:03');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(480,'alpaca:61890221','benzinga','2026-09-21 11:00:05','Diesel Hits Historic $6.51/Gal: Commodity Strategist Warns We Are Facing a Deficit That ''No Handshake'' Can Refill','Diesel hits a historic $6.51/gal. A commodity strategist warns Middle East disruptions caused a refining deficit &#39;no handshake&#39; can fix.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/commodities/26/09/61890221/diesel-hits-historic-6-51-gal-commodity-strategist-warns-we-are-facing-a-deficit-that-no-handshake-can-refill','["QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-21 11:28:46.012211','macro','bearish',4,3,'days',1,'High diesel prices and warnings of a refining deficit could negatively impact the broader economy.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-22 11:32:56.078381','2026-09-21 11:28:40.306074','61890221',replace('The national average price for diesel reached $6.51 per gallon on Monday. A commodity strategist stated the supply disruption has moved into a diesel market that “no handshake can refill.”\n\nRecord Prices Hit Harvest and Freight\n\nThe U.S. average diesel price hit an all-time high of $6.5107 per gallon on Sept. 21, 2026, according to AAA data. According to economist Steve Hanke, the surge is increasing costs for the domestic agricultural and logistics sectors.\n\nHanke notes that farm fuel costs have risen by $11 per acre for corn and $7 per acre for soybeans compared to last year. The price spike is also placing independent trucking firms under the threat of diesel-driven bankruptcies.\n\nRecord-high diesel prices are CRUSHING American farmers and truckers during harvest season.Farm fuel costs are up $11/acre for corn and $7/acre for soybeans from last year.DIESEL PRICES ARE ONE BIG REASON WHY FARMERS AND TRUCKERS ARE TURNING AGAINST TRUMP. pic.twitter.com/HXDgABDB4P— Steve Hanke (@steve_hanke) September 20, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nChuck Grassley Asks Why Trump Doesn''t Embargo Diesel Exports Like Presidents Did in the ''70s: Prices Are ''Killing Farmers'' Income''\n\nRed Sea Diplomacy and Pipeline Closures\n\nThe fuel rally follows weekend meetings in Muscat, Oman, between U.S. officials and Houthi representatives. According to a recent note by commodity strategist Giacomo Prandelli, the Houthis offered safe passage to U.S. and commercial vessels, but Saudi Arabian shipping remains an exception.\n\nPrandelli stated that Saudi Arabia’s crude oil export routes are currently compromised. He stated that traffic through the Strait of Hormuz dropped to four vessels on Monday, down from a pre-war average of roughly 125.\n\nAdditionally, the East-West Pipeline to Yanbu remains offline following a Sept. 10 drone attack. While U.S. Energy Secretary Chris Wright expects the pipeline back in “days,” Prandelli wrote that trading estimates range up to 8 weeks.\n\nRefinery Shortages Override Markets\n\nPrandelli highlighted that a deal protecting American ships but targeting Saudi vessels protects the “wrong ships for the oil market.” Consequently, European refiners like Poland’s ORLEN are tendering for alternative grades including Grane, Johan Sverdrup, and WTI Midland, according to his newsletter.\n\nAsian diesel margins have crossed $87 a barrel, and New York diesel futures settled at an all-time high. “The screen says the risk premium is negotiable,” Prandelli wrote. “The refinery gate says the shortage is not”.\n\nSustained Price Pressures\n\nConstrained global supplies have pushed Brent crude futures to $101.60 per barrel, at the last check. Meanwhile, its tracker, United States Brent Oil Fund LP (NYSE:BNO), was down 1.39% in premarket on Monday.\n\nSimilarly, the West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude was 3.16% lower at $93.04 per barrel, with United States Oil Fund LP (NYSE:USO) down 1.57% in Monday’s premarket trading.\n\nThe S&P; 500 index has advanced 11.76% year-to-date. Similarly, the Nasdaq Composite index was up 14.11%, and the Dow Jones gained 7.53% YTD.\n\nOn Friday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed higher. SPY rose 0.13% to $761.69, while QQQ rose 0.63% to $721.45. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), ended 0.25% lower at $515.88.\n\nIn premarket on Monday, SPY was up 0.62%, QQQ advanced 0.94%, and DIA gained 0.61%.\n\nRead Also:\n\nWill Howie Buffett Keep Berkshire Ahead of the S&P; 500? What Retail Investors Need to Know\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'4f9b0872fdc614154a7ca5846bd1e2ce1704ca70','2026-09-21 11:00:05','2026-09-21 11:28:40.289297',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 11:00:05');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(481,'alpaca:61891392','benzinga','2026-09-21 11:53:25','Why Is IREN Stock Gaining Monday?','IREN stock rose ~3% premarket following a new $99 price target from Northland Capital. Read the latest rating &amp; forecast details.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61891392/why-is-iren-stock-gaining-monday','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 12:28:55.310039','analyst','bullish',2,3,'days',1,'New price target from a credible analyst firm.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 13.014}}','2026-09-22 12:33:10.206201','2026-09-21 12:28:50.690297','61891392',replace('IREN Ltd. (NASDAQ:IREN) stock rose about 3% in Monday’s premarket trading, supported by a fresh bullish analyst call, strength in Bitcoin and a broader risk-on market backdrop.Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) climbed about 4.9% over the past 24 hours, lifting sentiment across crypto-linked stocks. Meanwhile, Nasdaq futures gained 0.92%, while S&P; 500 futures rose 0.68%.Northland Starts IREN With $99 Price ForecastNorthland Capital Markets analyst Nehal Chokshi initiated coverage of IREN on Friday with an Outperform rating and a $99 price forecast.Bitcoin’s latest rally is providing support for crypto-linked stocks, including IREN, which operates a Bitcoin mining business alongside its growing artificial intelligence infrastructure operations.The cryptocurrency was up about 4.9% over the past 24 hours as investors continued to assess recent U.S. regulatory developments.On Friday, crypto-linked companies also traded higher after the Commodity Futures Trading Commission submitted a proposal Thursday covering crypto asset transactions and markets, according to Benzinga Pro.The move followed separate announcements from the CFTC and Securities and Exchange Commission. Together, the developments signaled continued regulatory activity after the Clarity Act failed to advance in the Senate.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nTechnical AnalysisIREN remains above several key moving averages.The stock is trading well above its 20-day simple moving average of $41.83 and its 50-day SMA of $40.38. It is also above its 200-day SMA of $45.54.However, the 50-day SMA remains below the 200-day average after a death cross formed in August. That keeps the longer-term technical picture mixed.Still, shorter-term momentum has improved. The 20-day SMA is above the 50-day average. Meanwhile, the MACD is above its signal line, and the histogram remains positive.Resistance sits near $49, while support is around $46.Analyst OutlookIREN carries a Buy consensus rating and an average price forecast of $81.18.Northland initiated coverage with a $99 price forecast on Sept. 18. JPMorgan upgraded the stock to Overweight and raised its price forecast to $65 on Sept. 14. BTIG maintained a Buy rating and an $80 price forecast the same day.Benzinga EdgeIREN has a Benzinga Edge Momentum score of 45.82, placing it in neutral territory.The improving technical setup suggests momentum is rebuilding. However, traders may watch whether the stock can break above nearby resistance and remain above its 200-day moving average.Price ActionIREN shares were up 2.91% at $48.04 in Monday’s premarket trading, according to Benzinga Pro data.Photo via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nWill Howie Buffett Keep Berkshire Ahead of the S&P; 500? What Retail Investors Need to Know','\n',char(10)),'a073ce38de1dcdb4b8a61c80f69ad1eb539d2e6d','2026-09-21 11:53:25','2026-09-21 12:28:50.626040',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 11:53:25');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(482,'alpaca:61891282','benzinga','2026-09-21 11:44:48','Jensen Huang Says AI CEOs May Have ''Ulterior'', Maybe ''Political'' Reasons For AI Doomsday Warnings: ''Go and Read Between The Lines''','Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang accused AI lab leaders of seeking less regulation while warning that U.S. AI slowdowns could benefit China.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61891282/jensen-huang-says-ai-ceos-may-have-ulterior-maybe-political-reasons-for-ai-doomsday-warnings-go-and-read-between-the-lines','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 12:28:56.672707','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Comments from a notable CEO about industry politics and regulation.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-22 12:33:10.206201','2026-09-21 12:28:50.698322','61891282',replace('Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang accused AI lab leaders of being “irresponsible” and resorting to “too much drama” in their calls for more AI oversight. \n\nDuring the CBS News’ Face The Nation interview on Sunday, Huang suggested, “They’re actually not asking for more laws. They’re asking to be relieved of the laws we do have.” \n\n“Go and read between the lines,” he added. \n\nHuang also speculated about the motives of AI labs, suggesting they might be “political,” attention-seeking, or for other “ulterior” reasons. He reiterated his concerns that a slowdown in U.S. labs could give China an advantage in the global AI race.\n\nHuang argued that AI companies are capable of managing safety themselves and that existing laws provide the government with tools to address unsafe products. He also pushed back on AI doomsday predictions and said, “It’s wrong because it’s not grounded on science.”\n\nRead Also:\n\nPalantir CTO Warns AI Safety ‘Effective Altruists’ Are Attempting a ‘Coup’ — Says ‘Tiny Group of Technocrats’ Shouldn’t Decide for Everyone\n\nHuang Rejects Calls For AI Rules\n\nEarlier this month, Huang pushed back on calls for new antitrust rules that could allow AI companies to coordinate a slowdown in the development of increasingly powerful models. \n\nHe stated that AI companies do not need new laws or regulatory exemptions to properly test their products before releasing them. His comments came after Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei’s proposal for AI labs to coordinate the pace of frontier-model development.\n\nWhite House science adviser Michael Kratsios said AI companies concerned about their technology’s safety can voluntarily slow or halt development without government intervention.\n\nTrump Plans AI Czar, ‘AI Force’\n\nPresident Donald Trump, who also echoes the Nvidia CEO’s stance, announced plans to appoint a new artificial intelligence adviser, or "AI czar," and establish an "AI force," to oversee the growth of the AI industry. \n\n"We will not in any way hinder or stifle the Growth of this incredible Industry. Rather, we will cherish it, help it, and watch over it, as it grows,” Trump wrote on Truth Social. The President added that said the U.S. would address harmful AI use through the existing criminal and civil justice system.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAI Capex Boom Risks ''Massive Capital Destruction'' in the US, Warns Veteran Market Strategist: ''You Could Get Some News Item That Suddenly…''\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'cbc23b838d491bef36f3ecc743f3218a29751a8a','2026-09-21 11:44:48','2026-09-21 12:28:50.626040',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 11:44:48');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(483,'alpaca:61891212','benzinga','2026-09-21 11:39:47','Tesla Audits Chinese Suppliers as Elon Musk’s Optimus Robot Moves Closer to Mass Production: Report','Tesla is reportedly auditing Chinese suppliers ahead of Optimus humanoid robot production, targeting compliance and quality checks.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61891212/tesla-audits-chinese-suppliers-as-elon-musks-optimus-robot-moves-closer-to-mass-production-report','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 12:28:58.212794','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Audit process reported by credible sources.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-22 12:33:10.206201','2026-09-21 12:28:50.702160','61891212',replace('Elon Musk-led Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) is reportedly auditing its suppliers in China as the EV giant looks to ramp up production of the Optimus Humanoid Robot.\n\nTesla Prepping Optimus Ramp?\n\nOn Monday, Chinese media outlet The Paper published a report, citing anonymous sources familiar with the matter, that Tesla was auditing its suppliers like Tuopu Group, Sanhua Intelligent Control and Joyson Electronics, which supply actuators, joint modules and more, the report said.\n\nRead Also:\n\nElon Musk Agrees Viral Robot Moves Were ‘Essentially Remote Controlled’ — Tesla AI Chief Warns Robot Safety is a Bigger Challenge Than AI Safety\n\nThe anonymous source cited in the report said that the companies had already received orders for Optimus before the audits began. The audits are aimed at compliance and quality checks before production begins, the report said.\n\nTesla did not immediately respond to Benzinga‘s request for comment.\n\nTesla’s Optimus Goals\n\nMusk, on multiple occasions, has charted out Tesla’s goal of producing 1 million units of the Optimus robot annually at scale. Tesla also sunset the production of the premium Model S and Model X units in Fremont, California, to build the Optimus production line there instead.\n\nTesla’s VP of Vehicle Engineering, Lars Moravy, confirmed that the Fremont facility would have at least 40 different production lines to produce the Optimus Robot, given the Robot’s complex design and architecture.\n\nMusk has also said Optimus could eventually become the world’s first Von Neumann machine — a theoretical self-replicating machine capable of using available resources to reproduce itself.\n\nAccording to Benzinga Edge Rankings, Tesla scores moderately on the Growth and Quality metrics, but offers poor Value and Momentum. TSLA also fails to provide a favorable price trend in the Medium and Long term.\n\nPrice Action: TSLA shares rose 1.39% to $369.34 during pre-market trading on Monday.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla AI Chief Ashok Elluswamy Says Optimus Has ''Big Shoes to Fill'' After Model S, X Production Line Closure\n\nCheck out more of Benzinga’s Future Of Mobility coverage by following this link.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'4394599d3ae1657cba78c896d6538b970195bb10','2026-09-21 11:39:47','2026-09-21 12:28:50.626040',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 11:39:47');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(484,'alpaca:61891053','benzinga','2026-09-21 11:34:53','‘Septemberphobia’ Could Give Way to a Big October Rally Despite Trump Uncertainty: Market Strategist Points to S&P 500’s Best Midterm Month','Why is October the best month for stocks? Ryan Detrick breaks down S&amp;P 500 midterm seasonality and looks past the Trump election noise.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/market-summary/26/09/61891053/septemberphobia-could-give-way-to-a-big-october-rally-despite-trump-uncertainty-market-strategist-points-to-sp-500s-best-midterm-month','["QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-21 12:28:59.474810','macro','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'The headline discusses potential market trends without confirmation.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-22 12:33:10.206201','2026-09-21 12:28:50.708470','61891053',replace('The S&P; 500 averages a 3.0% return in October during midterm election years, making it the “best month” for stocks. Ryan Detrick, Chief Market Strategist at Carson Group, uses this historical midterm seasonality to forecast a rally, overriding investor fear and election noise surrounding President Donald Trump.\n\nThe Historical Midterm Catalyst\n\nAccording to data spanning 1950 to 2025, the S&P; 500 posts higher returns in October during midterm years 73.7% of the time. Detrick stated that the “best month of the year in a midterm year is October.”\n\nHe noted that November follows closely behind as a catalyst for market growth. Calling it “the second best month of the year,” Detrick shared data showing November averages a 2.7% return in midterm years, trading higher 78.9% of the time.\n\nThe best month of the year in a midterm year is October.The second best month of the year in a midterm year is November.Almost there. pic.twitter.com/O1t0RkLT6T— Ryan Detrick, CMT (@RyanDetrick) September 21, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nS&P; 500 Has Delivered ‘Muted Returns’ During Fed Cycles With More Than 5 Rate Hikes, Says Ryan Detrick\n\nConfronting ‘Septemberphobia’\n\nThis seasonal fourth-quarter forecast arrives amid a period of elevated market anxiety. Detrick observed that “Septemberphobia is real,” pointing to technical indicators such as longtime bulls cutting targets, the American Association of Individual Investors (AAII) showing the most bears since Liberation Day, and the NAAIM Exposure Index dropping 30% over three weeks.\n\nAdditionally, a market sentiment gauge recently registered a “Fear” level of 29 out of 100.\n\nSeptemberphobia is real* Longtime bulls are cutting targets* AAII bears most since Liberation Day* NAAIM down 30% the past 3 weeks pic.twitter.com/QLJBpqQ5WI— Ryan Detrick, CMT (@RyanDetrick) September 21, 2026 \n\nTechnical Resilience\n\nDespite the fear, the S&P; 500 has demonstrated stability. Detrick asked, “Don’t short a dull market?” He noted that the index avoided a single 1% drop in September, nor did it gain or lose 1% for a full week for four consecutive weeks. The index continues holding above its early June peak and the upward-sloping 20-week moving average.\n\nDon''t short a dull market? They told us all month how bearish September is, yet we haven''t seen a single 1% drop and the S&P; 500 hasn''t gained or lost 1% for the full week for four weeks in a row. Holding above the early June peak and now the upward sloping 20-wk. Our call… pic.twitter.com/St4SrF6tAB— Ryan Detrick, CMT (@RyanDetrick) September 21, 2026 \n\nWhile market breadth weakened recently, Detrick pointed out a technical positive: breadth peaked simultaneously with price, whereas major market peaks typically see breadth peak well before price.\n\nAs nearly everyone has noted, breadth has been weak the past month or so.@scottcharts noted one positive is breadth peaked with price this time. Remember, at major peaks you see breadth peak well before price. pic.twitter.com/dg0isDovhV— Ryan Detrick, CMT (@RyanDetrick) September 21, 2026 \n\nHow Has the Index Performed?\n\nThe S&P; 500 currently holds a year-to-date gain of 11.76%, a six-month return of 15.48%, and a one-year return of 15.36%. Maintaining his firm’s technical forecast, Detrick stated, “Our call for a choppy to weak first half of September, then a big rally the second half hasn’t been a popular call. We still think it is possible.”\n\nLooking ahead to the historical October midterm seasonality, Detrick added, “Almost there.”\n\nOn Friday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed higher. SPY rose 0.13% to $761.69, while QQQ rose 0.63% to $721.45. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), ended 0.25% lower at $515.88.\n\nIn premarket on Monday, SPY was up 0.62%, QQQ advanced 0.94%, and DIA gained 0.61%.\n\nRead Also:\n\nStock Market Today: S&P; 500, Nasdaq 100 Futures Gain as Trump Issues Fresh Warning to Iran — MRVL, AAPL, ACN in Focus\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'2201a92a91ad467761dcd030c6709b5ed8c655c9','2026-09-21 11:34:53','2026-09-21 12:28:50.626040',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 11:36:06');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(485,'alpaca:61894356','benzinga','2026-09-21 13:24:38','XRP Jumps 8% as Ripple Says Asset Managers Eye XRPL Upgrade','XRP rallies as Ripple’s Batch V1.1 upgrade nears activation, with asset managers preparing adoption and traders watching $1.50 resistance.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61894356/xrp-jumps-8-as-ripple-says-asset-managers-eye-xrpl-upgrade','["BTC/USD", "XRP/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 13:29:07.168924','product','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'The news of the XRPL upgrade and interest from asset managers suggests positive market sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 13.156}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 17.1}}','2026-09-22 13:33:30.055993','2026-09-21 13:29:02.911853','61894356',replace('XRP (CRYPTO: XRP) spiked after Ripple said asset managers and commercial projects are preparing to use a major XRP Ledger payments upgrade that is nearing activation.\n\nWill XRPL Upgrade Push XRP Higher?\n\nRippleX head of engineering Ayo Akinyele that asset managers are preparing to use Batch V1.1, which can bundle up to eight transactions into a single operation.\n\nIts all-or-nothing structure allows linked transactions to settle together or fail together, supporting use cases such as delivery-versus-payment.\n\n"We’ll be sharing more once the feature is live, including work with key asset managers," Akinyele told CoinDesk.\n\nBatch V1.1 has support from 30 of 35 tracked validators and is projected to activate after Sept. 29 if support remains above 80%.\n\nThe upgrade replaces Batch V1.0, which was withdrawn after researchers found a critical signature-validation flaw. The vulnerable version never activated, and no funds were exposed.\n\nCan XRP Break $1.50?\n\nTrader DOM said XRP tested its three-month and six-month rolling volume-weighted average prices as support for the first time in more than a year.\n\nHe sees $1.50 as the immediate level that matters after XRP spent roughly 230 days below it.\n\nFlipping it into support could open the door to a move above $1.80, he said.\n\nCastillo Trading also highlighted a clean setup from the range lows, saying XRP has a clear invalidation level and could see momentum accelerate.\n\nXRP Leaves Bitcoin Behind on Upbit\n\nXRP ranked as the most traded cryptocurrency on South Korea’s Upbit, ahead of Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) and Tether (CRYPTO: USDT).\n\nUpbit recorded 11.2 trillion won, or roughly $8 billion, in weekly trading volume, up 6.74% from the previous week, BSCN News noted.\n\nThe heightened activity coincides with XRP’s 8.4% daily rally and its push toward a resistance level that traders have watched for months.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nXRP Skyrockets 6% as Whale Binance Inflows Hit 6-Month High','\n',char(10)),'7354258e26492bd7eedba1ee4d25e639ef53e94c','2026-09-21 13:24:38','2026-09-21 13:29:02.908053',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 13:24:38');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(486,'alpaca:61893682','benzinga','2026-09-21 13:03:59','Microsoft To Rally Over 23%? Here Are 10 Top Analyst Forecasts For Monday','Analysts raised targets for INSP, SECZ, CLF and WAT, while cutting targets for CRDO, CL and TTMI; ratings remained unchanged.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61893682/microsoft-to-rally-over-23-here-are-10-top-analyst-forecasts-for-monday','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-21 13:29:12.003508','analyst','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'Analyst forecasts are speculative and do not guarantee price movement.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 498.48}','{}','2026-09-22 13:33:30.055993','2026-09-21 13:29:02.931339','61893682',replace('Top Wall Street analysts changed their outlook on these top names. For a complete view of all analyst rating changes, including upgrades and downgrades, please see our analyst ratings page.\n\nFreedom Capital Markets raised the price target for Inspire Medical Systems Inc (NYSE:INSP) from $71 to $97. Freedom Capital Markets analyst Keith Hinton maintained a Buy rating. Inspire Medical shares closed at $76.78 on Friday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nRosenblatt increased Securitize Corp (NYSE:SECZ) price target from $11 to $13. Rosenblatt analyst Chris Brendler maintained a Buy rating. Securitize shares closed at $10.86 on Friday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nGLJ Research raised price target for Cleveland-Cliffs Inc (NYSE:CLF) from $15.6 to $17.48. GLJ Research analyst Gordon L. Johnson maintained a Buy rating. Cleveland-Cliffs shares closed at $12.50 on Friday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nMizuho cut the price target for Credo Technology Group Holding Ltd (NASDAQ:CRDO) from $290 to $245. Mizuho analyst Vijay Rakesh maintained an Outperform rating. Credo Technology shares closed at $175.89 on Friday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nPiper Sandler cut Colgate-Palmolive Company (NYSE:CL) price target from $98 to $95. Piper Sandler analyst Michael Lavery maintained an Overweight rating. Colgate-Palmolive shares closed at $87.47 on Friday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nNeedham slashed TTM Technologies Inc (NASDAQ:TTMI) price target from $220 to $175. Needham analyst James Ricchiuti maintained a Buy rating. TTM Technologies shares closed at $117.97 on Friday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nGoldman Sachs increased Waters Corp (NYSE:WAT) price target from $465 to $515. Goldman Sachs analyst Evie Koslosky maintained a Buy rating. Waters shares closed at $421.63 on Friday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nCantor Fitzgerald raised the price target for Microsoft Corp (NYSE:MSFT) from $522 to $608. Cantor Fitzgerald analyst Thomas Blakey maintained an Overweight rating. Microsoft shares closed at $493.78 on Friday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nEvercore ISI Group raised Ciena Corp (NYSE:CIEN) price target from $375 to $550. Evercore ISI Group analyst Amit Daryanani upgraded the stock from In-Line to Outperform. Ciena shares closed at $348.80 on Friday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nJP Morgan cut T-Mobile Us Inc (NASDAQ:TMUS) price target from $275 to $260. JP Morgan analyst Sebastiano Petti maintained an Overweight rating. T-Mobile shares closed at $168.18 on Friday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nConsidering buying MSFT stock? Here’s what analysts think:\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'9774d4a1d3911864d2fadaed295b0e24a846fdd0','2026-09-21 13:03:59','2026-09-21 13:29:02.908053',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 13:03:59');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(487,'alpaca:61893246','benzinga','2026-09-21 12:51:50','Bitcoin Hits 7-Month High as Coinbase CEO Sees $400,000, Says Crypto Won’t Wait for Congress','Bitcoin tops $84,000 as Coinbase CEO Armstrong predicts $300K-$400K by 2030, says $60,000 may be cycle bottom and backs AI, tokenization and crypto growth.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61893246/bitcoin-7-month-high-coinbase-ceo-sees-400000','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 13:29:14.137246','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Bitcoin reaching a 7-month high is notable news and reflects positive market sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 13.014}}','2026-09-22 13:33:30.055993','2026-09-21 13:29:02.940660','61893246',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) surged above $84,000 on Monday as Coinbase Global Inc. (NASDAQ:COIN) CEO Brian Armstrong said the world’s largest cryptocurrency could reach $300,000 to $400,000 by 2030.\n\nHe added that the crypto king’s recent drop to $60,000 may have marked the bottom of the latest cycle.\n\nBitcoin’s $60,000 Bottom in?\n\nArmstrong noted Bitcoin’s historical cycle pattern, where rallies around halving events have typically been followed by downturns lasting roughly a year.\n\n"We’ve just gone through one of those recently," Armstrong told Scott Melker in an interview on Sep.20 pointing to $60,000.\n\n"My hope is by 2030 we could see a $300,000, $400,000 Bitcoin," he said.\n\nArmstrong’s bullish outlook extends beyond Bitcoin’s price. He said stablecoins, perpetual futures, prediction markets and AI-powered finance continue growing regardless of Bitcoin’s short-term swings.\n\nHe also sees AI creating another major use case for blockchain payments.\n\nCoinbase is building infrastructure around its Base blockchain, USDC and the x402 payment protocol.\n\nArmstrong expects the trend to accelerate as AI shifts from answering questions to completing tasks that require spending money.\n\nCrypto Won’t Wait for Congress\n\nArmstrong’s comments come after the Senate failed to advance the Clarity Act, dealing a setback to efforts to establish a permanent U.S. crypto market structure framework.\n\nArmstrong said Coinbase supported the latest draft after lawmakers addressed four major concerns the company previously raised.\n\nHe said he would now operate under the assumption that the legislation is dead unless lawmakers revive it.\n\nThat doesn’t mean crypto regulation stops.\n\nArmstrong expects the SEC and CFTC to use their existing authority to push forward rules covering tokenized equities, perpetual futures and other crypto products.\n\nHe specifically pointed to the SEC’s innovation exemption as a potential route for bringing tokenized stocks to U.S. investors.\n\nCoinbase Wants to “Tokenize Everything“\n\nArmstrong said Coinbase’s tokenization ambitions stretch far beyond publicly traded stocks.\n\n"We want to tokenize everything," he said, pointing to private companies, Treasuries, investment funds and other assets as potential candidates.\n\nArmstrong said tokenized equities can offer 24/7 trading, global access and easier settlement while retaining rights tied to the underlying shares.\n\nPerpetual futures are another product Armstrong expects to gain traction in the U.S., calling them a "pretty killer product" because they combine around-the-clock trading with leverage.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin, Zcash, Hyperliquid in Focus as Industry Expert Sees Crypto Nearing a ''Major Turning Point''','\n',char(10)),'f96420da01568acb9a3339f8c82e13836e80c267','2026-09-21 12:51:50','2026-09-21 13:29:02.908053',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 12:51:50');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(488,'alpaca:61893128','benzinga','2026-09-21 12:47:26','Why Is BitMine Immersion Stock Surging Monday?','BitMine (BMNR) stock jumped over 5% premarket as its Ethereum treasury neared 6M tokens ($17.1B total assets) amidst a crypto rally.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61893128/why-is-bitmine-immersion-stock-surging-monday','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 13:29:15.923316','other','bullish',3,3,'hours',1,'Stock rising due to increased asset value amidst positive market conditions.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 13.014}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 12.919}}','2026-09-22 13:33:30.055993','2026-09-21 13:29:02.944160','61893128',replace('BitMine Immersion Technologies Inc. (NYSE:BMNR) stock rose more than 5% in Monday’s premarket trading as cryptocurrency prices climbed and the company disclosed a larger Ethereum treasury.\n\nBitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) jumped 5.5% over the past 24 hours to $85,262.62. Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) gained 5.9% to $2,728.49.\n\nBroader market sentiment was also positive. Nasdaq futures rose 0.93%, while S&P; 500 futures gained 0.65%.\n\nBitMine Ethereum Holdings Approach 6 Million Tokens\n\nBitMine said Monday that its Ethereum holdings reached 5,983,940 tokens as of Sept. 20.\n\nAt an Ethereum price of $2,688, the position represented about 4.9% of the cryptocurrency’s 122.1 million-token supply.\n\nThe company reported $17.1 billion in total crypto, cash, marketable securities and other investments. That included 212 Bitcoin, $714 million in cash and marketable securities, a $180 million stake in Beast Industries and a $105 million stake in Eightco Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:ORBS).\n\nBitMine said it has staked 5.07 million Ethereum tokens worth about $13.6 billion. That represents roughly 85% of its Ethereum holdings.\n\nThe company estimated annualized staking revenue of about $357 million. Its seven-day annualized staking yield was 2.62%.\n\nChairman Tom Lee said BitMine acquired another 27,562 Ethereum tokens during the past week. He also said he expects institutional crypto exposure to increase during the final quarter of 2026.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nTechnical Analysis\n\nBMNR remains above its major moving averages despite signs that near-term momentum has cooled.\n\nAt Monday’s premarket price, the stock was about 12% above its 20-day simple moving average of $24.48 and roughly 24% above its 200-day average of $22.08.\n\nHowever, MACD remains below its signal line, while the histogram is negative. That suggests recent upside momentum has weakened.\n\nResistance sits near $30.50. Support is around $23, close to key moving-average levels.\n\nThe stock remains well below its 52-week high of $65.60, despite rebounding sharply from its June low of $12.80.\n\nETF Exposure\n\nBMNR is held by several crypto-focused funds, including the Corgi Crypto Infrastructure ETF (NASDAQ:BLCK), Bitwise Crypto Industry Innovators ETF (NYSE:BITQ) and Global X Blockchain ETF (NASDAQ:BKCH).\n\nPrice Action\n\nBMNR Stock Price Activity: BitMine shares rose 5.19% to $27.34 in Monday’s premarket trading, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nWill Howie Buffett Keep Berkshire Ahead of the S&P; 500? What Retail Investors Need to Know','\n',char(10)),'347c9c059f8dd8393cb0794a8d79020d840d1def','2026-09-21 12:47:26','2026-09-21 13:29:02.908053',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 12:47:26');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(489,'alpaca:61892414','benzinga','2026-09-21 12:26:51','What''s Going On With AMD Stock Monday?','AMD gains 3% premarket near 52-week highs. Deep dive into technical indicators, moving averages &amp; Wall Street analyst ratings.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61892414/whats-going-on-with-amd-stock-monday-10','["AMD"]','stocks','2026-09-21 13:29:17.143224','analyst','bullish',3,3,'hours',1,'AMD is showing positive movement in premarket trading and analysis.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78}','{}','2026-09-22 12:33:10.206201','2026-09-21 13:29:02.963356','61892414',replace('Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) stock rose about 3% in Monday’s premarket trading as investors returned to growth stocks. Nasdaq futures gained 0.98%, while S&P; 500 futures rose 0.67%.AMD’s move appears tied largely to the stronger market backdrop. There was no single company-specific headline driving the stock early Monday.Still, AMD remains one of the market’s strongest semiconductor performers. The stock has gained about 250% over the past 12 months and is trading close to its 52-week high.That momentum can make AMD especially sensitive to broader shifts in risk appetite.Technical AnalysisAMD remains in a strong long-term uptrend.At its premarket price of $576.90, the stock was 18.1% above its 20-day simple moving average of $490.75. It was also 16.9% above its 50-day SMA of $495.85 and 63.5% above its 200-day SMA of $354.62.However, the near-term setup is less clear. The 20-day SMA remains below the 50-day average. That bearish crossover can signal consolidation.The broader trend remains bullish because the 50-day SMA is well above the 200-day average.Momentum has also improved. The MACD is above its signal line, while the histogram is positive. That suggests buyers are regaining control after the stock’s previous pullback.Resistance sits near $584.50, close to AMD’s 52-week high. Support is around $498, near its shorter-term moving averages.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nAnalyst OutlookAMD carries a Buy consensus rating with an average price forecast of $604.Piper Sandler initiated coverage Sept. 10 with an Overweight rating and a $600 price forecast. Raymond James upgraded AMD to Strong Buy on Aug. 25 and raised its price forecast to $641. BMO Capital initiated coverage Aug. 21 with an Outperform rating and a $550 price forecast.The stock trades at a price-to-earnings ratio of about 142.8, reflecting a premium valuation.Benzinga Edge RankingsAMD scores highly for momentum, growth and quality on the Benzinga Edge Rankings.Its Momentum score stands at 99.07, while Growth is 95.61 and Quality is 94.57. However, its Value score is just 3.68.The combination reflects AMD’s strong price momentum and growth profile, alongside a valuation that leaves less room for disappointment.Top ETF ExposureThe iShares Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SOXX) has an 8.74% weighting in AMD. The First Trust Nasdaq Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:FTXL) carries a 6.79% weighting, while the Pacer Data and Digital Revolution ETF (NYSE:TRFK) has a 6.52% weighting.Those positions can add another source of trading activity when semiconductor ETFs see heavy inflows or outflows.Price ActionAMD shares rose 3.05% to $576.89 in Monday’s premarket trading, according to Benzinga Pro data.Image via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nMicron Stock Soars 517% in a Year, Jim Cramer Still Calls It ‘Incredibly Cheap’','\n',char(10)),'b917d57b9cdb2314302af4bc6e24688647663f2a','2026-09-21 12:26:51','2026-09-21 13:29:02.908053',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 12:26:51');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(490,'alpaca:61897669','benzinga','2026-09-21 14:22:31','SpaceX Finds Way Around Data Center Moratorium As 300-Plus Restrictions Delay 3 Projects','SpaceX sidestepped Brownsville restrictions as SemiAnalysis says 300+ data-center rules have delayed just three U.S. projects.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61897669/spacex-data-center-moratorium-texas','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-21 14:29:28.926877','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The event details SpaceX''s regulatory challenges without impacting AMZN directly.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18}','{}','2026-09-22 14:33:44.831104','2026-09-21 14:29:24.242675','61897669',replace('Elon Musk’s SpaceX (NASDAQ:SPCX) had roughly 444 acres near Starbase removed from Brownsville’s jurisdiction as the Texas city weighed restrictions on new data centers, a maneuver SemiAnalysis says helps explain why hundreds of local moratoriums have barely dented the U.S. AI buildout.\n\nBrownsville commissioners approved the de-annexation on Aug. 29, putting the 444-acre site outside the city’s zoning authority three days before they voted to begin a 90-day moratorium process. At the same meeting, SpaceX agreed to provide up to $220 million for regional water infrastructure.\n\nSemiAnalysis says SpaceX plans a data center there, although SpaceX has not publicly confirmed the property’s use. \n\n77 Projects Become Just Three\n\nSemiAnalysis, an AI and semiconductor research firm, mapped more than 300 enacted local moratoriums and bans against its U.S. data-center pipeline.\n\nResearchers initially identified 77 campuses, representing roughly 20 gigawatts, inside jurisdictions with data-center restrictions. After checking each project against the local rules, SemiAnalysis found that only three were actually being delayed.\n\nThose three projects total 1,525 megawatts of delayed capacity and include an Amazon campus in Ohio. Adding New York’s statewide executive action lifts SemiAnalysis’s estimate of delayed capacity to about 2.3 GW.\n\nSemiAnalysis says most restrictions never translate into actual delays. A moratorium may not cover the specific site, may expire before the developer needs approval or may arrive after key permits are already in hand. Developers can also qualify for exemptions, redesign projects or move them elsewhere.\n\nSemiAnalysis forecasts roughly 38 GW of U.S. data-center capacity coming online in 2027, more than double 2026, with 22 GW already under construction.\n\nPower Moves off the Grid\n\nThe firm says the restrictions could accelerate “behind-the-meter” development, where data centers generate electricity onsite instead of relying entirely on the grid. It tracks 75 GW of firm equipment orders for such projects, with more of that capacity headed to Texas than any other state.\n\nThat could benefit GE Vernova Inc. (NYSE:GEV) and Bloom Energy Corp. (NYSE:BE), which are already seeing strong demand tied to AI power needs. GE Vernova’s gas-power backlog and slot reservations rose from 100 GW to 116 GW in the second quarter, and the company expects at least 125 GW by year-end.\n\nBloom reported second-quarter revenue of $1.07 billion, up 166% year over year, and said all major U.S. hyperscalers have approved its onsite power systems for their AI infrastructure.\n\nA live Polymarket contract gives a 46% chance that a U.S. state enacts a statewide data-center moratorium by year-end, with about $16,400 wagered. New York’s existing moratorium does not count because it was imposed by executive order, while the market requires a state law.\n\nFor now, SemiAnalysis expects developers to keep relocating projects, redesigning them or bringing their own power rather than abandoning the buildout. The firm said a broad statewide restriction that also covered off-grid projects, particularly in a major market such as Texas, could materially change its buildout forecast.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBrad Gerstner Says AI Labs Need $180B Revenue Run Rate to Keep Nvidia Trade Alive\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'f7407899e4cd831a82572ac9048b8233690a9451','2026-09-21 14:22:31','2026-09-21 14:29:24.238808',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 14:22:31');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(491,'alpaca:61897075','benzinga','2026-09-21 14:10:55','Is Solana''s Next ''Token Supercycle'' Taking Shape? Expert Identifies Three Key Indicators','Solana targets a tokenization boom as institutions adopt its network, with $4 billion in real-world assets, $5 trillion stablecoin volume and major bank involvement.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61897075/solana-token-supercycle-expert-identifies-three-key-indicators','["ETH/USD", "SOL/USD"]','degen','2026-09-21 14:29:30.635095','rumour','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'Speculative commentary on potential future growth of Solana''s market.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"ETH/USD": 2445.59, "SOL/USD": 101.29}','{"ETH/USD": {"60m": 13.489}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": 17.169, "1d": 15.559}}','2026-09-22 14:33:44.831104','2026-09-21 14:29:24.252746','61897075',replace('Solana’s (CRYPTO: SOL) significant jump comes amidst the public blockchain platform positioning for its next growth cycle.\n\nSolana Foundation executive Nick Ducoff highlighted institutional adoption, tokenized assets and stablecoin activity expanding across the network.\n\nSolana’s ‘Token Supercycle‘\n\nDucoff told the Coin Bureau podcast on Sep.18 that Solana now hosts more than $4 billion in real-world assets, has seven global systemically important banks building on the network and has processed nearly $5 trillion in stablecoin volume year-to-date.\n\nHe expects a broader "token super cycle" as money, financial assets and ownership increasingly migrate on chain.\n\nTokenized equities are already showing growing usage on Solana, Ducoff said, as investors seek access to assets ranging from international companies to U.S. pre-IPO firms.\n\nHe expects the long-term migration of money and assets to the internet to increasingly rely on blockchain infrastructure, with Solana positioned to capture some of that activity.\n\nDucoff also argued that the previous meme coin boom strengthened Solana’s institutional case.\n\nHow Wall Street Is Building On SOL\n\nDucoff highlighted institutional deployments involving JPMorgan, Morgan Stanley, Citi, Société Générale, State Street, Standard Chartered and BNY.\n\nAsset managers including BlackRock, Invesco, Apollo and Hamilton Lane have also launched funds or products using Solana, according to Ducoff.\n\nThe products span different investor groups, ranging from permissionless tokenized assets to offerings restricted to accredited or qualified investors.\n\nSolana’s biggest institutional hurdle may be familiarity.\n\nDucoff acknowledged that financial institutions generally have more experience with Ethereum’s (CRYPTO: ETH) EVM than the Solana Virtual Machine.\n\nHowever, he argued Solana’s scalability, capacity and transaction costs could make the SVM increasingly attractive.\n\nThe 3 Key Metrics\n\nDucoff identified real-world assets, bank adoption and network upgrades as three key indicators to watch over the next year.\n\nHe wants the number of global systemically important banks building on Solana to rise from seven to roughly 14, representing about half of the 29 banks in that category.\n\nDucoff pointed to execution on Solana’s scaling roadmap, including independent validator clients and the Alpenglow consensus mechanism.\n\nWill institutional activity translate into sustained network demand as Solana moves beyond the meme coin-driven growth of its previous cycle?\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin, Zcash, Hyperliquid in Focus as Industry Expert Sees Crypto Nearing a ''Major Turning Point''','\n',char(10)),'9d005c77d48c5a90f405419da9b886a739f364a3','2026-09-21 14:10:55','2026-09-21 14:29:24.238808',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 14:10:55');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(492,'alpaca:61896983','benzinga','2026-09-21 14:09:14','Critical Metals, Priority Technology, Meta Platforms And Other Big Stocks Moving Higher On Monday','U.S. stocks rose Monday, with Nasdaq up 1%. Critical Metals jumped 38% on Greenland deal news as tech and other shares broadly gained.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61896983/critical-metals-priority-technology-meta-platforms-and-other-big-stocks-moving-higher-on-monday','["AMD", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-21 14:29:32.802858','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Broad market gains and specific news about Critical Metals driving interest.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-22 14:33:44.831104','2026-09-21 14:29:24.255281','61896983',replace('U.S. stocks were higher, with the Nasdaq Composite gaining over 1% on Monday.\n\nShares of Critical Metals Corp (NASDAQ:CRML) rose sharply during Monday’s session after President Donald Trump announced a U.S.-Denmark agreement that would give the United States permanent control over Greenland’s security, putting the Arctic island’s strategic mineral resources back in focus.\n\nCritical Metals shares jumped 38.3% to $9.30 on Monday.\n\nHere are some other big stocks recording gains in today’s session.\n\nPriority Technology Holdings Inc (NASDAQ:PRTH) gained 33.6% to $7.79 after the company announced an all-cash take-private deal.\n\nNew Era Energy & Digital Inc (NASDAQ:NUAI) rose 25.5% to $7.36 after the company announced a 20-year, 200-207 MW power purchase agreement with Vistra’s Luminant for Texas Data Center Phase 1.\n\nGrail Inc (NASDAQ:GRAL) gained 20.4% to $97.20.\n\nVista Gold Corp (NYSE:VGZ) rose 18.4% to $2.67. Artemis Gold agreed to acquire Vista Gold.\n\nAXT Inc (NASDAQ:AXTI) gained 9.9% to $76.99.\n\nIntel Corp (NASDAQ:INTC) surged 9.2% to $118.62 as chip stocks gained alongside the broader market.\n\nModerna Inc (NASDAQ:MRNA) gained 8.9% to $167.71.\n\nStrategy Inc (NASDAQ:MSTR) gained 8.8% to $167.43 alongside Bitcoin, which is trading around 6% higher.\n\nAdvanced Micro Devices Inc (NASDAQ:AMD) rose 8.5% to $607.84 as investors returned to growth stocks.\n\nArm Holdings PLC – ADR (NASDAQ:ARM) surged 8.4% to $298.75.\n\nMaxlinear Inc (NASDAQ:MXL) rose 8.1% to $87.68.\n\nTwenty One Capital Inc (NYSE:XXI) gained 7.4% to $6.26.\n\nMeta Platforms Inc (NASDAQ:META) rose 6.8% to $710.84. Wells Fargo analyst Ken Gawrelski maintained Meta with an Overweight rating and raised the price target from $640 to $796.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'fe9ab13304f5e1c8ba5b26140aed0979a701f3a6','2026-09-21 14:09:14','2026-09-21 14:29:24.238808',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 14:09:14');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(493,'alpaca:61896484','benzinga','2026-09-21 14:01:34','Why Is Nokia Stock Surging Monday?','Wall Street turns bullish on Nokia (NOK) with Buy ratings &amp; targets up to $21 as AI growth accelerates. Get full stock analysis.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61896484/why-is-nokia-stock-surging-monday','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-21 14:29:34.325306','analyst','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Increased analyst ratings are affecting investor sentiment positively.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 498.48}','{}','2026-09-22 14:33:44.831104','2026-09-21 14:29:24.259482','61896484',replace('Nokia Corporation (NYSE:NOK) stock rose nearly 2% on Monday as the company returned to the EURO STOXX 50 index and investors focused on its growing artificial intelligence exposure.\n\nThe Nasdaq gained 1.38%, while the S&P; 500 rose 0.69%.\n\nNokia officially rejoined the EURO STOXX 50 on Monday. \n\nMeanwhile, Nokia continues to build its AI and cloud presence. The company is expanding its collaboration with Microsoft Corporation (NASDAQ:MSFT), combining Nokia Data Suite with Microsoft Fabric to give telecom operators faster access to network data for AI-driven operations.\n\nThe developments come as analysts turn more constructive. B. Riley Securities initiated coverage with a Buy rating and $15 price target on Sept. 17. Rosenblatt also started coverage with a Buy rating and $15 target on Sept. 15, citing opportunities tied to high-speed optical connectivity.\n\nTechnical Analysis\n\nNokia remains in a constructive longer-term trend. The stock is trading about 9.3% above its 200-day simple moving average of $9.82.\n\nIts 50-day SMA also remains above the 200-day SMA, maintaining the bullish "golden cross" that emerged in October 2025.\n\nHowever, Nokia is still about 10.7% below its 100-day SMA of $12.02. That puts the $12 area in focus if the stock extends its gains.\n\nThe relative strength index stands at 53.94, signaling neutral momentum.\n\nMeanwhile, Nokia is about 4.2% above its 20-day SMA of $10.30 and 6.2% above its 50-day SMA of $10.11.\n\nNear-term resistance sits around $11, while support is near $9.50.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nAnalyst Outlook\n\nThe stock carries a Buy consensus rating with an average price forecast of $16.50.\n\nB. Riley Securities initiated coverage with a Buy rating and $15 price target on Sept. 17. Rosenblatt also started coverage with a Buy rating and $15 target on Sept. 15. JPMorgan maintained an Overweight rating in June and raised its price target to $21.\n\nBenzinga Edge Rankings\n\nNokia has a Benzinga Edge Momentum score of 93.58, indicating strong relative price performance.\n\nIts Quality score is 47.31, Value score is 45.79 and Growth score is 46.77.\n\nInvestors can track Nokia and other stocks using the Benzinga Edge scorecard.\n\nETF Exposure\n\nThe Spear Alpha ETF (NASDAQ:SPRX) has a 4.15% weighting in Nokia.\n\nPrice Action\n\nNOK Price Action: Nokia shares were up 1.69% at $10.86 at the time of publication Monday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nJensen Huang Isn''t ''Afraid'' of Paying $8 Billion in California''s Billionaire Tax: Nvidia CEO Says This Is What Scares Him Instead','\n',char(10)),'4e092711fa090a94c95b28763a821c36b458eafc','2026-09-21 14:01:34','2026-09-21 14:29:24.238808',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 14:01:34');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(494,'alpaca:61895613','benzinga','2026-09-21 13:46:05','Scott Bessent Says AI Companies Must Take Responsibility, Rejects Calls for Federal Liability Shield: ‘It Is Humans Who Are Responsible, Not the AI’','Bessent says AI leaders shouldn’t expect a federal liability shield, arguing humans must remain accountable for AI actions.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/politics/26/09/61895613/scott-bessent-says-ai-companies-must-take-responsibility-rejects-calls-for-federal-liability-shield-it-is-humans-who-are-responsible-not-the-ai','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 14:29:35.517589','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Comments from an industry leader discussing accountability in AI.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-22 14:33:44.831104','2026-09-21 14:29:24.268879','61895613',replace('Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said AI companies should take responsibility for their products rather than rely on a federal “liability shield,” adding to the debate over how Washington should regulate the rapidly developing technology\n\nBessent told CNBC’s Squawk Box on Monday that humans should be held accountable for the actions of their creations, instead of AI.\n\n"It is humans who are responsible, not the AI," the Treasury Secretary said when asked if he backs President Donald Trump’s opposition to a regulatory crackdown on the AI industry amid calls to slow down. \n\nNotably, Trump announced plans to appoint an artificial intelligence adviser, or "AI czar," and create an "AI force" to oversee the industry’s growth.\n\nRead Also:\n\nGoldman Sachs Strategist Sees AI Boom Outpacing Bonds as Higher Rates Raise Market Risks: ''Long compute…Long Neoclouds…Long Data Centers''\n\nBessent Proposes US-China AI Alerts\n\nBessent’s comments came amid concerns from some AI leaders about risks from rapidly advancing models. \n\nOn Sunday, the Treasury Secretary suggested a mechanism for the U.S. and China to notify each other about AI incidents that could affect national security. This proposal was unveiled after a meeting with Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng, just days before a scheduled summit between Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping.\n\nOfficials have not disclosed what would trigger the alert or how the system would work, while Chinese state media only said the two sides discussed AI-related matters without providing details.\n\nMeanwhile, Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang accused AI lab leaders of being "irresponsible" and resorting to "too much drama" in their calls for more AI oversight. Huang suggested that these leaders are not seeking more laws, but rather, they are looking to be relieved of existing laws.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nY Combinator Co-Founder Says AI Labs May be ''Scared Enough'' to Seek Government Regulation: ''Models Could be Dangerous''','\n',char(10)),'531a96f2f782ce8752a710fa91e19b6791e2fc2a','2026-09-21 13:46:05','2026-09-21 14:29:24.238808',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 13:46:05');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(495,'alpaca:61894513','benzinga','2026-09-21 13:32:04','Top 6 Crypto Stocks Climbing with Bitcoin Right Now','Bitcoin crosses $85,000, lifting crypto markets and stocks including MSTR, COIN, HOOD, MARA, RIOT and CLSK.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61894513/top-6-crypto-stocks-climbing-with-bitcoin-right-now','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-21 14:29:36.996296','other','bullish',2,3,'hours',1,'Bitcoin''s price increase is positively influencing related stocks.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "SOL/USD": 101.29, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 13.156}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 13.489}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": 17.051}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 17.724}}','2026-09-22 13:33:30.055993','2026-09-21 14:29:24.277884','61894513',replace('Crypto-linked equities are jumping Monday morning as Bitcoin (CRYPTO:BTC) pushes to fresh multi-month highs, lifting the broader digital-asset market. Here’s how the six most-watched crypto stocks are reacting.\n\nCOIN stock is climbing. See the chart and price action here. \n\nWhy Bitcoin Is Up\n\nBitcoin is trading near $85,400, up roughly 5% over the past 24 hours after crossing $85,000 for the first time since January. Ethereum (CRYPTO:ETH), XRP (CRYPTO:XRP) and Solana (CRYPTO:SOL) are all posting solid gains as well, with the entire crypto market firmly in the green.\n\nA few forces appear to be behind the move. Oil prices have fallen for four straight sessions, easing inflation worries and pulling the 10-year Treasury yield back below the 5% level it touched earlier this month. \n\nRead Also:\n\nThese 10 Stocks Are Squeeze Candidates Waiting to Happen\n\nThis boosted investor confidence that the Federal Reserve’s rate decision on Sept. 16, along with other macro headwinds like the Bank of Japan’s hike and the Senate’s rejection of the Clarity Act, are now priced in. \n\nOn top of that, a wave of short-seller liquidations — hundreds of millions of dollars’ worth — has added forced buying pressure as Bitcoin cleared key resistance levels, accelerating the rally.\n\nCrypto-Linked Stocks Rally\n\nStrategy (NASDAQ:MSTR): Shares traded at $166.23, up 8% in early trading as the Bitcoin-holding company tracks the broader crypto rally.\n\nCoinbase Global (NASDAQ:COIN): Coinbase stock was trading at $204.87, up 5.47% Monday morning as trading volumes and crypto sentiment improved.\n\nRobinhood Markets (NASDAQ:HOOD): Robinhood shares moved to $126.38, up 5.47% in premarket trading, buoyed by renewed retail crypto trading activity.\n\nMarathon Digital Holdings (NASDAQ:MARA): MARA traded at $13.90, up 4.98%, as Bitcoin miners rally alongside the underlying asset’s price surge.\n\nRiot Platforms (NASDAQ:RIOT): Riot shares climbed to $25.04, up 5.42% in Monday trading, according to Benzinga Pro market data.\n\nCleanSpark (NASDAQ:CLSK): CLSK stock rose to $15.17, up 4.92% as miner stocks broadly benefit from Bitcoin’s push toward $85,000.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nThe Bottom Line\n\nWith Bitcoin reclaiming key technical levels and short sellers getting squeezed out of the market, crypto-adjacent equities are seeing outsized gains to start the week. \n\nTraders will be watching whether Bitcoin can hold above $85,000 and whether these stocks can sustain their premarket momentum through the full session.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNetflix Viewer Trends ''Look Worrying'': Wells Fargo Slashes Target on Stock\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'3bc8687218cc1a22c2e462d7f652000e9df215fe','2026-09-21 13:32:04','2026-09-21 14:29:24.238808',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 13:32:04');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(496,'alpaca:61899869','benzinga','2026-09-21 15:24:51','Apple iPhone 18 Estimates Are ''Too Conservative'', Gene Munster Says Duo to Account for 8% of Units','Early demand for the iPhone 18 Pro could signal revenue estimates are too low for Apple, a leading market expert says.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/09/61899869/apple-iphone-18-estimates-are-too-conservative-gene-munster-says-duo-to-account-for-8-of-units','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-21 15:29:44.745987','analyst','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Expert opinion suggests revenue estimates for Apple may be underestimated.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}','2026-09-22 15:34:02.702336','2026-09-21 15:29:40.488597','61899869',replace('Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL) changed things up this year with its iPhone release schedule. The company is releasing the Pro and Pro Max more expensive models first, months before the base iPhone model. A market expert says that move is paying off for the company.\n\nApple’s Decision is Working\n\nApple recently began shipping the iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max, smartphones that come with slight price increases due to rising component costs for the technology giant.\n\nTracking from Deepwater Asset Management Managing Partner Gene Munster shows that these iPhone models are seeing lead times 15% longer than a year ago. This means buyers may be opting for the more expensive iPhone models rather than waiting for the base model’s release in the spring.\n\nThe investor tracks the lead times from eight countries daily. The countries include the United States, United Kingdom, China, Canada, Switzerland, France, Japan and Germany.\n\nMunster said he expected the lead times to be shorter this year.\n\nThe foldable Duo smartphone will begin preorders on Oct. 16 with deliveries on Oct. 23. Munster said the early demand for that phone will show if the trend is continuing of consumers buying the premium more expensive iPhone models and not waiting for the base model in spring 2027.\n\nRead Also:\n\nApple Stock: 64% of Benzinga Viewers Have Owned It. Here’s How Many Still Do\n\nAre Street Estimates Too Low?\n\nConsensus estimates for iPhone revenue in fiscal 2027 are $9.5 billion, according to Munster.\n\n"I think the Street is still 10% too low on iPhone revenue for FY27," Munster said.\n\nMunster said estimates show only around 4.5 million Duo sales expected in fiscal 2026, but the revenue estimate may not account for this $2,100 average selling price phone.\n\nThe investor said it may be hard for Apple to win over some existing foldable smartphone users from rival companies, but the Duo could hit 35% market share in its first year.\n\n"I would consider that an understandable outlook, but also too conservative."\n\nMunster estimates that a third of Pro Max users could make the jump to Duo, which could increase iPhone revenue by 10%, due to the higher average selling prices. The investor estimates that the Duo will make up around 8% of iPhone units next year and 14% of iPhone revenue.\n\nApple Stock Price Action\n\nApple stock is up 0.1% to $336.48 on Monday versus a 52-week trading range of $243.42 to $344.57. Apple stock is up 24.2% year-to-date in 2026.\n\nRead Also:\n\nApple Duo Foldable iPhone a ‘Must Have Product,’ Gary Black Says ‘Don’t Underestimate the Power of the $AAPL Marketing Machine’\n\nApple iPhone 18 Pro | Photo courtesy: Apple','\n',char(10)),'9d4e70190dff994e265b5f57ce2226ac0eec0829','2026-09-21 15:24:51','2026-09-21 15:29:40.484649',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 15:24:51');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(497,'alpaca:61899751','benzinga','2026-09-21 15:20:47','Strategy Buys 950 Bitcoin For $76M as MSTR Surges 8%: What''s Going On?','Strategy buys 950 Bitcoin for $75.7 million as MSTR extends its rally with an 8% premarket gain.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61899751/strategy-buys-950-bitcoin-for-76m-as-mstr-surges-8-whats-going-on','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 15:29:46.028170','other','neutral',3,3,'hours',1,'A significant purchase of Bitcoin by Strategy, but lacking details on future implications.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 13.156}}','2026-09-22 15:34:02.702336','2026-09-21 15:29:40.492517','61899751',replace('Strategy (NASDAQ:MSTR) bought 950 Bitcoin for $75.7 million last week, ending another month without purchases as the stock surges another 8% in Monday’s session following Friday’s 16% rally.\n\nWhat the Filing Shows\n\nAccording to a Monday 8-K filing with the SEC, Strategy acquired the Bitcoin between Sept. 14 and Sept. 20 at an average price of $79,670 per coin. \n\nTotal holdings now stand at 846,000 Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC), worth roughly $71.9 billion, bought at an average price of $75,416 per coin for a total cost of $63.8 billion including fees.\n\nThat stake equals more than 4% of Bitcoin’s 21 million supply cap and implies roughly $8.1 billion in paper gains at current prices.\n\nThe company also repurchased 1.77 million STRC preferred shares for around $174 million and used $57.4 million to fund dividends on preferred stock and interest on outstanding debt.\n\nAs of Sept. 20, the USD Reserve stood at $5.04 billion with USD Cash at $1.05 billion.\n\nWhy This Purchase Matters\n\nAs Benzinga reported last week, Strategy skipped Bitcoin purchases for two straight weeks through Sept. 13, funneling capital instead toward STRC buybacks as the preferred stock struggled to hold par value. \n\nThat drought followed a single Bitcoin purchase on Aug. 31, when Saylor ended a two-month freeze by buying 4,603 BTC. \n\nLast week’s 950 BTC purchase marks the first real follow-through since that late-August buy, suggesting the STRC stabilization effort has freed up room for renewed accumulation.\n\nExecutive Chairman Michael Saylor posted Strategy’s acquisition tracker chart on X Sunday with the caption “A little more orange,” a signal that has historically preceded purchase announcements.\n\nMSTR Price Analysis: Key Levels to Watch\n\nMSTR closed Friday up 16.39% at $153.92, breaking decisively above its descending trendline from the May $199 high and reclaiming the 200-day EMA at $152.12 for the first time since the peak. \n\nMonday’s trading extends the move to $167.25, up another 8.6% at the time of publication, confirming follow-through rather than a fade.\n\nKey levels for MSTR:\n\n$180 — May consolidation zone, next major test\n\n$152.12 — 200-day EMA, Friday’s breakout level\n\nRead Also:\n\nCoinbase Stock Climbs Monday as Bitcoin Surges Past $85,000\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'9cfbb5f0d802455e9fa515898654f1fc0aba65c4','2026-09-21 15:20:47','2026-09-21 15:29:40.484649',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 15:20:47');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(498,'alpaca:61899004','benzinga','2026-09-21 14:58:06','Meta Stock Is Surging: What''s Happening Today?','Meta Platforms shares are popping Monday. Wells Fargo raised its price target on the stock ahead of this week&#39;s Meta Connect event.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61899004/meta-stock-is-surging-whats-happening-today','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-21 15:29:47.881945','analyst','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Wells Fargo raised its price target on Meta ahead of an event.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-22 15:34:02.702336','2026-09-21 15:29:40.501374','61899004',replace('Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) shares are popping Monday. Wells Fargo raised its price target on the stock, with additional excitement building around this week’s Meta Connect event. Here’s what you should know.\n\nMeta Platforms stock is charging ahead with explosive momentum. Why is META stock up today?\n\nWells Fargo Raises its Meta Price Target to $796\n\nWells Fargo analyst Ken Gawrelski maintained an Overweight rating on Meta while raising his price target to $796 from $640 on September 21. Meta carries an overall Buy rating on Wall Street, with an average price target of $780.58.\n\nOther recent analyst actions include Citigroup maintaining a Buy rating with an $800 target on September 16, and Rosenblatt maintaining a Buy rating with an $886 target the same day.\n\nMeta Connect Kicks Off This Week\n\nMeta’s annual Connect event begins Wednesday, September 23, with a keynote at 7 p.m. ET led by founder and CEO Mark Zuckerberg, who is expected to lay out the company’s broader product vision.\n\nThe event continues Thursday, September 24, with a developer-focused state of the union session at 1 p.m. ET, where Meta representatives plan to detail new tools and technologies for developers building on the company’s platforms.\n\nMeta Introduces Muse, a New Personal AI Agent\n\nAdding to the buildup, Meta recently introduced Muse, a personal AI agent built to carry out tasks and work toward a person’s goals rather than just answer questions. Muse runs on a dedicated secure virtual machine, communicates through the Muse app or WhatsApp and can independently browse the web, fill out forms and complete purchases on a person’s behalf, checking in for approval before sensitive actions.\n\nMeta built Muse around significant privacy and security controls, including an isolated computing environment, no visibility into a user’s passwords or payment details, and full user control over which apps the agent can access. Muse is rolling out now in the U.S. on iOS, Android and muse.ai, with support for Meta’s AI glasses coming soon, and is free for most everyday use.\n\nMETA Shares Are Jumping\n\nMETA Price Action: Meta shares were up 6.83% at $711.20 at the time of publication on Monday, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAI Investment Boom Is ''Massive'' — Top Economist Says US Spending Is Moving Away From Homes and Toward Data Centers\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'30cba83f1a98a594c1ff65f38a942a8540950e5a','2026-09-21 14:58:06','2026-09-21 15:29:40.484649',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 14:58:06');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(499,'alpaca:61898941','benzinga','2026-09-21 14:55:53','SpaceX’s Nasdaq-100 Weight Just More Than Doubled. Here’s Where ETF Money Is Heading','SpaceX’s Nasdaq-100 weighting jumps to 2.82%, triggering billions in potential passive buying. Here’s what the rebalance means for QQQ, QQQM and other ETFs.','https://www.benzinga.com/etfs/broad-u-s-equity-etfs/26/09/61898941/spacexs-nasdaq-100-weight-just-more-than-doubled-heres-where-etf-money-is-heading','["QQQ"]','stocks','2026-09-21 15:29:49.338636','macro','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Increased weighting may lead to increased ETF buying pressure.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 716.89}','{}','2026-09-22 15:34:02.702336','2026-09-21 15:29:40.504189','61898941',replace('SpaceX (NASDAQ:SPCX) is about to become a much bigger piece of the ETF universe, and investors may feel the impact even if they never buy the stock directly.\n\nThe space and satellite company will represent 2.82% of the Nasdaq-100 after Monday’s quarterly rebalance, more than doubling its current 1.28% weighting, according to Bloomberg data. The final weight was calculated using Friday’s closing prices. \n\nThe shift is notable because SpaceX is already the seventh-largest Nasdaq-100 company by market capitalization, with a value above $2 trillion. Its relatively small initial index weight reflected the limited public float following its July IPO.\n\nNow, the gap is narrowing — and passive funds have to follow.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nQQQ Isn’t the Only ETF Buying SpaceX\n\nThe obvious beneficiary of the rebalance is the Invesco QQQ Trust (NASDAQ:QQQ), which had about $484 billion in assets as of Sep. 19. A move from 1.28% to 2.82% would imply roughly $7.4 billion of additional SpaceX exposure for QQQ, assuming its asset base remained unchanged.\n\nBut QQQ isn’t the only vehicle affected.\n\nThe Invesco Nasdaq 100 ETF (NASDAQ:QQQM) had about $106 billion in assets as of Sept. 19 and tracks the same index. The new weighting would imply roughly $1.6 billion of additional SpaceX exposure for QQQM on the same static-AUM assumption. \n\nAnd the Nasdaq-100 ecosystem is considerably larger than those two ETFs. Nasdaq’s own data show that the benchmark is linked to $351 billion in QQQ assets, $53 billion in QQQM, $41 billion in leveraged/inverse ETFs and another $94 billion in other ETFs, based on average 2025 AUM. \n\nMarket estimates have put the broader passive buying associated with the rebalance at roughly $15.5 billion to $22 billion.\n\nChanging What ‘Nasdaq Exposure’ Means\n\nThe bigger story for ETF investors is concentration.\n\nThe Nasdaq-100 was already heavily tilted toward mega-cap companies. As of mid-June, its top 10 holdings accounted for roughly 46% of the index, according to Direxion. SpaceX’s new 2.82% weighting adds another major company to that concentration.\n\nThat creates an interesting contrast with the Direxion NASDAQ-100 Equal Weighted ETF (NASDAQ:QQQE). Rather than allowing the biggest companies to dominate, QQQE resets each Nasdaq-100 constituent to roughly equal weight at its quarterly rebalance. SpaceX therefore doesn’t become a 2.82% position simply because its market value exploded. \n\nThe impact also extends to leveraged Nasdaq ETFs. ProShares UltraPro QQQ (NASDAQ:TQQQ), which seeks 3x the daily performance of the Nasdaq-100, already had 1.05% exposure to SpaceX as of Sep. 18, according to ProShares. The fund uses a combination of individual securities, index swaps and futures to obtain its targeted exposure.\n\nThe ETF Takeaway\n\nSpaceX’s rising Nasdaq-100 weight is more than an index housekeeping exercise. It is gradually turning the newly public company into a built-in allocation across a huge ecosystem of passive and leveraged products.\n\nFor investors holding QQQ or QQQM, Monday’s rebalance means a materially larger automatic SpaceX exposure. For investors using equal-weight Nasdaq strategies, the effect is much more limited.\n\nAnd that difference matters: the same "Nasdaq" label can now mean very different levels of SpaceX exposure depending on how an ETF weights its holdings.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAI Investment Boom Is ''Massive'' — Top Economist Says US Spending Is Moving Away From Homes and Toward Data Centers\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'98ace9f981abc3e88e9dbfa161a36dd6efea79a8','2026-09-21 14:55:53','2026-09-21 15:29:40.484649',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 14:55:53');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(500,'alpaca:61898703','benzinga','2026-09-21 14:48:43','Bitcoin, Ethereum, XRP Surge as $400 Million in Shorts Get Liquidated','Bitcoin tops $85,000 as a short squeeze wipes out $400 million, ETF inflows rebound and falling oil prices support crypto.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61898703/bitcoin-ethereum-xrp-surge-400-million-in-shorts-get-liquidated','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD", "XRP/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 15:29:50.647345','other','bullish',5,5,'hours',1,'A significant liquidation event and positive market conditions have driven up cryptocurrency prices.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 13.156}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 13.489}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 19.192, "1d": 21.599}}','2026-09-22 15:34:02.702336','2026-09-21 15:29:40.507899','61898703',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) surged above $85,000 for the first time in nine months Monday, liquidating over $400 million in leveraged shorts.\n\nWhat Triggered the Rally\n\nThe Kobeissi Letter posted on X Monday that the shorts got wiped out in just four hours, a classic squeeze accelerating an already strong move.\n\nU.S. spot Bitcoin ETFs added to the momentum, pulling in $593 million over Thursday and Friday alone last week to fully reverse earlier weekly outflows and close the week with a modest net inflow according to SoSoValue.\n\nCoinDesk reported Monday that oil helped fuel the move, with Brent crude falling for a fourth straight session, its longest losing streak in three months, as diplomatic signals between Washington and Tehran pointed toward easing tensions. \n\nMeanwhile, Donald Trump told Fox News he would “probably” meet Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian at this week’s UN General Assembly. \n\nHow Crypto-Linked Stocks Reacted\n\nCrypto equities rallied alongside the token rally Monday:\n\nCompanyTickerMoveStrategy(NASDAQ:MSTR)+6%Strive Asset Management(NASDAQ:ASST)+6%MARA Holdings(NASDAQ:MARA)+6%Bullish(NYSE:BLSH)+5%Coinbase(NASDAQ:COIN)+5%Robinhood(NASDAQ:HOOD)+4%Trader Notes\n\nBTC, ETH, XRP Price Analysis: Key Levels to Watch\n\nBitcoin breaks decisively out of its descending triangle Monday, surging to $84,220 and touching $85,257 intraday, its highest level since the September 3 high near $82,700. \n\nRSI at 70.19 marks its strongest reading since early September, confirming genuine momentum rather than a weak retest.\n\nResistance: $85,257 (fresh territory)\n\nSupport: $81,000 (breakout retest), $75,559 (SAR)\n\nXRP (CRYPTO: XRP) jumps 5.5%, clearing the symmetrical triangle that compressed price for five weeks. The entire EMA stack now sits below price as support.\n\nResistance: $1.55 to $1.56 (August supply zone)\n\nSupport: $1.37 (20-day EMA)\n\nEthereum (CRYPTO: ETH) climbs 2.5% to $2,714, clearing both the 0.618 Fibonacci retracement of its October 2025 to January 2026 decline and its long descending trendline from the $3,396 high in the same move.\n\nResistance: $2,990 (0.786 Fib)\n\nSupport: $2,672 (breakout retest)\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Hits 7-Month High as Coinbase CEO Sees $400,000, Says Crypto Won’t Wait for Congress\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'33613a3e34f96be3f42dfb922ff2b316d1ebc2c3','2026-09-21 14:48:43','2026-09-21 15:29:40.484649',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 14:48:43');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(501,'alpaca:61898194','benzinga','2026-09-21 14:35:47','Einride Taps NVIDIA to Put More Self-Driving Trucks on the Highway','Einride partners with NVIDIA to scale autonomous electric trucks using the DRIVE Hyperion platform and Blackwell AI computing.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61898194/einride-taps-nvidia-to-put-more-self-driving-trucks-on-the-highway','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 15:29:51.845466','partnership','bullish',3,4,'weeks',1,'Partnership with NVIDIA could enhance product capabilities and market presence.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-22 15:34:02.702336','2026-09-21 15:29:40.514231','61898194',replace('Einride AB (NASDAQ:ENRD) said Monday it entered a strategic collaboration with NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) to accelerate the development and deployment of autonomous heavy-duty trucks across highway and suburban routes.\n\nEinride will build the next generation of its autonomous-driving system, known as the Einride Driver, on NVIDIA’s DRIVE Hyperion platform.\n\nThe companies will adapt NVIDIA’s compute, sensor, software and safety architecture for heavy-duty freight operations. The collaboration is expected to support Einride’s broader push into highway and suburban autonomous trucking.\n\nTargets Bigger Autonomous Fleet\n\nEinride operates hundreds of electric trucks for major shippers across the U.S., Europe and the Middle East. Its network also includes autonomous trucks in contracted customer deployments.\n\nThe company expects its fleet to expand to 1,500 to 2,000 vehicles by 2028. The company said said about 80% of the demand currently captured on its platform could be suitable for automation over the medium term.\n\nEinride develops its autonomous-driving system in-house. That includes safety validation, regulatory approvals and customer deployments. NVIDIA provides the underlying computing platform and AI development tools.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nNVIDIA AI Tools Support Development\n\nThe company plans to use NVIDIA Blackwell infrastructure through an NVIDIA Exemplar Cloud partner to train and test its autonomous-driving models.\n\nIt is also using NVIDIA Cosmos to identify difficult driving scenarios and create synthetic training data. Einride said this could improve the diversity of data used to train and validate its autonomous vehicles.\n\nNVIDIA Hyperion provides a production-ready compute and sensor architecture designed for Level 4 autonomous driving.\n\nEinride Chief Technology Officer Henrik Green said the collaboration could help the company scale autonomous deployments across its existing freight network.\n\nPrice Action\n\nENRD Price Action: Einride shares were down 5.28% at $3.72 at the time of publication on Monday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla''s 500-Semi Einride Order Finally Gets a Timeline: ''75 Approximately'' This Year, CEO Says','\n',char(10)),'7d057a22d62477885743d9628953a672cd72aa73','2026-09-21 14:35:47','2026-09-21 15:29:40.484649',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 14:35:47');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(502,'alpaca:61898099','benzinga','2026-09-21 14:33:08','Bitmine Buys 27,562 ETH as Tom Lee Says Crypto''s Bull Market Is ''Underway''','Bitmine buys 27,562 Ethereum, nearing its 5% supply target, as Tom Lee declares the crypto bull market underway.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61898099/bitmine-buys-27562-eth-as-tom-lee-says-cryptos-bull-market-is-underway','["ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 15:29:52.968436','mna','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'A notable purchase of ETH by Bitmine and a bullish market declaration.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"ETH/USD": {"60m": 13.489}}','2026-09-22 14:33:44.831104','2026-09-21 15:29:40.516983','61898099',replace('Bitmine Immersion Technologies (NYSE:BMNR) bought 27,562 Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) last week as Chairman Tom Lee declared the crypto bull market already underway.\n\nWhat the Latest Purchase Shows\n\nAccording to a Monday press release, Bitmine now holds 5.98 million ETH worth roughly $16.08 billion at current prices, representing 4.9% of Ethereum’s total supply and putting the company 98% of the way to its 5% target. \n\nBitmine has bought ETH every single week since launching its treasury strategy on June 30, 2025. \n\nTotal crypto plus cash holdings now stand at $17.1 billion, with 5.07 million ETH staked through its MAVAN platform generating projected annualized staking revenue of $357 million.\n\nWhy Lee Sees the Bull Market Underway\n\nLee pointed to Ethereum’s Q3 outperformance as the clearest signal, with ETH beating the S&P; 500 by 6,519 basis points quarter to date, up sharply from the 5,866 basis points Bitmine flagged just two weeks earlier. \n\nHe attributes the move to a rotation away from AI stocks back into crypto, strengthening fundamentals around tokenization and AI infrastructure, and the ending of the four-year cycle.\n\nLee expects institutions to substantially increase crypto exposure in the final three months of 2026, arguing they entered the year underweight after AI stocks dominated early gains. \n\nHe sees Q3’s outperformance as a prelude to a stronger Q4 move rather than the peak of the trend. Lee delivers the keynote at Korea Blockchain Week on September 30 in Seoul.\n\nWhere Bitmine Ranks Among Crypto Treasuries\n\nBitmine remains the largest Ethereum treasury in the world and the second largest crypto treasury globally, trailing only Strategy (NASDAQ:MSTR), which holds 846,000 BTC worth approximately $75 billion. \n\nBitmine also holds a $105 million stake in Eightco Holdings (NASDAQ:ORBS), giving investors indirect exposure to OpenAI through a public equity.\n\nTrading volume tells its own story: Bitmine’s average daily dollar volume hit $1.2 billion over the past five days, ranking 100th among all 5,704 US-listed stocks, ahead of established names like Ciena Corp.\n\nBMNR Price Analysis: Key Levels to Watch\n\nBMNR climbed 6% Monday, breaking cleanly above the $24 resistance zone that capped every rally since February. \n\nThe move also clears the ascending channel that has guided the recovery since the July $13 low, signaling acceleration rather than another retest. \n\nRSI at 64.72 sits above its moving average and climbing, confirming momentum without stretching into overbought territory.\n\nKey levels for BMNR:\n\n$24 — 20-day EMA, now flipped to support\n\n$22.5 — 200-day EMA, deeper support below\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'ceba86450869ad2dc51278956ea185bce52a6457','2026-09-21 14:33:08','2026-09-21 15:29:40.484649',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 14:33:08');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(503,'alpaca:61901669','benzinga','2026-09-21 16:19:52','This Analyst Raises Price Targets For Microsoft And This AI Infrastructure Stock','Cantor Fitzgerald raised Microsoft’s and ServiceNow’s price targets, citing AI demand and security opportunities.','https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/price-target/26/09/61901669/this-analyst-raises-price-targets-for-microsoft-and-this-ai-infrastructure-stock','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-21 16:30:01.657236','analyst','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst raises imply improved outlook based on demand factors.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 498.48}','{}','2026-09-22 16:34:19.642738','2026-09-21 16:29:56.408732','61901669',replace('In a note covering infrastructure and AI Software, Cantor Fitzgerald analyst Thomas Blakey raised the price targets for:\n\nMicrosoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT) – from $522 to $608, while maintaining an Overweight rating.\n\nServiceNow Inc (NYSE:NOW) – from $141 to $174, while reiterating an Overweight rating.\n\nSoftware as a group has declined by 1.4% year-to-date, versus an 11.4% gain in the S&P500; and NASDAQ rising 13.6%, respectively, while the PHLX Semiconductor Sector Index (NASDAQ:SOX) has been the best-performing tech index up 65.7%, analyst Blakey noted.\n\nCheck out other analyst stock ratings.\n\nMicrosoft: The analyst highlighted the following initiatives:\n\nPartnered with Marvell Technology Inc (NASDAQ:MRVL) and privately-held Utimaco to launch Azure Payment HSM v2, a managed cloud payment-security platform.\n\nPublished a provisional AI Code of Conduct setting model behavior standards, emphasizing human autonomy, and warning against user dependency or sycophancy.\n\nMicrosoft recently reorganized its business segments, shifting slower-growth industry solutions like Healthcare out of Azure and moving higher-growth businesses, such as GitHub Cloud and Security, into Microsoft 365 Cloud, Blakey said.\n\nAzure’s underlying growth is accelerating, supported by faster capacity rollouts and hardware/software efficiency gains, the analyst stated. Despite operational improvements, overall demand continues to outpace available infrastructure capacity, he further noted.\n\nServiceNow: "We expect the uptick in agentic AI to drive modernizations and security demand higher, favoring infrastructure and security software in general and specifically platform plays in our coverage," Blakey wrote.\n\nInvestor sentiment on ServiceNow has turned positive, driven by strong AI-driven tier upgrades and growing demand for security-focused agentic platforms, the analyst stated.\n\nDespite stock pressure from revenue adjustments, steady organic growth of between 18%-20.5%) and strong US Federal performance position the company well to meet its expanding AI targets, he added.\n\nMSFT, NOW Price Action: Shares of Microsoft had risen by 0.08% to $494.2, while ServiceNow’s stock by 1.71% to $137.45 at the time of publication on Monday.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAI Investment Boom Is ''Massive'' — Top Economist Says US Spending Is Moving Away From Homes and Toward Data Centers\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'b82cf74dd7bcb0938a9a7382576ffc1b8c2ad247','2026-09-21 16:19:52','2026-09-21 16:29:56.403778',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 16:19:52');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(504,'alpaca:61901357','benzinga','2026-09-21 16:09:38','Coinbase Wins Either Way? Why a Dead Bill Isn''t Bad News','The stalled CLARITY Act delays Coinbase’s long-term regulatory upside, but trading volume, volatility and new revenue streams support COIN now.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61901357/coinbase-wins-either-way-dead-bill-isnt-bad-news','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 16:30:03.937279','regulatory','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The article discusses the implications of stalled legislation without indicating any immediate impact.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 13.156}}','2026-09-22 16:34:19.642738','2026-09-21 16:29:56.417493','61901357',replace('The Senate’s crypto market structure bill flatlined again last week. A cloture vote on the CLARITY Act failed 49-50, with Democrats citing unresolved ethics provisions tied to Trump’s crypto business interests and a handful of Republicans crossing over to sink it. \n\nCOIN stock is up today. See the real-time price action here. \n\nNo Clarity Yet\n\nThe bill needed 60 votes to advance and would have handed the CFTC primary authority over digital assets. Coinbase Global Inc. (NASDAQ:COIN) shares dipped on the news, the usual reflex whenever “regulatory clarity” stalls.\n\nBut the stock’s reflexive dip misreads what’s actually driving Coinbase’s numbers. The company spent over a year publicly pushing for this legislation, and even torched a January markup by pulling its support the night before the vote over stablecoin and DeFi language it didn’t like. \n\nRead Also:\n\nThese 10 Stocks Are Squeeze Candidates Waiting to Happen\n\nThe lobbying was real, but it was aimed at 2027 and beyond. Even a passed bill would still need an estimated 45 separate agency rulemakings across the SEC, CFTC and Treasury before it changed how the business runs day to day. \n\nA dead cloture vote doesn’t erase revenue Coinbase is already collecting. It pushes the structural upside further out, roughly where most people already expected it to land.\n\nVolume Pays the Bills Now\n\nThe current model is holding up fine without the bill. William Blair analysts Andrew Jeffrey and Adib Choudhury cut their 2026 revenue estimate for Coinbase, according to the Block, but see earnings troughing in the back half of the year before rebounding in 2027. \n\nThey expect total trading volume to fall roughly 44% this year before rebounding more than 32% in 2027, and they argue this cycle is structurally different from 2022. Spot Bitcoin ETFs now exist, institutional flows have deepened and the regulatory backdrop has already matured even without new legislation.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nPut simply, Coinbase doesn’t need Congress to hand it a rulebook to keep monetizing volume and volatility. Retail derivatives revenue alone has already crossed $200 million annualized, and the same analysts point to prediction markets as further diversification beyond spot trading fees.\n\nShort-term, Coinbase’s P&L; runs on how much people trade and how wildly prices swing — both have kept the lights on through a choppy 2026 regardless of what the Senate does. \n\nLong-term, an eventual CLARITY-style framework opens product lines Coinbase can’t fully build under today’s patchwork rules for tokenized securities and broader derivatives access. \n\nThe bill’s death last week doesn’t kill either story. It confirms the rulemaking dividend was never a 2026 catalyst to begin with.\n\nCOIN Stock Price Activity: Coinbase stock was up 5.08% at $204.12 at the time of publication Monday, according to data from Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNetflix Viewer Trends ''Look Worrying'': Wells Fargo Slashes Target on Stock\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'72c5aa171da5e16297e9fa48c2ac065d93559622','2026-09-21 16:09:38','2026-09-21 16:29:56.403778',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 16:09:38');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(505,'alpaca:61900672','benzinga','2026-09-21 15:49:01','$6.51 Diesel Should Be Crushing the Economy: Here’s Why It Has Rarely Grown Faster','Despite record fuel prices, U.S. growth remains strong, driven by resilient consumer spending and a surge in AI-related corporate investment.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/macro-economic-events/26/09/61900672/6-51-diesel-should-be-crushing-the-economy-heres-why-it-has-rarely-grown-faster','["AMZN", "META", "MSFT", "QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-21 16:30:05.310988','macro','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The statement discusses broader economic trends without direct implications for specific assets.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48, "QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-22 16:34:19.642738','2026-09-21 16:29:56.461319','61900672',replace('The national average price of a gallon of diesel has hit a record $6.51, while gasoline remains near historic highs.\n\nYet, the U.S. economy does not seem to care.\n\n • State Street SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust stock is moving in positive territory. Why are SPY shares climbing?\n\nThe Federal Reserve Bank of Atlanta’s GDPNow model estimates third-quarter real gross domestic product growth at 5.1% on a seasonally adjusted annual rate, as of Sept. 21.\n\nThose two numbers reveal the strangest feature of the U.S. economy. \n\nA 5.1% growth would be the strongest rate since the fourth quarter of 2021. Excluding the post-COVID-19 pandemic rebound, it would be the strongest since the second quarter of 2014.\n\nSince 2000, the economy has grown faster than 5.1% in only eight of 106 quarters.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nThe Fuel That Moves Goods Has Never Cost More\n\nDiesel sits inside almost everything Americans buy. \n\nIt powers trucks, farms, construction equipment and parts of the manufacturing supply chain.\n\nAt the start of the war against Iran in late February, the national average was about $3.76 a gallon. Diesel is now 73% above that level. \n\nRegular gasoline, at $4.48 a gallon, is up about 41% from a year ago, according to AAA.\n\nThat should operate like a tax on companies and households. Freight becomes more expensive, margins narrow and consumers have less money left for other purchases.\n\nYet August retail sales jumped 1.2% from July and 6% from a year earlier.\n\nEven after stripping out cars, gasoline, building materials and restaurants, core sales recorded a 1.4% monthly gain. That would be the strongest since September 2024.\n\nThe data says U.S. consumers remain strong despite sky-high fuel prices. \n\n“The nominal economy is booming,” Bank of America economist Aditya Bhave said in a recent note. \n\nBank of America raised its third-quarter personal consumption growth estimate to 3.4% from 2.6%. GDPNow is even stronger, tracking real consumer spending at 4.1%.\n\nRead Also:\n\nExxonMobil Stock Falls Monday: What''s Happening?\n\nAI Investment Is Acting Like Private-Sector Stimulus\n\nConsumption is only half the story. \n\nThe second engine is corporate investment in data centers, chips and software.\n\nMicrosoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT), Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN), Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOGL) and Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) plan to spend about $725 billion combined on capital expenditures in 2026, up 77% from $410 billion last year.\n\nThat money flows into data centers, chips, electrical equipment, cooling systems and power generation. It creates income far beyond the technology sector.\n\nOn Sept. 10, GDPNow was tracking third-quarter real private investment growth at 19.1% annualized. AI is not the entire category, but it is a major force behind the expansion. \n\nOn Monday, Chicago Fed President Austan Goolsbee said AI investment could be "spilling out of its own lane and raising aggregate output beyond what the economy can absorb."\n\nNotably, this spending is largely insensitive to fuel costs.\n\nThe Fed Has Started Hiking Into The Boom\n\nStrong growth and energy-driven inflation have pushed the Fed to act.\n\nOn Sept. 16, the Federal Open Market Committee voted 12-0 to raise its benchmark rate by a quarter point, to a range of 3.75% to 4%. \n\nIt was the first increase since July 2023. Sixteen of the 18 participants who submitted projections expect another hike this year.\n\nBhave said strong nominal growth gives Fed Chair Kevin Warsh little reason to stop. Bank of America’s base case is a total of 75 basis points in hikes. \n\nBhave flagged two risks: wages could re-accelerate if unemployment keeps falling, and the Iran conflict could leave more inflation in the pipeline than expected. \n\nIn that case, the Fed would face a choice between tolerating above-target inflation for longer or slowing demand more sharply, at the risk of a recession.\n\nWhat It Means For Investors\n\nA strong economy and booming earnings have supported risk assets, despite high inflation and rising interest rates.\n\nThe SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) is up about 12.8% year to date, while the Invesco QQQ Trust Series 1 (NASDAQ:QQQ) has gained roughly 19.6%. \n\nBoth are on track for their fourth straight year of gains.\n\nChipmakers have led the rally. \n\nThe iShares Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SOXX) has surged about 83% since the start of the year, the clearest market expression of the AI investment boom.\n\nLong-duration bonds have faced the opposite setup.\n\nThe iShares 20+ Year Treasury Bond ETF (NASDAQ:TLT) is down about 6.3% year to date. On Sept. 15, it closed at $80.71, below its October 2023 low. \n\nBond prices fall when yields rise, and investors are demanding more to lend long-term to a government facing hotter growth, sticky energy inflation and a hiking Fed.\n\nWhat the data shows so far is an economy absorbing a record fuel shock without slowing, and a central bank that now sees that strength as a reason to keep tightening.\n\nRead Also:\n\nFed’s Goolsbee Sounds the Alarm on Inflation: October Hike Odds Stay Above 50%','\n',char(10)),'655212c88a60b740a5450290ac413275cb4b9411','2026-09-21 15:49:01','2026-09-21 16:29:56.403778',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 15:49:01');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(506,'alpaca:61900525','benzinga','2026-09-21 15:44:26','''No One Violates Privacy Like Meta'': Scott Galloway Says Years of User Data Could Become an AI Advantage','Scott Galloway says Meta’s years of user data could give Muse an AI edge even if its models lag Anthropic and OpenAI.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61900525/meta-user-data-ai-advantage-galloway','["AMZN", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-21 16:30:06.948522','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Commentary on potential competitive advantages of user data in AI.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-22 16:34:19.642738','2026-09-21 16:29:56.465111','61900525',replace('NYU Stern professor and entrepreneur Scott Galloway says Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) may be turning years of user data into an AI advantage as its new Muse agent gains traction.\n\n"No one violates privacy like Meta," Galloway said on Prof G Markets, arguing that the personal context Meta has accumulated could make Muse more useful than rivals starting from scratch.\n\nMeta Already Knows You\n\nGalloway called Meta "the largest first-party data miner in history," saying CEO Mark Zuckerberg understands the value of information accumulated through Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp.\n\nGalloway said Muse can start with context about where users eat and live and who their friends are that another AI company might take "years to build."\n\nMuse, launched Sept. 8, can send emails, book travel, shop and carry out tasks across services users choose to connect. Meta says users decide how much access the agent receives.\n\nThe app climbed to the No. 1 spot among free apps on Apple’s U.S. App Store, ahead of ChatGPT.\n\nMeta May Not Need the Best AI Model\n\nPolymarket traders give Meta about a 3% chance of having the world’s best AI model at the end of 2026, well behind Anthropic at roughly 72%. More than $1.3 million has traded on the market.\n\nThat is the race Galloway argues Meta may not need to win.\n\nHis point is that consumers may care less about which company has the highest-ranked model than what its AI can actually do for them. Muse is built around everyday tasks such as booking reservations, managing schedules, shopping and canceling subscriptions.\n\nIn an informal Prof G Markets test, Muse reportedly booked a restaurant in under a minute. ChatGPT and Claude failed to complete the reservation, while Google’s Gemini got there only after several confirmations.\n\nBut that approach depends on other companies letting Muse act on their platforms.\n\nAmazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) blocked Muse from shopping on its site Sunday night, citing privacy, security and transparency concerns. Meta says Muse cannot see users’ passwords or payment details.\n\nMeta’s internal testing reportedly revealed security and reliability problems before launch.\n\nTrust may also limit adoption. An Oppenheimer survey found only 8% of U.S. consumers would trust Meta with passwords, compared with 30% for Google and 16% for ChatGPT.\n\nMeta is trading around $711 Monday morning, up roughly 16% since Muse launched Sept. 8.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBrad Gerstner Says AI Labs Need $180B Revenue Run Rate to Keep Nvidia Trade Alive','\n',char(10)),'25969b7306746664c6d9e9506b9e4fba7d91b696','2026-09-21 15:44:26','2026-09-21 16:29:56.403778',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 15:44:26');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(507,'alpaca:61900130','benzinga','2026-09-21 15:33:57','QUICK SPARK: AMD Stock Hits Fresh Record High, Up 183% This Year','AMD climbed 8.4% to a record $606.98 Monday on the OpenAI 6-gigawatt deal, Oracle&#39;s 50,000-chip MI450 order and a Raymond James upgrade.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61900130/amd-stock-record-high-openai-oracle-mi450-raymond-james','["AMD"]','stocks','2026-09-21 16:30:08.312756','other','bullish',3,4,'hours',1,'AMD reached a record high due to significant orders and a broker upgrade.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78}','{}','2026-09-22 15:34:02.702336','2026-09-21 16:29:56.471920','61900130',replace('Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) hit a fresh all-time high Monday, climbing 8.4% to $606.98 and extending its 2026 advance to roughly 183%.\n\nThe catalyst stack is unusually deep. \n\nOpenAI agreed to deploy 6 gigawatts of AMD Instinct GPUs across multiple hardware generations, starting with a 1-gigawatt MI450 rollout in the second half of this year. \n\nOracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL) separately committed to 50,000 MI450 accelerators over the same window. Raymond James upgraded the stock to Strong Buy with a $641 target.\n\nManagement calls the OpenAI arrangement immediately accretive, with a path to tens of billions in annual AI data center revenue from 2027.\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'43b889f408e12574d6b8a4638b351c9cc36f2175','2026-09-21 15:33:57','2026-09-21 16:29:56.403778',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 15:33:57');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(508,'alpaca:61900011','benzinga','2026-09-21 15:30:15','Steve Eisman Says AI CEOs Are Faking the ‘Doomsday Crisis’ — Anthropic May Be Speeding Up Anyway','Steve Eisman says AI CEOs are exaggerating doomsday fears as Anthropic weighs speeding up model releases under competitive pressure.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61900011/steve-eisman-ai-doomsday-anthropic','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-21 16:30:09.538717','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The comment reflects speculation about industry behavior without confirming any specific events.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-22 15:34:02.702336','2026-09-21 16:29:56.476092','61900011',replace('"Big Short" investor Steve Eisman says AI executives are faking a "doomsday crisis" to protect their businesses, as competitive pressure pushes Anthropic to consider another model release.\n\nAnthropic is weighing a new model aimed at countering OpenAI’s GPT-6 Astra, Reuters reported Friday, days after CEO Dario Amodei called for the industry to slow improvements in AI capabilities. OpenAI CEO Sam Altman backed Amodei’s slowdown push.\n\nEisman Says AI Labs Have No Pricing Moat\n\n"There are no pricing moats in this business," Eisman said Friday on The Real Eisman Playbook. "Today I have the best LLM and tomorrow yours is better and cheaper."\n\nFriday’s episode was titled "Why Dario Amodei and Sam Altman Are Faking the AI Doomsday Crisis." Eisman argued neither company can afford to slow down, saying they have hundreds of billions of dollars in commitments to hyperscalers.\n\nEisman said the labs are encouraging regulation that would protect their pricing power by making it harder for new rivals to compete. He expects increasingly capable open-weight models to drive a price war.\n\nAnthropic, which published its Responsible Scaling Policy in 2023, is evaluating the new model’s safety before deciding whether to release it, Reuters reported.\n\nOpenAI, Meta Turn Up the Pressure\n\nOpenAI’s Astra is gaining ground with business customers. It accounted for about 13% of enterprise AI spending tracked by Ramp, compared with 8% for Anthropic’s Claude Fable, Reuters reported.\n\nOpenAI also overtook Anthropic last week on OpenRouter, a platform developers use to access different AI models. It was the first time OpenAI led Anthropic in spending there in more than two-and-a-half years.\n\nThe competitive pressure extends beyond OpenAI. Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META), one of Anthropic’s largest customers, is looking to reduce its use of Anthropic models as it builds more AI capabilities internally, the report said. Open-weight models, whose underlying parameters developers can download and run themselves, could give other customers another way to rely less on commercial AI providers.\n\nMeta this month launched Muse, its first personal AI agent, powered by Muse Spark, which the company described as its most capable model to date.\n\nPrediction Traders Price an Anthropic IPO\n\nFor prospective public investors, Eisman’s price-war argument raises a question about margins. A price war would make it harder for Anthropic to preserve the economics investors may be expecting from a blockbuster listing.\n\nPolymarket traders give Anthropic a 78% chance of going public by Dec. 31, in a market with about $3.7 million in volume. \n\nReuters reported Anthropic may wait until after November’s U.S. midterm elections to list. Its annualized revenue run rate exceeded $65 billion by the end of July, up from roughly $9 billion at the end of 2025.\n\nIf Eisman is right about a coming price war, Meta could benefit from cheaper outside models while its own AI efforts let it rely less on Anthropic.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBrad Gerstner Says AI Labs Need $180B Revenue Run Rate to Keep Nvidia Trade Alive','\n',char(10)),'39c84a6046b5b98dafad9e1904bc4a8adbdd267a','2026-09-21 15:30:15','2026-09-21 16:29:56.403778',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 15:30:15');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(509,'alpaca:61903966','benzinga','2026-09-21 17:28:54','Michael Saylor Says ''Welcome Back'' as Bitcoin Bear Admits: ''I Was Wrong''','Michael Saylor jabs Benjamin Cowen over his failed bearish Bitcoin call as BTC hits $86,000 and short covering fuels the rally.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61903966/michael-saylor-says-welcome-back-as-bitcoin-bear-admits-i-was-wrong','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 17:30:18.178529','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Public statements from notable figures often influence market sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 11.95}}','2026-09-22 17:34:33.755310','2026-09-21 17:30:13.153813','61903966',replace('Michael Saylor replied “Welcome ₿ack” Monday after Into The Cryptoverse founder Benjamin Cowen admitted his bearish Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) call failed.\n\nWhat Cowen Said\n\nCowen posted on X Monday that he was wrong and would not make excuses. \n\n“I deserve to be dunked on,” he wrote. Strategy (NASDAQ:MSTR) Executive Chairman Michael Saylor replied with a two-word jab.\n\nWhy the Reversal Matters\n\nCowen leaned on cycle analysis for months, arguing history pointed toward lower prices before any durable recovery. \n\nOn September 8, he put a 65% probability on Bitcoin’s cycle low still being ahead, repeatedly flagging the realized price near $53,000 as a level earlier bear markets had tested or undercut. \n\nHis July memo centered on a fourth-quarter bottom, most likely in October, with some scenarios contemplating a drop to $44,000.\n\nEven as Bitcoin reclaimed the mid-$70,000s, Cowen held his ground, citing historical pullbacks after golden crosses and warning a lower peak similar to 2014 and 2015 remained possible. \n\nHe finally conceded in a September 20 update that the rally had lasted longer than expected, noting that rising yields, energy prices, and a firmer dollar never delivered the pressure he anticipated.\n\nWhat Glassnode’s Data Shows\n\nGlassnode posted on X that Bitcoin touched $86,000, up more than 10% from last Sunday’s close. \n\nSpot and perpetual buyers drove the move, while leverage and profit-taking climbed at a slower pace. ETF flows were the one signal still lagging behind.\n\nShorts had piled up between $82,000 and $86,000 for months. The rejection at that level barely held, and once Bitcoin broke through, those positions turned into forced buying.\n\nOptions leverage is building back up too, with put/call ratios rising, though nowhere near the frothy levels seen at Bitcoin’s prior top. \n\nFunding on perpetuals sits below neutral, meaning speculative excess hasn’t caught up to price yet.\n\nBTC Price Analysis: Key Levels to Watch\n\nBTC explodes 5.5% Monday, breaking decisively out of the descending triangle that capped price since the September 15 high near $82,000. \n\nRSI at 72.71 marks its strongest reading since the early September peak, confirming genuine momentum while nearing stretched territory.\n\nRead Also:\n\nStrategy Buys 950 Bitcoin For $76M as MSTR Surges 8%: What''s Going On?\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'e277f3ca3d50082e302b8e187ac3917245d05075','2026-09-21 17:28:54','2026-09-21 17:30:13.149258',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 17:28:54');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(510,'alpaca:61902796','benzinga','2026-09-21 16:54:14','S&P 500 Will ‘Easily’ Top 8,000 Before Historic Crash, ‘Black Swan’ Fund Manager Says','Mark Spitznagel says the S&amp;P 500 will top 8,000 before an eventual 80% crash as traders put 65% odds on 8,000 this year.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61902796/sp-500-8000-mark-spitznagel-crash','["SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-21 17:30:19.417776','analyst','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'The statement reflects analyst opinion and speculation about future market movements.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-22 17:34:33.755310','2026-09-21 17:30:13.221268','61902796',replace('Mark Spitznagel, founder of Universa Investments, built his reputation protecting investors from market crashes. Now the Universa Investments founder says the S&P; 500 will “easily” top 8,000 in one final euphoric rally before plunging 80%.SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) climbed 1.3% Monday, leaving the index less than 4% from his target.What Happened“Let me just say, I’m pretty f—ing bullish,” Spitznagel told Puck in an interview published Sunday.Spitznagel said he has been bullish for four years and still sees a “helluva rally” ahead as investor psychology swings toward euphoria.Then comes the reversal. “It’s going to collapse 80 percent,” he said, repeating an 80% crash warning he made last year.Spitznagel blames the bubble on years of near-zero interest rates and believes higher borrowing costs will eventually break it. He expects the resulting downturn to force the Fed to restart quantitative easing, buying bonds to lower longer-term rates and support the economy.He expects the Fed’s balance sheet to “explode in the year ahead” and believes that intervention would eventually revive inflation.The Bullish Half Is WorkingSpitznagel put the 8,000 target on record in September 2025, when the S&P; 500 traded near 6,653. It has since gained roughly 16%, leaving his target less than 4% away.Spitznagel told Puck that three sharp selloffs were bear traps rather than the beginning of the final crash. He cited the August 2024 rush to unwind trades financed with cheap Japanese yen, President Donald Trump’s tariffs and the Iran war.A bear trap draws investors into betting on further losses before stocks rebound. Puck said Spitznagel was largely right as markets recovered after each episode, strengthening the bullish half of his forecast while leaving the predicted 80% collapse untested.Prediction traders also favor a move to 8,000. Kalshi prices a 65.4% chance that the S&P; 500 touches that level before 2027. The contract does not predict whether a collapse follows.Kalshi and Benzinga have an existing data collaboration agreement.Why Spitznagel Gets AttentionUniversa’s strategy works like disaster insurance for an investment portfolio. It spends a small portion of a client’s money on options designed to rise sharply when markets plunge.Those options often expire worthless during calm periods, creating a recurring cost similar to an insurance premium. During a severe crash, however, their gains can offset losses elsewhere and give investors cash to buy stocks at depressed prices.Nassim Nicholas Taleb, who popularized the term “black swan” for a rare and highly disruptive event, serves as Universa’s scientific adviser. Puck reported that Universa returned more than 115% to investors during the 2008 financial crisis. The firm reported a 3,612% return on capital invested in its hedge during the March 2020 COVID crash, not on clients’ entire portfolios.Not every Spitznagel forecast has landed. He said in September 2024 that a U.S. recession was “imminent” and could begin before year-end. Nearly two years later, the NBER still lists the brief 2020 COVID downturn as the country’s most recent recession.Photo by AciiDesign via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nSteve Eisman Says AI CEOs Are Faking the ‘Doomsday Crisis’ — Anthropic May Be Speeding Up Anyway','\n',char(10)),'e9df97b158d9029c15e1a4d6c400d06eb9665098','2026-09-21 16:54:14','2026-09-21 17:30:13.149258',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 16:54:14');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(511,'alpaca:61902221','benzinga','2026-09-21 16:34:16','An Nvidia Earnings Miss Is Almost Unthinkable—VanEck Says There’s a Real Risk','Nvidia has a long track record of beating analyst estimates. VanEck warns the streak could be at risk. Here&#39;s why.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/09/61902221/nvidia-earnings-miss-unthinkable-vaneck-flags-real-risk','["AMD", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 17:30:21.431060','earnings','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst warning reflects potential risk, not confirmed earnings data.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-22 16:34:19.642738','2026-09-21 17:30:13.229098','61902221',replace('An Nvidia (NASDAQ:NVDA) earnings miss has become almost unthinkable after 15 straight quarters of beating estimates. Quarter after quarter, the AI chip giant has trained Wall Street to expect another blowout. But VanEck says the biggest threat to that streak may have little to do with demand for Nvidia’s chips — and everything to do with whether customers can actually get enough electricity to run them.\n\nNvidia Earnings at Risk\n\nAfter consistently beating analyst estimates for revenue and earnings per share, VanEck analysts see some risk for Nvidia for the upcoming third quarter.\n\nVanEck projects that chips sold by Nvidia, Advanced Micro Devices (NASDAQ:AMD) and Broadcom (NASDAQ:AVGO) will collectively require about 30 gigawatts of U.S. power through 2027. However, only about 15 to 25 gigawatts of new U.S. data centers with power available to run their equipment are expected to come online each year, the asset manager estimates.\n\n"We see more risk that NVDA misses estimates because its customers cannot get power than that the miners fail to lease their megawatts," VanEck analysts including Patrick Bush and Matthew Sigel wrote in a note.  \n\nBased on that assessment, the unthinkable could happen: Nvidia could keep extraordinary AI demand, but still fall short of Wall Street earnings estimates.\n\nThe analysts estimate that every 1GW its customers can’t energize represents around $37 billion of revenue, or around 6% of the total, that Nvidia could lose out on. A potential 3GW shortfall could lead to an 18% revenue drop.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia Stock: 84% of Benzinga Viewers Have Owned It. Here’s How Many Still Do.\n\nNvidia Earnings Estimates\n\nAnalysts expect Nvidia to post third-quarter earnings per share of $2.38, up from $1.30 in the year-earlier period. The company has beaten analyst expectations for earnings per share in 15 straight quarters, Benzinga Pro data show.\n\nFor revenue, analysts expect the chip giant to report a third quarter total of $104.19 billion. This would be up significantly from the $57.01 billion reported a year earlier and top the record set in the second quarter ($96.22 billion) of this fiscal year.\n\nNvidia has beaten analyst estimates for revenue in 16 straight quarters.\n\nVanEck’s warning could be early with third-quarter earnings likely coming in November, but show a real threat of Nvidia not being able to hit optimistic estimates from analysts due to supply.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia Stock ''Valuation Remains Conservative'': Early 2028 Guidance Has Analysts Increasing Price Targets\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'8f794dbb0fa2cdbdbca399b4d89e7feeaa01944e','2026-09-21 16:34:16','2026-09-21 17:30:13.149258',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 16:34:16');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(512,'alpaca:61902168','benzinga','2026-09-21 16:32:32','Sunrun, Tesla Set Record With 580 MW California Grid Dispatch','Sunrun and Tesla deliver California’s largest recorded distributed power plant dispatch, supplying more than 580 megawatts during an extreme heat event.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/mid-cap/26/09/61902168/sunrun-tesla-set-record-with-580-mw-california-grid-dispatch','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 17:30:22.853222','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'This event highlights a record achievement without directly implying future price movements.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-22 16:34:19.642738','2026-09-21 17:30:13.232037','61902168',replace('Sunrun Inc (NASDAQ:RUN) shares are trading higher on Monday after the company, along with Tesla, Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA), said their home battery fleets supplied more than 580 megawatts of peak power to California’s grid on the evening of Sept. 9, 2026.\n\n • Sunrun stock is surging to new heights today. What’s driving RUN stock higher?\n\nDetails\n\nThis marked the largest recorded distributed power plant dispatch and provided enough capacity to power all households in Sacramento County during peak hours.\n\nThe three-hour evening dispatch came as California faced extreme heat, elevated electricity demand and higher wholesale energy prices. \n\nThe 580 megawatts included 517 megawatts from Tesla Powerwalls and 63 megawatts from other residential batteries. About 110,000 Powerwalls participated, with 55% owned and operated by Sunrun. \n\nSunrun also dispatched more than 30,000 customer batteries from other manufacturers.\n\nAt the request of the California Energy Commission and utilities, the companies discharged customers’ home batteries to strengthen the grid’s operating margin and help lower real-time power prices.\n\nRUN Technical Outlook: Trend, Support and Resistance\n\nAt $8.73, the stock is hovering right around its short-term trend line, sitting about 0.8% above the 20-day SMA ($8.75), but it remains in a clear longer-term downtrend at 9.6% below the 50-day SMA ($9.77) and 36.9% below the 200-day SMA ($13.99). The bigger-picture trend damage is reinforced by the Death Cross that formed in April (the 50-day moving below the 200-day), which often keeps rallies "sellable" until price can reclaim key averages.\n\nMomentum is best described as "not stretched": RSI is 45.08, a neutral reading that suggests neither overbought pressure nor capitulation-level selling. In plain English, RSI helps gauge whether recent buying or selling has become too extended; here it points to a market that’s still trying to base rather than rip.\n\nKey Resistance: $9.50 — Nearby round-number zone that also sits close to the declining 50-day area, where rebounds can stall\n\nKey Support: $8.50 — Nearby floor near the recent lows, where buyers have shown up as price sits not far above the $8.19 52-week low\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nRUN Earnings Preview and Wall Street Analyst Targets\n\nLooking further out, the next major catalyst for the stock arrives with the Nov. 5, 2026 (estimated) earnings report.\n\nEPS Estimate: 37 cents (Up from 6 cents year-over-year)\n\nRevenue Estimate: $830.62 million (Up from $724.56 million YoY)\n\nValuation: P/E of 5.8x (Indicates value opportunity relative to peers)\n\nAnalyst Consensus & Recent Actions: The stock carries a Buy rating with an average price target of $15.15. Recent analyst moves include:\n\nGoldman Sachs: Buy (Lowers target to $13 on Sept. 21)\n\nGLJ Research: Sell (Maintains target to $4.63 on Aug. 17)\n\nWells Fargo: Overweight (Lowers target to $17 on Aug. 14)\n\nTop ETFs Holding Sunrun Stock\n\nCorgi Battery Energy Storage Systems ETF (NASDAQ:WATS): 3.67% Weight\n\nInvesco Solar ETF (NYSE:TAN): 3.79% Weight\n\nSignificance: Because RUN carries significant weight in these funds, any significant inflows or outflows for these ETFs will likely trigger automatic buying or selling of the stock.\n\nRUN Stock Price Moves Higher In Monday Trading\n\nRUN Stock Price Activity: Sunrun shares were up 3.63% at $8.83 at the time of publication on Monday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock \n\nRead Also:\n\nCrude Oil Down 4%; Intel Shares Move Higher','\n',char(10)),'54822e2e705b9654997e3fb6afddd25228a98496','2026-09-21 16:32:32','2026-09-21 17:30:13.149258',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 16:32:32');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(513,'alpaca:61904615','benzinga','2026-09-21 17:51:25','Nasdaq 100 Rallies, Intel Soars 14%: Stock Market Today','A fourth straight decline in crude oil handed Wall Street a fresh leg higher Monday, with the Nasdaq 100 jumping to a three-month high as semiconductors led the tape. Intel surged nearly 14% on SK Hynix foundry optimism while AMD crossed the $1 trillion mark. Energy was the lone sector in the red as WTI slid more than 5% to an 11-day low','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61904615/nasdaq-100-rallies-intel-soars-14-stock-market-today','["AMD", "BTC/USD", "META", "QQQ"]','stocks','2026-09-21 18:30:30.554699','macro','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'The Nasdaq 100''s rise indicates positive market momentum.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "BTC/USD": 76528.6, "META": 682.7, "QQQ": 716.89}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 11.95}}','2026-09-22 18:34:46.161225','2026-09-21 18:30:26.275378','61904615',replace('U.S. equities extended their winning streak to a third session Monday, with a fourth consecutive slide in crude oil relieving pressure on Treasury yields and clearing the runway for a semiconductor-led rally that lifted the Nasdaq 100 to a three-month high.\n\n • Intel stock is charging ahead with explosive momentum. Why is INTC stock surging?\n\nTreasury Secretary Scott Bessent wrapped up talks with Chinese Vice Premier He Lifeng in New York on Sunday, calling them “very successful” and floating an AI safety notification mechanism for President Donald Trump and President Xi Jinping to weigh at their Sept. 24 summit in Washington, alongside potential agreements on tariffs and critical minerals.\n\nThe bigger macro release valve was energy. \n\nWest Texas Intermediate crude sank 5.1% to $95.16 a barrel, an 11-day low, after satellite shipping data showed Saudi Aramco loading 14 million barrels onto seven large tankers through the Strait of Hormuz and Gulf Cooperation Council states pressed Tehran to lift its blockade on fuel tankers.\n\nAcross U.S. equity markets by midday Monday, gains were broad but heavily skewed toward technology, with 10 of 11 S&P; 500 sectors higher and energy the sole decliner.\n\nThe S&P; 500 rose 1.3% to 7,746.92 and the Dow Jones Industrial Average added 0.6%, or about 283 points, to 51,964.32. \n\nThe Nasdaq 100 jumped 2.4%, or roughly 720 points, to 30,363.70. The broader tech index is now just 1.5 percentage points below record highs.\n\nWithin Magnificent Seven stocks, Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) surged 8.7% on positive early responses to its Muse AI agent. \n\nSofter energy prices took the edge off inflation angst that has dominated the rates market in recent months. \n\nThe 10-year Treasury yield slipped 2 basis points to 4.97%, the 30-year eased 2 basis points to 5.30% and the 2-year held near 4.75%.\n\nTraders are still pricing another 25-basis-point hike before year-end. \n\nChicago Fed President Austan Goolsbee said he remains open to inflation resuming its decline toward 2% but warned rates may need to rise if it does not, while Minneapolis Fed President Neel Kashkari said Sunday that inflation remains too high across the economy rather than being driven solely by oil. \n\nThe dollar index pushed above 100 to an almost three-month high. Gold fell 0.7% to $4,353 an ounce as a firmer dollar and rising odds of another Fed hike weighed on bullion, leaving the metal down 6.5% month-to-date. \n\nBitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) jumped 6% to $85,000 amid continued appetite for digital assets. \n\nMonday’s Performance In Major U.S. Indices\n\nIndexLast% ChangeMTDYTDS&P; 5007,746.92+1.3%+0.9%+13.4%Dow Jones51,964.32+0.6%-2.4%+8.0%Nasdaq 10030,363.70+2.4%+3.0%+20.1%Russell 20002,879.97+0.7%-2.7%+16.1%Updated by 12:15 p.m. ET\n\nAccording to the Benzinga Pro platform:\n\nThe Vanguard S&P; 500 ETF (NYSE:VOO) gained 1.3%.\n\nThe SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA) rose 0.6%.\n\nThe Invesco QQQ Trust (NASDAQ:QQQ) climbed 2.3%.\n\nThe iShares Russell 2000 ETF (NYSE:IWM) added 0.6%.\n\nChips Rip and AMD Tops $1 Trillion While Energy Bleeds Out\n\nThe Communication Services Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLC) led all sectors with a 3.4% gain, powered by Meta and a violent move in media names. \n\nThe Technology Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLK) followed with a 2.2% advance.\n\nBehind them, the Consumer Discretionary Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLY) rose 1.24%, the Industrials Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLI) added 0.5%, the Consumer Staples Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLP) was up 0.03% and the Utilities Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLU) gained 0.10%. The Energy Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLE) was the only sector in the red by any meaningful margin, down 1.91%.\n\nAt the industry level, the VanEck Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SMH) jumped 3.2% for the best move on the board, with the First Trust Dow Jones Internet Index Fund (NASDAQ:FDN) up 2.4% and the U.S. Global Jets ETF (NYSE:JETS) gaining 2.1% on cheaper jet fuel. On the other side, the SPDR S&P; Oil & Gas Exploration & Production ETF (NYSE:XOP) sank 3.1%, the VanEck Oil Services ETF (NYSE:OIH) lost 1.2% and the VanEck Gold Miners ETF (NYSE:GDX) fell 1.1%.\n\nIntel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) was the single best performer in the Russell 1000, soaring 13.71% to $123.49 as reports that SK Hynix Inc. (NASDAQ:SKHY) could lease part of Intel’s future Ohio fab or form a memory joint venture there continued to build.\n\nTigress Financial lifted Intel’s price target to $145 from $118, flagging Terafab, stronger Xeon demand and 18A execution.\n\nThe move pulled the entire complex higher. \n\nAdvanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) rallied 9.1% to $610.51 and joined the $1 trillion market capitalization club, while QUALCOMM Inc. (NASDAQ:QCOM) added 7.5% and Micron Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MU) rose 2.4%.\n\nDigitalOcean Holdings Inc. (NYSE:DOCN) was the second-best large-cap gainer, up 12.75% to $146.61, extending a September run built on the company’s AI-native cloud pivot, its Managed AI Agents launch and a $725 million financing facility earmarked for AI infrastructure.\n\nRambus Inc. (NASDAQ:RMBS) climbed 11.3% to $97.47, with the memory-interface IP name appearing to trade as a high-beta proxy for the SK Hynix-Intel memory headlines rather than on anything company-specific.\n\nAkamai Technologies Inc. (NASDAQ:AKAM) also rose 11.3%, to $116.28. The move builds on a cluster of recent analyst upgrades tied to edge AI inference, including a Bank of America upgrade to Buy with a $175 target and a DA Davidson target increase to $185.\n\nWarner Bros. Discovery Inc. (NASDAQ:WBD) jumped 10% to $30.57 after reports that Paramount Skydance is in advanced talks with California Attorney General Rob Bonta to settle the antitrust suit that has blocked its $110 billion takeover since July. \n\nParamount Skydance Corp. (NASDAQ:PSKY) climbed about 5% alongside it.\n\nOn the downside, Summit Therapeutics Inc. (NASDAQ:SMMT) was the worst Russell 1000 performer, down 5.91% to $16.80, with the stock is giving back part of a roughly 28% weekly surge driven by partner Akeso’s data showing ivonescimab cut the risk of death 27% versus Keytruda in late-stage lung cancer.\n\nMatador Resources Co. (NYSE:MTDR) slid 4.72% to $54.13, a straight read-through from the 5.1% drop in WTI.\n\nThe rest of the shale complex went with it, with Chord Energy Corp. (NASDAQ:CHRD) off 3.6%, Permian Resources Corp. (NYSE:PR) down 3.4%, Ovintiv Inc. (NYSE:OVV) lower by 3.3% and ConocoPhillips (NYSE:COP) and Exxon Mobil Corp. (NYSE:XOM) down 3.3% and 3%, respectively.\n\nForgent Power Solutions Inc. (NYSE:FPS) dropped 4% to $37.86, unwinding part of the advance that followed record fourth-quarter results.\n\nHP Inc. (NYSE:HPQ) fell 3.78% to $33.10 after a regulatory filing disclosed the company’s planning assumption that industry-wide PC unit volumes will decline roughly mid-single digits in percentage terms in calendar 2027 versus 2026.\n\nElsewhere, freight names struggled. \n\nUnited Parcel Service Inc. (NYSE:UPS) lost 3.7% and FedEx Corp. (NYSE:FDX) fell 3.6%. \n\nThe earnings calendar was empty Monday, with AutoZone Inc. (NYSE:AZO) opening the week’s reporting slate Tuesday morning and Costco Wholesale Corp. (NASDAQ:COST) the marquee name Thursday afternoon.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Growth Stocks\n\nMonday’s Russell 1000 Top Gainers\n\nName% changeIntel Corporation+13.71%DigitalOcean Holdings, Inc.+12.65%Rambus Inc.+11.27%Akamai Technologies, Inc.+11.25%Warner Bros. Discovery, Inc.+10%\n\nMonday’s Russell 1000 Top Losers\n\nName% changeSummit Therapeutics Inc.-5.91%Mohawk Industries, Inc. (NYSE:MHK)-5.37%Matador Resources Company-4.72%Forgent Power Solutions, Inc.-4%HP Inc.-3.78%\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nFed’s Goolsbee Sounds the Alarm on Inflation: October Hike Odds Stay Above 50%','\n',char(10)),'5ba0107e018422ba5b364b0d0b4b19e5041886a0','2026-09-21 17:51:25','2026-09-21 18:30:26.265343',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 17:51:26');
