eded to be split into 6 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $26.7K, with a price of $1574.0 per contract. There were 201 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 855 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• Regarding MU (NASDAQ:MU), we observe a put option trade with bearish sentiment. It expires in 11 day(s) on October 2, 2026. Parties traded 5 contract(s) at a $1050.00 strike. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $28.8K, with a price of $5770.0 per contract. There were 87 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 573 contract(s) were bought and sold. \nOptions Alert Terminology\n - Call Contracts: The right to buy shares as indicated in the contract.\n - Put Contracts: The right to sell shares as indicated in the contract.\n - Expiration Date: When the contract expires. One must act on the contract by this date if one wants to use it.\n - Premium/Option Price: The price of the contract. \nFor more information, read more about unusual options activity. \nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'dc47d7e2915dc7c9de5501739a2c92fbcebfbc5b','2026-09-21 17:35:17','2026-09-21 18:30:26.265343',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 17:35:17');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(515,'alpaca:61904100','benzinga','2026-09-21 17:33:27','Microsoft’s Azure Has Another Growth Lever Waiting in the Wings, Analyst Says','BNP Paribas sees upside for Microsoft (MSFT) with a $549 target as Azure price increases gradually roll out to renewing contracts.','https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/analyst-color/26/09/61904100/microsofts-azure-has-another-growth-lever-waiting-in-the-wings-analyst-says','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-21 18:30:33.605796','analyst','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst predicts potential price increase for Microsoft due to Azure contract renewals.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 498.48}','{}','2026-09-22 17:34:33.755310','2026-09-21 18:30:26.294174','61904100',replace('Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT) could see additional upside from Azure pricing over time, even as recent cloud growth has largely been driven by capacity expansion and efficiency gains, according to BNP Paribas Equity Research.\n\nAnalyst Stefan Slowinski reiterated a positive view on Microsoft with a $549 price target, implying about 11% upside from the stock’s Sept. 18 closing price of $493.80.\n\nBNP Paribas spoke with Microsoft Investor Relations ahead of the company’s fiscal first-quarter 2027 quiet period. Microsoft did not change its guidance or provide an intra-quarter update.\n\nAzure Pricing Benefits Could Build Gradually\n\nSlowinski said GPU rental pricing has become one of the biggest topics in recent investor discussions.\n\nMicrosoft acknowledged that Azure pricing is moving higher. However, the company does not plan to alter existing contract economics. Instead, new pricing would take effect as contracts renew.\n\nThat means pricing benefits are likely to flow into Azure revenue gradually rather than trigger an immediate jump in growth, the analyst said.\n\nImportantly, Microsoft indicated that recent Azure strength has not been driven by pricing. Instead, fleet efficiency improvements and additional capacity remain the main growth drivers.\n\nBNP Paribas called that encouraging because Azure growth has already accelerated into the mid-40% range before any significant pricing impact.\n\nMicrosoft Still Hunting For AI Capacity\n\nThe company also pushed back on a Bloomberg report suggesting it plans to scale computing capacity to 38 gigawatts by 2032, although it did not provide its own target.\n\nIt declined to address speculation that it may have sourced capacity from SpaceX. However, Microsoft reiterated that it continues to seek additional compute capacity as demand remains ahead of supply.\n\nSlowinski said near-term access to infrastructure that meets Microsoft’s specifications remains difficult.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nOpenAI Economics Remain In Focus\n\nMicrosoft also confirmed that a cumulative cap exists on its revenue-sharing arrangement with OpenAI, although it did not disclose the amount.\n\nThe Information previously reported a $38 billion cap. BNP Paribas estimates that level could allow revenue sharing to continue through early fiscal 2029 if OpenAI tracks toward reported long-term revenue targets.\n\nMicrosoft said OpenAI revenue sharing has not been a meaningful source of Azure outperformance in recent quarters. The company also said it would disclose the contribution if it became material.\n\nMeanwhile, the company reiterated that its recent segment restructuring reflects how the company increasingly manages its businesses internally. It also maintained its expectation for Microsoft 365 growth to accelerate through fiscal 2027.\n\nMicrosoft carries a Buy consensus rating and an average price forecast of $563.04.\n\nCantor Fitzgerald maintained an Overweight rating Monday and raised its target to $608. Citizens maintained a Market Outperform rating with a $550 target on Sept. 15. Stifel maintained a Hold rating and raised its target to $530 on Sept. 4.\n\nMicrosoft Stock Performance And Technical Analysis\n\nMicrosoft stock traded higher Monday as a broad technology rally lifted large-cap stocks.\n\nThe stock remains above its 50-day SMA of $466.92, 100-day SMA of $435.27 and 200-day SMA of $431.64.\n\nHowever, the stock trades slightly below its 20-day SMA of $498.20. MACD is also below its signal line, pointing to softer near-term momentum.\n\nResistance sits near $513.50, while support is around $486.\n\nPrice Action\n\nMicrosoft shares were up 0.54% at $496.44 at the time of publication Monday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nMicrosoft Consolidates Business Into Two Segments in Sweeping AI-Driven Overhaul','\n',char(10)),'7701983207bac5f9da030e3ad64446b600cd0176','2026-09-21 17:33:27','2026-09-21 18:30:26.265343',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 17:33:27');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(516,'alpaca:61906962','benzinga','2026-09-21 19:09:47','QUICK SPARK: Meta Stock Adds Over $200 Billion in Value Today','Meta shares surged 12%, adding $207.5B in value as analysts raised targets on Muse and ahead of Meta Connect.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61906962/quick-spark-meta-stock-adds-over-200-billion-in-value-today','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-21 19:30:41.479532','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Analysts raised targets on Meta''s Muse as the stock surged.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-22 19:35:11.450071','2026-09-21 19:30:37.086116','61906962',replace('Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) shares surged over 12% Monday, adding more than $200 billion in market value in a single session, according to Benzinga Pro market data. \n\nThe company tacked on roughly $207.5 billion in market capitalization intraday, climbing from about $1.695 trillion at the prior close to about $1.902 trillion.\n\nWells Fargo’s Meta Price Target Boost\n\nIn a Monday note, Wells Fargo raised its price target for Meta to $796 from $640, maintaining an Overweight rating. \n\nThe adjustment comes as excitement builds around the upcoming Meta Connect event, where founder and CEO Mark Zuckerberg is expected to outline the company’s broader product vision. \n\nThe event will feature a keynote on Wednesday, Sept. 23, followed by a developer-focused session on Thursday, Sept. 24. Meta recently introduced Muse, a personal AI agent designed to assist users with tasks and goals.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBuy These 4 Cybersecurity Stocks, Skip These 2: Josh Brown Names Names\n\nRosenblatt’s Bullish Outlook on Meta\n\nRosenblatt Securities maintained its Buy rating on Meta, setting a price target of $886 in a recent note. \n\nThe firm highlighted Meta’s upcoming product launches, including camera-free smart glasses, code-named Luna, expected this fall. \n\nThe glasses will feature six microphones for AI interactions. Additionally, Meta has started rolling out parental supervision tools for Threads across Asia Pacific, allowing parents to manage privacy settings and monitor usage.\n\nCitigroup also maintained a Buy rating with an $800 price target, citing the Connect event as a near-term catalyst.\n\nTechnical Analysis\n\nMeta’s RSI stands at 78.35, indicating overbought conditions. The stock trades 22.75% above its 50-day SMA of $608.94 and 19.67% above its 200-day SMA of $624.66, with the 50-day SMA still below the 200-day SMA.\n\nMETA Stock Price Activity: Meta stock was up 12.27% at $747.46 at the time of publication Monday, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nThese 10 Stocks Are Squeeze Candidates Waiting to Happen\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'b6c32cc28e489261709be504073ba7b37d3de690','2026-09-21 19:09:47','2026-09-21 19:30:37.079272',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 19:09:47');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(517,'alpaca:61906918','benzinga','2026-09-21 19:07:54','Bitcoin Hits $86,000 as Dogecoin Leads; Ethereum, XRP Rally Pushing Liquidations Towards $1 Billion','Bitcoin nears an eight-month high amid institutional inflows, while oil and Treasury yields fall. Traders see the higher highs of BTC signal a new bull market.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61906918/bitcoin-hits-86000-as-dogecoin-leads-ethereum-xrp-rally-pushing-liquidations-towards-1-billion','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "ETH/USD", "SHIB/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-21 19:30:42.536767','macro','bullish',4,3,'days',1,'Bitcoin''s price reaching a significant high indicates strong market momentum.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "SHIB/USD": 5.21e-06, "SOL/USD": 101.29, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 11.95}, "DOGE/USD": {"60m": 22.182, "1d": 23.16}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 12.012}, "SHIB/USD": {"60m": 14.971, "1d": 17.054}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": 15.925, "1d": 17.208}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 16.298, "1d": 23.425}}','2026-09-22 19:35:11.450071','2026-09-21 19:30:37.090304','61906918',replace('Bitcoin rallied to an almost eight-month high as institutional interest surged, while crude oil prices fell below $100 and Treasury yields slipped below 5%.CryptocurrencyTickerPriceBitcoin(CRYPTO: BTC)$85,996.27Ethereum(CRYPTO: ETH)$2,748.30Solana(CRYPTO: SOL)$117.42XRP(CRYPTO: XRP)$1.51Dogecoin(CRYPTO: DOGE)$0.09882Shiba Inu(CRYPTO: SHIB)$0.055937Notable Statistics:\nCoinglass data shows 130,362 traders were liquidated in the past 24 hours for $928.11 million.       \n\nSoSoValue data shows net inflows of $433 million from spot Bitcoin ETFs on Friday. Spot Ethereum ETFs saw net inflows of $143.8 million.\n\nIn the past 24 hours, top gainers include Bitway, Pepe and Dogecoin.\nNotable Developments:\nStrategy Buys 950 Bitcoin For $76M as MSTR Surges 8%: What’s Going On?\n\nTop 6 Crypto Stocks Climbing with Bitcoin Right Now\n\nBitmine Buys 27,562 ETH as Tom Lee Says Crypto’s Bull Market Is ‘Underway’\n\nIs Solana’s Next ‘Token Supercycle’ Taking Shape? Expert Identifies Three Key Indicators\n\nBitcoin Hits 7-Month High as Coinbase CEO Sees $400,000, Says Crypto Won’t Wait for Congress\n\nMichael Saylor Says ‘Welcome Back’ as Bitcoin Bear Admits: ‘I Was Wrong’\n\nXRP Jumps 8% as Ripple Says Asset Managers Eye XRPL Upgrade\nTrader Notes:Heavily followed crypto trader CrediBULL Crypto said Bitcoin is now pushing into higher-timeframe resistance, raising the risk of a short- to medium-term pullback.He said such a move could still form a higher low above $60,000 before BTC resumes toward $100,000-plus, while consolidation could give altcoins room to rally.Jelle noted Bitcoin’s higher high signals the start of a new bull market, with a weekly close at $83,000 or above providing further confirmation.He believes traders now face a choice between buying immediately, waiting for confirmation or hoping for a better entry on a pullback.Image: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nIs Solana''s Next ''Token Supercycle'' Taking Shape? Expert Identifies Three Key Indicators','\n',char(10)),'96b32778f240ffe240273b8d89e57431b35dcf17','2026-09-21 19:07:54','2026-09-21 19:30:37.079272',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 19:07:54');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(518,'alpaca:61906729','benzinga','2026-09-21 19:03:16','Bitcoin Trails Nasdaq This Year: Why One Analyst Calls It ‘Helpful’','Bitcoin trails the Nasdaq in 2026, but rising adoption and regulatory progress could fuel a run toward $100,000.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61906729/bitcoin-trails-nasdaq-this-year-why-one-analyst-calls-it-helpful','["BTC/USD", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-21 19:30:43.659112','analyst','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'Analyst commentary on future potential likely to stir interest but not based on confirmed events.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "SPY": 762.63}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 11.95}}','2026-09-22 19:35:11.450071','2026-09-21 19:30:37.093701','61906729',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) trades down around 7% on the year while the Nasdaq climbs 14%, and macro investor Dave Weisberger says that gap is exactly what a healthy setup looks like.\n\n • How is Bitcoin doing today? \n\nWhy the Underperformance Is a Good Sign\n\nWeisberger told The Wolf of All Streets Macro Monday panel that Bitcoin lagging the Nasdaq right now separates genuine long-term holders from short-term speculators. \n\nPeople still holding through this stretch are betting on dollar depreciation playing out over time, not chasing quick gains. \n\nOnce that cycle turns, he expects Bitcoin to outperform the metrics most of the crypto community tracks, leaving real room to run before the asset even approaches its $126,000 all-time high, a level still roughly 40% above current prices.\n\nWhere the Bull and Bear Cases Clash\n\nBloomberg macro strategist Mike McGlone and Weisberger sparred over how to value Bitcoin from here:\n\nMcGlone’s case — Bitcoin divided by the Nasdaq total return sits at the same level it traded in 2017. Same performance over eight years while carrying two to three times the volatility makes it a weak risk-adjusted bet next to simply picking Nasdaq stocks. He also flagged that Bitcoin’s 200-day moving average, divided by the State Street SPDR S&P; 500 (NYSE:SPY), has dropped below it for only the second time since 2022.\n\nWeisberger’s case — McGlone’s framework ignores adoption entirely. Every Bitcoin adoption metric keeps climbing, and by that model fair value sits between $105,000 and $155,000, well above current levels. Ignoring adoption while looking only at price charts, he argued, is like ignoring corporate earnings while looking only at stock charts.\n\nWhy the Clarity Act’s Failure May Not Matter\n\nAcademy Securities’ Peter Tchir noted that seven Democrats who initially voted no on the Clarity Act quickly signaled openness to revisiting it, a sign they realized blocking the bill freed regulators to move faster rather than slower. \n\nWeisberger agreed, arguing the failure hands the SEC and CFTC more room to advance crypto rulemaking independently over the next two years, particularly around Bitcoin’s use as collateral within the traditional financial system.\n\nWhat the Fed Decision Means Going Forward\n\nTchir said he is adding to his Bitcoin position rather than selling, expecting a run back toward $100,000 as momentum builds. \n\nHe pointed to growing interest in agentic AI and its potential use of crypto rails for moving money as a fresh catalyst separate from the regulatory debate. \n\nMcGlone maintained his preference for shorting Bitcoin rallies, arguing the asset still trades more like a risk proxy tied to the broader stock market than an independent store of value.\n\nRead Also:\n\nCoinbase Launches IPO Access for US Traders as Part of its ''Complete Global Financial Platform''\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'0c119e1cd8164109a301c5362e44593c407a33f9','2026-09-21 19:03:16','2026-09-21 19:30:37.079272',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 19:03:16');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(519,'alpaca:61906130','benzinga','2026-09-21 18:42:13','Stocks Jump On Iran, China, and Bitcoin Hopium—But The Big Conflicts Have Not Gone Away',replace('\n\n\n\nBuying On Hopium\n\n\n\nPlease click here for an enlarged chart of Direxion Daily Semiconductor Bull 3X ETF (NYSE:SOXL).\n\n\n\nNote the following:\n\n\n\n\nSemiconductors reflect the AI trade, and SOXL is the momo crowd’s','\n',char(10)),'https://www.benzinga.com/Opinion/26/09/61906130/stocks-jump-on-iran-china-and-bitcoin-hopium-but-the-big-conflicts-have-not-gone-away','["AAPL", "AMZN", "META", "MSFT", "NVDA", "QQQ", "SPY", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 19:30:44.595525','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The headline suggests an ongoing market sentiment without confirming specific developments.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48, "NVDA": 219.37, "QQQ": 716.89}','{}','2026-09-22 19:35:11.450071','2026-09-21 19:30:37.099784','61906130',replace('Buying On Hopium\n\nPlease click here for an enlarged chart of Direxion Daily Semiconductor Bull 3X ETF (NYSE:SOXL).\n\nNote the following:\n\nSemiconductors reflect the AI trade, and SOXL is the momo crowd’s favorite.\n\nThe chart shows SOXL bounced above the top band of zone 3 (support) on Friday due to triple witching buying.  Friday also saw aggressive call buying in several semiconductor stocks including Sandisk (SNDK) and Micron (MU).\n\nThe chart shows SOXL is jumping again in the early trade on very aggressive buying.\n\nThere is very aggressive buying in the stock market this morning, especially in the AI trade.  There are five main factors:\n\nHopium about Iran\n\nHoping about China\n\nBitcoin jumping above $85K\n\nGreenland deal\n\nAnthropic IPO\n\nPresident Trump is likely to meet Gulf leaders in New York this week.  The stock market is assuming that the talks will lead to a resolution of the Iran war.  Prudent investors should note that Iran is not part of these talks.  Iran has laid out its demands to end the war, and the U.S. is unlikely to accept Iran’s demands.\n\nWe previously shared with you that a Houthi attack had shut down the East-West Pipeline in Saudi Arabia.  Saudi Arabia had been using the pipeline to bypass the Strait of Hormuz to send oil from its eastern fields to the Red Sea.  This morning, there is hopium that Saudi Arabia could repair the pipeline soon.  In our analysis, prudent investors should note that technical hurdles remain and Houthis can attack the pipeline again at any time.  \n\nPresident Xi of China will be meeting President Trump.  Secretary Bessent says he has had productive talks with his counterpart ahead of the summit.  In our analysis, prudent investors should note that there are tough issues regarding Taiwan, trade, and AI.  Irrespective of this morning’s hopium, China is going to continue its quest to get ahead of the U.S. in AI and to replace the U.S. as the world’s superpower.  \n\nBitcoin jumping over $85K is creating significant positive sentiment that is resulting in buying in tech stocks.  In our analysis, a large number of investors who aggressively buy bitcoin also aggressively buy speculative tech stocks.  Further, prudent investors should note the jump in bitcoin is primarily the result of a short squeeze.  Short squeezes tend to end.  \n\nPresident Trump has been wanting to make Greenland part of the U.S.  Now, the matter has been resolved.  There is a deal that falls short of a takeover but allows the U.S. to expand its military presence in Greenland and permanently bars China and Russia from investing in Greenland.  Shares of Greenland related stocks such as Greenland Energy Co (NASDAQ:GLND), Greenland Mines Ltd (NASDAQ:GRML), and Critical Metals Corp (NASDAQ:CRML) are jumping.\n\nAnthropic’s IPO now appears to be scheduled for November.  This is generating additional enthusiasm for AI stocks.\n\nNasdaq quarterly rebalancing that takes effect today increases Space Exploration Technologies Corp (NASDAQ:SPCX) weighting to 2.82% from 1.28%.  This is causing index funds to buy SPCX stock.\n\nMagnificent Seven Money Flows\n\nMost portfolios are now heavily concentrated in the Mag 7 stocks.  For this reason, it is important to pay attention to early money flows in the Mag 7 stocks on a daily basis. \n\nIn the early trade, money flows are positive in Amazon.com, Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN), Alphabet Inc Class C (NASDAQ:GOOG), Meta Platforms Inc (NASDAQ:META), Microsoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT), NVIDIA Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA), and Tesla Inc (NASDAQ:TSLA).\n\nIn the early trade, money flows are neutral in Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL).\n\nIn the early trade, money flows are positive in SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust Series 1 (NASDAQ:QQQ).\n\nMomo Crowd And Smart Money In Stocks\n\nInvestors can gain an edge by knowing money flows in SPY and QQQ.  Investors can get a bigger edge by knowing when smart money is buying stocks, gold, and oil.  The most popular ETF for gold is SPDR Gold Trust (GLD).  The most popular ETF for silver is iShares Silver Trust (SLV).  The most popular ETF for oil is United States Oil ETF (NYSE:USO).\n\nBitcoin\n\nBitcoin (BTC) is seeing buying.\n\nWhat To Do Now\n\nConsider continuing to hold good, very long term, existing positions and add tactical positions based on signals.\n\nThe Arora Report is known for its accurate calls. The Arora Report correctly called the big artificial intelligence rally before anyone else, the new bull market of 2023, the bear market of 2022, new stock market highs right after the virus low in 2020, the virus drop in 2020, the DJIA rally to 30,000 when it was trading at 16,000, the start of a mega bull market in 2009, and the financial crash of 2008. Please click here to sign up for a free forever Generate Wealth Newsletter.\n\nBenzinga Disclaimer: This article is from an unpaid external contributor. It does not represent Benzinga’s reporting and has not been edited for content or accuracy.','\n',char(10)),'8b22371092872fdfeea4b5feb85160201beea9c5','2026-09-21 18:42:13','2026-09-21 19:30:37.079272',2,NULL,'2026-09-21 19:55:31');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(520,'alpaca:61905909','benzinga','2026-09-21 18:33:33','Morgan Stanley Says AI Adoption Has Barely Started: ''We''re at the National Anthem''','Morgan Stanley says AI adoption has barely begun, with measurable benefits still rare across corporate America.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61905909/morgan-stanley-ai-adoption-national-anthem','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 19:30:46.434589','analyst','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Commentary on AI adoption trends and their current impact.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-22 18:34:46.161225','2026-09-21 19:30:37.110789','61905909',replace('NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) has become the world’s largest company as AI infrastructure spending surges, but Morgan Stanley (NYSE:MS) says the corporate adoption cycle that comes next has only just started.\n\n“We’re at the national anthem” when it comes to AI adoption, Dan Skelly, head of market research and strategy at Morgan Stanley Wealth Management, told CNBC Monday.\n\n • NVIDIA stock is building positive momentum. Why is NVDA stock advancing?\n\nAI Spending Came First\n\nSkelly said Morgan Stanley has heard “nothing but accelerating demand” during the past three weeks of corporate conference season.\n\nInvestors often ask what inning the AI adoption cycle is in, Skelly said. His answer has been that it is still at the “national anthem,” although he said the “first pitch of the top of the first inning” may now have been thrown.\n\nBut he separated that early adoption cycle from the infrastructure spending boom already underway.\n\n“We’re not early in the spending cycle, but the adoption cycle is what’s going to matter next for this market,” Skelly said.\n\nHe expects tech-focused companies to adopt AI sooner and faster and said the benefits have only begun to show up in earnings. Skelly recommended investors remain biased toward higher-quality Magnificent Seven names.\n\nAn August Citi note showed the scale of the first phase. Google, Microsoft and Amazon’s combined cloud backlog reached $1.69 trillion in the second quarter, up from $1.45 trillion in the first, while backlog growth accelerated to 151% year over year.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Quality Stocks\n\nAI Benefits Are Growing\n\nMorgan Stanley’s Mike Wilson said in July that roughly 25% of S&P; 500 companies cited measurable benefits from AI adoption in the second quarter, up from 14% a year earlier.\n\nThat means roughly three-quarters of the index still had not cited a measurable AI benefit, underscoring Skelly’s argument that the earnings impact remains early.\n\nA separate February survey of 935 executives found companies using AI for at least a year reported an average 11.5% net productivity gain over the previous 12 months.\n\nNvidia Leads Year-End Market-Cap Odds\n\nNvidia has been the biggest market winner from the spending cycle Skelly says is already well underway. The question now is whether broader corporate adoption can justify that buildout.\n\nPolymarket traders currently give Nvidia a 74% chance of finishing 2026 as the world’s largest company, compared with 16% for Apple and 8% for Alphabet.\n\nThe market has attracted about $7.45 million in trading volume.\n\nNvidia CEO Jensen Huang said last week the AI spending flywheel is “really, really flying.”\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nS&P; 500 Will ‘Easily’ Top 8,000 Before Historic Crash, ‘Black Swan’ Fund Manager Says','\n',char(10)),'5fb9e087717d5530081ad34ea7a077b68fa11254','2026-09-21 18:33:33','2026-09-21 19:30:37.079272',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 18:33:33');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(521,'alpaca:61908373','benzinga','2026-09-21 20:02:53','Meta''s Muse Hits No. 1, Carrying AMD Into the $1-Trillion Club','AMD topped $1 trillion as Meta’s Muse led the U.S. free iPhone app chart, fueling bets that AI agents will boost demand for CPUs and AI chips.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61908373/meta-muse-app-store-amd-stock-trillion-ai-agents','["AMD", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-21 20:30:53.901327','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'AMD''s market valuation increased due to positive associations with AI demand driven by Meta''s app.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-22 20:35:17.180005','2026-09-21 20:30:49.689884','61908373',replace('Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) crossed $1 trillion in market value for the first time Monday. \n\nThe milestone followed the rise of Muse, the AI agent from Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META), to the top of the U.S. iPhone download chart.\n\nWhy Muse’s App Ranking Moved AMD\n\nThe connective tissue is a claim AMD management has been making for the better part of a year: agentic workloads lean disproportionately on CPUs rather than on accelerators. \n\nChaining tool calls, orchestrating steps and handling the logic between model invocations is general-purpose compute, and that is AMD’s EPYC franchise. \n\nOn the second-quarter earnings call, AMD CEO Lisa Su put agentic AI at the center of the opportunity.\n\n“We actually see this agentic AI or these agentic sandboxes being the largest piece of the TAM,” she said.\n\nThat’s where Meta’s Muse comes in.\n\nMuse is Meta’s personal AI agent. It has been the most downloaded free iPhone app in the U.S. for three straight days, according to Sensor Tower data. \n\nAn AI agent carries out tasks for users, often in many steps. \n\nThat work is called inference. \n\nIt runs heavily on server central processing units (CPUs), the general-purpose chips that coordinate data center workloads. \n\nAMD has guided to a server CPU addressable market expanding roughly 50% by 2030, to about $220 billion, but the agentic slice of it has so far been a projection rather than a revenue line. \n\nA consumer agent topping the App Store is the first mass-market data point suggesting the projection might be right.\n\nRead Also:\n\n$6.51 Diesel Should Be Crushing the Economy: Here’s Why It Has Rarely Grown Faster\n\nOther Server AI Chips Also Rallied\n\nThe rally spread across the industry. \n\nArm Holdings plc (NASDAQ:ARM) and Intel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) each rose more than 10%. Qualcomm Inc. (NASDAQ:QCOM) gained about 6%. \n\nThe VanEck Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SMH) climbed 3.2%. \n\nThe Numbers Underneath\n\nIn the second quarter ended June 27, AMD reported revenue up 50% year-over-year to $11.5 billion, with non-GAAP diluted earnings per share up 246% to $1.66. \n\nData center revenue more than doubled, rising 107% to $6.7 billion.\n\nAMD also has a direct commercial relationship with Meta. Their February agreement covers planned AMD graphics-chip deployments across infrastructure with up to six gigawatts of power capacity.\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'55162f21ee02e5bf690d66432d1dd3dd6188945b','2026-09-21 20:02:53','2026-09-21 20:30:49.678809',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 20:02:53');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(522,'alpaca:61907952','benzinga','2026-09-21 19:51:07','Ethereum Eyes $3,000 as Mystery Whale Rotates $87 Million Out of Bitcoin','Ethereum tops $2,700 as whales rotate $86.8M from Bitcoin into ETH; record wallet growth and staking fuel bullish momentum toward $2,760-$3,000.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61907952/ethereum-eyes-3000-as-mystery-whale-rotates-87-million-out-of-bitcoin','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 20:30:55.232499','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Whales transferring funds may indicate positive sentiment toward Ethereum.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 11.95}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 12.012}}','2026-09-22 20:35:17.180005','2026-09-21 20:30:49.701349','61907952',replace('Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) climbed above $2,700, its highest level since January, as whale activity accelerated and one large holder rotated a significant amount of Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) into ETH.\n\nOn-chain tracker Lookonchain reported that a mysterious whale sold 1,107 BTC worth $86.76 million on Hyperliquid before buying 34,422 ETH worth $86.5 million and staking the entire position.\n\nThe transactions occurred over the past five days, according to data reported on Sept. 21.\n\nAnother swing trader is also buying back into Ethereum at higher prices.\n\nTrader 0x4cee, who sold 10,500 ETH for $23.64 million at an average price of $2,252 a month ago, bought back 7,567 ETH worth $19.93 million. The earlier sale generated a $3.66 million profit.\n\nOn Chain Activity Shows Strength\n\nSantiment Intelligence data shows whale transactions are climbing as Ethereum breaks higher, suggesting large holders are becoming increasingly active.\n\nEthereum’s holder base has also expanded to a record 207.17 million non-empty wallets.\n\nMore than 40 million ETH is currently staked, while the Ethereum network secures roughly $50 billion in decentralized finance total value locked, supported by stablecoins, lending, decentralized exchanges and liquid staking.\n\nCan ETH Break $3,000?\n\nCrypto analyst Ali Martinez said Ethereum confirmed a breakout after clearing $2,560 and successfully retesting the level as support.\n\nMartinez sees $2,760 as the next major target.\n\nTrader CrediBULL Crypto, meanwhile, said ETH has cleared previously untapped highs and is approaching a key $2,800-$3,000 resistance zone.\n\nHe sees that area as a logical point for a rejection and potentially a deeper pullback toward equal lows. However, a decisive break above the zone could reduce the likelihood of that downside move.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nEthereum Reclaims $2,600 After a Week — Is a Bigger Rally Ahead?','\n',char(10)),'c2e85319f6a27c05b9c29702f749316a74e38ac3','2026-09-21 19:51:07','2026-09-21 20:30:49.678809',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 19:51:07');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(523,'alpaca:61909226','benzinga','2026-09-21 20:37:14','Apple Should Acquire Disney, Robinhood, Uber or these Companies, All-In Podcast Host Says','Could Apple look for acquisitions under a new CEO? All-In Podcast host Jason Calacanis has a list of potential names.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/09/61909226/apple-should-acquire-disney-robinhood-uber-or-these-companies-all-in-podcast-host-says','["AAPL", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-21 21:31:02.715823','rumour','neutral',1,1,'weeks',1,'This is speculation about potential acquisitions by Apple.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-22 21:35:27.257673','2026-09-21 21:30:58.564030','61909226',replace('Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL) investors enjoyed sizable returns during the time with Tim Cook leading the company as CEO from 2011 to 2026. New CEO John Ternus has big shoes to fill and entrepreneur/investor Jason Calacanis has some ideas of what Apple could do to get a head start.\n\n • Apple stock is showing upward bias. What should traders watch with AAPL?\n\nCalacanis Lays out Apple Acquisition Ideas\n\nWhile Apple is focused on the launch of the iPhone 18 and the highly anticipated foldable iPhone Duo, Calacanis would like to see the tech giant start to make some acquisitions.\n\nThe All-In Podcast co-host came ready with a list recently shared on social media of 10 companies, some private and some public, that Apple should acquire.\n\n"Spend that Apple war chest on big swings — only takes on breakout," Calacanis tweeted.\n\nThe 10 companies named are, with some descriptions from Calacanis:\n\nPerplexity AI: search/default LLM\n\nWispr Flow: voice to test, Siri\n\nSuperhuman: AI office suite\n\nExo Labs: Local open-source AI\n\nRobinhood Markets Inc (NASDAQ:HOOD): finance platform\n\nGo.AI: AI infrastructure\n\nDigital Ocean Holdings Inc. (NYSE:DOCN): create an AWS competitor\n\nDisney Co. (NYSE:DIS): obvious\n\nDoorDash Inc (NASDAQ:DASH) and Uber Technologies (NYSE:UBER): get into the real world of logistics\n\nOf the 10 companies named by Calacanis, five are currently publicly traded and five are privately traded. Here’s a look at the current market capitalizations or private valuations for the companies that have information available:\n\nPerplexity: could be worth $30 billion in a funding round led by NVIDIA Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA)\n\nWispr Flow: $2 billion valuation in August 2026\n\nSuperhuman: Acquired by Grammarly for a reported $825 million\n\nExo Labs: no information\n\nRobinhood: $112 billion market capitalization\n\nGo.AI: No information\n\nDigital Ocean: $17 billion market capitalization\n\nDisney: $180 billion market capitalization\n\nDoorDash: $84 billion market capitalization\n\nUber: $145 billion market capitalization\n\nIt’s important to note that Calacanis admitted on X to a comment in the replies that he owns shares of four of the 10 companies he mentions that Apple should buy.\n\nRead Also:\n\nApple CEO John Ternus Enters Role More Like Steve Jobs Than Tim Cook: Here''s How\n\nWill Apple Make a Big Acquisition?\n\nSome analysts and investors have been calling for Apple to make a big acquisition for years, especially in the AI space where the company has lagged behind some rivals.\n\nCurrently, the largest acquisition in Apple history is its $3 billion deal to buy Beats in 2014. Unlike other large technology companies, Apple has grown mostly through new products and internal launches. The company has made only two acquisitions that totaled $1 billion or more in its history.\n\nSome of the names shared by Calacanis could be done for a few billion dollars or less, while others would be huge company-changing deals.\n\nThe Perplexity deal may stand out the most given the rise of AI companies and Apple’s role in the sector.\n\nApple previously almost merged with media giant Disney. A deal to acquire a major media company such as Disney could change the course for Apple and see the company with a larger emphasis on streaming, movies and TV.\n\nThe Services segment has been a big driver for Apple growth and profits. Calacanis pushing for an acquisition of DoorDash and/or Uber could expand on that focus.\n\nApple ended the third quarter with $147 billion in cash, which is not enough to acquire the entire shopping list or companies such as Disney or Uber.\n\nWith Ternus now in charge of Apple, acquisitions could become more normal than in the past as he looks to put his stamp on the future of the technology giant.\n\nRead Also:\n\nWithout Steve Jobs, ''Toy Story'' Might Not Exist. Its New Villain? The Kind Of Screen He Made Famous\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'813d226fb7768bc92d3eafa646d33aa95a6b4afc','2026-09-21 20:37:14','2026-09-21 21:30:58.523998',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 20:37:14');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(524,'alpaca:61909013','benzinga','2026-09-21 20:30:31','Polymarket CEO Reportedly Put Growth Over Fraud Concerns as Kalshi Fights ''Fake Crypto Volume'' Claims','Polymarket faces a reported CFTC probe after a fraud attempt, while Kalshi disputes claims of fake ETH-perpetual volume.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61909013/polymarket-cftc-probe-kalshi-crypto-volume','["ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-21 21:31:03.938457','regulatory','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'Polymarket is under investigation but details are still emerging.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"ETH/USD": {"60m": 12.012}}','2026-09-22 20:35:17.180005','2026-09-21 21:30:58.569925','61909013',replace('Polymarket CEO Shayne Coplan urged staff to focus on growth over regulatory consequences as fraudsters attempted to steal at least $10 million from its U.S. platform, the Wall Street Journal reported.\n\nAsked about the report, a Polymarket spokesperson told Benzinga: “Polymarket is rapidly growing and getting better every day. We are proud of our key leadership hires and continuous infrastructure upgrades and we have quickly scaled and remain focused on growing responsibly at the frontier of finance, tech, and culture.”\n\nKalshi, a Polymarket rival, is separately facing scrutiny over unusual trading in its Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) perpetual futures market.\n\nEmployees Raised Concerns as Fraud Surged\n\nThe Wall Street Journal reported that fraudsters used stolen debit cards to fund Polymarket U.S. accounts in February, place bets, and tried to withdraw the proceeds elsewhere.\n\nAt the height of the attack, payment processor Checkout.com rejected more than 80% of the Polymarket U.S. deposits it handled as fraudulent, compared with roughly 1% normally, according to the Journal.\n\nPolymarket loosened a withdrawal safeguard despite employee warnings that the change could increase money-laundering risks, The Journal reported, citing sources. U.S. compliance chief Andrew Clifford resigned in April after sending executives a report detailing the fraud problems.\n\nThe Journal also reported that the CFTC is investigating Polymarket. The agency told The Block it could neither confirm nor deny an investigation.\n\nLaw firm Sullivan & Cromwell, which has ties to the Trump family, concluded that Polymarket complied with applicable regulations. Donald Trump Jr., President Trump’s eldest son, is on Polymarket’s advisory board.\n\nKalshi’s 174x Ratio Draws Scrutiny\n\nPseudonymous quant analyst and Stealth Neolab co-founder Beni flagged $539 million in 24-hour volume on Kalshi’s Ethereum perpetual futures, which never expire. Open interest, or positions still outstanding, was just $3.1 million.\n\nBeni also identified repeated $5,500 trades that accounted for as much as 58% of Kalshi’s Ethereum perpetual volume across four separate days.\n\nCoinDesk described the 174-to-1 ratio as a red flag for wash or fake trading because trading activity was unusually high while outstanding positions remained small.\n\nKalshi crypto lead IcoBeast pushed back on X, arguing that the fee structure should deter wash trading and that critics had mixed up Kalshi’s prediction-market activity with its perpetual-futures business.\n\nKalshi did not immediately respond to Benzinga’s request for comment.\n\nBenzinga has an existing data collaboration agreement with Kalshi.\n\nWall Street Has Billions Riding on Prediction Markets\n\nIntercontinental Exchange Inc. (NYSE:ICE) has invested $1.6 billion in Polymarket and struck a deal to distribute Polymarket’s prediction-market data to institutional investors. Polymarket was valued at $21 billion in a $1 billion funding round announced last month, with Donald Trump Jr.’s 1789 Capital leading the raise.\n\nRobinhood Markets Inc. (NASDAQ:HOOD) generated $156 million from event contracts in the second quarter, more than the $129 million it made from equities trading or the $100 million from crypto.\n\nRobinhood still routes some event contracts through Kalshi, making the exchange part of the infrastructure behind a rapidly growing business for the brokerage.\n\nRead Also:\n\nS&P; 500 Will ‘Easily’ Top 8,000 Before Historic Crash, ‘Black Swan’ Fund Manager Says\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'da503d9c2212e4157173001f566de2aea2ea4265','2026-09-21 20:30:31','2026-09-21 21:30:58.523998',1,NULL,'2026-09-21 20:30:31');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(525,'alpaca:61911457','benzinga','2026-09-22 02:01:49','Bitcoin Tops $87,000, Ethereum, XRP, Dogecoin Also Lift Amid ''Extreme Greed''—Analyst Declares Bear Market Over, Says This is the ''Next Stop'' for BTC','Leading cryptocurrencies jumped to multi-month highs on Monday, September 21, amid rampant optimism and growing &#34;fear of missing out.&#34;','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61911457/bitcoin-ethereum-xrp-dogecoin-crypto-greed-sentiment','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "ETH/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-22 02:31:22.168812','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Cryptocurrencies reached multi-month highs due to optimism and FOMO.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "SOL/USD": 101.29, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 12.332}, "DOGE/USD": {"60m": 20.556, "1d": 24.434}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 12.092}, "SOL/USD": {"60m": 15.412, "1d": 16.895}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 17.768, "1d": 22.229}}','2026-09-23 02:35:45.807172','2026-09-22 02:31:18.389197','61911457',replace('Leading cryptocurrencies jumped to multi-month highs on Monday amid rampant optimism and growing “fear of missing out.”\n\nCryptocurrency24-Hour Gains +/-Price (Recorded at 9:30 p.m. EDT)Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC)+5.42%$85,789.27Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH)               +2.88%$2,752XRP (CRYPTO: XRP)                         +6.55%$1.51Solana (CRYPTO: SOL)                         +5.18%$117.96Dogecoin (CRYPTO: DOGE)             +12.25%$0.09956\n\nCrypto Market Erupts\n\nBitcoin stormed past $87,000 for the first time since January, while trading volume jumped nearly 150% over the last 24 hours.\n\nEthereum also rallied to a nearly 10-month high of $2,800, while XRP and Dogecoin recorded sharp upticks.\n\nCryptocurrency-related stocks advanced, with Strategy Inc. (NASDAQ:MSTR) and Bitmine Immersion Technologies Inc. (NYSE:BMNR) closing up 9.47% and 8.70%, respectively. \n\nOver $1 billion was liquidated from the cryptocurrency market in the last 24 hours, with $840 million in bearish short bets wiped out, according to Coinglass data.\n\nBitcoin’s open interest soared 8.44% over the last 24 hours. A jump in open interest alongside a jump in price typically indicates strong bullish momentum and fresh money entering the market.\n\n"Extreme Greed" sentiment swept the market, according to the Crypto Fear & Greed Index.\n\nTop Gainers (24 Hours) \n\nCryptocurrency (Market Cap>$100 M)Gains +/-Price (Recorded at 9:30 p.m. EDT)AIOZ Network (AIOZ)      +40.05%    $0.1289Four (FORM)                   +34.29%    $0.3533Pepe (PEPE)              +24.66%    $0.000005052\n\nThe global cryptocurrency market capitalization spiked to $2.91 trillion, representing a 4.28% increase over the last 24 hours.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Trails Nasdaq This Year: Why One Analyst Calls It ‘Helpful’\n\nStocks Rally, Nasdaq Closes at Record\n\nThe stock market kicked off the new trading week strongly. The Dow Jones Industrial Average rallied 366.19 points, or 0.71%, to settle at 52,048.83. The S&P; 500 rose 1.49% to end at 7,764.70, while the tech-focused Nasdaq Composite surged 2.26% to close at a record high of 27,122.09.\n\nIran relayed conditions to the U.S. for re-engaging in negotiations aimed at ending the war. Meanwhile, President Donald Trump told Fox News he would "probably" be open to meeting with Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian during the United Nations General Assembly this week\n\nEnd of Bear Market?\n\nMichaël van de Poppe, a widely followed cryptocurrency analyst and trader, stated that Bitcoin’s surge won’t stop anytime soon, targeting $90,000-$91,000 next, with potential extension to $98,000-$100,000.\n\n“I don’t think I’d be betting against this trend,” Van De Poppe added. “The bear market is over.”\n\nWhat a breakout of #Bitcoin.I don''t think I''d be betting against this trend. This won''t stop soon. Not after a day like this.Next stop: $90,000-91,000.If there''s enough strength, we might even run to $98,000-100,000 in this rally.The bear market is over. pic.twitter.com/XrSQZcecbU— Michaël van de Poppe (@CryptoMichNL) September 21, 2026 \n\nAt the same time, Bitcoin’s bullish commentary surged to its highest level since 2024, according to on-chain analytics firm Santiment.\n\n“Crypto often punishes crowded expectations,” Santiment warned. “Extreme fear can appear near exhaustion lows, while synchronized ‘higher from here’ confidence can develop near local tops.”\n\n🚨 BREAKING: Bitcoin FOMO Hits Highest Level Since 2024!🚀 Crypto’s mood has flipped hard into celebration. Talk of Bitcoin and crypto expected to go even "higher" or staying bullish has surged far above bearish language as $BTC pushed toward $87K, helped by a massive short… pic.twitter.com/8lt1zw3yfm— Santiment Intelligence (@SantimentData) September 21, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nIs Solana''s Next ''Token Supercycle'' Taking Shape? Expert Identifies Three Key Indicators\n\nPhoto: KateStock / Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'210b814b19613c63d61c55a7d548979013df26cd','2026-09-22 02:01:49','2026-09-22 02:31:18.381640',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 02:01:49');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(526,'alpaca:61911445','benzinga','2026-09-22 02:00:43','Nvidia-Backed AI Drug Discovery Company Iambic Therapeutics Files for Nasdaq IPO, to Use Proceeds for Cancer Drug Development','Iambic Therapeutics, an AI drug discovery company backed by Nvidia and the Qatar Investment Authority, filed to go public Monday.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/ipos/26/09/61911445/nvidia-backed-ai-drug-discovery-startup-iambic-therapeutics-files-for-ipo','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 02:31:23.718061','listing','neutral',3,3,'weeks',1,'Iambic Therapeutics has filed for an IPO, which is notable news but does not directly impact Nvidia''s stock.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-23 02:35:45.807172','2026-09-22 02:31:18.392085','61911445',replace('Iambic Therapeutics, Inc., an AI drug discovery company backed by Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) and the Qatar Investment Authority, filed for an initial public offering, according to an S-1 filing with the SEC on Monday.\n\nPlans to List on Nasdaq, Under Ticker ‘IAM’\n\nIambic said it plans to use the IPO proceeds, along with its existing cash, to continue advancing its three cancer drug candidates through clinical development, with any remaining funds going toward general operating costs.\n\nIt will go public on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the ticker “IAM.”\n\nThe filing did not disclose the number of shares to be offered or an expected price range. \n\n J.P. Morgan, Jefferies, BofA Securities and Citigroup are underwriting the offering.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMeta Platforms, Greenland Mines, Intel, AMD and GameStop: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors'' Radars Today\n\nThe Company’s AI Drug Platform\n\nFounded in 2019, Iambic combines proprietary AI models with automated lab experiments to discover new drugs, an approach it calls “molecular superintelligence.”\n\nIts lead drug candidate, an experimental cancer pill designed to target tumors driven by the HER2 protein, is currently in early human trials. \n\nTwo additional cancer drug candidates remain in earlier lab-stage testing, with Iambic planning to seek FDA clearance to begin human trials on both by the end of the year.\n\nThe Delaware-based company has raised roughly $461.8 million in capital since its founding through Sept. 18, from investors including Catalio, Nexus Ventures, Q Healthcare Holding, Nvidia, and Coatue Ventures, its five largest shareholders.\n\nThe company also holds partnerships with major pharmaceutical firms, including AbbVie Inc. (NYSE:ABBV), Takeda Pharmaceutical Company Limited (NYSE:TAK), and Jazz Pharmaceuticals PLC (NASDAQ:JAZZ). \n\nRevenue Growing, But Losses Widening\n\nIambic’s full-year 2025 revenue was $9.4 million, up from $1.2 million in 2024, while its net loss widened to $77.3 million from $47.9 million over the same period.Benzinga edge rankings indicate Nvidia’s stock has a Momentum score in the 81st percentile and a Growth score in the 98th percentile. \n\nSee More:\n\nTop Growth Stocks\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto: fadfebrian on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'8fc6e52e750d37d6b836127b225b29bceb21a4d5','2026-09-22 02:00:43','2026-09-22 02:31:18.381640',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 02:00:43');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(527,'alpaca:61911416','benzinga','2026-09-22 01:38:59','Meta Platforms, Greenland Mines, Intel, AMD and GameStop: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors'' Radars Today','META, GRML, INTC, AMD, GME were among the stocks seen trending on Monday, Sept. 21, 2026.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61911416/meta-platforms-greenland-mines-intel-amd-and-gamestop-why-these-5-stocks-are-on-investors-radars-today','["AMD", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 02:31:24.941716','other','neutral',1,3,'days',1,'The headline indicates ongoing interest in the stocks without specifying any particular event.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-23 02:35:45.807172','2026-09-22 02:31:18.397154','61911416',replace('Major U.S. indices ended higher on Monday, with the Dow Jones Industrial Average rising 0.7% to 52,048.83, the S&P; 500 gaining 1.49% to 7,764.70 and the Nasdaq climbing 2.26% to 27,122.09.These are the top stocks that gained the attention of retail traders and investors through the day:Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META)Meta Platforms saw its shares surge by 11.43% to close at $741.25. The stock reached an intraday high of $753 and a low of $679.60, with a 52-week range of $520.26 to $785.73. The Mark Zuckerberg-led company added over $200 billion in market value, climbing from a market cap of about $1.695 trillion to approximately $1.902 trillion. Meta’s RSI indicates overbought conditions, trading significantly above its 50-day and 200-day SMAs.On Monday, Zuckerberg said Meta was teaming up with Shopify Inc. to make shopping and checkout ‘easier’ with its Muse personal AI agent. “Shoppers find more. Shops sell more. More partnerships like this coming soon,” said the CEO.\nTeaming up with Shopify to make shopping and checkout easier in Muse. Shoppers find more. Shops sell more. More partnerships like this coming soon. https://t.co/ccak4J7IIb— Mark Zuckerberg (@finkd) September 21, 2026 \nGreenland Mines Ltd (NASDAQ:GRML)Greenland Mines shares skyrocketed by 230.53% to close at $9.42, hitting an intraday high of $11.68 and a low of $6.63. The stock’s 52-week range is $2.82 to $27.48. In the after-hours session, the stock rose 16.03% to $10.93. The surge followed the company’s expansion of its Sarfartoq rare earth magnet district land position in West Greenland. The expansion adds 262 square kilometers, bringing the total to approximately 454 square kilometers. The expansion comes after President Donald Trump announced a U.S.-Denmark Greenland Security Agreement that reinforces the territory’s strategic importance.\n\nRead Also:\n\nPeter Schiff Says Trump ''Gave Up'' on Greenland and His Deal Only Lasts Until NATO ''Remains in Place'': ''He Settled For…''\n\nIntel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC)Intel Corp. rose by 12.14% to close at $121.78, with an intraday high of $124.73 and a low of $114.93. The stock’s 52-week range is $28.73 to $142.34. In extended trading, the stock rose 1.7% to $123.85.Intel shares rose, extending a rally that had lifted the stock roughly 278% over the past year, while the company benefited from broader strength in technology and semiconductor stocks. Recent catalysts included Altera’s confidential U.S. IPO filing and reports that SK hynix was considering producing memory chips at Intel facilities, while Intel’s Momentum score stood at 98.93 and its Hold consensus carried an average price target of $112.74.Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD)Advanced Micro Devices Inc. climbed 9.95% to close at $615.52, reaching an intraday high of $616.69 and a low of $582.27. The stock’s 52-week range is $154.78 to $616.69. AMD shares hit a record high after gaining 8.4% to $606.98, extending their 2026 rally to about 183%, following major AI infrastructure commitments. The company crossed the $1 trillion market cap mark on Monday.OpenAI agreed to deploy 6 gigawatts of AMD Instinct GPUs, while Oracle committed to 50,000 MI450 accelerators; AMD said the OpenAI deal was immediately accretive and could support tens of billions of dollars in annual AI data center revenue from 2027.GameStop Corp. (NYSE:GME)GameStop Corp. shares edged up by 0.53% to close at $22.76, with an intraday high of $23.11 and a low of $22.52. The stock’s 52-week range is $17.79 to $28.10. In the after-hours session, the stock rose 3.21% to $23.49. The increase followed CEO Ryan Cohen’s purchase of an additional $26 million worth of shares, pushing his ownership past 40 million shares. Benzinga Edge Stock Rankings indicate Meta stock has a Momentum score in the 45th percentile and Value in the 49th percentile.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.Photo Courtesy: Arsenii Palivoda on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'0ea3867527da82cf285371f662443f68a36de167','2026-09-22 01:38:59','2026-09-22 02:31:18.381640',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 01:38:59');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(528,'alpaca:61911633','benzinga','2026-09-22 03:17:26','Anthony Pompiano Reiterates Bitcoin Has ''No Top'' Because the Dollar Has ''No Bottom,'' Bets BTC Will Go ''Way Higher''','Anthony Pompliano, CEO of ProCap Financial Inc., reiterated his long-held view on Monday, September 21, that Bitcoin’s future growth is tied to an increase in the money supply.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61911633/anthony-pompiano-bitcoin-no-top-dollar-no-bottom-btc-higher','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 03:31:32.878138','analyst','bullish',2,3,'weeks',1,'Analyst''s opinion may influence market sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 12.332}}','2026-09-23 03:35:57.761537','2026-09-22 03:31:28.902815','61911633',replace('Anthony Pompliano, CEO of ProCap Financial Inc. (NASDAQ:BRR), reiterated his long-held view on Monday that Bitcoin’s (CRYPTO: BTC) future growth is tied to an increase in the money supply.\n\n‘Dollar Has No Bottom’\n\nIn a Fox News interview, Pompliano said Bitcoin does not depend on the CLARITY Act, but is shaped more by global liquidity and fiat money printing.\n\nHe further emphasized the U.S.’s burgeoning national debt, currently over $40 trillion, and argued that Bitcoin’s value has no ceiling as long as the dollar continues to devalue. \n\n“Bitcoin has no top because the dollar has no bottom,” Pompliano reiterated.\n\nDebasement Trade Is Back?\n\nCoinGlass data largely backs Pompliano’s view that Bitcoin tends to benefit from a growing global money supply. But that link has weakened in the 2025-2026 bear market, with Bitcoin prices falling despite rising liquidity.\n\nSource: Coinglass\n\n“If the government keeps printing money, Bitcoin is going to go way higher in the coming years,” Pompliano projected.\n\nThe Treasury said last month it would at least double the maximum size of its buyback operations from $2 billion to $4 billion, targeting securities in the 10- to 20-year and 20- to 30-year maturity ranges.\n\nThe move sent yields and the dollar lower, prompting renewed interest in Bitcoin as a hedge against debasement.\n\nRead Also:\n\nIs Solana''s Next ''Token Supercycle'' Taking Shape? Expert Identifies Three Key Indicators\n\nBitcoin Takes Off\n\nPompliano said last month that people in Washington, D.C., are “absolutely ridiculous,” and he’s willing to bet on their "stupidity" to print more money. \n\nHe maintains that Bitcoin will eventually reach $1 million due to this play.\n\nBitcoin reached an intraday high of $87,363 on Monday, its highest since late January, as the SEC’s push to build a regulatory framework for cryptocurrency, including tokenized U.S. stocks, outweighed the CLARITY Act’s failure.\n\nPrice Action: At the time of writing, BTC was exchanging hands at $85,736, up 5.13% in the last 24 hours, according to data from Benzinga Pro.\n\nProCap Shares rose 1.47% in after-hours trading. The stock closed 8.24% higher at $4.07 during Monday’s regular trading session.\n\nAccording to Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings, the stock shows a stronger price trend in the short- and medium- term but lags over the long term.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Quality Stocks\n\nPhoto: Hi my name is Jacco on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'2b86238958231e753a3105935ff4c67e341b836c','2026-09-22 03:17:26','2026-09-22 03:31:28.898895',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 03:17:26');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(529,'alpaca:61911620','benzinga','2026-09-22 03:12:36','Google Partners With Southern Co''s Georgia Power for AI Data Centers, Deal Projected to Deliver $900 Million in Customer Benefits','Southern Company&#39;s Georgia Power and Google announced an agreement to support nuclear power uprates to secure clean power for data centers.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61911620/google-georgia-power-nuclear-energy-ai-data-centers','["AMZN", "META", "MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-22 03:31:34.132921','partnership','bullish',3,4,'weeks',1,'The partnership is expected to deliver significant customer benefits and enhance data center operations.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48}','{}','2026-09-23 03:35:57.761537','2026-09-22 03:31:28.905638','61911620',replace('Southern Company‘s (NYSE:SO) subsidiary Georgia Power and Alphabet Inc.‘s (NASDAQ:GOOG) (NASDAQ:GOOGL) Google announced Monday an agreement to support nuclear power uprates at the Vogtle and Hatch plants to secure more clean power for its data centers. \n\nWhat the Deal Involves\n\nThe deal is expected to deliver roughly $900 million in projected benefits to customers over the life of the units. \n\nIt will add about 96 megawatts of new capacity to the grid by upgrading Georgia Power-owned portions of the nuclear units at Vogtle and Hatch.\n\nAs part of the deal, Google will subscribe to the new tariff and receive Zero-Emission Credits tied to the nuclear power generated.\n\nThe agreement is subject to approval by the Georgia Public Service Commission.\n\nRead Also:\n\nParamount''s $110B Warner Bros. Discovery Merger Clears Legal Hurdle; Elizabeth Warren Says Letting Trump-Aligned Entity ''Dominate'' News Is ''Disastrous''\n\nPushback Against Data Centers in Georgia\n\nThe deal also comes amid growing pushback in Georgia, where state Rep. Ruwa Romman (D-Ga.) introduced a bill earlier this year proposing a statewide moratorium on new data centers through March, citing concerns over their environmental and economic impact.\n\nGoogle’s director of Advanced Energy Technologies, Lucia Tian, said the company’s data centers serve as “a proof point” for bringing new nuclear capacity online by expanding existing plants, adding that the deal helps deliver “a more affordable, clean, and reliable energy system for all Georgia residents.”\n\nData Center Spending Is Exploding\n\nData-center capital expenditure is projected to rise from 1.4% of GDP in 2025 to 3.1% by 2027, with hyperscaler capex expected to reach roughly $916 billion over the next 12 months and nearly $1.2 trillion the year after. \n\nS&P; Global has estimated combined capex from Alphabet, Amazon.com, Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN), Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT), Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META), Oracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL) and Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) will exceed $1.3 trillion in 2027.\n\nPrice Action: Southern Co closed 0.07% lower on Monday at $85.46 and gained 0.48% in extended trading. \n\nBenzinga edge rankings indicate Southern Co’s stock has a Momentum score in the 18th percentile and a Growth score in the 59th percentile. \n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto Courtesy: ZikG on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'94e38c92ff628a1b24201d952dd6de4f2dc72551','2026-09-22 03:12:36','2026-09-22 03:31:28.898895',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 03:12:36');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(530,'alpaca:61911752','benzinga','2026-09-22 04:26:24','XRP Will Advance to $5.40? Veteran Trader Peter Brandt Shares Long-Term Forecast, Another Popular Analyst Says Coin Has ''Room to Run''','Veteran trader Peter Brandt forecast on Monday, September 21, a potential fourfold jump in XRP&#39;s price as the fifth-largest cryptocurrency regained momentum.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61911752/xrp-peter-brandt-bullish-price-target','["BTC/USD", "XRP/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 04:31:41.298962','other','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'The headline presents speculation about XRP''s price without confirmation.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 12.332}, "XRP/USD": {"60m": 17.843}}','2026-09-23 04:36:08.563965','2026-09-22 04:31:37.513233','61911752',replace('On Monday, seasoned trader Peter Brandt forecast a potential fourfold jump in XRP’s (CRYPTO: XRP) price as the fifth-largest cryptocurrency regained momentum.\n\nXRP’s Long-Term Forecast\n\nBrandt shared a long-term monthly chart of XRP on X, which projected an “eventual advance” to $5.40, citing trend channels and moving averages. This represents a potential upside of 257%.\n\nBrandt, a technical analyst with nearly 50 years of experience,  stressed that presenting a chart is not a trade recommendation or “call.”\n\nThis is my long-term chart of ripple:native It implies an eventual advance to $5.40 A claim of a "call" or simple presentation of a chart is NOT a trade People who claim "trades" need to provide proof or else the claims are BS An X post is NOT proof pic.twitter.com/Szu6FiZq2T— The Factor Report (@PeterLBrandt) September 21, 2026 \n\nBuy What Happens in the Short Term?\n\neditorial.benzinga.com/wp-admin/post.php?post=1653468&action;=edit\n\nMeanwhile, Ali Martinez, another renowned chartist and cryptocurrency trader, highlighted that XRP whales had been heavily accumulating tokens lately\n\nMartinez added that there may “still be room to run,” citing data from the Unspent Transaction Output Realized Price Distribution chart.\n\nThe indicator maps out the exact price levels where existing coin supplies last moved or were acquired on-chain.\n\n“The URPD shows relatively little resistance ahead until $1.60, where roughly 2.50 billion XRP previously changed hands,” Martinez stated. “That’s the next major level I’m watching for potential profit-taking.”\n\nXRP RALLIES AFTER WHALES BUY. WHERE NEXT?Recently, whales accumulated more than $2 billion worth of $XRP.Now that demand appears to be showing up in price, with XRP rallying 8.22% in just three days.But on-chain data suggests there may still be room to run.The URPD shows… https://t.co/yWD0rDhj2X pic.twitter.com/wjiQ9hLz8R— Ali Charts (@alicharts) September 21, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nTop 6 Crypto Stocks Climbing with Bitcoin Right Now\n\nWill XRP Bulls Remain in Charge?\n\nXRP has climbed 6.82% over the past week, supported by broad optimism in the cryptocurrency market and developments within its own ecosystem.\n\nRipple said asset managers and commercial projects are preparing to use a major XRP Ledger payments upgrade nearing activation. Its structure allows linked transactions to settle or fail together, supporting use cases such as delivery-versus-payment.\n\nMoreover, the SEC’s push to build a regulatory framework for cryptocurrency after the CLARITY Act’s failure has reignited bullish sentiment, also driving XRP higher.\n\nThe Moving Average Convergence Divergence indicator, which compares the 12-period and the 26-period exponential moving averages, flashed a “Buy” signal for XRP, according to TradingView.\n\nConversely, the Bull Bear Power indicator, which measures the strength of buyers and sellers, signaled a “Sell.” \n\nPrice Action: At the time of writing, XRP traded at $1.51, up 6.40% in the last 24 hours, according to data from Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nXRP Price Prediction as Multiple Catalysts Point to Further Gains\n\nPhoto: Stanslavs on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'f48e9777d4c03362d044bdda7603c2261c0c04b6','2026-09-22 04:26:24','2026-09-22 04:31:37.509484',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 04:26:24');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(531,'alpaca:61911651','benzinga','2026-09-22 03:29:38','Cloudflare (NET) Stock Is Trending After Hours: Here''s Why','Cloudflare shares rose 0.25% after hours Monday, extending gains after the stock surged 8.67% during regular trading.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61911651/cloudflare-shares-025-higher-after-hours','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 04:31:42.486794','other','neutral',1,3,'hours',1,'The stock''s movement is part of routine trading activity and trending interest.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-23 03:35:57.761537','2026-09-22 04:31:37.575274','61911651',replace('Cloudflare Inc. (NYSE:NET) shares are trending on Monday night.\n\nShares of the California-based cloud-networking and cybersecurity company edged 0.25% higher to $352.56 in after-hours trading on Monday.\n\nIn the regular session, NET surged 8.67% to close at $351.67, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nOn Monday, NET experienced an elevated trading session. Volume reached 3.89 million shares, topping the average of 3.61 million.\n\nCFO Sells Shares\n\nAccording to a Monday Securities and Exchange Commission filing, Cloudflare Chief Financial Officer Thomas J. Seifert exercised an employee stock option on Sept. 17 to acquire 10,000 shares of Class B Common Stock at $2.04 per share. He converted the shares into Class A Common Stock on the same day.\n\nSeifert then sold all 10,000 Class A shares that day in a series of transactions ranging from $318.90 to $336.51 per share. The sales were made under a pre-arranged trading plan adopted last year.\n\nBased on the weighted-average prices reported in the filing, the sales were worth an estimated $3.32 million. After the transactions, Seifert directly held 107,902 Class A shares.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMeta Platforms, Greenland Mines, Intel, AMD and GameStop: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors'' Radars Today\n\nWhat You Should Know\n\nOn the same day of the transaction, Bernstein‘s Peter Weed maintained a Market Perform rating on Cloudflare, raising his price target to $181 from $164. The analyst’s price target is well below the stock’s trading price at the time.\n\nCloudflare made Ritholtz Wealth Management CEO  Josh Brown and colleague Sean Russo‘s “Best Stocks in the Market” list Monday. The list tracks high-performing equities meeting strict fundamental and technical criteria.\n\nThe tech stock recently drew fresh attention when Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) unveiled Muse, a personal AI agent built to handle tasks like booking travel and sending emails on a user’s behalf. This came as Cloudflare and Meta have partnered since 2023, when Llama 2 launched on Cloudflare Workers AI.\n\nTrading Metrics, Technical Analysis\n\nCloudflare has a market capitalization of $125.22 billion. Its 52-week high is $352.45, while its 52-week low is $158.83.\n\nNET’s Relative Strength Index (RSI) is currently 65.41.\n\nThe large-cap stock has risen 54.05% over the past 12 months.\n\nNET is currently trading close to its 52-week high.\n\nWith a strong Momentum score in the 93rd percentile, Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings show that Cloudflare stock has maintained a positive price trend across all time frames.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Sundry Photography on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'33c78b741347c07967b10c5e985b83877093664d','2026-09-22 03:29:38','2026-09-22 04:31:37.509484',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 03:29:38');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(532,'alpaca:61911829','benzinga','2026-09-22 04:59:18','Mark Zuckerberg Says ''More Partnerships'' Coming as Meta Teams With Shopify to Power AI Purchases: ''Shoppers Find More, Shops Sell More''','Meta and Shopify announced that they are partnering to enable AI-powered shopping and checkout through Meta’s Muse agent.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61911829/meta-shopify-ai-shopping-partnership-zuckerberg','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 05:31:50.141754','partnership','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Meta''s partnership with Shopify could enhance its e-commerce offerings.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}','2026-09-23 05:36:32.647500','2026-09-22 05:31:46.178424','61911829',replace('Meta Platforms, Inc. (NASDAQ:META) and Shopify Inc. (NASDAQ:SHOP) are teaming up to bring AI-powered shopping and checkout to Meta’s Muse personal AI agent.\n\nMeta Muse Partners With Shopify For AI Shopping\n\nMeta’s Muse will integrate with Shopify’s e-commerce infrastructure, allowing the AI assistant to help users shop across stores powered by Shopify and complete purchases through Shop Pay, the company’s accelerated checkout service.\n\nShop Pay lets customers save payment and shipping details for faster checkout.\n\nShopify CEO Tobias Lütke also shared the development on X, describing it as an effort to create an "easy and delightful way to shop and check out with Muse."\n\nWe are excited to announce we are partnering deeply with Muse to enable agentic checkout with Shop Pay on all Shopify stores, offering people an easy and delightful way to shop and check out with Muse. pic.twitter.com/KmRlKjoLoq— tobi lutke (@tobi) September 21, 2026 \n\n"Teaming up with Shopify to make shopping and checkout easier in Muse," Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg said in a post on X. "Shoppers find more. Shops sell more. More partnerships like this coming soon."\n\nTeaming up with Shopify to make shopping and checkout easier in Muse. Shoppers find more. Shops sell more. More partnerships like this coming soon. https://t.co/ccak4J7IIb— Mark Zuckerberg (@finkd) September 21, 2026 \n\nNeither Meta nor Shopify immediately responded to Benzinga’s requests for additional details.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMeta Stock Adds Over $200 Billion in Value Today\n\nMeta’s Muse Moves Toward Autonomous Shopping\n\nMeta introduced Muse earlier this month as a personal AI agent that can handle tasks such as scheduling appointments, managing finances and assisting with shopping.\n\nMeta Chief AI Officer Alexandr Wang said the Shopify partnership will give Muse users access to a broader selection of stores and products.\n\n"We want to give our musers access to a wide range of stores to find the absolute perfect products," Wang said.\n\nwe are excited for muse to be partnering deeply with @Shopify to enable agentic checkout with Shop Pay on all Shopify stores!we want to give our musers access to a wide range of stores to find the absolute perfect products ♥️ https://t.co/ckj3BMBxqg— Alexandr Wang (@alexandr_wang) September 21, 2026 \n\nWang also addressed confusion surrounding Muse by sharing an image of the AI assistant’s mascot and directing users to the Muse app for more information.\n\nwell first you''re going to need to learn about this lil guythen you''re gonna have to catch up on the multi-year history of shopify vs amazonthen just gotta download the app! https://t.co/oGzBjKtAyn https://t.co/3IMYwlORzp pic.twitter.com/yInyOOe80s— Alexandr Wang (@alexandr_wang) September 21, 2026 \n\nWhy Shopify Matters to AI Agents\n\nIn a note, Deutsche Bank analysts said the partnership offers further evidence that major AI platforms are adopting Shopify’s commerce infrastructure, the Wall Street Journal reported. \n\nThis could ease investor concerns that AI agents and virtual shopping assistants could disrupt its business.\n\nThe analysts said the deal instead highlights Shopify’s core strengths, including structured product data through Shopify Catalog, access to merchants, Shop Pay’s checkout capabilities and the infrastructure needed to process orders.\n\nPrice Action: Meta shares closed at $741.24 on Monday, up 11.43%. The shares traded at $740 in after-hours trading, down 0.17%. Shopify shares closed at $137.92 during regular hours, up 7.33% and rose another 0.70% to $138.88 in after-hours trading, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nAccording to Benzinga Edge Stock Rankings, Meta ranks in the 79th percentile for Growth, with its stock showing positive short-, medium- and long-term price trends.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Growth Stocks\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Harmony Video Production on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'4ab17ba976699446b5d20093b55b8df8dc2ff18c','2026-09-22 04:59:18','2026-09-22 05:31:46.170756',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 04:59:18');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(533,'alpaca:61911814','benzinga','2026-09-22 04:47:54','SpaceX, Tesla Share Chips, Robots And Compute; Morgan Stanley Calls It A ''Shared Mission'' To Turn Energy Into Intelligence: Merger Next?','&#34;SpaceX and Tesla are tightening shared infrastructure as they push into &#39;physical AI,&#39; a dynamic that could lead to a merger, according to Morgan Stanley.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61911814/morgan-stanley-says-spacex-and-teslas-deepening-ai-ties-could-lead-to-a-merger','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 05:31:51.766736','mna','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'Speculation about a potential merger with no confirmed details.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}','2026-09-23 05:36:32.647500','2026-09-22 05:31:46.181080','61911814',replace('Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) and Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) are tightening a web of shared infrastructure and technology as the Elon Musk-led companies push into “physical AI,” a dynamic Morgan Stanley believes could lead to a potential merger.\n\nDeepening Web Of Shared Infrastructure\n\nAnalysts at the bank led by Adam Jonas said the companies “share tech, talent, and infrastructure in a shared mission of converting energy to intelligence,” according to an Investing.com report. \n\nAs large language models approach potential performance limits, the firm expects investor attention to shift toward physical AI, arguing the two companies may be “uniquely capable of addressing” that opportunity, “separately or, more likely, jointly.” \n\nThe analysts counted 71 mentions of “Tesla” in SpaceX’s S-1 filing, with 34% referencing direct collaboration and 41% tied to governance and related-party transactions. \n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump TV Launched on YouTube by White House Amid Growing Dispute with CNN, MS NOW and Others: ''It''s Live''\n\nCompute And Connectivity Flow Both Ways\n\nThe two companies are jointly building Terafab, a Texas chip factory with Intel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) costing over $119 billion, and co-developing an AI platform called Macrohard. \n\nSpaceX bought $506 million worth of Tesla Megapacks and $131 million worth of Cybertrucks in 2025 for its Colossus compute cluster. The rocket maker’s quarterly filing showed Megapack purchases totaled $329 million in the first half of this year.\n\nSpaceX supplies Tesla compute, set to reach 4.9 gigawatts by 2027, and Starlink connectivity starting with Cybercab. \n\nTesla, in turn, provides SpaceX with data-collecting robots, energy storage tech and manufacturing expertise from a workforce over six times SpaceX’s size, Morgan Stanley noted.\n\nMusk Has Fueled Merger Talk \n\nMusk has repeatedly stoked speculation about a future Tesla-SpaceX merger, telling the All In Podcast with SpaceX President Gwynne Shotwell this month that, given “all this collaboration on so many levels,” people should “imagine what action one might take when there’s so much close collaboration in so many areas.” \n\nInvestor Ross Gerber has said a merger could become a “must-have” for global investors, though he’s warned it would be dilutive for SpaceX shareholders and a poor deal for Tesla investors given the two companies’ current valuations.\n\nSpaceX has a valuation of $2.06 trillion compared to Tesla’s ‪$1.48 trillion, according to TradingView. \n\nPrice Action: SpaceX’s shares closed 0.56% lower on Monday at $151.85 and climbed 0.58% in extended trading. Tesla closed 3.03% higher at $375.30 and fell 0.01% in after-hours trading. \n\nBenzinga edge rankings indicate SpaceX’s stock has a positive price trend across the short, medium, and long term. \n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Walter Cicchetti on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'60cab6a48478df90c2dee895e827731bef0185ec','2026-09-22 04:47:54','2026-09-22 05:31:46.170756',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 04:47:54');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(534,'alpaca:61912020','benzinga','2026-09-22 05:55:14','Stock Market: Will S&P 500 Open Up or Down Today?','Will the S&amp;P 500 open higher? Polymarket odds sit at 53% as Wall Street weighs Iranian airline sanctions, $101 Brent oil, and AZO earnings.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61912020/stock-market-will-sp-500-open-up-or-down-today-42','["QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-22 06:31:59.173355','other','neutral',1,1,'minutes',1,'The headline poses a question without definitive information.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-23 06:36:43.730880','2026-09-22 06:31:54.871459','61912020',replace('U.S. stock futures are showing a mixed-to-slightly-flat picture early Tuesday as Wall Street balances new U.S. sanctions targeting Iranian airlines against fresh corporate earnings reports and lingering market optimism from Monday’s AI-led rally.\n\nThe Polymarket (CRYPTO: POL) crowd is leaning slightly bullish for the Sept. 22 trading session. The “S&P; 500 (SPX) Up or Down on September 22?” contract currently reflects a 53% chance of a higher open.\n\nWhy That Number Matters\n\nTraders are navigating a mix of geopolitical escalations, oil price movements, and central bank commentary:\n\nMixed Index Futures: Equity futures are pointing to a quiet, mixed open across major benchmarks. S&P; 500 futures dipped 0.01%, Dow Jones futures fell 0.06%, and Russell 2000 futures dropped 0.07%. Meanwhile, Nasdaq 100 futures ticked up 0.08%.\n\nGeopolitics & Rising Oil: U.S. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent announced that Iranian airlines will be “shut down” worldwide by Wednesday, warning foreign entities that providing fuel or landing services will result in exclusion from the dollar-based financial system. Treasury also targeted major foreign financial institutions in Egypt, Turkey, and Russia for facilitating Iranian transactions. Energy prices bounced higher following the news, with Brent crude futures advancing 1.38% to $101.72 per barrel and WTI crude rising 1.13% to $93.41 per barrel.\n\nFed Speeches & Economic Data: Richmond Fed President Thomas Barkin is scheduled to speak to the CFA Society Baltimore at 1:00 p.m. ET, giving investors further perspective on central bank policy following last week’s interest rate hike.\n\nEarnings Docket: Tuesday’s earnings lineup includes reports from AutoZone Inc. (NYSE:AZO), Thor Industries Inc. (NYSE:THO), KB Home (NYSE:KBH), Worthington Enterprises Inc. (NYSE:WOR), and MillerKnoll Inc. (NASDAQ:MLKN).\n\nThe Bull Case and Market Outlook\n\nAccording to Nigam Arora, equities surged on Monday as investors bought into momentum surrounding potential diplomatic proposals, a U.S.-Greenland security agreement, and reports that Anthropic’s IPO is slated for November. Big tech names led the charge, with positive early money flows lifting Big Tech stocks.\n\nHowever, the Arora Report advised caution, noting that while Bitcoin’s push above $85,000 and optimism ahead of the Trump-Xi summit are driving short-term sentiment, core geopolitical conflicts and technical hurdles remain unresolved. Prudent investors will want to see if corporate earnings can sustain the rally if Middle East frictions escalate further.\n\nHow the Previous Bet Played Out\n\nThe Sept. 21 Polymarket contract resolved “Up” after the S&P; 500 opened higher on Monday. The contract recorded $60,240 in total trading volume.\n\nOn Monday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed higher. SPY rose 1.55% to $773.50, while QQQ rose 2.88% to $741.47. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), ended 0.76% higher at $519.78.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMeta Platforms, Greenland Mines, Intel, AMD and GameStop: Why These 5 Stocks Are on Investors'' Radars Today\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'8aad779ec503e48ee5ae7e6c568e6e79719ddeb9','2026-09-22 05:55:14','2026-09-22 06:31:54.863815',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 05:55:14');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(535,'alpaca:61912006','benzinga','2026-09-22 05:53:16','Nvidia, Apple Drive Demand for Coinbase-Issued Tokenized Stocks— Brian Armstrong Notes ''Good Traction So Far''','Coinbase Global Inc. CEO Brian Armstrong highlighted on Monday, September 21, growing traction for the tokenized U.S. stocks issued by the company.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61912006/nvidia-apple-drive-demand-coinbase-tokenized-stocks-armstrong','["AAPL", "BTC/USD", "NVDA", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 06:32:00.173066','product','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Growing demand for tokenized stocks indicates a positive reception in the market.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "BTC/USD": 76528.6, "NVDA": 219.37, "TSLA": 366.04}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 12.921}}','2026-09-23 06:36:43.730880','2026-09-22 06:31:54.874377','61912006',replace('Coinbase Global Inc. (NASDAQ:COIN) CEO Brian Armstrong highlighted on Monday growing traction for its tokenized U.S. stocks,\n\nCoinbase-Backed Tokens Off to a Good Start\n\n“Very early days, but good traction so far,” said Armstrong, as holders of Coinbase-issued stocks on the Base blockchain jumped 9,697% in a month.\n\nOn-chain analytics firm Token Terminal put total asset holders at 46,700, with tokenized versions of NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA), Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) and Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) leading the chart.\n\nVery early days, but good traction so far. https://t.co/az07gns3Mg— Brian Armstrong (@brian_armstrong) September 21, 2026 \n\nWhat’s the Fuss About?\n\nCoinbase launched its tokenized stocks last month for eligible users outside the U.S. Each digital token represents a real, 1:1-backed direct claim on an underlying traditional stock, held by a regulated custodian. The tokens also carry dividend and voting rights.\n\nOne of the key differentiators is that, unlike a traditional stock, Coinbase-issued stocks can be used as collateral for on-chain loans on platforms like Aave (CRYPTO: AAVE).\n\nRead Also:\n\nQUICK SPARK: Want Nvidia on Crypto Rails? ‘Tokenized Stock Is the Honest Way’\n\nUS to Welcome Tokenized Stocks?\n\nArmstrong said Coinbase’s tokenization ambitions stretch far beyond publicly traded stocks, pointing to private companies, Treasuries and investment funds as potential candidates.\n\nThe total value of the tokenized stock market was at $3.4 billion, with over 4 million asset holders and $70 billion in monthly volume, according to Token Terminal.\n\nLast week, the SEC created a five-year temporary regulatory pathway for trading certain tokenized U.S. stocks on blockchain-based venues, granting conditional exemptions from exchange and dealer-registration rules.\n\nPrice Action: Coinbase shares rose 0.47% in after-hours trading, according to Benzinga Pro. The stock closed 3.5% higher at $201.05 during Monday’s regular trading session.\n\nAccording to Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings, COIN shows a stronger price trend in the short- and medium-term but lags over the long term.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nPhoto: Camilo Concha / Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'6ff349b44198b18905a22be4ad03602c27cb787a','2026-09-22 05:53:16','2026-09-22 06:31:54.863815',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 05:53:16');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(536,'alpaca:61912697','benzinga','2026-09-22 08:04:24','Alibaba Just Supercharged its AI Ambitions: New Zhenwu V900 AI Chip Promises 3X Performance, Targets 20GW Data Center Expansion by 2032','Alibaba unveils its Zhenwu V900 AI chip and plans to expand global data center capacity to over 20GW by 2032.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61912697/alibaba-just-supercharged-its-ai-ambitions-new-zhenwu-v900-ai-chip-promises-3x-performance-targets-20gw-data-center-expansion-by-2032','["META", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 08:32:11.342382','product','bullish',3,3,'weeks',1,'Alibaba''s new AI chip and data center expansion are notable advancements.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}','2026-09-23 08:37:06.001005','2026-09-22 08:32:07.633821','61912697',replace('Alibaba Group Holding Ltd. (NYSE:BABA) unveiled its latest artificial intelligence (AI) chip and announced plans to significantly expand its data center capacity at Alibaba Cloud’s annual Apsara Conference.\n\nOn Tuesday, the tech giant introduced Zhenwu V900, its new AI chip. The chip is touted to deliver triple the performance of its predecessor, the Zhenwu M890, launched in May.\n\nThe new Zhenwu AI chip is slated to enter mass production and commercial release in the first quarter of 2027. Meanwhile, existing Zhenwu chips are already deployed by more than 650 customers across industries including automotive, finance, energy and manufacturing.\n\nAlibaba also revealed plans to increase Alibaba Cloud’s global data center capacity to over 20 gigawatts by 2032. CEO of Alibaba Group, Eddie Wu, likened today’s AI development to the early stages of electrification, stating, “AI coding is simply the light bulb of the machine intelligence era.”\n\nRead Also:\n\nGoldman Sachs Strategist Sees AI Boom Outpacing Bonds as Higher Rates Raise Market Risks: ''Long compute…Long Neoclouds…Long Data Centers''\n\nAlibaba Expands AI And Cloud Footprint\n\nEarlier this month, Alibaba Group announced the expansion of its enterprise AI tools with an upgraded QoderWake platform that creates AI-powered "digital employees" capable of working across DingTalk, ByteDance’s Feishu and Tencent’s WeCom. Alibaba said nearly 100,000 digital employees have been deployed since April, completing about 2 million tasks in the past three months.\n\nFurthermore, Alibaba Cloud is launching its first Latin American cloud region in São Paulo, Brazil. The new region includes two data centers offering computing, storage, networking, and AI-related cloud services. The move follows its Mexico cloud region, launched in February 2025, and is aimed at providing lower latency, stronger resilience, and local data governance for Brazilian businesses.\n\nTech Giants Ramp Up AI Infrastructure\n\nAlibaba’s move comes amid a global trend of tech giants expanding their AI infrastructure. Earlier this month, Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) announced a collaboration with Australian partners to expand land, power, and shell capacity to host NVIDIA DSX AI factories, aiming for a 2-gigawatt buildout by 2027.\n\nIn July, Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) announced that it is investing more than C$13 billion ($9.27 billion) in a 1-gigawatt AI data center in Alberta, its first in Canada. The project is expected to support 3,000 construction jobs and 300 operational jobs, while Meta will spend another C$60 million ($42.77 million) on local infrastructure. The facility will run on 100% renewable energy and use water-efficient cooling technology.\n\nShares of Alibaba closed 2.19% higher at $115.75 on Monday, while the stock rose about 1.12% after-hours. \n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBig Tech Looks To Argentina As US Data Center Projects Face Resistance\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'a3a85a56432ed353920fcd698c7354ce0a8daf4e','2026-09-22 08:04:24','2026-09-22 08:32:07.622322',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 08:04:24');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(537,'alpaca:61912571','benzinga','2026-09-22 07:36:44','Vitalik Buterin Welcomes Prediction Market Contender to Ethereum Base Chain, Says It Does ''Interesting and Meaningful'' Things Ethically','Ethereum co-founder Vitalik Buterin endorsed Trueo, a new cryptocurrency-based prediction market, describing it as ethical and free of “corposlop.”','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61912571/vitalik-buterin-ethereum-prediction-market-ethical-ethereum-base-chain','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 08:32:13.194142','listing','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Vitalik Buterin''s endorsement of Trueo adds credibility to the new prediction market on Ethereum.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{"BTC/USD": {"60m": 12.921}, "ETH/USD": {"60m": 12.182}}','2026-09-23 07:36:55.110727','2026-09-22 08:32:07.636683','61912571',replace('Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) co-founder Vitalik Buterin endorsed Trueo as a strong prediction market contender on Monday, calling it ethical and free of "corposlop."\n\nBitarin Welcomes Trueo on Layer 1\n\nIn an X post, Buterin said he was “glad to see” Trueo migrating from Base—where it initially launched in March 2025—to the Ethereum L1 chain.\n\nHe highlighted Trueo’s commitment to “decentralization,” positioning it as an alternative to corporate-influenced platforms in the growing prediction market sector.\n\nButerin previously defined “corposlop” as prioritizing profits over consumers’ well-being.\n\nButering added that the platform was trying to do “interesting and meaningful things” with its economic primitive.\n\nGlad to see that Ethereum L1 will have a new strong prediction market contender that is dedicated to decentralization, and being ethical and not corposlop, and to actually trying to do interesting and meaningful things with this class of economic primitive.…— vitalik.eth (@VitalikButerin) September 21, 2026 \n\nMore Impartial and Credible?\n\nTrueo aims to deliver a more “impartial and credible” resolution than what market leaders such as Polymarket and Kalshi offer.\n\n“Due process in dispute resolution is severely lacking despite the growth of prediction markets over the past five years,” Trueo said.\n\nSome outcomes have been the subject of disagreement. Kalshi was sued earlier this year for refusing to pay millions of dollars to bettors who predicted Iran’s supreme leader would leave office before a March deadline.\n\nTrueo also issues the True Yield Dollar (TYD) stablecoin, which rewards users for holding or maintaining positions in prediction markets. TYD is fully backed by and redeemable for USDC (CRYPTO: USDC).\n\nRead Also:\n\nStock Market: Will S&P; 500 Open Up or Down Today?\n\nButerin Backs Prediction Markets\n\nButerin was among the notable backers of Polygon (CRYPTO: POL)-based Polymarket’s $70 million funding round in 2024.\n\nBroadly, he supports prediction markets, arguing that wrong bets could lead to financial losses, which, over time, make the system more "truth-seeking" and better at reflecting "genuine" probabilities.\n\nOn the flip side, he said these platforms could theoretically give people a reason to cause harm because they’d be able to profit from bad outcomes.\n\nKalshi and Polymarket together account for nearly 94% of the monthly notional volume on prediction market platforms, according to Dune Analytics.\n\nPrice Action: As of this writing, ETH is up 2.67% in the last 24 hours to $2,739, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nPolymarket CEO Reportedly Put Growth Over Fraud Concerns as Kalshi Fights ''Fake Crypto Volume'' Claims\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Alexey Smyshlyaev on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'d862b3f5c501c1a96a1b7ba86c6580ebb781b498','2026-09-22 07:36:44','2026-09-22 08:32:07.622322',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 07:36:44');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(538,'alpaca:61912560','benzinga','2026-09-22 07:36:17','S&P 500 Nears Record High But Breadth Flashes Rare 1929, 1999 Signal — Analyst Says ‘We’ve Never in Almost 100 Years Seen Breadth This Bad’','The S&amp;P 500 nears record highs, but Jason Goepfert warns of a rare technical anomaly last seen before the 1929 and 1999 market crashes.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/market-summary/26/09/61912560/sp-500-nears-record-high-but-breadth-flashes-rare-1929-1999-signal-analyst-says-weve-never-in-almost-100-years-seen-breadth-this-bad','["QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-22 08:32:14.209993','analyst','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst highlights a concerning technical signal related to market breadth.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{}','2026-09-23 07:36:55.110727','2026-09-22 08:32:07.639155','61912560',replace('The S&P; 500 index advanced to within 1% of its record high on Monday while its constituents simultaneously registered more 52-week lows than highs, triggering a market signal observed only twice in the past century.\n\nHistorical Market Breadth Signal\n\nOn Monday, the S&P; 500 rose 1.49% to close at 7,764.70. This places the index 0.67% below its 52-week high of 7,816.70. Despite the top-level index gains, internal market participation deteriorated.\n\nAccording to Jason Goepfert, founder of SentimenTrader, there are only two dates in history when the S&P; 500 rallied at least 1% to within 1% of a new high while more of its component stocks fell to new lows than highs: July 23, 1929, and Dec. 21, 1999.\n\n“We’ve never in almost 100 years seen breadth this bad,” Goepfert posted on social media platform X. “The S&P; $SPY is knocking on new highs but there are (many) more stocks at lows than highs.”\n\nLook, I know…perma-bear blah blah blah.But this is crazy stuff.There are 2 days in history like today, when the S&P; 500 $SPY rallied at least 1% to within 1% of a new high, and more of its stocks fell to new lows than highs.• Jul 23, 1929• Dec 21, 1999 https://t.co/yBvtgtPJh9 pic.twitter.com/vMcZ9FasMJ— Jason Goepfert (@jasongoepfert) September 21, 2026 \n\nGoepfert noted that the percentage of stocks in long-term uptrends is plunging. Factoring in historical market contexts, he stated that “out of 83 dates with similar or better participation, the S&P; rallied over the next year only 16% of the time.” Consequently, his firm’s price projection is now negative for the first time since they began publishing the data six months ago.\n\nEven broadening the parameters so we can get more signals doesn''t improve the outlook much.Out of 83 dates with similar or better participation, the S&P; rallied over the next year only 16% of the time. pic.twitter.com/gUolrA6cdK— Jason Goepfert (@jasongoepfert) September 20, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nDiesel Hits Record $6.51 a Gallon as Fuel Crisis Deepens: Commodity Strategist Warns ‘No Handshake Can Refill’ the Market\n\nUnder the Surface of the Rally\n\nDuring Monday’s session, 30 stocks within the S&P; 500 hit new 52-week lows, while only seven reached fresh highs. Art Hogan, chief market strategist at B. Riley Wealth, told CNBC that the divergence was a result of current sector leadership.\n\n"The leadership’s battling against weaker performance in the near term, and what’s selling off has been selling off, so the creation of new lows has an easier glide path than the creation of new highs with today’s leadership," Hogan said.\n\nHogan indicated that the market could experience similar sporadic trading days moving forward. He sees no new highs in this market if the war persists, energy prices remain stubbornly high, and if the Fed continues to hike rates.\n\nHow Has the Index Performed?\n\nThe S&P; 500 index has advanced 13.43% year-to-date. Similarly, the Nasdaq Composite index was up 16.69%, and the Dow Jones gained 8.29% YTD.\n\nOn Monday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed higher. SPY rose 1.55% to $773.50, while QQQ rose 2.88% to $741.47. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), ended 0.76% higher at $519.78.\n\nIn premarket on Tuesday, SPY was up 0.62%, QQQ advanced 0.94%, and DIA gained 0.61%.\n\nRead Also:\n\nS&P; 500 Could Deliver Another 6% by Year-End as JPMorgan Calls Bears an ‘Extinct Species’ — Polymarket Bettors Price 35% Odds\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'f6b489196123b0ca66ddb48eb4ed709431bced9e','2026-09-22 07:36:17','2026-09-22 08:32:07.622322',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 07:36:17');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(539,'alpaca:61913229','benzinga','2026-09-22 09:29:33','Nasdaq Surges To Record Amid Easing Oil And Yields: Investor Sentiment Improves, But Fear & Greed Index Remains In ‘Fear’ Zone','Stocks surged Monday, led by Nasdaq’s 2.26% gain and tech shares, while CNN’s Fear &amp; Greed Index improved to 34 but stayed in “Fear.”','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/market-summary/26/09/61913229/nasdaq-surges-to-record-amid-easing-oil-and-yields-investor-sentiment-improves-but-fear-greed-index-remains-in-fear-zone','["AMD", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 09:32:23.325829','macro','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Major index surge indicates improved investor sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 09:32:18.634131','61913229',replace('The CNN Money Fear and Greed index showed some improvement in the overall market sentiment, while the index remained in the “Fear” zone on Monday.\n\nU.S. stocks settled higher on Monday, with the Nasdaq Composite gaining around 600 points, closing at a record high, with a fourth consecutive slide in crude oil relieving pressure on Treasury yields.\n\nMajor stock indices recorded a mixed week, with the Dow falling 1.7% and the S&P; 500 losing about 0.1%. However, the tech-heavy Nasdaq recorded a weekly gain of 0.7%.\n\nShares of Intel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) jumped 12%, while Advanced Micro Devices (NASDAQ:AMD) added around 10% on Monday. Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) surged 11% on positive early responses to its Muse AI agent.\n\nOn the economic data front, the Chicago Fed National Activity Index fell to -0.04 in August versus a revised reading of +0.08 in the previous month.\n\nMost sectors on the S&P; 500 closed on a positive note, with communication services, information technology and consumer discretionary stocks recording the biggest gains on Monday. However, energy and utilities stocks bucked the overall market trend, closing the session lower.\n\nThe Dow Jones closed higher by around 366 points to 52,048.83 on Monday. The S&P; 500 gained 1.49% to 7,764.70, while the Nasdaq Composite surged 2.26% at 27,122.09 during Monday’s session.\n\nInvestors are awaiting earnings results from AutoZone Inc (NYSE:AZO), Thor Industries Inc (NYSE:THO) and KB Home (NYSE:KBH) today.\n\nAt a current reading of 34, the index remained in the “Fear” zone on Monday, versus a prior reading of 30.\n\nWhat is CNN Business Fear & Greed Index?\n\nThe Fear & Greed Index is a measure of the current market sentiment. It is based on the premise that higher fear exerts pressure on stock prices, while higher greed has the opposite effect. The index is calculated based on seven equal-weighted indicators. The index ranges from 0 to 100, where 0 represents maximum fear and 100 signals maximum greediness.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'3eb09a81724c534ab683657664d2420cd7957e3f','2026-09-22 09:29:33','2026-09-22 09:32:18.617468',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 09:29:33');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(540,'alpaca:61912876','benzinga','2026-09-22 08:43:30','Elon Musk Says Tesla Has Offered FSD to Legacy Automakers, but ‘None’ Have Accepted So Far','Elon Musk reitartes that Tesla has offered Full Self-Driving system as licenses to legacy automakers, but none accepted.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61912876/elon-musk-says-tesla-has-offered-fsd-to-legacy-automakers-but-none-have-accepted-so-far','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 09:32:24.415126','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Tesla''s licensing offer is noted but no acceptance reported.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 09:32:18.655991','61912876',replace('Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) CEO Elon Musk has reaffirmed that the automaker has offered the Full Self-Driving (FSD) system to legacy manufacturers via licensing deals.\n\nFSD Licenses?\n\nIn a post on X on Monday, Boom Supersonic CEO and founder Blake Scholl predicted that the Tesla FSD will be “an in-house advantage for a couple years,” but will be offered to manufacturers via licensing deals when competitors start ramping up autonomous efforts.\n\nScholl compared the move to Tesla’s Supercharger network, which was initially only available to the automaker’s EVs, but was eventually opened up to other manufacturers as well.\n\nInfluencer Sawyer Merritt quoted Scholl’s post, saying that Tesla and Musk had “for years openly invited other automakers to license FSD,” but said that “none” of the manufacturers have accepted the invitation.\n\nTesla has for years openly invited other automakers to license FSD. None of them have accepted. https://t.co/kgz4idpoUM— Sawyer Merritt (@SawyerMerritt) September 22, 2026 \n\nMusk responded to Merritt’s post on X, backing the Tesla investor’s claim. “Exactly,” the billionaire said in his response. Back in November last year, the CEO had made similar claims, saying that the FSD system had been offered to legacy automakers, but they show little interest.\n\nMusk then said that when the legacy automakers do reach out, they “tepidly” hold discussions about “implementing FSD for a tiny program in 5 years.”\n\nExactly— Elon Musk (@elonmusk) September 22, 2026 \n\nTesla’s Vision-Only Approach\n\nNotably, Tesla’s FSD system has been criticized for its vision-only approach to autonomous driving as opposed to a camera+LiDAR-based approach that has become a mainstay in several autonomous driving suites today.\n\nTesla’s self-driving technology features various speed modes, including a “Mad Max” setting, but it does not offer full autonomy and requires drivers to be attentive at all times and ready to take over driving duties\n\nThe automaker’s AI chief Ashok Elluswamy recently said that Tesla will be betting on relying on a “smarter FSD system” rather than on company-imposed ceilings, echoing Musk’s comments made in July about the FSD system becoming capable of being tailored to individual driver preferences.\n\nPrice Action: TSLA shares rose 0.15% to $375.79 during pre-market trading on Tuesday.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla Audits Chinese Suppliers as Elon Musk’s Optimus Robot Moves Closer to Mass Production: Report\n\nCheck out more of Benzinga’s Future Of Mobility coverage by following this link.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'ca36661777ddbdd52d4cc6c777c330081d8932c2','2026-09-22 08:43:30','2026-09-22 09:32:18.617468',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 08:43:30');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(541,'alpaca:61914217','benzinga','2026-09-22 10:31:15','Economist Justin Wolfers Warns AI Could Leave Workers Earning ‘Two Pennies an Hour’ While OpenAI Gets ‘Infinitely Rich’','&#34;Economist Justin Wolfers warned AI could leave workers earning &#39;two pennies an hour&#39; while some companies grow &#39;infinitely rich.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/economic-data/26/09/61914217/justin-wolfers-warns-ai-could-leave-us-in-lives-of-grinding-misery-while-openai-gets-infinitely-rich','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-22 10:32:32.489132','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'Commentary on potential future economic impacts of AI.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 498.48}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.009094','61914217',replace('Economist Justin Wolfers warned that artificial intelligence could eventually eliminate most jobs, leaving workers competing for wages “two pennies an hour above subsistence” while a AI developers like OpenAI grow “infinitely rich” off the technology.\n\n‘They Forgot to Ask’\n\nWolfers, in his podcast ‘The Professor Is In,’ released Monday, said AI has given new urgency to the case for universal basic income, calling it a payment society is owed rather than a form of redistribution.\n\nHe noted that companies like OpenAI, Anthropic, Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOG) (NASDAQ:GOOGL), and Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT) “created a few lines of code,” while it was the rest of society that “created all the world’s knowledge” those AI models were trained on, “and we never charged them for it.”\n\n“They forgot to ask,” he said, adding that “we live lives of grinding misery while OpenAI gets infinitely rich as the only productive force in the economy.”\n\nRead Also:\n\nSenator Rand Paul Sounds Alarm on Trump’s $5,000 Checks: ‘Piling on More Debt’ Won’t Fix Affordability Crisis\n\nSome Workers Could Come Out Ahead\n\nEarlier this month, Morgan Stanley economist Heather Berger said that the workers most exposed to AI disruption could also capture some of its biggest gains.\n\nHigh-income, college-educated, city-dwelling workers stand to benefit from AI-driven productivity gains, new job creation, and long-term disinflation, even as younger workers face greater risk of AI replacing entry-level tasks.\n\nPalantir CEO Alex Karp warned in July that AI could become America’s “biggest driver of wealth inequality,” with AI industry leaders potentially becoming “10 to 100 times wealthier” while ordinary workers see far smaller gains than in past technological revolutions.\n\nA Widening Pay Gap\n\nAdvertised pay in the most AI-exposed occupations has surged 46% since the start of 2021, compared with 41% growth in moderately AI-exposed jobs, 39% across all U.S. postings, and just 25% in the least AI-exposed roles, according to The Kobeissi Letter, citing Indeed data.\n\n The gap between these categories began widening materially in mid-2025 and has continued growing throughout the year.\n\nAI-exposed jobs are seeing the largest pay growth in the US:Advertised pay in the most AI-exposed occupations has surged +46% since the start of 2021.At the same time, moderately AI-exposed jobs have seen +41% growth.This compares to a +39% increase in all US posted wages… pic.twitter.com/gdr6qveJFk— The Kobeissi Letter (@KobeissiLetter) September 21, 2026 \n\nIn August, the U.S. economy added 162,000 jobs, sharply beating estimates of 56,000, while unemployment held steady at 4.1% and average hourly earnings rose 3.1% year-over-year.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Says US Negotiating ‘Massive’ Belarus Potash Deal Amid Trade Tussle With Canada, Putin Ally Cites Shortage: ‘We Simply Do Not Have…’\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'5610785058289f7466a256df4c7386cd907bb199','2026-09-22 10:31:15','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 10:31:15');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(542,'alpaca:61914047','benzinga','2026-09-22 10:16:28','Amazon Blocks Meta’s Muse AI From Shopping — Elon Musk Says AMZN ‘Won’t Be Able to Tell’ Humans From Agents','Amazon blocks Meta’s Muse AI shopping agent, escalating a dispute over automated access as both companies expand AI-powered commerce.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61914047/amazon-blocks-metas-muse-ai-from-shopping-elon-musk-says-amzn-wont-be-able-to-tell-humans-from-agents','["AMZN", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 10:32:34.509962','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The event reflects ongoing competition in the AI-commerce space without immediate financial implications.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.015031','61914047',replace('Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) has blocked Meta Platforms Inc.’s (NASDAQ:META) Muse AI agent from shopping on Amazon.com, escalating a dispute over how third-party agents access online stores. Amazon’s 2026 agent rules require automated systems to identify themselves and stop accessing its services when requested.\n\nMusk Questions Amazon’s Ability To Detect Agents\n\nElon Musk questioned whether those restrictions will remain enforceable as agents become tied to users’ browsing sessions. "Amazon won’t be able to tell whether the buyer is a human or an AI acting on their behalf if access is via the user’s IP address & cookies," Musk wrote Monday on social media platform X.\n\nAmazon won’t be able to tell whether the buyer is a human or an AI acting on their behalf if access is via the user’s IP address & cookies— Elon Musk (@elonmusk) September 21, 2026 \n\nMuse, launched on Sept. 8, can browse the web, fill forms and make purchases after receiving user approval. Meta says each Muse runs inside a dedicated Secure VM, while passwords and payment methods remain hidden from the agent in protected credential storage. Meta delayed Muse for months while addressing safety concerns before release.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMeta''s Muse Hits No. 1, Carrying AMD Into the $1-Trillion Club\n\nAmazon Tightens Rules As Agent Competition Grows\n\nThe clash comes as Amazon builds its agentic shopping ecosystem. The company combined Rufus and Alexa+ this year into Alexa for Shopping, which can compare products, track prices, build carts and automate purchases. Amazon said in July that active users were nearly double, while interactions rose more than fivefold year over year.\n\nAmazon has fought similar battles before. It sued Perplexity AI over its Comet shopping agent, alleging the tool accessed customer accounts without authorization while disguising automated browsing as human activity. A federal judge temporarily blocked Perplexity’s agent in March, though the company appealed.\n\nMeta Expands Muse Across Online Commerce\n\nMeta, meanwhile, is pushing Muse deeper into commerce. Its launch materials say the agent can check out through Stripe’s Link, with Shop Pay support planned. Shopify now lists Meta as an AI sales channel, and a partnership will let Muse users shop across Shopify stores and complete purchases through Shop Pay.\n\nRead Also:\n\nElon Musk Says Tesla Has Offered FSD to Legacy Automakers, but ‘None’ Have Accepted So Far\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'08cd1620eb7f148ea8e8283e4167937b0855ea0f','2026-09-22 10:16:28','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 10:16:28');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(543,'alpaca:61913604','benzinga','2026-09-22 10:01:08','Fidelity’s Jurrien Timmer Says Bitcoin’s New 4-Year Bull Market May Be Underway as BTC Hits Highest Level Since January','Bitcoin pushed above $87,000 on Monday, September 21, after Jurrien Timmer, Director of global macro at Fidelity Investments, noted that the cryptocurrency’s bull market is underway.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61913604/fidelitys-jurien-timmer-says-bitcoins-new-bull-market-is-underway-as-apex-crypto-rises-to-highest-level-since-january','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 10:32:35.762956','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'A prominent expert suggests a new bull market for Bitcoin.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.020902','61913604',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) pushed above $87,000 on Monday after Jurrien Timmer, Director of global macro at Fidelity Investments, noted that the cryptocurrency’s bull market may be underway.\n\nIs the Bear Market Over?\n\nIn an X post on Saturday, Timmer stated Bitcoin broke out after holding $60,000 support for nearly a year.\n\n“That’s how long a typical Bitcoin winter lasts, so I’m sensing that a new 4-year cycle bull market is underway,” he added. Since the remark, BTC has spiked 5.70%.\n\nTimmer also posted Bitcoin’s Power law chart that maps the asset’s long-term value over time.\n\nThe pink bars on the chart show the 52-week Z-score of the BTC/gold price ratio, which measures how many standard deviations the current ratio deviates from its historical mean. \n\nAfter remaining negative for an extended period, the Z-score has turned positive, a signal that Timmer noted has historically marked market bottoms\n\nFinally, Bitcoin has been on the move after holding the $60k support zone for almost a year. That’s how long a typical Bitcoin winter lasts, so I’m sensing that a new 4-year cycle bull market is underway. Note that the Z-score of BTC/gold has turned positive after being -100%. In… pic.twitter.com/puzGPamPmg— Jurrien Timmer (@TimmerFidelity) September 18, 2026 \n\nBitcoin Tops $87,000\n\nBitcoin reached an intraday high of $87,363 on Monday, its highest since late January, as the SEC’s push to build a regulatory framework for cryptocurrency, including tokenized U.S. stocks, outweighed the CLARITY Act’s failure.\n\nThe Crypto Fear & Greed Index is flashing "Extreme Greed," even as almost $400 million worth of Bitcoin positions, mostly shorts, were liquidated in the last 24 hours.\n\nRead Also:\n\nNvidia, Apple Drive Demand for Coinbase-Issued Tokenized Stocks— Brian Armstrong Notes ''Good Traction So Far''\n\nWill the Rally Sustain?\n\nCoinbase Global Inc. (NASDAQ:COIN) CEO Brian Armstrong said the world’s largest cryptocurrency could reach $300,000 to $400,000 by 2030.\n\nBitcoin’s bullish commentary on social media also surged to its highest level since 2024, according to on-chain analytics firm Santiment. However, the firm warned that the cryptocurrency market typically moves against the crowd’s expectations\n\nPrice Action: As of this writing, BTC is up 2.81% in the last 24 hours to $85,862.94, according to Benzinga Pro. \n\nRead Also:\n\nAnthony Pompiano Reiterates Bitcoin Has ''No Top'' Because the Dollar Has ''No Bottom,'' Bets BTC Will Go ''Way Higher''\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'18c15edeaec603d2cbbf11810ef9bed6417e6a1d','2026-09-22 10:01:08','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 10:01:08');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(544,'alpaca:61913457','benzinga','2026-09-22 09:58:39','In-Depth Analysis: Amazon.com Versus Competitors In Broadline Retail Industry','Amidst today&#39;s fast-paced and highly competitive business environment, it is crucial for investors and industry enthusiasts to conduct comprehensive company evaluations. In this article, we will delve into an','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61913457/depth-analysis-amazon-com-versus-competitors-broadline-retail-industry','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-22 10:32:36.676185','other','neutral',1,2,'days',1,'The headline presents an analysis without impacting asset prices.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.026248','61913457',replace('Amidst today''s fast-paced and highly competitive business environment, it is crucial for investors and industry enthusiasts to conduct comprehensive company evaluations. In this article, we will delve into an extensive industry comparison, evaluating Amazon.com (NASDAQ:AMZN) in comparison to its major competitors within the Broadline Retail industry. By analyzing critical financial metrics, market position, and growth potential, our objective is to provide valuable insights for investors and offer a deeper understanding of company''s performance in the industry.\nAmazon.com Background\nAmazon is the leading online retailer and marketplace for third party sellers. Retail related revenue represents approximately 74% of total, followed by Amazon Web Services (17%), and advertising services (9%). International segments constitute 22% of Amazon''s total revenue, led by Germany, the United Kingdom, and Japan.\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nAmazon.com Inc\n20.79\n5.05\n3.62\n12.61%\n$102.16\n$104.83\n19.62%\n\nMercadoLibre Inc\n49.52\n11.78\n2.62\n6.17%\n$0.96\n$4.16\n49.76%\n\neBay Inc\n22.75\n10.33\n4.15\n12.12%\n$0.83\n$2.3\n14.8%\n\nDillard''s Inc\n14.65\n4.71\n1.51\n4.71%\n$0.17\n$0.62\n-0.36%\n\nGlobal E Online Ltd\n45.10\n7.38\n6.40\n5.26%\n$0.05\n$0.13\n39.15%\n\nMacy''s Inc\n8.13\n1.18\n0.27\n3.46%\n$0.46\n$2.21\n1.2%\n\nOllie''s Bargain Outlet Holdings Inc\n17.84\n2.50\n1.75\n4.51%\n$0.13\n$0.32\n9.09%\n\nKohl''s Corp\n7.48\n0.47\n0.13\n3.69%\n$0.43\n$1.62\n-0.87%\n\nSavers Value Village Inc\n61.47\n3.18\n0.85\n4.95%\n$0.07\n$0.25\n7.43%\n\nHour Loop Inc\n43.50\n6.89\n0.40\n12.6%\n$0.0\n$0.02\n25.24%\n\nAverage\n30.05\n5.38\n2.01\n6.39%\n$0.34\n$1.29\n16.16%\n\nWhen closely examining Amazon.com, the following trends emerge: \n\nA Price to Earnings ratio of 20.79 significantly below the industry average by 0.69x suggests undervaluation. This can make the stock appealing for those seeking growth.\n\nThe current Price to Book ratio of 5.05, which is 0.94x the industry average, is substantially lower than the industry average, indicating potential undervaluation.\n\nWith a relatively high Price to Sales ratio of 3.62, which is 1.8x the industry average, the stock might be considered overvalued based on sales performance.\n\nThe company has a higher Return on Equity (ROE) of 12.61%, which is 6.22% above the industry average. This suggests efficient use of equity to generate profits and demonstrates profitability and growth potential.\n\nWith higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $102.16 Billion, which is 300.47x above the industry average, the company demonstrates stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nThe gross profit of $104.83 Billion is 81.26x above that of its industry, highlighting stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nWith a revenue growth of 19.62%, which surpasses the industry average of 16.16%, the company is demonstrating robust sales expansion and gaining market share.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio helps evaluate the capital structure and financial leverage of a company.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nWhen assessing Amazon.com against its top 4 peers using the Debt-to-Equity ratio, the following comparisons can be made:\n\nAmazon.com is in a relatively stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers, as evidenced by its lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.4.\n\nThis implies that the company relies less on debt financing and has a more favorable balance between debt and equity.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor Amazon.com in the Broadline Retail industry, the PE and PB ratios are low compared to peers, indicating potential undervaluation. However, the high PS ratio suggests a premium valuation based on revenue. In terms of profitability, Amazon.com shows high ROE, EBITDA, and gross profit, outperforming industry peers. Additionally, the high revenue growth rate further highlights Amazon.com''s strong performance in the Broadline Retail sector.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'fd5fa2be7fff3ae4bb64ad856e498b74ffd40a71','2026-09-22 09:58:39','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 09:58:39');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(545,'alpaca:61913456','benzinga','2026-09-22 09:58:34','Exploring The Competitive Space: Microsoft Versus Industry Peers In Software','In the fast-paced and highly competitive business world of today, conducting thorough company analysis is essential for investors and industry observers. In this article, we will conduct an extensive industry','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61913456/exploring-competitive-space-microsoft-versus-industry-peers-software','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-22 10:32:37.693747','other','neutral',2,1,'days',1,'The headline discusses market competition without providing definitive news.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 498.48}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.028687','61913456',replace('In the fast-paced and highly competitive business world of today, conducting thorough company analysis is essential for investors and industry observers. In this article, we will conduct an extensive industry comparison, evaluating Microsoft (NASDAQ:MSFT) in relation to its major competitors in the Software industry. Through a detailed examination of key financial metrics, market standing, and growth prospects, our objective is to provide valuable insights and illuminate company''s performance in the industry.\nMicrosoft Background\nMicrosoft develops and licenses consumer and enterprise software. It is known for its Windows operating systems and Office productivity suite. The company is organized into three equally sized broad segments: productivity and business processes (legacy Microsoft Office, cloud-based Office 365, Exchange, SharePoint, Skype, LinkedIn, Dynamics), intelligence cloud (infrastructure- and platform-as-a-service offerings Azure, Windows Server OS, SQL Server), and more personal computing (Windows Client, Xbox, Bing search, display advertising, and Surface laptops, tablets, and desktops).\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nMicrosoft Corp\n27.94\n8.42\n11.27\n8.35%\n$55.91\n$60.48\n17.75%\n\nOracle Corp\n23.29\n7.27\n6.08\n9.42%\n$10.39\n$11.61\n29.61%\n\nPalo Alto Networks Inc\n929.40\n11.06\n24.74\n-1.02%\n$0.07\n$2.3\n34.46%\n\nCrowdStrike Holdings Inc\n6649.33\n50.05\n47.27\n0.11%\n$0.11\n$1.1\n25.83%\n\nServiceNow Inc\n86.05\n11.37\n9.74\n2.46%\n$0.91\n$2.82\n24.01%\n\nFortinet Inc\n61.92\n82.89\n17.41\n47.73%\n$0.76\n$1.64\n25.64%\n\nGen Digital Inc\n17.05\n6.57\n3.52\n8.16%\n$0.57\n$1.03\n6.28%\n\nCheck Point Software Technologies Ltd\n13.77\n5.01\n5.19\n6.98%\n$0.2\n$0.57\n1.26%\n\nUiPath Inc\n20.28\n3.63\n4.24\n1.87%\n$0.04\n$0.33\n13.42%\n\nQualys Inc\n31.43\n11.14\n9.22\n9.26%\n$0.06\n$0.15\n11.04%\n\nCommVault Systems Inc\n93.41\n116.03\n5.25\n71.0%\n$0.04\n$0.26\n11.4%\n\nDolby Laboratories Inc\n24.40\n2.08\n4.07\n1.1%\n$0.06\n$0.26\n-3.34%\n\nBlackBerry Ltd\n85.30\n6.66\n8.76\n1.14%\n$0.02\n$0.12\n25.64%\n\nTenable Holdings Inc\n603.75\n20.11\n4.09\n1.7%\n$0.02\n$0.21\n8.58%\n\nMonday.Com Ltd\n37.27\n6.02\n3.21\n0.5%\n$0.02\n$0.32\n21.94%\n\nTeradata Corp\n6.18\n4.60\n1.67\n8.0%\n$0.08\n$0.24\n0.49%\n\nAverage\n578.86\n22.97\n10.3\n11.23%\n$0.89\n$1.53\n15.75%\n\nThrough a thorough examination of Microsoft, we can discern the following trends: \n\nThe Price to Earnings ratio of 27.94 is 0.05x lower than the industry average, indicating potential undervaluation for the stock.\n\nConsidering a Price to Book ratio of 8.42, which is well below the industry average by 0.37x, the stock may be undervalued based on its book value compared to its peers.\n\nThe Price to Sales ratio of 11.27, which is 1.09x the industry average, suggests the stock could potentially be overvalued in relation to its sales performance compared to its peers.\n\nThe Return on Equity (ROE) of 8.35% is 2.88% below the industry average, suggesting potential inefficiency in utilizing equity to generate profits.\n\nWith higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $55.91 Billion, which is 62.82x above the industry average, the company demonstrates stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nCompared to its industry, the company has higher gross profit of $60.48 Billion, which indicates 39.53x above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nWith a revenue growth of 17.75%, which surpasses the industry average of 15.75%, the company is demonstrating robust sales expansion and gaining market share.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio helps evaluate the capital structure and financial leverage of a company.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nWhen comparing Microsoft with its top 4 peers based on the Debt-to-Equity ratio, the following insights can be observed:\n\nMicrosoft exhibits a stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers in the sector, as indicated by its lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.13.\n\nThis suggests that the company has a more favorable balance between debt and equity, which can be seen as a positive aspect for investors.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor Microsoft in the Software industry, the PE and PB ratios suggest the stock is undervalued compared to peers, indicating potential for growth. However, the high PS ratio implies the stock may be overvalued based on revenue. In terms of ROE, Microsoft''s performance is lower than industry peers, while its high EBITDA and gross profit indicate strong financial health. The high revenue growth further highlights Microsoft''s competitive position in the industry.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'99d2839bf8e04e65d9609c45c91c7c235094116a','2026-09-22 09:58:34','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 09:58:34');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(546,'alpaca:61913455','benzinga','2026-09-22 09:58:31','Performance Comparison: Apple And Competitors In Technology Hardware, Storage &amp; Peripherals Industry','In today&#39;s rapidly changing and fiercely competitive business landscape, it is vital for investors and industry enthusiasts to carefully evaluate companies. In this article, we will perform a comprehensive industry','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61913455/performance-comparison-apple-and-competitors-technology-hardware-storage-amp-peripherals-industry','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-22 10:32:38.569577','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The article compares performance but does not report on specific changes or impacts.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.031159','61913455',replace('In today''s rapidly changing and fiercely competitive business landscape, it is vital for investors and industry enthusiasts to carefully evaluate companies. In this article, we will perform a comprehensive industry comparison, evaluating Apple (NASDAQ:AAPL) against its key competitors in the Technology Hardware, Storage & Peripherals industry. By analyzing important financial metrics, market position, and growth prospects, we aim to provide valuable insights for investors and shed light on company''s performance within the industry.\nApple Background\nApple is among the largest companies in the world, with a broad portfolio of hardware and software products targeted at consumers and businesses. Apple''s iPhone accounts for the majority of the firm''s sales, and Apple''s other products, such as the Mac, iPad, and Watch, are designed around the iPhone as the focal point of an expansive software ecosystem. Apple has progressively worked to add new applications, such as streaming video, subscription bundles, and augmented reality. The firm designs its own software and semiconductors and works with subcontractors such as Foxconn and TSMC to build its products and chips. Slightly less than half of Apple''s sales come directly through its flagship stores, with the majority coming indirectly through partnerships and distribution.\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nApple Inc\n38.87\n46.01\n10.73\n27.84%\n$39.02\n$54.77\n16.36%\n\nSanDisk Corp\n23.95\n16.44\n13.52\n46.78%\n$7.89\n$7.58\n371.59%\n\nSeagate Technology Holdings PLC\n63.11\n92.06\n16.47\n79.34%\n$1.64\n$1.9\n48.49%\n\nWestern Digital Corp\n16.65\n18.23\n13.29\n34.3%\n$3.36\n$2.03\n43.84%\n\nHewlett Packard Enterprise Co\n31.83\n3.09\n2.09\n5.83%\n$2.33\n$4.9\n33.68%\n\nNetApp Inc\n27.99\n26.03\n5.37\n26.35%\n$0.55\n$1.42\n29.89%\n\nEverpure Inc\n155.70\n24.58\n9.25\n4.97%\n$0.11\n$0.81\n37.73%\n\nSuper Micro Computer Inc\n12.64\n2.64\n0.74\n12.83%\n$1.57\n$1.94\n93.16%\n\nLogitech International SA\n19.29\n6.40\n3.14\n10.33%\n$0.28\n$0.61\n6.93%\n\nDiebold Nixdorf Inc\n20.98\n2.22\n0.59\n1.56%\n$0.09\n$0.24\n1.7%\n\nCorsair Gaming Inc\n43.58\n2.20\n1\n1.04%\n$0.02\n$0.1\n-1.8%\n\nImmersion Corp\n21.60\n0.82\n0.14\n1.93%\n$0.01\n$0.06\n0.81%\n\nAverage\n39.76\n17.7\n5.96\n20.48%\n$1.62\n$1.96\n60.55%\n\nAfter examining Apple, the following trends can be inferred: \n\nThe stock''s Price to Earnings ratio of 38.87 is lower than the industry average by 0.98x, suggesting potential value in the eyes of market participants.\n\nThe elevated Price to Book ratio of 46.01 relative to the industry average by 2.6x suggests company might be overvalued based on its book value.\n\nWith a relatively high Price to Sales ratio of 10.73, which is 1.8x the industry average, the stock might be considered overvalued based on sales performance.\n\nThe company has a higher Return on Equity (ROE) of 27.84%, which is 7.36% above the industry average. This suggests efficient use of equity to generate profits and demonstrates profitability and growth potential.\n\nThe company exhibits higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $39.02 Billion, which is 24.09x above the industry average, implying stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nWith higher gross profit of $54.77 Billion, which indicates 27.94x above the industry average, the company demonstrates stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nThe company is witnessing a substantial decline in revenue growth, with a rate of 16.36% compared to the industry average of 60.55%, which indicates a challenging sales environment.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio is a financial metric that helps determine the level of financial risk associated with a company''s capital structure.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nWhen assessing Apple against its top 4 peers using the Debt-to-Equity ratio, the following comparisons can be made:\n\nApple demonstrates a stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers in the sector.\n\nWith a lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.78, the company relies less on debt financing and maintains a healthier balance between debt and equity, which can be viewed positively by investors.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor Apple in the Technology Hardware, Storage & Peripherals industry, the PE ratio is low compared to peers, indicating potential undervaluation. The PB and PS ratios are high, suggesting overvaluation relative to industry standards. In terms of ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and revenue growth, Apple demonstrates strong performance compared to its industry peers, reflecting favorable financial health and operational efficiency.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'33bc2377a47832ed8876d365a01d1a00b432a212','2026-09-22 09:58:31','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 09:58:31');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(547,'alpaca:61913454','benzinga','2026-09-22 09:58:27','Comparative Study: NVIDIA And Industry Competitors In Semiconductors &amp; Semiconductor Equipment Industry','In today&#39;s rapidly changing and fiercely competitive business landscape, it is vital for investors and industry enthusiasts to carefully evaluate companies. In this article, we will perform a comprehensive industry','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61913454/comparative-study-nvidia-and-industry-competitors-semiconductors-amp-semiconductor-equipment-industr','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 10:32:39.544397','other','neutral',1,2,'days',1,'The article discusses a comparative study without providing actionable insights.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.033521','61913454',replace('In today''s rapidly changing and fiercely competitive business landscape, it is vital for investors and industry enthusiasts to carefully evaluate companies. In this article, we will perform a comprehensive industry comparison, evaluating NVIDIA (NASDAQ:NVDA) against its key competitors in the Semiconductors & Semiconductor Equipment industry. By analyzing important financial metrics, market position, and growth prospects, we aim to provide valuable insights for investors and shed light on company''s performance within the industry.\nNVIDIA Background\nNvidia is a leading developer of graphics processing units. Traditionally, GPUs were used to enhance the experience on computing platforms, most notably in gaming applications on PCs. GPU use cases have since emerged as important semiconductors used in artificial intelligence to run large language models. Nvidia not only offers AI GPUs, but also a software platform, Cuda, used for AI model development and training. Nvidia is also expanding its data center networking solutions, helping to tie GPUs together to handle complex workloads.\n\nCompany\nP/E\nP/B\nP/S\nROE\nEBITDA (in billions)\nGross Profit (in billions)\nRevenue Growth\n\nNVIDIA Corp\n28.75\n23.98\n18.31\n28.12%\n$72.86\n$72.14\n105.85%\n\nBroadcom Inc\n46.26\n17.37\n19.88\n13.97%\n$18.27\n$20.46\n85.5%\n\nMicron Technology Inc\n23.60\n11.71\n13.17\n32.62%\n$35.58\n$35.06\n345.72%\n\nAdvanced Micro Devices Inc\n157.02\n14.95\n24.58\n3.49%\n$3.35\n$6.2\n50.11%\n\nTexas Instruments Inc\n41.17\n13.74\n12.73\n11.32%\n$2.95\n$3.35\n22.82%\n\nMarvell Technology Inc\n85.23\n12.48\n24.15\n1.68%\n$0.77\n$1.46\n36.55%\n\nQualcomm Inc\n22.20\n7.50\n4.74\n7.29%\n$3.04\n$5.28\n-4.03%\n\nAnalog Devices Inc\n45.49\n5.53\n13.55\n3.98%\n$2.13\n$2.71\n39.63%\n\nMonolithic Power Systems Inc\n77.95\n16.12\n19.10\n6.8%\n$0.32\n$0.54\n47.56%\n\nNXP Semiconductors NV\n19.83\n5.14\n4.48\n6.87%\n$1.27\n$2.0\n19.48%\n\nMicrochip Technology Inc\n109.97\n6.29\n8\n3.14%\n$0.49\n$0.94\n38.05%\n\nCredo Technology Group Holding Ltd\n65.94\n12.90\n22.44\n5.4%\n$0.14\n$0.31\n114.73%\n\nON Semiconductor Corp\n46.88\n3.87\n4.67\n3.12%\n$0.43\n$0.62\n9.18%\n\nGLOBALFOUNDRIES Inc\n37.95\n2.29\n3.91\n1.41%\n$0.48\n$0.51\n5.81%\n\nTower Semiconductor Ltd\n92.42\n8.56\n15.61\n2.99%\n$0.17\n$0.14\n23.66%\n\nFirst Solar Inc\n12.32\n2.08\n4\n4.18%\n$0.61\n$0.61\n-3.73%\n\nMACOM Technology Solutions Holdings Inc\n88.89\n13.83\n18.41\n6.81%\n$0.14\n$0.2\n35.77%\n\nAverage\n60.82\n9.65\n13.34\n7.19%\n$4.38\n$5.02\n54.18%\n\nUpon a comprehensive analysis of NVIDIA, the following trends can be discerned: \n\nWith a Price to Earnings ratio of 28.75, which is 0.47x less than the industry average, the stock shows potential for growth at a reasonable price, making it an interesting consideration for market participants.\n\nIt could be trading at a premium in relation to its book value, as indicated by its Price to Book ratio of 23.98 which exceeds the industry average by 2.48x.\n\nThe Price to Sales ratio of 18.31, which is 1.37x the industry average, suggests the stock could potentially be overvalued in relation to its sales performance compared to its peers.\n\nThe company has a higher Return on Equity (ROE) of 28.12%, which is 20.93% above the industry average. This suggests efficient use of equity to generate profits and demonstrates profitability and growth potential.\n\nThe company exhibits higher Earnings Before Interest, Taxes, Depreciation, and Amortization (EBITDA) of $72.86 Billion, which is 16.63x above the industry average, implying stronger profitability and robust cash flow generation.\n\nCompared to its industry, the company has higher gross profit of $72.14 Billion, which indicates 14.37x above the industry average, indicating stronger profitability and higher earnings from its core operations.\n\nThe company''s revenue growth of 105.85% exceeds the industry average of 54.18%, indicating strong sales performance and market outperformance.\n\nDebt To Equity Ratio\n\nThe debt-to-equity (D/E) ratio provides insights into the proportion of debt a company has in relation to its equity and asset value.\nConsidering the debt-to-equity ratio in industry comparisons allows for a concise evaluation of a company''s financial health and risk profile, aiding in informed decision-making.\nBy considering the Debt-to-Equity ratio, NVIDIA can be compared to its top 4 peers, leading to the following observations:\n\nNVIDIA has a stronger financial position compared to its top 4 peers, as evidenced by its lower debt-to-equity ratio of 0.17.\n\nThis suggests that the company has a more favorable balance between debt and equity, which can be perceived as a positive indicator by investors.\n\nKey Takeaways\nFor NVIDIA, the PE ratio is low compared to peers, indicating potential undervaluation. The high PB and PS ratios suggest strong market sentiment and revenue multiples. In terms of ROE, EBITDA, gross profit, and revenue growth, NVIDIA outperforms industry peers, reflecting strong financial performance and growth prospects.\nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'b7049ae3fdda6dc08901ebb526bcc1890792772f','2026-09-22 09:58:27','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 09:58:27');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(548,'alpaca:61913428','benzinga','2026-09-22 09:53:44','Amazon Blocks Meta’s Muse AI Shopping Assistant, Raising Stakes in Battle Over the Future of E-Commerce: ‘Bigger Battle Than Anyone Anticipates’','Amazon’s decision to block Meta’s Muse has fueled concerns that AI agents could reshape online shopping and e-commerce platforms.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61913428/amazon-blocks-metas-muse-ai-shopping-assistant-raising-stakes-in-battle-over-the-future-of-e-commerce-bigger-battle-than-anyone-anticipates','["AAPL", "AMZN", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 10:32:40.584038','other','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'Amazon''s actions in blocking a competitor''s AI tool has implications for the e-commerce landscape.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.036039','61913428',replace('Amazon.com, Inc.’s (NASDAQ:AMZN) decision to block Meta Platforms, Inc.’s (NASDAQ:META) AI shopping assistant Muse has sparked warnings that the standoff could signal a much bigger fight over who controls the future of online commerce.\n\nAmazon Blocks Meta’s Muse AI From Shopping\n\nUsers trying to shop on Amazon through Meta’s Muse began seeing a message Sunday saying continued access by an unauthorized AI agent violated Amazon’s Conditions of Use, according to GeekWire.\n\nThe move highlights growing tensions as AI agents increasingly move beyond answering questions and begin handling tasks such as product discovery and purchases.\n\nWhile Amazon operates its own AI infrastructure and models, it may also have practical reasons to restrict third-party agents. If an AI agent makes a purchasing mistake, Amazon could ultimately face the resulting customer-service and seller issues.\n\nRead Also:\n\nGenerac Stock Soars on $8 Billion Amazon Data Center Deal\n\n‘Bigger Battle’ Ahead for Agentic Commerce\n\nPalo Alto Networks CEO Nikesh Arora said the dispute could become significantly broader as more AI-powered assistants emerge.\n\n"This will be a bigger battle than anyone anticipates," Arora said on X, predicting AI agents from Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL), Alphabet Inc.’s (NASDAQ:GOOG) (NASDAQ:GOOGL) Google and TikTok could eventually compete alongside frontier AI systems.\n\nArora said platforms will have to decide whether to open their services to consumer agents, strike commercial agreements or risk losing relevance as consumers increasingly rely on a single AI assistant rather than individual apps.\n\nThis will be a bigger battle than anyone anticipates. It is only a matter of time before there is an Apple and Google version of Muse and possibly TikTok, in addition to the frontier LLM agents. Maybe a commerce agent from Amazon. Every app that is a services, marketplace or… https://t.co/kZYd8lchPp— Nikesh Arora (@nikesharora) September 21, 2026 \n\nInvesting commentator Joseph Carlson similarly argued that agentic commerce will continue regardless of Amazon’s decision, suggesting Meta could direct shoppers toward retailers such as Walmart Inc. (NASDAQ:WMT) or merchants using Shopify Inc. (NASDAQ:SHOP).\n\nAmazon will have to change directions quickly. I can already see the Meta representatives talking to Amazon "Sure, if you want to block us, that''s unfortinate, we''ll just send all our customers to Walmart and shopify"Amazon does not win in that situation, and agentic commerce… https://t.co/72RWXmsllO— Joseph Carlson (@joecarlsonshow) September 21, 2026 \n\nOn Monday, Meta and Shopify announced a partnership to enable AI-powered shopping and checkout through Meta’s Muse personal AI assistant.\n\nAI Agents Could Reshape E-Commerce Advertising\n\nFinancial writer Oguz Erkan argued that agentic shopping could also disrupt advertising on Google and Amazon by allowing consumers to delegate product searches and purchasing decisions to AI.\n\nHere is another bullish angle for $META:It’ll take ad spend not just from $GOOG but also from $AMZN and other marketplaces, thanks to agentic shopping.$AMZN cut off Muse, which proves how effective it is. The future of shopping, especially commodity shopping, will be agentic.… https://t.co/lRtbK1V49b pic.twitter.com/FOD0bxIMS3— Oguz Erkan (@oguzerkan) September 21, 2026 \n\nAndreessen Horowitz general partner Angela Strange described the development as part of emerging "agent/data wars," as platforms consider whether to block AI agents, negotiate business deals with them, or pursue another strategy.\n\nThis is just the beginning of the agent/data wars: Amazon cuts off Muse. Every platform who has done the hard work of aggregating users is trying to figure out how not to become "dumb pipes". Do they: 1/ Try to block the agents — but risk pissing off their customers — in… https://t.co/v9F599W766— angela strange (@astrange) September 21, 2026 \n\nPrice Action: Meta Platforms closed at $741.24 on Monday, up 11.43%. The shares gained another 0.40% to $744.18 in Tuesday’s premarket trading, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nAccording to Benzinga Edge Stock Rankings, Meta’s Growth score is in the 79th percentile, and the stock maintains positive short-, medium-, and long-term price trends.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAmazon''s Latest Warehouse Experiment Could Eliminate Millions Of Labor Hours: Report\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'147b10005af94d9410619e389643041c3ea0cd61','2026-09-22 09:53:44','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 09:53:44');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(549,'alpaca:61913386','benzinga','2026-09-22 09:44:28','Jamie Dimon Says AI Spending Could Hit $1 Trillion in 2027 But JPMorgan CEO Warns it Could Add ''Little Bit'' to Inflation: ''That’s Like 1% Increase to GDP...''','JPMorgan CEO Jamie Dimon says AI spending could hit $1 trillion in 2027 and add to inflation as the AI investment boom continues.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61913386/jamie-dimon-says-ai-spending-could-hit-1-trillion-in-2027-but-jpmorgan-ceo-warns-it-could-add-little-bit-to-inflation-thats-like-1-increase-to-gdp','["AMZN"]','stocks','2026-09-22 10:32:42.261391','macro','neutral',2,3,'weeks',1,'Commentary on future AI spending and its potential economic impact.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.043158','61913386',replace('The artificial intelligence (AI) investment surge is showing hardly any signs of abating, with spending across the hyperscaler ecosystem potentially hitting $1 trillion in 2027, according to JPMorgan Chase‘s (NYSE:JPM) CEO Jamie Dimon.\n\nDimon, at the sidelines of the 11th annual JPMorgan India Conference, on Monday told CNBC-TV 18 that the hyperscaler ecosystem has more than doubled from around $300 billion last year to about $700 billion this year.\n\n"That’s like 1% increase to GDP each year,” he said, but added that the spending "may add a little bit to inflation.”\n\nDimon also suggested that AI could eventually have a deflationary impact, describing it as an “unbelievable technology” whose rapid growth “looks like it’s going to continue.”\n\nWhen asked about the returns from AI spending, Dimon said such investments cannot always be measured through a straightforward ROI calculation, pointing to improvements in customer experience as a benefit that can be difficult to quantify.\n\nDimon hinted at a potential market correction but was uncertain if AI would be the trigger. He also cautioned that it was premature to identify the winners of the AI boom, citing the internet bubble as an example of how the AI industry could evolve.\n\n“You can’t look at an ecosystem like that and declare, you know, all the winners and losers,” said Dimon.\n\nRead Also:\n\nScott Bessent Says US, China to Meet in 2 Months on AI Threats: ‘We Want to Start Discussing Protocols’\n\nAI Boom Reshapes US Investment Trends\n\nThe AI investment boom has been described as “massive” by Adam Shapiro, Vice President of the Federal Reserve Bank of San Francisco. He noted a pivotal shift in the U.S. economy, with spending moving away from residential investment and towards computers. Data from the Bureau of Economic Analysis released in August shows real private residential fixed investment at $748 billion in the second quarter, while information-processing equipment reached $752 billion.\n\nIn May, Goldman Sachs raised its 2026 U.S. business investment growth forecast to 7.8% from 6.5%, citing a surge in AI spending. The bank expects AI investment to exceed $800 billion by the end of 2026, making AI infrastructure a growing driver of equipment and structures investment.\n\nMeanwhile, Anshul Sehgal, Goldman Sachs’ global co-head of Fixed Income, Currency and Commodities, sees AI infrastructure offering opportunities even with rates remaining elevated. He noted that the U.S. equity market is now more leveraged than a year ago, with higher interest income going to savers, who then lent that capital to hyperscalers, neoclouds and other sectors, increasing leverage across the domestic equity market.\n\nChris Wood Warns of AI Capex Risks\n\nJefferies’ Chris Wood questioned the sustainability of the AI investment boom, citing the enormous capital being deployed by U.S. hyperscalers and a growing reliance on debt financing. He said AI investments may fail to generate returns sufficient to justify the spending, potentially leading to capital losses.\n\nWood added that semiconductor stocks could continue benefiting as long as markets remain comfortable with the spending, but a sudden withdrawal of credit could bring the trend to an abrupt end.\n\nCurrent consensus estimates indicate that six hyperscalers — Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN), Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOGL), Microsoft Corp., Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ: META), Oracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL), and Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) could collectively spend roughly $916 billion over the next 12 months, rising to nearly $1.2 trillion the following year, as per Apollo Global Management Chief Economist Torsten Slok.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAlibaba Just Supercharged its AI Ambitions: New Zhenwu V900 AI Chip Promises 3X Performance, Targets 20GW Data Center Expansion by 2032\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'4c243de536cfb8acfb12c55119d1beed353b0cb0','2026-09-22 09:44:28','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 09:44:28');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(550,'alpaca:61913313','benzinga','2026-09-22 09:38:15','Why Is Meta Platforms Stock Gaining Tuesday?','Meta stock surges in premarket trading following an 11% rally driven by Muse AI enthusiasm and analyst price target hikes.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61913313/why-is-meta-platforms-stock-gaining-monday','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 10:32:43.559328','analyst','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst price target hikes typically encourage investor interest.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.046256','61913313',replace('Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) stock is trading higher Tuesday in premarket trading, extending a sharp rally fueled by excitement around the company’s new Muse AI agent and bullish analyst commentary. \n\nNasdaq futures slipped 0.02%, while S&P; 500 futures fell 0.03%.\n\nMeta stock closed up 11.34% Monday, reaching its highest level since January as investors cheered early traction for Muse. Shares are now up about 28% in September.\n\nA Sept. 21 Benzinga report also highlighted the scale of Monday’s move. \n\nMeta gained more than $200 billion in market value intraday, with its market capitalization rising by about $207.5 billion to roughly $1.902 trillion from $1.695 trillion at the prior close, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nWells Fargo added to the bullish tone Monday by raising its Meta price forecast to $796 from $640 while maintaining an Overweight rating. The firm cited growing excitement ahead of Meta Connect, where CEO Mark Zuckerberg is expected to outline the company’s broader product vision.\n\nThe event includes a keynote Wednesday, Sept. 23, followed by a developer session Thursday, Sept. 24. Meta’s recently launched Muse AI agent is designed to help users complete tasks and pursue personal goals.\n\nMuse AI Gains Early Traction\n\nPiper Sandler senior research analyst Tom Champion told CNBC on Monday said Muse has had a strong start. He pointed to high usage, positive ratings and its position atop Apple’s App Store.\n\nChampion said the reception could strengthen investor confidence in Zuckerberg’s heavy spending on artificial intelligence.\n\n"The market is coming to terms with the fact that maybe Mark Zuckerberg’s investment plans are fairly rational after all," Champion said.\n\nChampion added that Meta already operates one of the world’s largest digital media platforms, with about 3 billion people using its apps daily. He said AI agents could add another major use case across Meta’s ecosystem.\n\nHe also described Meta as an increasingly essential advertising platform because of its massive reach.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nAnalysts See More Catalysts Ahead\n\nRosenblatt Securities recently maintained its Buy rating and $886 price forecast. The firm highlighted upcoming Meta products, including camera-free smart glasses code-named Luna that are expected this fall. The glasses are expected to include six microphones designed to support AI interactions.\n\nCitigroup analyst Ronald Josey also recently maintained a Buy rating and an $800 price forecast, calling Meta a "top pick" and flagging next week’s Connect event as a near-term catalyst.\n\nBenzinga Edge Rankings\n\nMeta scores strongly on growth and momentum in the Benzinga Edge rankings.\n\nMomentum stands at 78.64, while growth scores 79.79. Quality comes in at 75.36 and value at 46.83.\n\nThe readings point to strong growth and momentum characteristics. However, the lower value score and elevated RSI show the stock has become more extended after its rally.\n\nTop ETF Exposure\n\nThe Global X Social Media ETF (NASDAQ:SOCL) has a 9.26% weighting in Meta. The Invesco AI and Next Gen Software ETF (NYSE:IGPT) has an 8.43% weighting, while the Natixis Loomis Sayles Focused Growth ETF (NYSE:LSGR) has an 8.12% weighting.\n\nLarge ETF inflows or outflows can therefore add to buying or selling pressure in Meta shares.\n\nPrice Action\n\nMeta Platforms shares were up 0.57% at $745.48 in Tuesday’s premarket session, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nImage via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nMicrosoft’s Azure Has Another Growth Lever Waiting in the Wings, Analyst Says','\n',char(10)),'36b8e205792c482aadec9708d003b5267d3cdcc1','2026-09-22 09:38:15','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 09:44:19');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(551,'alpaca:61913270','benzinga','2026-09-22 09:36:56','Stock Market Today: S&P 500, Dow, Futures Gain Nasdaq 100 Slips as Trump Administration Targets Iranian Airlines— Lennar, Greenland Mines, Accenture in Focus (UPDATED)','U.S. stock futures were mixed on Tuesday, as the Dow Jones and S&amp;P 500 indices rose and the Nasdaq 100 index fell.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61913270/stock-market-today-sp-500-futures-gain-nasdaq-100-slips-as-trump-administration-targets-iranian-airlines-len-grml-acn-in-focus','["BTC/USD", "QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-22 13:33:29.873851','macro','neutral',2,3,'hours',1,'U.S. stock futures showed mixed performance without significant impacts on individual stocks.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "QQQ": 716.89, "SPY": 762.63}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 10:32:28.048787','61913270',replace('U.S. stock futures were mixed on Tuesday, as the Dow Jones and S&P; 500 indices rose and the Nasdaq 100 index fell, following Monday’s higher close.\n\nU.S. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent announced that Iranian airlines will be "shut down" worldwide by Wednesday, warning foreign entities that providing fuel or landing services will result in exclusion from the dollar-based financial system. Treasury also sanctioned major foreign financial institutions in Egypt, Turkey, and Russia for facilitating Iranian transactions. Following the news, energy prices moved higher, with Brent crude futures rising 1.05% to $101.39 per barrel. \n\nTuesday’s earnings include reports from AutoZone Inc. (NYSE:AZO), Thor Industries Inc. (NYSE:THO), KB Home (NYSE:KBH), Worthington Enterprises Inc. (NYSE:WOR), and MillerKnoll Inc. (NASDAQ:MLKN).\n\nMeanwhile, the 10-year Treasury bond yielded 4.97%, and the 2-year Treasury bond yielded 4.77%, at the last check. The CME Group’s FedWatch tool projections show markets pricing in a 57.6% likelihood of the Federal Reserve hiking interest rates after its October meeting. –\n\nIndexPerformance (+/-)Dow Jones0.16%S&P; 5000.03%Nasdaq 100-0.03%Russell 20000.72%\n\nThe SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 index and Nasdaq 100 index, respectively, were mixed in premarket trading on Tuesday. The SPY was up 0.063% at $773.99, while the QQQ declined 0.097% to $740.75.\n\nRead Also:\n\nStock Market: Will S&P; 500 Open Up or Down Today?\n\nStocks In Focus\n\nOn Holding\n\nOn Holding AG (NYSE:ONON) rose 2.67% in premarket on Tuesday after it announced a buyback of up to $1 billion through 2029 and new long-term financial targets, according to Global Banking and Finance on Sept. 22.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that ONON maintains a weak price trend in the short, medium, and long terms, with a good growth score.\n\nLennar\n\nLennar Corp. (NYSE:LEN) was up 1.09% in premarket after Berkshire Hathaway Inc. (NASDAQ:BRK) (NASDAQ:BRK), under CEO Greg Abel, disclosed a stake of about $1.2 billion in the homebuilder.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that LEN maintains a weak price trend in the short, medium, and long terms, with a bad quality score.\n\nAccenture\n\nAccenture Plc (NYSE:ACN) was 0.47% higher after it announced with Google Cloud that Volvo Cars has become the lead industry partner for software firm Horizon. It also formed a new partnership with Anthropic on Monday focused on AI safety and model evaluation.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that ACN maintains a strong price trend in the medium and short terms but a weak trend in the long term, with a poor value score.\n\nLockheed Martin\n\nLockheed Martin Corp. (NYSE:LMT) was up 0.17% in premarket on Tuesday after it secured a $1.2 billion Army contract for a missile system on Monday.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that LMT maintains a weak price trend in the long, medium and short terms.\n\nGreenland Mines\n\nGreenland Mines Ltd. (NASDAQ:GRML) jumped 11.46% in premarket following the company’s expansion of its Sarfartoq rare earth magnet district land position in West Greenland. The expansion adds 262 square kilometers, bringing the total to approximately 454 square kilometers.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that GRML maintains a weak price trend in the long, medium, and short terms.\n\nRead Also:\n\nS&P; 500 Nears Record High But Breadth Flashes Rare 1929, 1999 Signal — Analyst Says ‘We’ve Never in Almost 100 Years Seen Breadth This Bad’\n\nCues From Last Session\n\nCommunication services, information technology, and consumer discretionary sectors gained the most on Monday, whereas energy, utilities, consumer staples, and materials declined.\n\nIndexPerformance (+/-)ValueDow Jones0.71%52,048.83S&P; 5001.49%7,764.70Nasdaq Composite2.26%27,122.09Russell 20000.52%2,875.36\n\nInsights From Analysts\n\nLPL Financial expects S&P; 500 profit margins and the broader market to face a reality check, arguing that current forward-looking consensus estimates are overly optimistic and “appear stretched.”\n\nWhile acknowledging that structural changes—specifically the rising weight of high-margin technology companies—justify a higher baseline operating margin than historical averages, LPL cautions investors against assuming margins will rise indefinitely.\n\nLPL decomposes recent margin gains into structural, cyclical, and temporary forces. A key concern is that current record margins are heavily powered by the cyclical AI trade, with the semiconductor industry driving “nearly half of S&P; 500 margin expansion since 2019.”\n\nLPL warns that “the market is effectively underwriting a future return on AI infrastructure before that return is fully visible,” while hyperscaler accounting has yet to absorb the full depreciation burden of recent capital expenditures.\n\nConsequently, LPL advocates a framework where margins “are still mean-reverting, but the mean has moved,” advising investors to differentiate between durable structural gains and vulnerable cyclical spikes.\n\nUpcoming Economic Data\n\nHere’s what investors will be keeping an eye on Tuesday.\n\nFederal Reserve Bank of Richmond President Thomas Barkin will speak to the CFA Society Baltimore at 1:00 p.m. ET.\n\nCommodities, Crypto, And Global Equity Markets\n\nCrude Oil WTI futures were trading lower in the early New York session by 0.26% to hover around $92.61 per barrel.\n\nGold Spot US Dollar fell 1.14% to hover around $4,294.59 per ounce. The U.S. Dollar Index spot was 0.21% higher at the 100.6380 level.\n\nMeanwhile, Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) was trading 3.50% higher at $85,400.34 per coin over the last 24 hours.\n\nAsian markets were higher on Tuesday, except India’s Nifty 50 index. Australia’s ASX 200, Japan’s Nikkei 225, South Korea’s Kospi, China’s CSI 300, and Hong Kong’s Hang Seng indices rose. European markets were lower in early trading.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Growth Stocks\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'aea27fbcfaa3842ab04014af5e804f86bd188bb1','2026-09-22 09:36:56','2026-09-22 10:32:28.004196',2,NULL,'2026-09-22 12:32:37');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(552,'alpaca:61914657','benzinga','2026-09-22 10:59:09','Big Tech’s AI Debt Spree Hits a Wall as Bond Investors Demand Higher Yields From Alphabet, Meta and Nvidia','Alphabet, Meta, and Nvidia face rising borrowing costs as bond markets demand higher yields to absorb Big Tech&#39;s massive AI debt spree.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/bonds/26/09/61914657/big-techs-ai-debt-spree-hits-a-wall-as-bond-investors-demand-higher-yields-from-alphabet-meta-and-nvidia','["META", "MSFT", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 11:32:54.197825','macro','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'Rising borrowing costs could negatively impact the financials of these companies.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 11:32:49.965088','61914657',replace('Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOG) (NASDAQ:GOOGL), Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META), and Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) face higher borrowing costs as bond markets adjust pricing for debt issuances funding artificial intelligence infrastructure.\n\nAccording to financial analyst Nicholas Mugalli, credit spreads have widened across technology issuers as debt offering sizes scale upward.\n\nSpreads Widen Across Major Issuers\n\nMugalli noted that “bond markets are officially penalizing scale” as larger corporate offerings command wider yields and credit spreads.\n\nAlphabet saw credit spreads widen by 15 basis points, moving from 56 to 71 basis points as issuance sizes expanded from $1.25 billion to $3.50 billion. Meta and Nvidia exhibited similar pricing trends, where $4 billion bond offerings pushed spreads out by 15 to 19 basis points.\n\nMugalli stated that credit markets no longer treat big tech debt as “risk free paper.” He added that institutional investors demand concessions to absorb the “supply deluge,” creating an “explicit funding tax” on scale.\n\nBond markets are officially penalizing scale. Larger issuance sizes across big tech are commanding meaningfully wider yields and credit spreads across the board.  $GOOGL saw spreads widen 15 bps (56 to 71 bps) as issue sizes scaled from $1.25B to $3.50B. $META and $NVDA mirror… https://t.co/SXD15YORbw pic.twitter.com/4LOS001bI0— Nicholas Mugalli (@RealNickMugalli) September 22, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nS&P; 500 Nears Record High But Breadth Flashes Rare 1929, 1999 Signal — Analyst Says ‘We’ve Never in Almost 100 Years Seen Breadth This Bad’\n\nCapital Needs Outstrip Cash Flow\n\nThe increase in borrowing costs coincides with expanding capital requirements for infrastructure. Data shared by Mugalli indicates that total required funding has reached $5.5 trillion, alongside a $400 billion upward revision in capital expenditure forecasts.\n\nOrganic cash flow of $1 trillion and incremental equity of $0.4 trillion cover only about a quarter of the total requirement, Mugalli said, while noting that as a result, issuers rely on $2.1 trillion in high-grade bond markets and $1.4 trillion in alternative capital.\n\nHyperscaler debt expanded 92% year-over-year alongside an 81% increase in capital expenditures, compared to a 4% debt increase across the remainder of the high-grade corporate bond market. \n\nTotal AI capex forecasts just got revised up by $400B, but total funding required has blown out to a massive $5.5T.  Organic cash flow ($1.0T) and incremental equity ($0.4T) cover barely a quarter of the bill. Big tech is being forced to turn massive tap lines to high grade… https://t.co/iqPzBLBAOp pic.twitter.com/3bj9LtMTrr— Nicholas Mugalli (@RealNickMugalli) September 20, 2026 \n\nCloud Revenue and Operating Margins\n\nDespite added leverage, cloud operating metrics reflect top-line growth. According to another X post by Mugalli, Quarterly cloud and AI revenue growth accelerated to 52% in 2Q26.\n\nAccording to Mugalli, operating margins across AWS, Google Cloud and Microsoft Corp.’s (NASDAQ:MSFT) Intelligent Cloud converged within a 36% to 41% corridor in the second quarter of 2026, while cloud operating profit growth reached 65%.\n\nRead Also:\n\nCathie Wood-led Ark Invest Bets Big On Prediction Markets, Snaps Up Kalshi Shares Across 3 Funds, Dumps Brera Holdings\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'049958ee608cdfdf736c0c77a8730ad4b943a792','2026-09-22 10:59:09','2026-09-22 11:32:49.941870',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 10:59:09');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(553,'alpaca:61914488','benzinga','2026-09-22 10:44:09','Chamath Palihapitiya Warns Amazon’s Blocking of Meta’s Muse AI Signals Bigger Battle Ahead: ''Everyone Will Start Blocking Everyone''','Palihapitiya warns Amazon’s block of Meta’s Muse AI shopping agent may spark wider AI platform battles as agents reshape e-commerce.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61914488/chamath-palihapitiya-warns-amazons-blocking-of-metas-muse-ai-signals-bigger-battle-ahead-everyone-will-start-blocking-everyone','["AMZN", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 11:32:55.954009','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Palihapitiya''s comments suggest potential industry tensions without a direct impact on stock prices.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 11:32:49.971359','61914488',replace('Venture Capitalist Chamath Palihapitiya warned that Amazon.com, Inc.’s (NASDAQ:AMZN) decision to block Meta Platforms, Inc.’s (NASDAQ:META) AI shopping assistant Muse could signal a broader battle over how AI agents interact with online platforms.\n\nChamath Warns of AI Agent Blocking\n\nOn Monday, in a post on X, Palihapitiya said the dispute between Amazon and Meta highlights a larger problem with the development of AI agents.\n\n"This wrinkle is indicative of a bigger problem: the behavior of agents are still quite naive and help amplify a bunch of issues wrt the direction of AI – most importantly including those of strategy and long term competitiveness," Palihapitiya said.\n\nHe added, "I suspect everyone will start blocking everyone shortly. Plan accordingly."\n\nThis wrinkle is indicative of a bigger problem: the behavior of agents are still quite naive and help amplify a bunch of issues wrt the direction of AI – most importantly including those of strategy and long term competitiveness. I suspect everyone will start blocking everyone… https://t.co/YRVitf06FZ— Chamath Palihapitiya (@chamath) September 21, 2026 \n\nAmazon Blocks Meta’s Muse AI\n\nHis comments came after Amazon blocked Meta’s Muse AI shopping assistant from accessing its platform, with users seeing a message saying the agent violated Amazon’s Conditions of Use. \n\nThe move highlighted growing tensions as AI agents increasingly handle product discovery and purchases online.\n\nAmazon’s restriction of third-party AI agents could also help the company avoid potential customer-service and seller issues arising from purchases made by autonomous AI systems.\n\nRead Also:\n\nChamath Palihapitiya Sounds Alarm on AI Coding: ‘We Are Turning an Entire Generation’ Into ‘Slot Machines’\n\nMeta’s Muse AI Shopping\n\nMeta and Shopify Inc. (NASDAQ:SHOP) teamed up to bring AI-powered shopping and checkout to Muse, allowing users to shop across Shopify-powered stores and complete purchases through Shop Pay. \n\nShopify CEO Tobias Lütke and Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg said the partnership would make shopping with Muse easier, with Zuckerberg noting that more partnerships were coming.\n\nNYU Stern professor and entrepreneur Scott Galloway said Meta’s years of user data from Facebook, Instagram and WhatsApp could give Muse an advantage by providing personal context that rival AI companies would take years to build. \n\nMuse had climbed to No. 1 among free apps on Apple’s U.S. App Store but was later blocked by Amazon from shopping on its platform over privacy, security and transparency concerns.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nHoward Lutnick Calls AI Data Center Water Concerns ‘Propaganda by Our Adversaries’ — Federal Research Tells a Different Story\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'0a5909bd58d814260407dac37153c1a4dec1e7b0','2026-09-22 10:44:09','2026-09-22 11:32:49.941870',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 10:44:09');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(554,'alpaca:61917279','benzinga','2026-09-22 12:27:06','Bitcoin Just Hit a Seven-Month High. The Analyst Calling the Bottom Expects a Pullback','Bitcoin analyst Kevin Capital sees a 90%-95% chance the bear-market bottom is in, targeting $93K-$100K while warning of a pullback.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61917279/bitcoin-just-hit-a-seven-month-high-the-analyst-calling-the-bottom-expects-a-pullback','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 12:33:04.159608','analyst','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst commentary on Bitcoin price expectations.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 12:33:00.179237','61917279',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) surged 11% over the past week, hitting a seven-month high, as analyst Kevin Capital pointed to a series of higher-timeframe technical signals suggesting the bear-market bottom is likely in.\n\nHe now assigns a 90%-95% probability that Bitcoin’s roughly $60,000 low marked the cycle bottom, up from his previous 70% estimate.\n\nHowever, he expects a pullback after the latest breakout.\n\nWhy BTC Bull Market Is Here?\n\nIn a podcast on Sep.21, Kevin pointed to Bitcoin breaking above the daily moving averages that capped price throughout the bear market, followed by consolidation and another move higher.\n\nHe also highlighted a golden cross that occurred more than 300 days into the bear market and a bullish two-week MACD crossover.\n\nKevin said similar signals in previous cycles appeared after Bitcoin’s lows were already established.\n\nBitcoin has also closed above its 50-week moving average, broken its previous lower-high structure and moved through the $85,000 (0.5) Fibonacci level.\n\n"The bottom is obviously in," Kevin said, adding that it would take a major shock to invalidate the developing trend.\n\nIs $100,000 Bitcoin Next?\n\nKevin sees “plenty of juice in the tank” if Bitcoin holds its latest higher-timeframe breakout.\n\nHis next major target zone sits between $93,000 and $100,000, where a high-volume area and major technical resistance converge.\n\nHowever, he does not expect Bitcoin to move straight up. A run toward $93,000-$100,000 could set up a correction as Bitcoin becomes increasingly extended from its daily moving averages.\n\nKevin said the key from here is for Bitcoin to continue forming higher lows, which would preserve the broader bullish structure even during a pullback.\n\nThe analyst compared the setup to Bitcoin’s 2022-2023 bear-market exit, when it reclaimed key moving averages before rallying from $25,000 to $73,000.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin, Zcash, Hyperliquid in Focus as Industry Expert Sees Crypto Nearing a ''Major Turning Point''\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'f454eb89715cb8199e695836ccedaaf908c29b4e','2026-09-22 12:27:06','2026-09-22 12:33:00.168972',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 12:27:06');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(555,'alpaca:61916719','benzinga','2026-09-22 12:07:10','Mark Zuckerberg Adds $27 Billion to Net Worth Monday, More Than Rest of Top 10 Combined','Mark Zuckerberg&#39;s wealth made a big jump Monday as Meta stock soared.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61916719/mark-zuckerberg-adds-27-billion-to-net-worth-monday-more-than-rest-of-top-10-combined','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 12:33:05.949226','other','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Zuckerberg''s net worth increase is linked to a significant rise in Meta''s stock price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 12:33:00.192688','61916719',replace('Monday was a great day if your name is Mark Zuckerberg or you own Meta Platforms (NASDAQ:META) stock. Here’s how much, in dollars, Meta’s strong stock performance helped CEO Zuckerberg’s wealth grow.\n\nMark Zuckerberg’s Wealth Gains\n\nMeta stock soared 11.4% to close at $741.24 on Monday, a move that was helped by the strength of the company’s recently released Muse AI personal agent.\n\nWith the stock movement, Zuckerberg added $27.3 billion to his wealth, increasing his net worth by 11.9% to $255.4 billion, according to Forbes.\n\nZuckerberg is the sixth-richest person in the world, but on Monday he outpaced all 10 of the top billionaires combined.\n\nThe other nine richest people in the world gained a combined $24.14 billion, less than the $27.3 billion Zuckerberg added to his own net worth.\n\nRanking second on the day was Larry Page, a Google co-founder, who added $5.2 billion to his net worth. Page ranks third with a net worth of $291 billion.\n\nMonday’s gain wasn’t enough for Zuckerberg to join the top five richest, but it got him closer to Sergey Brin, who is worth $267.7 billion and rounds out the top five.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMeta''s Muse Hits No. 1, Carrying AMD Into the $1-Trillion Club\n\nMeta Stock in the Spotlight\n\nMeta stock could remain in the spotlight over the coming days. The launch of Muse, a personal AI agent to assist users with tasks and goals, has been well received. Muse is the most downloaded free iPhone app in the United States in recent days.\n\nThe social media and AI company is also set to host Meta Connect on Sept. 23 and Sept. 24, an event that will feature speeches from Meta executives and partners and could show investors where the company is headed in the future when it comes to AI and other growth areas.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMeta Reports Mixed Q2 Results, Raises Low End of CapEx Guidance Range, Shares Move Lower\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'ad7668df633650d115659435bdf9c1857b0fa182','2026-09-22 12:07:10','2026-09-22 12:33:00.168972',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 12:07:10');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(556,'alpaca:61916462','benzinga','2026-09-22 12:03:44','Bitcoin ETFs Add $999 Million In Best Day Since October 2025: What''s Going On?','Bitcoin ETFs drew $999 million in their biggest inflow in 11 months, fueling BTC’s surge above $87,000 and hopes the bear market is over.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61916462/bitcoin-etfs-add-999-million-in-best-day-since-october-2025-whats-going-on','["BTC/USD", "ETH/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 12:33:07.495834','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Significant inflow into Bitcoin ETFs suggests renewed interest in BTC.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 12:33:00.221416','61916462',replace('U.S. spot Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) ETFs pulled in $998.95 million Monday, their largest single-day inflow in 11 months, as Bitcoin briefly surged above $87,000.\n\nWhat the ETF Data Shows\n\nAccording to SoSoValue data, BlackRock’s IBIT (NASDAQ:IBIT) led the inflows with $381.4 million, followed by Ark & 21Shares‘ ARKB (BATS:ARKB) at $289.1 million and Fidelity’s FBTC (BATS:FBTC) at $238.8 million. \n\nGrayscale, Bitwise, and Morgan Stanley (NYSE:MS) funds also logged positive flows. Monday’s total marks the biggest day since Oct. 6, 2025, when inflows hit $1.2 billion.\n\nMeanwhile, Spot Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH) ETFs matched the momentum, pulling in $269.98 million, their largest single-day inflow since Oct. 7, 2025.\n\nWhy the Move Happened So Fast\n\nCryptoQuant broke down the mechanics on X, noting that ETF demand was only part of the story. Three forces stacked together to drive the move:\n\nFresh ETF demand — the $999 million inflow represents nearly 12,000 BTC bought in a single day\n\nShort squeeze — $345 million in Bitcoin shorts got liquidated on top of that demand\n\nThin resistance — URPD data shows little historical trading activity between $80,000 and $85,000, letting price move through that zone almost unopposed\n\nTogether, these pushed Bitcoin from $81,146 to $86,600, a 7% move in one day.\n\nOne caution stands out for follow-through: the Coinbase Premium Gap has turned negative, suggesting U.S. spot demand has already cooled since the initial surge. \n\nThat puts the next test squarely on ETF flows, which need to sustain momentum if Bitcoin is going to push through the $85,000 to $95,000 resistance zone.\n\nWhy Analysts Call This the Bear Market’s End\n\nCryptoQuant Analyst Ki Young Ju posted on X that Bitcoin reclaimed the 365-day moving average at $83,000 and now sits above $84,000, a level widely watched as the line separating the bear market from the bull market. \n\nIf it holds, he expects momentum traders and institutions to start chasing the move.\n\nMoreover, Bitwise senior analyst Joe Consorti added on X that Bitcoin closing above its 50-week moving average has historically carried a 75% chance of marking the cycle low, and a 100% hit rate excluding the COVID crash black swan. \n\n“The bear is slain,” Consorti wrote. “Welcome, tentatively, to the bull market,” he added.\n\nBTC Price Analysis: Key Levels to Watch\n\nBTC trades down 0.5% Tuesday, after Monday’s sharp 7% breakout candle shattered the descending triangle that capped price since early September. \n\nTuesday’s session reflects healthy consolidation rather than reversal, with price simply retesting the breakout zone from above. \n\nThe Parabolic SAR at $76,269 sits well below price, keeping the bullish trend structure intact.\n\nKey levels for BTC:\n\n$86,610 — yesterday’s high, immediate resistance\n\n$79,334 — Bollinger basis, deeper support\n\nRead Also:\n\nXRP Will Advance to $5.40? Veteran Trader Peter Brandt Shares Long-Term Forecast, Another Popular Analyst Says Coin Has ''Room to Run''\n\nPhoto: Frame Stock Footage / Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'22e4b2367f7b753a897d88e56b5be5e7f05ae265','2026-09-22 12:03:44','2026-09-22 12:33:00.168972',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 12:03:44');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(557,'alpaca:61916439','benzinga','2026-09-22 12:03:25','Why Is Shopify Stock Surging on Tuesday?','Shopify Inc. stock gained Tuesday after announcing a partnership with Meta Platforms, Inc. to enable AI-powered shopping and checkout through Meta’s Muse assistant.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61916439/why-is-shopify-stock-surging-on-tuesday','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 12:33:08.586707','partnership','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Shopify announced a partnership with Meta to enhance shopping through AI.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 12:33:00.224023','61916439',replace('Shopify Inc. (NASDAQ:SHOP) stock gained Tuesday following the announcement of a partnership with Meta Platforms, Inc. (NASDAQ:META). \n\nThe agreement integrates Shopify’s e-commerce infrastructure with Meta’s Muse personal AI agent, allowing users to shop across Shopify-powered merchants and process purchases via Shop Pay. \n\nNasdaq futures are up 0.07% while S&P; 500 futures have gained 0.07%.\n\nPartnership Integrates Shop Pay Into Meta Muse\n\nThe deal enables autonomous, AI-driven purchasing capabilities through Shop Pay, Shopify’s accelerated checkout tool that stores customer payment and delivery information.\n\nShopify CEO Tobias Lütke announced the partnership on X on Monday, describing it as an effort to create an “easy and delightful way to shop and check out with Muse.” Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg confirmed the integration on X early Tuesday.\n\n“Teaming up with Shopify to make shopping and checkout easier in Muse,” Zuckerberg wrote. “Shoppers find more. Shops sell more. More partnerships like this coming soon.”\n\nRead Also:\n\nStock Market Today: S&P; 500 Futures Gain, Nasdaq 100 Slips as Trump Administration Targets Iranian Airlines\n\nTechnical Analysis\n\nFrom a trend perspective, Shopify is trading above its major moving averages, sitting 1.9% above the 20-day SMA ($139.31), 4.1% above the 50-day SMA ($136.38), and 9% above the 200-day SMA ($130.25). That alignment keeps the intermediate trend constructive, with the 20-day SMA above the 50-day SMA (bullish) and the golden cross (50-day above 200-day) still in place since August.\n\nMomentum is more "reset than stretched," with RSI at 51.09, which signals neutral conditions rather than an overbought chase. In plain terms, RSI helps gauge whether buying or selling has become extended; near-50 readings often show a stock in balance and more sensitive to breakouts from nearby levels.\n\nKey Resistance: $156.50 — a nearby pivot area where upside attempts can stall if buyers can’t build follow-through\n\nKey Support: $124 — a prior demand zone that lines up with a key "line in the sand" from earlier swings\n\nZooming out, the stock is still down 12.22% over the past 12 months, which helps explain why rallies can face overhead supply even as the moving-average structure improves. The 52-week range ($94.00 to $182.19) also frames $156.50 as a meaningful mid-to-upper band test, while $124 sits closer to the lower half of the yearly range where buyers previously defended.\n\nSHOP Price Action: Shopify shares were up 3.68% at $142.99 during premarket trading on Tuesday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAmazon Blocks Meta’s Muse AI Shopping Assistant, Raising Stakes in Battle Over the Future of E-Commerce: ‘Bigger Battle Than Anyone Anticipates’\n\nPhoto: El editorial / Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'009695dd0e765d3a65233a56ac186706aaf9e58c','2026-09-22 12:03:25','2026-09-22 12:33:00.168972',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 12:03:25');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(558,'alpaca:61915842','benzinga','2026-09-22 11:45:21','What''s Going On With AMD Stock Tuesday?','AMD cools after reaching a 52-week high and $1T market cap. Overbought technicals pull shares back, but analyst outlook remains bullish.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61915842/whats-going-on-with-amd-stock-tuesday-12','["AMD", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 12:33:10.074103','analyst','neutral',2,2,'hours',1,'The headline discusses technical indicators and analyst outlook without new information.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 12:33:00.241259','61915842',replace('Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) stock fell more than 1% in Tuesday premarket trading after gaining 9.95% in the previous session. Traders took some profits near recent highs while weighing fresh signs that agentic AI could drive greater demand for CPU-heavy inference workloads.Nasdaq futures were up 0.03%, while S&P; 500 futures gained 0.06%.The stock is also trading near its 52-week high after a sharp rally. That can encourage investors to lock in gains, especially after Monday’s nearly 10% advance.However, investors are also watching a potentially important new AI demand driver.AMD crossed $1 trillion in market value for the first time Monday after Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) said its Muse personal AI agent ranked as the most-downloaded free iPhone app in the U.S. for three straight days, according to Sensor Tower.The traction adds another data point to AMD’s argument that agentic AI could expand demand for server CPUs.Muse Traction Supports AMD’s Agentic AI ThesisAMD has argued that agentic AI workloads rely heavily on CPUs. AI agents often coordinate multiple tool calls and carry out multi-step logic between model invocations.That workload structure could increase the amount of traditional computing needed alongside GPUs and other AI accelerators.AMD expects the server CPU addressable market to grow about 50% by 2030 to roughly $220 billion.Muse’s early App Store traction therefore gives investors a real-world signal to watch. If AI agents gain broader adoption, rising inference activity could support stronger CPU demand across data centers.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nTechnical AnalysisAMD remains in a strong uptrend. The stock is trading 22.1% above its 20-day simple moving average of $497.87. It is also 70.4% above its 200-day SMA of $356.63.Those gaps show strong momentum. However, they also suggest the stock is trading well above its longer-term trend.AMD’s relative strength index stands at 72.63. An RSI above 70 typically signals overbought conditions and can precede consolidation or a pullback.Still, the moving-average structure remains bullish. The 20-day SMA is above the 50-day SMA, while the 50-day SMA remains above the 200-day SMA.The RSI moved into overbought territory in September. Meanwhile, the stock continued its latest leg higher after forming a swing low in July.Key support: About $498, near the 20-day moving average and an area where buyers could look for support.Analyst OutlookAMD trades at a price-to-earnings ratio of about 157 times, reflecting the market’s high growth expectations. The stock carries a Buy consensus rating with an average price forecast of $604.Recent analyst actions include Piper Sandler initiating coverage with an Overweight rating and a $600 price target on Sept. 10. Raymond James upgraded AMD to Strong Buy and raised its target to $641 on Aug. 25. BMO Capital initiated coverage with an Outperform rating and a $550 target on Aug. 21.Benzinga Edge RankingsThe Benzinga Edge scorecard highlights AMD’s strong momentum, growth and quality scores.AMD has a Momentum score of 99.26, a Quality score of 95.33 and a Growth score of 95.61.However, its Value score is just 3.46. That reflects the premium investors are paying for AMD’s expected growth.Overall, AMD’s Edge scores point to strong momentum and growth. However, its elevated valuation and overbought RSI could leave the stock more vulnerable to pullbacks.Top ETF ExposureThe iShares Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SOXX) has an 8.74% weighting in AMD. The First Trust Nasdaq Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:FTXL) has a 6.79% weighting, while the Pacer Data and Digital Revolution ETF (NYSE:TRFK) has a 6.52% weighting.AMD’s sizable weight in these funds means large ETF inflows or outflows can contribute to buying or selling pressure in the stock.Price ActionAMD Stock Price Activity: Advanced Micro Devices shares were down 1.22% at $608 in Tuesday premarket trading, according to Benzinga Pro data.Photo via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nWhat If the AI Boom Cracks? S&P; Says Taiwan Semiconductor Is Built to Withstand the Shock','\n',char(10)),'f484ab2f2b5a630f611b83354157b9e9a35e4d3b','2026-09-22 11:45:21','2026-09-22 12:33:00.168972',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 11:45:21');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(559,'alpaca:61919777','benzinga','2026-09-22 13:31:31','China Slams Brakes on Humanoid Robot IPOs After Unitree’s 55% Plunge — Tesla Optimus Faces Commercialization Test','China is slowing humanoid robot IPOs after Unitree’s 55% plunge as Tesla pushes Optimus toward commercialization.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61919777/china-humanoid-robot-ipos-unitree-tesla','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 13:33:19.169049','regulatory','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'Regulatory action may impact Tesla''s robotics plans and investor sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 13:33:14.303746','61919777',replace('Chinese regulators are slowing a rush of humanoid robot IPOs after Unitree Robotics plunged roughly 55% from its peak, as Beijing questions whether soaring valuations match real-world demand.The scrutiny comes as Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) faces its own Optimus test: turning a headline-grabbing robot into a viable business.China Puts IPO Rush on IceUnitree’s volatile debut has prompted Chinese regulators to slow a wave of humanoid robot IPOs, Reuters reported.At least half a dozen companies, including Deep Robotics, X Square Robot and AGIBOT, are preparing to list. Regulators are now holding some deals back through informal “window guidance,” with one source describing humanoid IPOs as effectively frozen for now.Regulators are also questioning how much demand is truly commercial. Local governments can fund 80% to 90% of some robot data centers and joint ventures, helping generate revenue and support IPO valuations.One person close to investors told Reuters that valuations at some robot companies could fall 60% to 70% if revenue tied to those data-collection centers were removed.Unitree Became the Warning SignUnitree went public in August at a roughly $9 billion valuation. Retail investors ordered more than 8,000 times the shares available, and the stock briefly pushed the company’s value to around $67 billion on its first trading day.Shares have since fallen roughly 55% from that peak.Unitree’s underlying business is growing quickly. Revenue more than quadrupled to 1.7 billion yuan, or about $252 million, in 2025, but its IPO still valued the company at roughly 219 times last year’s earnings.Only about 7,000 humanoid robots were sold worldwide for industrial and professional uses in 2025, according to the International Federation of Robotics.By comparison, manufacturers installed about 542,000 conventional industrial robots in 2024, nearly 80 times the humanoid tally.Tesla Faces the Same TestTesla CEO Elon Musk recently confirmed on an earnings call that the company will convert space in Fremont for Model S and Model X manufacturing into an Optimus factory.But Musk has also acknowledged how difficult that transition could be. He called Optimus the “hardest product to scale manufacturing” Tesla has ever attempted and warned that the production ramp will initially be “quite flat and long,” with the company effectively building a new supply chain from scratch.Prediction-market traders remain skeptical about a near-term consumer launch. Polymarket puts the chance of Tesla making a humanoid robot available for public purchase before Dec. 31 at about 6%.Factory deployments and enterprise pilots do not count, meaning Tesla could make significant progress on Optimus without the market resolving “Yes.”Benzinga reported earlier this month that Tesla had reportedly placed its first large-scale component order covering roughly 5,000 Optimus robots as it moves from prototypes toward production.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMorgan Stanley Says AI Adoption Has Barely Started: ''We''re at the National Anthem''\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'532be90c9346600f9798a98f24f7c94d74092fcb','2026-09-22 13:31:31','2026-09-22 13:33:14.267772',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 13:31:31');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(560,'alpaca:61919218','benzinga','2026-09-22 13:12:46','Meta To Rally Around 18%? Here Are 10 Top Analyst Forecasts For Tuesday','Analysts upgraded Fifth Third to Buy and adjusted price targets for Exelon, Alaska Air, Fair Isaac, Meta, Alkermes, Twilio and Warner Bros. Discovery.','https://www.benzinga.com/analyst-stock-ratings/price-target/26/09/61919218/meta-to-rally-around-18-here-are-10-top-analyst-forecasts-for-tuesday','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 13:33:20.955135','analyst','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Analysts adjusted price targets but this is routine coverage of analyst opinions.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 13:33:14.336382','61919218',replace('Top Wall Street analysts changed their outlook on these top names. For a complete view of all analyst rating changes, including upgrades and downgrades, please see our analyst ratings page.\n\nCitigroup raised the price target for Fifth Third Bancorp (NYSE:FITB) from $59 to $62. Citigroup analyst Benjamin Gerlinger upgraded the stock from Neutral to Buy. Fifth Third Bancorp shares closed at $53.31 on Monday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nArgus Research cut Exelon Corp (NASDAQ:EXC) price target from $52 to $49. Argus Research analyst Marie Ferguson maintained a Buy rating. Exelon shares closed at $41.98 on Monday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nUBS raised price target for Alaska Air Group Inc (NYSE:ALK) from $52 to $54. UBS analyst Atul Maheswari maintained a Buy rating. Alaska Air shares closed at $41.90 on Monday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nWells Fargo cut the price target for Fair Isaac Corp (NYSE:FICO) from $1,450 to $1,350. Wells Fargo analyst Jason Haas maintained an Overweight rating. Fair Isaac shares closed at $924.52 on Monday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nJefferies raised Meta Platforms Inc (NASDAQ:META) price target from $710 to $875. Jefferies analyst Brent Thill maintained a Buy rating. Meta shares closed at $741.24 on Monday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nBaird slashed Alkermes Plc (NASDAQ:ALKS) price target from $58 to $61. Baird analyst Joel Beatty maintained an Outperform rating. Alkermes shares closed at $44.18 on Monday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nRosenblatt increased Twilio Inc (NYSE:TWLO) price target from $275 to $290. Rosenblatt analyst Catharine Trebnick maintained a Buy rating. Twilio shares closed at $266.06 on Monday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nMorgan Stanley raised the price target for Warner Bros Discovery Inc (NASDAQ:WBD) from $29 to $31. Morgan Stanley analyst Sean Diffley maintained an Equal-Weight rating. Warner Bros Discovery shares closed at $30.80 on Monday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nB of A Securities raised Eldorado Gold Corp (NYSE:EGO) price target from $32 to $54. B of A Securities analyst Lawson Winder upgraded the stock from Underperform to Buy. Eldorado Gold shares closed at $42.37 on Monday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nPiper Sandler boosted Metlife Inc (NYSE:MET) price target from $99 to $110. Piper Sandler analyst Paul Newsome upgraded the stock from Neutral to Overweight. Metlife shares closed at $96.64 on Monday. See how other analysts view this stock.\n\nConsidering buying META stock? Here’s what analysts think:\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'78a91ded1222c2190bb00d6a5e59065158eb784e','2026-09-22 13:12:46','2026-09-22 13:33:14.267772',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 13:12:46');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(561,'alpaca:61919107','benzinga','2026-09-22 13:08:52','Strategy Swings From $10B Loss to $8B Profit as Bitcoin Hits $85K','Strategy swings from a $10 billion Bitcoin loss to an $8 billion profit as BTC hits $85,000 and MSTR gains 48% in a month.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61919107/strategy-swings-from-10b-loss-to-8b-profit-as-bitcoin-hits-85k','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 13:33:22.090448','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Significant change in strategy profit associated with Bitcoin''s price increase.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 13:33:14.350817','61919107',replace('Strategy (NASDAQ:MSTR) swung from a $10 billion unrealized loss to an $8 billion unrealized profit in just weeks, as Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) hit $85,000.\n\nWhat Triggered the Swing\n\nBull Theory posted on X Monday that the reversal happened fast: Bitcoin’s climb off the summer lows directly repriced Strategy’s massive holdings, turning paper losses into paper gains almost overnight.\n\nWidely-followed market commentator Scott Melker posted on X that Bitcoin sits down 4% on the year while MSTR is up 8%. \n\n“A few months ago, Strategy ‘had to go to 0.’ Remember?” Melker wrote.\n\nAdding to the picture, Cointelegraph reported Sunday that MSTR was the Nasdaq-100’s top performer over the past month, surging 48%.\n\nWhy the Company Keeps Adding Bitcoin\n\nAs Benzinga reported Monday, Strategy bought 950 Bitcoin for $75.7 million between Sept. 14 and Sept. 20 at an average price of $79,670 per coin. \n\nThat purchase ended nearly a month-long buying pause and brought total holdings to 846,000 BTC, worth roughly $71.9 billion and equal to more than 4% of Bitcoin’s 21 million supply cap. \n\nExecutive Chairman Michael Saylor‘s “A little more orange” post on X Sunday preceded the announcement, a pattern that has historically signaled fresh purchases.\n\nThe company also repurchased 1.77 million STRC preferred shares for around $174 million during the same stretch, continuing efforts to stabilize the preferred stock near par value while resuming Bitcoin accumulation.\n\nWhy the Treasury Narrative Could Be Coming Back\n\nScott Melker broke down the mechanics, noting Strategy “did not do any financial wizardry this week” to buy Bitcoin, instead tapping its own USD reserve to fund the $75.7 million purchase and $174 million of STRC buybacks as the preferred stock climbed near par. \n\nMeanwhile, Strive (NASDAQ:ASST) is running the older playbook, selling shares to fund immediate Bitcoin buys. \n\nMelker argued that much higher Bitcoin prices could be the single biggest cure for the battered treasury sector.\n\nMSTR Price Analysis: Technical Analysis\n\nMSTR surged 9.47% Monday, breaking decisively above both the 200-day EMA at $152.28 and the multi-month descending trendline that capped every rally since May. \n\nTuesday’s premarket trades at $167.77, down roughly 0.4% from Monday’s close in what looks like a healthy cooldown rather than distribution.\n\nThe EMA structure has flipped constructive, with the 20-day EMA trending above both the 50-day and 100-day, confirming the shift out of the summer downtrend. \n\nRSI Divergence Indicator reads 70.90, firmly overbought and echoing the same zone that preceded May’s bearish divergence, warranting caution on chasing entries here.\n\nKey levels for MSTR:\n\n$168.50 — Monday’s high, now resistance-turned-pivot on any retest\n\n$152 — 200-day EMA, key support below\n\nRead Also:\n\nScott Bessent Says US, China to Meet in 2 Months on AI Threats: ‘We Want to Start Discussing Protocols’\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'1a890f93ee78ad037ae5f3fd7438fb161d007f6a','2026-09-22 13:08:52','2026-09-22 13:33:14.267772',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 13:08:52');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(562,'alpaca:61918920','benzinga','2026-09-22 13:06:07','Top Analyst Says There’s 80% Chance Could Put Tesla and SpaceX ‘Under One Hood’ by 2027 — ‘Golden Goose’ Could Create the ‘Biggest Company in the World’','Tech analyst Dan Ives predicts an 80% chance Tesla and SpaceX will merge by late 2027 to build the &#34;golden goose&#34; of physical AI.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61918920/top-analyst-says-theres-80-chance-could-put-tesla-and-spacex-under-one-hood-by-2027-golden-goose-could-create-the-biggest-company-in-the','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 13:33:23.307899','rumour','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'It presents a speculation about a potential future merger.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 13:33:14.354971','61918920',replace('Technology analyst Dan Ives predicts a high probability of around 80% that Tesla Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) and Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) will combine operations by late 2027 to dominate the autonomous technology sector.\n\nThe ‘Golden Goose’ of Tech\n\nDuring a live recording of The Compound and Friends podcast from Sept. 18, Ives detailed his thesis on the next phase of artificial intelligence investments. Asked by host Josh Brown how investors can capitalize on the autonomous future, Ives highlighted Elon Musk’s companies.\n\nIves, a partner and senior managing director at Yorkville Ives and Co., noted that the real investment opportunity lies in systems interacting with the physical world.\n\n“Physical AI to me is the golden goose,” Ives stated. “Like autonomous, true autonomous technology, I believe will be one of the biggest technology innovations that we ever see.”\n\nRead Also:\n\nSpaceX-Tesla Merger: Ron Baron Told Elon Musk ''Whatever You Decide… Is What I''m Going to Support''\n\nThe Merger Vision\n\nTo capture this expanding market, Ives anticipates an imminent corporate consolidation. He expects the electric vehicle manufacturer and the space exploration firm to unite their artificial intelligence initiatives.\n\n“It’s my view at some point by the end of next year those companies merge,” Ives said.\n\nHe emphasized that the integration would share more than just information.\n\n“Obviously that’s going to be the big question, but for us that’s the golden vision that Tesla and SpaceX are under one hood,” Ives stated. “Not just from a data perspective but in terms of all the AI technology that they’re building, that ultimately becomes one company, the biggest company in the world.”\n\nIves concluded, “I view it, like we’ve said, it’s over an 80% chance by the end of next year that Tesla and SpaceX ultimately merge.”\n\nMacroeconomic Impact\n\nFundstrat Capital co-founder Tom Lee echoed the significance of autonomous technologies during the panel. Lee stated that if robots act as a new productive unit rather than merely replacing human labor, they could act as “economic consumers and taxpaying units,” potentially allowing the broader economy to grow without triggering inflation.\n\nHow Has TSLA Performed in 2026?\n\nPrice Action: At the last check, the TSLA stock was trading 0.82% higher in Tuesday’s premarket. It was down 11.92% over the last year, 16.55% year-to-date, and 3.43% higher over the last month. The stock closed 3.03% higher at $375.30 on Monday.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that TSLA maintains a weak price trend in the medium and long terms but a strong trend in the short term, with a moderate growth score.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBig Tech’s AI Debt Spree Hits a Wall as Bond Investors Demand Higher Yields From Alphabet, Meta and Nvidia\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'f278ceaf7e34cddb4d3d628b2ab1775615e475b4','2026-09-22 13:06:07','2026-09-22 13:33:14.267772',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 13:06:08');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(563,'alpaca:61918726','benzinga','2026-09-22 13:01:24','QUICK SPARK: Wall Street Is Moving Nvidia Onto Crypto Rails. 24/7 Trading Is Next','Tokenized equities and perpetuals are putting Nvidia and other stocks onto crypto-style rails with 24/7 access, fractional trading and leverage.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61918726/nvidia-crypto-trading-rails','["AAPL", "MSFT", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 13:33:24.734816','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'This news introduces a new trading mechanism but does not confirm any immediate impact on Nvidia''s price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "MSFT": 498.48, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 13:33:14.359497','61918726',replace('Nvidia Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) may be a Wall Street stock, but the way investors trade it, is starting to look increasingly like crypto. \n\nTokenized equities and equity perpetuals are putting traditional names onto digital trading rails. This is creating a market that never has to wait for the opening bell.\n\nThe Trading Rail Changes\n\nCoinMarketCap’s Alice Liu told Benzinga in an exclusive email interview that the convergence between traditional equities and crypto is happening at the "distribution layer, not the asset layer." The company’s trending board recently featured tokenized Nvidia alongside tokenized Nasdaq-100, Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL), Micron Technology, Inc. (NASDAQ:MU), Microsoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT) and Alphabet Inc (NASDAQ:GOOGL) (NASDAQ:GOOG) products.\n\nThe category has expanded rapidly. CoinMarketCap tracks 1,851 tokenized-stock instruments with roughly $2.3 billion in combined market capitalization, and about $2 billion in daily trading volume. \n\nTokenized stocks were turning over roughly 89% of their market cap daily. That’s far above the turnover seen in Bitcoin, memes or AI tokens.\n\nEquity perpetuals are expanding, too. Their share of Hyperliquid’s perpetual volume rose from about 2% at the start of the year to roughly half.\n\nFor investors, the bigger shift is not simply that Nvidia can be tokenized. It is that stocks are gaining crypto-style rails — 24/7 access, fractional trading and leverage — potentially reshaping how equities are traded.\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'433396c49338b5fa3949cce866875b942aa1b68d','2026-09-22 13:01:24','2026-09-22 13:33:14.267772',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 13:01:24');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(564,'alpaca:61918037','benzinga','2026-09-22 12:45:08','Buying SOFI Is Like Buying ''AMD or Nvidia'' at the Bottom: Strategists Highlight Bold Bull Case for SoFi Technologies','Strategists compare buying SoFi stock to &#39;Nvidia at the bottom,&#39; citing 30% revenue growth, a 40% EPS target, and strong banking moats.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61918037/buying-sofi-is-like-buying-amd-or-nvidia-at-the-bottom-strategists-highlight-bold-bull-case-for-sofi-technologies','["AMD", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 13:33:25.829083','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'The headline presents a bullish comparison but remains speculative.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 13:33:14.375233','61918037',replace('On the latest episode of “The Deep End” podcast, co-host Brad Freeman, co-host Shay Boloor, and Future Investing creator Tannor Manson outlined a bullish case for SoFi Technologies Inc. (NASDAQ:SOFI).\n\nMarket Mispricing and the Nvidia Comparison\n\nAddressing the stock’s recent market underperformance, Freeman stated that purchasing SoFi stock at current valuation levels “is like buying Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) or Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) at the depths of their” cyclical bottoms.\n\nValuation Disconnect and Growth Outlook\n\nBoloor stated that SoFi is currently valued like a tech company while trading like a lender, leaving the stock vulnerable to daily swings in interest rates, credit concerns, and lending sentiment.\n\nManson stated that SoFi management functions as a “compulsive sandbagger” regarding financial guidance, despite management projecting 30% revenue growth and 40% earnings per share growth over the next three years.\n\nFreeman added that market sentiment around SoFi has turned overly negative, arguing that most bad news is already priced into the stock.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Hit $85,000 Today — SoFi Stock Barely Moved\n\nCredit Metrics and Cost Advantages\n\nManson noted that SoFi has expanded to 16 million members and over $45 billion in deposits, with revenue growing at approximately 30%. Freeman cited 90-day delinquency rates of 0.40% and an annualized charge-off ratio of 3.7% as evidence of credit book resilience.\n\nFreeman also stated that SoFi operates with a structural cost advantage over legacy financial institutions because it avoids branch real estate expenses and utilizes its bank charter to fund loans via lower-cost deposits rather than expensive warehouse debt.\n\nBalance Sheet Structure and Capital Strategy\n\nAddressing historical capital raises, Freeman stated that balance sheet optimizations allowed SoFi to eliminate high-interest debt and substitute it with low-cost deposit funding.\n\nManson explained that SoFi’s loan platform business generates fee-based revenue by originating loans for third-party institutional capital without consuming SoFi’s balance sheet capacity.\n\nAll three analysts confirmed they hold long positions in SoFi stock, with Boloor noting he remains invested despite being down 20% on his position.\n\nHow Has SOFI Performed in 2026?\n\nPrice Action: At the last check, the SOFI stock rose about 5.95% to $17.98 premarket on Tuesday. It was down about 43% over the last year, and 35.18% year-to-date.\n\nBenzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings indicate that SOFI maintains a weak price trend in the short, medium, and long terms, with a poor growth score.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSoFi Stock Offers an ‘Attractive Entry Point’: Analyst\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'2e0378587aa3ef32d55d5c5b48d74afff5b6d7e5','2026-09-22 12:45:08','2026-09-22 13:33:14.267772',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 12:45:08');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(565,'alpaca:61917745','benzinga','2026-09-22 12:37:48','Elon Musk''s X Launches Cashtag Trading Program With Coinbase, Kraken, Gemini for Bitcoin, Stocks','X launched a Cashtag Partner Program, linking stock and crypto discussions to brokers such as Coinbase, Kraken, and Interactive Brokers.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61917745/elon-musk-x-launches-cashtag-trading-program-with-coinbase-kraken-gemini-for-bitcoin-stocks','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 13:33:27.300610','partnership','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'The partnership could increase trading activity and user engagement.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 13:33:14.379753','61917745',replace('Elon Musk‘s X just added a new “Trade” option to support the so-called Cashtag Partner Program. \n\nThe social media platform, previously known as Twitter, now lets users move directly from stock and cryptocurrency conversations to executing trades through participating brokerages, such as Interactive Brokers (NASDAQ:IBKR), Moomoo, Gemini, Kraken and Coinbase (NASDAQ:COIN).\n\nUnder the new program, users tapping a supported Cashtag can view the asset’s price information and conversation on X before selecting “Trade” to continue to a participating brokerage.\n\nUsers can then log into an existing brokerage account or create a new one and complete the transaction directly through the broker’s mobile app or website.\n\n"Cashtags close the gap between a ticker on the timeline and the market itself," Mridul Singhai, Product Engineering Lead at X, said.\n\nX Links Financial Conversation With Trading\n\nThe feature positions Cashtags as a bridge between discovering an asset on X and acting on that information through a brokerage.\n\nMonique Pintarelli, Head of Global Advertising at SpaceXAI, said the partnerships are designed to connect financial conversations with real-time action.\n\n"With our Cashtag partners, we’re connecting the financial conversation to action," Pintarelli said.\n\nThe program covers both stocks and cryptocurrencies like Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC), with X saying the feature makes it easier for traders and investors to move from market discussions and live charts to participating trading platforms.\n\nRead Also:\n\nIs Bitcoin Quantum-Proof? Yes and No, VanEck''s Matthew Sigel Says\n\nX History\n\nMusk co-founded X.com in 1999 and merged it with Confinity in 2000. That year, the company replaced him as CEO with Peter Thiel. Confinity became PayPal in 2001. \n\nEBay Inc. (NASDAQ:EBAY) acquired PayPal in 2002 for $1.5 billion in stock, with Musk as its largest shareholder.\n\nIn 2017, Musk bought back the X.com domain from PayPal, saying it had "great sentimental value" to him. At the time, he said he had no plans for it.\n\nIn 2022, Musk purchased Twitter and, by 2023, renamed it X.\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'d75918722940a33647286d9096a993fecd2e00b6','2026-09-22 12:37:48','2026-09-22 13:33:14.267772',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 12:37:48');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(566,'alpaca:61917672','benzinga','2026-09-22 12:35:26','Cardano Joins Solana, XRP in AI Payments Race as ADA Surges 8%','Cardano jumps 8% after joining Coinbase’s x402 payment standard, enabling AI agents to pay for online services as ADA targets $0.2563.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61917672/cardano-joins-solana-xrp-in-ai-payments-race-as-ada-surges-8','["ADA/USD", "AMZN", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','stocks','2026-09-22 13:33:28.866408','product','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'Cardano''s integration into a new payment standard is confirmed and positively affecting its price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"ADA/USD": 0.20462, "AMZN": 251.18, "SOL/USD": 101.29, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 13:33:14.383215','61917672',replace('Cardano (CRYPTO: ADA) surges 8% over the past 24 hours, joining the official x402 software kit that gives AI agents a direct rail to pay for services in ADA.\n\nWhat x402 Actually Does\n\nCoinDesk reported Tuesday that x402 turns the web’s largely unused “402 Payment Required” response into a built-in checkout for internet requests. \n\nA service sends its price and payment instructions, an AI agent signs the payment, and the transaction unlocks the requested data or computing power automatically. \n\nThat means an agent building a report could buy a single dataset the moment it needs one, without a person opening an account or paying for a monthly subscription.\n\nCoinbase (NASDAQ:COIN) created x402 in 2025 before handing it to a Linux Foundation-backed organization whose members include Visa (NYSE:V), Mastercard (NYSE:MA), Stripe, Alphabet’s (NASDAQ:GOOGL) Google, and Amazon’s (NASDAQ:AMZN) Web Services. \n\nMeanwhile, Solana (CRYPTO: SOL) and the XRP (CRYPTO: XRP) Ledger already support the standard, alongside several Ethereum-compatible networks.\n\nHow Cardano’s Integration Works\n\nCardano Foundation engineers built the client and server software needed to request and verify payments after the specification got accepted in June. Here’s where things stand:\n\nLanguage support: TypeScript ships first, Python comes next\n\nTesting status: Completed a real transaction on Cardano’s pre-production network, not yet live on mainnet\n\nWhat this means: Developers can start integrating now, though agents aren’t yet paying for commercial services with ADA at scale\n\nCardano Foundation posted on X Monday that any app or AI agent can pay for an API call in ADA or any Cardano native token over a standard web request, with no account, API key, or checkout page required. \n\n“Every service already on x402 can switch Cardano on,” the foundation wrote. “The agent economy just got a Cardano rail.”\n\nWhy Hoskinson Sees This as Bigger Than Payments\n\nWidely-followed crypto analyst Wendy O posted on X that Cardano founder Charles Hoskinson predicts crypto will “eat” AI within five to ten years. \n\nHis reasoning: crypto solves payments, alignment, and data provenance problems that centralized AI systems cannot handle on their own.\n\nADA Price Prediction: Key Levels to Watch\n\nADA trades at $0.2477 Tuesday, up 1% and extending Monday’s sharp 7% surge that pushed price through the 0.618 Fibonacci retracement at $0.2310 and out of its recent consolidation range. \n\nThe EMA stack sits fully bullish, with the 20-day EMA above the 50-day and 100-day, while the Supertrend flipped green at $0.20.\n\nKey levels for ADA:\n\n$0.2563 — 0.786 Fib, next resistance overhead\n\n$0.2310 — 0.618 Fib retest, immediate support\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'0dc8c6389806b582395df155184f1574d730612d','2026-09-22 12:35:26','2026-09-22 13:33:14.267772',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 12:35:27');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(567,'alpaca:61922028','benzinga','2026-09-22 14:11:02','Tesla’s Cybercab Strategy Hinges on One Giant, Unanswered Question','Tesla is courting Cybercab fleet buyers, but one key detail remains unclear: how revenue from each robotaxi ride will be split.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/09/61922028/tesla-cybercab-strategy-robotaxi-revenue-split-question','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 14:33:39.636823','other','neutral',2,2,'weeks',1,'The uncertainty around revenue splits may impact investor sentiment but is ultimately speculative.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 14:33:35.350128','61922028',replace('Tesla Inc (NASDAQ:TSLA) is finally opening the door for outside businesses to buy Cybercabs. But there is one number investors still cannot see: Tesla’s cut of each robotaxi ride. The company has laid out the hardware, the network and the ambition. \n\nWhat it has not disclosed is the revenue split that could determine whether Cybercab becomes a car business, a software business or something closer to Uber Technologies, Inc. (NYSE:UBER).\n\nTesla Wants Fleet Buyers\n\nTesla’s September interest form asks businesses to consider "Cybercab fleet vehicle purchasing" as it looks to expand its Robotaxi network. The company is also soliciting interest in mobility hubs and infrastructure, signaling that Tesla does not necessarily want to finance, park and operate every Cybercab itself.\n\nThat matters because robotaxi scale requires more than manufacturing cars. Someone has to provide the capital, charging, parking, cleaning and maintenance needed to keep thousands of autonomous vehicles on the road. Axios reported that Tesla’s push could shift some of that burden toward entrepreneurs and fleet operators.\n\nThe potential economics are why this model is getting investor attention. ARK Invest estimates robotaxis could eventually be priced as low as 25 cents per mile, roughly one-tenth the cost of human-driven ride-hail. That is a forecast, not a Tesla commitment, but it illustrates the scale of the potential cost advantage.\n\nThe unanswered question is what happens to that 25 cents.\n\nWho Gets the Robotaxi Dollar?\n\nTesla has not publicly disclosed the commercial terms for third-party Cybercab owners. Its own support page confirms that commercial fleet buyers can express interest, but does not spell out a purchase price, revenue-sharing arrangement or owner economics.\n\nThat missing split is more important than it looks.\n\nIf outside operators finance the vehicles while Tesla controls the software, booking, pricing and dispatch, Tesla could potentially collect revenue without carrying the full capital burden of the fleet. That would give the company an unusual combination: automaker economics when the Cybercab is sold and platform economics every time it moves a passenger.\n\nBut the balance of that split will determine who has the incentive to keep buying more vehicles.\n\nA fleet operator needs enough revenue to cover the Cybercab, financing, insurance, charging, maintenance and downtime. Tesla needs enough of each fare to make expanding the network economically meaningful.\n\nThat is why the exact terms matter more than the headline that Tesla is selling Cybercabs.\n\nThe Investor Number To Watch\n\nThere is already evidence that Tesla wants Cybercab rides to become materially cheaper than traditional ride-hailing. ARK said initial Austin fares were roughly 50% below Uber on comparable rides, while Tesla has said Cybercab is designed specifically for its Robotaxi fleet.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla''s Cybercab Can Be 50% Cheaper Than Uber—So Why Is It Sometimes Twice as Expensive?\n\nBut cheap rides alone do not create a valuable platform.\n\nThe next disclosures investors should watch are the first major fleet buyers, the number of vehicles they commit to and—most importantly—the revenue-sharing structure Tesla offers them.\n\nIf Tesla can attract outside capital while retaining a meaningful portion of every autonomous mile, Cybercab starts looking less like another vehicle launch and more like a recurring-revenue network.\n\nThat is the number investors still do not have.\n\nWhy it Matters\n\nTesla’s Cybercab story is moving from autonomy to economics. The company has shown it can build the vehicle and is now asking others to help scale the fleet. \n\nThe next catalyst is not simply how many Cybercabs Tesla produces—it is how the money from each ride gets divided between Tesla and the people paying for the cars.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla Cybercab vs. Uber: Who Wins the Robotaxi Race?\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'f74d096b7138a53d105376d96bce341358ad2a76','2026-09-22 14:11:02','2026-09-22 14:33:35.336046',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 14:11:02');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(568,'alpaca:61921031','benzinga','2026-09-22 13:55:05','Dan Ives Says Tech Stocks Are in a ''1997 Moment'' as Tom Lee Predicts: ‘Probability of a Massive Rally’ Ahead','Dan Ives and Tom Lee see a massive stock market rally ahead, citing AI spending, strong earnings and investor pessimism.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61921031/dan-ives-says-tech-stocks-are-in-a-1997-moment-as-tom-lee-predicts-probability-of-a-massive-rally-ahead','["AMZN", "MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-22 14:33:40.857646','analyst','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Analysts express predictions about market trends, which are speculative.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "MSFT": 498.48}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 14:33:35.359132','61921031',replace('Yorkville Ives founder Dan Ives and Fundstrat‘s Tom Lee predict a massive rally in the stock market, despite high pessimism and the possibility of a further Federal Reserve rate hike.\n\nIn episode 260 of The Compound and Friends podcast, published on Friday, Dan Ives likened the current market scenario to the 1997 moment, not the 1999-2000 one, indicating growth potential. \n\nIn May, Ives used the same analogy and elaborated that the current AI boom resembles 1996 more than the excesses of 1999, arguing that rising tech spending is still in its early stages with Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT), Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOG) (NASDAQ:GOOGL), and Amazon.com Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN) He believes investors are underestimating the scale of upcoming AI investment, with an estimated $3 trillion in spending over the next three years and more than $550 billion in capex already underway.\n\nMeanwhile, Tom Lee expressed that while no one welcomes a Fed tightening, the current situation could set up a bullish moment. He noted that even with high pessimism, robust earnings could trigger a massive rally.\n\nLee also pointed out that people often overlook the fact that companies have adapted to various crises by utilizing technology and cutting costs. This year, earnings have increased by 25%, while the market has only risen by 10%, making the market cheaper, he added.\n\nHe emphasized that investors are entrusting their money to CEOs who have proven their worth by constantly adapting and cutting costs, even in crisis mode.\n\n“I think the probability of a massive rally starting tomorrow is really high,” Lee said.\n\nRead Also:\n\nGoldman Sachs Strategist Sees AI Boom Outpacing Bonds as Higher Rates Raise Market Risks: ''Long compute…Long Neoclouds…Long Data Centers''\n\nMarket Outlook Turns Cautious\n\nThese predictions come amid mixed market sentiment. Universa Investments founder Mark Spitznagel had earlier stated that the S&P; 500 will "easily" top 8,000 in one final euphoric rally before plunging 80%. Spitznagel attributes the bubble to years of near-zero interest rates and expects higher borrowing costs to eventually trigger a downturn. He predicts the Fed will respond with renewed quantitative easing, causing its balance sheet to expand sharply and potentially reigniting inflation.\n\nFurthermore, Ed Yardeni, President of Yardeni Research, revised his year-end S&P; 500 target downwards, cautioning investors to be wary in the face of increasing rates. He also slashed his S&P; 500 year-end target from 8,400 to 7,900.\n\nPrice Action: Year-to-date, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (ARCA: SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ: QQQ) have surged 13.58% and about 21%, respectively, as per Benzinga Pro.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nJamie Dimon Says AI Spending Could Hit $1 Trillion in 2027 But JPMorgan CEO Warns it Could Add ''Little Bit'' to Inflation: ''That’s Like 1% Increase to GDP…''\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'8213f06c169dd65ca7d23789cbd0817cb289faf6','2026-09-22 13:55:05','2026-09-22 14:33:35.336046',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 13:55:05');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(569,'alpaca:61920390','benzinga','2026-09-22 13:40:49','Forget Dogecoin: PEPE Is Outrunning Bitcoin and XRP—Is FLOKI Next?','Pepe jumps 20% to lead crypto gains as traders target $0.00001 and watch Floki test a key breakout level at its 200-day EMA.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61920390/forget-dogecoin-pepe-is-outrunning-bitcoin-and-xrp-is-floki-next','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "PEPE/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 14:33:42.722140','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'Speculative commentary on crypto trends without confirmed events.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "PEPE/USD": 3.625e-06, "SOL/USD": 101.29, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 14:33:35.368336','61920390',replace('Pepe (CRYPTO: PEPE) leads all crypto with a 20% gain over 24 hours, outpacing Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) and XRP (CRYPTO: XRP), as traders watch whether Floki (CRYPTO: FLOKI) breaks out next.\n\nWhy PEPE Is Leading the Pack\n\nAnalyst Lana Valentis posted on X that PEPE is forming an inverse head and shoulders pattern on the daily chart, with breakout conditions aligning alongside real momentum. \n\nThe move puts PEPE well ahead of Dogecoin (CRYPTO: DOGE), which is up 6% over the same 24-hour stretch as capital rotates toward newer names. \n\nMoreover, she pointed to $40 million in trading volume on Solana (CRYPTO: SOL) in a single day and a holder count approaching 600,000 as evidence the crowd is arriving. \n\nHer target levels for the breakout run from $0.00000455 up to $0.00001.\n\nWhy FLOKI Could Be Next\n\nAnalyst Prof. Clifton posted on X Monday that FLOKI is testing a falling wedge pattern on the weekly timeframe, and a decisive break higher with strong momentum could trigger a massive rally in the coming days.\n\nFLOKI carries more infrastructure than most meme tokens. It powers the Valhalla gaming mainnet as in-game currency, and the project relaunched its redesigned Valhalla website on Sept. 16, amplified directly by the official FLOKI account. \n\nThe token also has a European FLOKI ETP from Valor that gives regulated investors exposure, a past Robinhood (NASDAQ:HOOD) listing that pushed its market cap above $1 billion at the cycle peak, and a debit card in Europe that adds real-world utility beyond the meme narrative. \n\nNone of those catalysts are driving this week’s move directly, but they explain why investors remain comfortable taking risk on a token still roughly 91% below its all-time high.\n\nFLOKI Price Prediction: Key Levels to Watch\n\nFLOKI trades flat on Tuesday after surging 10% the previous day and pushing directly into the 200-day EMA at $0.0000293, the key resistance separating this bounce from a genuine trend reversal. \n\nMeanwhile, the EMA stack has turned bullish, with the 20-day, 50-day, and 100-day EMAs now aligned above each other after months of downtrend. \n\nKey levels for FLOKI:\n\n$0.0000293 — 200-day EMA, breakout trigger for trend reversal\n\n$0.0000256 — 20-day EMA, immediate support\n\n$0.0000246 to $0.0000248 — deeper support zone\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin ETFs Add $999 Million In Best Day Since October 2025: What''s Going On?\n\nPhoto: Koshiro K on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'80950c01efc760edef117247f075feb55c2ae982','2026-09-22 13:40:49','2026-09-22 14:33:35.336046',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 13:40:49');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(570,'alpaca:61919954','benzinga','2026-09-22 13:36:24','Sovereign AI Isn’t so Sovereign: Meta’s Llama Powers 38% of Adapted Models','Counterpoint Research finds Meta&#39;s Llama drives 38% of adapted sovereign AI models worldwide, topping rivals like Qwen and Mistral.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61919954/sovereign-ai-isnt-so-sovereign-metas-llama-powers-38-of-adapted-models','["META", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 14:33:44.705273','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Report highlights market share of Meta''s Llama in AI models.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 14:33:35.371188','61919954',replace('Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) has emerged as the leading foundation for sovereign artificial intelligence models built on foreign open-source technology, according to new research from Counterpoint Research.Meta’s Llama Leads Sovereign AI ModelsCounterpoint found that 56% of the sovereign large language models it tracks are adapted models, meaning they are fine-tuned versions of existing open-source models. The remaining 44% are foundational models trained on native data.Meta’s Llama accounts for 38% of adapted sovereign LLMs, making it the most widely used foreign base-model family. Alibaba Group Holding Ltd. (NYSE:BABA)-backed Qwen follows with a 20% share, while France’s Mistral holds 19%.Counterpoint evaluated more than 170 models across more than 55 countries as part of its H1 2026 Sovereign AI LLM Index. The firm said Llama was the dominant base model across every region covered by the research.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nAnalyst Sees Push Toward Greater AI AutonomyCounterpoint Research Director Marc Einstein said sovereign AI ultimately centers on control and strategic autonomy, but that independence exists on a spectrum.“A slight majority of ‘sovereign’ LLMs are fine-tuned on open-source foreign bases, so true autonomy is still the exception,” Einstein said. He added that countries are increasingly moving toward foundational models built from scratch using domestic data.Counterpoint said Qwen is gaining adoption across Central and Eastern Europe, Asia-Pacific and Africa, helped by its multilingual capabilities. Mistral, meanwhile, has gained traction in Europe, Asia-Pacific and the Middle East through partnerships including Abu Dhabi-based G42.The research also points to growing use of other foundations, including Alphabet Inc.’s (NASDAQ:GOOGL) (NASDAQ:GOOG) Gemma, NVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) Nemotron and DeepSeek, as countries diversify their AI technology stacks and reduce dependence on a single provider.Photo via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nIf There’s a Problem With Google Search, There’s a Problem With Google Stock: Analyst','\n',char(10)),'0cedd36b923de6275e6c2987f6a364424bb4d711','2026-09-22 13:36:24','2026-09-22 14:33:35.336046',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 13:36:24');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(571,'alpaca:61925516','benzinga','2026-09-22 15:30:39','Why Billionaire Tim Draper Calls Apple, Meta ''Irresponsible'' for Not Holding Bitcoin','Bitcoin bull Tim Draper urges Apple, Meta and others to hold BTC as an inflation hedge, predicting $250,000 after halvings and wider adoption.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61925516/tim-draper-calls-apple-meta-irresposible-for-not-holding-bitcoin','["AAPL", "BTC/USD", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 15:33:55.025752','other','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'Tim Draper''s opinion on Bitcoin relevance for companies is speculative.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "BTC/USD": 76528.6, "META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 15:33:50.321810','61925516',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) bull and billionaire Tim Draper urged major companies including Apple (NASDAQ:AAPL) and Meta Platforms (NASDAQ:META) to hold Bitcoin on their balance sheets.\n\nHe argued that persistent government spending exposes corporate cash to inflation and higher interest rates.\n\nWhy Should Companies Hold BTC\n\nSpeaking on Bitcoin Magazine podcast on Sep.21, Draper said businesses should keep at least four weeks’ worth of Bitcoin in their corporate treasuries as protection against financial-system risks.\n\nHe singled out Apple and Meta as companies that should consider Bitcoin exposure, while pointing to SpaceX as an example of a forward-looking company holding the cryptocurrency.\n\nDraper argued continued government spending creates two potential risks:\n\npersistent inflation if interest rates remain low, or\n\nstress in the banking system if policymakers raise rates aggressively.\n\nHe sees Bitcoin as a hedge against both scenarios and said individuals should consider keeping six months’ worth of Bitcoin available.\n\nIn a move signaling deeper interest in crypto, Apple and Alphabet, Google’s parent company expressed interest to hire cryptocurrency developers and other digital asset specialists.\n\nCould Bitcoin Hit $250,000 After The Halving?\n\nDraper reiterated his long-standing $250,000 Bitcoin target, with the next halving central to his thesis.\n\nHe compared Bitcoin’s declining issuance to a sharp reduction in commodity production, arguing lower new supply could support higher prices.\n\nDraper also expects Bitcoin’s role to eventually expand beyond a store of value.\n\nHe predicted another two halving cycles may be needed before Bitcoin becomes widely used for everyday transactions, estimating broader retail adoption could arrive in roughly five years.\n\nThe venture capitalist envisions businesses eventually raising capital, paying employees and suppliers and conducting investments entirely in Bitcoin.\n\nSuch an economy could reduce reliance on traditional accounting, auditing and financial intermediaries because transactions would be recorded directly on the blockchain, he said.\n\nDraper sees Bitcoin and AI driving a broader shift toward decentralized systems, challenging traditional finance and other established industries.\n\nHis venture firm, Draper Associates, has made roughly 50 BTC-related investments and continues backing Bitcoin companies alongside AI, space, biotech, transportation and education companies.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Just Hit a Seven-Month High. The Analyst Calling the Bottom Expects a Pullback','\n',char(10)),'a278faa5777b4cc067fc4a42de9166e61be5f48d','2026-09-22 15:30:39','2026-09-22 15:33:50.315387',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 15:30:39');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(572,'alpaca:61925458','benzinga','2026-09-22 15:29:33','What Is Going on With Nebius Stock on Tuesday?','Nebius stock outperforms as reports of an upcoming 20% price hike on Nvidia GPU cloud capacity highlight soaring demand and pricing power.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61925458/what-is-going-on-with-nebius-stock-on-tuesday','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 15:33:56.536061','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Reports indicate increased demand for Nvidia GPUs potentially benefiting Nebius.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 15:33:50.324947','61925458',replace('Nebius Group N.V. (NASDAQ:NBIS) stock climbed about 5% Tuesday as investors focused on reports of another GPU cloud price increase, helping the stock outperform the broader technology sector.\n\nThe Technology sector gained 0.2%, while the S&P; 500 rose 0.1% and the Nasdaq advanced 0.47%.\n\nNebius Reportedly Plans Another GPU Price Increase\n\nNebius is reportedly preparing to raise GPU cloud prices by roughly 20% beginning Oct. 1, pointing to tight AI computing capacity and continued pricing power.\n\nThe reported increases cover several Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) GPU models, including the H100, H200, B200 and B300.\n\nThe H100 price is expected to rise to $4.50 from $3.85, while the H200 rate could increase to $5.40 from $4.50.\n\nNebius also outpaced the broader market Tuesday. The Russell 2000 gained 1.05%, while seven of 11 sectors traded higher.\n\nNBIS Maintains Strong Technical Trend\n\nNebius traded 10.8% above its 20-day simple moving average of $219.67 and 50.2% above its 200-day SMA of $162.11.\n\nThe 20-day SMA remains above the 50-day average, while the 50-day SMA sits above the 200-day average, maintaining a bullish longer-term setup.\n\nNebius Carries Heavy ETF Exposure\n\nNBIS represents 50.91% of the Leverage Shares 2X Long NBIS Daily ETF (NASDAQ:NBIG).\n\nSignificant inflows or outflows from the fund can translate into buying or selling of Nebius shares.\n\nPrice Action\n\nNBIS Stock Price Activity: Nebius Group shares were up 5.03% at $244.50 at the time of publication on Tuesday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'5e781ef439d4e85b66e0a014bfebffd865364170','2026-09-22 15:29:33','2026-09-22 15:33:50.315387',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 15:29:33');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(573,'alpaca:61925313','benzinga','2026-09-22 15:23:56','Alibaba Debuts AI Chip, Challenges Nvidia With Triple Processing Power','Alibaba stock climbs as the tech giant debuts its Zhenwu V900 AI chip and plans 20 gigawatts of global data center capacity.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61925313/alibaba-debuts-ai-chip-nvidia-claims-triple-processing-power','["META", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 15:33:57.509197','product','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Alibaba''s AI chip launch could positively impact investor sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 15:33:50.327683','61925313',replace('Alibaba Group Holding Limited (NYSE:BABA) stock rose Tuesday as investors weighed the company’s new AI chip and aggressive cloud infrastructure expansion plans.\n\nAt Alibaba Cloud’s Apsara Conference, the company introduced the Zhenwu V900, which it describes as China’s most powerful AI chip.\n\nThe company said the V900 delivers three times the computing power of its current M890 chip and can scale to clusters of as many as 500,000 chips. The company expects production to begin in the first quarter of 2027.\n\nNo international benchmark is available for the V900. CNBC noted that technology analysts in China have compared Alibaba’s existing M890 with NVIDIA Corp.’s (NASDAQ:NVDA) H200.\n\nAlibaba Targets 20 Gigawatts Of Data Center Capacity\n\nAlibaba plans to expand its global data center capacity to more than 20 gigawatts by 2032 as it responds to rising AI demand.\n\nThe company has committed $53 billion over three years to its broader AI expansion.\n\nAlibaba also previewed new AI models that it says will be more powerful and use between 5 trillion and 10 trillion parameters.\n\nTencent Steps Up China’s AI Competition\n\nTencent Holding Ltd. (OTC:TCEHY) is also increasing its AI efforts, introducing a new image model that it plans to integrate across its products.\n\nYoon said Tencent hopes the technology will allow AI to perform a wider range of tasks within its WeChat platform, drawing comparisons with Meta Platforms Inc.’s (NASDAQ:META) Muse AI.\n\nChinese technology companies remain largely focused on their domestic market, but Yoon said Alibaba is increasingly emphasizing global ambitions across AI infrastructure and cloud services.\n\nChinese leaders are also balancing rapid AI development with concerns about safety, political control and potential job disruption as companies including Alibaba and Tencent push to remain competitive.\n\nAlibaba Carries Significant ETF Exposure\n\nAlibaba represents 1.97% of the iShares MSCI Emerging Markets ETF (NYSE:EEM), 2.52% of the Schwab Emerging Markets Equity ETF (NYSE:SCHE) and 2.06% of the Baron Emerging Markets Select ETF (NYSE:BCEM).\n\nSignificant inflows or outflows from these funds can translate into buying or selling of Alibaba shares.\n\nPrice Action\n\nBABA Stock Price Activity: Alibaba Gr Hldgs shares were up 0.8% at $116.64 at last check on Tuesday, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAlibaba''s AI Shopping Bet Could Change How You Buy Online Forever\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'b72a2c50012b1f3cafbd6d71743f27c2d856d3b8','2026-09-22 15:23:56','2026-09-22 15:33:50.315387',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 15:23:56');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(574,'alpaca:61924135','benzinga','2026-09-22 14:59:21','Meta vs. Amazon: The Battle to Own E-Commerce’s ''Invisible Layer''','Meta and Amazon are entering a bigger battle over AI agents, e-commerce and who controls the transaction layer between consumers &amp; retailers.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/09/61924135/meta-amazon-ai-commerce','["AMZN", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 15:33:59.092826','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'Coverage of competitive developments in e-commerce and AI.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 15:33:50.336383','61924135',replace('The next battle in e-commerce may not be over who owns the biggest online store. It could be over who controls the AI agent deciding what consumers buy, where they buy it and how the transaction gets completed. \n\nJPMorgan’s Doug Anmuth sees that shift creating a potentially new revenue stream for Meta Platforms, Inc. (NASDAQ:META) — but also a new battleground with Amazon.com Inc (NASDAQ:AMZN) and other platforms.\n\nThe Agent Becomes the Middleman\n\nMeta’s Muse is being built to do more than answer questions. JPMorgan says early use cases already span shopping, restaurant reservations, travel planning and other multi-step tasks, while Meta has added Shop Pay for agentic checkout and opened Muse connectors to developers.\n\nThat matters because the economics of the internet could change if consumers increasingly ask an agent to complete a task rather than visit individual websites themselves.\n\nAnmuth expects transactions to eventually move toward agent-to-agent interactions, with businesses deploying their own agents on Muse. Meta could then potentially monetize those transactions through commissions or a take rate — essentially collecting a fee when its AI helps make the transaction happen.\n\nThe Information adds an important wrinkle: Amazon has blocked Muse from accessing its shopping site, while Palo Alto Networks, Inc. (NASDAQ:PANW) CEO Nikesh Arora has described the episode as part of a potentially much larger battle involving the major technology and AI companies.\n\nRead Also:\n\nJD.com Defies AI Disconnect With ''Measurable Progress''\n\nWho Owns the Transaction?\n\nThat conflict points to the bigger issue for investors. If an AI agent becomes the layer between a consumer and a retailer, the retailer may still own the inventory, fulfillment and customer relationship — but the agent could influence the decision that leads to the purchase.\n\nThe Information reported that Zuckerberg has discussed Muse making money by taking a small cut of transactions. It also noted that major platforms have an incentive to protect their data and customer relationships as agents begin operating across websites and apps.\n\nThat creates a new economic negotiation. Retailers may want the sales an agent generates, but they may not want to surrender part of the economics or control over how customers reach them.\n\nThe Next Meta Revenue Engine?\n\nFor Meta, that is why Muse could eventually become more important than another consumer AI app. \n\nJPMorgan says the company has laid out a path to monetize its AI investments through consumer and business agents, as well as model API access. Anmuth also sees a potential market opportunity in the tens of trillions of dollars beyond Meta’s core advertising business.\n\nFor investors, the next signals to watch are not simply Muse downloads. They are business adoption, new connectors, agent-driven transactions and evidence that Meta can establish an economic model around those interactions. \n\nThe Amazon dispute may ultimately matter less as a one-off access fight than as an early test of whether Meta can turn Muse into the invisible layer through which commerce increasingly flows.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: Father of AGI Warns Investors May Be Mispricing Meta''s AI Moat\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'40b144cc740713f12bf02c0a6f300e66d6a0d608','2026-09-22 14:59:21','2026-09-22 15:33:50.315387',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 14:59:21');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(575,'alpaca:61924091','benzinga','2026-09-22 14:58:18','Meta Stock Runs Overbought Into Connect — Wall Street Still Targets $800+','Meta rallies nearly 20% on AI optimism ahead of its developer conference, but elevated RSI and stretched averages warn of a pullback.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61924091/meta-stock-runs-overbought-into-connect-wall-street-still-targets-800','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 15:34:00.349354','analyst','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'Analysts are providing price targets amid ongoing market speculation.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 15:33:50.339469','61924091',replace('Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) heads into its annual developer conference Wednesday with Wall Street targets rising and momentum gauges flashing caution.\n\nMETA stock is moving. See the real-time price action here. \n\nThe Run-Up\n\nShares closed Monday at $741.24, up 11.34% on volume of 48.5 million — roughly 157% above the three-month average — lifting Meta’s market value to about $1.89 trillion. \n\nThe move capped a near-20% September rally driven by early traction for Muse, Meta’s personal AI agent, plus reports of custom AI chips built with Broadcom Inc. (NASDAQ:AVGO). \n\nMuse has been the most-downloaded free iPhone app in the U.S. for three straight days, per Sensor Tower.  \n\nRead Also:\n\nGreenland Stocks Explode After Trump''s Denmark Deal — GRML Up 245%\n\nTargets Chase the Tape\n\nJefferies raised its target to $875 from $710 Tuesday, keeping a Buy. Bank of America’s Justin Post reiterated a Buy and $810 target, built on 24 times projected 2027 earnings. \n\nWells Fargo’s Ken Gawrelski lifted his Overweight target to $796 from $640 Monday, saying Meta “now has a story to tell” on AI, according to CNBC.  \n\nThe catch: Meta’s 37-analyst average target sits at $784, barely 5% above Monday’s close, with bullish outliers doing the heavy lifting. \n\nThe Technical Warning\n\nMomentum is stretched. Daily RSI-14 hit 77.8, per Benzinga Pro data, well above the 70 overbought threshold. \n\nMETA’s price has also pulled far ahead of its moving averages, trading 18.4% above the 20-day SMA, 22.9% above the 50-day SMA, and 20.1% above the 200-day SMA—classic "price stretched" behavior that often invites either consolidation or sharper pullbacks. \n\nEven so, the 20-day SMA remains above the 50-day SMA (bullish near-term structure), which is typically what trend traders want to see during strong runs.\n\nFor context, Benzinga Edge Rankings score Meta strongest on Growth (79.64) and Quality (72.4), with Value at 49.74 and Momentum at 44.31, showing a fundamentals-led profile rather than a trend-led one. \n\nSee More:\n\nTop Growth Stocks\n\nWhat to Watch\n\nMeta CEO Mark Zuckerberg speaks at 7 p.m. ET Wednesday, with a developer state of the union at 1 p.m. ET Thursday. Experts are expecting camera-free “Luna” glasses, refreshed Ray-Ban and Oakley frames, a Project Phoenix headset preview and Muse updates.\n\nThe risk is timing, not thesis. Phoenix ships in 2027, and Meta has disclosed no Muse usage figures.\n\nMETA Stock Price Activity: Meta stock was up 0.69% at $746.35 at the time of publication Tuesday, according to Benzinga Pro market data. \n\nRead Also:\n\nGameStop CEO Ryan Cohen Buys Another $26 Million of GME Stock\n\nPhoto: PJ McDonnell / Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'e2030a3bd59a0065745ff6d17b4cea5b1cc6e0f7','2026-09-22 14:58:18','2026-09-22 15:33:50.315387',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 14:58:18');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(576,'alpaca:61923434','benzinga','2026-09-22 14:42:07','Not Dogecoin or Shiba Inu: Is This Meme Coin''s 27% Rally Just Getting Started?','Dogecoin and Shiba Inu rallied as Bitcoin topped $86,000, but Pudgy Penguins led gains; bullish signals could propel PENGU toward $0.045.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61923434/not-dogecoin-or-shiba-inu-is-this-meme-coins-27-rally-just-getting-started','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "SHIB/USD"]','degen','2026-09-22 15:34:01.312501','rumour','neutral',2,2,'days',1,'Speculative commentary on price movement without confirmed data.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "SHIB/USD": 5.21e-06}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 15:33:50.347210','61923434',replace('Dogecoin (CRYPTO: DOGE) and Shiba Inu (CRYPTO: SHIB) rallied roughly 18% and 15% over the past week, respectively, as Bitcoin’s (CRYPTO: BTC) push above $86,000 fueled renewed appetite for altcoins and meme coins.\n\nPudgy Penguins (CRYPTO: PENGU) stole the spotlight with a 27% weekly gain as crypto chart analyst Ali Martinez points to multiple technical signals flashing more potential upside.\n\nIs PENGU Flashing Multiple Buy Signals?\n\nPudgy Penguins’ weekly Bollinger Bands are squeezing, noted Martinez in an X post on Sep.22 signaling declining volatility that could precede a significant price move.\n\nHe sees several indicators suggesting that move could favor bulls.\n\nThe Tom DeMark Sequential is flashing buy signals on PENGU’s weekly chart, first a nine setup and then a Combo 13.\n\nThe Parabolic SAR has also turned bullish, with its dots moving below the price.\n\nSuperTrend indicator has generated a buy signal and the last comparable weekly signal preceded a 1,156% rally, though past performance does not guarantee a similar move.\n\n"Low volatility is meeting strengthening bullish momentum," Martinez said, adding that a breakout from the current squeeze could produce a substantial move.\n\nCould PENGU Rally Toward $0.045?\n\nPENGU remains within a parallel price channel, according to Martinez.\n\nHe identified the channel’s midpoint near $0.025 as the first upside target. A breakout above that level could put the upper boundary around $0.045 in focus.\n\nThat would represent roughly 430% upside from the levels referenced in Martinez’s analysis.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nElon Musk''s X Launches Cashtag Trading Program With Coinbase, Kraken, Gemini for Bitcoin, Stocks\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'b94e31cb91a9a1076c8e31ab1c395dbfa54650e9','2026-09-22 14:42:07','2026-09-22 15:33:50.315387',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 14:42:07');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(577,'alpaca:61923311','benzinga','2026-09-22 14:39:05','Analyst Sees More Upside for Microsoft Stock Following Management Meeting','Microsoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT) shares are trading slightly lower Tuesday, pulling back modestly even as Oppenheimer reiterated an Outperform rating and raised the price target on the stock. Here&#39;s what you should know.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61923311/analyst-sees-more-upside-for-microsoft-stock-following-management-meeting','["MSFT"]','stocks','2026-09-22 15:34:02.638387','analyst','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Analyst raised price target and rating after management meeting.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"MSFT": 498.48}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 15:33:50.357223','61923311',replace('Microsoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT) shares are trading slightly lower Tuesday, pulling back modestly even as Oppenheimer reiterated an Outperform rating and raised the price target on the stock. Here’s what you should know.\n\nMicrosoft stock is trending. What’s ahead for MSFT stock?\n\nOppenheimer Raises Microsoft Price Target to $570\n\nFollowing a visit to Microsoft’s headquarters, Oppenheimer analyst Brian Schwartz bumped the price target up to $570 from a prior $515, keeping the Outperform rating in place. The analyst came away from the sit-down convinced that Microsoft can keep growing faster while still spending capital wisely.\n\nSchwartz told clients he expects both Azure and the commercial side of Microsoft 365 to keep gaining speed into fiscal 2027, driven by strong Copilot subscription revenue, additional server capacity coming online and businesses increasingly settling on Microsoft as their go-to AI provider.\n\nExecutives steered clear of specifics on how the current quarter is trending, but Schwartz described their overall demeanor as upbeat, pointing to fresh agentic features, internal fixes addressing AI capacity constraints and solid customer demand. The Oppenheimer analyst said Microsoft’s outlook for positive free cash flow next fiscal year bodes well for the company hitting or topping its targets for the upcoming quarterly report.\n\nBeginning in fiscal 2027, Azure results will fall under a newly created Agents and Infrastructure segment. Customer demand, now spreading well past the handful of frontier AI labs that once dominated it, is expected to keep outstripping available capacity through year-end.\n\nRunning his own numbers, Schwartz calculated that Azure’s constant-currency growth could land near 46% for the upcoming quarter. That figure would top guidance and likely lift Microsoft’s stock multiple, with growth potentially climbing toward 50% the quarter after. \n\nThe analyst did note that AI-related disruption and pulled-forward IT spending could weigh on Azure and Microsoft 365 growth heading into 2027 or squeeze cloud margins.\n\nMSFT Shares Slip Tuesday\n\nMSFT Price Action: Microsoft shares were down 0.76%, trading at $497.71 at the time of publication on Tuesday, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nQUICK SPARK: Wall Street Is Moving Nvidia Onto Crypto Rails. 24/7 Trading Is Next\n\nImage: Tada Images/Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'2f15acd6648345ff3f23bc87f5f1adbd26c5541e','2026-09-22 14:39:05','2026-09-22 15:33:50.315387',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 14:39:05');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(578,'alpaca:61927489','benzinga','2026-09-22 16:27:47','EXCLUSIVE: ''Institutions Are Buying Bitcoin'' — Retail Is Trading Everything Else','Institutions are concentrating crypto exposure in Bitcoin ETFs while retail traders spread across memes, AI tokens and tokenized stocks.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61927489/institutions-buy-bitcoin-retail','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 16:34:11.912409','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses market behavior without indicating any specific event affecting Bitcoin''s price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 16:34:07.420722','61927489',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO:$BTC) is becoming the institutional crypto trade. Everything around it looks increasingly like retail territory. CoinMarketCap’s latest data shows institutions piling into spot Bitcoin ETFs while retail attention and trading activity spread across meme coins, AI tokens and tokenized stocks — creating a widening divide in how different investors are accessing crypto.\n\nInstitutions Choose Bitcoin\n\n"Institutions are buying Bitcoin through ETFs. Retail is trading everything else through a phone," Alice Liu, Head of Research at CoinMarketCap, told Benzinga in an exclusive email interview.\n\nU.S. spot Bitcoin ETF assets under management climbed from about $79 billion to $102 billion over the month as of Sept. 10, a roughly $23 billion increase.\n\nBitcoin’s dominance remained near 59%, close to the top of its 12-month range, even as capital and attention elsewhere in crypto accelerated.\n\nThat suggests institutional exposure is becoming increasingly concentrated around the largest digital asset rather than spreading evenly across the broader crypto market.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: ‘The AI Tag Is Free’: Crypto Is Finally Charging for AI Hype\n\nRetail Chases the Long Tail\n\nRetail activity tells a very different story.\n\nCoinMarketCap’s trending data recently placed a two-day-old meme token ahead of Solana, while AI projects, memecoins and tokenized equities continued attracting significant attention.\n\nMemecoins represented about $28.8 billion in market capitalization and $3.5 billion in daily volume, as of Sept. 10. AI & Big Data tokens accounted for $18.5 billion and $2.9 billion in daily volume, while tokenized stocks had only $2.3 billion in market capitalization but roughly $2 billion in daily trading volume, on the same day.\n\nThat last figure is particularly striking. Tokenized stocks were turning over almost their entire market capitalization each day, compared with roughly 12% for memes and 16% for AI tokens.\n\nThe difference points to a retail market increasingly interested not only in what it trades, but how and when it can trade it.\n\nCrypto Splits in Two\n\nBitcoin’s institutionalization has not eliminated speculative activity. Instead, it may be creating a two-track market.\n\nBitcoin ETF flows provide a regulated route for larger investors seeking exposure to the asset, while retail traders can move between memes, AI tokens, tokenized stocks and leveraged products around the clock.\n\nYet broad crypto participation has not necessarily translated into a full altcoin rotation. CoinMarketCap’s Altcoin Season Index stood at 37, well below the 75 threshold for an altcoin season. Funding rates had also fallen by more than half over the preceding month, even as open interest climbed 20% to $468 billion.\n\nFor investors, the split matters because "crypto" is increasingly becoming two different trades: institutional capital is building exposure through Bitcoin, while retail activity is driving the faster-moving experiments across the rest of the market.\n\nThe next catalyst may be whether that retail activity broadens into sustained altcoin rotation — or flows back toward Bitcoin.\n\nRead Also:\n\nQUICK SPARK: Wall Street Is Moving Nvidia Onto Crypto Rails. 24/7 Trading Is Next\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'612fc5b59056b4a07313103c3fc5a50f028cac4f','2026-09-22 16:27:47','2026-09-22 16:34:07.415058',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 16:27:47');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(579,'alpaca:61927022','benzinga','2026-09-22 16:12:56','EXCLUSIVE: Small AI Model Matches GPT-4.1 at Forecasting as Olas Founding Member Says Frontier Models Face ‘Increasing Economic Pressure’','Olas says its smaller AI model matched GPT-4.1 at forecasting, raising pressure on more expensive frontier models.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61927022/small-ai-model-gpt-4-1-forecasting-olas','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 16:34:13.471060','other','neutral',3,3,'days',1,'The announcement describes a competitive development in AI forecasting technology.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 16:34:07.432756','61927022',replace('Olas unveiled a new AI model Tuesday that was trained on more than 200,000 prediction market forecasts and matched OpenAI’s GPT-4.1 in a test of its ability to predict real-world events.\n\nOlas-Predict-R1-14B achieved 75.8% accuracy across 2,628 previously unseen markets, compared with 75.4% for GPT-4.1 and 71.4% for the underlying DeepSeek model, according to benchmark materials shared with Benzinga.\n\nDavid Minarsch, CEO of Valory and founding member of Olas, told Benzinga the results suggest cheaper, specialized AI models are putting “increasing economic pressure” on the industry’s most advanced general-purpose systems.\n\n • NVIDIA stock is trading near recent highs. What should traders watch with NVDA?\n\nPrediction Markets Become AI Training Data\n\nOlas, which develops autonomous AI agents that research and trade on prediction markets, trained the model using 214,529 forecasts from 5,116 resolved markets.\n\nEach forecast eventually gets an answer, letting researchers see which predictions were right and which were too confident.\n\nMinarsch said the models were not shown existing market odds during the benchmark, meaning they could not simply copy the crowd.\n\nFine-tuning also improved the model’s Brier score by roughly 20%. The metric rewards accurate probabilities and penalizes confident mistakes.\n\n“The headline in AI has been that better performance requires bigger, more powerful general-purpose models,” Minarsch said. “Our results point to another path.”\n\nSmaller Models Pressure AI Economics\n\nMinarsch said frontier models face “increasing economic pressure from such specialized models” and may need to find new markets to maintain their growth rates.\n\nThat comes as Big Tech pours record sums into AI infrastructure. TrendForce expects the nine largest cloud providers to spend more than $886.7 billion in total capital expenditures in 2026, up roughly 90%, with AI infrastructure driving much of the increase.\n\nNVIDIA Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) sits at the center of that spending boom because larger models generally require more GPUs and data-center capacity. If smaller specialist models can handle more workloads with less computing power, that could change the economics behind some of that demand.\n\nMinarsch stopped short of saying the spending is misplaced. Olas-Predict itself builds on a model that required far more computing power to create, but he argued cheaper specialist systems can pressure closed-model economics by handling particular jobs just as well.\n\nOlas says its model can run on a single GPU and its weights are publicly available, letting developers run it themselves instead of paying a closed AI provider for each forecast.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nThomson Reuters Bets on Specialist AI\n\nThomson Reuters Corp. (NASDAQ:TRI), which sells legal, tax and financial information and software, is making a similar bet. The company invested about $40 million to build a specialist model using an open foundation model and proprietary data, saying ownership gives it greater control over performance, privacy and costs.\n\nIn an experiment requested by Benzinga, Olas-Predict gave Nvidia a 70% chance of ending 2026 as the world’s largest company by market capitalization. Polymarket traders currently put Nvidia at 78%.\n\nOlas says the model is available for download on Hugging Face, while the Olas marketplace offers pay-per-call access.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nChina Slams Brakes on Humanoid Robot IPOs After Unitree’s 55% Plunge — Tesla Optimus Faces Commercialization Test','\n',char(10)),'5ffb90a9bbf3f0590fba44344bf1c0258582999a','2026-09-22 16:12:56','2026-09-22 16:34:07.415058',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 16:12:56');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(580,'alpaca:61926156','benzinga','2026-09-22 15:50:14','SpaceX, OpenAI, Anthropic Are Making the IPO Market Look Small','SpaceX, OpenAI and Anthropic show how AI-era companies are reaching extraordinary valuations before or around entering public markets.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/ipos/26/09/61926156/spacex-openai-anthropic-ipo-market','["META", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 16:34:14.904010','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses trends in IPO valuations without announcing specific events.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7, "TSLA": 366.04}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 16:34:07.440939','61926156',replace('For decades, technology companies went public and then spent years compounding into giants. The AI era is flipping that script. Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) already entered public markets at a $2 trillion valuation, while Anthropic and OpenAI are approaching potential valuations that could push the trio above $5 trillion, noted Jason Calacanis, co-host and producer of the popular All-In Podcast.\n\nThat’s a scale that makes decades of tech IPOs look surprisingly small.\n\n • SpaceX stock is building positive momentum. What’s pushing SPCX stock higher?\n\n$5 Trillion Before The Finish Line\n\nThe comparison is almost hard to process.\n\nSpaceX began trading in June at roughly a $2 trillion valuation. Anthropic’s investors are expecting the AI company to reach a $2 trillion valuation when it goes public, while OpenAI has been discussing a new funding round at about a $1.2 trillion valuation ahead of a potential listing.\n\nTogether, that puts the three companies at more than $5 trillion based on those current or prospective valuations.\n\nNow compare that with the entire U.S. technology IPO market from 1980 through 2025.\n\nAccording to data compiled by University of Florida professor Jay Ritter and cited by the Financial Times, 3,365 technology companies that went public during that 45-year period had a combined value of $4.1 trillion when they began trading.\n\nThe comparison isn’t perfectly apples-to-apples. The historical figure is measured at IPO, while Anthropic and OpenAI’s numbers are prospective valuations. It also doesn’t adjust the older figure for inflation. But the scale is still striking.\n\nRead Also:\n\nSpaceX''s AI Push Comes Into Focus as JPMorgan Sees Nearly 80% Upside\n\nPrivate Markets Got There First\n\nThere is another important shift underneath the headline.\n\nThe biggest technology companies of the past often created enormous value after going public. Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOGL) (NASDAQ:GOOG), Tesla, Inc. (NASDAQ:TSLA) and Meta Platforms, Inc. (NASDAQ:META) are obvious examples: public investors participated as those companies expanded into some of the world’s most valuable businesses.\n\nAI companies are reaching extraordinary valuations while still private.\n\nThe Financial Times estimates that private U.S. unicorns are collectively valued at about $5.3 trillion based on their latest funding rounds. That creates a very different starting point for public investors: instead of discovering a promising company early in its public life, they may be buying into businesses that have already accumulated enormous private-market valuations.\n\nThat doesn’t mean the public-market opportunity is over. It means the starting line has moved.\n\nThe IPO Market Is Changing\n\nSpaceX has already shown that Wall Street can absorb a mega-IPO of this scale. Axios reported SpaceX’s early investor outreach helped establish a playbook that could be replicated by Anthropic and OpenAI.\n\nBut the bigger question is what happens beyond these three companies.\n\nIf AI keeps producing companies capable of reaching trillion-dollar valuations before going public, the traditional IPO pipeline could become increasingly polarized: a small number of enormous listings commanding enormous attention, alongside a much larger pool of startups that struggle to reach public markets.\n\nWhy it Matters\n\nThe headline isn’t simply that SpaceX, OpenAI and Anthropic are worth trillions. \n\nIt is that the AI boom is changing when investors get access to technology’s biggest companies. For public-market investors, the next generation of mega-cap tech may arrive much later in the growth story — and at a dramatically larger scale.\n\nRead Also:\n\nCathie Wood Calls SpaceX ‘Deep Value’ at 66x Sales\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'0eb0a1d6368a06600fe2d13bf80e6352a67f1982','2026-09-22 15:50:14','2026-09-22 16:34:07.415058',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 15:50:14');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(581,'alpaca:61926004','benzinga','2026-09-22 15:45:26','AMD Stock Beat Nvidia By 160 Points In 2026: A Historic AI Boom First','AMD stock is up 188% in 2026 while Nvidia is up 22%, a 166-point gap and AMD&#39;s widest lead of the AI boom, as Meta&#39;s Muse puts CPUs in focus.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61926004/amd-stock-vs-nvidia-2026-ai-boom-meta-muse-agentic-cpu','["AMD", "META", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 16:34:18.043719','other','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'AMD''s significant stock gain relative to Nvidia suggests positive market sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMD": 544.78, "META": 682.7, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 16:34:07.445772','61926004',replace('Advanced Micro Devices Inc. (NASDAQ:AMD) spent most of the AI boom chasing Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) from a distance. In 2026, that relationship flipped.\n\nAMD shares have surged about 187% this year compared to roughly 22% for Nvidia—a massive 165-percentage-point lead that marks AMD’s widest gap over its rival since ChatGPT launched.\n\nThe historic shift suggests Wall Street is no longer viewing AMD merely as a low-cost alternative to Nvidia, but is instead revaluing a completely different layer of the AI stack.\n\nChart: Nvidia vs. AMD: Year-to-Date Performance\n\nWhy AI Agents Need More CPUs\n\nThe first phase of generative AI overwhelmingly rewarded graphics processing units (GPUs), as training massive language models and processing basic chatbot prompts required huge clusters of Nvidia accelerators.\n\nAgentic AI shifts that workload. Instead of simply generating a single output, an autonomous agent operates in a continuous loop—planning steps, executing tools like web browsers or calendars, analyzing results, and deciding the next action. That coordination runs on central processing units (CPUs), the general-purpose chips where AMD holds a strong footprint with its EPYC server line.\n\nAs a result, agentic workflows layer significant CPU demand on top of traditional GPU processing. On AMD’s first-quarter earnings call in May, CEO Lisa Su noted that server deployment ratios have shifted from one CPU for every four-to-eight GPUs toward “a 1:1 configuration.”\n\nFollowing that shift, AMD raised its 2030 server CPU market forecast from $60 billion (growing 18% annually) to over $120 billion (growing over 35% annually). On the Q2 call, Su went a step further, targeting “agentic sandboxes” as the single largest driver of that expanding market.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAMD CEO Lisa Su Says Wall Street Is Underestimating Its AI Business— Now She Sees a $2 Trillion Opportunity\n\nMeta Muse Just Made The Thesis Visible\n\nMeta’s new Muse agent offers the first large-scale consumer showcase of this computing shift. Capable of booking travel, sending emails, and executing transactions, Muse quickly surged to the top of Apple’s App Store. Apptopia estimates cited by TechCrunch show the app drew 1.8 million iOS downloads across the U.S. and Canada in its first 12 days—eclipsing ChatGPT’s 1.3 million over the same post-launch timeframe.\n\nThe market reaction was immediate. Semiconductor stocks rallied, sending AMD up nearly 10% on Monday to cross a $1 trillion market capitalization for the first time.\n\nThe buzz around Muse hinges on a fundamental shift in how software operates: agents don’t just wake up to process a prompt. Meta (NASDAQ:META) CEO Mark Zuckerberg called Muse a “24/7” personal assistant, while Chief AI Officer Alexandr Wang described it as “always-on.” That persistent, background coordination transforms AI from short bursts of GPU inference into an always-running workload—one that demands far more CPU power.\n\nThe 2026 Lead Doesn’t Erase Previous 3 Years\n\nFrom the start of 2023, AMD stock has risen about 9.5 times. Nvidia has risen about 15.6 times over the same period.\n\nFor this reason, AMD would need to outperform Nvidia by roughly another 64% just to match its return since the AI boom began.\n\nNvidia’s market value, at about $5.5 trillion, is also more than five times AMD’s.\n\nSu herself has not framed CPUs as a replacement for GPUs. She has called agentic CPU demand “largely additive,” because agents still depend on accelerators to run the underlying models.\n\nThis year’s gap therefore reflects a change in where investors expect the next wave of demand to come from. It does not show that GPU demand is fading.\n\nChart: AMD vs. Nvidia: Performance Since ChatGPT Release\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'b3bf8979dd4525a050fe16a2765d8262da2e132b','2026-09-22 15:45:26','2026-09-22 16:34:07.415058',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 15:45:26');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(582,'alpaca:61925693','benzinga','2026-09-22 15:36:30','No Warren Buffett, No Problem: Former Hedge Funder Says Berkshire Stock ‘Likely to Beat the S&P 500 Over the Next Five Years’','Berkshire Hathaway stock dropped after Warren Buffett announced he was stepping down as chairman. An investor says now&#39;s the time to buy.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/09/61925693/no-warren-buffett-no-problem-former-hedge-funder-says-berkshire-stock-likely-to-beat-the-sp-500-over-the-next-five-years','["SPY"]','stocks','2026-09-22 16:34:19.579115','other','neutral',2,3,'weeks',1,'Investor opinions are speculative and headline does not report a factual event.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"SPY": 762.63}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 16:34:07.449495','61925693',replace('Conglomerate Berkshire Hathaway (NYSE:BRK)(NYSE:BRK) has gone through several major changes over the past nine months, with longtime CEO Warren Buffett stepping down as CEO at the start of the year and recently announcing he was leaving the chairman role. The news sent Berkshire Hathaway shares lower, but one former hedge funder believes this is an overreaction.\n\n • Berkshire Hathaway shares are consolidating. What’s next for BRK-A stock?\n\nBerkshire Hathaway Shares Undervalued\n\nUnder Buffett’s leadership, Berkshire Hathaway stock often outperformed the S&P; 500, which is tracked by the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY).\n\nBuffett’s retirement CEO and chairman shouldn’t have a huge impact on the company’s financials, former hedge fund manager Whitney Tilson said in a recent newsletter.\n\n"This has no impact on the company. Greg Abel has been running Berkshire since he took over as CEO at the beginning of this year, and Buffett remains on the board," Tilson said.\n\nTilson said Buffett made plans for his son Howard to succeed him as chairman years ago.\n\n"Today’s news also has no impact on the company’s intrinsic value."\n\nTilson recalls highlighting Berkshire Hathaway stock as being undervalued back in August, while Buffett was still chairman.\n\n"My conclusion from back then hasn’t changed. I’m especially bullish because in addition to today’s discounted stock price, I’m optimistic that new CEO Greg Abel can create value via operational improvements and capital allocation."\n\nTilson estimates that Berkshire Hathaway is "highly likely to beat the S&P; 500 over the next five years." The former hedge funder predicts Berkshire Hathaway beating the S&P; 500 by two to three percentage points.\n\nRead Also:\n\nIf You Invested $1,000 In Berkshire Hathaway Stock When Warren Buffett First Did, Here''s How Much You''d Have Today\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nBerkshire Hathaway Stock vs. S&P; 500\n\nBerkshire Hathaway trailed the S&P; 500 in 2025, the last year with Buffett as CEO. Before, Berkshire Hathaway stock had beaten the S&P; 500 in three of the previous four years.\n\nOver the final 25 years of Buffett as CEO, Berkshire Hathaway beat the S&P; 500 13 years and trailed in 12.\n\nBerkshire Hathaway stock is up 1% year-to-date as of Monday, trailing the 13.2% gain of the SPY over the same time period. Berkshire stock is down around 2.5% over the past five days, falling on news of Buffett leaving the chairman role.\n\nOver the last five years, Berkshire Hathaway stock has posted a gain of 80.7%, outperforming the 74.3% gain of the SPY.\n\nTilson sees the long-term gains like this continuing, which could mean that the recent drop in price on the Buffett news is a buying opportunity for patient investors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nWarren Buffett Leaves Berkshire Hathaway: 3 Rules to Copy the Oracle of Omaha’s Investment Style\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'c21a8f58fa22644982d9a281e9347859afe284eb','2026-09-22 15:36:30','2026-09-22 16:34:07.415058',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 15:36:30');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(583,'alpaca:61929328','benzinga','2026-09-22 17:23:24','PayPal Stock Is Rising: What''s Going On Today?','PayPal Holdings Inc (NASDAQ:PYPL) shares are trading higher Tuesday. The company announced a partnership with Meta that will let customers shop and check out using Meta&#39;s Muse personal AI agent across PayPal merchants worldwide. Here&#39;s what you should know.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61929328/paypal-stock-is-rising-whats-going-on-today','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 17:34:29.843208','partnership','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'A partnership with Meta is likely to enhance PayPal''s service offerings and attract more users.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 17:34:25.034574','61929328',replace('PayPal Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:PYPL) shares are trading higher Tuesday. The company announced a partnership with Meta that will let customers shop and check out using Meta’s Muse personal AI agent across PayPal merchants worldwide. Here’s what you should know.\n\nPayPal Holdings shares are advancing steadily. What’s driving PYPL shares up?\n\nPayPal Partners With Meta to Power Checkout Through Muse\n\nPayPal announced a partnership with Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) that will allow customers to use Muse, Meta’s personal AI agent, to shop and complete purchases across PayPal’s global merchant network. The company said the deal will let PayPal customers “seamlessly shop and check out using their Muse personal AI agents” everywhere PayPal is accepted.\n\nThe companies already maintain an existing payment relationship through Meta Pay, which lets users link a PayPal account to make purchases across Meta’s platforms, including the Meta Store. Setting that up involves connecting an account through Meta’s Accounts Center and completing a billing agreement, after which users can set preferences like PayPal Credit or PayPal Balance as their default payment method for future purchases.\n\nWhat the Muse Partnership Could Mean For PayPal\n\nExtending that existing payment relationship to Muse positions PayPal at the center of an emerging shift toward AI agents completing purchases on behalf of consumers, rather than people manually navigating checkout pages themselves.\n\nIf Muse gains meaningful adoption, embedding PayPal as a default or preferred checkout option inside that experience could drive incremental transaction volume across PayPal’s merchant base without requiring those merchants to build separate integrations of their own.\n\nPYPL Shares Are Climbing\n\nPYPL Price Action: PayPal shares were up 1.14% at $53.22 at the time of publication on Tuesday, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nPalantir Golden Cross Brings This Key Level Into Focus\n\nImage: Ink Drop/Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'dea93b6dd56f7f4e00b1a27f31f18a2267e3f135','2026-09-22 17:23:24','2026-09-22 17:34:25.025315',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 17:23:24');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(584,'alpaca:61929091','benzinga','2026-09-22 17:15:39','Bitcoin Cash, Uniswap Surges as CME Announces New Futures Contracts: What''s Going On?','Bitcoin Cash jumps 21% on Tuesday after CME unveils BCH and Uniswap futures, expanding regulated crypto derivatives as institutional demand grows.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61929091/bitcoin-cash-uniswap-surges-as-cme-announces-new-futures-contracts-whats-going-on','["ADA/USD", "AVAX/USD", "BTC/USD", "ETH/USD", "LINK/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 17:34:31.038357','listing','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'CME announcing new futures contracts for Bitcoin Cash and Uniswap indicates growing institutional interest.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"ADA/USD": 0.20462, "AVAX/USD": 7.631703886, "BTC/USD": 76528.6, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "LINK/USD": 11.42345, "SOL/USD": 101.29}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 17:34:25.038603','61929091',replace('Bitcoin Cash (CRYPTO: BCH) exploded 21% Tuesday after CME Group (NASDAQ:CME) announced new futures contracts for BCH and Uniswap (CRYPTO: UNI).\n\n • CME Group shares are experiencing downward pressure. Why are CME shares declining?\n\nWhat CME Announced\n\nCME Group said in a Tuesday press release that the new contracts respond directly to client demand for institutional-grade risk tools in high-liquidity altcoin markets. Traders get a choice of contract sizes:\n\nBitcoin Cash futures — 250 BCH, or Micro Bitcoin Cash futures at 25 BCH\n\nUniswap futures — 10,000 UNI, or Micro Uniswap futures at 1,000 UNI\n\n“As crypto markets continue to mature, participants require broader, regulated tools to navigate evolving digital asset-related price risk,” said Giovanni Vicioso, CME Group’s Global Head of Cryptocurrency Products. \n\nRipple Prime President Noel Kimmel added that institutions need round-the-clock access to regulated derivatives, and these contracts extend that access alongside CME’s existing XRP and Bitcoin products.\n\nWhy This Adds to a Bigger Trend\n\nCME’s crypto suite already spans Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC), Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH), XRP (CRYPTO: XRP), Solana (CRYPTO: SOL), Cardano (CRYPTO: ADA), Chainlink (CRYPTO: LINK), Stellar (CRYPTO: XLM), Avalanche (CRYPTO: AVAX) and Sui (CRYPTO: SUI). \n\nThe numbers behind that lineup show institutional appetite keeps growing:\n\nFirst half of 2026 average daily volume: 279,800 contracts, worth $8.3 billion notional\n\nFirst half of 2026 average open interest: 264,600 contracts, worth $15.4 billion notional\n\n2026 altcoin expansion: Cardano, Chainlink, Stellar, Avalanche and Sui alone added over $1 billion in total notional value year-to-date\n\nBCH and UNI Technical Analysis\n\nBitcoin Cash surges 21%, reclaiming the 200-day EMA at $308 for the first time since the May breakdown. \n\nThe move also clears the $240 to $260 resistance shelf that capped every rally since June, flipping that zone into fresh support.\n\nResistance: $328.94 (today’s high), then $330 to $340\n\nSupport: $308 (200-day EMA), then $240 to $260\n\nUniswap climbs 3%, breaking out above the descending wedge that has compressed price since the 2024 highs. \n\nAll four EMAs now line up bullish for the first time in months, with the RSI Divergence Indicator reading 73.13, overbought but backed by a clean bullish divergence off the summer lows.\n\nResistance: $9.74 (weekly high), then the wedge apex near $10 to $11\n\nSupport: $7.83 (200-day EMA), then $6.01 (100-day EMA)\n\nPhoto via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nCircle, Binance Deepen USDC Ties with $100 Million Investment','\n',char(10)),'a48fd86b4a588430906cd6d947cbb87ade9d0780','2026-09-22 17:15:39','2026-09-22 17:34:25.025315',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 17:15:39');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(585,'alpaca:61928535','benzinga','2026-09-22 16:59:30','Commodity ETF Delivers Double Nvidia’s YTD Returns; Muse Ignites CPU Fever',replace('\n\n\n\nCPU Fever\n\n\n\nPlease click here for an enlarged chart comparing NVIDIA Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) and Invesco Optimum Yield Diversified Commodity Strategy No K-1 ETF (PDBC)\n\n\n\nNote the following:\n\n\n\n\nThe chart shows that','\n',char(10)),'https://www.benzinga.com/Opinion/26/09/61928535/commodity-etf-delivers-double-nvidias-ytd-returns-muse-ignites-cpu-fever','["AAPL", "AMD", "AMZN", "BTC/USD", "META", "MSFT", "NVDA", "QQQ", "SPY", "TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 17:34:32.427962','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The comparison highlights performance but does not indicate a significant market event.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "AMD": 544.78, "AMZN": 251.18, "BTC/USD": 76528.6, "META": 682.7, "MSFT": 498.48}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 17:34:25.083684','61928535',replace('CPU Fever\n\nPlease click here for an enlarged chart comparing NVIDIA Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) and Invesco Optimum Yield Diversified Commodity Strategy No K-1 ETF (PDBC)\n\nNote the following:\n\nThe chart shows that king of AI NVDA has returned 20.11% year to date.\n\nThe chart shows that commodity ETF PDBC has returned 46.39% year to date.  PDBC’s return is 131% of NVDA’s return.\n\nThe chart illustrates how diversifying beyond AI increases returns and lowers risks.  Higher return with lower risk is the holy grail of investing.  \n\nAt this time when most portfolios are very heavy in AI positions, prudent investors should take time to review their portfolios for adequate diversification beyond AI stocks.  In our analysis, if there is a market downturn because AI deployment slows or AI monetization does not live up to expectations, diversification within AI will not help as all AI stocks will go down together.  \n\nAs a full disclosure, PDBC and NVDA are in our portfolios. \n\nCPU fever has gripped the stock market.  The fever was triggered by the popularity of Muse from Meta Platforms Inc (META). While GPUs have been used extensively for LLM training and inference, CPUs are important for AI agents.  Intel Corp (NASDAQ:INTC) and Advanced Micro Devices Inc (NASDAQ:AMD) are the two primary providers of CPUs.  Qualcomm Inc (NASDAQ:QCOM) and Arm Holdings PLC – ADR (NASDAQ:ARM) have also jumped into the business of providing CPUs.  As a full disclosure, taking advantage of the strength in CPU stocks, profits have been taken on a trade around position in INTC.\n\nIn our analysis, in spite of the uber bullishness about Meta and CPUs, prudent investors should note that for Muse to work well users will need to give Muse access to a multitude of their accounts.  How many users are going to trust AI and give their account information to Muse is yet to be seen.  Amazon.com, Inc. (AMZN) has banned Muse.  On the other hand, Shopify Inc. (NASDAQ:SHOP) will allow Muse for agentic check out. As a full disclosure, META is in our portfolio. The position is long from an average of $49.92. \n\nChina is making strides to reduce its dependence on U.S. AI chips ahead of Trump Xi talks.  Alibaba Group Holding Ltd – ADR (NYSE:BABA) is introducing a new powerful AI chip.\n\nOf special note for prudent investors is that SoftBank Group Corp – ADR (OTC:SFTBY) is delaying its datacenter unit IPO.  It appears the delay is due to AI safety fears and slowdown talk.  SoftBank is a big investor in ChatGPT maker OpenAI.  In our analysis, the delay will fuel the debate if the stock market is overpricing AI datacenter and chip stocks.  \n\nPresident Trump will address the U.N. General Assembly this morning.  President Trump’s speech may be market moving.\n\nYields are slipping as oil pulls back.  Oil is pulling back on Saudi Arabia restarting the East-West Pipeline.  Prudent investors should note the pipeline is pumping at a low rate and is vulnerable to Houthi attacks.  Also adding to the oil drop is a report that Iran is willing to open the Strait of Hormuz in seven days if the U.S. lifts the naval blockade.\n\nMagnificent Seven Money Flows\n\nMost portfolios are now heavily concentrated in the Mag 7 stocks.  For this reason, it is important to pay attention to early money flows in the Mag 7 stocks on a daily basis.\n\nIn the early trade, money flows are positive in Apple Inc (NASDAQ:AAPL), Alphabet (NASDAQ:GOOG),  Microsoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT), and Tesla Inc (NASDAQ:TSLA).\n\nIn the early trade, money flows are negative in Amazon (NASDAQ:AMZN), Meta (NASDAQ:META), and Nvidia (NASDAQ:NVDA).\n\nIn the early trade, money flows are neutral in SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust Series 1 (NASDAQ:QQQ).\n\nMomo Crowd And Smart Money In Stocks\n\nInvestors can gain an edge by knowing money flows in SPY and QQQ.  Investors can get a bigger edge by knowing when smart money is buying stocks, gold, and oil.  The most popular ETF for gold is SPDR Gold Trust (GLD).  The most popular ETF for silver is iShares Silver Trust (SLV).  The most popular ETF for oil is United States Oil ETF (NYSE:USO).\n\nBitcoin\n\nBitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) is seeing buying.\n\nWhat To Do Now\n\nConsider continuing to hold good, very long term, existing positions and add tactical positions based on signals.\n\nThe Arora Report is known for its accurate calls. Most recently, The Arora Report correctly called the rally from recent stock market lows and the 2026 semiconductor decline before a 25% drop in the Semiconductor ETF (SMH). In gold, The Arora Report bought at an average price near $1,105, close to cycle lows, and took partial profits near $5,400, close to cycle highs.. Please click here to get The Arora Report’s insights with the free forever Generate Wealth Newsletter.\n\nBenzinga Disclaimer: This article is from an unpaid external contributor. It does not represent Benzinga’s reporting and has not been edited for content or accuracy.','\n',char(10)),'6bf8b4df72ee300500c3b58443c866e15e5c429b','2026-09-22 16:59:30','2026-09-22 17:34:25.025315',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 17:03:43');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(586,'alpaca:61927717','benzinga','2026-09-22 16:35:07','Apple’s New Macs Are Faster, Smarter and Built for AI','Apple unveils the new Mac mini and Mac Studio powered by M6 and M5 chips, featuring boosted AI performance and up to 512GB memory.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61927717/apples-new-macs-are-faster-smarter-and-built-for-ai','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-22 17:34:33.692348','product','bullish',3,4,'days',1,'New product release with enhanced performance may boost demand.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 17:34:25.099028','61927717',replace('Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) is refreshing its Mac lineup with new high-powered desktops as Wall Street weighs steady iPhone demand, mounting excitement around the upcoming Duo foldable and a valuation already near historic highs.Apple Launches New Mac Mini And Mac StudioApple released a new Mac mini powered by the M6 and M5 Pro chips and a new Mac Studio featuring the M5 Max and M5 Ultra.The company said the M6 Mac mini delivers up to four times faster AI performance, twice the graphics performance and 40% faster CPU performance. The Mac Studio targets professional workloads, with the M5 Ultra configuration supporting up to 512GB of unified memory.Both desktops also emphasize on-device AI through Apple Intelligence and Siri AI in macOS 27.Mac mini with M6 starts at $899, while the M5 Pro model starts at $1,699. Mac Studio starts at $2,499 with M5 Max and $5,499 with M5 Ultra.Wall Street Watches iPhone Demand And DuoMorgan Stanley analyst Erik Woodring recently said early demand for the iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max “seems fine,” with delivery lead times broadly unchanged from last year despite about 18% higher production.Woodring believes some Chinese consumers may be waiting for Apple’s Duo foldable, which Apple expects to make available in mid-October. He remains highly optimistic about the product and expects Apple could sell nearly every foldable it produces over the next 12 months.CNBC’s Jim Cramer called Duo “revolutionary,” contrasting it with the more incremental iPhone 18 upgrade.Woodring said Apple trades at a “relatively rich” valuation of about 33 times fiscal 2027 earnings, near its historical peak multiple of roughly 34 to 35 times.He said further gains may require higher earnings estimates. Woodring also expects Services growth to reaccelerate after falling below 10% in the September quarter, while warning that a deeper slowdown could pressure Apple’s valuation.Apple Stock Rises Near 52-Week HighApple stock rose about 1% Tuesday, outperforming the broader technology sector as investors favored mega-cap tech. The Nasdaq gained 0.43%, while the S&P; 500 slipped 0.04%. Technology rose about 0.2%.Apple remains in a strong uptrend, trading above its 20-day, 50-day, 100-day and 200-day simple moving averages. Shares are also just below the 52-week high of $344.57, putting the stock in a potential breakout zone.Momentum remains positive, with MACD above its signal line. Traders may watch $344.50 as resistance and $300.50 as support.Apple carries a Buy consensus rating with an average price forecast of $335.57. Recent analyst calls include Evercore ISI’s $380 price forecast, Bank of America’s $370 forecast and TD Cowen’s $400 forecast.Top ETF Exposure\nDirexion Daily Technology Bull 3X ETF (NYSE:TECL): 9.68% Weight\n\nMotley Fool 100 Index ETF (BATS:TMFC): 9.74% Weight\n\nVistaShares Target 15 Berkshire Select Income ETF (NYSE:OMAH): 9.97% Weight\nSignificance: Because AAPL carries such a heavy weight in these funds, any significant inflows or outflows for these ETFs will likely force automatic buying or selling of the stock.AAPL Price ActionAAPL Stock Price Activity: Apple shares were up 0.98% at $342.31 at the time of publication on Tuesday. The stock is trading near its 52-week high of $344.56, according to Benzinga Pro data.Image via Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nApple’s Customers Can Take a Price Hike, Analyst Says Retention Hardly Moves','\n',char(10)),'72210570afeac43f08de319e65e262a0978ca3e8','2026-09-22 16:35:07','2026-09-22 17:34:25.025315',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 16:35:07');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(587,'alpaca:61931124','benzinga','2026-09-22 18:27:14','Stock of the Day: Is Apple Breaking Out?','Apple shares rise toward resistance; a breakout could signal buyers overpowering sellers and launch the stock into a new uptrend.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/technicals/26/09/61931124/stock-of-the-day-is-apple-breaking-out','["AAPL"]','stocks','2026-09-22 18:34:42.833940','other','neutral',1,2,'days',1,'The headline poses a question and suggests speculation about a potential breakout.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 18:34:37.841610','61931124',replace('Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) shares are moving higher on Tuesday.  They may be breaking resistance.\n\nThis could be a bullish dynamic that would suggest a further move higher. This is why Apple is the Stock of the Day.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nIf a stock is in an uptrend, it is out of equilibrium. There are more shares to be purchased than to be sold.\n\nBecause of this, investors and traders who wish to buy are forced to be aggressive and outbid each other. This forces the shares into an uptrend.\n\nAt a resistance level, the dynamic changes. There are enough shares for sale to fill all of the buy orders. This is why the price stops moving higher when a stock reaches resistance.\n\nSometimes stocks sell off after they reach these levels.\n\nThis happens when some of the people who created the resistance become anxious and impatient. They worry that other sellers will undercut them, knowing buyers will gravitate toward the lowest price. They don’t want to miss the trade, so they reduce their offer prices; other anxious sellers see this and do the same thing.\n\nThis results in a snowball effect that can force the price lower.\n\nBut sometimes when a stock reaches resistance, buyers eventually overpower sellers and push the price higher. When this happens, traders say it’s a “breakout.”\n\nBreakouts are considered a bullish dynamic because they show that the sellers who created the resistance have left the market. They have either finished or canceled their orders.\n\nWith these sellers gone, buyers will once again be forced to outbid each other to get new sellers interested. This could force Apple into a new uptrend.\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nMicron Earnings Are Set for a 10x Jump: The Stock Is Still the Cheapest in Tech','\n',char(10)),'b10ca8c5a913f62f3a5ac727857693c7b804cf82','2026-09-22 18:27:14','2026-09-22 18:34:37.832807',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 18:27:14');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(588,'alpaca:61930818','benzinga','2026-09-22 18:15:04','Nasdaq 100 Flirts with Records, Oil Sinks for Fifth Day: Stock Market Today','Nasdaq 100 printed an intraday record on AI enthusiasm while financials slid nearly 2% and crude fell for a fifth straight session.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61930818/nasdaq-record-banks-fall-oil-fifth-decline-whats-moving-markets-tuesday','["QQQ"]','stocks','2026-09-22 18:34:43.986384','macro','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Nasdaq 100''s upward movement on AI enthusiasm indicates potential positive investor sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 716.89}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 18:34:37.862296','61930818',replace('The Nasdaq 100 carved out a fresh intraday record by midday Tuesday as the artificial intelligence trade powered ahead.\n\nSpeaking at the United Nations General Assembly on Tuesday, President Donald Trump said he faces a “big decision” on whether to negotiate with Tehran or “annihilate the Islamic Republic,” adding, “I believe we’ll make a deal right after the election because it doesn’t make sense for them not to.”\n\n • Viking Therapeutics stock is surging to new heights today. Why are VKTX shares rallying?\n\nWest Texas Intermediate crude fell 0.6% to $91.81 a barrel, a fifth consecutive daily decline and the lowest level in two weeks, as flows through the Strait of Hormuz and alternative routes edged back toward pre-war levels.\n\nThe S&P; 500 was effectively unchanged at 7,761.28, while the Dow Jones Industrial Average shed 263 points, or 0.51%, to 51,785.94, pressured by a fall in financial names.\n\nThe Nasdaq 100 rose 0.41% to 30,607.20 after touching its first intraday record since June. \n\nOn the rates front, St. Louis Fed President Alberto Musalem said further increases may be needed to bring inflation back toward target. \n\nThe 10-year Treasury yield reversed an early decline to sit at 4.98%, up 2 basis points, while the 2-year added 2 basis points to 4.77% and the 30-year rose 2 basis points to 5.31%.\n\nTuesday’s Performance In Major U.S. Indices\n\nIndexLast% ChangeMTDYTDS&P; 5007,761.28-0.04%+0.8%+13.4%Dow Jones51,785.94-0.51%-2.7%+7.6%Nasdaq 10030,607.20+0.41%+3.9%+21.2%Russell 20002,885.25+0.34%-2.5%+16.4%Updated by 12:30 PM ET\n\nAccording to the Benzinga Pro platform:\n\nThe Vanguard S&P; 500 ETF (NYSE:VOO) was flat, easing less than 0.1%.\n\nThe SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA) slid 0.5%.\n\nThe Invesco QQQ Trust (NASDAQ:QQQ) climbed 0.5%.\n\nThe iShares Russell 2000 ETF (NYSE:IWM) rose 0.4%.\n\nBanks Buckle While the AI Complex Runs Away\n\nThe Financial Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLF) was the session’s worst performer by a wide margin, sinking 1.9% as the yield rebound and lingering credit-quality worries sent lenders lower. JPMorgan Chase & Co. (NYSE:JPM) fell 3.4%, Wells Fargo & Co. (NYSE:WFC) dropped 3.4% and Morgan Stanley (NYSE:MS) lost 2.9%.\n\nDefensives took the lead instead. The Consumer Staples Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLP) gained 1%, the Materials Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLB) rose 1% and the Health Care Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLV) added 0.7%. The Technology Select Sector SPDR Fund (NYSE:XLK) managed only a 0.2% gain.\n\nAt the industry level, the iShares U.S. Home Construction ETF (BATS:ITB) topped the board with a 2.2% advance, followed by the iShares Biotechnology ETF (NASDAQ:IBB) at 1.7% and the SPDR S&P; Metals & Mining ETF (NYSE:XME) at 1.3%. The VanEck Gold Miners ETF (NYSE:GDX) rose 1.2% even as spot gold eased 0.4% to $4,324.67 an ounce.\n\nViking Therapeutics Inc. (NASDAQ:VKTX) was the day’s runaway winner, surging 30.7% after its VK2735 maintenance study showed patients switching from weekly to every-other-week dosing preserved up to 97% of prior weight loss, with monthly dosing preserving up to 90%.\n\nThe dual GLP-1/GIP agonist delivered 22% placebo-adjusted weight loss at 33 weeks on the 17.5 mg dose, and Truist analyst Gregory Renza called the readout a “best-case scenario.” \n\nThe company plans to start Phase 3 trials by year-end.\n\nVicor Corp. (NASDAQ:VICR) jumped 13.7% after sharply raising its third-quarter revenue outlook late Monday, guiding to sequential growth above 20% versus a prior estimate of roughly 10%, driven by royalties from a new licensing agreement covering its Vertical Power Delivery technology.\n\nOn Holding AG (NYSE:ONON) rallied 10.2% on the back of its Zurich investor day, where management targeted at least CHF 5.6 billion in net sales and a 22% adjusted EBITDA margin by 2029, authorized a $1 billion buyback through 2029 and announced entry into football and golf. \n\nMonolithic Power Systems Inc. (NASDAQ:MPWR) climbed 7.5% and Rambus Inc. (NASDAQ:RMBS) was up 7.38%, extending Monday’s move in AI power delivery and memory interface names.\n\nThe trade also lifted Micron Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MU) by 3.4%, Astera Labs Inc. (NASDAQ:ALAB) by 7.3% and SanDisk Corp. (NASDAQ:SNDK) by 6.5%.\n\nOn the downside, Planet Fitness Inc. (NYSE:PLNT) slumped 9.9%, on a day when obesity-drug headlines dominated, with Viking’s readout landing alongside a fresh wave of GLP-1 commentary on the long-term structural threat oral obesity drugs pose to fitness operators. Planet Fitness is now down more than 55% year to date after cutting its 2026 outlook and withdrawing its three-year growth in May.\n\nNew York Times Co. (NYSE:NYT) tumbled 9.3%. Gen Digital Inc. (NASDAQ:GEN) fell 6.8%, extending a multi-session slide in a software cohort that also saw Intuit Inc. (NASDAQ:INTU) drop 4.7%.\n\nRyan Specialty Holdings Inc. (NYSE:RYAN) dropped 6.6% and LPL Financial Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:LPLA) fell 6.2%. \n\nIn the only notable earnings print of the session, AutoZone Inc. (NYSE:AZO) rose 5.8% after reporting quarterly earnings of $56.06 per share versus the $54.51 consensus. Peer O’Reilly Automotive Inc. (NASDAQ:ORLY) gained 4.3% in sympathy. Elsewhere, Lennar Corp. (NYSE:LEN) climbed 4.6% to lead the homebuilder bounce.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Value Stocks\n\nTuesday’s Russell 1000 Top Gainers\n\nName% changeViking Therapeutics, Inc.+30.65%Vicor Corporation+13.73%On Holding AG+10.21%Monolithic Power Systems, Inc.+7.52%Rambus Inc.+7.38%\n\nTuesday’s Russell 1000 Top Losers\n\nName% changePlanet Fitness, Inc.-9.9%The New York Times Company-9.34%Gen Digital Inc.-6.79%Ryan Specialty Holdings, Inc.-6.63%LPL Financial Holdings Inc.-6.23%\n\nPhoto: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nMicron Earnings Are Set for a 10x Jump: The Stock Is Still the Cheapest in Tech','\n',char(10)),'ae26790f1c69eb496ebf1d4db6a9de461162f2a3','2026-09-22 18:15:04','2026-09-22 18:34:37.832807',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 18:15:04');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(589,'alpaca:61930209','benzinga','2026-09-22 17:56:04','JPMorgan Stock Slips as Traders Shift to Tech Sector','JPMorgan Chase shares are sliding Tuesday amid a broad financial sector selloff as investors rotate into tech stocks.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61930209/jpmorgan-stock-slips-as-traders-shift-to-tech-sector','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 18:34:44.939774','other','bearish',2,3,'days',1,'JPMorgan shares are affected by a sector rotation to tech stocks.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 18:34:37.882461','61930209',replace('JPMorgan Chase & Co. (NYSE:JPM) shares are sliding Tuesday as financial stocks broadly sell off, with traders rotating into technology names amid growing concern that AI shopping agents like Meta’s Muse could disrupt traditional payment and financial companies.\n\nJPMorgan Chase shares are retreating from recent levels. What’s pressuring JPM stock?\n\nJPMorgan Leads a Broad Decline in Financial Stocks\n\nThe stock is giving back ground after climbing steadily through the back half of summer, now retreating from the peak it touched in August as it runs into technical resistance following that extended rally. That weakness stands out against an otherwise upbeat session, with the Nasdaq adding 0.52% while the S&P; 500 sits nearly flat, down just 0.03%.\n\nPart of what’s weighing on shares may also be investors recalculating how this week’s rate increase will flow through to banks’ net interest income going forward.\n\nThe broader financial sector is having an even rougher session, sitting dead last among the 11 S&P; sectors and down 1.89% on the day, even though it’s still managed a 2.11% gain over the past three months. JPMorgan is actually trailing that already-struggling group by 1.5 percentage points.\n\nToday’s gains are showing up mostly in defensive, commodity-tied corners of the market, namely Materials, Consumer Staples and Healthcare, while Financials sit at the bottom alongside Communication Services and Industrials, a lineup that points to money moving away from cyclical, rate-sensitive names, including into technology stocks.\n\nAI Shopping Agents Raise Questions About Traditional Finance’s Role\n\nCompounding the pressure on financial stocks, a fresh wave of deals linking Meta Platform Inc.’s (NASDAQ:META) newly launched Muse AI agent to e-commerce and checkout systems has investors questioning whether these agents might eventually cut traditional financial middlemen out of the picture.\n\nPayPal Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:PYPL) unveiled its own tie-up with Meta this week, saying the arrangement will let customers “seamlessly shop and check out using their Muse personal AI agents” wherever PayPal is accepted.\n\nShopify Inc. (NASDAQ:SHOP) moved higher Tuesday after announcing a new partnership with Meta that connects Shopify’s merchant network directly to Muse. The integration lets shoppers browse and buy from Shopify‑powered stores while completing checkout through Shop Pay, the company’s fast one‑click payment system.\n\nShopify CEO Tobias Lütke announced the deal on X Monday, describing it as an effort to create an “easy and delightful way to shop and check out with Muse.” Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg confirmed the integration the following morning, writing on X, “Teaming up with Shopify to make shopping and checkout easier in Muse. Shoppers find more. Shops sell more. More partnerships like this coming soon.”\n\nDeals like these, which route commerce and payments directly through Meta’s own AI agent rather than traditional bank-linked payment rails, are part of what’s fueling investor concern that companies like JPMorgan could eventually see a smaller role in how consumers pay for everyday purchases.\n\nJPM Shares Are Dropping\n\nJPM Price Action: JPMorgan shares were down 3.12% at $341.07 at the time of publication on Tuesday, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nGoldman, Morgan Stanley Ride $17.2B China Tech Boom as AI Truce Odds Sit at 10%\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'3a75796c7cb7126684f62e27549c9abb03fdd6e2','2026-09-22 17:56:04','2026-09-22 18:34:37.832807',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 17:56:04');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(590,'alpaca:61929691','benzinga','2026-09-22 17:35:36','4 Communication Services Stocks Whale Activity In Today’s Session',replace('This whale alert can help traders discover the next big trading opportunities.\nWhales are entities with large sums of money and we track their transactions here at Benzinga on our options activity scanner.\nTraders often','\n',char(10)),'https://www.benzinga.com/markets/options/26/09/61929691/4-communication-services-stocks-whale-activity-today-s-session','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 18:34:46.024346','other','neutral',2,3,'hours',1,'Whale activity in stocks is generally regarded as notable but lacks specific positive or negative implications.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 18:34:37.897027','61929691',replace('This whale alert can help traders discover the next big trading opportunities.\nWhales are entities with large sums of money and we track their transactions here at Benzinga on our options activity scanner.\nTraders often look for circumstances when the market estimation of an option diverges away from its normal worth. Abnormal amounts of trading activity could push option prices to hyperbolic or underperforming levels. \nBelow are some instances of options activity happening in the Communication Services sector: \n\nSymbol\nPUT/CALL\nTrade Type\nSentiment\nExp. Date\nStrike Price\nTotal Trade Price\nOpen Interest\nVolume\n\nBIDU\nPUT\nTRADE\nBEARISH\n01/15/27\n$65.00\n$27.6K\n534\n249\n\nGOOGL\nCALL\nTRADE\nBULLISH\n12/18/26\n$335.00\n$41.8K\n1.2K\n59\n\nMETA\nPUT\nSWEEP\nBEARISH\n12/18/26\n$470.00\n$28.9K\n799\n21\n\nAPP\nPUT\nTRADE\nBEARISH\n01/15/27\n$710.00\n$87.2K\n76\n3\n\nExplanation\nThese bullet-by-bullet explanations have been constructed using the accompanying table. \n• Regarding BIDU (NASDAQ:BIDU), we observe a put option trade with bearish sentiment. It expires in 115 day(s) on January 15, 2027. Parties traded 199 contract(s) at a $65.00 strike. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $27.6K, with a price of $139.0 per contract. There were 534 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 249 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• For GOOGL (NASDAQ:GOOGL), we notice a call option trade that happens to be bullish, expiring in 87 day(s) on December 18, 2026. This event was a transfer of 10 contract(s) at a $335.00 strike. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $41.8K, with a price of $4183.0 per contract. There were 1204 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 59 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• For META (NASDAQ:META), we notice a put option sweep that happens to be bearish, expiring in 87 day(s) on December 18, 2026. This event was a transfer of 20 contract(s) at a $470.00 strike. This particular put needed to be split into 3 different trades to become filled. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $28.9K, with a price of $1450.0 per contract. There were 799 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 21 contract(s) were bought and sold. \n• Regarding APP (NASDAQ:APP), we observe a put option trade with bearish sentiment. It expires in 115 day(s) on January 15, 2027. Parties traded 3 contract(s) at a $710.00 strike. The total cost received by the writing party (or parties) was $87.2K, with a price of $29070.0 per contract. There were 76 open contracts at this strike prior to today, and today 3 contract(s) were bought and sold. \nOptions Alert Terminology\n - Call Contracts: The right to buy shares as indicated in the contract.\n - Put Contracts: The right to sell shares as indicated in the contract.\n - Expiration Date: When the contract expires. One must act on the contract by this date if one wants to use it.\n - Premium/Option Price: The price of the contract. \nFor more information, read more about unusual options activity. \nThis article was generated by Benzinga''s automated content engine and reviewed by an editor.','\n',char(10)),'9e9d8e7a0975b7868778df33b5101908414f82b0','2026-09-22 17:35:36','2026-09-22 18:34:37.832807',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 17:35:36');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(591,'alpaca:61932828','benzinga','2026-09-22 19:32:50','Apple Takes Aim at Nvidia’s AI Economics: New Macs Have ‘No Cost per Token,’ Hardware Chief Says','Apple says new Macs can run AI locally with no per-token cloud cost, challenging Nvidia’s compute-heavy economics.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61932828/apple-macs-ai-no-cost-per-token-nvidia','["AAPL", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 19:34:56.882922','product','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Apple''s development may enhance its competitive position in the AI hardware market.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 19:34:52.225014','61932828',replace('Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) is pitching its newest Macs as a way for businesses to run powerful AI models without paying per-token cloud charges, taking aim at the economics behind the AI infrastructure boom.“There’s no cost per token. You’re just using the machine again and again,” Apple hardware chief Johny Srouji told Reuters.Apple demonstrated four Mac Studios running a trillion-parameter AI model together, with Reuters reporting the cluster could operate from a single wall outlet.Apple Pushes AI Onto the MacIn Apple’s framing, businesses can pay upfront for the hardware and run AI models locally instead of continually paying cloud providers or AI companies for usage.That hardware cost is substantial. The M5 Ultra Mac Studio starts at $5,499, while a version with 256GB of memory and 16TB of storage costs $18,299. Apple’s 512GB configuration, which can handle even larger models, arrives in late October.Apple raised Mac prices in June citing surging memory and storage costs.Jensen Huang Says ‘Compute Is Revenue’Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang has described the AI economy differently.“Its tokens are productive and profitable. Now, compute is revenue,” Huang said in Nvidia’s latest earnings release.Nvidia’s Data Center revenue reached $89 billion last quarter, up 117% from a year earlier, as cloud providers and AI companies continued spending heavily on computing infrastructure.Apple’s pitch suggests some inference workloads could shift away from rented data-center capacity and onto local machines.Nvidia is also pursuing the same shift. Its DGX Spark and RTX Spark products are designed to run increasingly capable AI models locally, making desktop AI another battleground between the companies.Apple Faces an Enterprise ClimbPrediction-market traders still expect Nvidia to stay on top. Polymarket gives Nvidia a 78% chance of ending 2026 as the world’s largest company, compared with 15% for Apple, on about $7.5 million in trading volume.Apple held just 4.6% of the enterprise PC market compared with 91.3% for Windows, according to IDC data cited by Reuters.Apple’s own most advanced cloud model, meanwhile, reportedly runs on Nvidia GPUs through Google Cloud.Image: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nGoldman, Morgan Stanley Ride $17.2B China Tech Boom as AI Truce Odds Sit at 10%','\n',char(10)),'68605ee073ef1a545b740685e7d01c4060dd7e2d','2026-09-22 19:32:50','2026-09-22 19:34:52.218940',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 19:32:50');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(592,'alpaca:61932749','benzinga','2026-09-22 19:27:25','Bitcoin, Ethereum Flat as XRP, Dogecoin Gain on $1B ETF Inflows: ''Real Capital Is Coming Back''','Bitcoin stays above $86K as spot ETFs draw nearly $1 billion. Trader predicts it could first extend towards $89K and later a retest of $80K.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61932749/bitcoin-ethereum-flat-as-xrp-dogecoin-gain-on-1b-etf-inflows-real-capital-is-coming-back','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "ETH/USD", "SHIB/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','degen','2026-09-22 19:34:58.047713','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses current market conditions without a decisive event affecting the assets.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "SHIB/USD": 5.21e-06, "SOL/USD": 101.29, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 19:34:52.230076','61932749',replace('Bitcoin held firmly above $86,000 as U.S. spot Bitcoin ETFs attracted nearly $1 billion in net inflows, signaling renewed institutional demand.CRYPTOCURRENCYTICKERPRICEBitcoin(CRYPTO: BTC)$86,586.09Ethereum(CRYPTO: ETH)$2,751.65Solana(CRYPTO: SOL)$117.98XRP(CRYPTO: XRP)$1.57Dogecoin(CRYPTO: DOGE)$0.09957Shiba Inu(CRYPTO: SHIB)$0.056028Notable Statistics\nCoinglass data shows 93,939 traders were liquidated in the past 24 hours for $437.68 million.       \n\nSoSoValue data shows net inflows of $998.95 million from spot Bitcoin ETFs on Monday. Spot Ethereum ETFs saw net inflows of $269.98 million.\n\nIn the past 24 hours, top gainers include Bitcoin Cash, NEAR Protocol and Quant.\nNotable Developments\nThis Analyst is Expects a BTC Pullback\n\nWhy Billionaire Tim Draper Calls Apple, Meta ‘Irresponsible’ for Not Holding Bitcoin\n\nEXCLUSIVE: ‘Institutions Are Buying BTC’ — Retail Is Trading Everything Else\n\nBitcoin Cash, Uniswap Surges as CME Announces New Futures Contracts: What’s Going On?\n\nStrategy Swings From $10B Loss to $8B Profit as Bitcoin Hits $85K\n\nForget Dogecoin: PEPE Is Outrunning Bitcoin and XRP—Is FLOKI Next?\n\n‘Crypto Winter Is Over,’ Fundstrat Says: Why Ether and Solana ETFs Matter Now\n\nElon Musk’s X Launches Cashtag Trading Program With Coinbase, Kraken, Gemini\n\nNot Dogecoin or Shiba Inu: Is This Meme Coin’s 27% Rally Just Getting Started?\nTrader NotesDigital asset trader Castillo Trading expects Bitcoin to retest $80,000, though it could first extend toward $89,000. He views dips as buying opportunities rather than a reason to turn bearish.Heavily followed trader Michael van de Poppe anticipates a sweep of the $84,000 level, which he sees as a potential area to look for long entries.Trader CryptosBatman points to nearly $1 billion in latest-session Bitcoin ETF inflows as evidence that institutional demand is returning after months of weakness. “Real capital is coming back,” he added.He suggests BTC’s bottom may already be in.\n\nRead Also:\n\nWhy Billionaire Tim Draper Calls Apple, Meta ''Irresponsible'' for Not Holding Bitcoin\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'b402e752450489f282bf2a744ce6e19b4562e35c','2026-09-22 19:27:25','2026-09-22 19:34:52.218940',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 19:27:25');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(593,'alpaca:61932012','benzinga','2026-09-22 19:02:09','Meta’s Muse Beat ChatGPT’s Early Download Pace: Is Zuckerberg’s AI Bet Finally Paying Out?','Meta&#39;s Muse AI agent topped ChatGPT&#39;s early iOS downloads, Bank of America says, but meaningful revenue may not arrive before 2028.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61932012/meta-muse-chatgpt-downloads-zuckerberg-ai-bet','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 19:35:00.092782','product','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'Meta''s Muse showing strong early download performance may indicate growing interest in their AI offering.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 19:34:52.240633','61932012',replace('On Sept. 8, Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META) launched Muse, a personal AI agent that browses websites, sorts email and completes multi-step tasks on its own. \n\nTwo weeks later, the app is outrunning some of the biggest consumer launches in tech.\n\nSensor Tower data cited by Bank of America showed Muse reached roughly 2.5 million U.S. downloads through Sept. 19 and about 557,000 daily active users. \n\nOn iOS, its first 12 days produced 1.43 million downloads, slightly ahead of ChatGPT’s comparable launch trajectory.\n\nBank of America analyst Justin Post reiterated a Buy rating and an $810 price objective, saying early traction is lifting sentiment on Meta’s AI strategy.\n\nMuse Is Outpacing ChatGPT’s Early Download Curve\n\nAfter 12 days, Muse had 1.43 million cumulative U.S. iOS downloads. \n\nChatGPT had 1.37 million over the same post-launch window, Gemini 0.71 million, Grok 0.36 million and Claude 0.11 million.\n\nAcross all U.S. platforms, Muse reached about 2.5 million downloads. \n\nFor comparison, Instagram had 1.6 million and ChatGPT 3.6 million over the same period.\n\nDaily downloads topped 300,000. Daily active users, the people who open the app on a given day, reached about 557,000 as of Sept. 19.\n\nThe app also holds a 4.9-star rating across more than 25,000 reviews.\n\nMeta Muse Is Showing Something Wall Street Was Missing\n\nPost said early reviews show Muse’s ability to handle "multi-step tasks and workflows with limited user intervention."\n\nThat distinction matters. Chatbots answer questions. Agents increasingly perform actions.\n\nPost said investors had been "concerned about Meta’s ability to build a differentiated AI product," but Muse’s functionality has driven greater optimism around returns on Meta’s AI investments.\n\nMeta now has something its AI spending previously lacked: a consumer product investors can measure.\n\nNat Friedman, head of product at Meta Superintelligence Labs, said in an X post that Muse was built from scratch but “heavily inspired as a product by openclaw.”\n\nWhy Investors Are Rerating Meta Stock\n\nThe stock surged 11.4% on Monday, its best single-day gain since April. On Tuesday, shares traded near $750.80, up 1.3%.\n\nSince Muse’s launch, Meta Platforms has gained over 20%. \n\nMeta now trades at 21 times its expected 2027 earnings, up from 16 times a few months ago, according to Bank of America.\n\nRevenue from ads, subscriptions or commissions inside Muse looks unlikely to be material before 2028, the note said. \n\nUntil then, the stock would depend on “multiple expansion, vs 2027 estimate revisions,” Post said.\n\nIn other words, investors would be paying a higher price for the same expected profits, rather than seeing those profit forecasts rise.\n\nThe next test arrives Wednesday at Meta Connect, where investors expect details on the Muse Spark model and early engagement trends.\n\nRead Also:\n\nAmazon Blocks Meta’s Muse AI From Shopping — Elon Musk Says AMZN ‘Won’t Be Able to Tell’ Humans From Agents\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'18cded0243b5e31f04f4bcaff79f70feb677e09f','2026-09-22 19:02:09','2026-09-22 19:34:52.218940',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 19:02:09');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(594,'alpaca:61932004','benzinga','2026-09-22 19:02:01','Gary Cardone Made $750,000 on Strategy''s STRC Instead of Bitcoin, Says He''ll Buy BTC at $70,000','Gary Cardone earned $750,000 from Strategy’s STRC while avoiding Bitcoin’s rally, expecting a possible pullback to the $70,000s.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61932004/gary-cardone-made-750000-on-strategys-strc-instead-of-bitcoin-says-hell-buy-btc-at-70000','["BTC/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-22 19:35:01.500504','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The statement reflects personal investment choices without significant market impact.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 19:34:52.246793','61932004',replace('Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) approached $86,000 after a 44% quarterly rally, but investor Gary Cardone says he isn’t chasing the move. \n\nCardone generated roughly $750,000 from Strategy’s (NASDAQ:MSTR) STRC while waiting for a better BTC entry.\n\n • Where is MSTR stock headed?\n\nCardone Says STRC Trade Paid Him $750K\n\nCardone told Scott Melker in an interview on Sep.22 that he could have bought Bitcoin around $98,000 several months ago but instead deployed capital into STRC near par.\n\n"I’ve made $750,000 on STRC while I didn’t know what the market was doing," Cardone highlighted, adding that the position paid him roughly $63,000 per month.\n\nHe said the income allowed him to acquire about 12 Bitcoin while avoiding much of crypto’s underlying price volatility.\n\nThe trade also gave him flexibility to eventually rotate back into cash and Bitcoin rather than remaining on the sidelines while waiting for lower prices.\n\nWhy Cardone Isn’t Chasing BTC\n\nCardone revealed he was bearish over the summer partly because he wanted to accumulate more Bitcoin at $57,000 or lower. \n\n"No one should chase Bitcoin ever again," he noted, and instead pay close attention to their entry price.\n\nCardone said he would not buy Bitcoin at $120,000 and suggested another move into the mid-to-low $70,000s remains possible.\n\nBitcoin’s recent rally does not mean prices will move straight higher.\n\nWall Street Is Taking Over Bitcoin\n\nDespite expecting another buying opportunity, Cardone sees Bitcoin’s market structure becoming stronger as institutional participation expands.\n\n"Wall Street’s taking over and it’s awesome," he said, describing the shift as evidence that Bitcoin is maturing.\n\nGrowing demand through spot Bitcoin ETFs and wealth-management channels could create a stronger underlying bid during future pullbacks.\n\nCardone ultimately expects Bitcoin to become increasingly valuable as collateral, allowing investors to borrow against their holdings rather than sell them.\n\nImage: Shutterstock\n\nRead Also:\n\nWhy Billionaire Tim Draper Calls Apple, Meta ''Irresponsible'' for Not Holding Bitcoin','\n',char(10)),'17c58b79a3015ca88db36f227bcf2798553a1c5e','2026-09-22 19:02:01','2026-09-22 19:34:52.218940',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 19:02:01');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(595,'alpaca:61931658','benzinga','2026-09-22 18:48:22','EXCLUSIVE: Nvidia Is a Stock And a Token — When ‘Retail No Longer Distinguishes Between Ticker and Rail’','Nvidia exposure is spreading from stocks to tokenized equities and crypto derivatives as traditional and digital trading rails converge.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61931658/nvidia-stock-token-crypto','["AAPL", "MSFT", "NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 19:35:02.406718','other','neutral',2,3,'days',1,'The headline discusses a trend without a direct impact on Nvidia''s price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AAPL": 337.09, "MSFT": 498.48, "NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 19:34:52.258276','61931658',replace('Nvidia Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) used to be a stock-market trade. Now, the same company can show up as a traditional equity, a tokenized stock and even a crypto-adjacent leveraged trade — sometimes for the same investor, on the same screen. CoinMarketCap’s data suggests the bigger story may be the trading rails connecting these markets.\n\nNvidia Leaves the Stock Market\n\n"The trending board is a real-time attention index for global retail," Alice Liu, Head of Research at CoinMarketCap, told Benzinga in an email. "Right now, it is telling us retail has stopped distinguishing between the ticker and the rail."\n\nCoinMarketCap’s trending board recently featured tokenized Nvidia alongside a tokenized Nasdaq-100 ETF, tokenized Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX), Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL), Micron Technology, Inc. (NASDAQ:MU), Microsoft Corp (NASDAQ:MSFT) and Alphabet Inc (NASDAQ:GOOGL) (NASDAQ:GOOG).\n\nRoughly one in four of the top 76 trending assets was a tokenized equity, Liu said. As of Sept. 10, the tokenized-stocks category on CoinMarketCap included 1,851 instruments with a combined market capitalization of about $2.3 billion and roughly $2 billion in daily trading volume — a market that barely existed 18 months earlier.\n\nThe striking part is not that Nvidia can be tokenized. The striking part is that the token can sit beside crypto-native assets on the same trading interface.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: Nvidia''s AI Token Trade Has a Catch\n\nSame Screen, Different Trade\n\nLiu described the shift as a convergence happening at the "distribution layer, not the asset layer."\n\nA tokenized Nvidia product can track Nvidia closely. CoinMarketCap’s NVDAX was roughly flat over the month covered by the interview, broadly matching the underlying stock.\n\nBut the surrounding crypto market can behave very differently.\n\nCoinMarketCap’s data showed tokenized stocks turning over roughly 89% of their market capitalization daily, compared with about 12% for meme tokens, 16% for AI tokens and less than 2% for Bitcoin. Equity perpetuals have also expanded rapidly, accounting for about half of Hyperliquid’s perpetual volume versus roughly 2% at the start of the year.\n\nThat creates a new market structure where an investor can move between traditional Nvidia exposure and crypto-style products without necessarily changing screens.\n\nThe Appeal is Partly Structural\n\nTokenized equities can trade 24/7, support fractional ownership and move across borders. Perpetual venues can also offer leverage that is unavailable through conventional cash equity markets.\n\nYet the scale remains tiny compared with Nvidia itself. Tokenized stocks have about $2.3 billion in market capitalization versus Nvidia’s roughly $5.4 trillion equity value.\n\nThat makes tokenization an access layer, not a replacement for the stock market.\n\nFor investors, the more consequential development may be what happens when traditional equities, crypto and derivatives increasingly share the same distribution infrastructure. Nvidia is simply one of the clearest examples of a market where the ticker may stay the same while the rail underneath it keeps changing.\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: ‘The AI Tag Is Free’: Crypto Is Finally Charging for AI Hype\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Sudarsan Thobias on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'89a1c600a2a5dd25cadd3424916b3235c1b7ab52','2026-09-22 18:48:22','2026-09-22 19:34:52.218940',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 18:48:22');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(596,'alpaca:61931641','benzinga','2026-09-22 18:46:22','Tesla Faces ‘Rampant Racism’ Allegations in Trial: What Investors Should Know','A lawsuit from 2022 against Tesla over allegations of racist behavior and illegal practices began its court case Monday. Here are the details.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/large-cap/26/09/61931641/tesla-faces-rampant-racism-allegations-in-trial-what-investors-should-know','["TSLA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 19:35:03.869912','legal','bearish',3,4,'weeks',1,'The trial could negatively impact Tesla''s reputation and stock price.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"TSLA": 366.04}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 19:34:52.261604','61931641',replace('A trial against electric vehicle giant Tesla Inc (NASDAQ:TSLA) began Monday. The lawsuit comes from 2022 and follows a history of allegations against the company, with some settled out of court.\n\n • What’s going on with TSLA shares today?\n\nCalifornia Civil Rights Department v. Tesla\n\nOpening statements began Monday in the trial of the California Civil Rights Department v. Tesla. Similar to past lawsuits against the company, allegations include usage of the N-word and other racist slurs.\n\nOther allegations include unequal pay and promotions for Black workers, bullying by supervisors, worker segregation and racist imagery at the California factory, according to a report from The Guardian.\n\nBenzinga reached out to Tesla for comment and did not hear back.\n\nCalifornia Civil Rights Department lawyer Brett Watson showed Judge Peter Borkon photographs from the Fremont factory of items like the N-word on a wall, "KKK," swastikas, the Confederate flag and "go back to Africa” on workplace areas such as lockers and lunch tables.\n\n"These experiences cannot be dismissed as a few bad apples … hundreds of complaints to Tesla and [the Civil Rights Department] will show these experiences were not isolated," Watson said.\n\nWatson accused Tesla of "rampant racism" that Tesla did not address for years.\n\nThe state of California called three witnesses after opening arguments, all former Black Tesla employees who witnessed or were subject to racism themselves while working at the Fremont factory.\n\nThe lawsuit was filed against Tesla back in February 2022.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Growth Stocks\n\nTesla has called the lawsuit "misguided" and denied wrongdoing, according to the report. The EV giant says it previously disciplined and terminated employees who were involved in wrongdoing.\n\nOn Monday, Tesla attorney Tyree Jones argued in opening statements that Black employees use language like the N-word with themselves.\n\n"The state is blaming the employer, when it’s the victim," Jones said.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla Gets Love From Ron Baron for Not Hitting Ducks: ‘Time to Buy The Stock is Now’\n\nWhat Happens Next\n\nThe trial is expected to last through Oct. 30.\n\nUnlike some past Tesla trials, this will not be decided by a jury, and instead will see Borkon make a final ruling.\n\nThere is no cap on damages, with Reuters estimating that a win by the state of California could mean tens of millions of dollars and changes to Tesla’s policies.\n\nTesla CEO Elon Musk is not expected to be called as a witness in the case and so far has not addressed the trial on social media in recent days.\n\nThe EV company has faced past allegations of racism before, including a 2022 case that saw a federal jury award former Tesla employee Owen Diaz $137 million. That sum was one of the largest awards ever from a discrimination lawsuit, but was later reduced to $15 million upon appeal and later to $3.2 million by a second jury after Diaz rejected the $15 million amount.\n\nThe potential loss of tens of millions of dollars for Tesla won’t be a huge financial loss, but the trial could have a larger impact on potential changes to the company’s factory policies and labor practices, along with getting negative attention for the way it treated workers in the past.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla Stock Down 29% from All-Time Highs, Analyst Sees 93% More Downside — ‘Sell the News’\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'9e8b63abac2f7cabff240107bb77c1da40f0740f','2026-09-22 18:46:22','2026-09-22 19:34:52.218940',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 18:46:23');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(597,'alpaca:61931556','benzinga','2026-09-22 18:43:37','Intuit Stock Slides Amid Meta''s AI Collaboration Uncertainty','Intuit shares are trading lower Tuesday amid concerns Meta&#39;s Muse AI agent could disrupt legacy software offerings.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/movers/26/09/61931556/intuit-stock-slides-amid-metas-ai-collaboration-uncertainty','["META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 19:35:05.158696','other','bearish',2,3,'days',1,'Concerns about potential disruption to Intuit''s software offerings.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 19:34:52.265056','61931556',replace('Intuit Inc. (NASDAQ:INTU) shares are slipping Tuesday as traders lean into a risk-off move in the stock, with enterprise software names broadly under pressure amid growing questions about whether Meta’s new Muse AI agent could reduce demand for legacy software offerings.\n\nIntuit stock is taking a hit today. What’s behind INTU decline?\n\nIntuit Drops Sharply Despite a Constructive Broader Market\n\nToday’s decline looks out of step with the rest of the market. The Nasdaq is up 0.66% and the S&P; 500 has added 0.08%, and Technology stocks as a group are higher by 0.55%. Seven sectors are advancing against just four declining, a backdrop that points to something specific to Intuit driving the move rather than a broader risk-off wave.\n\nIntuit’s own chart may offer a clue. Shares have slid considerably over the trailing 12 months, and traders have periodically used bounces back toward the stock’s moving averages as chances to lighten positions rather than buy in. Today’s weakness looks consistent with that same pattern playing out again.\n\nMuse Partnerships Raise Questions About Legacy Software Demand\n\nSeparately, a wave of new deals connecting Meta Platforms Inc.’s (NASDAQ:META) recently launched Muse AI agent to online shopping and checkout tools has investors rethinking how much business legacy software platforms might lose if AI agents start handling more day-to-day tasks on their own.\n\nPayPal Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ:PYPL) disclosed its own arrangement with Meta this week, saying the setup would let customers “seamlessly shop and check out using their Muse personal AI agents” anywhere PayPal is accepted.\n\nShopify Inc. (NASDAQ:SHOP) shares climbed too after revealing a comparable partnership, linking its merchant base directly into Muse so buyers can finish transactions through Shop Pay, the company’s streamlined one-click payment system. Shopify chief executive Tobias Lütke described the goal as making the Muse shopping experience “easy and delightful.”\n\nMeta chief executive Mark Zuckerberg confirmed the news on X, framing it as a way to help both shoppers and merchants while hinting that additional similar partnerships are on the way. Since these deals push commerce and payment activity through Meta’s own AI system rather than relying on dedicated third-party software, some investors appear to be weighing whether companies like Intuit could see less demand for their standalone tools as more everyday tasks shift toward agentic AI.\n\nWall Street Remains Bullish Despite Today’s Drop\n\nDespite today’s selloff, Intuit carries an overall Buy rating on Wall Street, with an average price target of $378. Recent analyst actions include Evercore ISI maintaining an Outperform rating with a $400 target on September 18, Mizuho maintaining an Outperform rating with a $430 target that same day, and Stifel maintaining a Hold rating with a $300 target, also on September 18.\n\nINTU Shares Are Slipping\n\nINTU Price Action: Intuit shares were down 4.79% at $289.56 at the time of publication on Tuesday, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTwilio Stock Jumps As Analysts See AI Agents Dialing Up Growth\n\nImage: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'cdd4d2da5263cd63766716acd749d770e2bb645b','2026-09-22 18:43:37','2026-09-22 19:34:52.218940',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 18:43:37');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(598,'alpaca:61931341','benzinga','2026-09-22 18:34:19','Meta Stock ‘Has More Room to Run’: Former Hedge Fund Manager Calls It His ‘Favorite Large-Cap Tech Stock’','Meta&#39;s recent stock surge could be only the beginning. Strong reviews for Muse have one investor calling for more upside.','https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/long-ideas/26/09/61931341/meta-stock-has-more-room-to-run-former-hedge-fund-manager-says','["AMZN", "META"]','stocks','2026-09-22 19:35:06.322506','analyst','bullish',3,3,'days',1,'A former hedge fund manager''s positive commentary on Meta indicates potential for further stock growth.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"AMZN": 251.18, "META": 682.7}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 19:34:52.268589','61931341',replace('Meta Platforms (NASDAQ:META) stock soared Monday on the strength of the company’s Muse AI Agent rollout. A former hedge fund manager thinks there’s more upside for the stock.\n\nMore Meta Stock Upside\n\nMeta shares jumped 11.4% on Monday taking shares to $741.24, adding over $200 billion to the company’s market capitalization.\n\nThe stock has surged in valuation since July 31, when former hedge fund manager Whitney Tilson recommended the stock to investors after earnings. The thesis was based on a drop in the shares amid capex concerns, as well as stock valuation.\n\nWhile the stock is up 23.5% since that call, Tilson calls Meta his "favorite large-cap tech stock" in a tie with Amazon.com Inc (NASDAQ:AMZN).\n\n"I think Meta has more room to run thanks to the rollout of Muse – a personal AI agent that completed multistep tasks across apps, browsers and devices," Tilson said.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMeta''s Muse Hits No. 1, Carrying AMD Into the $1-Trillion Club\n\nScott Galloway’s Muse Review\n\nTilson admits he has not yet tried out the Muse AI Agent, but shared a "raving review" given by his friend Scott Galloway.\n\n"The most successful companies have one thing in common: They are time machines. What do I mean by that? They give people time back," Galloway said.\n\nThe author calls Muse a "time machine" and says that that app already knows you based on your history with Instagram, Facebook and WhatsApp, something that would take another company months to build.\n\nTilson says Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg is doing what he promised: building consumer products, including a useful AI offering.\n\n"Galloway has been negative on the prospects for Meta for a very long time, so if he likes the product, it must really be good."\n\nMeta Stock Price Action\n\nMeta stock is up 0.9% to $748.04 on Tuesday versus a 52-week trading range of $520.26 to $770.60. Meta shares are up 15% year-to-date in 2026.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMark Zuckerberg Says ''More Partnerships'' Coming as Meta Teams With Shopify to Power AI Purchases: ''Shoppers Find More, Shops Sell More''\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'1019ed470d9659b3a1c3abe0a112924e9f315ca0','2026-09-22 18:34:19','2026-09-22 19:34:52.218940',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 18:34:19');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(599,'alpaca:61931324','benzinga','2026-09-22 18:33:57','QUICK SPARK: Nasdaq 100 on Track for Best 4-Year Rally Since 1999','The Nasdaq 100 is up 180% over four years, on pace for the best four-year run since the dot-com peak. Memory names are doing the work.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61931324/nasdaq-100-best-four-year-rally-since-1999-memory-chips-lead','["QQQ"]','stocks','2026-09-22 19:35:11.384836','macro','bullish',3,3,'weeks',1,'The positive trend suggests strong market performance throughout the Nasdaq 100.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"QQQ": 716.89}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 19:34:52.272075','61931324',replace('The Nasdaq 100 has gained 180.1% since the start of 2023, putting the tech-heavy index on track for its best four-year run since 1999. \n\nThe index — tracked by the Invesco QQQ Trust, Series 1 (NASDAQ:QQQ) — has recorded four straight 20%-plus years: 53.8% in 2023, 24.9% in 2024, 20.2% in 2025 and 21.3% so far in 2026.\n\nMemory and semiconductor stocks are carrying the index. \n\nSanDisk Corp. (NASDAQ:SNDK) has surged 695.8% year to date, Micron Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MU) 278.9% and Intel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) 229.6%\n\nSeagate Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:STX), Marvell Technology Inc. (NASDAQ:MRVL) and Arm Holdings plc (NASDAQ:ARM) each rallied over 200% thus far this year.\n\nDispersion is brutal with software names being the worst performers: Intuit Inc. (NASDAQ:INTU) has lost 56.2%, AppLovin Corp. (NASDAQ:APP) 51.8%. \n\nImage: Envato Elements\n\nRead Also:\n\nNasdaq 100 Flirts with Records, Oil Sinks for Fifth Day: Stock Market Today','\n',char(10)),'6443d8319678313d8bcb6ce4e2ec2f3d2f372a51','2026-09-22 18:33:57','2026-09-22 19:34:52.218940',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 18:33:57');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(600,'alpaca:61934916','benzinga','2026-09-22 20:40:49','Michael Burry Bets Against the Memory Boom: These ETFs Could Be Exposed if He’s Right','Michael Burry is betting against the memory boom as Chinese supply rises. Here’s why some semiconductor ETFs could face risks if his thesis plays out.','https://www.benzinga.com/etfs/sector-etfs/26/09/61934916/michael-burry-bets-against-the-memory-boom-these-etfs-could-be-exposed-if-hes-right','["NVDA"]','stocks','2026-09-22 21:35:27.175499','analyst','bearish',3,3,'days',1,'A prominent investor''s negative outlook may impact sentiment towards related ETFs.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"NVDA": 219.37}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-22 21:35:22.294264','61934916',replace('Michael Burry is doubling down on his bearish semiconductor thesis just as fresh warnings raise questions about how long the memory shortage can last.\n\nIn a recent Substack post, which he also highlighted on X, Burry cited Acer CEO Jason Chen’s comments that memory inventories are building and Chinese suppliers are releasing more volume into the market. Chen expects additional Chinese capacity to eventually pressure prices, with the impact becoming more visible from late 2027.\n\n"Regarding memory chips—which have seen the sharpest price surges this year—Chen observed that while many industry players continue to publicly predict price increases extending through the end of next year, the reality is that inventories are actually overflowing. Suppliers from…— Cassandra Unchained (@michaeljburry) September 22, 2026 \n\nBurry said the developments align with his view that the conventional memory shortage was partly created by manufacturers shifting capacity toward high-bandwidth memory (HBM) to meet surging AI demand. As production of conventional DRAM ramps back up, he believes the supply-demand balance could shift.\n\nAccording to an X post by Michael Burry Stock Tracker, Burry has shorted Micron Technology (NASDAQ:MU) and the iShares Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SOXX), while also holding bearish positions in NVIDIA Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA), Applied Materials (NASDAQ:AMAT), Nebius Group (NASDAQ:NBIS) and Palantir Technologies Inc (NASDAQ:PLTR).\n\nBreaking: Michael Burry just doubled down on his shorts He:• Added to Micron $MU shorts• Added to Nebius $NBIS shorts• Added to Semiconductor ETF $SOXX shorts• Added to Palantir $PLTR shorts• Bought more QXO $QXO• Bought more Build-A-Bear $BBW• Bought more Sprouts… pic.twitter.com/8PIP9GzxyT— Michael Burry Stock Tracker ♟ (@burrytracker) September 22, 2026 \n\nSOXX Has Direct Exposure to Burry’s Trade\n\nSOXX offers a particularly direct way to track the semiconductor trade Burry is challenging.\n\nMicron accounts for 8% of SOXX, Nvidia represents 7.5%, while Applied Materials has a 3.7% weight.\n\nThat means a reversal in the semiconductor cycle could have implications beyond individual memory stocks, particularly for broad semiconductor ETFs.\n\nChina Adds Another Supply Threat\n\nThe China factor makes the memory debate more complicated.\n\nChangXin Memory Technologies (CXMT) recently said its fifth-generation memory platform had entered mass production. The company is also expanding its manufacturing footprint as China seeks to increase domestic memory production.\n\nMeanwhile, Samsung, SK Hynix Inc (NASDAQ:SKHY) and Micron have redirected capacity toward HBM to capitalize on AI infrastructure spending.\n\nThat has created a delicate equation: AI demand is rising rapidly, but so is the industry’s incentive to add capacity.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nThe ETF Question\n\nThe key question for semiconductor investors is no longer simply whether AI demand remains strong.\n\nIt is whether new memory supply can grow faster than AI-driven demand.\n\nIf that happens, Burry’s trade could gain another data point and semiconductor ETFs such as SOXX and VanEck Semiconductor ETF (NASDAQ:SMH) could find themselves caught between the AI boom and the semiconductor cycle that follows it.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBillionaire Howard Marks Says America’s $40T Debt Problem Isn’t a Reason to Sell Stocks. Here’s Where ETFs Come In\n\nPhoto: This photo was created using artificial intelligence.','\n',char(10)),'60c9f5902003625791076a1985a5d131e2da3e84','2026-09-22 20:40:49','2026-09-22 21:35:22.255730',1,NULL,'2026-09-22 20:40:49');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(601,'alpaca:61937290','benzinga','2026-09-23 02:04:11','Bitcoin, Ethereum, XRP, Dogecoin Gain as Trump Touts ''Good Meeting'' With Iran: Analyst Says BTC ''Sitting'' Above Strong Support','Leading cryptocurrencies ticked higher on Tuesday, September 22, as investors digested President Donald Trump&#39;s latest remarks on Iran peace negotiations.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61937290/bitcoin-ethereum-xrp-dogecoin-gain-trump-iran-btc-support','["BTC/USD", "DOGE/USD", "ETH/USD", "SOL/USD", "XRP/USD"]','crypto','2026-09-23 02:35:45.542802','macro','bullish',2,3,'days',1,'Market reacts positively to geopolitical statements influencing investor sentiment.',1,'gpt-4o-mini','{"BTC/USD": 76528.6, "DOGE/USD": 0.081663915, "ETH/USD": 2445.59, "SOL/USD": 101.29, "XRP/USD": 1.30018}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 02:35:41.641113','61937290',replace('Leading cryptocurrencies ticked higher on Tuesday as investors digested President Donald Trump’s latest remarks on Iran peace negotiations.Cryptocurrency24-Hour Gains +/-Price (Recorded at 9:26 p.m. EDT)Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC)+1.10%$86,640.83Ethereum (CRYPTO: ETH)               +0.70%$2,767.86XRP (CRYPTO: XRP)                         +0.90%$1.59Solana (CRYPTO: SOL)                         +0.20%$118.97Dogecoin (CRYPTO: DOGE)             +0.30%$0.1024Crypto Market StabilizesBitcoin faced resistance near the upper-$86,000 range after climbing above $87,000 the previous day. Ethereum oscillated in the $2,700 region, while XRP and Dogecoin held on to their gains.Over $266 million was liquidated from the cryptocurrency market in the last 24 hours, as short positions suffered heavier losses than long bets, according to Coinglass data.Bitcoin’s open interest rose 0.85% over the last 24 hours. Binance’s retail derivatives traders held a net short position on Bitcoin, while whales marginally increased their long exposure.Market sentiment cooled from “Extreme Greed” to “Greed,” according to the Crypto Fear & Greed Index.Top Gainers (24 Hours) CryptocurrencyGains +/-Price (Recorded at 9:26 p.m. EDT)Bitcoin Cash (BCH)      +29.00%    $342.11Uniswap (UNI)                   +17.70%    $10.63Bitway (BTW)              +18.40%    $0.8967The global cryptocurrency market cap today is $3.03 trillion, marking a 0.5% change in the last 24 hours.\n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Just Hit a Seven-Month High. The Analyst Calling the Bottom Expects a Pullback\n\nNasdaq Rises to New RecordStocks delivered a mixed performance on Tuesday. The Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 185.14 points, or 0.36%, to end at 51,863.39. The S&P; 500 closed near flat at 7,764.64. The tech-focused Nasdaq Composite rallied 0.5% to close at a new record of 27,244.27.Investors remained on edge as Trump sent mixed signals on Iran. He told reporters that U.S. officials had a “very good” meeting with the Iranian delegation at the United Nations General Assembly.\n\nDuring the UNGA address, Trump said he has a “big decision” to make, whether to make a deal with Iran or “annihilate” the country.Bitcoin to Reclaim $100,000?Cryptocurrency analyst Ali Martinez identified Bitcoin’s “strong support” at $84,569, with additional support near $77,000, citing the Unspent Transaction Output Realized Price Distribution chart.The indicator maps out the exact price levels where existing coin supplies last moved or were acquired on-chain.“With support below, overhead resistance is thinning out,” Martinez added. “The next major URPD resistance sits near $104,765, where roughly 283,000 BTC were traded.”\n4/6 Meanwhile, Bitcoin is sitting above strong support at $84,569, where nearly 600,000 $BTC were previously traded. A second major demand zone sits near $77,000.With support below, overhead resistance is thinning out. The next major URPD resistance sits near $104,765, where… pic.twitter.com/BrofFv8Izv— Ali Charts (@alicharts) September 22, 2026 \nMichaël van de Poppe, another widely followed cryptocurrency commentator, anticipated Bitcoin’s potential liquidity sweep to $84,000“If the markets are giving me this opportunity, that’s where you’ll need to be getting interested in potential longs,” Van De Poppe added.\nAt some point, I''m going to be getting this sweep of the $84,000 level on #Bitcoin.I''m just putting it out here.If the markets are giving me this opportunity, that''s where you''ll need to be getting interested in potential longs. pic.twitter.com/SQ9WqTntUp— Michaël van de Poppe (@CryptoMichNL) September 22, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nGary Cardone Made $750,000 on Strategy''s STRC Instead of Bitcoin, Says He''ll Buy BTC at $70,000\n\nPhoto Courtesy: vinnstock on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'eadf68823131c4b86387f2f7fc3308838a505c1a','2026-09-23 02:04:11','2026-09-23 02:35:41.622484',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 02:04:11');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(602,'alpaca:61937464','benzinga','2026-09-23 03:07:29','Gary Black Cites Kalshi, Says Democrats Set for Senate and House Wins in Midterms—Crypto Punters Agree','Gary Black, managing partner at The Future Fund, pointed on Tuesday to growing odds of a Democratic sweep in both chambers of Congress in the November midterms.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61937464/gary-black-kalshi-democrats-senate-house-midterm-wins-crypto-punters','["BTC/USD"]','crypto',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 03:35:50.307676','61937464',replace('Gary Black, managing partner at The Future Fund, pointed on Tuesday to growing odds of a Democratic sweep in both chambers of Congress in the November midterms.\n\nDems Set to Win Midterms?\n\nCiting Kalshi, Black said Democrats have a 61% chance of taking control of the Senate and a 91% chance of winning the House.\n\nRepublicans currently hold a 53–47 majority in the Senate and control the House by a slim 218–214 margin. The midterm elections are scheduled for Nov. 3.\n\nKalshi now puts 61% odds on Dems taking back the U.S. Senate in November; Republicans now hold a 4-seat advantage 53-47. Kalshi now attaches a 91% chance to Dems taking control of the U.S. House which Rs now control 218-214 with 1 independent and 2 vacancies. 35 of 100 Senate…— Gary Black (@garyblack00) September 22, 2026 \n\nKalshi bettors priced in a 62% chance of a Democrat sweep, up from 46.5% a month ago.\n\nMeanwhile, the odds of the Democrats winning more than 52 seats in the Senate stood at 37%, alongside a14% chance of holding over 249 seats in the lower chamber.\n\nSource: Kalshi\n\nRead Also:\n\nEXCLUSIVE: ''Institutions Are Buying Bitcoin'' — Retail Is Trading Everything Else\n\nCrypto Bettors in Sync\n\nBettors on Polygon (CRYPTO: POL)-based Polymarket broadly agreed with their Kalshi counterparts, assigning a 66% chance of a Democratic sweep.\n\nDemocrats were the frontrunners to take control of the House, with 93% odds. The Senate race was closer, with Dems holding a 66% chance of reclaiming control.\n\nRead Also:\n\nWhy Billionaire Tim Draper Calls Apple, Meta ''Irresponsible'' for Not Holding Bitcoin\n\nKalshi and Benzinga have an existing data collaboration agreement.\n\nImage Courtesy: gguy on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'0e955e837fdbeba63eca03a0907730e537ecad92','2026-09-23 03:07:29','2026-09-23 03:35:50.302504',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 03:07:30');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(603,'alpaca:61937639','benzinga','2026-09-23 04:27:14','Gavin Newsom Says California Has ‘Strongest Data Center Protections In the Nation,’ Takes Aim at Trump’s Deregulation Push','Newsom says California enacted tough data center protections for electricity, water and land, while criticizing Trump’s deregulation approach.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61937639/gavin-newsom-says-california-has-strongest-data-center-protections-in-the-nation-takes-aim-at-trumps-deregulation-push','["NVDA"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 04:36:02.205299','61937639',replace('Gov. Gavin Newsom (D-Calif.) said the state has enacted new data center protections aimed at increasing oversight of rapidly expanding data centers and preventing their electricity, water and infrastructure costs from being shifted onto local communities and ratepayers, while criticizing President Donald Trump’s approach to deregulation.\n\nNewsom Targets Trump\n\nOn Monday, Newsom said on X that California had enacted the "STRONGEST data center protections in the nation."\n\n"We’re protecting Californians from higher costs and giving communities more control over their electricity, water, and land," he added.\n\nHe contrasted California’s approach with Trump’s policies, saying the president "pushes deregulation and lets industry reap massive profits at the expense of working people."\n\n"We’re making sure Californians remain in the driver’s seat," Newsom added.\n\nCalifornia just enacted the STRONGEST data center protections in the nation.We’re protecting Californians from higher costs and giving communities more control over their electricity, water, and land.While Donald Trump pushes deregulation and lets industry reap massive…— Gavin Newsom (@GavinNewsom) September 21, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Compares AI Data Centers To Oil Boom — Nvidia CEO Agrees\n\nNewsom Orders AI Oversight\n\nLast week, Newsom ordered officials to accelerate AI oversight and develop recommendations for an emergency “kill switch” for frontier AI models.\n\nNewsom’s order directs officials to implement recently enacted laws establishing independent AI verification organizations and a registry for AI auditors. \n\nExperts will also study whether frontier AI companies should have independent evaluators onsite and whether advanced models need emergency shutdown mechanisms.\n\n"The federal government’s abject failure to create any form of meaningful AI oversight or accountability should alarm every American," Newsom said.\n\nHe added, "With Donald Trump and Congress failing to lead, California is stepping up to keep all Americans safe."\n\nDebate Over AI Data Centers\n\nLast month, Nvidia Corp (NASDAQ:NVDA) CEO Jensen Huang defended the U.S. AI data center boom, saying it could boost manufacturing, create jobs and strengthen the power grid while urging developers to work with communities.\n\nRep. Ro Khanna (D-Calif.), however, warned that data centers were increasing environmental and infrastructure pressures and shifting costs to residents and utility ratepayers. \n\nHe supported giving communities more power to oppose projects.\n\nMeanwhile, investor Kevin O’Leary defended modern data centers over water-use concerns, arguing that newer facilities used closed-loop cooling systems and should not be compared with older facilities.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nHoward Lutnick Calls AI Data Center Water Concerns ‘Propaganda by Our Adversaries’ — Federal Research Tells a Different Story\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'018e8d8a2f9d23c2da8efe67e648c0667844714c','2026-09-23 04:27:14','2026-09-23 04:36:02.201445',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 04:27:14');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(604,'alpaca:61937628','benzinga','2026-09-23 04:26:29','Peter Schiff Says Michael Saylor''s ''Self-Serving'' Bullish Comments Behind Bitcoin''s ''Big'' Rally: He''ll Be ''Selling At Low Prices Again'' Soon','Economist Peter Schiff linked Bitcoin&#39;s latest spike to Strategy Inc.&#39;s acquisition and Michael Saylor&#39;s &#34;self-serving&#34; commentary.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61937628/peter-schiff-saylor-bitcoin-rally-selling-low-prices','["BTC/USD"]','crypto',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 04:36:02.207981','61937628',replace('Economist Peter Schiff linked Bitcoin’s (CRYPTO: BTC) latest spike to Strategy Inc.’s (NASDAQ: MSTR) acquisition and Michael Saylor’s “self-serving” commentary.\n\nSchiff Weighs in on BTC Rally\n\nBitcoin reached an intraday high of $87,363 on Monday, its highest since late January, and is up nearly 18% over the week.\n\nSchiff attributed the rally to Strategy’s purchase of 950 BTC for $75.7 million, which ended a nearly month-long buying pause.\n\nBitcoin rallied big yesterday. The catalyst seemed to be Strategy''s latest Bitcoin buy and self-serving bullish comments from @Saylor that the failure to pass the Clarity Act is actually bullish for Bitcoin. I''m sure he''d have said the same thing had the Act been passed into law.— Peter Schiff (@PeterSchiff) September 22, 2026 \n\nSchiff Jabs Saylor\n\nSchiff described Saylor’s remarks that the CLARITY Act’s failure marked a positive turning point for Bitcoin as "self-serving," which ended up being another catalyst for the rally.\n\n“I’m sure he’d [Michael Saylor] have said the same thing had the Act been passed into law,” the longtime Bitcoin critic took a dig.\n\nMy thoughts on why the rejection of CLARITY marks a positive inflection point for Digital Assets, and why supportive rules and free markets should now accelerate innovation and growth. https://t.co/qmahxXuG6L— Michael Saylor (@saylor) September 19, 2026 \n\nSchiff also slammed the company’s decision to sell Bitcoin at lower prices and later acquire it at higher prices.\n\n“It won’t be long before he’s selling at lower prices again,” the economist predicted.\n\nStrategy didn’t return Benzinga’s request for comment.\n\nDuring its last Bitcoin selling spree, Strategy sold 6,948 Bitcoin for approximately $431.8 million in net proceeds, or about $62,150 per Bitcoin. Now he''s buying back some of what he sold for over $80K per Bitcoin. It won''t be long before he''s selling at lower prices again.— Peter Schiff (@PeterSchiff) September 22, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nBitcoin Just Hit a Seven-Month High. The Analyst Calling the Bottom Expects a Pullback\n\nStrategy’s Impressive Rebound\n\nStrategy has flipped from a $10 billion unrealized loss to $8 billion unrealized profit in recent weeks, aided by Bitcoin’s rapid climb. MSTR was also the Nasdaq-100’s top performer over the past month, surging 48%.\n\nAs of this writing, Strategy holds 845,050 BTC, worth $73.34 billion, making it the world’s largest corporate buyer of the apex cryptocurrency.\n\nStrategy CEO Phong Le previously defended the firm’s practice of selling Bitcoin low and buying it high, adding that the company does not base its decisions specifically on the price of Bitcoin.\n\nPrice Action: As of this writing, BTC is up 0.80% in the last 24 hours to $86,475, according to Benzinga Pro. \n\nStrategy shares rose 0.37% in after-hours trading. The stock closed 0.69% lower at $167.33 during Tuesday’s regular trading session.\n\nAccording to Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings, MSTR displays a stronger price trend in the short and medium term, but trails over the long term.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Quality Stocks\n\nPhoto: Hi my name is Jacco on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'192c8426912704d5d3a49c526b700e80f16dc2ed','2026-09-23 04:26:29','2026-09-23 04:36:02.201445',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 04:26:30');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(605,'alpaca:61937563','benzinga','2026-09-23 03:54:22','Melania Trump to Ring NYSE''s Opening Bell Wednesday, Launch New Initiative for Female CEOs in Her ''Week of American Excellence''','First Lady Melania Trump will ring the NYSE&#39;s opening bell Wednesday and launch IMPERIA, an invite-only initiative for female CEOs.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/politics/26/09/61937563/melania-trump-nyse-opening-bell-female-ceos-initiative','["AMZN"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 04:36:02.212099','61937563',replace('First Lady Melania Trump will ring the New York Stock Exchange‘s opening bell Wednesday and launch IMPERIA, an invite-only initiative bringing together female CEOs, capping a high-profile week of appearances tied to the U.N. General Assembly. The NYSE is owned by the holding company Intercontinental Exchange Inc. (NYSE:ICE)\n\n‘A Week of American Excellence’\n\nThe NYSE announced on X that the First Lady will open the markets as the 81st U.N. General Assembly heads into its second day, with her keynote address following the opening bell.\n\nTomorrow, September 23, First Lady @MELANIATRUMP opens the markets from NYSE as the 81st @UN General Assembly continues. Tune in at 9:45AM ET for @FLOTUS'' keynote address following the Opening Bell. pic.twitter.com/trQWb4FuWf— NYSE 🏛 (@NYSE) September 22, 2026 \n\nIn a post on X on Saturday, Trump called it a “week of American Excellence” as she hosted world leaders, launched a new business initiative, and is expected to welcome Chinese President Xi Jinping and his wife, Madame Peng Liyuan to the White House. \n\nA WEEK OF AMERICAN EXCELLENCEA Global Coalition, Global Commerce, & Global Diplomacy Next week, the world will witness 3 impactful events, but what it won’t see is the months of vision, preparation, and relentless attention to detail required to create them. Tuesday, during… https://t.co/E8nx1AqVjE— MELANIA TRUMP (@MELANIATRUMP) September 20, 2026 \n\n In January, she opened the exchange to mark the release of her documentary.\n\nRead Also:\n\nCathie Wood Trims Alphabet Even as Google Regains Search Share, Ark Bets Big on This Space Stock\n\nA ‘Davos for Women’\n\nThe invite-only IMPERIA initiative brings together female CEOs and executives, aiming to build business relationships, move capital, influence policy, and foster collaboration across industries, her senior advisor Marc Beckman told USA Today. \n\nThe launch event, organized and hosted by the NYSE, is billed as a “Davos for Women,” a nod to the World Economic Forum’s annual gathering in Switzerland. \n\nAt Tuesday’s event, the First Lady welcomed leaders from nearly 60 nations, expanding the coalition’s membership, and announced new private-sector technology partnerships with Adobe Inc., Amazon.com, Inc., Intel Corp., Starlink, Google, and Zoom Communications Inc.\n\nPrice Action: NYSE’s parent company, Intercontinental Exchange Inc., closed 1.57% lower on Tuesday at $152.93 and gained 0.18% in extended trading.\n\nBenzinga edge rankings indicate Intercontinental Exchange’s stock has a Momentum in the 43rd percentile and a Growth score in the 25th percentile. \n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nImage via Shutterstock/ Evan El-Amin','\n',char(10)),'a68889d2c353368cd87894e119acade931c82ebf','2026-09-23 03:54:22','2026-09-23 04:36:02.201445',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 03:54:22');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(606,'alpaca:61937785','benzinga','2026-09-23 05:11:48','Gary Black Says Legacy Automakers Will Not License Tesla FSD, Instead Bet on In-House Self-Driving Efforts: ‘Inclined to Build’','Gary Black says legacy automakers won’t license Tesla FSD, preferring in-house autonomy as self-driving becomes essential.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61937785/gary-black-says-legacy-automakers-will-not-license-tesla-fsd-instead-bet-on-in-house-self-driving-efforts-inclined-to-build','["TSLA"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 05:36:22.300202','61937785',replace('Investor Gary Black says that legacy automakers such as General Motors Co. (NYSE:GM), Ford Motor Co. (NYSE:F) and others will not license Tesla Inc.‘s (NASDAQ:TSLA) Full Self-Driving (FSD) technology.\n\nLegacy Automakers Will Bet on In-House Self-Driving Efforts\n\nResponding to a post by Tesla investor and influencer Sawyer Merritt, the Future Fund LLC co-founder said that he had “predicted for years that no legacy auto makers would license $TSLA ‘s FSD technology from them.”\n\nThe investor added that “unlike charging capabilities, the legacy OEMS” would be “inclined to build” their own unsupervised autonomous technology as “autonomy becomes table stakes for remaining in the auto business.”\n\nI have predicted for years that no legacy auto makers would license $TSLA ‘s FSD technology from them. https://t.co/nUPlcBh78k. Unlike charging capabilities, the legacy OEMS are inclined to build unsupervised autonomy themselves as autonomy becomes table stakes for remaining…— Gary Black (@garyblack00) September 22, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nTesla’s Cybercab Strategy Hinges on One Giant, Unanswered Question\n\nNotably, Ford CEO Jim Farley had, during the company’s first-quarter 2026 earnings call in April, signaled that Ford is closely watching the robotaxi market. Ford’s upcoming Universal EV Platform will also support Level 3 autonomous driving capabilities.\n\nTesla’s Roadster Reservations, Ross Gerber Touts Waymo Lot\n\nTesla also opened up reservations for its upcoming high-performance vehicle Roadster ahead of its launch on October 1st. The automaker is charging $50,000 for reservations, including an initial $5,000 credit card payment that’s refundable followed by a $45,000 wire transfer payment no later than 10 days from the initial payment.\n\nOn the other hand, investor Ross Gerber of Gerber Kawasaki Wealth Management said that he had spotted a car lot filled with Alphabet Inc.‘s (NASDAQ:GOOGL) (NASDAQ:GOOG) Waymo Robotaxis, predicting that a major scaling up of operations could happen in California.\n\nNotably, Waymo recently expanded to Las Vegas, taking the total number of cities to 15 and has said that it plans to roll out its service in Tokyo next year.\n\nPrice Action: Tesla shares were up 0.05% to $379.10 during overnight trading on Tuesday. \n\nRead Also:\n\nTop Analyst Says There’s 80% Chance Could Put Tesla and SpaceX ‘Under One Hood’ by 2027 — ‘Golden Goose’ Could Create the ‘Biggest Company in the World’\n\nCheck out more of Benzinga’s Future Of Mobility coverage by following this link.','\n',char(10)),'167c37f1d4746cbc2f5a28fa5a9bd226113f3a17','2026-09-23 05:11:48','2026-09-23 05:36:22.200476',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 05:11:48');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(607,'alpaca:61938176','benzinga','2026-09-23 06:32:07','Apple Bringing Stablecoins to Billions of Devices? Binance CEO Weighs In After Job Listing Fuels Speculation','Binance Co-CEO Richard Teng reacted with interest on Tuesday, September 22, to speculation of Apple Inc. adding stablecoin support on Apple Pay.','https://www.benzinga.com/news/26/09/61938176/apple-stablecoins-billions-devices-binance-ceo-job-listing-speculation','["AAPL", "BTC/USD", "SOL/USD"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 06:36:36.272788','61938176',replace('Binance (CRYPTO: BNB) Co-CEO Richard Teng reacted with interest on Tuesday to speculation that Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) will add stablecoin support on Apple Pay.\n\nApple Set to Welcome Stablecoins?\n\n“Stablecoins on billions of devices?” Teng posted on X, paired with a wide-eyed emoji.\n\nCuriosity grew after Coin Bureau reported that Apple had posted a job listing seeking “stablecoin expertise” for its Apple Pay team.\n\nStablecoins on billions of devices? 👀 https://t.co/8tGDAGAwrT— Richard Teng (@_RichardTeng) September 22, 2026 \n\nNotably, the application, posted on Aug. 26, did not mention stablecoins, cryptocurrency or blockchain infrastructure—an observation echoed by Mike MacCana, a Solana (CRYPTO: SOL) software developer.\n\nThe role involves partnering with the Apple Card and Apple Cash teams to shape long-term strategy, identify growth and support business planning across wallets, payments, and commerce opportunities.\n\nApple didn’t immediately return Benzinga’s request for comment.\n\nThere is no mention of crypto, stablecoins or blockchain in that page.— Mike MacCana (@mikemaccana) September 22, 2026 \n\nRead Also:\n\nStock of the Day: Is Apple Breaking Out?\n\nApple’s Crypto Stance\n\nApple Pay does not natively support stablecoins, including USDC (CRYPTO: USDC), for direct consumer spending. However, you can use stablecoins indirectly through third-party cryptocurrency debit cards and payment networks like Mesh.\n\nApple’s former CEO Tim Cook said in 2021 that the company doesn’t invest in cryptocurrency because consumers do not buy AAPL stock for cryptocurrency exposure. He, however, admitted to owning cryptocurrency personally.\n\nBillionaire Tim Draper urged Apple to consider Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) exposure, citing Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (NASDAQ:SPCX) $1.6 billion BTC holdings as an example.\n\nPrice Action: Apple shares rose 0.03% in after-hours trading, according to Benzinga Pro. The stock closed 0.23% higher at $339.75 during Tuesday’s regular trading session. Year to date, the stock has rallied nearly 25%.\n\nApple stock maintains a stronger price trend over the short, medium, and long terms, according to Benzinga’s Edge Stock Rankings.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Adrian Tusar on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'c2ecdfcbf11315b29ae96fe41afd414b08f686a2','2026-09-23 06:32:07','2026-09-23 06:36:36.268140',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 06:32:07');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(608,'alpaca:61938049','benzinga','2026-09-23 06:03:48','Stock Market: Will S&P 500 Open Up or Down Today?','Will S&amp;P 500 open higher? Polymarket odds favor a green open as Wall Street digests cooling oil, Trump&#39;s UN address, and fresh AI momentum.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/prediction-markets/26/09/61938049/stock-market-will-sp-500-open-up-or-down-today-43','["META", "QQQ", "SPY"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 06:36:36.282736','61938049',replace('U.S. stock futures are posting slight gains early Wednesday as Wall Street digests an aggressive UN address from President Donald Trump on Iran, cooling crude oil prices, and fresh bullish momentum in the AI sector.\n\nThe Polymarket (CRYPTO: POL) crowd is leaning bullish for the Sept. 23 trading session. The “S&P; 500 (SPX) Up or Down on September 23?” contract currently reflects a 62% chance of a higher open.\n\nWhy That Number Matters\n\nTraders are navigating mixed geopolitical signals, falling energy markets, and incoming PMI data:\n\nPositive Index Futures: Equity futures are pointing to a green open across major benchmarks. Dow Jones futures rose 0.16%. S&P; 500 futures advanced 0.11%. Nasdaq 100 futures gained 0.06%, and Russell 2000 futures ticked up 0.02%.\n\nGeopolitics & Cooling Oil: Addressing the UN General Assembly, President Trump issued a stark ultimatum, stating he would “annihilate the Islamic Republic and do it quickly” if Iran does not reach a peace deal. Despite the rhetoric, Trump noted diplomacy remains possible after the November midterms, and U.S. envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held talks with Iran mediators. Consequently, energy prices dropped below the $100 mark; Brent crude fell 1.00% to $98.26 per barrel. WTI crude declined 1.65% to $89.03 per barrel.\n\nEarnings & Eco Data: Investors await September’s flash U.S. manufacturing and services PMIs, scheduled for release at 9:45 a.m. ET. Wednesday’s earnings docket includes major reports from Cintas Corp. (NASDAQ:CTAS), Paychex Inc. (NASDAQ:PAYX), General Mills Inc. (NYSE:GIS), and Cracker Barrel Old Country Store Inc. (NASDAQ:CBRL) among others.\n\nThe Bull Case and Market Outlook\n\nInstitutional confidence in the artificial intelligence buildout continues to strengthen, masking broader market anxieties. According to technology strategist Luke Lango, Meta Platforms Inc.‘s (NASDAQ:META) Muse app is tracking near 70% of ChatGPT’s historic adoption curve, suggesting it will generate massive, continuous inference compute demand.\n\nFurthermore, SoftBank’s recent $11 billion bond sale to fund its OpenAI investment was nearly 2x oversubscribed. Lango points out that this enthusiasm from conservative bond investors reflects genuine confidence in the durability of AI cash flows, rather than speculative hype.\n\nHow the Previous Bet Played Out\n\nThe Sept. 22 Polymarket contract resolved “Down.” The contract recorded $88,211 in total trading volume.\n\nOn Monday, the SPDR S&P; 500 ETF Trust (NYSE:SPY) and Invesco QQQ Trust ETF (NASDAQ:QQQ), which track the S&P; 500 and Nasdaq-100, respectively, closed mixed. SPY rose 0.016% to $773.38, while QQQ rose 0.81% to $747.46. Meanwhile, the Dow tracker, State Street SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust (NYSE:DIA), ended 0.34% lower at $518.00.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMcDonald''s Takes a Chance by Bringing Back Monopoly: Can It Change Its Fortunes Passing Go or Is the Stock Going to Remain in Jail?\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto courtesy: Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'767c9dd4a57ae3daa70517d5777c7d559a4185b3','2026-09-23 06:03:48','2026-09-23 06:36:36.268140',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 06:03:48');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(609,'alpaca:61937890','benzinga','2026-09-23 05:54:55','D-Wave, Rigetti and Other Quantum Stocks Are Trending Overnight: Here''s Why','IonQ shares surged 12.17% after hours, while D-Wave and Rigetti also gained as quantum stocks rallied Tuesday.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61937890/d-wave-rigetti-quantum-stocks-trending-overnight','["MSFT"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 06:36:36.286046','61937890',replace('Quantum computing stocks moved higher in after-hours trading Tuesday.\n\nIonQ Leads\n\nIonQ Inc. (NYSE:IONQ) surged 12.17% after hours to $45.70, the sector’s biggest mover. In the regular session the stock of the Maryland-based company edged 0.57% higher to $40.74, according to Benzinga Pro data. The company announced the industry’s first end-to-end real-time quantum error correction decoder that runs on a single, standard off-the-shelf CPU. IonQ said the decoder was validated across benchmark circuits simulating 408 logical qubits and more than 31.5 million quantum operations, adding just 0.02% processing overhead. Nicolas Delfosse, IonQ’s quantum research lead and paper co-author, said: “Successfully validating real-time decoding across hundreds of logical qubits and over millions of logical operations is an important milestone.”\n\nThe announcement came one day after IonQ announced a multiyear hardware agreement with South Korea’s SDT, Inc. Under the deal, IonQ will supply a Superion 256 quantum computer and silicon vacancy quantum memory modules.\n\nD-Wave, Rigetti Ride the Momentum\n\nD-Wave Quantum Inc. (NASDAQ:QBTS) gained 5.41% after hours to $18.51. In regular trading, the stock of the Palo Alto-based company dipped 0.79% to $17.56, according to Benzinga Pro data. The company this week appointed Bernard Gavgani, former Group Chief Information Officer of BNP Paribas, to its board of directors and cybersecurity committee. D-Wave said Gavgani’s experience in cybersecurity, risk management and large-scale technology transformation would support the company’s long-term strategy.\n\nRigetti Computing Inc. (NASDAQ:RGTI) rose 5.63% after hours to $17.45. In regular session, the stock of the Berkeley-based company slipped 0.06% to $16.52, according to Benzinga Pro data. Rigetti recently signed a definitive $100 million funding agreement with the U.S. Department of Commerce under the CHIPS Act to accelerate superconducting quantum computing R&D;, with the department receiving a minority equity stake in the company as a condition of the award.\n\nXanadu Recovers From a Rough Session\n\nXanadu Quantum Technologies Ltd. (NASDAQ:XNDU) added 2.58% after hours to $5.93. In regular session, the stock of the Toronto-based company tumbled 21.57% to $5.78, according to Benzinga Pro data.\n\nThe company announced on Tuesday Tara Deakin as Chief People Officer.Meanwhile, the sharp decline came as Xanadu’s IPO lock-up period expired, potentially allowing previously restricted shareholders to sell additional shares into the market.\n\nAnalyst Sentiment in Focus\n\nSector optimism was also reportedly bolstered by bullish notes on IonQ, D-Wave and Rigetti ahead of the Sep. 23-25 Quantum World Congress, where the Department of Energy, the White House Office of Science and Technology Policy, and executives from Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT) and IBM Corp. (NYSE:IBM) are expected to address the shift from quantum research toward commercialization.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Pete Hansen on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'d4ec110dfa668d4be86d2794e02fe437b56bcff7','2026-09-23 05:54:55','2026-09-23 06:36:36.268140',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 05:54:55');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(610,'alpaca:61937866','benzinga','2026-09-23 05:40:27','Australia’s Social Media Algorithm Rules Could ‘Facilitate Censorship,'' Says US Embassy: Will Influence What People ''See, Say and Hear''','On Tuesday, U.S. Embassy warns Australia’s social media rules could enable censorship and suppress protected speech.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61937866/australia-social-media-algorithm-rules-censorship-us-embassy','["META"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 06:36:36.288532','61937866',replace('The Donald Trump administration has raised concerns that Australia’s proposed social media algorithm rules could give regulators too much influence over how platforms recommend and filter content.\n\nUS Embassy Raises Censorship Concerns\n\nOn Tuesday, in a formal submission to Australia’s public consultation, the U.S. Embassy in Canberra said it had "serious concerns" about legislation that would dictate how social media platforms manage content and user feeds, Reuters reported.\n\nUnder the proposed rules, platforms would have to provide users with an algorithm-driven feed while also offering an option to view posts only from accounts they follow.\n\nThe U.S. said regulators could impose "one-size-fits-all" requirements, including chronological feeds or recommendation systems requiring user opt-in.\n\nWashington warned that such mandates could influence what people "see, say and hear" beyond Australia if global platforms adopt broader changes.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump Threatens to ‘Annihilate’ Iran If No Peace Deal Is Reached; Brent Hovers Near $100''\n\nUS Warns Rules Could Suppress Speech\n\nThe embassy also urged Australia to establish clear standards for determining what constitutes "harm" and "risk."\n\nIt warned that vague definitions could encourage platforms to over-moderate content to avoid regulatory penalties, potentially affecting protected speech based on viewpoint.\n\nThe U.S. said aggressively filtering algorithmic content could effectively suppress a speaker or media outlet even when the underlying content remains online.\n\n"The US government would likely consider" such a measure as "facilitating censorship," the embassy said.\n\nAustralia is seeking feedback from technology companies, industry groups, civil society organizations and advocates. The government expects to introduce the Digital Duty of Care legislation to Parliament later this year.\n\nSocial Media Rules for Children Under 16\n\nAustralia’s latest effort to address online harms comes less than a year after it introduced a social media ban for children under 16. Elon Musk’s X was the last major platform to comply, issuing a statement just hours before the deadline and saying, "It’s not our choice – it’s what the Australian law requires."\n\nByteDance’s TikTok, Snap Inc.’s (NYSE:SNAP) Snapchat and Alphabet Inc.’s (NASDAQ:GOOG) (NASDAQ:GOOGL) YouTube also notified users during the time.\n\nMeta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META), which owns Facebook and Instagram, said in August this year that it had deactivated more than 756,000 Australian accounts suspected of belonging to users under 16 as part of its compliance efforts.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nMelania Trump to Ring NYSE''s Opening Bell Wednesday, Launch New Initiative for Female CEOs in Her ''Week of American Excellence''\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Sasirin Pamai on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'28d49727b0944126ad62b5e290b2cf8343a2f967','2026-09-23 05:40:27','2026-09-23 06:36:36.268140',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 05:40:27');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(611,'alpaca:61938628','benzinga','2026-09-23 07:30:10','Bitcoin At $80,000 Today Vs. Bitcoin At $80,000 in May: ''Very Different,'' Says This Analyst','CryptoQuant Head of Research Julio Moreno contrasted Bitcoin crossing above $80,000 in September versus May, noting much stronger fundamentals today.','https://www.benzinga.com/crypto/cryptocurrency/26/09/61938628/bitcoin-80000-today-vs-may-analyst-different','["BTC/USD"]','crypto',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 07:36:47.738903','61938628',replace('CryptoQuant Head of Research Julio Moreno contrasted Bitcoin (CRYPTO: BTC) (CRYPTO: BTC) crossing above $80,000 in September versus May, noting much stronger fundamentals today.\n\nBulls Are Back?\n\nMoreno highlighted on X that Bitcoin’s Bull Score Index has risen to 80, flashing “Extra Bullish” sentiment. Back in May, at the same price, the score was only 50 and labeled "Neutral."\n\nThe Bull Score Index measures Bitcoin’s overall market cycle phase and ranges from 0 to 100. Scores above 60 are seen as bullish, indicating sustainable upward momentum and favorable market conditions.\n\nThe composite indicator measures network demand, stablecoin liquidity and trader profit margins to determine the scores.\n\nFundamentally, Bitcoin > $80K right now is very different from Bitcoin > $80K back in May.Bull Score Index (BSI) is at 80 right now (extra bullish, green), whereas it was at 50 (neutral, gray) back in May.Bull Score Index: https://t.co/NG7ruGAE8b pic.twitter.com/qn5E7Q56hY— Julio Moreno (@jjcmoreno) September 22, 2026 \n\nBitcoin Rebounds in Style\n\nBitcoin has surged 14% over the past week, hitting a seven-month high of $87,000, as broader cryptocurrency sentiment improved on the SEC’s push to build a regulatory framework for cryptocurrencies.\n\nStrategy Inc.’s (NASDAQ:MSTR) latest Bitcoin purchase following a nearly month-long buying pause also contributed to the rally.\n\nThe surge galvanized institutional demand as U.S. spot Bitcoin exchange-traded funds pulled in $998.95 million on Monday, their largest single-day inflow in 11 months.\n\nCryptoQuant founder Ki Young Ju noted that Bitcoin reclaimed the 365-day moving average at $83,000 and now sits above $84,000, a level widely watched as the line separating the bear market from the bull market. \n\nRead Also:\n\nStrategy Swings From $10B Loss to $8B Profit as Bitcoin Hits $85K\n\nOdds for $100,000 Spike\n\nCryptocurrency analyst Kevin Capital, however, does not expect Bitcoin to move straight up, adding that a run toward $93,000-$100,000 could set up a correction.\n\nPolygon (CRYPTO: POL)-based Polymarket now sees a 42% chance that Bitcoin will top $100,000 before the year ends, up from 16% the week before.\n\nSource: Polymarket\n\nPrice Action: As of this writing, BTC is up 1.20% in the last 24 hours to $86,483.14, according to Benzinga Pro. \n\nRead Also:\n\nPeter Schiff Says Michael Saylor''s ''Self-Serving'' Bullish Comments Behind Bitcoin''s ''Big'' Rally: He''ll Be ''Selling At Low Prices Again'' Soon\n\nPhoto Courtesy: KateStock on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'8c0d21599ac33eb7ccf6eb001e28579b1722ead6','2026-09-23 07:30:10','2026-09-23 07:36:47.735146',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 07:30:10');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(612,'alpaca:61938598','benzinga','2026-09-23 07:20:40','AI Boom Will Dwarf the Industrial Revolution, Push Real GDP Growth to 7%: Cathie Wood Says, ''Get on the Right Side of Change''','Ark Invest CEO Cathie Wood said the AI-driven technology revolution could reshape the global economy more powerfully than the Industrial Revolution.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/economic-data/26/09/61938598/cathie-wood-ai-boom-industrial-revolution-real-gdp-growth-7-percent','["QQQ"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 07:36:47.742708','61938598',replace('Ark Invest CEO Cathie Wood said the artificial intelligence-driven technology revolution underway will reshape the global economy more powerfully than the Industrial Revolution.\n\nTechnology Revolution Reshaping Global Economy\n\nIn her latest investor letter, published Tuesday, Wood said the shift will show up directly in economic growth and inflation data, as advances in AI and other technologies drive productivity higher and push costs down. \n\nShe called the current environment “back-to-the-future.”\n\nWood highlighted five innovation platforms — AI, robotics, energy storage, blockchain technology, and multiomics sequencing — as technologies that could meaningfully impact economic growth and inflation.\n\nAs the stock market hits record highs in the face of higher interest rates, I believe the current Technology Revolution will continue to impact the global economy and equity markets more than the Industrial Revolution. This letter charts that perspective back through the 1800s. https://t.co/oVyTMvcRCW— Cathie Wood (@CathieDWood) September 22, 2026 \n\n“In our view, bottom line, get on the right side of change and ride this innovation super cycle!” she added. \n\nRead Also:\n\nApple Pendant? Tim Cook, Eddy Cue Also Reportedly Throwing Weight Behind Another Mystery Device, Says This Analyst\n\nAI’s Falling Costs Could Fuel a Deflationary Boom\n\nThe investor said the cost of AI inference fell by more than 99% per year, while demand for AI inference tokens surged 25-fold in 2025.\n\nWood added that productivity gains could create a "deflationary boom," allowing the economy to grow faster even as technology companies reduce the cost of products and services. \n\nRising memory chip prices amid a global supply shortage have pushed up costs in the AI buildout, with the crunch expected to persist until 2028 as manufacturers work to expand capacity.\n\nReal GDP growth could accelerate to 7% or more over the next five years, Wood said, driven by technology-enabled productivity gains, compared with roughly 3% since the Industrial Revolution. \n\nFor the second quarter, real GDP grew at an annual rate of 1.5%, down from 2.1% in the first quarter.\n\nThe Market Backdrop\n\nThe S&P; 500, which is up 13.21% so far this year and 16.64% over the past year, ended Tuesday essentially flat. Meanwhile, the tech-heavy Nasdaq-100 climbed 0.82% to a fresh high. \n\nThe Nasdaq-100 is up 21.92% and 25.03% over 2026 and the past year, respectively. \n\nThe Invesco QQQ Trust (NASDAQ:QQQ) has climbed 21.91% year-to-date and has returned 24.95% over the past year. \n\nThe iShares PHLX SOX Semiconductor Sector Index Fund (NASDAQ:SOXX) has gained 82.59% so far this year and climbed 112.53% over the past year. \n\nPrice Action: QQQ Trust closed 0.81% higher on Tuesday at $747.46 and rose 0.12% in extended trading. \n\nBenzinga edge rankings indicate Invesco QQQ Trust has a Momentum score in the 78th percentile and a positive price trend in the short, medium, and long term. \n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nPhoto Courtesy: jira pliankharom on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'d40a5e7e8a1a4f5638d425711dd87f67efdc632b','2026-09-23 07:20:40','2026-09-23 07:36:47.735146',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 07:20:40');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(613,'alpaca:61938327','benzinga','2026-09-23 06:45:40','Apple Pendant? Tim Cook, Eddy Cue Also Reportedly Throwing Weight Behind Another Mystery Device, Says This Analyst','Apple is reportedly developing a screen-free fitness tracker and AI pendant to expand beyond the Apple Watch.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61938327/apple-pendant-tim-cook-eddy-cue-mystery-device-analyst','["AAPL"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 07:36:47.754027','61938327',replace('Apple Inc. (NASDAQ:AAPL) is reportedly working on a new screen-free fitness tracker and an AI-heavy pendant to broaden its wearable lineup beyond the Apple Watch.\n\nApple Tests Screen-Free Fitness Tracker\n\nThe screen-free health and fitness tracker will resemble Whoop’s bands, according to Bloomberg’s Mark Gurman.\n\nThe tech giant has reportedly developed prototypes, but nothing is certain yet. The device could have a fabric band with sensors that monitor heart rate and other health metrics.\n\nAccording to Gurman, former Apple CEO and now chairman Tim Cook and services chief Eddy Cue are "throwing their weight behind the product."\n\nNEW: Apple is developing a Whoop competitor. https://t.co/Mz0Ua1qk9r pic.twitter.com/CnFbUBTRjp— Mark Gurman (@markgurman) September 22, 2026 \n\nWhile the future of this device remains uncertain, Gurman said that if Apple proceeds with this tracker, it is unlikely to arrive before 2028.\n\nRead Also:\n\nWhy Billionaire Tim Draper Calls Apple, Meta ''Irresponsible'' for Not Holding Bitcoin\n\nApple’s AI Pendant Could Bring Camera-Powered Siri\n\nIn a separate post on X, Gurman noted that Apple has also been working on an AI pendant. This device will have a camera and could hang around the neck or attach to clothing.\n\nThe columnist reported that development has been postponed, but if it works, it could give Siri more "visual data" to process.\n\nApple has also been working on an AI pendant with a camera, though that project has been postponed. The device was conceived as something users could wear as a necklace, attach to clothing or place elsewhere on the body, gathering visual data for processing by the new Siri AI. https://t.co/4X55GDMihT— Mark Gurman (@markgurman) September 22, 2026 \n\nApple did not immediately respond to Benzinga’s request for comment.\n\nApple Expands Health Tracking Beyond the Watch\n\nThe latest Apple Watch model has features that overlap with competitors. This includes readiness scores and biological-age estimates. The company is currently testing a redesigned Health app in iOS 27.2.\n\nIn its latest earnings report in July, Apple noted $7.88 billion in revenue from its Wearables, Home and Accessories segment. This figure is up from $7.40 billion a year earlier.\n\nPrice Action: On Tuesday, Apple closed at $339.75, up 0.23%. The stock was trading at $339.84 in after-hours trading, up 0.026%, according to Benzinga Pro.\n\nAccording to Benzinga Edge Stock Rankings, Apple ranks in the 97th percentile for Quality, while its stock shows positive short-, medium- and long-term price trends.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Quality Stocks\n\nPhoto Courtesy: Laura Hutton on Shutterstock.com','\n',char(10)),'93e7bfe35470f3cd815294451d923d5819ae26cd','2026-09-23 06:45:40','2026-09-23 07:36:47.735146',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 06:45:40');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(614,'alpaca:61939050','benzinga','2026-09-23 08:28:40','AI Trade Is ‘Dead Money’: Fidelity Strategist Warns $3.3 Trillion Buildout Is Inflationary With ‘Unknown Returns’','The AI trade has been &#39;dead money&#39; for months, Fidelity&#39;s Jurrien Timmer said, even as hyperscalers keep spending billions.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/equities/26/09/61939050/ai-is-dead-money-right-now-jurrien-timmer-says-could-a-productivity-miracle-still-be-coming','["AMZN", "META", "MSFT", "QQQ"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 08:36:59.026407','61939050',replace('The artificial intelligence trade has been “dead money” for more than three months, Director of Global Macro at Fidelity Investments, Jurrien Timmer, said Tuesday, even as hyperscalers keep pouring hundreds of billions into the technology’s buildout.\n\n‘The Price of Memory Seems to Be the Only Thing Still Going Up’\n\n“On the AI front, the trade has been dead money for more than 3 months now,” Timmer said in a post on X, adding that token expenditures and GPU lease rates are “all flat to down.”\n\nMeanwhile, the price of memory seems to be the only thing that is still going up, he added. \n\nFidelity data show the Silicon Data LLM token expenditure index down 49% on a 50-day basis, while GPU rental rates for both H100 and A100 chips have cooled sharply after peaking earlier this year at gains of 56% and 16%, respectively. \n\nOn the AI front, the trade has been dead money for more than 3 months now. The metrics I am following (token expenditures and GPU lease rates) are all flat to down. The price of memory (DRAM) seems to be the only thing that is still going up. 🧵(1/2) pic.twitter.com/jU3wGienuP— Jurrien Timmer (@TimmerFidelity) September 23, 2026 \n\nA global memory chip shortage has pushed up costs across the AI buildout, a crunch expected to persist until 2028.\n\nA $3.3 Trillion Capital Grab With No Guaranteed Return\n\nTimmer said the buildout “is inflationary with an unknown return for the companies who are investing trillions into compute,” adding that corporate demand for capital, both debt and equity, is climbing at “a $3.3 trillion clip.”\n\nU.S. hyperscalers are on pace to spend roughly $916 billion on capital expenditures over the next 12 months, with combined capex from Alphabet Inc. (NASDAQ:GOOG)(NASDAQ:GOOGL), Amazon.com, Inc. (NASDAQ:AMZN), Microsoft Corp. (NASDAQ:MSFT), Meta Platforms Inc. (NASDAQ:META), Oracle Corp. (NYSE:ORCL), and Space Exploration Technologies Inc. (NASDAQ:SPCX) expected to exceed $1 trillion in 2027.\n\n‘Down the Road, It May Well Unleash a Productivity Miracle’\n\nDespite the near-term stall, Timmer said he still believes AI “will change our lives” and could eventually “unleash a productivity miracle that raises the economy’s non-inflationary speed limit.” \n\nArk Invest’s Cathie Wood believes the AI revolution could ultimately dwarf the Industrial Revolution’s economic impact, projecting real GDP growth could hit 7% or more within five years.\n\nPrice Action: The Invesco QQQ Trust (NASDAQ:QQQ) closed 0.93% higher on Tuesday at $$747.46 and rose 0.12% in extended trading, while the iShares PHLX SOX Semiconductor Sector Index Fund (NASDAQ:SOXX) gained 2.56% to close at $572.78 and rose 0.15% in after-hours. \n\nBenzinga edge rankings indicate Invesco QQQ Trust has a Momentum score in the 78th percentile and a positive price trend in the short, medium, and long term.\n\nSee More:\n\nTop Momentum Stocks\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'f149f68074ac78a868656d7e842ca4b3f8a49c81','2026-09-23 08:28:40','2026-09-23 08:36:59.022333',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 08:28:40');
INSERT INTO main_app_newsitem VALUES(615,'alpaca:61938821','benzinga','2026-09-23 07:58:41','Broadcom Faces China Data Center Threat as Beijing Finds Its Switches in Up to 90% of State-Owned Firms: Report','China probes Broadcom’s data center switches as Beijing pushes state-backed facilities to adopt domestic chip technology.','https://www.benzinga.com/markets/tech/26/09/61938821/broadcom-faces-china-data-center-threat-as-beijing-finds-its-switches-in-up-to-90-of-state-owned-firms-report','["AMD", "NVDA"]','stocks',NULL,'','',0,0,'',1,'',1,'','{}','{}',NULL,'2026-09-23 08:36:59.037231','61938821',replace('Chinese authorities are reportedly probing the use of hardware from Broadcom Inc. (NASDAQ:AVGO) in state-backed data centres.\n\nChina’s State-owned Assets Supervision and Administration Commission (Sasac) has been evaluating the prevalence of Broadcom switches in state-controlled data centres to boost domestic reliance, the Financial Times reported Tuesday. These high-end switches are essential for transmitting large volumes of data at high speeds in data centres.\n\nThe investigation is part of Sasac’s “domestic chips for domestic use” campaign, which aims to boost the utilization of homegrown semiconductors and AI products across China’s public sector. Preliminary findings indicate that Broadcom switches could be present in up to 90% of state-owned companies, according to the report.\n\nThis high penetration rate might prompt Sasac to issue informal guidance to decrease the use of Broadcom switches in domestic data centres, as per the report. \n\nThe commission is also investigating whether Broadcom has exploited its market leader status to bundle other products or enforce large purchase requirements. The U.S.-tech giant’s alleged tactics are said to have limited Chinese firms such as H3C Technologies and Ruijie Networks from sourcing switches from other suppliers, including Huawei, the publication reported.\n\nBroadcom did not immediately respond to Benzinga’s request for comments. \n\nRead Also:\n\nAlibaba Just Supercharged its AI Ambitions: New Zhenwu V900 AI Chip Promises 3X Performance, Targets 20GW Data Center Expansion by 2032\n\nNvidia, AMD Caught Amid China’s Domestic Tech Push\n\nThis development comes as part of China’s broader push to strengthen its domestic AI infrastructure. Broadcom, Nvidia Corp. (NASDAQ:NVDA) and Huawei sell high-end switches in China, with state-backed data centers still using a significant number of Broadcom switches despite restrictions on Nvidia products, as per FT. \n\nLast week, Chinese tech giant Huawei unveiled over 10 new chipsets for AI computing infrastructure. The move is seen as a bid to challenge the dominance of Nvidia, Advanced Micro Devices (NASDAQ:AMD), and Intel Corp. (NASDAQ:INTC) in the market.\n\nEarlier this month, Chinese AI chipmaker Enflame Technology surged more than 223% in its Shanghai debut after raising 6.12 billion yuan ($912 million) in its IPO, as investors bet domestic chipmakers can challenge Nvidia’s dominance in China’s AI accelerator market.\n\nDisclaimer: This content was partially produced with the help of AI tools and was reviewed and published by Benzinga editors.\n\nRead Also:\n\nTrump May Hold Off on Major Taiwan Arms Deal Until Year-End as China''s Xi Jinping Visits Washington: Report\n\nImage via Shutterstock','\n',char(10)),'8cc4293eb3c149dbc716c8fa0f6ed79d9a867d52','2026-09-23 07:58:41','2026-09-23 08:36:59.022333',1,NULL,'2026-09-23 07:58:41');
INSERT INTO main_app_newssession VALUES(1,'2026-09-15 23:14:13.634663','2026-09-15 23:15:20.920566','gpt-5.6-sol','The dominant tape is macro risk-off: oil above $105 and the 10-year yield above 5% are pressuring growth stocks ahead of a heavily anticipated Fed hike. Crypto faces an additional regulatory setback from the CLARITY Act negotiations, but this desk cannot express that bearish view because crypto is long-only. Most AI and single-stock stories are commentary or distant themes rather than fresh catalysts.',40,1,0,0.041970000000000000639,67.286032915115354668,'');
