cts": ["last_close", "evidence:TSLA prior close"]}, {"claim": "The Texas solar project received a local tax incentive, but it remains conditional and operationally distant rather than a near-term trading catalyst.", "facts": ["evidence:Texas solar tax incentive"]}, {"claim": "The stock is not technically extended at either extreme of the supplied 20-day range.", "facts": ["position_in_20d_range", "distance_from_50d_mean_pct"]}]','[{"claim": "Cybercab compliance is under an active NHTSA Audit Query focused on self-certification of a vehicle lacking traditional human controls.", "facts": ["evidence:NHTSA audit announcement"]}, {"claim": "Today\u2019s report adds a near-dated response deadline and identifies questions on current safety-standard compliance, increasing headline risk into September 30.", "facts": ["evidence:Cybercab special-order report"]}, {"claim": "Fundamental context is vulnerable: earnings growth is negative while valuation and estimate-revision balance are unfavorable.", "facts": ["earnings_growth_yoy", "trailing_pe", "forward_pe", "eps_revision_balance"]}]','[{"condition": "NHTSA or another federal authority issues a new enforcement action, stop-deployment order, recall, denial, or formal finding against Cybercab.", "direction": "bearish", "metric": "regulatory_action", "comparator": "any", "threshold": null, "window_hours": 24}, {"condition": "Tesla files or publicly releases its sworn Cybercab response and it confirms unresolved compliance gaps or deployment restrictions.", "direction": "bearish", "metric": "cybercab_response_risk", "comparator": "any", "threshold": null, "window_hours": 24}, {"condition": "Tesla files or publicly releases its sworn Cybercab response and it confirms full compliance with no deployment restriction, while TSLA holds above the supplied last close.", "direction": "bullish", "metric": "last_price", "comparator": "gt", "threshold": 358.1, "window_hours": 24}, {"condition": "A fresh regulatory headline is followed by TSLA trading below the supplied 20-day low.", "direction": "bearish", "metric": "last_price", "comparator": "lt", "threshold": 335.7, "window_hours": 24}]',replace('**Decision: no trade.** The only actionable firm-specific item is regulatory and bearish: NHTSA’s Cybercab self-certification audit is confirmed, and the reported special order requires sworn answers to 21 questions by September 30. The issue goes directly to whether a vehicle without conventional human controls complies with current federal safety standards. [NHTSA Cybercab audit; evidence:NHTSA audit announcement; evidence:Cybercab special-order report]\n\nThis is not a fresh enough clean short catalyst for the desk’s 240-minute trade. The original audit was public on September 4, and today’s report is elaboration of that process rather than a new restriction, recall, halt, or adverse ruling. The supplied last close is 358.1 USD [last_close], versus the reported prior regular-session close of 356.58 USD [evidence:TSLA prior close], so the available tape check does not show an obvious immediate repricing lower after the story. Do not force a short just because the headline is negative.\n\n**Context:** TSLA is near the middle of its 20-day range [position_in_20d_range] and only modestly above its 50-day mean [distance_from_50d_mean_pct], so technical position does not supply a stretched-entry advantage. Estimate revisions are unfavorable: 4 upward revisions versus 15 downward revisions [eps_revisions_up_30d; eps_revisions_down_30d], with a -57.89% revision balance [eps_revision_balance]. Market regime is also soft, with SPY and QQQ both near the lower end of their 20-day ranges [MARKET REGIME]. That supports caution but cannot turn this already-public regulatory story into a higher-conviction intraday short.\n\n**Thesis:** Revenue growth remains positive [revenue_growth_yoy], but earnings growth is negative [earnings_growth_yoy] and valuation is demanding on both trailing and forward P/E [trailing_pe; forward_pe]. The regulatory review is material to the autonomous-vehicle narrative, while the Texas solar-project approval is a long-dated, conditional capital project—not a near-term earnings catalyst. The desk should wait for a genuinely new regulatory action or a verified Tesla response, then trade only if price confirms.','\n',char(10)),'','',NULL,4,3,3,'none',0.33000000000000002664,0.6,0.070000000000000008881,0.34000000000000003552,NULL,NULL,0.32201646090534978839,0.25,'No position today: the NHTSA audit is genuine but was announced on September 4, while the September 16 article mainly details the already-open process. The reported prior close and supplied last close do not establish immediate downside confirmation. With a 240-minute holding limit, this is headline','dropped: NHTSA audit announcement: no value | catalyst undated or stale, demoted to context',0,'gpt-5.6-terra','flex',1,27630,2360,686,0.046723999999999996646,26.980474948883057528,'',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'',NULL);
