 is the September 18 worldwide availability of the new iPhone, Watch, and AirPods lineup; it is already two calendar days old as of the stated time and cannot justify an intraday entry now. Apple is also near the top of its recent range (position_in_20d_range) and above its 50-day mean (distance_from_50d_mean_pct), while current-quarter estimate revisions are net negative (eps_revision_balance). The official product rollout supports the medium-term product-cycle thesis, but it is not a fresh trading trigger. Retain the supplied no-news base-rate distribution for the defined 240-minute setup rather than inventing an edge. In addition, the stated timestamp is Sunday, September 20, 2026, when regular U.S. equity trading is closed.','','',NULL,1,3,6,'none',0.36600000000000001421,0.57899999999999991473,0.055,0.37000000000000001776,0.31000000000000000888,0.42999999999999998223,0.36625514403292180887,0.25,'Veto: no qualifying fresh Apple catalyst, the defined setup’s supplied no-news base rate is unfavorable, and the stated time falls on Sunday, September 20, 2026, outside regular U.S. equity-market hours. Do not carry a position into the October 29, 2026 earnings release (next_earnings_date).','',0,'gpt-5.6-terra','flex',1,16026,1568,588,0.030367999999999999438,15.537502765655517578,'',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'',NULL);
