ic earnings, guidance, contract, regulatory, or product catalyst for the next regular session.", "facts": ["official Microsoft September 21 India South Central announcement", "next_earnings_date"]}, {"claim": "The stock is above its 50-day mean while QQQ is near the top of its recent range, leaving less room for a weak catalyst to produce clean upside follow-through.", "facts": ["distance_from_50d_mean_pct", "qqq_position_in_20d_range", "qqq_distance_from_50d_mean_pct"]}, {"claim": "For the prescribed 240-minute geometry, MSFT\u2019s observed no-news stop-first frequency substantially exceeds its target-first frequency; weak analyst commentary is not sufficient evidence to alter that base rate.", "facts": ["measured base rate: target first", "measured base rate: stop first", "measured base rate: neither"]}]','[{"condition": "MSFT trades above the 20-day high on sustained regular-session trading after a timestamped company disclosure of material Azure demand, pricing, guidance, or a named customer order.", "direction": "bullish", "metric": "last price", "comparator": "gt", "threshold": 517.8, "window_hours": 240}, {"condition": "MSFT trades below the 20-day low, indicating the supportive estimates and AI-capacity narrative are not supporting price.", "direction": "bearish", "metric": "last price", "comparator": "lt", "threshold": 481.9, "window_hours": 240}, {"condition": "Microsoft releases timestamped guidance, an earnings preannouncement, or a material customer/capacity disclosure that explicitly changes near-term revenue or margin expectations.", "direction": "bullish", "metric": "company disclosure", "comparator": "any", "threshold": null, "window_hours": 24}, {"condition": "Microsoft releases timestamped guidance, a capacity-delay disclosure, or a material regulatory/customer development that explicitly reduces near-term revenue or margin expectations.", "direction": "bearish", "metric": "company disclosure", "comparator": "any", "threshold": null, "window_hours": 24}]',replace('**No trade today.** There is no verified, timestamped MSFT-specific event with enough immediacy or cash-flow significance to override the symbol’s measured no-news tape. Microsoft did announce its India South Central datacenter region on September 21, but the official item provides a publication date rather than a precise event time; it is a capacity-expansion announcement, not new guidance, an earnings release, a contract award, or a disclosed pricing change. ([news.microsoft.com](https://news.microsoft.com/source/asia/2026/09/21/ai-ambition-into-action-microsoft-brings-ai-ready-capabilities-across-its-india-cloud-infrastructure-establishes-india-south-central-region-as-a-strategic-hub-for-asia-and-global-south/?utm_source=openai)) The closest market read is muted: the news feed showed MSFT at $501.61 at the September 21 close and $501.49 after hours, not evidence of a fresh repricing. ([benzinga.com](https://www.benzinga.com/quote/MSFT/news?utm_source=openai))\n\nContext is constructive but not an intraday entry signal. Estimates are being raised on balance [eps_revisions_up_30d; eps_revisions_down_30d; eps_revision_balance], while the stock is in the middle of its 20-day range [position_in_20d_range]. It is nevertheless materially above its 50-day mean [distance_from_50d_mean_pct] while broad technology is near the top of its own 20-day range [qqq_position_in_20d_range]; that combination argues for smaller risk, not a chase. The structural picture remains favorable—growth, margins, and the latest filed quarter are strong [revenue_growth_yoy; earnings_growth_yoy; gross_margin; profit_margin; filed_revenue; filed_net_income; filed_eps_diluted]—but that is thesis, not a reason to put on a 240-minute trade.\n\nUse the measured no-news distribution essentially unchanged. The base geometry has a much higher stop-first rate than target-first rate, and the current information does not justify claiming that today is different. The desk should stand aside until a timestamped company disclosure or a decisive price confirmation supplies an actual catalyst.','\n',char(10)),'','',NULL,1,5,6,'none',0.26900000000000003907,0.64900000000000002131,0.082000000000000010658,0.3,NULL,NULL,0.26851851851851855634,0.25,'Veto opening a position today: no verified, timestamped, firm-specific catalyst capable of overcoming MSFT’s unfavorable measured stop-first base rate for this exact 240-minute setup. The available news is either analyst context, macro/AI sentiment, or a non-financial regional infrastructure announc','',0,'gpt-5.6-terra','flex',1,18254,2921,1387,0.040713999999999996859,25.075281143188474786,'',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'',NULL);
